inl note_of_eoie_dogfood_1 () = Note ("EOIE-DOGFOOD", 1u32, "2026-10-16T01:19Z", "claude", "Friction (2026-10-15 21:19 -04:00, Claude b7595ac3): agile note without --as records author=user silently, so an agent note on APP-TIMELINE was attributed to the user; notes cannot be edited, only corrected by a second note. Proposal: require --as (or default to the calling agent) and print the author in the receipt before writing.")
inl note_of_eoie_dogfood_2 () = Note ("EOIE-DOGFOOD", 2u32, "2026-10-18T05:58Z", "claude", "(2026-10-18 01:58 -04:00, Claude fc1568a6) agile rename rewrites the item's own rows but not mentions of the old ID inside other items' note text: renaming HARNESS-AGREE-FAIL/RUN-ONLY-USEFUL left 4 stale references (agile.spi notes of other items), fixed with text-replace --all. Rename should rewrite every quoted or bare mention and report the count.")
inl note_of_zig_float_format_1 () = Note ("ZIG-FLOAT-FORMAT", 1u32, "2026-10-14T12:30Z", "main-thread", "08:30 re-measured on zig 0.18.0-dev.146 (machine loaded by a compiler build): cold ReleaseFast build of a std.debug.print {d} program is 57-75 s for both i32 and f64 (fresh cache each); the float delta is under the load noise. 0.18-dev cold std builds are ~6x slower than the 0.17 figures, so the cache matters more than the printer. Next: measure quiet with a warm global cache, i32 vs f64.")
inl note_of_zig_float_format_2 () = Note ("ZIG-FLOAT-FORMAT", 2u32, "2026-10-15T10:49Z", "main-thread", "06:49 groom: toolchain check: the scoop zig is 0.17.0, while the 10-14 measurement says 0.18.0-dev.146 (the harness Zig may come from a different path). Next grain: print the harness tools.Zig path and version, then re-measure std.fmt float cost on that exact binary.")
inl note_of_zig_float_format_3 () = Note ("ZIG-FLOAT-FORMAT", 3u32, "2026-10-15T10:52Z", "main-thread", "06:52 groom: resolved. The harness Zig is the scoop shim zig -> scoop/apps/zig-dev/current/zig.exe (SPIRAL_ZIG unset), version printed alongside this note; scoop/apps/zig/current is a separate stable 0.17.0. So the 10-14 0.18-dev measurement matches the harness, and the next re-measure must call zig-dev explicitly.")
inl note_of_zig_float_format_4 () = Note ("ZIG-FLOAT-FORMAT", 4u32, "2026-10-17T10:02Z", "main-thread", "06:02 main-thread night: root cause found and fixed in staging: the ~1.1 s per float-printing program is std.fmt.allocPrint generic float path, not the algorithm. pack-c/zig-float-render.ps1 adds spiralFloatText (std.fmt.float.render .decimal into a stack buffer); builds in 1,450-1,524 ms (i32 1,406-1,597). Output equivalence with {d}: 400,048 values (edge cases, NaN, inf, subnormals, 200k random f64 and f32 bit patterns), 0 mismatches. The lib half for show is staged too (pack-c/lib-zig-float-text.ps1, show_floats passes on the candidate); left: the mixed int/float branches in obj_to_string_zig. Pack: night pack 10-17 (scripts %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin\\packs\\night-1017, each with -DryRun; final review single-flight-20261017-053315 on the exact pack: 6,906 rows, DISAGREE 0, residual-only Zig 457 and Rust 415, 3 intended Rust exit cells (shown as 2 NATIVE-DIFF rows); builds in single-flight, hopacsota and gpt5parallel; hopacsota inline and random:23 equal single-flight on every compile and residual cell; corpus 144 of 144; Zig at C speed on the bench).")
inl note_of_zig_float_format_5 () = Note ("ZIG-FLOAT-FORMAT", 5u32, "2026-10-19T12:33Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 08:33 lap 1 grain: closed: the build-time fix staged 10-17 (spiralFloatText over std.fmt.float.render .decimal into a stack buffer instead of the generic allocPrint path; float programs build in about 1.45-1.52 s like i32 ones; 400,048 values identical to {d}) is in spiral_compiler.fs (2 references) and in every accepted pack since; today's pack 5 review has Zig with 1 row not ok of 467 and DISAGREE 0 Next: -")
inl note_of_zig_float_format_6 () = Note ("ZIG-FLOAT-FORMAT", 6u32, "2026-10-24T11:49Z", "main", "2026-10-19 laps folded from the deleted history ledger (docs/agents/history/2026-10-19-backlog-laps, HISTORY-BACKLOG-LAPS-DRIFT): lap 2 09:25 (subagent2): already Done in lap 1 (status Done 100 verified) -> next: -")
