inl note_of_kino_parallel_cache_4 () = Note ("KINO-PARALLEL-CACHE", 4u32, "2026-10-19T13:27Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 09:27 lap 2: DONE, with the sample migration handed to its duplicate. Evidence this item's own question is answered: dep HOPAC-WARM-SERVER is Done; the daemon-side pool is in the tree (compiler_daemon.ex:80 SPIRAL_CELLS_DAEMON_POOL, auto by default; Spiral.Cells.CompilerPool, default 3 workers; compiler_pool_test.exs); the 10-14 stress measurement over lib stream.spi (16 tests over one shared prefix) found identical per-cell stdout and status across sequential, 1-compiler and pool-3 runs (17/17, no cross-request leak) and 2.9x wall over sequential, and the earlier 6-cell stress matched seq vs par across pools. What remained is the conditional follow-up (migrate single-module samples to notebooks), which is exactly SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS (main thread's samples work, first slice in lab/SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS, 799 single-module dirs on 10-15). Decision: track that migration only there, so the two items cannot diverge; the dep link stays as history")
