inl note_of_source_boundary_authority_7 () = Note ("SOURCE-BOUNDARY-AUTHORITY", 7u32, "2026-10-15T01:53Z", "lane-b", "21:53 lane B: --test-blocks cannot serve the last 2 consumers (both need every top-level block, not just tests); drafted host --source-blocks OUT|- IN... (rows: input#, first, header, last_content, last, header text from the same state.blocks walk testBlockRows now reuses) + session request + capability, patch tmp/lane-b/patches/source-blocks.patch (main applies at pack time); consumers staged (land after the pack): zed test-at-row.ps1 takes block spans from --source-blocks (no line heuristic; refuses a DLL without the capability), Kino memo.ex program_blocks/compiled_part replaced by Spiral.Kino.SourceBlocks (one batched dotnet call per run, keys fall back to the whole source when the DLL lacks source-blocks: sound, no heuristic)")
inl note_of_source_boundary_authority_8 () = Note ("SOURCE-BOUNDARY-AUTHORITY", 8u32, "2026-10-15T02:17Z", "lane-b", "22:17 lane B: scratch host with --source-blocks builds (0 errors); staged zed test-at-row.ps1 on it vs the heuristic one: -ImpactTable identical on stream 38, am' 77, parsing 65, dice 11 definitions, -Row dry runs on 32 test rows identical; trap found: dot-sourcing compiler env.ps1 turns StrictMode 3 on and broke .Count, so the staged script sets StrictMode off after it; test-blocks byte-identity corpus run (1,893 .spi over spiral lib+apps, eoie, dice, alphabet, polyglot lib+apps) in progress")
