inl note_of_kino_test_timeout_1 () = Note ("KINO-TEST-TIMEOUT", 1u32, "2026-10-14T13:09Z", "lane-b", "cause: notebook.spi walk takes a step's budget only from its own cell's ///- line; .spi test blocks become cells with their own '///- --test' line, so the file's first-line --timeout never reached them; fix in a private Kino copy: the first spiral cell's --timeout is the default budget of test steps and the whole-file step (a cell's own still wins); proof pending")
inl note_of_kino_test_timeout_2 () = Note ("KINO-TEST-TIMEOUT", 2u32, "2026-10-14T13:49Z", "lane-b", "landed (uncommitted, apps/kino/spi/notebook.spi, README, notebook_report_test.exs): the first spiral cell's --timeout (a .spi's first ///- line) is the budget of test cells without their own and of the whole-file run; test asserts >300 s left at compile time under --timeout 1800000 and <=300 s without; NotebookCli/run_notebook pass no caller timeout, so it reaches pack_sim's path; real 310 s sleep run queued")
inl note_of_kino_test_timeout_3 () = Note ("KINO-TEST-TIMEOUT", 3u32, "2026-10-14T14:49Z", "lane-b", "real proof with the tree Kino: a .spi whose first line is '///- --timeout 600000' and whose test block sleeps 310 s passed (1/1, run_notebook wall 364 s, no 300 s timeout); job tmp lane-b/slowtest")
