inl note_of_rust_union_impls_3 () = Note ("RUST-UNION-IMPLS", 3u32, "2026-10-19T12:46Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 08:46 helper-lane lap 1: DONE with evidence: the title's fix (emit Default/tag only when used) is in the committed, accepted compiler: across today's 441 samples/*/main.rs there are exactly 57 impl Default for (the reachable set predicted on 10-17, was 478) and 4 fn tag( (the 4 stale outputs of SAMPLES-STALE-OUTPUTS, was 194); x/apps/client's 16 crates have 0 of either, and view.rs went 1,786 -> 991 lines. The other half of the title's measurement, the per-element-type array loops, is not a union-impl or backend issue: today's from_N functions in x (digest 8, refs 4, fetch 3, thread 3, locate 3 ...) are monomorphized copies of x's own recursive JSON-array-to-list helper (from_7, from_10 in digest.rs each walk serde_json as_array for one element type), which every backend specializes the same way; shrinking them is a source-level change in x (decode the array once, then map), which belongs to the x lane.")
