inl note_of_kit_ci_parity_9 () = Note ("KIT-CI-PARITY", 9u32, "2026-10-31T23:48Z", "kit", "10-31 19:5x kit, pause re-decision (main pre-night groom; R3 is now \"never auto-pause for silence\"): Paused -> PLANNED. It was paused by the 10-28 silence groom (\"nothing queued\"), not by a blocker, and no note names an external condition. Back in agile next at its priority; its first step stays the one in the 10-28 note: check whether the remaining milestone shipped in a later train (installed kit 4983F9C0, TRAIN6) and close it with that evidence, else do the next milestone.")
inl note_of_kit_ci_parity_10 () = Note ("KIT-CI-PARITY", 10u32, "2026-11-04T20:13Z", "kit", "11-04 20:4x kit: DONE, verified on the INSTALLED kit (TRAIN14c): `kit ci parity C:\\home\\git\\kit` reads the workflow setup pins and prints one row per tool (rust ci=nightly-2026-10-18 local=same; otp 29 vs 29.1.2 same; elixir 1.20 vs 1.20.4 same; gleam 1.19.2 same; rebar3 3.28.0 same; zig ci=0.17.0 local=0.18.0-dev differs with \"fix: SPIRAL_ZIG=...\\zig\\0.17.0\\zig.exe\"), then \"kit ci parity refused: 1 tool(s) differ\" with exit 1. Every clause of the title holds. Side finding (real, not a bug): the box's default zig is a 0.18 dev build while CI pins 0.17.0; the printed SPIRAL_ZIG fix points at the installed 0.17.0.")
