inl note_of_fsharp_outside_compiler_30 () = Note ("FSHARP-OUTSIDE-COMPILER", 30u32, "2026-11-03T05:03Z", "main", "main 11-03 01:0x NEXT STEP (orphan sweep, 53 h silent): of the 72 lib '///> fsharp' targets left, the cheapest movable slice is the 5 MISSING RUST ARMS from n24 (sm' format_debug + format_debug_2, optionm' of_obj, resultm from_try_keeps_values_and_catches_failures, seq new_seq): give each lib function a Rust arm through backend_switch, then add '///> rust' and apply the 1.5x rule per test. After that the 2 F#-shaped assertions (listm' item_2, reflection get_functions_types: make the expected text backend-aware). The rest (FParsec 8, .NET IO 3, IDisposable 3, GUID 4, native-slower 14) stays F# by the n10 triage rule. Lib lands go through lib_land with every guard, gated on the node.")
inl note_of_fsharp_outside_compiler_31 () = Note ("FSHARP-OUTSIDE-COMPILER", 31u32, "2026-11-03T05:06Z", "main", "main 11-03 01:1x TRIAGE of n30's 5 'missing Rust arm' tests, read from the live lib: (1) optionm' of_obj: NOT a missing arm. Rust already has 'Some(!x.clone())' and of_obj_2 runs on rust; the F#-target test feeds 'null ()', a .NET null with no Rust meaning, so it stays F# (n10 rule, F#-by-nature). (2) resultm from_try_keeps_values_and_catches_failures: from_try has arms for Lua/Fsharp/Python/TypeScript/Zig but not Rust; a Rust arm must catch failwith's panic (std::panic::catch_unwind + AssertUnwindSafe) and build an exn value on Rust, a design question for compiler (Rust exn representation), not a one-line arm. (3) sm' format_debug and format_debug_2: the lib function is backend-generic (format_debug_real); what's missing is a Rust key in the TESTS' expected-value backend_switch (no_agree tests). Adding it means reading Rust's rendering from a node run, then a sm' land: CPU-heavy (sm' gate), so it goes after 02:00. (4) seq new_seq: still to read. So the real slice is 3 test-side edits (format_debug x2, new_seq?) plus 1 compiler-side design item (from_try on Rust). (4) READ: seq new_seq is a generator (F# 'seq { ... yield ... }' wrapping the yield-emitting fn); Rust has no stable generators, so it is F#-by-nature and stays F#. FINAL: of the 5, only format_debug + format_debug_2 move (test-side Rust expected strings, after 02:00 on the node); from_try on Rust is a compiler design question; of_obj and new_seq stay F#.")
inl note_of_fsharp_outside_compiler_32 () = Note ("FSHARP-OUTSIDE-COMPILER", 32u32, "2026-11-03T11:34Z", "main", "main 11-03 07:4x DRAFT for the 2 movable tests (n31): %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\FSHARP-OUTSIDE-COMPILER\\sm'.spi, recorded base 7C5111CA557EB4EF (memory draft-base-recorded-not-live). Exactly 4 added lines: a rust target line on format_debug and format_debug_2, plus a Rust arm in each test's expected-value backend_switch expecting Rust's Debug form of a 3-string tuple, (\"1\", \"2\", \"3\"). If the gate shows otherwise, its actual value is pinned. Both are no_agree tests of each backend's native rendering, so Rust is ADDED and F# stays (they are not 1.5x-retirement tests). NEXT: gate sm'.spi in a node spiral mirror (serial, after main's current node chain), then lib_land_window with the base check.")
inl note_of_fsharp_outside_compiler_33 () = Note ("FSHARP-OUTSIDE-COMPILER", 33u32, "2026-11-03T14:01Z", "main", "main 11-03 09:4x LANDED lib/spiral/sm'.spi (draft DA64EBB2, base 7C5111CA): format_debug and format_debug_2 gain rust targets with the Rust backend's native renderings (tuple '1, 2, 3'; record '{ c = 1; a = 2; b = 3 }'). The first draft guessed Rust's {:?} form and failed 2/68 on europa; corrected from the observed outputs, then europa 68/68 (6 unsupported = lua/cuda absent there). Round-trip canonical+fixpoint; lib_land_window closed green (consumers compile, document_test, type_probe pass); undo 20261103-094700.")
inl note_of_fsharp_outside_compiler_34 () = Note ("FSHARP-OUTSIDE-COMPILER", 34u32, "2026-11-05T07:40Z", "main", "11-05 03:40 main TRIAGE, the last open rows of n31: (4) seq new_seq STAYS F#: new_seq emits an F# seq { ... } computation expression (lazy generator with yield) and has Gleam/Fsharp/Python arms but no Rust arm, because stable Rust has no generators; F#-by-nature under the n10 rule, like the FParsec rows. (5) listm' item_2 (an F#-shaped assertion): DRAFTED as a no_agree test with rust added (expected text by run_target: F# 'System.Exception: Option does not have a value.', others 'Option does not have a value.', the sm' format_exception pattern); draft %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\FSHARP-OUTSIDE-COMPILER\\listm'.spi on base B42788D0FE8A2539, round trip clean; node proof + land queued (job main-item2). (6) reflection get_functions_types: next, the same way. resultm from_try's Rust arm stays a compiler design question (Rust exn representation).")
inl note_of_fsharp_outside_compiler_35 () = Note ("FSHARP-OUTSIDE-COMPILER", 35u32, "2026-11-05T08:56Z", "main", "11-05 04:56 main LANDED BOTH remaining F#-shaped assertions (unstaged lib/spiral), each a no_agree test that keeps F# and ADDS rust with a backend-aware expectation: (1) listm'.spi item_2 (B42788D0 -> 2E75EDF3): exception text F# 'System.Exception: Option does not have a value.' / others 'Option does not have a value.'; (2) reflection.spi get_functions_types (A2DCD347 -> BC60005C): type name F# 'int32' / others 'i32'. PROOF on a quiet codespace (Ubuntu, 4 cores; the node attempt was VOID from load, headroom 1.24/1.29, and stopped): listm' control 35/35, draft 35/35; reflection control 15/15, draft 15/15, with the compiler REBUILT from the box's live sources (HEAD's committed compiler lacks pack39's UnionCaseName op that live reflection.spi and metrics.spi already use: a first pass with the HEAD compiler failed 'Unbound term variable: case_name', an environment mismatch, not the draft). Box closes green for both: signatures unchanged, spiral.spi compiles, document_test 26/26, type_probe pass (35 and 15 typed), 0 respell drift; undo 20261105-044743 and -045137. STATUS of the n24/n31 inventory: every row has an outcome, Rust added or F#-by-nature (FParsec, .NET IO, IDisposable, GUID, seq computation expressions, of_obj null). Left: resultm from_try's Rust arm, a compiler design question (Rust exn representation, catch_unwind), handed to the compiler lane.")
inl note_of_fsharp_outside_compiler_36 () = Note ("FSHARP-OUTSIDE-COMPILER", 36u32, "2026-11-05T09:27Z", "main", "11-05 05:27 main WINDOWS confirmation after landing (box, one run_notebook --gate over the LIVE landed files): file_system.spi + listm'.spi + reflection.spi = 93/93 passed, 0 failed, 0 unsupported; no_agree reasons registered: 'exception text is backend-specific' (item_2) and 'type names are backend-specific' (get_functions_types). With the Linux codespace proofs, tonight's three lib lands are green on both OSes.")
inl note_of_fsharp_outside_compiler_37 () = Note ("FSHARP-OUTSIDE-COMPILER", 37u32, "2026-11-05T10:05Z", "compiler", "11-05 06:0x compiler (main's low-priority ask, the item's last row): resultm.from_try HAS A RUST ARM, landed (unstaged). No new representation was needed: base.spi already maps exn to Rc<str> on Rust (exn_switch), catch_unwind_rust turns failwith's panic_any::<String> payload into text (rust_panic_text), and rust_exn_of_text builds the exn. So the Rust arm is identical to the Lua arm: 'try (\\\\ () => Ok (fn ()) : result t exn) caught |> optionm::value' with caught = Some (Error (ex_fn \\\\ () => ex)). The test from_try_keeps_values_and_catches_failures gained ///> rust. Proof: lib_gate on a lib copy, test filtered: passed, failed_targets {}, unsupported 0, type errors 0 (Rust included). lib_land_window closed GREEN at 05:5x after the kernel replay gate released the lib: apps/spiral compiles, document_test 26, type_probe PASS (7 typed), 0 respell drift; live resultm.spi 8014CE936593 (base FAEDC603), lib digest DBF22F263592444A, undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261105-055148.")
inl note_of_fsharp_outside_compiler_38 () = Note ("FSHARP-OUTSIDE-COMPILER", 38u32, "2026-11-05T10:05Z", "main", "11-05 06:05 main DONE: the last row closed by compiler (resultm.from_try's Rust arm, landed green 05:5x, live resultm.spi 8014CE936593; it reused base.spi's exn = Rc<str> and catch_unwind_rust, so no new representation was needed). Every row of the n24/n31 inventory now has an outcome: Rust ADDED (format_debug x2, item_2, get_functions_types, from_try) or F#-by-nature (FParsec, .NET IO, IDisposable, GUID, seq computation expressions, of_obj null) per the n10 rule. Tonight's three adds are green on Linux and Windows (93/93 on the box).")
inl note_of_kit_hand_crate_units_1 () = Note ("KIT-HAND-CRATE-UNITS", 1u32, "2026-10-25T00:59Z", "eoie", "20:59 Filed from the CLEAN preflight (EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN notes 149-150) and x's build research (X-PARALLEL-BUILD notes 5-6, relayed at the user's request). User ruling via x: no automatic splitting or dedup in the compiler; model by hand and export, sharpening eoie's method (whole verbs into sibling crates, calls across crates through exports, shared types in Spiral-only packages, let/inl chosen by measured size). Over the limit with all 33 slices: eoie_ci_parity 1956, eoie_job_host 1852, eoie_log_sequences 1743, eoie_agile_mutation 1646, eoie_job_launch 1512, eoie_jobs_doctor 1435, eoie_job_rechain 1367, command_spec_domain 1278, eoie_job_control 1217, eoie_do_write 1184, eoie_table_sequences 1111, eoie_adoption 1110, agile_task_next 1087, eoie_cli 1034, eoie_do_git 1020, eoie_jobs 1017, eoie_machine_watch 1016. Research to apply: group crates by sharing unit (the strongly connected component of the topology), not one per tiny entry, with a wide, shallow graph and a small root types crate; keep crate boundaries monomorphic (share-generics is off at opt-level 2/3); split inside a crate with modules where a unit is one concern. Rule, written before splitting: work the largest overage first; a split must keep every exported name and every test, and each resulting crate must be at most 950 lines (50 lines of headroom). Done when the whole-train preflight (chain emulation plus regen and cargo check over the parked slices) reports 0 crates over 1000 and cargo check passes.")
inl note_of_kit_hand_crate_units_2 () = Note ("KIT-HAND-CRATE-UNITS", 2u32, "2026-10-25T02:00Z", "eoie", "22:00 State. (1) Landing the 33 slices into eoie/src failed twice before writing anything (fmt-rebase applies to a work copy first): edition-3 lib text broke the slices' 'requires lib' checks ('inl write_error_line' is now ':= write_error_line', 'let' is ':~', forall is '\\*'). All 7 checks in the 56 scripts the slices reach now match either spelling and pass on the live lib. Snapshot 20261024-210629-before-land-33.zip taken; spec case 47 appended (part of this landing). (2) Lever to test first: the over-limit crates are mostly inl helpers re-inlined per call site (eoie_ci_parity is about 480 Spiral lines making 1956 Rust lines across 51 fns, none over 284). Probe: switch the top-level inl helpers in model.spi to let and regen that one crate (train-cargo-root copy, model edited; original at scratch clean\\ci-model-inl.spi). Split into a sibling crate only if it is still over 950. (3) At 21:2x Claude Code's memory reaper killed both the re-emulation and the probe (free RAM 2.7 of 15.9 GB). No orphans, no lease. Not restarted without the user's go.")
inl note_of_kit_hand_crate_units_3 () = Note ("KIT-HAND-CRATE-UNITS", 3u32, "2026-10-25T02:15Z", "eoie", "22:15 The 33 parked slices are landed in eoie/src as an unstaged layer: 215 writes, 19 formatted, 0 removals (fmt-rebase stage LAND33; snapshot 20261024-210629-before-land-33.zip). The parked-train scratch is now only a backup. In-tree fix: eoie_notebook_progress's eoie_notebook_batch_line export tupled ((command, age_minutes) : string * u64 -> string) so eoie_machine_watch's two-argument host call compiles. Probe running: eoie_ci_parity model.spi with top-level inl helpers as let (original kept at scratch clean\\ci-model-live-inl.spi), regenerated without publishing alongside notebook_progress and machine_watch, with cargo check. The reap switch now lives in ~/.claude/settings.json env, so background runs survive memory pressure.")
inl note_of_kit_hand_crate_units_4 () = Note ("KIT-HAND-CRATE-UNITS", 4u32, "2026-10-25T03:22Z", "eoie", "23:22 Progress. The tree was made consistent (115 stale crates regenerated and published, cargo check passed). Splits published with notebooks green: eoie_ci_parity 1812 -> eoie_ci_probe 917 + eoie_ci_verdict 502 + eoie_ci_parity 932 (shared Spiral-only eoie_ci_model); eoie_table_sequences 1111 -> eoie_table_sequences 950 + eoie_table_sections 818 (Spiral-only eoie_table_sequence_args); eoie_job_rechain 1367 -> eoie_job_rechain 847 + eoie_job_chain 622 (Spiral-only eoie_job_after_model). Checked, publishing: eoie_jobs_doctor 1435 -> eoie_jobs_doctor 891 + eoie_jobs_doctor_env 687 (Spiral-only eoie_jobs_doctor_model). Applied, checking: eoie_log_sequences -> eoie_log_sections (section modules). Measured levers: inl->let on helpers -7% only; dropping union_reflection.union_case_where for one small lookup -46 lines in a crate (it builds a closure per case; making it cheaper is a lib-level lever worth an item); an option-returning helper cost +8 lines against an inline match; list equality (= Nil, = []) generates a structural eq function, so match instead. Method in memory spiral-macro-gotchas (hand crate splits). Owed before the release: the spiral-test registry (eoie_dev_spiral_tests/registry.spi) needs the new test modules (eoie_ci_model tools, eoie_ci_probe probe, eoie_ci_verdict verdict, eoie_ci_parity parity, eoie_job_rechain rechain, eoie_job_chain chain, eoie_jobs_doctor_env env, eoie_jobs_doctor check) and the moved paths (eoie_job_rechain/model.spi -> eoie_job_after_model/model.spi, eoie_jobs_doctor/model.spi -> eoie_jobs_doctor_model/model.spi, eoie_log_sequences section_* -> eoie_log_sections).")
inl note_of_kit_hand_crate_units_5 () = Note ("KIT-HAND-CRATE-UNITS", 5u32, "2026-10-25T04:28Z", "eoie", "00:28 Progress: 9 of 16 published with notebooks green. Since note 4: eoie_jobs_doctor 1435 -> 891 + eoie_jobs_doctor_env 687 (its module was renamed environment: a module named env shadows lib env in the notebook build); eoie_log_sequences 1743 -> 868 + eoie_log_sections 942 (sequences.spi's notebook test passes, but Cells then compiles main for Zig, which rejects multi-argument exports; that file was never in a release notebook list, and the limitation predates the split); eoie_do_write 1184 -> 937 + eoie_do_file_steps 347; eoie_do_git 1020 -> 895 + eoie_do_git_reports 349; eoie_adoption 1110 -> 649 + eoie_adoption_habits 587; eoie_machine_watch 1016 -> 932 + eoie_machine_window_watch 112 (model moved to Spiral-only eoie_machine_watch_model; eoie_process_table repointed). Measured and reverted: an eoie_jobs trim (union <> replaced by a match, known_job inl->let) gave 1017 -> 1018. Left (7): eoie_jobs 1017, eoie_job_control 1211, eoie_job_launch 1512, eoie_job_host 1852, agile_task_next 1087, command_spec_domain 1278, eoie_agile_mutation 1646. Plan for the job family, the sharing unit (x finding 2): control, launch and host each inline eoie_jobs' job_summary (134), job_state_now (83), gate_wait_of (76) and job_state_of (76), about 370 lines per crate. A new crate eoie_job_state, below all of them (eoie_jobs dispatches to them, so they cannot call eoie_jobs directly), exports eoie_job_summary(verb, id) and eoie_job_state_parts(id) -> word * exit * detail. A Spiral decoder in eoie_jobs.model rebuilds job_state, so callers keep matching on the union. Single giants left: eoie_job_launch job_started 479, eoie_agile_mutation agile_entry 955, command_spec_domain command_more_usages 322.")
inl note_of_kit_hand_crate_units_6 () = Note ("KIT-HAND-CRATE-UNITS", 6u32, "2026-10-25T04:55Z", "eoie", "00:55 The shared job state crate is published (23 crates regenerated, 7 changed, cargo check green; notebooks: eoie_jobs model with a new round-trip test, eoie_job_host queue and host_model). eoie_job_state (755) exports eoie_job_summary and eoie_job_state_parts; a decoder in eoie_jobs.model rebuilds job_state. Results: eoie_jobs 1017 -> 508, eoie_job_control 1211 -> 763, eoie_job_launch 1512 -> 1350, eoie_job_host 1852 -> 1740. 11 of 16 under the limit. Left: eoie_job_launch (drafted: eoie_job_create crate takes job_launched and its helpers; Spiral-only eoie_job_launch_model holds the shapes), eoie_job_host, agile_task_next, command_spec_domain, eoie_agile_mutation. Regens are paused for main's 5j compiler install, whose codegen passes (dead helpers dropped, const locals) change generated output. After it: re-measure the 5 on the new compiler before cutting further, and re-prove the published splits (memory: recompile drafts after a compiler change).")
inl note_of_kit_hand_crate_units_7 () = Note ("KIT-HAND-CRATE-UNITS", 7u32, "2026-10-25T05:22Z", "eoie", "01:22 Post-5j re-measure, 40 crates regenerated without publishing. Gain is small: eoie_job_launch 1350 -> 1336, eoie_job_host 1740 -> 1726, eoie_agile_mutation 1646 -> 1626, agile_task_next 1087, command_spec_domain 1278; near-limit and split crates moved 0-11 lines, and every split stays at or under 950. Blocker: 5j regression. A clone-elision pass moved a captured variable inside a fold closure (eoie_log_sections group_in: method7(v2) instead of method7(v2.clone()) inside am'.vec_fold'), so rustc rejects it with E0507. Reported to main with a repro. Nothing regenerated on 5j is published until main fixes or rolls back. The tree keeps its pre-5j generated Rust, which is consistent and cargo-check green.")
inl note_of_kit_hand_crate_units_8 () = Note ("KIT-HAND-CRATE-UNITS", 8u32, "2026-10-25T05:58Z", "eoie", "01:58 All 16 over-limit crates now measure at or under 950 (measured on 5j). Published on the pre-5j compiler: 11 (see notes 4-6). Checked, not yet published: eoie_job_launch 1336 -> 593 + eoie_job_create 341 (job directory, argv, supervisor launch) + eoie_job_start_args 559 (flags, options, every refusal); agile_task_next 1087 -> 933 + eoie_agile_next_args 187; eoie_agile_mutation 1626 -> 723 + eoie_agile_routes 692 (usage error; begin, set and edit routes with validation); command_spec_domain 1278 -> 693 + eoie_command_help 865 (more usages, agile subcommand known, and the root-flag refusal, which sits beside the subcommand fold it needs: putting it in routes cost +515 there); eoie_job_host 1726 -> 731 + eoie_job_queue 549. That last one came from two moves: a one-call delete in place of lib file_system.file_delete, whose Rust path traces errors at about 200 generated lines, worth a lib item; and the held-job decision behind eoie_job_queue_decide. The registry is updated: 3 moved paths fixed, 10 notebooks added, 111 total. Publishing waits for 5k (the fix for 5j's move-on-last-use bug), which main is building. Then: prove eoie_log_sections on the 5k candidate, regenerate and publish every changed crate with cargo check, run the new modules' notebooks, then the single release.")
inl note_of_kit_hand_crate_units_9 () = Note ("KIT-HAND-CRATE-UNITS", 9u32, "2026-10-25T06:16Z", "eoie", "02:16 5k candidate proven for main: eoie_log_sections, eoie_log_sequences and eoie_table_sections regenerated with SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL = pack-next5k (core 3DC18876); cargo check exit 0, with the fold's v2.clone() restored. Publishing waits for the install. Also packed for SLATE: S5's job chain --serial rebased onto the post-split layout (scratch clean\\s5-rebase\\job-chain-serial.do: eoie_job_rechain/model.spi -> eoie_job_after_model/model.spi, chain.spi -> eoie_job_chain/chain.spi); it applies cleanly on a copy of the current tree (11 replacements, 6 files) and lands with the SLATE prep.")
inl note_of_kit_hand_crate_units_10 () = Note ("KIT-HAND-CRATE-UNITS", 10u32, "2026-10-25T07:05Z", "eoie", "03:05 S5 (job chain --serial) landed in the tree; on 5k it put eoie_job_chain at 981, over the 950 rule. Step 1, a shared capture/print helper for its three process calls: 959, still over. Step 2, the prewritten fallback: new crate eoie_job_serial (549) holds the in-job --run-serial runner, exported as eoie_job_serial_run () -> i32. It re-parses its own command line through the Spiral-only eoie_job_after_model (arguments_from moved there, along with its test), so no Spiral list crosses a crate. eoie_jobs/jobs.spi dispatches on argument 2 = --run-serial, which keeps eoie_job_chain HostFree (a dispatch in its entry would have broken that). Result: eoie_job_chain 878, eoie_jobs 544, rechain 843; cargo check is green with create/start_args/queue regenerated beside them; notebooks after_model, chain and jobs model pass. make-SLATE lists eoie_job_serial in the census merge, and job-script-check is ok. Next: agile_subcommand_shape via agile_subcommand_of, which drops the second union_cases_fold; baseline and trial both on 5k.")
inl note_of_kit_hand_crate_units_11 () = Note ("KIT-HAND-CRATE-UNITS", 11u32, "2026-10-25T18:07Z", "eoie", "14:07 kit: fresh-clone gap reported by main (second laptop, HEAD a12135b): 8 crates have Cargo.toml, .spi and package.spiproj committed but no generated .rs: eoie_agile_list_args, eoie_agile_next_args, eoie_agile_routes, eoie_command_help, eoie_job_create, eoie_job_queue, eoie_job_serial, eoie_job_start_args. They are SLATE's new hand-split crates; their sources were committed ahead of the regen, so uild.ps1 on a clean clone fails ('couldn't find eoie_job_queue\\decide.rs'; eoie_job_host depends on it).\n- Closes when SLATE publishes: its single-workspace regen writes the .rs for all 234 crates, these 8 included (make-SLATE newPackages), and the user's next commit carries them.\n- Guard for next time (CRATE-GATE-HARDEN scope): the release preflight refuses a tree where a workspace member's [lib]/[[bin]] path names a .rs that is missing, so a split never ships source without output. One check, no driver regen step: generation stays a release concern.")
inl note_of_kit_hand_crate_units_12 () = Note ("KIT-HAND-CRATE-UNITS", 12u32, "2026-10-25T18:09Z", "eoie", "14:09 kit: SLATE measure on 5l'' (234 crates, two batches regenerated in one workspace): all ≤1000. Ten are over the 950 margin:\n- agile_task_creation 960, agile_todo_lines 983, agile_todo_scan 959, eoie_do_edit 981, eoie_do_program 999, eoie_experiment_analysis 992, eoie_memory_query 981, eoie_repo_accept_review 970, eoie_style_census 959, patch_compat_driver 982.\n- Rule (950 margin): none of these may grow until split. eoie_do_program (999) is the first hand split after KIT-RENAME, then eoie_experiment_analysis (992); both before any feature work in those packages.\n- The heal stages that touch them (Cons->:: sugar, granular migration) must measure them first: a respell or heal that adds even one generated line to eoie_do_program fails the gate.")
inl note_of_kit_hand_crate_units_13 () = Note ("KIT-HAND-CRATE-UNITS", 13u32, "2026-10-25T18:12Z", "eoie", "14:12 kit: split design for eoie_do_program (999 lines on 5l''; first split after KIT-RENAME). Measured attribution of do_program.rs, generated lines per function:\n- header_options 111, prelude 87, rule_at 79, rules_at 67, step_at 55, patch_at 51, query_words 50, count_at 48, steps_encoded 47, edit_at 41, compiled 34, steps_at 34, rule_record 30, edit_header_at 28, edit_record 27.\n- No tests are compiled in. Host blocks (tokens_of 2748 chars) are one line each, so line count comes from the parser and encoder functions, not from host code.\nCut by what the pieces share:\n- New crate eoie_do_rules holds the rules grammar: count_at, rule_at, patch_at, hunk_rules, rules_at, hunks_of, patch_stray_line, plus rule_record and rules_encoded. Its one export is eoie_do_rules_at(tokens: Rc<Vec<(i32, Rc<str>)>>, index: i32) -> (i32 next, bool ok, Rc<str> encoded rules or rejection, i32 rule count).\n  The token list is a plain Rust type, so it crosses crates without encoding. The rules come back already in the 31/30-separated record form, which is exactly what compiled emits, so no decode step is needed.\n- eoie_do_program keeps the tokenizer, steps, edit header, show and query. Its edit_block carries the encoded rules text (a field in its own block type), and steps_encoded splices that text in.\n- Estimates: eoie_do_rules ~370 lines, eoie_do_program ~710 (999 - ~310 + ~20 glue), both under 950. Rejected: deduping only. The two duplicated Word/Quoted arm pairs (except, edit target) and the three repeated 'expect files' rejections save ~25 lines, which is ~975, still over the margin.\n- Tests: the rules test blocks (patch hunks, pattern rules, regex escapes, block strings) move to eoie_do_rules. The program-level tests stay, plus one e2e test that compiles a program with rules and compares records byte for byte against today's output (the golden from today's binary).")
inl note_of_kit_hand_crate_units_14 () = Note ("KIT-HAND-CRATE-UNITS", 14u32, "2026-10-25T18:13Z", "eoie", "14:13 kit: split design for eoie_experiment_analysis (992 lines on 5l''; second after eoie_do_program). analysis.spi is 165 source lines but compiles to 986, because packages are inlined: eoie_experiments (the plan model), eoie_table_query, agile_note_model, union_reflection.\n- Generated lines per function: analyzed_plan 226, prelude 74, analyzed 61, plan_trusted 53, terms_of 45, test_of 39, tallied 39, test_plan_of 37, values_of 36, prediction_of 36, numeric_note 34, early_rows 33, argument 27, look_of 26, arm_counts 25.\nCut by what the pieces share:\n- New crate eoie_experiment_tally holds the table side: table_read and column_of (inlined from eoie_table_query), in_arm, in_scope, tallied, early_rows, values_of, median_terms. Its one export is eoie_experiment_arm_tally(table_path, mask, group_column, time_column, since, arm, metric_column) -> (rows, count, sum, squares, successes, early, values text).\n  The analysis crate calls it once per arm and keeps the plan model, the look/verdict logic and the ledger writes.\n- Why there: the table cells never leave the tally crate (table_cells stays crate-local), and only plain numbers and text cross. The plan model stays in one crate, so test_of and test_plan_of aren't duplicated.\n- Estimate: tally ~250-300 lines, analysis ~720. Unverified until measured: how much of analyzed_plan's 226 lines is inlined table code. Step 1 after the rename regenerates with the tally functions stubbed and measures that share before cutting.\n- Tests: the tally test blocks move with the tally functions, plus one e2e test running analyze on a fixture ledger and table and comparing output byte for byte against today's binary.")
inl note_of_kit_hand_crate_units_15 () = Note ("KIT-HAND-CRATE-UNITS", 15u32, "2026-10-25T21:07Z", "eoie", "17:07 kit: compiler delta on the near-gate crates, from the tree's current .rs (written 10-18 to 10-24 by earlier compilers; SLATE publishes only at the end of its regen) against the 5l'' measure. eoie_do_program 999 = 999, agile_todo_lines 983 = 983, patch_compat_driver 982 = 982, eoie_do_edit 981 = 981, eoie_memory_query 981 = 981, but eoie_experiment_analysis 986 to 992 (+6 on 5l''). So that crate's growth comes from the compiler, not from source; the note-14 split covers it either way.")
inl note_of_kit_hand_crate_units_16 () = Note ("KIT-HAND-CRATE-UNITS", 16u32, "2026-10-30T14:13Z", "kit", "10-30 10:1x kit: SIZE RISK, measured on the TRAIN5-applied tree (generated .rs lines per crate). 17 crates are at 950 or more: kit_do_program 999, kit_do_edit 996, kit_memory_query 996, kit_ci_probe 996, kit_job_gate 994, agile_todo_scan 993, kit_experiment_analysis 992, kit_job_host 991, agile_task_listing 988, agile_task_creation 977, kit_style_census 977, kit_command_help 972, kit_repo_accept_review 970, agile_task_notes 966, kit_lint_scan 965, kit_cli 964, agile_task_next 954. The first 8 sit within 9 lines of the gate, so one more compiler respell (#15 saw +6 on experiment_analysis from the compiler alone) or one small feature fails the release train's crate gate. Order rule: split the 5 crates at 994 or more before PACK-8 lands, starting with do_program (#13 design) and experiment_analysis (#14 design); the rest go when a change touches them. The splits are scratch-copy work (CPU-light until the regen) and run after the TRAIN5 rerun, which needs the user's OK.")
inl note_of_kit_hand_crate_units_17 () = Note ("KIT-HAND-CRATE-UNITS", 17u32, "2026-10-30T15:02Z", "compiler", "10-30 11:0x compiler, for n16 (kit's ask via main): PACK-8 adds NO lines to the 5 crates at 994 or more. Box job job-1793371864251-compiler-kit-crate-delta2 ran kit's own compiler-contracts\\test-regeneration.ps1 -Package <crate> -KeepStaged (staged copy, no kit tree write) twice per crate, through SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL: once with the installed compiler (control) and once with the pack8 candidate (core 17DDB2DCEF2A2D52, host EEBCBFF8658A1EF9, equal to main's node build). Generated .rs lines, tree / installed / pack8: kit_do_program 999/999/999, kit_do_edit 996/996/996, kit_memory_query 996/996/996, kit_ci_probe 996/996/996, kit_job_gate 994/994/994. Delta 0 on all five, and the control reproduces the tree exactly, so the method measures what TRAIN5 would publish. PACK-8 itself does not push any of them over 1,000. The margin is still 1-6 lines, so n16's split order stands for the next respell or feature. Script: C:\\home\\data\\pack8-review\\kit-crate-delta.ps1 (reusable: edit the package list and the expected hashes).")
inl note_of_kit_hand_crate_units_18 () = Note ("KIT-HAND-CRATE-UNITS", 18u32, "2026-10-30T18:49Z", "kit", "10-30 14:5x kit: GROOM FINDING. The crate gate is now what gates kit's feature work. Today, three features were stopped by generated size, not by design:\n- GRANULAR-LINT --tsv: kit_lint_macros 910 -> 962.\n- EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES --median: kit_table_measures is at 921 and inlines kit_table_query's stats, so a per-measure sorted value list lands near 970.\n- EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES --in-set: kit_table_sequences is at 948.\nThree more were shipped only by cutting a new unit: kit_memory_save (kit_memory 666 -> 954 inlined), kit_lint_flow* (one crate measured 1529), kit_do_git_reports (git status moved; kit_do_git 892 -> 980 otherwise).\nCurrent near-gate list (generated lines, live tree after the pack-8 regen): kit_do_program 999, kit_do_edit 996, kit_memory_query 996, kit_ci_probe 996, kit_job_gate 994, agile_todo_scan 993, kit_experiment_analysis 992, kit_job_host 991, agile_task_listing 988, kit_command_help 972, agile_task_notes 970, agile_task_next 967, kit_lint_scan 965, kit_table_sequences 948, kit_machine_watch 935, kit_memory_save 933, kit_table_measures 921.\nPLAN (after TRAIN5, so its review stays readable): split in this order, each by what the pieces share (n13/n14 designs):\n- kit_lint_macros' file walker -> kit_lint_walk (unblocks --tsv)\n- stats out of kit_table_measures -> a kit_table_stats crate with one export (unblocks --median)\n- kit_table_sequences' capture parsing -> its own unit (unblocks --in-set)\n- then the five at 994-999.\nEstimate: D6, 720m total, unchanged.")
inl note_of_kit_hand_crate_units_19 () = Note ("KIT-HAND-CRATE-UNITS", 19u32, "2026-10-30T19:07Z", "kit", "10-30 14:5x kit: split 1 of n18's plan DONE (unstaged): kit_lint_walk out of kit_lint_macros (910 -> 855; 907 with the TSV feature it unblocked). Proof in GRANULAR-LINT n34. Next in order: stats out of kit_table_measures (unblocks --median), then kit_table_sequences' captures (unblocks --in-set), then the five at 994-999.")
inl note_of_kit_hand_crate_units_20 () = Note ("KIT-HAND-CRATE-UNITS", 20u32, "2026-10-30T19:54Z", "kit", "10-30 15:5x kit: n18's table split REVISED by measurement (attribution of kit_table_measures' generated code, read-only while the box is held). The biggest shared cost is not the stats module but the where-filter, inlined from kit_table_query's wheres module: filters_from 114 + row_passes 83 + operator_from 37 = 234 of 921 lines. Stats is about 200 (stats_added 68, measure_value 63, measure_headers 45, measure_cells 35).\nDESIGN: a new crate kit_table_filter with one export, kit_table_passing(cells : table_cells, wheres : string) -> (rows : Rc<Vec<i32>>, missing : string). table_cells is already a plain Rust type (Rc<Vec<Vec<Rc<str>>>>), so it crosses the boundary without encoding. The five crates that inline wheres switch to it: kit_table_measures, kit_table_plain, kit_table_test, kit_table_diff, and kit_experiment_analysis (992, on the near-gate list). Each loops over the matched row indices instead of calling row_passes per row.\nExpected: measures 921 -> about 700 (room for --median), experiment_analysis 992 -> about 770, and the others shrink too.\nProof plan: differential 'kit table query/test/diff' runs on today's fixtures and tibia's tables (rows and receipts byte-identical to the installed kit), plus the existing table CLI tests.\nThis replaces n14's experiment_analysis-only design and the stats-only cut. Do it before --median.")
inl note_of_kit_hand_crate_units_21 () = Note ("KIT-HAND-CRATE-UNITS", 21u32, "2026-10-30T19:55Z", "kit", "10-30 15:5x kit: CORRECTION to n20, found while drafting. kit_table_query already exports kit_table_rows_kept(path, wheres) -> (ok, kept-row mask), so no new filter crate is needed. Only kit_table_measures and kit_table_plain inline wheres (filters_from/row_passes); the other table crates go through exports. The cut: measures and plain call the existing export and iterate its mask instead of inlining the 234 lines (measures 921 -> about 690). The cost is one extra read of the table file per query (rows_kept re-reads by path); acceptable for the CSV/TSV sizes in use, and remeasured on tibia's largest table before landing. kit_experiment_analysis (992) does not inline wheres, so its split stays n14's tally design. Still before --median.")
inl note_of_kit_hand_crate_units_22 () = Note ("KIT-HAND-CRATE-UNITS", 22u32, "2026-10-30T21:46Z", "kit", "10-30 17:4x kit: measures split DONE (unstaged), and the n21 route changed. kit_table_measures could not call kit_table_query's kit_table_rows_kept export, because query already depends on measures (a cargo cycle). New crate kit_table_filter (326 -> 374 lines, HostFree + LibReferenced, kit standards 0 findings) sits below both and exports kit_table_filter_kept(path, wheres) -> (ok, mask). measures reads the mask once per row with an O(1) byte lookup. measures 921 -> 838 lines including --median and its merge sort; query 708; command_spec_domain 889; kit_command_help 972 (help text only, near the gate: watch it). The mask is built as a list of marks joined once (sm'.concat_list); the per-row concat5 copy was O(n^2). kit_table_query still has its own copy of kept_mask/rows_kept, with the same O(n^2) concat5, behind kit_table_rows_kept (used by table test and experiment analysis). Next: make that export delegate to kit_table_filter, so one copy remains and the quadratic path is fixed. Lib follow-up: am'.sort's Rust arm is an insertion sort (am'.spi:697), O(n^2); a lib list/array sort in O(n log n) would replace the merge sort in stats.spi.")
inl note_of_kit_hand_crate_units_23 () = Note ("KIT-HAND-CRATE-UNITS", 23u32, "2026-10-30T22:07Z", "kit", "10-30 18:0x kit: delegation DONE (unstaged). kit_table_query's kit_table_rows_kept export now calls kit_table_filter_kept, so one copy of the filter and mask code remains, and the O(n^2) per-row concat5 mask copy is gone from table test and experiment analyze too. kit_table_query 708 -> 397 lines (it no longer inlines the where filters). Candidate B4D2A64C, built from a scratch copy identical to the live tree (0 mismatches, staged 0). Proof: table test 5/5 byte-identical to the installed kit (welch, median with --where, one-sample with !=, a missing --where column, a 20k-row welch with --where); table query 18/18 identical (fixture, tibia damage-cyclops, 100k synthetic); stats.spi test blocks 4/4 pass in cells (rust), including the new median test. Crate sizes now: filter 374, measures 838, query 397. Remaining from n22: the lib O(n log n) sort (am'.sort's Rust arm is an insertion sort), for the next lib window.")
inl note_of_kit_hand_crate_units_24 () = Note ("KIT-HAND-CRATE-UNITS", 24u32, "2026-10-30T22:42Z", "kit", "10-30 18:3x kit: kit_table_sequences split DONE (unstaged). verb.spi is now a router (counts / sections / measures); the --interval/--window/--order/--latency path moved to the new crate kit_table_sequence_measures, migrated on the way (Nil/Cons to list sugar). verb.rs 976 -> 125; kit_table_sequence_measures 908. Most of those 908 lines are kit_table_sequence_args (paths_from/files_in plus lib file_system), which is inlined into all three sequence crates: kit_table_counts 924, kit_table_sequence_measures 908, kit_table_sections 813. Next cut, if any of them grows: export the args helpers once from a small crate rather than inlining them. Proof on candidate 9BB99BD0: 10/10 sequence cases identical to the installed kit (stdout and stderr compared separately; the usage text gains the --count line), and the pz-in-traces comparison is still 4/4 SAME.")
inl note_of_kit_hand_crate_units_25 () = Note ("KIT-HAND-CRATE-UNITS", 25u32, "2026-10-31T09:51Z", "kit", "2026-10-31 05:5x kit: headroom ranking of the generated functions in the two crates nearest the 1000-line gate. (1) kit_do_program 999/1000: header_options was the largest function (111 generated lines), because it parsed 'expect files <n> replacements <n>' through three nested matches with three copies of the rejection. It is now an :~ expectation_at returning option expectation (a tuple match over tokens index+2 and index+4), and header_options keeps one Some/None arm. A test case for a non-numeric expectation was added. Notebook and regen running. (2) agile_task_creation 990/1000: agile_add_entry_0 alone is 576 of 990 generated lines, the legacy host blob behind 'agile add'. No cheap :~ win exists there; the real headroom is migrating that blob into typed Spiral (EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION's scope), and until then any growth in task_creation needs a split first.")
inl note_of_kit_hand_crate_units_26 () = Note ("KIT-HAND-CRATE-UNITS", 26u32, "2026-10-31T10:07Z", "kit", "2026-10-31 06:0x kit: CORRECTION to n25 part (1). The expectation_at extraction was measured and reverted. Its notebook passed 8/8, but the regen grew do_program.rs from 999 to 1014 lines: header_options fell 111 -> 84, while the new :~ function cost 37 lines plus an option wrapper. An :~ split only pays when the extracted body was duplicated INLINE (like owner_text in watch, which shrank 986 -> 849). The three copies here were cheap string rejections. The function is back to its original shape and is being regenerated back to 999. The new test case (a non-numeric expectation is rejected) stays, because test blocks don't generate into the crate. Real headroom for kit_do_program means a hand-modeled split: the rule/patch parsers (rule_at 79, rules_at 67, patch_at 51) can become their own unit.")
inl note_of_kit_hand_crate_units_27 () = Note ("KIT-HAND-CRATE-UNITS", 27u32, "2026-11-01T03:36Z", "kit", "10-31 23:4x kit groom (main 23:33, user: cadence/drift): Active -> PLANNED. No note in over 12 h, so nobody is working it this week; Planned keeps it in agile next at its priority (never auto-Paused, R3). First step when picked = the next step in its latest note.")
inl note_of_kit_hand_crate_units_28 () = Note ("KIT-HAND-CRATE-UNITS", 28u32, "2026-11-02T14:01Z", "x", "2026-11-02 09:59 x: DECISION RECORD (typed; groom of user waits, user 11-02: 'decisions waiting on me get met autonomously/deterministically with tests/benchs/typefeatureset modeling/backups'). kind=ByDefault. QUESTION: May the TRAIN5 release-train rerun proceed? RULE (written before acting): Default = run TRAIN5 in preflight mode (no publish). It is local, reversible, and only produces reports. Any publish step stays the user's (release-preflight-publish-gates). Split order: the 5 crates at 994+ lines first. BACKUP/UNDO: The rerun works on a scratch copy. kit state-backups before the regen. OWNER: kit. NEXT: Run the TRAIN5 preflight rerun, then split kit_do_program and kit_experiment_analysis on scratch copies per designs #13/#14. VETO: the user can reverse this at any time; the backup above is the undo.")
inl note_of_kit_hand_crate_units_29 () = Note ("KIT-HAND-CRATE-UNITS", 29u32, "2026-11-04T08:03Z", "kit", "DONE 11-04 04:4x (kit, closing with evidence): the parked train slices all publish under the limit now. TRAIN18's node run published 231 changed owners and the crate gate measured 295 crates, 294 under 1000. The one over was the new kit_heal_nameof, since split into kit_heal_nameof 531 + kit_nameof_findings 857. The grouping method is in practice: linked units with array_base row exports (kit_job_entry/kit_job_query, kit_agile_lock, kit_style_scoreboard, kit_do_facts_receipt, kit_flag_words, kit_nameof_findings), sized on the node with a one-package regen before each train (memory join-points-shrink-generated, spiral-link-boundary-shapes).")
inl note_of_kit_hand_crate_units_30 () = Note ("KIT-HAND-CRATE-UNITS", 30u32, "2026-11-06T11:21Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 07:4x kit, KIT-RENAME: renamed from EOIE-HAND-CRATE-UNITS (item IDs follow the tool name; older notes keep the old ID as history).")
inl note_of_tibia_park_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARK", 1u32, "2026-10-25T01:12Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-24 21:12 PARK RULE, written before sorting any item (user 2026-10-24 21:1x: 'groom the backlog until it's clearer when we can park tibia for dota2'). Parking means tibia goes Paused, with every open item carrying a resume condition, so Dota work can start. 'Park' isn't 'Done'. K1, an item is in scope iff at least one holds: (a) it fixes something wrong in tibia's current state: a tree that removes the user's committed tests, red tests, or a violation of a standing user rule (no hand-written Lua, granular macros); (b) it produces lib, Cells or harness code Dota reuses (Lua arms in lib, the Lua-from-Spiral bot pattern, process and world control); (c) it closes a pre-registered experiment whose next live run is already designed, so its result isn't lost. K2: a gate owned by another team holds the park only if tibia can't do the work itself. Lib, Cells and compiler gaps belong to whichever lane needs them (lane-roles memory), so they're in scope here and never a reason to wait. A release of another team's tool (an eoie verb) doesn't hold it, and the item becomes Paused with resume condition 'that release installed'. K3: nothing new enters scope after this note except a user directive or a K1(a) break found later. K4 closing pass, about 60 min: build.ps1 green on the final tree, README and BENCHMARK current, lab/ empty, live/ harness-only, then TIBIA goes Paused with its resume condition and the user commits. Applying K1/K2 at 21:2x: IN (deps of this item): TIBIA-PARTY (c, P11 then PR-28, about 4 h incl. 80 min live), TIBIA-FIDELITY (c, close with pointers after PARTY, 0.5 h), TIBIA-LIB-MIGRATION (b, about 3.2 h incl. the RED file_exists Lua arm), TIBIA-CELLS-APPS (a, the tree undoes commit 695c708, plus 4 reds, 2.5 h), TIBIA-GRANULAR-HEAL (a, 2.75 h), TIBIA-NO-HAND-LUA (a and b, 7 h), LIB-PROCESS-HANDLE (b, 2.5 h incl. edition-3 re-anchoring), TIBIA-BACKEND-MAP (b, user's BACKEND-BALANCE epic, OS-port arm and executor wiring, 2.6 h). OUT under K2: TIBIA-TOOLS-TO-EOIE (stays Blocked on EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES; parks with resume condition 'eoie release with table sequences installed'). Already parked with resume conditions and unchanged: BASELINES, ARENA-RELEASE, GPU-RENTAL, STORAGE-BOUNDARY, 2048-ANCHOR, the headless-client chain. Dota's own start conditions are on DOTA.")
inl note_of_tibia_park_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARK", 2u32, "2026-10-25T01:13Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-24 21:13 WHEN, from per-item hours (progress fields aligned to them at 21:1x), nothing top-down. In-scope work is about 25 h plus the 1 h K4 pass. It runs as four independent chains. L, lib and Lua, the longest at about 10.2 h: fix the RED file_exists Lua arm (re-gate on edition-3 lib), then gate-via-lib and the Lua-retire S1, S2 and S3 slices plus the smoke clear (LIB-MIGRATION), then NO-HAND-LUA M1-M5 (its lib log-append Lua arm comes from the same arm family). C, Cells, about 5.3 h: CELLS-APPS (HEAD's test blocks back as the base, sm'.pad_left and map's C arms, the competitor Lua over 200 locals, measure rerun), then the 3 proven client slices and the 9 remaining GRANULAR-HEAL sites. P, process, about 5.1 h: LIB-PROCESS-HANDLE's split by subject in edition 3 (after main's Cells ':!' fix), then BACKEND-MAP's joint land and executor wiring. Y, party, about 4.5 h: P11 sim and pins, the predictions job, PR-28's pre-registration, then one live-gui window (PR-28 about 80 min, which also carries the LIB-MIGRATION smoke clear and the NO-HAND-LUA M4 parity check), the read, then the FIDELITY close. Calendar: one lane alone, about 26 h, about 2 working days, so the park lands around the evening of 2026-10-26. With 2 extra agents on chains C and P (max-three-agents), the bound is chain L plus K4, about 11-12 h of wall time plus CPU contention, so around midday 2026-10-26. The one live window needs a slot from main. Risks that move the date (re-estimate in this note, never a new guess): the file_exists arm hypothesis failing (chain L), the competitor 200-locals limit needing a Lua backend change, and PR-28 failing its pre-registration (one more model round, about 2 h, as PR-25 and PR-27 did). UPDATE 2026-10-24 22:3x: LIB-MIGRATION goes from about 3.2 h to about 1.6 h (Lua file I/O landed in lib; gate-via-lib, S1, S2 and S3a landed in tibia). CELLS-APPS goes from about 2.5 h to about 3.5 h: the C reds need a char-to-string capability on C (CELLS-APPS note 21), and the user staged the tree without the candidate tests (note 20). Total about 24.5 h plus K4; calendar unchanged (park around 2026-10-26). UPDATE 2026-10-25 06:30 (per item; the overnight standing run): about 17 h left including K4, down from about 25.5. TIBIA-EDITION3 DONE. TIBIA-NO-HAND-LUA 95%: all hand-written .lua files replaced by Spiral and stub-proven; left is live confirmation (PR-11 parity counts) in the next live window, about 0.3 h inside PARTY's window. LUA-FUNCTION-LIMITS (new dep, 85%): both slices handed to main for the next pack; left is main's review plus install, then re-running the heal and competitor checks, about 0.5 h here. TIBIA-GRANULAR-HEAL: batches 1-4 re-derived and type-checked, landing after that install; 5 real sites left (forget_dead goes with LIB-MIGRATION S3), about 1.5 h. TIBIA-CELLS-APPS: the C capability is drafted as a compiler slice (c-prim-to-string) plus lib arm, candidate build queued; then re-land the candidates on the staged base, about 2.5 h. LIB-MIGRATION about 1.6 h (S3 families), PARTY about 4 h (P11, PR-28 live), FIDELITY 0.5 h, LIB-PROCESS-HANDLE about 2.5 h, BACKEND-MAP about 2.6 h, unchanged. Critical path now: PARTY's live window (needs a slot from main), plus main's pack with LUA-FUNCTION-LIMITS and c-prim-to-string. Calendar unchanged: park around 2026-10-26.")
inl note_of_tibia_park_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARK", 3u32, "2026-10-25T14:42Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-25 10:42 PARK status by chain (K1-K4 unchanged). L, lib and Lua: S1, S2, S3a and S3 families 1, 2 and 4 landed (arena now has lua.* only for random_between and native tables); family 3 lands in job-1792939269273 behind the lib gate for common.random's Lua arm; family 5 (native tables plus the 4 client sites) waits on main's 5l'' install for the healed client. NO-HAND-LUA at 95%. About 2 h left. C, Cells: CELLS-APPS candidates re-land and client-let-b5 also wait on 5l''; about 4 h. P, process: the anchored LIB-PROCESS-HANDLE slice (6 lib files plus new erlang_port, module order corrected) is in its kit gate job-1792938470349; then land, then BACKEND-MAP's joint land; about 3 h. Y, party: the combined candidate-2 + P11 land was red only on 2 gpu_sim WGSL tests timing out at 7x load (C oracles green); gpu_sim alone reruns in job-1792934707921; then the predictions job, PR-28 pre-registration and one live window from main; about 3.5 h including the window. Also sent main the fix for the LUA-FUNCTION-LIMITS chunk-main regression its 5l review found (the pair moves to the next pack). With K4 (1 h), about 13 h of one-lane work remains, so the park lands around midday 2026-10-26. Gates owned by others: the 5l'' install (C and L) and one live-gui slot (Y).")
inl note_of_tibia_park_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARK", 4u32, "2026-10-25T21:16Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-25 17:16 PARK status by chain. Y, party: DONE up to the live window: candidate 2 + P11 landed 14:55 (gpu_sim green with its new 900 s cell budget); PR-28 pre-registered 15:40 (control reproduced PR-27 exactly; predictions 16.73 kills, 6.68 potions); live-gui window requested ('tibia PR-28', 80 min), queued behind kit's uninterruptible SLATE release and two x compile windows; main stops its queue at the go. The window also carries NO-HAND-LUA M4 and the LIB-MIGRATION smoke clear, so three items close on it. L, lib and Lua: samples list sugar landed; random's lib arm, family 3 and the dead lua.spi helpers wait for a regate (the first gate was red only on load timeouts in untouched retry_fn cells; the retest copy now gets a 900 s cell budget); family 5 and the client heal wait on pack 5m (LUA-FUNCTION-LIMITS pair, fixed and staged with main). P, process: split gate red only on a load timeout (old retest rule), requeued with the fixed rule in serial-c, then world_port, the executor and the process heal. C, Cells: obj-to-string-c lands in serial-c, then the CELLS-APPS re-land. Also in serial-c: postable batches 1-7 (68 of 399 cells). Remaining one-lane work about 10 h, gated by the live window and pack 5m, so the park moves to the evening of 2026-10-26 unless the window opens tonight. The worker node isn't usable for lib gates yet (missing toolchains and the spiral rust runner; kit2 provisioning).")
inl note_of_tibia_park_5 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARK", 5u32, "2026-10-25T22:38Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-25 18:38 Queue reshaped: serial-b (job-1792945250381) died at 18:10 inside the time_span gate. Its heavy wrapper lost its console pipe ('No process is on the other end of the pipe') after about 221 of its 240 hold minutes, while the gate worked on scratch copies only (the live lib checked by hash: date_time.spi 2E01152111D969A3, unchanged; no orphan processes). Its process gate was RED only on load timeouts under the old retest rule. The queued serial-c is replaced by three heavy jobs, each kept under the 240 min hold: tibia-serial-lands (job-1792967832980: postable batches 1-7, obj-to-string-c, CELLS-APPS 13 arena files plus map and predict), tibia-serial-lib (job-1792967838479: random regate and lands, process-split gate and lands with world_port and the executor), tibia-serial-heals (job-1792967843150: process heal, time_span heal, date-casts heal); each starts after the previous ends.")
inl note_of_tibia_park_6 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARK", 6u32, "2026-10-26T00:11Z", "tibia-lane", "00:11Z PARK status 6.\nY, party: PR-28 is RUNNING. The live-gui window was granted at 23:5xZ after about 4 h queued. 11 duo hunts started 00:04Z in that held window, with PR-27's exact arguments and the first live run of the apps/arena parity prelude (NO-HAND-LUA M4). It ends about 01:10Z. A first launch was stopped by me after 70 s, inside the smoke hunt, and relaunched detached because of a shell-timeout risk. Its whole process tree was verified mine and gone, the scenario script self-restores its spawn and config files at the next start, and the results table holds only its header. main and tibia queues were stopped by hand; main's EOIE-MACHINE-WINDOWS note 34 records why that is needed.\nL, P, C: the 4 queued jobs were stopped at the go, none had started, and all 19 postable batch files were verified unchanged by hash. They get requeued at block end as 4 chained jobs, each under the 240 min hold: lands; slices plus live-retire; lib; heals.\nDrafted tonight on POSTABLE-ALL-REPOS (notes 14-21): slices for combat, geometry, search, network, terrain and arena_host, about 80 of 402 tibia cells to one post, all format-clean; plus live-retire (deletes src/live.spi and the SpiralPolicy path, lands right after PR-28).\nRemaining one-lane work: about 8 h of gated jobs after the block (lands 2 h, slices 2.5 h, lib 2.5 h, heals 2 h). Pack 5m still gates family 5, the client heal and competitor CELLS-APPS. Park forecast: midday 2026-10-26 if the queue runs through the night; the PR-28 read (descriptive only) closes chain Y tonight.")
inl note_of_tibia_park_7 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARK", 7u32, "2026-10-26T01:17Z", "tibia-lane", "01:17Z PARK status 7.\nY, party: PR-28 DONE and both tests hold (BENCHMARK.md row; TIBIA-PARTY note 98). Candidate 2 with modelled entry is adopted. Its named duo_default constructor, with a test, lands at the end of slices-a. Two follow-ups stay open on TIBIA-PARTY: the 10-14 saturation sweep rerun on duo_default (a heavy job, queued after the chain), and the ally potion-share gap (live 52 percent against 27 predicted).\nTIBIA-NO-HAND-LUA: Done (M4's live check passed in all 11 hunts).\nQueue after the block, 5 chained jobs each under the 240 min hold:\n- job-1792976709886 lands (running): postable 1-7, obj-to-string-c, CELLS-APPS;\n- slices-a: live-retire, combat, geometry, search, network, duo-default;\n- slices-b: terrain, host, hunt_sim, gpu_sim;\n- lib;\n- heals.\nKit's rename release (about 21:25 local) needs one quiet moment; tibia pauses at kit's message and requeues on \"done\" (plan sent). The tibia scripts already resolve kit-first.\nhunting_pack draft at 40 of 84 over one post (POSTABLE notes 26-27); the rest waits on the wide-record nesting design.\nPark forecast: the gated work is about 8 h of queue (lands 2, slices 3, lib 2.5, heals 2), plus the sweep. Midday 2026-10-26 if the queue runs overnight without a long kit pause.")
inl note_of_tibia_park_8 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARK", 8u32, "2026-10-26T02:36Z", "tibia-lane", "02:36Z PARK status 8.\nQueue, 6 chained jobs: lands (running, at obj-to-string-c), slices-a, slices-b, lib, heals, and the new slices-c (job-1792982017293).\n- obj-to-string-c: its first gate went red on a typing gap in the draft. The draft is fixed, and heals retries it with CELLS-APPS (TIBIA-CELLS-APPS note 26).\n- slices-c: hunting_pack and pack_sim postable slices, the last two big src files. hp-slice gained a pack_sim call fix that would otherwise have reddened its gate (POSTABLE-ALL-REPOS note 33).\nAfter slices-c, these tibia src items remain before park: the wide-record slice (needs hp-slice landed), the features input record (needs live.spi retired), the duo_default saturation sweep (a heavy job), and the map.spi postable chunks (need cells-apps-mp). Each is 1 job or less; none needs new live hours.")
inl note_of_tibia_park_9 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARK", 9u32, "2026-10-26T04:17Z", "tibia-lane", "04:17Z PARK status 9.\nslices-a is running: live.spi retired (live-retire landed 23:1x), combat-swinger landed, geometry gating. Then search, network and duo-default.\nslices-c grew to 9 steps, every src step proven offline or by stub: b3 (gate fix: untested files), hp-slice (with the pack_sim dance_step call fix), ps-slice, evolve (plus the features split; hunting_pack goes to 8 over, all wide records), skills, samples, ground_trace and lead_trace (list sugar too), parity (16/16 stub identical).\nNew: the crash rule is in run-arena (TIBIA-PARTY note 99); P12's duo sweep is queued after slices-c with amendment A1 (6 by 6 on the validated arm, about 85 min); P13 found no lead for the ally potion gap, only a descriptive hit-split shape, plus the entry-delay candidate (notes 103-104).\nBefore park, after the queue: the wide-record slice (after hp lands), offscreen (rule pre-registered as POSTABLE note 43; FFI-name trade-off; the land needs a window free of live-gui), lua.spi (after the random lands), the cells-apps arena files plus map.spi (after cells-apps), client and competitor (pack 5l), and P12's reading. No new live hours are needed for any of them.")
inl note_of_tibia_park_10 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARK", 10u32, "2026-10-26T07:50Z", "tibia-lane", "07:50Z 07:5xZ PARK status 10.\nQueue: serial-lib is running and parked at its reader guard: the random lands wait for main's pack-5m2 lib Cells run on date_time.spi (started 07:36Z). Queued behind it: heals, slices-c, P12's duo sweep, gaps. Kit's rename release is 20-30 min out. No new chained local jobs until kit's \"done\"; queued jobs stop at its \"pause\".\n- Two slices went red and were restored by hash, each on a WGSL closure, never on behaviour. slices-a geometry: sight's top-level join points took the blocker function. slices-b hunt_sim: summed took a function. Rule (POSTABLE note 45): a top-level join point never takes a function value on code a wgsl test reaches. The loop goes inside an inline function as an inner join point.\n  - Geometry v2 is proven: compiles to WGSL, the C run exits 0, and v1 fails with the gate's exact error.\n  - hunt_sim's fixed summed is proving on the remote kit worker node with tree, v1 and fix controls (job-1793001021626). It runs hunt_sim's own test notebook, because hunt_sim, gpu_sim and pack_sim are test-only files that no spiproj lists.\n  - terrain was red because geometry.xy was missing. It re-enters after geometry lands.\n- Same risk found before it fired: hp-slice and the evolve candidate had three such join points (foes_from, soonest_from, best_heal_from) on gpu_sim's WGSL path. The fix is drafted as inner-joins-apply.ps1: 4 anchors, 0 left. Its gpu_sim notebook probe runs on the node with tree, old and fix (job-1793000887195). The fix goes into hp-final and evolve only if the old candidate is red there and the fix is green.\n- Node offload: the gaps gates ran there. LIB-PATH-JOIN-NATIVE, LIB-EXIT-WITH and LIB-ARRAY-BASE are GREEN. Their touched files are byte-identical to this box, so the local gaps step reuses the verdicts. The node's heals REDs were apply failures, because the node lib lacks the lands they stack on, not test reds. They re-gate locally after serial-lib.\n- LUA-FUNCTION-LIMITS: the CRLF root cause is fixed and node-proven (omniledger runs, 14 of 14 arena entries load). Main put it in pack 5n. The client heal lands after 5n installs.\nLeft before park, unchanged: geometry, then terrain and hunt_sim re-lands; hp, ps and evolve (slices-c); the wide-record slice; offscreen; lua.spi keywords; the cells-apps arena files plus map.spi; client and competitor after 5n; P12's reading; the edition-3 manifests once the converter installs. About 8 h of gated queue; the node takes the read-only probes and gates. Forecast: evening of 2026-10-26, moved by kit's pause plus the two WGSL re-lands.")
inl note_of_tibia_park_11 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARK", 11u32, "2026-10-26T09:55Z", "tibia-lane", "09:55Z 09:5xZ PARK status 11.\nLocal queue, unchanged in order: serial-lib is running (process-split gate), then heals, slices-c, P12's duo sweep and gaps. Kit's rename pause has moved to after about 12:30Z; I stop the queued jobs at kit's \"pause\".\n- Correction to note 10: the random lands did NOT land. The reader guard waited 90 minutes on main's pack-5m2 Cells run, then refused before writing anything (TIBIA-LIB-MIGRATION note 54). The retry is packed as heals' first step, guarded by 'common.spi has no lua_math_random'. It still runs before cells-apps, which touches the same arena files. Its dead-helpers step also clears lua.spi's 5 granular sites and 3 edition-3 inl lines (66 lines become 12, dry run clean).\n- WGSL re-lands are now proven on the remote kit worker node, each with a negative control showing the exact codegen error: geometry v2; hunt_sim (11 of 11, v1 fails a gpu test); and hp-slice and evolve (3 function-param join points became inner join points; old fails 3 of 3 with YFun; fixed matches the tree row for row). huntsim-slice is back as the last step of slices-c (POSTABLE notes 51-52).\n- GRANULAR-HEAL P0, lib, this session (LIB-MACRO-HEAL notes 27-33): LIB-RESULT-DEBUG (node GREEN, 12 of 12 rows including its new test; verdict imported), LIB-TRY-LUA, LIB-RESULT-UNBOX, LIB-LIST-CASTS, LIB-THROWS-TRY and LIB-SEQ-LENGTH. Each is proven on the consumer path against the tree and a patched copy, then gated on the node one at a time, with its land packed into gaps. Gaps' earlier three lib gates (path-join-native, exit-with, array-base) are node GREEN and imported.\n- LIB-PAR-MAP had stalled after its compiler marker installed. LIB-PAR-GLEAM converts it to edition 3: the BEAM arm, plus sequential elsewhere. It prints 338350 via gleam run and via dotnet fsi, and its node gate is queued. The Rust arm waits on a granular rule for thread::scope (note 13), which GLEAM-RUST-SPLIT part 4 needs.\n- Node health: lib gates for sm' and date_time run 0 tests there (diagnosis queued), so obj-to-string-c, time-span and date-casts gate locally in heals.\nBefore park, unchanged apart from the above: the slices-c chain, the wide-record slice, offscreen, cells-apps arena files plus map.spi, client and competitor after pack 5n (not installed yet), P12's reading, and the edition-3 manifests once the converter installs (rechecked 09:0xZ: `format --manifest toml` still writes nothing). Forecast stays the evening of 2026-10-26. The local queue is about 8 h; the node carries probes and lib gates.")
inl note_of_tibia_park_12 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARK", 12u32, "2026-10-26T12:11Z", "tibia-lane", "12:11Z 12:1xZ PARK status 12.\nLANDED since note 11:\n- LIB-PROCESS-HANDLE-SPLIT, with tibia apps/host world_port and world_executor on it (all green).\n- LIB-RANDOM-LUA's lib arm, LIB-TIME-SPAN-HEAL and LIB-DATE-CASTS-HEAL.\nLIB-PROCESS-HANDLE now has only the process heal (re-anchored on the post-split base) and BACKEND-MAP's executor wiring left.\nFailed in serial-heals, root-caused and requeued in tibia-serial-gaps:\n- tibia family 3: wrote common.random', but common is unqualified (`common-`); it now writes random'. measure and random compile to Lua and load.\n- process-heal: the split had already moved its tests to list sugar; re-anchored, all 5 anchors match.\n- obj-to-string-c: its C arm made PrimToString type-check on every target; now a typed obj_to_string_c helper, so builder programs compile again on Gleam, F# and Rust.\n- client-heal: waits on cells-apps, which waits on obj-to-string-c.\nQueue: slices-c is running now (hp, ps and evolve with the inner-join WGSL fix; skills; samples; the canary traces; parity; geometry v2; terrain; hunt_sim), then P12's duo sweep, then gaps. gaps carries, in order:\n- the retries (process-heal, family 3, dead helpers, the obj-to-string chain plus cells-apps);\n- 14 lib slices (GRANULAR-HEAL P0, LIB-MACRO-HEAL notes 27-39);\n- the alphabet documents and polyglot exit heals;\n- LIB-PAR-GLEAM.\nThe 11 composed slices were proven together on F# and Rust (note 36). The newest gaps lib slices since then are LIB-DATE-CASTS2 and LIB-DATE-LUA-OR (date_time Rust casts and Lua 'or' fallbacks, proven identical on chrono 0.4.45 and lua 5.1).\nRemote kit worker node: lib gates one at a time.\n- Imported GREEN: seq-length, result-debug, result-unbox, exit-with and array-base. Each verdict file carries a bases line; process-handle-kit gate.ps1 now re-gates when a base moved.\n- Mirror fix: one bad single-file copy made 3 gates void. The mirror is now a whole-lib snapshot; try-lua, contains-char and par-gleam are re-gating behind date-casts2 and date-lua-or.\nStill before park: pack 5n's install (client and competitor), cells-apps arena files plus map.spi, the wide-record slice after hp, offscreen, P12's reading, and the edition-3 manifests once the converter installs. Forecast unchanged: the evening of 2026-10-26, or into the night if gaps' lib gates run locally.")
inl note_of_tibia_park_13 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARK", 13u32, "2026-10-26T13:41Z", "tibia-lane", "13:41Z 13:4xZ Queue repair. tibia-serial-gaps had started beside tibia-slices-c2: duo-sweep-p12, its predecessor, exited at once on its own guard ('the evolve slice has not landed; P12 waits'), and slices-c2 had been requeued with no --after when it yielded to main's install. Before I stopped gaps it LANDED family 3 (random.spi on lib random', arena build and cells lua green) and the dead-helpers cleanup (lua.spi 66 lines down to 12, which clears its 5 granular sites and 3 edition-3 inl lines). It was stopped mid-gate on a lib copy, with nothing in the tree mid-write (sm'.spi still at base 2E259892). Leaving it running would have run src slices and gaps' lib lands at once, and gaps' land reader guard would have timed out behind slices-c2's Cells runs. New serial chain, with timeouts sized as queue wait plus run: slices-c2 (running, hp-slice), then job-1793022032317 duo-sweep-p12b, then job-1793022039544 serial-gaps2 (its guarded retries skip what already landed), then job-1793022048985 serial-gaps-lib2.")
inl note_of_tibia_park_14 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARK", 14u32, "2026-10-26T15:49Z", "tibia-lane", "15:49Z Status 14 (since 13:41Z).\n- slices-c2 is still running. parity-slice landed (canary build LUA-OK, stub traces identical). geometry-slice went red only on Cells daemon contention (geometry: 16/20, the 4 failures are \"could not start the compiler on port 13905: lock_timeout\"; every other gate file was green) and restored geometry.spi by hash. slices-c-hp now starts with geometry-slice and ends with terrain-slice and huntsim-slice. A step that already landed in c2 fails at apply (anchor or control-hash refusal) before any build, so the re-runs are free.\n- Wide-record slice (the last design-blocked hunting_pack part) is drafted: census 0 over one post on hunting_pack, pack_sim and gpu_sim (POSTABLE-ALL-REPOS notes 58, 60, 61). Node pre-proof tibia-wide-probe is queued. Local tibia-wide-land is queued after cid-land4 and refuses unless c-hp has landed the evolve candidate.\n- Local chain: slices-c2 (running), then c-hp, duo-sweep-p12c, serial-gaps3, serial-gaps-lib4, polyglot-cid-land4, wide-land. Node: try-lua-gate3 (running), contains-char2, par-gleam2, obj-to-string-c, shim-sha256, shim-clock, sweep-rust, wide-probe, with kit and fiscal jobs interleaved.\nStill before park: everything in that chain, pack 5n's install (client and competitor), cells-apps arena files plus map.spi, offscreen, P12's reading, the edition-3 manifests once the converter installs, and predict's 4 over-cells (unchanged by this slice). Forecast: tonight, 2026-10-26, set by the local chain (about 9-10 h of queue).")
inl note_of_tibia_park_15 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARK", 15u32, "2026-10-26T17:10Z", "tibia-lane", "17:10Z Status 15. slices-c2 finished. Landed: skills, samples, ground-trace, lead-trace, parity and huntsim (hunt_sim gate green, memo off). Red: geometry (Cells port 13905 lock_timeout, contention) and terrain. Terrain's red is a real dependency, not a flake: its candidate's test calls geometry.xy, which only geometry-slice adds ('The module does not have the key: xy'). slices-c-hp is running now with geometry-slice first and terrain-slice/huntsim-slice last, so terrain re-lands after geometry; huntsim's re-run will refuse at its control check, as designed. c-hp's evolve step lands the fixed evolve candidate (POSTABLE note 63: worth/trial_worth restored after a PowerShell comma-precedence slip in evolve-build). kit-release-FOLLOWUP holds the other heavy slot for up to 8 h. Queued after cid-land4: wide-land, host-slice2-land, combat-land (POSTABLE notes 61-66). Node: shim-sha256 imported (weak GREEN read: the only red is gleam hash_text, red on baseline too); shim-clock was a real red from my own test's precedence (|> binds tighter than <), fixed and re-gating; contains-char re-gating after a stale-verdict reuse fix in gate.ps1; try-lua re-gating with a 12 h cap.")
inl note_of_tibia_park_16 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARK", 16u32, "2026-10-26T20:29Z", "tibia-lane", "20:29Z status 16: parked tibia lands are queued serially on this box (serial-gaps3 running, then serial-gaps-lib4, cid-land4, wide-land, host-slice2-land, combat-land, offscreen-land, samples-sugar-land). kit-release-FOLLOWUP holds the other heavy slot. The node carries the read-only proofs (arena Lua checks final4-final7). No new parks since status 15; arena-f5 grew to carry the steps, observer and arena-rest postable splits under the same guard and restore.")
inl note_of_tibia_park_17 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARK", 17u32, "2026-10-26T22:47Z", "tibia-lane", "22:47Z status 17: serial-gaps3 finished at 17:26.\n- Landed: obj-to-string-c, cells-apps (13 merged arena files), client-heal, LIB-PROCESS-HEAL.\n- Restored: cells-apps-mp (a rule defect, now fixed and riding map-postable) and arena-f5 (fam5's game_calls test, fixed and riding arena-f5-retry). Both retries are proven on the node.\nserial-gaps-lib4 has run since 17:26. Landed so far: LIB-PATH-JOIN-NATIVE, LIB-EXIT-WITH, LIB-ARRAY-BASE and LIB-RESULT-DEBUG; LIB-TRY-LUA is re-running two candidate-only reds alone. Its last two steps are now arena-f5-retry and map-postable.\nStill queued behind it: cid-land4, wide-land, host-slice2-land, combat-land, offscreen-land, samples-sugar-land.\nNo new parks.")
inl note_of_tibia_park_18 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARK", 18u32, "2026-10-27T00:55Z", "tibia-lane", "00:55Z status 18: kit's pause at 20:3x for the rename finalize; tibia went clear. I stopped serial-gaps-lib4 while it sat in LIB-TRY-LUA's land reader-wait (no writes; base.spi verified untouched), plus 8 queued lands. The manifest is scratch clear-manifest-203134.json, and clear-requeue.ps1 -Go requeues with kit.exe after \"rename finalized\": gaps-lib5 (which now also carries par-rust-stack, text-order and try-parse-f64), then cid5, wide, host-slice2, combat, offscreen, samples-sugar.\nThe land reader guard (process-handle-kit land.ps1) no longer counts Cells runs whose notebook paths all lie in %TEMP% or spiral-bin\\runs, i.e. gates on lib copies. On 10-26 those starved LIB-TRY-LUA's land for over an hour. Unit-tested on four command-line shapes; a live Cells run or a path-unknown mix run still counts.")
inl note_of_tibia_park_19 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARK", 19u32, "2026-10-27T01:02Z", "tibia-lane", "01:02Z Lost-update audit of today's tibia lib lands (scratch land-audit.ps1: parses '/ land / edit' lines from the runner logs in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\jobs and compares each 'after' hash with the live file).\n- Unchanged since their land: sm'.spi (LIB-OBJ-TO-STRING-C), runtime.spi and process.spi (LIB-PROCESS-HEAL), file_system.spi (LIB-PATH-JOIN-NATIVE), am'.spi (LIB-ARRAY-BASE), resultm.spi (LIB-RESULT-DEBUG).\n- env.spi changed after LIB-EXIT-WITH landed (another lane's edit at 18:45 local), but exit_with is still present and intact, so the land was built on, not lost.\n- A first parser version flagged base.spi wrongly: its edit line came from LIB-TRY-LUA's gate applying to a copy, not from a land (that land was stopped at the rename pause before applying). The audit now reads land lines only.")
inl note_of_tibia_park_20 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARK", 20u32, "2026-10-27T10:55Z", "tibia-lane", "10:55Z status 20 (10-27 06:5x). Framing: per the user on 10-25, the game after tibia is WoW addons (WOW-LUA-SANDBOX, Spiral to Lua 5.1), not Dota 2. This item's title and its dota tag predate that. The park gate itself is unchanged.\nDeps: Done: TIBIA-NO-HAND-LUA, LIB-PROCESS-HANDLE, TIBIA-EDITION3. Open: TIBIA-BACKEND-MAP 95% (only the first live use of world_executor remains), TIBIA-GRANULAR-HEAL 92% (9 sites, all pure arity adapters; the client casts moved into Spiral tonight), TIBIA-LIB-MIGRATION 91%, TIBIA-CELLS-APPS 85% (predict test blocks in the tree, gated in e5), LUA-FUNCTION-LIMITS 85%, TIBIA-FIDELITY 75% Blocked, TIBIA-PARTY 70%.\nTree: tonight's WIP is in the tree unstaged (wide records with E5 join points, pack_sim order fix, terrain split and regenerated tables, network inputs_of, client casts, README Codespaces badge), with gates e5 (job-1793091712654) and after-e5 (job-1793095859847) deciding green. Postable census for tibia: 5 over now, 0 over once after-e5 writes the tables and the network split.")
inl note_of_tibia_park_21 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARK", 21u32, "2026-10-27T12:57Z", "tibia-lane", "12:57Z README part of the park gate, 10-27 08:5x (unstaged in the tree). README \"Status\" is now 2026-10-27: 26 src modules (standards checked by `kit standards`, the eoie name retired), the six apps with their roles (arena 24 files / 13 Lua programs, map generating terrain's tables, predict, host with world port and executor, offscreen, canary), plus two new lines. Postable: 65 files, 3,531 cells, 0 over one post, with the generated tables proven equal to the old ones. Lib: every app references lib/spiral (checked in all six package.spiproj files); casts and parsing go through typed Spiral (env, convert, csv). The Codespaces badge (main's CODESPACES-BUTTON-ALL-REPOS) is under the title. docs/BENCHMARK.md exists and is tracked; the README's PR-n citations resolve. BENCHMARK content is unchanged tonight (no live runs since its last entry), so it stays current. Still open for the park gate: the in-scope items (CELLS-APPS 95%, BACKEND-MAP 95%, GRANULAR-HEAL 92%, LIB-MIGRATION 91%, LUA-FUNCTION-LIMITS 85%, FIDELITY 75% Blocked, PARTY 70%) and a green scripts/build.ps1 on the final tree (E8's gpu_sim timing is in flight).")
inl note_of_tibia_park_22 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARK", 22u32, "2026-10-27T19:56Z", "tibia-lane", "19:56Z Status 21 (10-27 16:0x local). The last design-blocked tree item is resolved: hunting_pack's postable re-split (r9) is in the tree, unstaged, after a green node gate (pack_sim 39/39, hunting_pack, hunt_sim, gpu_sim C). Its GPU shader runs in 281 s against a 450 s limit, where E11a timed out past 900 s (POSTABLE-ALL-REPOS notes 101-110). tibia postable: 65 files, 3572 cells, 0 over. README updated.\nStill open, unchanged in kind:\n- follow-up node gates for predict (job-1793128890409) and terrain, network and creatures (job-1793131069660) on the r9 tree;\n- TIBIA-GRANULAR-HEAL's live login check, which needs a live block;\n- TIBIA-BACKEND-MAP's first live world_executor use, which needs a live block;\n- LUA-FUNCTION-LIMITS (85 %), which gates TIBIA-CELLS-APPS' close;\n- TIBIA-FIDELITY (Blocked) and TIBIA-PARTY (70 %) follow-ups.\nNo new parks.")
inl note_of_tibia_park_23 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARK", 23u32, "2026-10-27T23:16Z", "tibia-lane", "23:16Z 23:2xZ PARK status 11, by dependency (each from its own latest note; K1-K4 unchanged).\nDone: TIBIA-NO-HAND-LUA, LIB-PROCESS-HANDLE, TIBIA-EDITION3.\nTIBIA-PARTY: chain Y's last pre-registered experiment is closed. P12 ran tonight on the worker node: saturation stands (evolved rules 63 percent below the validated arm's held-out profit, kills -4, deaths +1), and the validated arm reproduced PR-28's 16.73 kills (notes 106-107; a BENCHMARK.md row under PR-28, unstaged). By P12 (5) the model work closes. Only the named ally potion-share gap (note 98) stays open, and under K2/K3 it can park with a resume condition.\nTIBIA-FIDELITY: blocked on PARTY and EVENT-TIME. With PARTY's model work closed, what's left is the 0.5 h close with pointers.\nTIBIA-BACKEND-MAP 95%: one step left, the first live use of world_executor in the next live-gui window (run alone).\nTIBIA-CELLS-APPS 95%: the scope is complete (10-27 07:3x). It waits only on its dep LUA-FUNCTION-LIMITS (85%, main's pack).\nTIBIA-GRANULAR-HEAL 92%: the 9 remaining sites are pure arity adapters, the accepted shape (note 16).\nTIBIA-LIB-MIGRATION 95%: LIB-LUA-NARROW-PARSE landed 10-27 09:0x.\nLib work tonight (GRANULAR-HEAL and POSTABLE-ALL-REPOS, not park gates): 12 gated-GREEN lib slices wait in land-after-train.ps1 for kit's TRAIN window.\nWhat gates park now: one live-gui window (BACKEND-MAP's executor run), main's pack with LUA-FUNCTION-LIMITS, the FIDELITY close, and K4 (build.ps1 green, README and BENCHMARK current, lab/ empty).")
inl note_of_tibia_park_24 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARK", 24u32, "2026-10-28T10:36Z", "tibia-lane", "10-28 07:0x PARK status 12. Deps now Done: NO-HAND-LUA, LIB-PROCESS-HANDLE, EDITION3, LIB-MIGRATION, CELLS-APPS, GRANULAR-HEAL, LUA-FUNCTION-LIMITS, FIDELITY. TIBIA-PARTY is Paused (model work closed by P12; the ally potion-share gap has a resume condition), as K1/K2 allow. Left: (1) TIBIA-BACKEND-MAP's first live world_executor block, 08:30-09:30 (P-EXEC1, pre-registered in BACKEND-MAP note 28); (2) K4: README is updated (the party paragraph now carries PR-28's confirmation and P12's rerun), BENCHMARK has the P12 row, lab/ is empty, and live/ is harness-only (new: run-hunt.ps1 and run-policy-scenario.ps1 -ExternalWorld for the executor); scripts/build.ps1 on the final tree runs in main's booked heavy slot 10:00-10:30. When both pass, TIBIA-PARK is Done and the TIBIA epic goes Paused with its resume condition.")
inl note_of_tibia_park_25 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARK", 25u32, "2026-10-28T12:57Z", "tibia-lane", "10-28 08:5x PARK status 13. TIBIA-BACKEND-MAP is Done: P-EXEC1 passed on attempt 2, A1 and A2 both hold, exact trace, counted x4 (BACKEND-MAP notes 29-30). Attempt 1 failed at the client step only. A PowerShell host started from an Erlang port without `hide` exits 0 and runs nothing. The fix is LIB-PORT-HIDE, which gates for the 14:00 window. Every dependency of PARK is now Done or Paused within the K1/K2 rules (TIBIA-PARTY Paused). Left: K4 only. That means scripts/build.ps1 green in the 10:00-10:30 heavy slot, with the tree at HEAD (the user's 07:07 commit) plus the README postable-line fix. Then PARK -> Done and the TIBIA epic -> Paused. TIBIA-EDITION3-ROUND (P0) follows PARK. It now accepts 0 overweight findings, with mention/hashtag findings left to the poster (POSTABLE-ALL-REPOS note 133).")
inl note_of_tibia_park_26 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARK", 26u32, "2026-10-30T04:22Z", "main", "10-30 00:22 main: tibia confirmed it is HOLDING under a direct user STOP in its own session, which relayed asks don't lift. That's correct, so main stops nudging it. Consequences listed for the user: tibia did NOT run the user's 21:54 heal+groom ask, and its 5 pre-retire node mirrors (tibia-envguard, tibia-envguard-neg, tibia-gaps, tibia-gates, tibia-luafix) stay in the pre-retire layout. That's harmless while nothing launches on them, but they need a resync or archive before reuse. Its resume packet is current: lib hashes after windows 4/5, listm' 220ACFE33776, file_system 81140E3E, sm' 2196F9C7, pack 7's Lua '\\0' -> real NUL.")
inl note_of_tibia_park_27 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARK", 27u32, "2026-10-30T11:24Z", "tibia-lane", "10-30 07:5x tibia RESUMED (user 06:5x: recover or rewrite 100% today). Resume packet: node and box compiler 9C899B30495F7DC5 (pack 7), lib file_system 81140E3E, listm' 220ACFE3, sm' 2196F9C7. K4's lost run (job-1793197502063) is redone as K4 = scripts/build.ps1 on HEAD 23d93fd plus the unstaged README, build.ps1 (apps/canary in the format check and test sources) and run-policy-scenario.ps1 (DELETE-ROOT-GUARD). It runs after healing's write all-clear, since builds write GBs to C:. The 5 pre-retire node mirrors are archived by move to C:\\home\\remote-archive\\20261030-tibia-pre-retire (junction targets verified, manifest.json). Next: K4, then PARK Done and TIBIA Paused.")
inl note_of_tibia_park_28 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARK", 28u32, "2026-10-30T17:50Z", "tibia-lane", "10-30 13:5x PARK status after the wipe redo. K1/K2 deps: all Done except TIBIA-PARTY (Paused with its resume condition, which the park rule allows). K4: lab/ removed (empty, untracked); docs/BENCHMARK.md is current (10-28 P12 sweep, no live runs since); README updated (status 2026-10-30, Postable 0 overweight, manifests line, live/setup.ps1 line); live/ is harness-only plus the new setup.ps1. Tree: ED3 + trim applied unstaged (TIBIA-EDITION3-ROUND note 15). Lib: 16 tibia slices landed and the window closed (document_test 22/22, type_probe 21/21). Running: post-land lib gate job-1793379899822 and the K4 build.ps1 on the post-land lib, job-1793379914468 (node mirror tibia-postland, digest BBB2B45D37BBC121 = box). When K4 is green: TIBIA -> Paused with its resume condition, and the user commits. The live world smoke (TIBIA-LOCAL-WORLD) waits for main's box-free signal.")
inl note_of_tibia_park_29 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARK", 29u32, "2026-10-30T22:42Z", "tibia-lane", "10-30 18:4x PARK DONE by the K1-K4 rule. Every in-scope dep is Done (TIBIA-PARTY is Paused with its resume condition); K4 passed (build.ps1 56/56 green on the post-land lib, TIBIA-EDITION3-ROUND note 17); README/BENCHMARK current; lab/ empty; live/ is harness-only plus setup.ps1; the world was rebuilt and its smoke passed (TIBIA-LOCAL-WORLD note 3). The tibia tree is unstaged for the user's review and commit. TIBIA goes Paused.")
inl note_of_gleam_compact_output_1 () = Note ("GLEAM-COMPACT-OUTPUT", 1u32, "2026-10-25T02:44Z", "x", "10-24 22:44 x: estimate from counting the two patterns in x-units/out-gleam probes (read-only; no post-processing kept): single-expression arms 64/168/335 and let-then-return 31/74/106 in g_split/g_rows/g_world. Byte-for-byte proof needed: matrix Gleam rows build and run, and x sim fixtures stay byte-identical. Do it in codegenGleam, never as a post-pass. x owns it (compiler work belongs to the lane that needs it); tell the lanes before packing or installing.")
inl note_of_gleam_compact_output_2 () = Note ("GLEAM-COMPACT-OUTPUT", 2u32, "2026-10-28T12:25Z", "x", "2026-10-28 08:25 x: CENSUS on today's real output (the 19 tracked Gleam modules that landed from verify25: apps/sim/frames 13 and apps/sim/split 6, 12,668 lines): 802 single-expression case arms (each 'P -> {', one line, '}' could be 'P -> expr', saving 2 lines) and 230 let-then-return endings ('let vN = e' then a bare 'vN' before the closing brace, saving 1), so 1,834 lines or 14.5%, confirming note 1's ~15% probe estimate. Pattern A alone is 1,604 lines (12.7%).\nDRAFT for pattern A (scratchpad gleam-compact\\compact.do, one kit do program on apps/compiler/spiral_compiler.fs, 5 replacements; applied cleanly to a copy of the installed core source, sha256 9ff1b708..., which is the 'installed core 9FF1B708' the compiler team named): a helper 'arm s head render' inside codegenGleam's op, next to 'complex', renders the arm body into a fresh StringBuilder copy of the env. If it is exactly one non-empty line and does not start with 'let ' (let is not an expression in Gleam), it emits 'head -> line'; otherwise it emits 'head -> {', appends the rendered text unchanged, then '}'. So every multi-line arm stays byte-identical to today's output. Call sites: TyIf (True, False including its Nil special case), TyIntSwitch (each arm and '_'), TyUnionUnbox (each case and the wildcard on_fail). TyWhile's True arm always has 2+ lines (body plus the loop call) and is left alone. Pattern B (let-then-return) is not in this draft.\nProof plan (heavy, the compiler pack's): build the single-flight core with the patch; Gleam matrix rows build and run; x's sim build (frames + split Gleam regenerated, gleam build, ExUnit 45/45) with every sim fixture byte-identical; then the census rerun on the regenerated modules, expected to drop by ~1,604 lines.")
inl note_of_gleam_compact_output_3 () = Note ("GLEAM-COMPACT-OUTPUT", 3u32, "2026-10-28T12:26Z", "x", "2026-10-28 08:26 x: taken by the compiler team (08:3x), queued behind its P3 lever and DELPHI-64BIT, folded into a compiler pack. x's remaining part: when the compiler team pings with a candidate DLL, run the Gleam rows plus x's sim build on the node with every sim fixture byte-identical, then rerun the census (expected about -1,604 lines over the 19 modules).")
inl note_of_gleam_compact_output_4 () = Note ("GLEAM-COMPACT-OUTPUT", 4u32, "2026-10-28T12:32Z", "compiler", "compiler 10-28 reviewed xs compact.do (build-free): SOUND, taken by compiler. The arm helper renders the body into a fresh StringBuilder, splits non-empty lines; EXACTLY 1 line and not let-starting -> \"head -> expr\" (compact), else \"head -> { <rendered> }\". BYTE-IDENTICAL for MULTI-LINE arms: arm emits \"head -> {\" at ss indent + the rendered body (binds at indent-of-indent = same as the current code) + \"}\" -- identical indentation and braces. Single-expr arms compact to \"head -> expr\" = valid + semantically identical Gleam (a 1-expr block == the expr). The let- exclusion guards the invalid { let x=.. } edge. binds side effects (globals) survive via the shared record refs ({s with text=fresh} copies the global-list ref, only text is fresh). 5 sites: TyIf True+False(incl False->Nil), TyIntSwitch cases+wildcard, TyUnionUnbox cases+wildcard; TyWhile untouched. BUILD-BOUND next: apply + single-flight build + Gleam matrix (expect only brace-removal residual diffs on single-expr arms, multi-line byte-identical) + xs sim byte-identical fixtures on the node. Queues behind P3 + DELPHI-64BIT.")
inl note_of_gleam_compact_output_5 () = Note ("GLEAM-COMPACT-OUTPUT", 5u32, "2026-10-29T14:37Z", "compiler", "10-29 10:37 compiler: compact.do REDONE after the wipe (x's draft, reviewed in n4) as apps/compiler/packs/apply-gleam-compact-arms.ps1, 5 anchors, dry-run clean on the live core, composes with the pack-7 set. An arm helper in codegenGleam's op (next to complex) renders the body into a fresh CodegenEnv at the body indent. If that is exactly one non-empty line that does not start with 'let ', it emits 'head -> expr'; otherwise 'head -> {', the rendered text unchanged, '}', so every multi-line arm stays byte-identical. Sites: TyIf True/False (False -> Nil compacts to 'False -> Nil'), TyIntSwitch cases + '_', TyUnionUnbox cases + on_fail wildcard. FOUND while reading: TyIntSwitch's Gleam emission never closes its 'case v{i} {' (no line s '}' after the wildcard arm, unlike TyUnionUnbox at :168698); kept byte-identical here, so a Gleam int switch either never reaches codegen or is a latent invalid-output bug (check in the pack review). Gate unchanged (n3/n4): Gleam matrix rows build and run, multi-line residuals byte-identical, x's sim fixtures byte-identical on the node, census about -1,604 lines.")
inl note_of_gleam_compact_output_6 () = Note ("GLEAM-COMPACT-OUTPUT", 6u32, "2026-10-29T15:03Z", "x", "2026-10-29 11:1x x: x's measurement half is ready as a tool. n2's one-off count (its method was only in a lost scratch script) is now x/scripts/gleam-compact-census.ps1 [-Path dirs] (default: apps/sim/frames/src + apps/sim/split/src). It REPRODUCES n2 exactly on today's tracked output: 19 modules, 12,668 lines, 802 single-expression arms (pattern A, 2 lines each), 230 let-then-return (pattern B, 1 line each), 1,834 compactable (14.5%). Positive control on a crafted sample: counts the 1-line arm and the let-return, skips the multi-line arm and the let-arm. After pack 7 (apply-gleam-compact-arms.ps1, n5) installs or a candidate DLL is pinned: sim build on the node, with every sim fixture byte-identical as the gate, then this census on the regenerated modules. Expected: pattern A goes to ~0, -1,604 lines, pattern B unchanged (230; n5 compacts arms only).")
inl note_of_gleam_compact_output_7 () = Note ("GLEAM-COMPACT-OUTPUT", 7u32, "2026-10-29T15:22Z", "compiler", "10-29 11:22 compiler: n5's TyIntSwitch question settled from the corpus: no committed samples/**/main.gleam contains a numeric case arm (ripgrep '^\\s+\\d+ -> \\{' = 0 files; positive control '^\\s+True -> \\{' = 2,341 arms in 363 files), so a Gleam TyIntSwitch never reaches codegen in today's matrix. The missing 'case' closing brace in codegenGleam's TyIntSwitch is a LATENT bug, not broken output. The compact applier keeps that branch byte-identical, so it neither fixes nor worsens it. A fix (add line s '}' after the wildcard arm) needs a sample that reaches it, so it is left out of this pack.")
inl note_of_gleam_compact_output_8 () = Note ("GLEAM-COMPACT-OUTPUT", 8u32, "2026-10-30T02:02Z", "compiler", "10-29 22:0x compiler (groom): progress 40 -> 85, deps - -> PACK-7. The compact-arms applier is in PACK-7 (its title lists 'Gleam compact arms'; candidate built and reviewed today, node rebuild hash-identical). Left: main's install, then the committed Gleam outputs show the compact arms. The latent TyIntSwitch closing-brace bug (n7) stays out until a sample reaches it.")
inl note_of_gleam_compact_output_9 () = Note ("GLEAM-COMPACT-OUTPUT", 9u32, "2026-10-30T03:18Z", "compiler", "10-29 23:3x compiler: CLOSED. Installed with pack 7. run single-flight-20261029-223356 (pack 7 -Accept, installed core 9C899B30495F7DC5) accepted exactly the 359 predicted Gleam rows (predicted-set.tsv, all residual-only, 0 compile-status changes, 0 Gleam verdict changes), so the committed main.gleam files now carry the compact single-expression arms. The latent TyIntSwitch closing-brace bug (n7) needs a sample that reaches it; not part of this item's done rule.")
inl note_of_x_edition3_respell_1 () = Note ("X-EDITION3-RESPELL", 1u32, "2026-10-25T03:03Z", "x", "10-24 23:03 x: from main's spread request (user 23:0x: 'if the lib experiment passed we gotta spread edition3 around everything'). Start after job-1792897109498-x-verify-landing8 ends, since it reads x's tree. Expected knock-ons: the sim fixtures embed prelude.spi's source text (re-accept and review the diff); x-compat weights change (rerun, expect fewer findings since symbols are shorter); the scratch apply scripts in %TEMP%\\x-units anchor on edition-2 text (they are history once landed, don't rerun). 'test' stays a word until Cells and tree-sitter read ':#' (main 5j).")
inl note_of_x_edition3_respell_2 () = Note ("X-EDITION3-RESPELL", 2u32, "2026-10-25T03:37Z", "x", "10-24 23:37 x: GREEN ON COPIES (job x-edition3-dry3, %TEMP%\\edition3-spread\\x\\{original,symbols,words,baseline-words}): 44 files respelled, 0 errors, 0 round-trip differences, 40 files changed by the installed formatter on top, x-compat 0 findings on the symbols copy, 0 files with fewer lines (no joined lines; 1 line over 120 left). Two false-RED cases were fixed in the shared tool (main told): 21 x files had no final newline and the respell adds one, which (a) tripped the line-count check and (b) the words round trip; both now accept only that difference (verified 21 differ only there, 0 real). Left: main's Cells round-trip scan on original vs symbols (identical failure sets; path asked of main), then -Apply after job-1792897109498-x-verify-landing8 ends, then re-accept the sim fixtures that embed prelude.spi and run a verify.")
inl note_of_x_edition3_respell_3 () = Note ("X-EDITION3-RESPELL", 3u32, "2026-10-25T03:40Z", "x", "10-24 23:40 x: CELLS ROUND-TRIP GATE PASSED. main's scan (lib-trip-all.exs, run from spiral/apps/cells with scoop erlang/elixir) gives 44 files, 43 failing on BOTH %TEMP%\\edition3-spread\\x\\original and \\symbols, with identical failure sets (0 only-original, 0 only-symbols). The failures are pre-existing and the same for every file: round trip changes the text at line 2, where the ///> rust backend line under the test header is dropped by spi -> livemd -> spi. That's a Cells gap, not the respell's (the backlog already mentions this scan 8 times). Left: -Apply once job-1792897109498-x-verify-landing8 ends (main's caution: the 21 files without a final newline gain one; intended), then re-accept the sim fixtures that embed prelude.spi and run a verify.")
inl note_of_x_edition3_respell_4 () = Note ("X-EDITION3-RESPELL", 4u32, "2026-10-25T03:53Z", "x", "10-24 23:53 x: LANDED (unstaged), spelling only. The first -Apply (with the installed formatter on top) made 28 cells overweight: x-compat 28, 28 spilled post-thread cells. The formatter lays records out one field per line (fields.spi 90 -> 118 lines), and the indentation adds weight. Restored from originals (hash-verified, 0 mismatches) and re-applied with a new -SkipFormat switch in the shared respell-repo.ps1: 44 files, 0 errors, 0 round-trip differences, x-compat 0, 0 spilled cells. Formatting x stays under X-FORMAT-CLIENT, which must re-split the cells the formatter makes heavier. Also fixed on the way: net/net.spi's main cell was 276 chars and spilled a post (it failed at HEAD too; earlier verifies never reached the postable step), so its two wire exports are now wire_exports (). Gate: job-1792900302663-x-verify-landing9.")
inl note_of_x_edition3_respell_5 () = Note ("X-EDITION3-RESPELL", 5u32, "2026-10-25T05:01Z", "x", "10-25 01:01 x: verify-landing9 (job-1792900302663) failed only at e2e: tutorial step 'xc post-thread --resume 9101 checks/checks.spi' exited 4. Cause: the e2e stub world's resume fixture (posts 9101-9103 = checks.spi's first 3 posts, 9201-9202 the tampered pair) carried the edition-2 text, the respell changed checks.spi, so resume correctly refused. Fix: replaced only those 5 text values in apps/client/e2e/world.json from xc post-thread --dry-run of the new checks.spi (5-line diff; the file's own formatting kept). Proven without a compile: the stub plus the release xc give 'resumed after post 3 of 9', posting 4..9. Also seen in verify9: e2e -Accept updated 5 of 36 tutorial outputs (dry-run texts of respelled files); review the README diff at the next verify. Next: verify-landing10 after main installs pack 5j.")
inl note_of_x_edition3_respell_6 () = Note ("X-EDITION3-RESPELL", 6u32, "2026-10-25T06:50Z", "x", "10-25 02:50 x: verify-landing10 (job-1792904826458, on installed 5j) is green through the first stage and the client build: gate 23 crates 0 over 1000, release build (no E0507), e2e 36 tutorial steps + 5 extras incl. resume, e2e -Accept, postable 1866 posts / 44 files / 0 cells over one post. Notebook tests: prelude 3/3, exsss 5/5, paging 5/5, glyphs 8/8, then protocol.spi 2/7, with all 5 failures on the zig target: 'main.zig:157:39: error: expected ';' after statement'. That's invalid generated zig, a codegen fault; the respell round-trips byte-identical, so the AST is unchanged. Reported to main for 5k. Notebooks after protocol are not yet run. Next verify after 5k installs.")
inl note_of_x_edition3_respell_7 () = Note ("X-EDITION3-RESPELL", 7u32, "2026-10-25T07:10Z", "x", "10-25 03:10 x: CORRECTION to n6. protocol.spi's 5 zig failures are a lib arm, not 5j codegen (main): the healed Zig arms of sm'.index_of/last_index_of end in optionm'.unwrap_or, which only has a Rust spelling. Exactly the 5 tests that reach index_of fail. My 'compile succeeds, so codegen' inference missed that a host-text arm can emit wrong-backend text the compiler never checks. Fix: main's job-1792912152676-main-serial-zig-index-of (Zig arms use optionm'.default_value', and the tests gain ///> zig). Rerun protocol.spi on zig once it lands.")
