inl note_of_x_edition3_respell_9 () = Note ("X-EDITION3-RESPELL", 9u32, "2026-10-28T11:10Z", "x", "2026-10-28 07:10 x: UNBLOCKED. The compiler team (07:0x) reports SPIRAL-PATH-SYNTAX, SPIRAL-ZWSP-TRANSPARENT and SPIRAL-MACRO-SIGIL-ESCAPES already in the installed core (composed into 5n), and closed all three Done. Installed DLL A4E480202BD4: x-compat 0 in 43 client + 24 sim files. Full functional proof: verify27 (job-1793185923019) pinned to that DLL (staged spiral-bin-p2).")
inl note_of_x_edition3_respell_10 () = Note ("X-EDITION3-RESPELL", 10u32, "2026-10-28T11:38Z", "x", "2026-10-28 07:38 x: 10-26 round APPLIED (tree, unstaged), the first run on the installed compiler after the compiler team confirmed the edition-3 features ship in it (DLL A4E480202BD4). i574n.github/scripts/respell-repo.ps1 -Name x -Root C:\\home\\git\\x -Compiler <installed DLL>: 67 files, 59 respelled, 337 test headers kept as written, 0 errors, words round trip byte-identical for every file, and the installed formatter normalizes 21 on top (net +50 lines: splits only, no joins; 0 lines over 120). Member and module access is now :: (sm'::replace, e::base; 62 files). Before applying, x-compat on the respelled COPY found 3 cells pushed over one post by the added ':' (wire post_json 283 > 271, sim memory_watch grown 276 > 273, scenario_checks frame_edit_shape 273 > 272). Fixed in the tree first with behaviour-neutral helpers (post_named, complete_after, framed_edit_count), then the respell re-run: x-compat 0 in 43 client + 24 sim files on the respelled copy, and on the tree after applying. checks.spi is not respelled, so the e2e resume fixture in world.json (hand-made from its text on 10-25) stays valid. Originals: %TEMP%\\x-respell-originals-1028 (67 files). Proof: verify28 (job-1793187520986, installed compiler, mirror xv28); its e2e and sim accepts regenerate the README thread/dry-run outputs and the sim fixtures that quote respelled sources. Left in this round's scope: the 51 raw !!!! exports to lib wrappers, then X-DEFUSE-LINKS-ONLY.")
inl note_of_x_edition3_respell_11 () = Note ("X-EDITION3-RESPELL", 11u32, "2026-10-28T11:38Z", "x", "2026-10-28 07:38 x: the round's '51 raw !!!! -> lib wrappers' step is already done: 0 raw !!!! in x/apps .spi (grep positive-controlled on kit's lint.spi, which still has one), and every export goes through lib's export wrapper (49 one-line call sites plus multi-line ones such as view.spi). The 9 lines over 120 and the 280-weight split are met too (0 lines over 120; x-compat 0 on the respelled tree). This item now closes on verify28 (job-1793187520986) green; X-DEFUSE-LINKS-ONLY closes on the same run.")
inl note_of_x_edition3_respell_12 () = Note ("X-EDITION3-RESPELL", 12u32, "2026-10-29T17:14Z", "x", "2026-10-29 13:1x x: CLOSED. Closes by its own n11 (closes on the respelled-tree verify going green) and X-WIP-VERIFY n15. verify29 (node job-1793273389666, compiler A4E480202BD4 pinned, mirror xv29 synced 10-29 07:27 with the respelled tree, the lint heals and the defuse links-only change) is GREEN on every X-WIP-VERIFY n6 clause: exit 0 after 20,493 s; sim accept 45/45; client gate 29 crates 0 over 1,000 and 149 files 0 over 1,000; x-compat 0 findings in 43 client + 29 sim files; all 42 client and all 23 sim notebooks passed; plain e2e 153 stub requests, 0 FAILED (the accept rewrote 1 of 37 answers, the respell inside the prelude-text fixture, reviewed: only . -> :: plus the splitter re-chunking it causes); sim build exit 0 with corpus commute=ok over 73 files; the tampered thread rejected (same_cells=false). Outputs landed three-way 10-29 13:1x: 20 files, 0 conflicts (node-proof -Land x-verify29 -Apply).")
inl note_of_x_edition3_respell_13 () = Note ("X-EDITION3-RESPELL", 13u32, "2026-10-29T19:17Z", "x", "2026-10-29 15:1x x: RE-PROOF PENDING (per main's sweep 5 and memory recompile-drafts-after-compiler-change). This item closed on verify29, which ran on the pre-6b compiler A4E480202BD4. Pack-6b (core 31CC96520D6B7269, DLL 9895730DAE80) is now installed on both boxes. The first 6b run, verify30, was RED for reasons outside this item (fields.spi's new test cell overweight; ExUnit 60 s load timeouts), both fixed. verify31 (node job-1793299160741, 6b) is this item's re-proof: if any of its clauses fails there, I reopen the item with the cause.")
