inl note_of_notebook_livemd_retire_1 () = Note ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", 1u32, "2026-10-26T06:36Z", "x", "2026-10-26 02:35 x: the three twins must flip before the respell runs, or the next export writes '.x' and word keywords back over the migrated .spi; alphabet mirrors dice, so dice_fsharp and hangul move together.")
inl note_of_notebook_livemd_retire_2 () = Note ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", 2u32, "2026-10-26T07:21Z", "main", "10-26 03:21 main: first twin drafted: spiral/apps/spiral/spiral.livemd. Both twins are already in symbols (0 word line-starts, 221 ':=' lines each), so the keyword class is safe; the flip protects the coming '::' and @@/## classes. The livemd-only lines are Livebook wrapping, and its smart-cell attrs hold a JSON copy of every cell's source, so respelling the livemd in place would need both copies changed: flip instead. %TEMP%\\livemd-flip-spiral\\apply.ps1 (dry run clean, 11 anchored edits, each once): apps/spiral/build.ps1 drops the --export-only pre-build and its $SkipPreBuild param; polyglot scripts/init.ps1 stops passing -SkipPreBuild 1 (the only caller); README.md links spiral.spi.html (the Tasks precedent, NOTEBOOKS-TO-SPI-SIBLINGS n3); lab/SPIRAL-CLI-GRANULAR/promote.ps1 routes by an anchored edit of spiral.spi in symbols (? / |? / |: () dispatch; every branch exits, so it equals the old run of ifs; its old words anchor no longer matched the respelled livemd, so promote was already broken); router_swap.py writes spiral.spi ('/// # spiral' + router.spi) instead of building a livemd, and its json import and builders go. Then spiral.livemd is deleted. Deletion rule, written first: only if exporting today's livemd reproduces the tracked spiral.spi byte-identically (LF-normalized), so nothing is lost. Proof job-1792999203047-main-livemd-flip-proof. Not proven here: the new dispatch compiles. SPIRAL-CLI-GRANULAR's promote build proves it at its next -Apply. Next twins: spiral_wasm.livemd, then polyglot Perf.livemd (F# cells, per-file reader check).")
inl note_of_notebook_livemd_retire_3 () = Note ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", 3u32, "2026-10-26T07:33Z", "main", "10-26 03:33 main: twins 1 and 2 flipped in the working tree (unstaged): spiral.livemd (proof GREEN, export == spiral.spi DA60B76F; it showed MD because the user had staged an earlier version, which the index keeps, while the working tree's later heal of the $'$\"...\"' literals survives in spiral.spi) and spiral_wasm.livemd (proof GREEN, F6CDF55D; apps/wasm/build.ps1 now runs spiral_wasm.spi as the notebook, --output-path spiral_wasm.spi.ipynb, and the fast path needs no export). Twin 3, polyglot Perf.livemd: the proof was RED by its rule, and correctly so. Code lines (158) and headings (14) are identical, but the livemd holds 70 more /// result-table rows than Perf.spi (livemd committed 10-25 14:35, the .spi 00:25). Rule tightened, not loosened: the flipped Perf.spi is the livemd's own export (table padding collapsed to single spaces, the compact form Perf.spi already uses; 2 table rows stay over 120 because markdown rows can't wrap), guarded by the livemd hash 5CBC199E. Then the four F#-only headings (TestCaseResult, run, runAll at the top and hasAnyPairCloseToEachotherTests at EOF) go with the 13 F# cells. No workflow or script runs apps/perf/build.ps1. Waiting on the by-stem reader check over all repos (scratchpad livemd-reader-check.ps1 -> %TEMP%\\livemd-readers.txt) before the apply. That same check decides the 13 F#-only files.")
inl note_of_notebook_livemd_retire_4 () = Note ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", 4u32, "2026-10-26T08:10Z", "main", "10-26 04:10 main: per-file decisions from the by-stem reader check (scratchpad livemd-reader-check.ps1, one pass over 18,950 tracked text files in 54 repos, %TEMP%\\livemd-readers.txt). Flipped (unstaged): spiral.livemd, spiral_wasm.livemd, polyglot Perf.livemd (its only readers, the README and its build.ps1, are retargeted; Perf.spi is now the livemd's own export, so the newer result tables are kept; 13 F# cells retire). Deleted: polyglot lib/fsharp/NotebooksHtml.livemd (a 7-line .NET Interactive formatter snippet, not in lib/fsharp/build.ps1's notebook list, 0 readers by stem or name). Kept by readers: dice_fsharp.livemd and hangul.livemd are the livemd round-trip corpus of spiral/apps/cells/test/spiral/document_test.exs (:213/:216/:348/:499); the polyglot F# cluster (Async, AsyncSeq, Common, CommonFSharp, FileSystem, Runtime, Notebooks, Testing, apps/parser JsonParser + Parser) is live in dice's build (dice/scripts/build.ps1 -> lib/fsharp/build.ps1; dice/scripts/init.ps1:28 runs polyglot/apps/parser/build.ps1), with Common.fs also read by mechahaze-album1 and FileSystem.fs by FsClr.fsproj. Retiring it means first porting dice's F# lib to Spiral, a separate item. No Spiral to convert, so they stay: spiral apps/cells/notebooks/spiral.livemd (the Cells README's sample), polyglot scripts build/init.livemd (pwsh notebooks their .ps1 runs), i574n.github scripts/workflow.livemd (read by workflow.ps1), polyglot examples/elixir/exercism.livemd. Still to decide: spiral apps/lisp/lisp.livemd (0 readers, 2 Spiral cells).")
inl note_of_notebook_livemd_retire_5 () = Note ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", 5u32, "2026-10-26T08:12Z", "main", "10-26 04:12 main: last open file decided: spiral apps/lisp/lisp.livemd stays. Its one cell equals apps/lisp/membership_short.spl minus that file's comment line, and apps/lisp/build.ps1 already builds and runs the .spl files. But its prose is the only description of the ///! lisp Cells feature, and the cell holds Lisp forms, not Spiral spelling, so the respell and '::' classes can't touch it. Nothing in the round needs it changed. All 21 files are decided: 3 twins flipped, 1 orphan deleted, the rest kept by readers or as non-Spiral notebooks (n4). Open follow-up outside this item: the polyglot/dice F# cluster can only retire after dice's F# lib is ported to Spiral.")
inl note_of_notebook_livemd_retire_6 () = Note ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", 6u32, "2026-10-26T18:38Z", "main", "10-26 14:38 main: 10-26 14:3x main: perf-flip-rerun-2 RED (job finished 1x:xx) read in full. The cause is not the flip's build retarget: the build stopped at the Cells parse gate, 'FatalError: The package of main has blocks that fail to tokenize or parse ... Perf.spi:393'. Line 393 is a bare '()' at column 0, the carried-over OUTPUT of the preceding 'rotate_strings_tests ()' code cell; that cell itself parses as an executable top-level cell, and only 393 is flagged. It is already in HEAD (lines 399/401), so the livemd era rendered it as a cell output, and the .spi notebook reads it as code. Fix: TEMP livemd-flip-builds/perf-output-cell.ps1 removes exactly that line (anchored, count 1, 0 bare unit lines left; dry run passes on the live file). The proof is the consumer build itself: perf-fix-run.ps1 backs up Perf.spi, applies the fix, and runs perf-only.ps1 (polyglot apps/perf/build.ps1 through Cells). Rule, written before the run: GREEN iff the build exits 0, the .spi stays byte-identical, and no livemd comes back; the fix is then kept unstaged. Otherwise Perf.spi is restored from the backup and verified by hash. Queued in the post-rename requeue (main-perf-output-cell-fix), since kit's pause would stop it now. Flip-tool follow-up: the livemd-to-.spi converter should carry a code cell's rendered output as a /// comment, never as code (the same shape can recur in other flipped notebooks; grep for '^\\(\\)$' lines in flipped .spi files).")
inl note_of_notebook_livemd_retire_7 () = Note ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", 7u32, "2026-10-29T08:05Z", "main", "10-29 04:0x main: n6's one-line fix is necessary but NOT sufficient (proved on the consumer path; Perf.spi restored by hash both times, polyglot clean). With line 393 ('()', the carried livemd output) removed, run_notebook.ps1 --path apps/perf/Perf.spi still fails at the parse gate, now on the line before it: 'FatalError: ... Perf.spi:391:1 (main.spi:71:1): Expected one of: inl, let, union, nominal, prototype, type, instance, and, open'. Line 391 is the bare top-level call 'rotate_strings_tests ()', the only non-definition at column 0 in the file (420 doc lines, 12 definitions). The 10-26 assumption that this cell parses as an executable top-level cell no longer holds for this compiler. The fix is to give that call a notebook home, a decision for this item: (a) 'test rotate_strings_runs =' with the call as its body (Cells runs test blocks, and the lib uses the same form), or (b) an 'inl main () =' entry, if CI should keep running the benchmark as a program. The body runs count = 2,000,000 unless is_fast (), so (a) needs is_fast or a smaller count under test. Line 393 goes in the same edit. The lost TEMP livemd-flip-builds/perf-output-cell.ps1 covered only line 393.")
inl note_of_notebook_livemd_retire_8 () = Note ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", 8u32, "2026-10-29T08:24Z", "main", "10-29 04:3x main: two reds in apps/cells document_test.exs on the committed tree (20/22 locally; neither touches tonight's edits). (1) 'the spiral library .spi files load as notebooks, one test cell per test block' fails on lib/spiral/dictm.spi at :512 (once == spi_text): the spi -> livemd -> spi round trip drops the blank line between a heading and the code after it (orig 5-7 '/// # dictm' / '' / ':< sm'_operators', round trip '/// # dictm' / ':< sm'_operators'; the same under '/// ## dict'; 179 lines become 176). The other lib files have no blank after a heading, so either dictm.spi gets the canonical layout (3 blank lines removed) or Document's round trip learns to keep that blank; that is the lib or Cells owner's call. The blanks predate 3f1b7588 (that commit only respelled list syntax). (2) 'a _real.spir interleaves with its .spi by heading and both round-trip through livemd' fails on lib/spiral/cli_args_real.spir (:453), not read deeper. Found while verifying CELLS-SECTION-TARGET-SPLIT.")
inl note_of_notebook_livemd_retire_9 () = Note ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", 9u32, "2026-10-29T10:44Z", "main", "10-29 06:4x main: red (2) diagnosed (mix run of the test's own round trip): cli_args.spi round-trips exactly (227 = 227 lines), but cli_args_real.spir does not (72 -> 98 lines). The .spir opens with '/// # cli_args_real' then '///- --real', while its .spi opens with '/// # cli_args'. Document interleaves a _real.spir with its .spi by heading, and the test's fixture (document_test.exs:433-434) gives both files the SAME top heading ('# demo'). With the names differing, the round trip writes the .spi's headings into the .spir. Fix, either: retitle the .spir's top heading to '/// # cli_args' (data, one line), or let Document treat '<name>_real' as the same heading as '<name>' (code). Owner's call, like red (1), dictm.spi's blank lines.")
inl note_of_notebook_livemd_retire_10 () = Note ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", 10u32, "2026-10-29T11:42Z", "main", "10-29 07:4x main: apps/cells document_test is GREEN (job-1793274082819-main-document-test-after-sm-spir, exit 0); it had been red since before the wipe. The cause was lib drift away from the canonical notebook spacing, so 13 lib files no longer survived the spi -> livemd -> spi round trip, and all 13 failed at HEAD too. Fixes, landed with the reader guard and hash-equal to the proven copies, with undo copies in the main scratchpad land-blank-undo:\n- Blank lines only, each a round-trip fixpoint with 0 non-blank changes: dictm, erlang_port, file_system, iggy, json_scan, listm', physics, runtime, schematron_run, util, xsd_regex.\n- cli_args_real.spir: its first line is now '/// # cli_args', and it gains 12 empty heading cells mirroring cli_args.spi, the same shape json_real.spir already has.\n- sm'_real.spir: 5 empty heading cells for headings recently added to sm'.spi (char_code, of_char, rust_char_offset, decimal_text, char_text).\nRule for authors: a new '/// ###' heading in X.spi needs the same empty heading cell at the matching place in X_real.spir, or the interleave test goes red. All 5 lanes cleared the land; it went in at 07:39, 6 minutes before the announced 07:45. kit said afterwards that nothing of its own was affected.")
inl note_of_notebook_livemd_retire_11 () = Note ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", 11u32, "2026-10-29T15:14Z", "main", "10-29 11:1x main: Perf GREEN (job-1793282982768-main-perf-output-cell-fix-5), the consumer build polyglot apps/perf/build.ps1 through Cells. Pre-registered rule met: build exit 0, Perf.spi unchanged by the build, no livemd back. Execution verified in the notebook output: '11:09:52 1v benchmark.run_all / { test_name = rotate_strings_tests; count = 2000000 }' with per-solution times, plus the binary_search run. Three fixes, all unstaged in Perf.spi: (1) the stray '()' cell output removed (n6's original finding); (2) the bare top-level call 'rotate_strings_tests ()' is not a valid notebook block (the parse gate failed at 391 after (1)), so main now runs both benchmarks: 'rotate_strings_tests () |> ignore' then 'binary_search_tests ()'; (3) the untargeted main defaulted to Cells' Zig target ('expected a record with the Zig field'), and the benchmark lib is F#-only (console_color and dollar-quote interpolation), so a header static prelude '///> fsharp' + 'test perf static =' restores the original backend. The build's two untracked renders (Perf.spi.html and .ipynb; CI deploys its own) are removed locally. New memory: notebook-main-default-zig.")
inl note_of_notebook_livemd_retire_12 () = Note ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", 12u32, "2026-10-29T16:01Z", "main", "10-29 12:0x main: document_test GREEN (job-1793289640498) over today's lib lands: main's env.spi plus fiscal's 8 (xsd, xsd_emit x4 stacked, xpath x2, xpath_eval x2, schematron). The first run (job-1793289568667) caught env.spi failing the round trip: ONE missing blank line between main's two inserted test blocks (an applier concatenation slip; 0 non-blank changes; the canonical form is a fixpoint). The canonical env.spi was landed with the reader guard, so its live hash is now FE223D11E435 (was BB39D5562692; blank line only). Lesson for anyone landing new lib cells: run the round trip (main scratchpad roundtrip-one.exs, RTNAME=<file>) on the drafted text BEFORE landing, not after.")
inl note_of_notebook_livemd_retire_13 () = Note ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", 13u32, "2026-10-31T13:39Z", "main", "10-31 09:39 main census (git ls-files '*.livemd', all repos). IN SCOPE, still tracked: spiral apps/cells/notebooks/spiral.livemd and apps/lisp/lisp.livemd; dice lib/fsharp/dice_fsharp.livemd (a live document_test fixture, so it stays until that test moves); alphabet apps/hangul/hangul.livemd (with HANGULIZE-IN-SPIRAL); i574n.github scripts/workflow.livemd; polyglot 13 (apps/parser x2, examples/elixir/exercism, lib/fsharp x8, scripts/build + init: they go with POLYGLOT-RETIRE). OUT OF SCOPE: futuresales 23 (its own Livebook notebooks), livebook 12 (the upstream Livebook repo's learn/test notebooks). Next decision per file: spiral's two and i574n.github's workflow.livemd (check with a dangling-check-by-stem whether anything still builds or reads them).")
inl note_of_notebook_livemd_retire_14 () = Note ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", 14u32, "2026-10-31T13:47Z", "main", "10-31 09:47 main: decisions by the item's rule (port or delete by whether anything still builds or reads the file; dangling check by stem). KEEP: i574n.github scripts/workflow.livemd (workflow.ps1:15 runs it through Invoke-PwshNotebook, README.md:52 links its render; a PowerShell notebook, not a Spiral export), spiral apps/cells/notebooks/spiral.livemd (the Cells README's sample notebook for the Livebook integration). REMOVED: spiral apps/lisp/lisp.livemd (no reference anywhere; apps/lisp/build.ps1 tests the three .spl samples, not the notebook), archived first as %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\20261031-094618, now an unstaged deletion. Noted, not fixed: apps/lisp/spl2spi.py is a .py helper in a repo (to port to PowerShell under the no-.py rule).")
inl note_of_notebook_livemd_retire_15 () = Note ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", 15u32, "2026-10-31T14:09Z", "main", "10-31 10:08 main: apps/lisp also lost its Python helper (the no-.py rule): spl2spi.py ported to spl2spi.ps1; A/B over the 3 real samples (membership, membership_short, membership_wrong) is BYTE-IDENTICAL; build.ps1 now calls the .ps1; spl2spi.py archived as %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\20261031-100356 and removed (unstaged). apps/lisp status: M build.ps1, D lisp.livemd, D spl2spi.py, ?? spl2spi.ps1.")
inl note_of_notebook_livemd_retire_16 () = Note ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", 16u32, "2026-11-01T21:37Z", "main", "main 17:3x CENSUS (git ls-files '*.livemd' over every C:\\home\\git repo): own repos hold 3. (1) i574n.github/scripts/workflow.livemd RETIRED (unstaged): a 4-cell pwsh notebook (pins, build, outdated, publish via Invoke-Block) that workflow.ps1 ran with Invoke-PwshNotebook. The four calls are now inline in workflow.ps1 after core.ps1, with nbs_header's ProgressPreference kept; the cells' working dir was already scripts/ (workflow.ps1 Set-Location). Proven by parse plus a line-for-line read; the end-to-end proof is i574n/.github's next gh-pages run. (2) alphabet/apps/hangul/hangul.livemd and (3) dice/lib/fsharp/dice_fsharp.livemd are F#-only notebooks still built by their build.ps1 (hangul: build.ps1:15 runs the notebook to produce hangul.fs). They need a Spiral port: mirrored pair, alphabet-mirrors-dice. Not ours, left alone: futuresales/ (24, the user's old Elixir project) and livebook/ (upstream learn notebooks). Next: port hangul.fs's transliteration into hangul.spi with test blocks (typed jamo/syllable unions), then mirror it in dice.")
inl note_of_notebook_livemd_retire_17 () = Note ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", 17u32, "2026-11-03T22:04Z", "main", "main 11-03 18:1x STATE (silent > 48 h, orphan sweep r8): tracked .livemd left in own repos = 3: alphabet apps/hangul/hangul.livemd, dice lib/fsharp/dice_fsharp.livemd, spiral apps/cells/notebooks/spiral.livemd. Both F# ones now BUILD GREEN on a non-UTF-8 node (CELLS-FSI-STDIN-UTF8 Done today: hangul 2/2, dice FSHARP-OK), so retiring them is a port, not a repair. NEXT STEP (owner main): port hangul.fs's transliteration (16 KB F#: jamo/syllable composition + romanization; cp949/hanja tables stay as data) into a Spiral hangul.spi with typed jamo/syllable unions and test blocks, keeping hangul.livemd's 2 tests as the oracle. CAUTION: spiral's document_test round-trips 'alphabet: ... hangul an F# notebook that round-trips through livemd', so that test case must move to the .spi in the same change. Then mirror it in dice (alphabet-mirrors-dice). spiral.livemd: check whether Cells' Livebook entry still needs it before deciding.")
inl note_of_notebook_livemd_retire_18 () = Note ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", 18u32, "2026-11-04T01:34Z", "main", "21:3x main (gate-claimed): HANGUL PORT SLICE 1 in alphabet/apps/hangul/syllables.spi (registered in its package.spiproj after hanja): syllable/lead/vowel/tail nominals, as_syllable (U+AC00..U+D7A3 only), decompose (s / 588, (s mod 588) / 28, s mod 28) and compose (0xAC00 + (l*21 + v)*28 + t). Oracles: 가 = (0,0,0), 국 = (0,13,1), 어 = (11,4,0) (the livemd's 국어 test word), round trip over all 11,172 syllables, U+ABFF/U+D7A4 refused. Europa Cells 2/2 (europa alphabet needed deps/spiral -> /home/remote/git/spiral, now linked). NEXT: hanja_convert over hanja.spi's table (the livemd's 國語 -> 국어 oracle), then the romanization from hangul.fs; then build.ps1 drops the --export-only notebook step and spiral's document_test hangul case moves to the .spi (n: CAUTION).")
inl note_of_notebook_livemd_retire_19 () = Note ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", 19u32, "2026-11-04T01:43Z", "main", "21:4x main: HANGUL SLICE 2, alphabet/apps/hangul/convert.spi (registered after syllables): hanja_reading scans hanja.spi's hanja_to_hangul_table and returns a typed syllable (as_syllable refuses any table value outside U+AC00..U+D7A3); readings maps a code list. Oracle = the livemd's own: 國語 (U+570B U+8A9E) -> 국어 (U+AD6D U+C5B4); 가 (not hanja) -> None. Europa Cells syllables + convert 3/3. NEXT: UTF-8 string <-> code list at the edges (hanja_convert : string -> string), then the romanization tables from hangul.fs, then drop build.ps1's --export-only step and move spiral document_test's hangul case to the .spi.")
inl note_of_notebook_livemd_retire_20 () = Note ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", 20u32, "2026-11-04T01:48Z", "main", "21:5x main: HANGUL SLICE 3: hangul.fs has no romanization (corrects n19's NEXT); its core is split/join between syllables and conjoining jamo. Ported into syllables.spi: split_jamo (lead U+1100+l, medial U+1161+v, tail None or U+11A7+t) and join_jamo, which returns option syllable where the F# returns char 0 / U+FFFD sentinels. Oracles from the F# arithmetic: 국 -> (U+1100, U+116E, Some U+11A8); 어 -> (U+110B, U+1165, None); join_jamo back to 국; out-of-range lead and the non-tail U+11A7 refused. Europa Cells 4/4 (syllables 3, convert 1). LEFT from hangul.fs: compatJamo/toCompatJamoMap, isHangul/isJaeum/isMoeum classifiers, splitCompat, strokeMap; then UTF-8 string edges, build.ps1 without --export-only, document_test's hangul case.")
inl note_of_notebook_livemd_retire_21 () = Note ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", 21u32, "2026-11-04T01:52Z", "main", "21:5x main: HANGUL SLICE 4: hangul.fs's three overlapping boolean probes (isHangul, isJaeum, isMoeum) become one closed union, letter = HangulSyllable syllable | JamoConsonant | JamoVowel | NotHangul, produced once by classify (compat jamo U+3131..U+314E / U+314F..U+3163, lead U+1100..U+1112, medial U+1161..U+1175, tail U+11A8..U+11C2, ranges copied from the F# literals). Europa Cells 5/5 (syllables 4, convert 1). LEFT: compatJamo map, splitCompat, strokeMap, UTF-8 string edges, then build.ps1 and document_test.")
inl note_of_notebook_livemd_retire_22 () = Note ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", 22u32, "2026-11-04T01:56Z", "main", "21:5x main: HANGUL SLICE 5: compat_vowel = the vowel half of hangul.fs compatJamo (medial U+1161..U+1175 -> compat U+314F..U+3163, compat vowels unchanged, else None). Europa Cells 6/6. NEXT (tomorrow): the consonant half is toCompatJamoMap's 46 lead/tail pairs; transcribe them as a typed table checked against hangul.fs's literals; then splitCompat, strokeMap, UTF-8 string edges, build.ps1 without --export-only, document_test's hangul case.")
inl note_of_notebook_livemd_retire_23 () = Note ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", 23u32, "2026-11-04T05:05Z", "main", "11-04 01:0x main INVENTORY, by git ls-files over 11 repos: 16 tracked .livemd remain, down from 21. Gone since the round started: spiral/apps/spiral/spiral.livemd (build.ps1 now compiles spiral.spi directly), spiral_wasm, Perf and apps/lisp. Per file, by reader check:\n(a) KEEP (live readers): dice/lib/fsharp/dice_fsharp.livemd is dice's 'F# rendition' (scripts/build.ps1 builds it to FSHARP-OK; document_test 213/525 uses it as the F# round-trip fixture). spiral/apps/cells/notebooks/spiral.livemd is the Cells app's own sample notebook (README 48).\n(b) PORTING NOW: alphabet hangul.livemd. Spiral modules so far: syllables (compose/decompose, jamo split/join, classify, compat vowel and consonant tables, join_letters, split_compat), convert (hanja readings), particles (typed particle union; replaces appendPostposition's string pairs), strokes (recursive compound decomposition; F#'s stroke threw KeyNotFound on the compound vowel WE because E is itself a compound), cp949_codes plus cp949. The two 733 KB F# tables hold the same 17048 pairs, so one table remains, 296 KB, sorted by cp949 and 1:1. cp949 has typed Decoded|Unmapped|Truncated and Encoded|Unencodable in place of U+FFFD/'?'. Retire step after the europa gate: delete hangul.livemd, hangul.fs, cp949*.fs, hanja.fs; build.ps1 runs the .spi notebooks (HANGUL-OK); document_test 216/348 drop the hangul fixture (dice_fsharp still covers the F# round trip); README row.\n(c) polyglot's 12 (parser x2, exercism, lib/fsharp x8, scripts build/init) go with POLYGLOT-RETIRE: decide at that repo's retirement.")
inl note_of_notebook_livemd_retire_24 () = Note ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", 24u32, "2026-11-04T05:29Z", "main", "11-04 01:3x main HANGUL RETIRED (unstaged in alphabet + spiral). Deleted: hangul.livemd, hangul.fs, hanja.fs, cp949.fs, cp949_from.fs, cp949_to.fs. apps/hangul/build.ps1 now gates the .spi notebooks (any .spi with a ///> block) via run_notebook --gate and prints HANGUL-OK. europa: 15/15 across 5 notebooks (syllables 7, convert 1, particles 2, strokes 2, cp949 3). README row rewritten. spiral/apps/cells/test/spiral/document_test.exs: the export-equality test and the alphabet test drop the hangul fixture (dice_fsharp still covers the F# round trip). The alphabet CI workflow never named hangul files; scripts/build.ps1 calls apps/hangul/build.ps1 unchanged. Tracked .livemd: 15 left = 2 KEEP (dice_fsharp, cells sample) + 12 polyglot + 1 polyglot scripts/init, all under POLYGLOT-RETIRE. This item's own remainder is that polyglot decision.")
inl note_of_notebook_livemd_retire_25 () = Note ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", 25u32, "2026-11-04T06:01Z", "main", "11-04 02:0x main: BLOCKED on POLYGLOT-RETIRE. Everything outside polyglot is decided (hangul ported and retired; dice_fsharp and the cells sample kept for their readers). The 13 polyglot notebooks go with polyglot, whose deletion other owners gate (POLYGLOT-RETIRE n22/n28). Blocked rather than Active, so the stop gate stops re-claiming it (x star-exchange #10).")
inl note_of_notebook_livemd_retire_26 () = Note ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", 26u32, "2026-11-04T06:07Z", "main", "11-04 02:0x main DICE F# RENDITION RETIRED, mirroring hangul (alphabet-mirrors-dice; this item's 11-01 note had paired them: 'they need a Spiral port: mirrored pair'). dice's port already exists, since lib/dice.spi IS the dice library and lib/fsharp was a hand-written F# rendition beside it, so retiring means removal. Unstaged in dice: lib/fsharp deleted (build.ps1, dice_fsharp.fs, dice_fsharp.livemd; plus 220 MB of untracked self-contained publish output in its dist), scripts/build.ps1 drops the lib/fsharp step, README row. setup-dotnet stays in dice CI (the Spiral compiler needs .NET). Unstaged in spiral apps/cells: document_test's CLI-export comparison builds its own small mixed F#+Spiral notebook inline instead of reading another repo's file; the dice test drops the F# round trip; the real-notebook livemd round trip now runs on the Cells sample notebook (apps/cells/notebooks/spiral.livemd, the kept one); README's CI paragraph names the .spi route. NOT YET RUN: document_test (next, on a remote with dice/alphabet synced). Tracked .livemd outside polyglot: 1 (the Cells sample, kept by design).")
inl note_of_notebook_livemd_retire_27 () = Note ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", 27u32, "2026-11-04T08:17Z", "main", "11-04 04:2x main: spiral apps/cells document_test GREEN 22/22 (box, private MIX_BUILD_PATH, with the spiral CLI present, so the CLI-export comparison really ran) after the hangul and dice fixture removals. The CLI-export test now builds an inline mixed F#+Spiral notebook; the dice test drops the F# round trip; the unused assert_livemd_round_trip/cells/fsharp_sources helpers are removed. The Cells sample notebook was tried as a round-trip fixture and dropped: it is a hand-made demo that does not round-trip byte for byte (europa run 02:3x, 21/23). The inline livemd round-trip tests still cover the code path.")
inl note_of_notebook_livemd_retire_28 () = Note ("NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE", 28u32, "2026-11-06T14:51Z", "main", "main 11-06 14:5x DONE, proof: git ls-files '*.livemd' across the 11 own repos returns 1 file, spiral/apps/cells/notebooks/spiral.livemd (last touched 10-17, linked from apps/cells/README.md); the 21 of the 10-26 round are otherwise gone, polyglot's 9 having left with polyglot (POLYGLOT-RETIRE Done). The one left is kept by rule: it is the Cells Livebook integration demo, and .livemd is Livebook's own file format, so the format is the point of that file (not a Spiral notebook in the wrong format). Cells' document_test is green 22/22 with the inline round-trip tests covering the livemd path (11-04).")
inl note_of_tibia_edition3_round_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-EDITION3-ROUND", 1u32, "2026-10-26T06:36Z", "x", "2026-10-26 02:35 x: round scope EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION note 32; X-compliance layers SPIRAL-PATH-SYNTAX notes 10-11. Classes in order: manifests (EDITION3-SPIRAL-TOML converter), lexer respells (keywords, ::, Cons sugar, macro sigils), macro wrappers (BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP lib helpers), formatter, 280 split (EDITION3-280-SPLIT); one identical-output gate per class.")
inl note_of_tibia_edition3_round_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-EDITION3-ROUND", 2u32, "2026-10-26T06:51Z", "tibia-lane", "06:51Z Tibia part started, rule written before any tree edit. About 15 queued tibia slices (slices-b and slices-c, the cells-apps snapshot, the client heal) are guarded by exact file hashes, so edition-3 tree edits land after that queue and are drafted against the post-queue state, never under it. Live inventory (src and apps, target/deps excluded): (1) Cons ( : 10 rows in the tree, not 17 (recent lands removed the rest); the queued canary slices already convert 8 (ground_trace 6, lead_trace 2) to list sugar, and offscreen's 2 go with its slice (POSTABLE note 43). (2) Line-start word keywords: 4; client.spi:58 (inl code = ...) vanishes with the queued client heal, and lua.spi:21/24/35 sit in the file the queued random lands touch, so they convert right after those land. (3) if/then/else/match/with/fun outside strings and host macros: 0 in tibia code; the 46 must count words inside host macros (Lua 'if ... then' text), which are host text, not Spiral keywords. (4) Manifests: 7 package.spiproj (apps arena, canary, host, map, offscreen, predict; src). The converter is not in the installed compiler: 'format --manifest toml' on a scratch copy exits 0 and writes nothing. This class waits for EDITION3-SPIRAL-TOML's install, then runs over the 7 with read-back. (5) '::' and '@@/##' wait for the compiler's respell pairs, as planned. (6) Formatter and 280-split: the postable slices queued in slices-c cover most of tibia's split (POSTABLE notes 33-46). Gate per class as the item says: compiled Lua/C/WGSL identical, tibia tests, x-compat 0.")
inl note_of_tibia_edition3_round_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-EDITION3-ROUND", 3u32, "2026-10-26T07:01Z", "tibia-lane", "07:01Z Raw !!!! class (BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP's tibia share): all 23 sit in src/terrain.spi (ArrayCreate 6, ArrayIndex 7, ArrayIndexSet 10). lib had index_base but no create or set wrapper for array_base (am'.init fills element i with i, so it isn't a drop-in for an unfilled array; array_dim.set needs dim-typed arrays). New lib slice, scratch lib-array-base/lib-array-base.ps1: am'.create_base n = !!!!ArrayCreate(`el, n) and am'.set_base ar i v = !!!!ArrayIndexSet(ar, i, v), beside index_base. The raw op lives only inside lib, as in array_dim.set. Consumer-path proof against the patched lib copy: a probe creates a u32 array of 4, sets it to 7/11/13/17 and sums it through index_base; it prints 'total 48' on Rust (rustc) and on C (gcc). Queued: gate-then-land LIB-ARRAY-BASE (-Files am') in tibia-serial-heals. Terrain conversion is ready: scratch lib-array-base/terrain-array-wrappers.ps1, a paren-aware converter (balanced arguments, index argument order swapped, a read in argument position wrapped in parentheses) turns all 23 into wrapper calls with 0 raw ops left and 0 lines over 120. It applies on top of the terrain slice, which is held for the geometry fix, after LIB-ARRAY-BASE lands, gated by the round's rule: terrain's compiled C/WGSL identical before and after, plus terrain tests.")
inl note_of_tibia_edition3_round_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-EDITION3-ROUND", 4u32, "2026-10-28T10:32Z", "tibia-lane", "GROOM 10-28 06:4x: Planned -> Blocked. All three deps are unfinished compiler features: SPIRAL-PATH-SYNTAX (Active 15%), SPIRAL-MACRO-SIGIL-ESCAPES (Planned 0%), SPIRAL-ZWSP-TRANSPARENT (Planned 0%), all owned by the compiler side. Resume when they land: the inventory (notes 1-2) and the terrain !!!! conversion through am'.create_base/set_base are drafted.")
inl note_of_tibia_edition3_round_5 () = Note ("TIBIA-EDITION3-ROUND", 5u32, "2026-10-28T11:02Z", "tibia-lane", "10-28 07:1x Blocked -> Planned. Compiler confirmed in source (relayed by main at 07:0x) that all three blockers were already in the installed compiler (core 9FF1B708, via the 5n composite) and closed them Done: SPIRAL-PATH-SYNTAX, SPIRAL-ZWSP-TRANSPARENT, SPIRAL-MACRO-SIGIL-ESCAPES. Next: validate against the installed compiler on tibia (box or node, outside 08:30-09:30), starting from the drafted inventory (notes 1-2: the remaining Cons sugar, line-start keywords, terrain's 23 raw !!!! via am'.create_base/set_base). Lib writes go in today's land windows (14:00-16:00, 20:00-21:00). Any red row goes back to compiler.")
inl note_of_tibia_edition3_round_6 () = Note ("TIBIA-EDITION3-ROUND", 6u32, "2026-10-28T11:04Z", "tibia-lane", "11:04Z INVENTORY refreshed 10-28 07:1x on the live tibia tree (src + apps, target/deps excluded; case-sensitive):\n(1) Nil -> [] list sugar: 14 rows. ground_trace 4, lead_trace 2, arena_host 5, character 1, scenario 2. 'Cons (' is already 0.\n(2) Raw !!!!: 4 rows. terrain.spi:1401-1405 holds the three wrappers base_create/base_read/base_write (ArrayCreate/ArrayIndex/ArrayIndexSet, 23 call sites). They become am'.create_base/index_base/set_base, which LIB-ARRAY-BASE landed in lib (am'.spi:29-36). hunting_pack.spi:1771 !!!!BackendSwitch is kept on purpose: the r9 knight_turn split needs its own Wgsl key (gpu-code-split rule), which lib's backend_switch doesn't expose.\n(3) Line-start word keywords: 0. if/match/fun outside host text: 0 (note 1).\n(4) spiral.toml: 0 of 7 package.spiproj converted. That's the main edit and needs the installed compiler's spiral.toml reader.\n(5) Then the formatter, the 280-weight check (tibia is already 0 over) and the gates: compiled Lua/C/WGSL identical per class, tibia tests, x-compat 0 findings.\nOrder: after TIBIA-PARK (the 08:30 executor block, then K4 at 10:00 on the current tree). apps/host files (arena_host, character, scenario) feed the 08:30 block and aren't touched before it. Proof: a node src gate plus Lua/C/WGSL output identity per module against pre-edit builds; any red row goes to compiler.")
inl note_of_tibia_edition3_round_7 () = Note ("TIBIA-EDITION3-ROUND", 7u32, "2026-10-28T11:07Z", "tibia-lane", "11:07Z spiral.toml step, trialled 10-28 07:2x on a scratch copy of tibia's 7 manifests: 'SpiralCompiler format --manifest toml <dir>' wrote all 7 (apps/arena, canary, host, map, offscreen, predict and src), each passing the converter's read-back check. Example: apps/canary -> edition = 3 / packageDir = '../../deps/spiral/lib' / packages = ['|core-', 'spiral-'] / modules = '''canary ground_trace lead_trace'''.\nPrecedence trap found before the tree edit. The compiler resolves spiral.toml FIRST when both files exist (spiproj_suffix, spiral_compiler.fs:184542). EDITION3-SPIRAL-TOML keeps the spiproj beside it on purpose, and Cells still reads package.spiproj directly (memo.ex 290/348/582, mounts.ex 62/163). So both files must stay in sync, and every script that rewrites package.spiproj text must rewrite spiral.toml too, or the compiler silently ignores its edit. In tibia that's scripts/predict.ps1:21-22 (packageDir -> absolute lib path; the module list gains a second entry for -Module sweep), plus my scratch runners (node-kit/predict-node.ps1, live-exec/stage.ps1) and the old push-src copy. Plan: the converter writes the 7 files; predict.ps1 patches both manifests (in spiral.toml, packageDir = '...' and a line added inside the modules ''' block); the proof includes a predict run whose module list and packageDir both take effect (sweep compiles via -Module sweep).")
inl note_of_tibia_edition3_round_8 () = Note ("TIBIA-EDITION3-ROUND", 8u32, "2026-10-28T11:09Z", "tibia-lane", "07:1x APPLY SCRIPT READY (scratch ed3-toml/ed3-apply.ps1), guarded by 7 recorded file hashes (bases taken at 07:1x). It refuses any typed 'Nil with a backtick' (no sugar form, per main's nil batch 3) and a changed Nil count: 15 tokens on 14 rows, since arena_host:143 holds two. Steps: Nil -> [] in ground_trace, lead_trace, arena_host, character and scenario; terrain's base_create/read/write delegate to am'.create_base/index_base/set_base (the 23 call sites are unchanged); predict.ps1 also patches apps/predict/spiral.toml; then format --manifest toml over src and apps. Trial on a full tree copy: 0 Nil left, 1 !!!! left (the intentional r9 BackendSwitch), 7 spiral.toml written. Runs after TIBIA-PARK. The typed proof is on the real tree (node src gate plus Lua/C/WGSL identity), because the copy has no deps link.")
inl note_of_tibia_edition3_round_9 () = Note ("TIBIA-EDITION3-ROUND", 9u32, "2026-10-28T11:54Z", "tibia-lane", "07:5x x-compat TRIM PASS drafted for src (scratch ed3-trim/trim.ps1, applied to a fresh copy): 21 findings -> 0 under --x-compat with the x profile. Mostly renames inside the one cell (repeated params/locals such as moved->q, entered_first/second->first/second, timed->q, camp->c, away->to, route->r, plan->p, elapsed->dt, ground->at, low/high->lo/hi), with guards so .field accesses are never renamed. Plus: a local alias at = geometry.position in spawns_of; the readiness type alias ready_ms = quantity.amount quantity.milliseconds; cave_rat_stats -> rat_stats (2 uses, creatures only); melee_every -> melee_each (2 uses); foe_melee returns pack -> pack, so its 4 arms drop the trailing p; and a cost_as_profit helper for clear_profit, which keeps 'clear_ms <= limit * count' as written. Proof on the real tree after PARK: compiled Lua/C/WGSL identity (identity-after.ps1) plus a node src gate. foe_melee's partial application is the one change that could move WGSL, and the identity check decides it. apps (18 overweight, 17 @-mentions) is next.")
inl note_of_tibia_edition3_round_10 () = Note ("TIBIA-EDITION3-ROUND", 10u32, "2026-10-28T11:56Z", "tibia-lane", "07:5x x-compat TRIM PASS COMPLETE on a fresh copy: tibia src 0/27 files and apps 0/38 under --x-compat with the x profile (was 56: 39 overweight, 17 mentions). Mentions: the 17 '@word' log stamps and the @god account literal are split right after the @ (' @t+' -> ' @' ++# 't+'), so the printed text is byte-identical and X sees no name. Overweights are fixed with in-cell renames (a guard keeps .field accesses untouched) plus the src structural five from note 9. Apply order on the real tree after TIBIA-PARK: ed3-apply.ps1 (Nil, terrain wrappers, toml), then ed3-trim/trim.ps1 -Tree C:\\home\\git\\tibia (without -Fresh), then identity-after.ps1 (arena Lua and predict C identical; the mention splits may fold to the same Lua if the compiler joins static strings, or differ in bytes with the same text, and the identity diff will show which), then a node src gate, then --x-compat 0 on src and apps. apps/host/world_executor.spi:109 (produced -> out) is touched only after the 08:30 block.")
inl note_of_tibia_edition3_round_11 () = Note ("TIBIA-EDITION3-ROUND", 11u32, "2026-10-28T14:47Z", "tibia-lane", "10-28 10:4x READY, waiting only for TIBIA-PARK -> Done (K4 build in progress, job-1793197502063, ETA about 12:35). Rechecked today on the tree after the user's 07:07 commit: ed3-apply's 7 bases (canary ground_trace/lead_trace, host arena_host/character/scenario, src terrain, scripts/predict.ps1) all match, and its dry run is clean (15 Nil -> [] tokens on 14 rows, 3 terrain wrappers, the predict.ps1 spiral.toml patch). The trim pass on a fresh copy gives x-compat src 0 findings and apps 0 overweight; apps' 17 remaining findings are @ mentions inside strings, which the poster defuses (POSTABLE-ALL-REPOS note 133, from X-DEFUSE-LINKS-ONLY). So the acceptance gate reads: overweight 0 under the x profile, mention/hashtag left to the poster, and trim.ps1's unmention edits are opt-in (-Unmention) and off. Order once PARK is Done: ed3-apply -Apply, trim -Tree C:\\home\\git\\tibia, identity-after (arena Lua 13 files, predict.c, compiler core), node src gate, x-compat recheck. All unstaged.")
inl note_of_tibia_edition3_round_12 () = Note ("TIBIA-EDITION3-ROUND", 12u32, "2026-10-30T11:24Z", "tibia-lane", "10-30 07:5x tibia: the x-compat census on today's tree (x profile) gives 56 findings, 39 overweight and 17 mentions, exactly the pre-trim count of note 10. So trim.ps1's work is lost from the tree, not just the script. ed3-apply.ps1, ed3-trim\\trim.ps1, identity-after.ps1 and xcompat-tibia-0750.txt are queued first in healing's undelete: their pre-wipe paths are this session's scratchpad (same id ac4b4e98), and the batch lands on the node about 08:3x. If they come back intact, re-anchor and apply after K4; if not, rewrite from notes 9-11 (each overweight is +1..+12, list in this session). The node copy of the tree for the work is C:\\home\\remote-stage\\tibia-trim\\tree.")
inl note_of_tibia_edition3_round_13 () = Note ("TIBIA-EDITION3-ROUND", 13u32, "2026-10-30T14:36Z", "tibia-lane", "10-30 10:3x REDO after healing's undelete. ed3-apply.ps1, trim.ps1, identity-after.ps1 and xcompat-tibia-0750.txt did not survive (BitLocker+TRIM: only files < ~700 B came back). What came back: the 7 converted spiral.toml (scratch ed3-toml). The installed converter (core 9C899B30) reproduces all 7 byte for byte on today's manifests, and the manifests match the pre-wipe bases. REWRITTEN from notes 6-11 (scratch ed3-redo/ed3-apply.ps1, trim/trim.ps1):\n(1) ed3-apply: 8 hash bases (adds live/paths.ps1, whose staleness check now also watches .toml). Dry run on the real tree: 15 Nil -> [] tokens on 14 rows, terrain base_create/read/write -> am'.create_base/index_base/set_base (0 raw !!!! left in terrain; hunting_pack's r9 BackendSwitch kept), predict.ps1 patches spiral.toml (packageDir + module line) beside package.spiproj, then format --manifest toml over the 7 dirs.\n(2) trim: 39 in-cell renames (101 tokens; guards skip .field, type positions and name collisions) + 6 structural edits (spawns_of 'at' alias, foe_melee eta-reduced, clear_loss helper for clear_profit, cave_rat_stats -> rat_stats). On an ED3-applied copy, x-compat (x profile) goes from 56 (39 overweight, 17 mentions) to 17 (0 overweight, 17 mentions, left to the poster per note 11). No string literal changed.\nPROOFS on node mirror tibia-ed3 (box HEAD cec8840c + delta, lib digest 6A4CA91C7F22EE10 = box): job-1793370397675-tibia-ed3-proof (19 outputs: arena+canary Lua, predict/sweep C, map/offscreen Rust, pre vs post ED3; then tests for terrain, ground_trace, lead_trace, arena_host, character, scenario) and job-1793370934978-tibia-trim-proof (identity ED3 vs ED3+trim, then the full build.ps1 over every test file = the K4 on the final tree). The real tree is unchanged until both are green.")
inl note_of_tibia_edition3_round_14 () = Note ("TIBIA-EDITION3-ROUND", 14u32, "2026-10-30T15:58Z", "tibia-lane", "10-30 12:0x PROOF RESULTS (node mirror tibia-ed3, lib = box). (1) The first proof caught a real bug in my rewrite: src's manifest is core-only (packages = ['|core-']), so terrain's base_create/read/write cannot call am'.create_base/index_base/set_base (ETY-UnboundVariable am'). The pre-wipe trial never type-checked, because its copy had no deps link. The terrain step is dropped: its 3 raw !!!! wrappers stay, confined like lib's own. (2) ED3 PROVEN (job-1793372417930): pre -> post 19 of 19 outputs byte-identical. That covers 13 arena Lua, canary ground_trace/lead_trace Lua (with Nil -> []), predict.c, map/offscreen Rust, and scripts/predict.ps1 -Module sweep, which compiles through the patched spiral.toml. (3) TRIM: 18 of 19 identical. sweep's C changed, because foe_melee's eta-reduction (note 9's risk) made the C backend emit a heap closure (Fun0/Closure0, ~170 params) instead of inlining. Replaced by renaming its 4 helpers melee_ready/once/every/round -> hit_* (used only there). x-compat stays at 0 overweight, 17 mentions. Re-prove: job-1793375880554 (pack 8, identity post -> trim). The full build.ps1 (K4) runs after today's lib land, on a post-land mirror.")
inl note_of_tibia_edition3_round_15 () = Note ("TIBIA-EDITION3-ROUND", 15u32, "2026-10-30T16:23Z", "tibia-lane", "10-30 12:2x APPLIED to C:\\home\\git\\tibia (unstaged). (1) ed3-apply: 15 Nil -> [], predict.ps1 patches spiral.toml as well, paths.ps1 staleness check also watches .toml, and 7 spiral.toml (untracked new files). (2) trim: 39 renames + 10 structural edits in 18 files (hit_* replaces the eta-reduction). Proofs: identity pre -> post 19/19 (job-1793372417930, pack 7) and post -> trim 19/19 (job-1793375880554, pack 8, core 17DDB2DC). All 32 changed sources and manifests on the real tree hash-equal the proven node tree. x-compat on the real tree: 0 overweight, 17 mentions (left to the poster). README: status 2026-10-30, the Postable line now says every cell fits one post, plus a manifests line and the setup.ps1 line. Left before Done: the K4 full build.ps1 on the post-land lib (postland-launch.ps1 runs it right after today's tibia lib window).")
inl note_of_tibia_edition3_round_16 () = Note ("TIBIA-EDITION3-ROUND", 16u32, "2026-10-30T21:24Z", "tibia-lane", "10-30 17:2x K4 (full build.ps1, 56 test files) on the post-land lib: back half map..world_port 31/31 green on the box (test-suite window, 14:55-15:39). Front half on the node (job-1793379914468, shared with the post-land gate): 7 files went red only by 300 s cell timeouts or not-run. The redo (node job-1793392093208, then the box at Idle) passes all 7: arena_host 7/7 on the node (it timed out at Idle on the box); blessings, hunt and hunt_sim fully green on the box, including their WGSL rows (the node tree has no WGSL runner, so those rows show as unsupported there). Left: 9 front files whose WGSL rows never ran today (catalog, coins, combat, cooldowns, creatures, damage, experience, geometry, gpu_sim; their CPU rows are green on the node), now on the box at BelowNormal in a test-suite window.")
inl note_of_tibia_edition3_round_17 () = Note ("TIBIA-EDITION3-ROUND", 17u32, "2026-10-30T22:43Z", "tibia-lane", "10-30 18:40 DONE. K4 = full build.ps1 over all 56 test files, GREEN on the post-land lib. map..world_port 31/31 on the box. activity..lua: CPU rows on the node; the 7 load-timeout files (arena_host, character, hunt_sim, hunt, hunting_pack, lead_trace, blessings) green on rerun; and the WGSL rows the node cannot run green on the box (blessings, hunt, hunt_sim, plus catalog, coins, combat, cooldowns, creatures, damage, experience, geometry, gpu_sim: 9/9 at 18:40). Round content: spiral.toml x7 (edition 3), Nil -> [] x15, predict.ps1/paths.ps1 aware of the toml, x-compat trim to 0 overweight (17 mentions left to the poster), identity 19/19 at each step. Terrain's 3 raw !!!! wrappers stay (src is core-only).")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 1u32, "2026-10-26T06:36Z", "x", "2026-10-26 02:35 x: round scope EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION note 32; X-compliance layers SPIRAL-PATH-SYNTAX notes 10-11. Classes in order: manifests (EDITION3-SPIRAL-TOML converter), lexer respells (keywords, ::, Cons sugar, macro sigils), macro wrappers (BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP lib helpers), formatter, 280 split (EDITION3-280-SPLIT); one identical-output gate per class.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 2u32, "2026-10-27T00:54Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-26 20:47 fiscal: manifest class prepared ahead of the compiler items. Main's converter draft (%TEMP%/pack-toml/to-toml.ps1) converts both fiscal manifest shapes cleanly on copies: src/package.spiproj (8 toml lines) and the per-family generated/*/package.spiproj. Those per-family manifests are written by generator.spi module_package, so converting files once would be undone by every regeneration: drafted session scratchpad edition3/generator_toml_transform.py (module_package emits the converter's exact TOML; write_generated_module writes spiral.toml). Verified: the emitted text equals the converter's output byte-for-byte once the converter's CRLF is normalized (the draft writes CRLF via WriteAllLines; reported to main with the fix); generator + its test probe type-check (0 errors). Lands when the compiler reads spiral.toml (EDITION3-SPIRAL-TOML pack), in the same round as converting src/package.spiproj.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 3u32, "2026-10-27T00:54Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-26 20:49 fiscal: lexer-class census of fiscal src (session scratchpad edition3/keyword_census.py, string-literal aware, control passes): word keywords in CODE: 0 in every file (fiscal's hand-written Spiral is already fully sigil-spelled, so the '21 word if/match' class is 0 here); 44 keyword occurrences sit INSIDE string literals (generator.spi 39, corpus_checks.spi 5): these are generated-module templates in the old dialect and a lexer respell must skip string literals or it will corrupt every generated module. Dotted accesses in code (the .x -> ::x class, module paths and record fields together): corpus_checks 116, generator 51, corpus 26, fiscal_paths 1 = 194; the respell needs the compiler's own member/module distinction (SPIRAL-PATH-SYNTAX), so it is applied by that tool, not by a regex here.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 4u32, "2026-10-28T10:44Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 06:44 fiscal: compiler ETAs (06:4x): SPIRAL-PATH-SYNTAX first, on its own candidate, aimed today before 21:00 (good odds, not promised); ZWSP-TRANSPARENT and MACRO-SIGIL-ESCAPES second batch, likely tomorrow. Plan: when PATH-SYNTAX has a candidate DLL, validate it on fiscal (manifest + lexer classes of this round), leave macro sigils for later.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 5u32, "2026-10-28T10:59Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 06:59 fiscal: UNBLOCKED: compiler (07:0x) says all three deps are already in the installed core 9FF1B708 (PATH-SYNTAX, ZWSP, macro-sigil escapes) and closed them Done. The round runs against the installed DLL; my generator + corpus_checks type-check and a node set-proof slice are the functional validation (HOLDS/BROKEN to compiler).")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 6u32, "2026-10-28T11:11Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 07:11 fiscal: ROUND STATE on the installed compiler A4E48020: (a) edition 3 is a package flag ('edition: 3' in package.spiproj, as x/tibia use); with it fiscal's generator + corpus_checks type-check, 0 errors (scratch copy), so edition 3 still accepts '.x'. (b) 'format' under edition 3 leaves the 4 sources unchanged: it lays out, it does not respell '.' -> '::'; asked compiler how to invoke the respell (spiral_compiler.fs:180678). (c) Classes still blocked on tools, not compiler: manifests -> EDITION3-SPIRAL-TOML (45%, converter draft), formatter/280 split -> EDITION3-280-SPLIT (Planned). (d) keywords: fiscal code has 0 word keywords (all 21 are inside generated-module string templates, which the lexer-aware respell must skip).")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_7 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 7u32, "2026-10-28T11:32Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 07:32 fiscal: RESPELL DRAFT (session scratchpad edition3/src): 'format --spelling symbols' (compiler: the string-aware respell, flag missing from usage) on fiscal's 4 sources changed 312 lines; verified line-by-line: 274 are pure '.'->'::' member access, 38 are 'test' -> ':#' (all 38 test blocks), 0 other; string templates untouched. A plain 'format' re-laid the 9 lines the respell pushed past 120 (0 left). With 'edition: 3' in package.spiproj both modules type-check. Gate on the node: generator-only mirrors gbase (today's sources) vs ge3 (respelled) on the same lib must give byte-identical generated/ trees and 21 discovered tests.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_8 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 8u32, "2026-10-28T12:23Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 08:23 fiscal: ge3 BROKEN was the PROOF COMPILER, not the respell: all 21 generator cells failed to tokenize (': is not allowed directly after a var' on each name::member). Node probe: pinned 4FD712E9 rejects helper::one (exit 5), installed A4E48020 accepts it (control helper.nope fails on both). Staged A4E48020 on the node (remote-stage/spiral-bin-1028-0530, 93 files, hash verified); rerun job-1793190257411 fiscal-set-ge3c on it, same mirror + overlays (5 hashes match). Gate unchanged: ge3c vs gbase identical.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_9 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 9u32, "2026-10-28T14:24Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 10:24 fiscal: RESCHEDULED: node 8 cpus at 100%, 12 jobs, 5 fiscal; 4 fiscal generator runs at once made each ~3x slower (setall 3 h, no new unit since 08:08). Stopped gls (3 units in 2 h 43 m) and ge3c (0 units) so P1 setall (XSD-ALL-GROUPS, 13:10 window) and the shared baseline gbase finish first. ge3 rerun = job-1793197542795 fiscal-set-ge3d, queued --after gbase (A4E48020, same mirror + 5 overlays).")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_10 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 10u32, "2026-10-28T15:07Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 11:07 fiscal: baseline gbase (job-1793187256068) VOID: 15 of 21 generator cells timed out at 1,400 s under node contention. Budget raised to 5,400,000 in the gbase/gls/ge3 stage copies only; reruns gbase2 job-1793200073729 + gls2 job-1793197514456 now, ge3e job-1793200091880 after gbase2 (ge3d stopped: it started before the patch).")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_11 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 11u32, "2026-10-29T11:47Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 07:47 fiscal: ROUND PROVEN: ge3e (job-1793200091880, 0 broken claims) regenerates all 70 units BYTE-IDENTICAL to gbase2 (sha256 per file on the node, 0 of 70 differ), so the edition-3 respell changes no generated output. The respell draft (session scratchpad edition3/src) was lost in the 10-28 wipe; regenerate it with 'format --spelling symbols' on the fiscal tree (mechanical) and re-check one unit before applying.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_12 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 12u32, "2026-10-30T02:01Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 22:01 fiscal: GROOM, ordering made explicit: the edition-3 respell of fiscal (and any respell touching lib files fiscal programs anchor in) waits until the held anchored programs land, because a respell stales their anchors. Held now: xpath-double-cast (xpath BD24C126 / xpath_eval BFFB32F6 bases, ready, next session's first window) and xsd-staged-element-signatures (xsd_emit 5606F4B4 base, 24/24 post-land, needs the MDF-e/CL end-to-end). The fiscal tree's own pending edits (corpus_checks 6695FADB, generator 414BE185) should be committed before the respell too.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_13 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 13u32, "2026-10-30T02:05Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 22:05 fiscal: DEPENDENCY WATCH: EDITION3-SPIRAL-TOML (main, 45%) was paused 10-29 by main's WIP rule. It becomes this row's blocker right after next session's first window lands the held programs (the round starts with spiral.toml). Fiscal told main it will drive it if main doesn't resume it first (compiler/lib work belongs to the lane that needs it); its own dep EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION has to be read first.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_14 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 14u32, "2026-10-30T02:08Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 22:08 fiscal: SECOND DEPENDENCY CYCLE REMOVED (found by main's whole-backlog scan): EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION -> FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND -> EDITION3-280-SPLIT -> EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION. 280-SPLIT's own text (user 10-19: 'split everything to 280 X weight per top-level block ... after the edition-3 symbol migration') makes 280-SPLIT -> SYMBOLS-MIGRATION the correct edge, and this round is part of the migration, so the edge from here to the global split was wrong and is dropped. deps now: SPIRAL-PATH-SYNTAX, SPIRAL-MACRO-SIGIL-ESCAPES, SPIRAL-ZWSP-TRANSPARENT, EDITION3-SPIRAL-TOML. Any fiscal file whose cells exceed 280 X weight under the x-compat gate is split inside this round, not deferred to the global split.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_15 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 15u32, "2026-10-30T03:16Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 23:16 fiscal: RESPELL DRY RUN GREEN ON COPIES (fiscal-p7-e3-respell-dry, job-1793329985332, node, pack-7 compiler pinned, i574n.github/scripts/respell-repo.ps1 -Name fiscal-e3dry -Root <fresh fiscal mirror e3dry>, no -Apply): 4 files respelled (every fiscal .spi: fiscal_paths, corpus, corpus_checks, generator), 45 test headers kept as written, 0 errors, words round trip differs 0, and the installed formatter normalizes 2 on top (corpus_checks, generator). So member access .x -> ::x and the sigil respell are mechanical for fiscal. Still to settle: (1) the GENERATED units: generator.spi's emitted text (module_package, xsd_emit output) must emit edition-3 spelling too, or every regenerated unit respells back; that's the 'generated code identical per class' gate; (2) spiral.toml (EDITION3-SPIRAL-TOML; the Cells support is drafted); (3) x-compat 0 findings and the 280 split on the respelled tree. Apply waits for tomorrow's lands (anchors) and your commit of the pending tree edits.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_16 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 16u32, "2026-10-30T03:44Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 23:44 fiscal: DESIGN for generated units (the 'generated code identical per class' gate). xsd_emit writes edition-2 spelling inside ~330 string literals (127 'xml.', 201 sm'.', 0 '::'), and generator.spi's own emitted helpers do the same, so respelling the emitter text by hand would be large and error-prone. Proposal: respell AFTER emission. format-generated.ps1 already runs the installed formatter over every generated unit (now with the toolchain dotnet, FISCAL-GENERATOR-FORMATS n27), so give it '--spelling symbols' (the same verb respell-repo.ps1 uses) once the fiscal tree is edition 3; module_package must then emit edition = 3 for generated packages (spiral.toml or spiproj 'edition: 3'). Gate per class: for each generated unit, respell(old emission) == new emission byte for byte, plus the unit tests green. Open question: does 'format --spelling symbols' keep the cache key (raw sha) stable? Probably not, since the respelled text differs, so the cache gains a spelling dimension. Not started; it waits for the respell apply and EDITION3-SPIRAL-TOML.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_17 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 17u32, "2026-10-30T04:13Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 00:13 fiscal: ROUND APPLIED ON A NODE MIRROR (e3ap, never the live tree): respell-repo.ps1 -Apply (pack 7) respelled all 4 sources (corpus_checks 78DD9F9C -> 5220335B, 284 '::'; corpus 8B45E3CB -> 54066D22; fiscal_paths 62FE941B -> D1AAA4C5; generator 414BE185 -> 96DF233F, 113 '::'), and src/package.spiproj gained 'edition: 3' (x's pattern: x keeps package.spiproj + edition: 3). Generated units keep their own edition-2 packages; the respell changes code, not string literals, so emitted text should be unchanged, which the regeneration diff will check. Proofs queued: fiscal-p7-e3-corpus -> fiscal-p7-e3-generator (22 tests incl. emission) -> fiscal-p7-e3-set-gen (regenerates every family; then diff e3ap/generated vs p7cl/generated, the 'generated code identical per class' gate). x-compat on the respelled tree and the 280 split come after.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_18 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 18u32, "2026-10-30T04:54Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 00:54 fiscal: X-COMPAT ON THE RESPELLED TREE (fiscal-p7-e3-xcompat, job-1793334221741, mix spiral.x_compat over src/, new Cells with Manifest-aware profiles): edition 2 (p7cl) 19 findings -> edition 3 (e3ap) 6, all 'autolink' (X shortens domain-looking text to a 23-char t.co link). The respell removed 13, since '::' doesn't look like a domain. All 6 left are in generator.spi STRING LITERALS: 5x 'listm.map' inside emitted code text (l.606, 708, 716, 717, 935; correct edition-2 spelling for the generated units' own packages) and 1x the corpus path 'DFe.NET' (l.303). So x-compat 0 is coupled to the generated-unit design (n16): emitting edition-3 spelling ('listm::map') clears the 5, but it changes emitted text, so the gate becomes respell(old emission) == new emission per class. The 'DFe.NET' path needs a non-autolinking spelling of the same path (e.g. built from parts), or a recorded x-compat exception. Corpus test green under edition 3; generator tests and regeneration still running.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_19 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 19u32, "2026-10-30T10:26Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 06:25 fiscal: GROOM: the edition-3 tree holds on node mirror e3ap (pack 7): corpus.spi 1/1, generator.spi 22/22 (job-1793333659784), and regeneration from the respelled tree gives 0 broken claims with CL + MDF-e passing every test (job-1793333678728). Left: x-compat 6 autolink findings (all generator.spi string literals: 5x emitted 'listm.map', 1x 'DFe.NET'), the generated-spelling decision (n16), the byte diff of generated/ e3ap vs p7cl, then apply to the live tree after your commit. 40 -> 70.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_20 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 20u32, "2026-10-30T10:33Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 06:33 fiscal: GATE MET, generated code identical per class: SHA-256 of every generated/*.spi on node mirror p7cl (edition-2 tree, regenerated 10-30 02:53 by fiscal-p7-set-cl-mdfe) vs e3ap (edition-3 respelled tree, regenerated 04:27 by fiscal-p7-e3-set-gen), both pack 7 on the same live lib: 74 units vs 74, 0 only on either side, 0 differing. The respell changes fiscal's code, not the emitted text. Gates now: generated identical MET; fiscal tests MET on the mirror (corpus 1/1, generator 22/22, regenerated CL + MDF-e pass); x-compat NOT yet (6 autolink, all generator.spi string literals). Deciding the 6 decides the generated-spelling question: emitting 'listm::map' would change emitted text, so keeping edition-2 emission and resolving the literals another way keeps this gate. 70 -> 80.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_21 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 21u32, "2026-10-30T10:35Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 06:35 fiscal: X-COMPAT OPTIONS for the last 6 findings (live generator.spi CB7E07C7; e3ap line numbers differ). Sites: listm.map inside emitted-code strings at l.603, 699, 707, 708 (+ l.922, a test expectation on emitted text), and the DFe.NET path literals (l.63, 72, 200, 300, 323; x-compat flagged the one that starts a literal, l.300). Options: (A) emit edition-3 spelling (listm::map) and give generated packages edition 3: clean, but changes emitted text, so the generated-identical gate becomes respell(old) == new and every unit is re-proven; (B) split the literals at the dot (listm + .map, DFe + .NET/...): emitted text stays byte-identical and the gate just met holds, at some readability cost; (C) a recorded x-compat exception for emitted-code strings and corpus paths, if the profile can express one. Recommendation: B for the DFe.NET path (a data literal, never meant for X); A or B for listm.map, decided with how generated units should read long-term (A if they are to become edition 3 anyway). Not decided at the end of the night run, to avoid a rushed change to emitted code.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_22 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 22u32, "2026-10-30T14:16Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 10:16 fiscal: X-COMPAT MET with option B (decided by the rule fixed in the previous note: B keeps the generated-identical gate already met, A would re-prove every unit). Applied on e3ap: generator.spi 96DF233F -> 800F8FC8, splitting each flagged literal at the dot (DFe ++# .NET/..., listm ++# .map ...), so emitted text is unchanged. fiscal-p7-e3b-xcompat (job-1793359322623, 07:24): x-compat report: 0 finding(s) in 4 file(s). fiscal-p7-e3b-generator (job-1793359334606) is VOID, not red: 12/22 passed, and all 10 failing rows died at the 1400 s cell cap (slowest 1406648 ms, headroom 1.0) while 3 generator-heavy jobs shared the node; the edition-3 tree went 22/22 before option B, which touches only string literals. Re-proof: fiscal-p7-e3b-set-gen (job-1793359345415) re-runs the generator plus regeneration on the quieter node; then diff e3ap/generated vs p7cl/generated (74 units). Live apply: e3ap's base was 414BE185, so it lacks the CB7E07C7 paren fix; the respell + option B gets redone on the live tree after you commit the current changes, not copied from e3ap.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_23 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 23u32, "2026-10-30T14:23Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 10:23 fiscal: LIVE-TREE DRAFT READY at C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\e3live\\src (apply after your commit; no repo writes). Built from the live tree (generator CB7E07C7) by respell-repo.ps1 -Name fiscal-e3live, dry, pinned to the installed pack 7 (F2F6F4CB5A18): 4 files respelled, 45 test headers kept, 0 errors, word round trip 0 differ, formatter normalized 2. Then option B on top. Draft hashes: generator 59AD5447, corpus_checks 5220335B, corpus 54066D22, fiscal_paths D1AAA4C5, package.spiproj FD0F957B (edition: 3). Equivalence to the proven mirror: corpus/corpus_checks/fiscal_paths/package.spiproj are byte-identical to e3ap's; generator differs from e3ap's 800F8FC8 only in the 3 size_drift pattern lines, which sit inside emitted-code strings (the CB7E07C7 paren fix), and from the plain live respell only in the 6 option-B splits. So e3ap's proofs (generator 22/22 pre-B, 74 generated units identical, x-compat 0) carry over, and the paren fix rides on fiscal-p7-set-ublj2. Also fixed respell-repo.ps1's dry-run message to count the unique files it would write (said 6 for 4).")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_24 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 24u32, "2026-10-30T14:34Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 10:34 fiscal: PROOF MOVED TO THE LANDING DRAFT. Stopped fiscal-p7-e3b-set-gen (exit 143, by rule: superseded, and its 4 h cap counted 2 h of queue wait, so it would have hit the cap about 11:22 mid-generator under load, a likely VOID). New node mirror e3lv = live tree (spiral cec8840c / fiscal 96cac200, REMOTE-SYNC-OK + MIRROR-DEPS-OK) + the 6-file draft from C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\e3live\\src, hash-checked on the node (generator 59AD5447, corpus_checks 5220335B, corpus 54066D22, fiscal_paths D1AAA4C5, package.spiproj FD0F957B, spiral.toml 6AB25EAD from format --manifest toml with edition = 3); lib xsd_emit 161D00F5, xpath_eval 34646246, xsd 147F773B. Chain (pack 7, F2F6F4CB5A18): fiscal-p7-e3lv-xcompat (job-1793370824574) -> fiscal-p7-e3lv-corpus (job-1793370834528, first compile through spiral.toml) -> fiscal-p7-e3lv-set-gen (job-1793370843334, after set-ublj2 so it runs uncontended, 6 h cap incl. wait). Pass lines fixed before looking: x-compat exactly 0 finding(s); corpus 1/1; set-proof 0 broken claims with generator 22/22; then generated/ on e3lv vs p7cl byte-identical (74 units).")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_25 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 25u32, "2026-10-30T14:40Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 10:40 fiscal: e3lv X-COMPAT MET on the landing draft: fiscal-p7-e3lv-xcompat (job-1793370824574) x-compat report: 0 finding(s) in 4 file(s). fiscal-p7-e3lv-corpus (job-1793370834528) is VOID (0 rows), not red. Cells' lib_gate.ps1:16 (the box's current, uncommitted copy, synced into e3lv) now walks up from -Lib for lib/spiral/testing.spi or deps/spiral/lib/spiral/testing.spi, and the fresh mirror had no fiscal\\deps\\spiral yet because nothing had run init.ps1 (e3ap had one from its earlier set-proof init). Requeued as fiscal-p7-e3lv-corpus2 (job-1793371221757-fiscal-p7-e3lv-corpus2) after fiscal-p7-e3lv-set-gen, whose first claim runs init.ps1. Lesson for fix-proof-d on fresh mirrors: init first.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_26 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 26u32, "2026-10-30T15:36Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 11:36 fiscal: e3lv INIT GAP, FIXED IN-RUN. fiscal-p7-e3lv-set-gen's init.ps1 aborted at :135 (BROKEN / init.ps1 completes (1)): the node (Win10 19045) can't fetch facturae.gob.es (TLS ProtocolVersion alert in PS5, pwsh and Schannel curl; python's OpenSSL completes the handshake but fails verifying the FNMT root). The box gets HTTP 200. init then skips every corpus after line 135, so e3lv had 609 of 1156 corpus files. At 11:3x (generator tests ~5 min in, run 2 at a time) I seeded the 21 missing corpus folders + root manifests FROM THE BOX (one tar, 57.1 MB, 638 entries). Not from e3ap: its CEN files are an older pin, and e3lv's freshly fetched CEN 1.3.17 matches the box. After: e3lv = box exactly, 1156 files / 72,079,269 bytes, Facturae XSD B4BBCD587F5F. The run's init claim stays BROKEN as logged. Its generator/regeneration claims run on the full corpus, unless a test read it in the first minutes, which the per-test rows will show. Memory node-cannot-fetch-facturae.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_27 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 27u32, "2026-10-30T19:14Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 15:14 fiscal: GATES MET ON THE LANDING DRAFT (e3lv = live tree + C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\e3live\\src, pack 7 staged F2F6F4CB5A18). Pass lines fixed at 10:34: (1) x-compat exactly 0 finding(s): MET (job-1793370824574). (2) corpus 1/1, the first compile through spiral.toml: MET, reads_the_whole_sefaz_corpus_like_dotnet 99 s (fiscal-p7-e3lv-corpus2, job-1793371221757). (3) set-proof (fiscal-p7-e3lv-set-gen, job-1793370843334): generator 22/22, 0 failed, 0 memo hits; the 4 UBL documents generated; generated_cl_envio_dte_v10 and generated_mdfe_v3_00 2/2 each; validated nominals private (2 files). The ONE broken claim is init.ps1 completes (1): the node's facturae.gob.es TLS failure, environment, with the corpus seeded from the box at 11:3x (n26), not the draft. (4) generated identical, 148/148 files byte-equal by SHA-256: 110 against p7ublj2/generated (the edition-2 regeneration from CB7E07C7 this morning, before ublj3 touched it; includes generated_ubl_invoice_2_1 and generated_ubl_creditnote_2_1 with the paren-fixed emitted size_drift code) and the other 38 (families whose generator rows timed out in set-ublj2: CR, HU-NAV...) against p7cl/generated. Snapshots in node C:\\home\\remote-stage\\dian-ns\\gen-{p7ublj2,e3lv,p7cl}.tsv. 80 -> 95. LEFT: your commit of the current fiscal tree; then I apply the 6-file draft (respell + option B + spiral.toml) to the live tree, unstaged, and re-run x-compat locally.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_28 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 28u32, "2026-10-31T04:55Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 00:55 fiscal: STATE AFTER THE USER'S 22:33 COMMIT (fiscal 85274a9): the commit blocker is gone. The tree's src is still edition 2 and unchanged since the respell base (generator CB7E07C7, corpus 8B45E3CB, corpus_checks 78DD9F9C, fiscal_paths 62FE941B, package.spiproj AFE1B886), so the e3live respell stays valid as drafted (generator 59AD5447, corpus 54066D22, fiscal_paths D1AAA4C5, package.spiproj FD0F957B = '+edition: 3', corpus_checks 1F0376FB with the DIAN layer, which m4 just passed in all 6 regional tests). HELD, not applied: main (22:4x) asks to hold package conversions until EDITION3-MANIFEST-MODEL lands (spiral.toml without a module list, order derived from the code), and every proof of this round (x-compat 0, corpus 1/1, set-gen, m4) compiled WITH spiral.toml 6AB25EAD present. Applying the respelled sources with only 'edition: 3' in package.spiproj would be an unproven configuration. Next: when the manifest schema lands, convert spiral.toml to it, apply e3live (+ the DIAN corpus_checks and the post-e3 generator layer, e3live-budget 62FDA504, after the Delphi lib land), regenerate, and let the generated/ drift guard confirm.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_29 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 29u32, "2026-10-31T20:46Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 16:46 fiscal: land program moved here from fiscal/lib-programs (a folder I invented; programs live in backlog notes so land-lib-program.ps1 -Note can read them): HELD: Cells spiral.toml manifest program from 10-29, waiting on EDITION3-MANIFEST-MODEL (may be superseded by main's manifest work; re-anchor before any use).\nPROGRAM (kit do <lib> -):\nwrite test/spiral/cells/manifest_test.exs <<<\ndefmodule Spiral.Cells.ManifestTest do\n  use ExUnit.Case, async: true\n\n  alias Spiral.Cells.Manifest\n\n  @toml \"\"\"\n  edition = 3\n  packageDir = '../deps/spiral/lib'\n  packages = ['|core-', 'spiral-']\n  modules = '''\n  fiscal_paths\n      corpus\n  '''\n  \"\"\"\n\n  test \"a spiral.toml reads as the spiproj text the parsers expect\" do\n    assert Manifest.from_toml(@toml) ==\n             Enum.join(\n               [\n                 \"edition: 3\",\n                 \"packageDir: ../deps/spiral/lib\",\n                 \"packages:\",\n                 \"    |core-\",\n                 \"    spiral-\",\n                 \"modules:\",\n                 \"    fiscal_paths\",\n                 \"        corpus\",\n                 \"\"\n               ],\n               \"\\n\"\n             )\n  end\n\n  test \"a list may span lines and a blank or comment line stays blank\" do\n    assert Manifest.from_toml(\"# note\\ncrates = [\\n  'serde',\\n  \\\"regex\\\"\\n]\\n\") ==\n             Enum.join([\"\", \"crates:\", \"    serde\", \"    regex\", \"\"], \"\\n\")\n  end\n\n  @tag :tmp_dir\n  test \"spiral.toml is preferred, and a spiproj alone still reads\", %{tmp_dir: dir} do\n    refute Manifest.exists?(dir)\n    File.write!(Path.join(dir, \"package.spiproj\"), \"packageDir: a\\n\")\n    assert Manifest.read!(dir) == \"packageDir: a\\n\"\n    File.write!(Path.join(dir, \"spiral.toml\"), \"packageDir = 'b'\\n\")\n    assert Manifest.path(dir) == Path.join(dir, \"spiral.toml\")\n    assert Manifest.read!(dir) == \"packageDir: b\\n\"\n  end\nend\n\n>>>\nwrite lib/spiral/cells/manifest.ex <<<\ndefmodule Spiral.Cells.Manifest do\n  @moduledoc false\n\n  @names [\"spiral.toml\", \"package.spiproj\"]\n\n  @spec names() :: [String.t()]\n  def names, do: @names\n\n  @spec path(String.t()) :: String.t() | nil\n  def path(dir) do\n    @names |> Enum.map(&Path.join(dir, &1)) |> Enum.find(&File.regular?/1)\n  end\n\n  @spec exists?(String.t()) :: boolean()\n  def exists?(dir), do: path(dir) != nil\n\n  @spec read(String.t()) :: {:ok, String.t()} | {:error, File.posix()}\n  def read(dir) do\n    case path(dir) do\n      nil ->\n        {:error, :enoent}\n\n      file ->\n        with {:ok, text} <- File.read(file) do\n          {:ok, if(String.ends_with?(file, \".toml\"), do: from_toml(text), else: text)}\n        end\n    end\n  end\n\n  @spec read!(String.t()) :: String.t()\n  def read!(dir) do\n    case read(dir) do\n      {:ok, text} -> text\n      {:error, reason} -> raise File.Error, reason: reason, action: \"read manifest in\", path: dir\n    end\n  end\n\n  @spec from_toml(String.t()) :: String.t()\n  def from_toml(text) do\n    text\n    |> String.replace(\"\\r\\n\", \"\\n\")\n    |> String.split(\"\\n\")\n    |> convert([])\n    |> Enum.reverse()\n    |> Enum.join(\"\\n\")\n  end\n\n  defp convert([], acc), do: acc\n\n  defp convert([line | rest], acc) do\n    trimmed = String.trim(line)\n\n    cond do\n      trimmed == \"\" or String.starts_with?(trimmed, \"#\") ->\n        convert(rest, [\"\" | acc])\n\n      not String.contains?(trimmed, \"=\") or String.starts_with?(trimmed, \"=\") ->\n        convert(rest, [line | acc])\n\n      true ->\n        [key, value] = String.split(trimmed, \"=\", parts: 2)\n        key = String.trim(key)\n        value = String.trim(value)\n\n        cond do\n          String.starts_with?(value, \"'''\") -> block(key, String.slice(value, 3..-1//1), rest, acc)\n          String.starts_with?(value, \"[\") -> list(key, value, rest, acc)\n          true -> convert(rest, [\"#{key}: #{unquoted(value)}\" | acc])\n        end\n    end\n  end\n\n  defp block(key, first, rest, acc) do\n    acc = [key <> \":\" | acc]\n    acc = if String.trim(first) != \"\", do: [\"    \" <> first | acc], else: acc\n    {body, after_body} = Enum.split_while(rest, &(not String.ends_with?(String.trim(&1), \"'''\")))\n    acc = Enum.reduce(body, acc, fn line, acc -> [if(String.trim(line) == \"\", do: \"\", else: \"    \" <> line) | acc] end)\n\n    case after_body do\n      [last | remaining] ->\n        [before | _] = String.split(last, \"'''\")\n        convert(remaining, if(String.trim(before) != \"\", do: [\"    \" <> before | acc], else: acc))\n\n      [] ->\n        acc\n    end\n  end\n\n  defp list(key, value, rest, acc) do\n    {collected, remaining} = collect(value, rest)\n    items = collected |> String.trim() |> String.trim_leading(\"[\") |> String.trim_trailing(\"]\") |> String.split(\",\")\n    items = items |> Enum.map(&unquoted/1) |> Enum.reject(&(&1 == \"\"))\n    convert(remaining, Enum.reverse(Enum.map(items, &(\"    \" <> &1))) ++ [key <> \":\" | acc])\n  end\n\n  defp collect(value, rest) do\n    if String.ends_with?(String.trim_trailing(value), \"]\") or rest == [] do\n      {value, rest}\n    else\n      [next | remaining] = rest\n      collect(value <> \" \" <> String.trim(next), remaining)\n    end\n  end\n\n  defp unquoted(value) do\n    value = String.trim(value)\n    quoted = String.length(value) >= 2 and String.first(value) in [\"\\\"\", \"'\"] and String.last(value) == String.first(value)\n    if quoted, do: String.slice(value, 1..-2//1), else: value\n  end\nend\n\n>>>\nedit lib/spiral/cells.ex\npatch <<<\n@@ -832,7 +832,7 @@ defmodule Spiral.Cells do\n \n   defp source_mtime(spi, opts) do\n     dirs =\n-      case File.read(Path.join(Path.dirname(spi), \"package.spiproj\")) do\n+      case Spiral.Cells.Manifest.read(Path.dirname(spi)) do\n         {:ok, text} ->\n           case Regex.run(~r/^packageDir:\\s*(.+)$/m, text) do\n             [_, dir] ->\n@@ -1111,7 +1111,7 @@ defmodule Spiral.Cells do\n         existing = Enum.find(entries, &(&1.name == name)) ->\n           {:halt, {:error, %ProcessError{message: \"package #{name} is listed twice: #{existing.target} and #{target}\"}}}\n \n-        not File.regular?(Path.join(target, \"package.spiproj\")) ->\n+        not Spiral.Cells.Manifest.exists?(target) ->\n           {:halt, {:error, %ProcessError{message: \"Spiral package was not found at #{target}\"}}}\n \n         true ->\n@@ -1135,7 +1135,7 @@ defmodule Spiral.Cells do\n   defp expand_package(path, root) when is_binary(root), do: Path.expand(path, root)\n   defp expand_package(path, _root), do: Path.expand(path)\n \n-  defp package_project?(path), do: File.regular?(Path.join(path, \"package.spiproj\"))\n+  defp package_project?(path), do: Spiral.Cells.Manifest.exists?(path)\n \n   defp exe_name, do: if(match?({:win32, _}, :os.type()), do: \"cell.exe\", else: \"cell\")\n \n>>>\nedit lib/spiral/cells/memo.ex\npatch <<<\n@@ -287,7 +287,7 @@ defmodule Spiral.Cells.Memo do\n     dir = Path.expand(dir)\n \n     with false <- MapSet.member?(seen, dir),\n-         {:ok, project} <- File.read(Path.join(dir, \"package.spiproj\")) do\n+         {:ok, project} <- Spiral.Cells.Manifest.read(dir) do\n       module_files(dir, project) ++ Enum.flat_map(Spiral.Cells.Mounts.declared_dependencies(dir), &tree_files(&1.target, MapSet.put(seen, dir)))\n     else\n       _ -> []\n@@ -345,7 +345,7 @@ defmodule Spiral.Cells.Memo do\n   defp package_index(dir, bounds) do\n     dir = Path.expand(dir)\n \n-    case File.read(Path.join(dir, \"package.spiproj\")) do\n+    case Spiral.Cells.Manifest.read(dir) do\n       {:ok, project} ->\n         modules =\n           for {file, opened} <- module_entries(dir, project) do\n@@ -579,7 +579,7 @@ defmodule Spiral.Cells.Memo do\n     else\n       seen = MapSet.put(seen, dir)\n \n-      case File.read(Path.join(dir, \"package.spiproj\")) do\n+      case Spiral.Cells.Manifest.read(dir) do\n         {:ok, project} ->\n           files = Enum.map(module_files(dir, project), &{&1, content_print(&1, bounds)})\n           deps = for dep <- Spiral.Cells.Mounts.declared_dependencies(dir), do: {dep.name, package_print(dep.target, seen, bounds)}\n>>>\nedit lib/spiral/cells/mounts.ex\npatch <<<\n@@ -59,7 +59,7 @@ defmodule Spiral.Cells.Mounts do\n \n   @spec share_mounted_deps?(String.t(), [String.t()]) :: boolean()\n   def share_mounted_deps?(target, sibling_names) do\n-    text = File.read!(Path.join(target, \"package.spiproj\"))\n+    text = Spiral.Cells.Manifest.read!(target)\n \n     case Regex.run(~r/^packageDir:\\s*(.+)$/m, text) do\n       [_, _dir] ->\n@@ -111,8 +111,8 @@ defmodule Spiral.Cells.Mounts do\n       |> Enum.map_join(\"\\n\", fn entry ->\n         stamp =\n           case entry.kind do\n-            :shadow -> \"\\t#{mtime(Path.join(entry.target, \"package.spiproj\"))}\"\n-            :patched -> \"\\t#{mtime(Path.join(entry.target, \"package.spiproj\"))}\\t#{patches_digest({entry.package_dir, entry.patches})}\"\n+            :shadow -> \"\\t#{mtime(Spiral.Cells.Manifest.path(entry.target))}\"\n+            :patched -> \"\\t#{mtime(Spiral.Cells.Manifest.path(entry.target))}\\t#{patches_digest({entry.package_dir, entry.patches})}\"\n             :link -> \"\"\n           end\n \n@@ -160,7 +160,7 @@ defmodule Spiral.Cells.Mounts do\n \n   defp shadow(link, target, skipped \\\\ MapSet.new(), package_dir \\\\ :siblings) do\n     File.mkdir_p!(link)\n-    text = File.read!(Path.join(target, \"package.spiproj\"))\n+    text = Spiral.Cells.Manifest.read!(target)\n     rewritten = project_for_mount(text, target, package_dir)\n     File.write!(Path.join(link, \"package.spiproj\"), rewritten)\n     File.write!(Path.join(link, \"spiral_cells_shadow\"), \"\")\n@@ -168,7 +168,7 @@ defmodule Spiral.Cells.Mounts do\n     case File.ls(target) do\n       {:ok, names} ->\n         Enum.reduce_while(names, :ok, fn name, :ok ->\n-          if name == \"package.spiproj\" or MapSet.member?(skipped, name) do\n+          if name in Spiral.Cells.Manifest.names() or MapSet.member?(skipped, name) do\n             {:cont, :ok}\n           else\n             case make_link(Path.join(link, name), Path.join(target, name)) do\n@@ -282,7 +282,7 @@ defmodule Spiral.Cells.Mounts do\n   end\n \n   defp source?(name) do\n-    name == \"package.spiproj\" or String.ends_with?(name, \".spi\") or\n+    name in Spiral.Cells.Manifest.names() or String.ends_with?(name, \".spi\") or\n       String.ends_with?(name, \".spir\")\n   end\n \n@@ -297,7 +297,7 @@ defmodule Spiral.Cells.Mounts do\n \n   @spec declared_dependencies(String.t()) :: [%{name: String.t(), target: String.t(), import: String.t()}]\n   def declared_dependencies(dir) do\n-    case File.read(Path.join(dir, \"package.spiproj\")) do\n+    case Spiral.Cells.Manifest.read(dir) do\n       {:ok, text} ->\n         base = package_base(dir, text)\n \n@@ -315,7 +315,7 @@ defmodule Spiral.Cells.Mounts do\n \n   @spec declared_crates(String.t()) :: [String.t()]\n   def declared_crates(dir) do\n-    case File.read(Path.join(dir, \"package.spiproj\")) do\n+    case Spiral.Cells.Manifest.read(dir) do\n       {:ok, text} ->\n         {crates, _mode} =\n           Enum.reduce(String.split(text, ~r/\\r?\\n/), {[], :out}, fn line, {crates, mode} ->\n@@ -363,7 +363,7 @@ defmodule Spiral.Cells.Mounts do\n     {named, found, queue} =\n       Enum.reduce(declared_dependencies(dir), {named, found, rest}, fn dependency, {named, found, queue} ->\n         if MapSet.member?(named, dependency.name) or\n-             not File.regular?(Path.join(dependency.target, \"package.spiproj\")) do\n+             not Spiral.Cells.Manifest.exists?(dependency.target) do\n           {named, found, queue}\n         else\n           {MapSet.put(named, dependency.name), [{dependency.target, dependency.name} | found],\n>>>\nedit lib/spiral/cells/notebook.ex\npatch <<<\n@@ -1257,21 +1257,21 @@ defmodule Spiral.Cells.Notebook do\n       lib_root_itself(dir) ||\n       Enum.find_value(@lib_rels, fn rel ->\n         candidate = Path.join(dir, rel)\n-        if File.regular?(Path.join(candidate, \"package.spiproj\")), do: Path.expand(candidate)\n+        if Spiral.Cells.Manifest.exists?(candidate), do: Path.expand(candidate)\n       end)\n     end) || spiral_lib_from_env(System.get_env(\"SPIRAL_LIB\"))\n   end\n \n   defp lib_root_itself(dir) do\n     expanded = Path.expand(dir)\n-    if String.ends_with?(String.replace(expanded, \"\\\\\", \"/\"), \"/lib/spiral\") and File.regular?(Path.join(expanded, \"package.spiproj\")), do: expanded\n+    if String.ends_with?(String.replace(expanded, \"\\\\\", \"/\"), \"/lib/spiral\") and Spiral.Cells.Manifest.exists?(expanded), do: expanded\n   end\n \n   @doc false\n   def spiral_lib_from_env(value) do\n     case value do\n       dir when is_binary(dir) and dir != \"\" ->\n-        if File.regular?(Path.join(dir, \"package.spiproj\")), do: Path.expand(dir)\n+        if Spiral.Cells.Manifest.exists?(dir), do: Path.expand(dir)\n \n       _ ->\n         nil\n>>>\nedit lib/spiral/cells/notebook_cli.ex\npatch <<<\n@@ -72,7 +72,7 @@ defmodule Spiral.Cells.NotebookCli do\n         main = Path.expand(main)\n         source = File.read!(main)\n         package = Path.dirname(main)\n-        header = if File.exists?(Path.join(package, \"package.spiproj\")), do: \"///- --package #{package}\\n\\n\", else: \"\"\n+        header = if Spiral.Cells.Manifest.exists?(package), do: \"///- --package #{package}\\n\\n\", else: \"\"\n         dir = Path.join(System.tmp_dir!(), \"spiral-probe-#{:erlang.phash2({main, source})}\")\n         File.mkdir_p!(dir)\n         path = Path.join(dir, \"probe.spi\")\n>>>\nedit lib/spiral/cells/x_compat.ex\npatch <<<\n@@ -220,15 +220,13 @@ defmodule Spiral.Cells.XCompat do\n   def edition3?(path) do\n     case nearest_project(path |> Path.expand() |> Path.dirname()) do\n       nil -> false\n-      project -> project |> File.read!() |> String.split(~r/\\r?\\n/) |> Enum.any?(&(String.trim(&1) == \"edition: 3\"))\n+      dir -> dir |> Spiral.Cells.Manifest.read!() |> String.split(~r/\\r?\\n/) |> Enum.any?(&(String.trim(&1) == \"edition: 3\"))\n     end\n   end\n \n   defp nearest_project(dir) do\n-    project = Path.join(dir, \"package.spiproj\")\n-\n     cond do\n-      File.regular?(project) -> project\n+      Spiral.Cells.Manifest.exists?(dir) -> dir\n       Path.dirname(dir) == dir -> nil\n       true -> nearest_project(Path.dirname(dir))\n     end\n>>>")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_30 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 30u32, "2026-11-01T03:41Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 23:41 fiscal: PAUSED (groom 10-31 night; it sat at the top of the light queue while not workable, which is how a window wait turns into idling). REASON: the round is held on EDITION3-MANIFEST-MODEL (main's, 95%, compiler pack 9); its drafts were also archived as stale against today's generator. RESUME CONDITION: EDITION3-MANIFEST-MODEL reaches Done; then resume as Active and re-derive the edition-3 respell from the current tree with format --spelling symbols, proving generated output byte-identical as on 10-29.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_31 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 31u32, "2026-11-01T03:45Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 23:58 fiscal: RESUMED (re-decided on main's word that EDITION3-MANIFEST-MODEL is Done: pack 10, Cells manifest.ex landed). The round needs only fiscal's own manifest (EDITION3-SPIRAL-TOML, Done), not lib's spiral.toml, so it does NOT wait on LIB-SPIRAL-TOML-MIGRATION. The held Cells spiral.toml program (n of 16:46) is RETIRED, replaced by main's manifest.ex; never land it. NEXT (CPU-light): re-derive the respell from the current tree (generator.spi now includes the bench-line edit, directory_create_all) with format --spelling symbols, and draft it on a scratch copy. Then (node): ONE regeneration proving generated output byte-identical to the edition-2 tree plus the bench-line change, shared with FISCAL-PACKAGE-COVERAGE n15.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_32 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 32u32, "2026-11-01T04:10Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 00:40 fiscal: RESPELL RE-DERIVED from the current tree (incl. tonight's generator edits and the DIAN/RO port). respell-repo.ps1 -Name fiscal-e3 (excluding generated/deps/bench) is GREEN on copies: 5 files, 4 respelled, 0 errors, words round trip differs 0; the installed formatter (pack 10 DFC86B91968D) re-lays 2. Extra check: the concatenated string-literal content is identical in all 5 files, so the respell cannot change emitted unit text and generated/ stays byte-identical by construction. Draft at scratchpad e3-src: 5 .spi, package.spiproj with edition: 3 as its first line, and spiral.toml from format --manifest toml (edition = 3). SCOPE: src only. The 32 generated units' package.spiproj are generator output (module_package) and stay edition 2, which their text is; converting them is a FOLLOW-UP generator change. PROOF: node mirror t1101 (synced from the tree), draft overlaid, then node-e3-regen.ps1: the generator cell at edition 3, format-generated, a check that generated/ changes only by the bench + samples-folder lines, then corpus/lifecycle/corpus_checks gates. Queued after the t1031 set-all job.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_33 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 33u32, "2026-11-01T04:17Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 00:55 fiscal: overlay refreshed before the regen job started: the respell was re-derived with the new pint_rules_read_fully test (still GREEN, 5 files, 0 errors, round trip 0, literals identical); t1101 src/corpus_checks.spi = DF6D8854.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_34 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 34u32, "2026-11-01T05:03Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 03:35 fiscal: overlay refreshed again before the job started: t1101 generator 367522F1 (respell of the tree, which now has the CL EnvioDTE prefix fix; literals identical to the tree's) and corpus_checks A5F2E6D3 (EN16931 981 pin). node-e3-regen.ps1 now runs pattern-oracle.ps1 -Write before the src gates (the mirror has no gitignored pattern files). EXPECTED unexpected-change list: generated_cl_envio_dte_v10 only (xmlns:SiiDte on the root). Lib route checked: each notebook resolves the mirror's fiscal\\deps\\spiral junction (process.spi BE258A03), not the node's stale C:\\home\\git\\spiral.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_35 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 35u32, "2026-11-01T05:14Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 03:45 fiscal: RESPELL TRAP SWEEP (main's warning: keyword-anchored source regexes match nothing after --spelling symbols, so gates count 0 and pass). fiscal scripts: build.ps1:44 already accepts ^(test|:#); delphi-reach.ps1:13 already accepts := and inl; delphi-reach.ps1:16 ^(test |///) -> ^(test |:# |///) (unstaged; this round keeps test headers as written, but a later -SymbolTestHeaders run would have broken it silently). sefaz/scripts/candidate-gate.ps1:29 ^inl xsd_table_ -> ^(inl|:=) xsd_table_. No other script anchors on test/inl/let/open/type/union. The src tests' \"inl ...\" checks read generated units, which this round keeps in edition-2 spelling; they must be revisited when the emitter itself moves to edition 3 (the follow-up on generated manifests).")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_36 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 36u32, "2026-11-01T12:34Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 08:40 fiscal: QUALITY SPEC (groom round 4). PRIORITY P0: every later emitter change (cluster B, 9 items in deps) waits on it.\nDONE WHEN: node job-1793506463392 prints (a) \"generator.spi / ... failed 0\" with the 14,400,000 ms cap, (b) \"changed beyond the bench + samples-folder lines\" = generated_cl_envio_dte_v10 + the CR units only, (c) \"corpus.spi / lifecycle.spi / corpus_checks.spi ... failed 0\"; then the tree''s src/*.spi equal the t1101 overlay hashes (respell-repo -Apply), src/package.spiproj starts \"edition: 3\" and src/spiral.toml exists (format --manifest toml), and CI is green on the push that carries them.\nNEXT STEP: read the job''s \"e3-regen /\" lines when it finishes; then pwsh i574n.github/scripts/respell-repo.ps1 -Name fiscal-e3 -Root C:\\home\\git\\fiscal -Exclude ''generated/*,deps/*,bench/*'' -Compiler <pack 10> -Apply, and copy package.spiproj + spiral.toml from the scratchpad e3-src.\nTYPEFEATURESET PLAN: none by design. The respell is mechanical and must not change emitted text (checked: the concatenated string-literal content of all 5 files is identical before and after). Model changes ride the cluster-B items after it.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_37 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 37u32, "2026-11-01T12:39Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 08:40 fiscal: PROOF PROGRESS: job-1793506463392 (t1101) gated the edition-3 respelled generator at 08:04: 23/23 passed, 0 failed, under the 14,400,000 ms cap (the set-all run lost this gate to the 1,400 s cap). It is now in format-generated / src gates. Its 4 node dotnet processes (17084/21816/13564 from 07:00, 10908 from 08:19) are idle compiler servers in its own tree: left for the job's end-of-tree reaping, checked after it ends.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_38 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 38u32, "2026-11-01T12:40Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 08:41 fiscal: CORRECTION to n37. The 3 node dotnet processes 17084/21816/13564 were NOT this job's: x proved them its own (command lines name spiral-cells-19304-, erl 19304 = x-verify46's client notebooks, the only node job at 07:00) and stopped them. I had attributed them by start time and a broken parent chain without reading the full command line. 10908 (under 18792, 08:19) is unattributed. At this job's end, check survivors by command line (spiral-cells-<erlpid> naming its job), never by a pid from a log. Idle orphans like these come from the CELLS-DAEMON-PARENT leak main is fixing.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_39 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 39u32, "2026-11-01T13:16Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 09:31 fiscal: PROOF RESULT (job-1793506463392 finished): generator 23/23 under edition 3 (cap 14,400,000 ms); format-generated 81/81; regeneration changed 44 files, and after normalising the size-derived timeout header + the bench/samples-folder lines only the predicted 7 remain (cl_envio xmlns:SiiDte + 6 CR units Canton/Distrito 00 -> 01); corpus 1/1, lifecycle 4/4; corpus_checks 23/26: (a) resolves_the_nfe_tree + resolves_the_corpus_like_dotnet fail in rustc ONLY under edition 3 (E0425 undeclared st; filed EDITION3-RUST-UNDECLARED-ASSIGN for the compiler lane, P0; same tests pass in edition 2 on CI and t1031u), (b) en16931_rules_parse_completely: a THIRD stale 1.3.17 pin, \"23 code-list tests become member tests\" (XML count of padded contains/concat member tests in 1.3.17: 24), fixed in the tree to 24 with the actual count in the message. DECISION: the respell is NOT applied to the tree until EDITION3-RUST-UNDECLARED-ASSIGN is fixed; the regenerated units (edition-2 emitter output, identical text) ARE brought home now because CI needs them. Mirror t1101 kept as the compiler repro.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_40 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 40u32, "2026-11-01T13:41Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 09:41 fiscal: UNBLOCKED: EDITION3-RUST-UNDECLARED-ASSIGN is fixed (pack14a) and verified by a box rerun of both resolves tests in edition 3 (2/2). All parts of the proof are now green or fixed: generator 23/23, corpus 1/1, lifecycle 4/4, corpus_checks resolves 2/2 (box), en16931 member pin fixed to 24 (counted from the XML; engine confirmation on the next CI run, whose message now prints the actual). ORDERING DECISION: the respell is NOT applied to the tree yet. The user's next commit is the CI-green one (44 regenerated units + pins + Windows retry, edition 2), and CI compiles with spiral main from GitHub, which must contain pack14a before an edition-3 src can pass there. NEXT: after that commit's CI is green AND pack14a is in spiral main, run respell-repo.ps1 -Name fiscal-e3 -Root C:\\home\\git\\fiscal -Exclude 'generated/*,deps/*,bench/*' -Compiler <installed> -Apply, copy src/package.spiproj (edition: 3) and src/spiral.toml from the scratchpad e3-src, and leave it unstaged for the user.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_41 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 41u32, "2026-11-01T13:42Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 09:50 fiscal: CONDITION (b) IS A USER STEP (main): pack14a's source is the live, unstaged spiral apps/compiler/spiral_compiler.fs (sha256 prefix F6F6879566C5A830, checked on the box); it reaches CI only when the user commits and pushes spiral (CI clones https://github.com/i574n/spiral.git main, per fiscal init.ps1). WATCHER armed (fiscal session background bh3hoy321): every 10 min it reads i574n/spiral main's head and, when it moves, downloads apps/compiler/spiral_compiler.fs at that commit and compares the hash; it prints \"PACK14A IN SPIRAL MAIN\" on a match. Then (and after the CI-green commit) apply the respell.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_42 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 42u32, "2026-11-01T13:53Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 09:58 fiscal: RESPELL APPLIED to the fiscal tree (unstaged). Trigger: the watcher saw pack14a in i574n/spiral main at 7a4c960e (09:52; apps/compiler/spiral_compiler.fs F6F6879566C5A830), so CI compiles with the fixed backend. Condition (a) (a separate CI-green commit first) is DROPPED on purpose: its only purpose was to keep an edition-3 src away from a CI without pack14a, and that risk is gone, so one commit saves a 2.5 h CI cycle. Applied with respell-repo.ps1 -Name fiscal-e3 -Apply (4 files respelled + formatted; restore: robocopy %TEMP%\\respell-repo\\fiscal-e3\\original C:\\home\\git\\fiscal /E) plus src/package.spiproj (\"edition: 3\") and new src/spiral.toml. The tree src is now byte-identical to the gated e3-src: corpus_checks 8CE3E213, corpus 54066D22, fiscal_paths D1AAA4C5, generator E187DAD2, lifecycle ABB9021B, package.spiproj C98B264E, spiral.toml A2445EBD (generator 23/23, corpus 1/1, lifecycle 4/4 on node; corpus_checks resolves 2/2 on box pack14a). DONE WHEN: CI on the user's next push (which carries this + the 44 regenerated units + the 283/24 pins + the Windows retry) concludes success on both OSes; the watcher is armed.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_43 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 43u32, "2026-11-01T18:46Z", "fiscal", "fiscal 11-01 14:4x: DONE. All three gates are met on CI run 41314140694 (push f6abb23, the edition-3 commit). (1) Generated code: \"generated / matches the committed copy\" on both OSes. (2) Fiscal tests: every src unit green on ubuntu AND windows-2025: generator 23/23, corpus_checks 26/26, lifecycle 4/4, corpus 1/1. (3) x-compat: 0 findings in each unit's output, plus 0 on the new src/canon.spi (node gate 11-01 14:44). Remaining windows red = 7 generated units crashing the compiler (COMPILER-WIN-STACK-OVERFLOW, fixed by the compiler lane, ships as pack15a). That failure predates edition 3 (every push since 10-25) and is tracked under FISCAL-CI-WORKFLOW.")
inl note_of_kit_table_empty_cells_1 () = Note ("KIT-TABLE-EMPTY-CELLS", 1u32, "2026-10-26T12:28Z", "eoie", "08:28 eoie: opened from the rename preflight. Release-train stage S2 (10-24) meant 'table query --where numeric comparisons fail on cells that are not numbers' (tibia's report), but its program changed only cell_passes, which table test uses (rows_kept), not the host closure plain table query filters with. So tibia's query case is still unfixed, and table test silently flipped against EOIE-TABLE-TEST-WHERE #1 (10-21: foreign_potions<=0 keeps empty cells as tibia expects). table_test_cli caught it: n=a 1 against the expected n=a 2 (candidate and control both; installed eoie gives a 2). Decided for the release: revert S2's cell_passes change (scratch clean\\kit-rename\\table-empty-cells-revert.do), keeping the test block as documentation of the installed behaviour (an empty cell compares as text). Next, with tibia: pick one rule (likely: non-numeric cells fail numeric comparisons everywhere, with --keep-empty for the potions case), apply it to query_rows, rows_kept and measures in one change, and update both CLI notebooks.")
inl note_of_kit_table_empty_cells_2 () = Note ("KIT-TABLE-EMPTY-CELLS", 2u32, "2026-10-26T12:30Z", "eoie", "08:30 eoie: tibia answered (10-26 08:3x). The rule fits: every one of its table query filters (at<200, run>1, run>2, gated>0, delay<=1000) wants an empty cell to FAIL; its table test calls take no --where; the 10-21 foreign_potions<=0 ask has no caller left (live/ retired 10-25), so --keep-empty needs no caller and is optional. Revert for the release accepted. Rule for the follow-up, settled: a non-numeric or empty cell fails every numeric comparison (>, >=, <, <=) in table query's plain path (query_rows host closure), table test (cell_passes via rows_kept) and the measured path, in one change; = and != stay text comparisons; table_test_cli's where fixture gets a second kept a row so its n stays meaningful, and table_cli gains an empty-cell case for delay<=1000.")
inl note_of_kit_table_empty_cells_3 () = Note ("KIT-TABLE-EMPTY-CELLS", 3u32, "2026-10-26T22:54Z", "tibia-lane", "22:54Z tibia design for the settled rule, written before drafting (read from eoie src at 19:0x local; the release holds the tree lease, so nothing is edited there).\n\nSites: there are three comparison stacks, not one.\n(a) table.spi query_rows: one host block. Its own compare closure falls back to text order for non-numbers.\n(b) table.spi cell_passes, used through rows_kept by table test and analysis: numbers_ordered, then texts_ordered.\n(c) kit_table_measures/measures.spi: a second copy of the whole stack (compare union, filters_from, row_passes, ordered with partial_cmp and a text fallback).\n\nAGENTS.md says touching a legacy function migrates it, so (a) moves to Spiral rather than getting a patched closure.\n\nPlan, in one change: a new module kit_table_query/wheres.spi holds where_op, where_op_of, the clause split, the single cell_passes (rule: >, >=, <, <= hold only when both sides parse as finite numbers; = and != stay text) and filters/filters_from/row_passes. table.spi (rows_kept and the migrated plain query) and measures.spi import it, and measures' copy is deleted.\n\nBehaviour kept byte-identical: header line, projection, limit, the 'kit table query ok total= matched= [groups=] shown=' lines, --quiet, the unknown-columns text and its order (filters, cols, group), and the read-error text (check kit_table_text::kit_table_problem against the old '{path}: {error}').\n\nKnown deltas, to be stated in the change:\n- A ragged row's missing cell now reads as \"\" in plain query, as table test already does. Before, every filter failed on it; now only = against a non-empty value and the numeric operators fail.\n- A no-operator clause can't reach any path: option parsing rejects it ('--where expects col=value').\n\nBlocker found: grouped output sorts by count descending, then value ascending. Spiral has no string ordering (`<` on strings is ETY-ConstraintError; tibia hit it today in a test), and lib's only code-point order is private to xpath_eval (text_order_from). So a lib slice comes first: a general text_order (a, b) : i32, either moved out of xpath_eval or added as a backend_switch with Rust str::cmp, plus a lib test.\n\nTests: table.spi's documented test becomes 'an empty or text cell fails every numeric comparison', expecting (!-, !-, !-, !+, !-) on (\"\" <= 1000, \"\" < 1001, \"\" > 1000, 999 <= 1000, abc < abd). table_cli gains latency_ms<=50000 on runs.tsv (row 2's latency is empty): matched=1, where the installed binary gives matched=2. table_test_cli's where fixture gets a second kept row.\n\nProof path: build the candidate kit on the remote kit worker node from a src copy (copy-eoie-src-only), run table_cli and table_test_cli against it, and hand the anchored apply script to the eoie lane after the release.")
inl note_of_kit_table_empty_cells_4 () = Note ("KIT-TABLE-EMPTY-CELLS", 4u32, "2026-10-26T23:44Z", "tibia-lane", "23:44Z tibia, design addendum (19:4x local).\nkit confirmed nothing of theirs has this in flight. The apply script anchors on the tree after kit's land-post-rename slices (several touch kit_table_query) and builds on the quoted-CSV fix; kit messages \"slices landed\".\n\nPrerequisites found while drafting the wheres module (lib-first per AGENTS.md: the touched host one-liners migrate to lib):\n1. LIB-TEXT-ORDER, for grouped output's value order: proven, gating as job-1793057877440.\n2. An optional float parse, for cell_passes' numeric test. No lib function returns option f64: float_native.parse assumes valid text, and convert.try_convert parses integers only. The Rust arm must match today's trim().parse::<f64>().ok(), including inf/NaN, which parse as numbers (NaN then fails every comparison, as now). Shape: float_native.try_parse_f64 (s : string) : option f64, a backend_switch with Rust one-call plus Some/None in Spiral, and a rust test over \"12.5\", \" 3 \", \"\", \"abc\", \"inf\".\n3. The clause split (operator_at, operator_width) and substrings come from sm' (index_of, substring), not host macros.\n\nUnchanged: --where without an operator is rejected at option parsing, so the paths' differing no-operator handling never matters. Order of work: lib slices 1-2 gate, then the eoie change against the post-slice tree, proven by table_cli and table_test_cli run against a candidate kit built on the node.")
inl note_of_kit_table_empty_cells_5 () = Note ("KIT-TABLE-EMPTY-CELLS", 5u32, "2026-10-27T00:17Z", "tibia-lane", "00:17Z tibia: code drafted in scratch eoie-table-empty-cells/draft. It is unproven, waits for kit's \"slices landed\", and needs the rebase anchors.\n- wheres.spi (new module, listed before table in kit_table_query's spiproj): where_op, the clause split over sm' (operator_from as a join point, operator_width, clause_of returning option clause), and cell_passes. The ordered ops compare float_native.try_parse_f64 results directly, and a non-number on either side fails. There is a NaN fix in passing: query_rows made every NaN comparison false, but cell_passes mapped NaN to 'equal' so <= passed; one rule now. Two rust tests, then filters/filters_from/row_passes.\n- plain-query.spi (replaces query_rows): projection (all columns or named, missing names appended in order), row_text, listed_rows counting total/matched/shown under below_limit, and grouped counting (key_rows counts plus a first-seen list, ranked by count descending then xml.text_order ascending, the same order as the old BTreeMap sort by byte).\nOpen before the rebase:\n(1) a cells.spi boundary primitive row_width (one host call) for all-columns projection;\n(2) whether ?= takes 'when' guards, or printed_groups needs an if;\n(3) for groups, matched = the sum of counts;\n(4) check that kit_table_problem's text equals the old '{path}: {error}', so 'kit error: table ...' is byte-identical;\n(5) measures.spi drops its compare/filters copy and imports wheres;\n(6) re-lay the three lines over 120 at the rebase.\nProof: table_cli and table_test_cli on a candidate kit built on the node, plus the new empty-cell case (latency_ms<=50000 gives matched=1).")
inl note_of_kit_table_empty_cells_6 () = Note ("KIT-TABLE-EMPTY-CELLS", 6u32, "2026-10-27T00:55Z", "tibia-lane", "00:55Z tibia: the draft is proven behaviourally before the rebase (scratch eoie-table-empty-cells/probe; compiler only, no kit build, done during kit's rename pause).\nThe probe package holds a lib copy with LIB-TEXT-ORDER and LIB-TRY-PARSE-F64 applied, copies of rust_std_string, union_reflection, query.spi and cells.spi (plus the new row_width primitive), the draft wheres.spi and plain.spi, and two probe mains, compiled to Rust and built with rustc. kit_table_text is stubbed with a plain file read.\n- wheres: printed '11 00 11 latency_ms|50000'. Numeric ops hold on numbers; empty and text cells fail <= and <; = and != stay text; the clause split works. Under the old text-fallback rule the middle pair would print 11.\n- plain query on table_cli's runs.tsv:\n  - latency_ms<=50000 with cols variant,latency_ms prints 'fast<TAB>40000', group '1<TAB>fast', matched=1 (the empty latency now fails; the installed binary gives matched=2).\n  - With all columns, '3<TAB>fast<TAB>9<TAB>40000'.\n  - With no filter, 4 rows, groups '3 fast' then '1 base', matched=4.\n  - Tie fixture b,z,a,z,B: groups '2 z', then '1 B', '1 a', '1 b', i.e. byte order like the old BTreeMap sort.\n- Partial evaluation pruned the all-columns branch while cols was a literal. Reading cols from the environment forced it in, and the generated Rust contains row_width.\nTop-level plain_query is now drafted (header, 'kit table query ok' lines with and without groups, unknown-columns error, --quiet) and run through query-probe.ps1 on table_cli's assertions. All match byte for byte: 'variant TAB retries / fast 5 / fast 9 / total=4 matched=2 shown=2'; variant!=base grouped gives matched=3; group variant gives 'count TAB variant / 3 fast / 1 base / total=4 matched=4 groups=2 shown=2'; '--cols nope' gives 'kit error: table unknown columns: nope (header: timestamp,variant,retries,latency_ms)' exit 2; --quiet hides the summary. New: latency_ms<=50000 gives matched=1. measures.spi with its private compare/filters/row_passes stack deleted and wheres imported (measures-probe.ps1) matches table_cli's measured rows byte for byte: '3 fast 5.333 46120 3.512 92240' and '1 base 4 60000 0 60000'; retries>=4 gives '2 fast 7' and '1 base 4'. New: latency_ms<=50000 with --count gives '1 fast 1', matched=1. Its read errors already go through table_read and rejected, like plain_query. Read errors: kit_table_text's table_problem only checks existence ('{path}: file not found', with its own rust test), while old query_rows printed the OS error text ('{path}: The system cannot find the file specified. (os error 2)'). Plain query now shares table_problem with the measured path and table test: a stated delta that no CLI notebook pins. Still open: then the rebase onto kit's post-slice tree and the CLI notebooks on a candidate kit.\nCLI notebook edits drafted (draft/cli-test-edits.ps1; anchors match once on today's tree, re-check after the rebase). table_test_cli's where fixture gains 'a 13 0 4', so errors<=0 keeps 'n=a 2, b 2' through a numeric row; the installed binary would show n=a 3 there, because the empty cell compares as text. Its passed-metric case becomes 'n=a 4 (3 numeric), b 3'. table_cli gains latency_ms<=50000 with expected 'kit table query ok total=4 matched=1 shown=1'.")
inl note_of_kit_table_empty_cells_7 () = Note ("KIT-TABLE-EMPTY-CELLS", 7u32, "2026-10-27T08:03Z", "tibia-lane", "08:03Z IN THE TREE (unstaged, about 03:55 local), on kit's post-slice src, per the user's WIP-in-place rule.\nFiles: kit_table_query/wheres.spi (new), table.spi (query_rows' host block replaced by a Spiral plain_query; the private where stack moved to wheres), cells.spi (+ row_width), package.spiproj (wheres), kit_table_measures/measures.spi (its private stack removed; imports wheres), table_cli.spi and table_test_cli.spi (the new cases).\nChecks done: layout clean after a formatter re-lay of my 6 long lines; table and measures compile to Rust from the tree files (probe package with the live lib), and the generated code carries row_width, xml.text_order and try_parse_f64, with no text-fallback compare left. Earlier probes matched every table_cli assertion byte for byte and showed the new rule (matched=1).\nOpen: table_cli and table_test_cli on a candidate kit built from this tree, asked of kit's build path. Prerequisites LIB-TEXT-ORDER and LIB-TRY-PARSE-F64 are landed (Done). Backup: tibia scratch eoie-table-empty-cells/tree-before-035516.")
inl note_of_kit_table_empty_cells_8 () = Note ("KIT-TABLE-EMPTY-CELLS", 8u32, "2026-10-27T11:01Z", "tibia-lane", "11:01Z LINE GATE FIX (07:0x). kit-release-SLICES refused kit_table_query/table_query.rs at 1,182 lines (limit 1,000), regenerated from this layer. Ranked: table_run_0 252 (the inlined plain path), filters_from 114, option_applied 100, row_passes 83, with no duplicated copies, so the crate was simply too big. A Spiral-package split wouldn't help (imported packages compile into the consumer); a crate boundary does.\nDone in kit's tree, unstaged: new crate src/kit_table_plain (plain.spi, package.spiproj, Cargo.toml modeled on kit_table_measures) holding the plain query path, migrated off concat5 to sm'_operators ++#, exported as kit_table_plain(&str x4, u64, bool) -> i32. table.spi calls it with a one-expression macro like measured_query. Tab-joined output lines live in a kit_table_query module, lines.spi, so the new package has no encoded rows. Wiring: lines module in the kit_table_query spiproj, the kit-table-plain Cargo dep, and the src/Cargo.toml member.\nProof (Spiral to Rust on a fresh copy of the live lib): table_query.rs 708 lines, plain.rs 769 lines, and table_query calls kit_table_plain. Release requeue asked of kit; its table_cli/table_test_cli run is the behavior check.\nFollow-up drafted (scratch lib-tsv-line/lib-tsv-line.ps1, dry-run clean): lib csv.tsv_line (fields : list string) over sm'.concat_list, with a test block. Once landed, lines.spi drops its 2 bare tab literals (kit_table_query has no census baseline, so the edit hook calls it a new package with encoded rows).")
inl note_of_kit_table_empty_cells_9 () = Note ("KIT-TABLE-EMPTY-CELLS", 9u32, "2026-10-27T19:51Z", "tibia-lane", "19:51Z Follow-up applied after kit's window closed (10-27 15:50 local): kit src/kit_table_query/lines.spi now uses lib csv.tsv_line for row_text, group_line and group_header. The 2 bare tab literals and the sm'_operators import are gone; the file goes F0BBA368A7FF -> 756CA76CC2B8, unstaged. The output text is unchanged (\"\" for no fields, the cell alone for one, tab-joined otherwise). It type-checks on Rust in a scratch copy of kit_table_query, rust_std_string and union_reflection with lib staged as src/spiral; the live file passes the same check as the control. Applied with scratch eoie-table-empty-cells/apply-lines-tsv.ps1, a live-hash guard that refuses a second run (checked). Kit has been told; behaviour is checked by kit's table_cli/table_test_cli in its next release run.")
inl note_of_kit_table_empty_cells_10 () = Note ("KIT-TABLE-EMPTY-CELLS", 10u32, "2026-10-30T01:58Z", "kit", "2026-10-30T01:58 kit groom: deps settled: LIB-TEXT-ORDER and LIB-TRY-PARSE-F64 are both Done, so this item is unblocked at 80%. The last follow-up (tibia, 10-27 15:50) applied the kit_table_query/lines.spi change. Next: verify the one empty/non-numeric cell rule on the installed kit (C528BE4D), then close; not run in this groom.")
inl note_of_kit_table_empty_cells_11 () = Note ("KIT-TABLE-EMPTY-CELLS", 11u32, "2026-10-30T11:12Z", "tibia-lane", "10-30 07:3x LIVE CHECK on the installed kit C528BE4D (scratch empty-cells.tsv: a=500, b='', c=abc, d=2000, e=1000). query: delay<=1000 -> a,e (matched=2); delay>0 -> a,d,e; delay<1001 -> a,e; delay= -> b; name!=a -> b,c,d,e (text). measured: --where delay<=5000 --mean delay -> n 3, mean 1166.667. test: one-sample --where delay<=5000 -> n=all 3. One rule on all three paths: an empty or non-numeric cell fails every numeric comparison, and = / != stay text. Closing.")
inl note_of_kit_table_empty_cells_12 () = Note ("KIT-TABLE-EMPTY-CELLS", 12u32, "2026-11-06T11:30Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 07:4x kit, KIT-RENAME: renamed from EOIE-TABLE-EMPTY-CELLS (item IDs follow the tool name; older notes keep the old ID as history).")
inl note_of_kit_evidence_refresh_1 () = Note ("KIT-EVIDENCE-REFRESH", 1u32, "2026-10-26T21:02Z", "kit", "17:02 kit: Found while preparing KIT-RENAME's post-install step (note 40: 'refresh evidence.spi's binary row for kit.exe with the closeout tool, never by hand-editing a hash'). No such verb exists. state/evidence.spi:47 is core.EvidenceRef ('eoie.exe', sha256, 8424960u64, core.BinaryMedia, core.BundlePath), which evidence_currentness_domain's closeout check reads and also requires a root binary named kit or kit.exe (terminal.spi 265-268). The only writers in src are register_coverage_evidence (coverage rows only, terminal.spi:297) and kit_toolchain_proxy's identity_line (portable toolchain rows, ExternalRequired). So after install, the check will truthfully report the binary evidence stale, and nothing can refresh it without a hand edit. Shape: 'kit evidence refresh <root> <relative path>' rewrites one EvidenceRef row from the file on disk (name, sha256 via the existing portable_sha256, byte length), keeps the media and custody fields, refuses a path outside the root or not already listed, and supports a dry run. Renaming a row (eoie.exe to kit.exe) is the same verb with --as <new relative path>. Test block: a fixture root with a two-row evidence file; refresh one, the other stays byte-identical, and the closeout check passes.")
inl note_of_kit_evidence_refresh_2 () = Note ("KIT-EVIDENCE-REFRESH", 2u32, "2026-10-27T12:55Z", "kit", "09:0x kit: built and proven on a probe copy, staged with the ceremony verbs (one CLI stage: clean/kit-rename/cli-ceremonies-evidence, 11 files with base hashes, applied by staged-apply.ps1 after kit-release-SLICES). 'kit evidence refresh <root> <relative path> [--as <new relative path>] [--dry-run]' lives in a new granular crate, kit_evidence (evidence.rs 428 lines): a typed refresh_outcome; pure rewritten_row and refreshed_text; one-expression host primitives for args, the existing kit_proxy_search::inspection_file_sha256 and the file length; the write goes through workspace_primitives' replace_file_checked. It is a direct verb (VerbEvidence, help line; kit.rs 958, command_spec.rs 862). Test block: one row rewritten (rename), the other byte-identical; an unlisted path refused; a path escaping the root refused. End-to-end on the generated Rust (fixture root with a two-row evidence.spi; sha256 via a stub with the same signature): --dry-run writes nothing; refresh --as kit.exe rewrites only that row, with sha256 equal to Get-FileHash and length 12, and the other row byte-identical; a missing file and ../escape exit 2 with their reasons. After the next install, 'kit evidence refresh <kit root> eoie.exe --as kit.exe' fixes evidence.spi:47 without a hand edit.")
inl note_of_kit_evidence_refresh_3 () = Note ("KIT-EVIDENCE-REFRESH", 3u32, "2026-10-30T01:58Z", "kit", "2026-10-30T01:58 kit groom (user, via main 21:54): SHIPPED: installed kit C528BE4D lists 'kit evidence refresh <root> <relative path> [--as <new relative path>] [--dry-run]'. Progress 70 -> 90. Close after one --dry-run against a real EvidenceRef row shows the rewritten row (not run in this groom).")
inl note_of_kit_evidence_refresh_4 () = Note ("KIT-EVIDENCE-REFRESH", 4u32, "2026-10-31T07:42Z", "kit", "10-31 03:3x kit: DONE line met. On the installed kit C528BE4D, 'kit evidence refresh C:\\home\\git\\kit evidence/coverage/current.lcov.receipt --dry-run' exits 0 and prints the rewritten row, core.EvidenceRef (\"evidence/coverage/current.lcov.receipt\", \"225416fa…426e\", 133u64, ...). Get-FileHash and the file length agree (sha256 225416fa…, 133 bytes).")
inl note_of_xsd_any_content_reader_1 () = Note ("XSD-ANY-CONTENT-READER", 1u32, "2026-10-27T04:19Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 00:19 fiscal: FOUND by the ours bench's round-trip check (compare-roundtrip.ps1, namespace-normalized, node job-1793060915958): parsing each family's own example with its generated reader and writing it back LOSES DATA in 5 of 12 families: CT-e v2.00/v3.00/v4.00 ('/CTe/infCte/infCTeNorm/infModal: missing modal') and MDF-e v1.00/v3.00 ('/MDFe/infMDFe/infModal: missing modal'). Those schemas put the transport-mode payload (road, air, rail, water, pipeline) under an xs:any inside infModal. Cause: xsd_emit's reading stage hard-codes 'any_part reading = any = Nil', so every generated reader silently discards wildcard content, while the writer writes x.any and the example puts a modal element there. For CT-e and MDF-e this drops the whole modal section of a real document without any error. Fix direction: the reader captures the children that no named element of the record claims (in document order) into the any field, instead of Nil: any_part reading needs the list of the record's own element names (from the walked parts) to filter children. Gate: the bench round-trip reports roundtrip-equal for CT-e and MDF-e; acyclic families without xs:any keep their bytes; regression test: a record with a wildcard reads back an unknown child unchanged.")
inl note_of_xsd_any_content_reader_2 () = Note ("XSD-ANY-CONTENT-READER", 2u32, "2026-10-27T07:34Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 03:34 fiscal: DRAFTED and TYPE-CHECKED on the live tree: session scratchpad recgroups/any_content_transform.py edits two lib files. xml.spi gains named_in and unclaimed_children (claimed names -> list xml_node -> the child elements whose local name no named element claims, in document order; test unclaimed_children_keep_only_unknown_elements). xsd_emit.spi gains claimed_names (every element tag of a record's content particle tree) and with_any_claims, applied at the single record_texts call site in record_walk: it rewrites only the reader's '        any = Nil' line to 'any = xml.unclaimed_children [<the record's element names>] children' (the exampling stage writes [xml.element ...] and the writer x.any, so neither matches); test a_wildcard_reads_the_children_no_named_element_claims. Checks: xml, xsd_emit, both test probes and json_schema 0 errors; no new over-120 lines. Node proof queued: job-1793086574129-fiscal-ac-proof after the full build. PASS rule (pre-written): transform applies; true baseline then fixed regeneration; generator 0 failed, 0 memo hits; every moved module reads its wildcard through xml.unclaimed_children; CT-e v2/v3/v4, CT-e Simp v4 and MDF-e v1/v3 each read their own example AND round-trip EQUAL (modal preserved).")
inl note_of_xsd_any_content_reader_3 () = Note ("XSD-ANY-CONTENT-READER", 3u32, "2026-10-27T08:21Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 04:21 fiscal: IN THE TREE, unstaged (per the user's WIP-in-repo practice; backup + both repos' git diff --cached in the session scratchpad backups/wip-drafts-20261027-0419, staged diffs verified unchanged). lib/spiral/xml.spi 321990D4F9120C50 and xsd_emit.spi 9EF79DB949E83D96 now hold this draft together with XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS (same two files; the combination with the emptiable readers type-checks: xml, xsd_emit, probe_xml, probe_xsd_emit, json_schema, fiscal generator + probe all 0 errors, installed formatter applied). One revision since note 2: named_in compares LOCAL names, so a prefixed claim (ds:Signature, cbc:ID) still claims its element. The node proof (job-1793086574129, queued after the full build) now applies the emptiable readers first, since CT-e Simp reads its example only with them; its pass rule is unchanged.")
inl note_of_xsd_any_content_reader_4 () = Note ("XSD-ANY-CONTENT-READER", 4u32, "2026-10-27T10:01Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 05:57 fiscal: PROOF PASSED (job-1793086574129-fiscal-ac-proof, node, exit 0, 0 broken claims, mirror restored hash-verified). Every pre-written claim HOLDS: the emptiable readers applied first (baseline = post-landing emitter); true baseline regeneration exits 0; the transform applies; the fixed regeneration exits 0 with every generator test run and passed (0 memo hits); it moved 12 modules and EVERY moved one reads its wildcard through xml.unclaimed_children; CT-e v2/v3/v4, CT-e Simp v4 and MDF-e v1/v3 each read their own example and measure a row; and each of them now ROUND-TRIPS EQUAL (modal preserved). Whole round-trip table for ours: 15 of 15 measured families roundtrip-equal (CFDI, CT-e OS v3/v4, CT-e Simp v4, CT-e v2/v3/v4, FatturaPA, GTV-e v3/v4, KSeF, MDF-e v1/v3, NF-e v2.00/v3.10). Rows (node, us parse / serialize): CT-e v2 580/446, v3 834/648, v4 776/615, CT-e Simp 1993/1673, MDF-e v1 841/665, v3 1194/915. For contrast, DFe.NET on the same documents round-trips 0 of 10 equal (FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH n38). The code is already in the tree unstaged (xml.spi 321990D4, xsd_emit.spi C6282D52). 90%, not Done: the local same-box bench (job-1793094391561-fiscal-local-bench) regenerates from the TREE copy itself; it closes this item when its CT-e/MDF-e rows and round trips match.")
inl note_of_xsd_any_content_reader_5 () = Note ("XSD-ANY-CONTENT-READER", 5u32, "2026-10-28T10:33Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 06:31 fiscal: DONE: in the live lib since 10-27 04:21, proof job-1793086574129 0 broken claims; node set-proof 10-27/28, compiler 4FD712E9E357: xml lib gate 14/14 incl claimed_children_keep_the_named_elements_in_order; CT-e/MDF-e units green (job-1793152028390).")
inl note_of_xsd_imported_namespace_elements_1 () = Note ("XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS", 1u32, "2026-10-27T05:54Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 01:54 fiscal: FOUND once UBL main compiled (XSD-RECURSIVE-TYPE-GROUPS proof job-1793077378367). The generated UBL example is <Invoice xmlns=...Invoice-2><ID>1</ID><IssueDate>..</IssueDate><AccountingSupplierParty/>...: every element is written in the Invoice namespace, but UBL 2.1 takes its vocabulary from imported schemas, so ID/IssueDate must be cbc: (urn:oasis:names:specification:ubl:schema:xsd:CommonBasicComponents-2) and AccountingSupplierParty etc. cac: (CommonAggregateComponents-2). Validation (with the validator fix below): 'The element Invoice ... has invalid child element ID in namespace ...Invoice-2'. Single-namespace families (NF-e, CT-e, MDF-e, CFDI, FatturaPA, KSeF) never needed this, which is why it is invisible elsewhere. Fix direction: carry each element's target namespace (from the schema that declares it, honoring elementFormDefault and element refs into imported schemas) into the writer, emit a prefix per namespace on the root (xmlns:cbc / xmlns:cac) and the reader matches on local name + namespace. Also visible in the example: required aggregates written empty (<AccountingSupplierParty/> needs Party), a second, example-side gap. Gate: family-gates reports 0 validation messages for generated_ubl_invoice_2_1_example.xml; the other 16 samples stay at 0. VALIDATOR FIX landed unstaged in fiscal/scripts the same night: UBL's xmldsig-core schema carries a DTD, which .NET prohibits by default, so the UBL schema set never compiled ('xmldsig#:Signature is not declared') and family-gates reported a 'fatal: null-valued expression' instead of validating; validate-example.ps1 now loads preloaded schemas with DTDs ignored, gained -Resolve (keep the resolver alongside preloads), and reports a fatal's script line; family-gates preloads UBL's xmldsig with -Resolve. Regression: all 16 node samples still 0 messages through the new scripts.")
inl note_of_xsd_imported_namespace_elements_2 () = Note ("XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS", 2u32, "2026-10-27T07:38Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 03:38 fiscal: DESIGN from a code read (no compile yet). Where the namespace is lost: xsd.spi takes an element's name from name= or ref= (line 229), so a UBL reference starts as 'cbc:ID' / 'cac:AccountingSupplierParty'; xsd_resolve.merge keeps ONE target_namespace for the merged schema; and xsd_emit's dereference pass replaces a ref-only element by the global element it names ('Element { root ?| occurs = e.occurs }'), whose name is the unprefixed 'ID'. So the prefix exists in the model and is dropped at dereference. Plan, four small changes: (1) dereference keeps the referencing element's (prefixed) name: Element { root ?| occurs = e.occurs; name = e.name }, so the writer emits cbc:ID; (2) xml.children_named compares local names on BOTH sides (today local_name name = target), so readers keep matching prefixed targets; a generic, safe lib change; (3) the root element declares every prefix the document uses (xmlns:cbc, xmlns:cac, ...), taken from the root schema's declared namespaces (xsd_resolve.declared_namespaces), the same way the generator already adds xmlns and with_namespace adds xmldsig; (4) field names use the local name (field_name (local_name ...)), so record fields stay prefix-free and acyclic families keep their bytes. Single-namespace families never use refs with prefixes into another namespace, so they should stay byte-identical (to verify with the true-baseline regeneration used for the emptiable proof). Also visible in the UBL example and separate: required aggregates written empty (<AccountingSupplierParty/> needs cac:Party), an example-side gap to look at once the namespaces are right.")
inl note_of_xsd_imported_namespace_elements_3 () = Note ("XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS", 3u32, "2026-10-27T08:21Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 04:21 fiscal: DESIGN REVISED after a census, and IN THE TREE unstaged (xml.spi 321990D4, xsd_emit.spi 9EF79DB9, fiscal src/generator.spi 80043D5F; type-checked with the emptiable and xs:any drafts; the backup is in the session scratchpad backups/wip-drafts-20261027-0419). Census of prefixed refs: cbc 1360 + cac 881 (UBL), but ALSO ds: in NF-e (77), CT-e (31+18), MDF-e (9), FatturaPA (3), UBL (33). Keeping the prefix at dereference alone would write <ds:Signature xmlns=...xmldsig#> with ds undeclared, which is invalid XML in four families that are green today. So the draft is five changes: (1) dereference keeps the ref's prefixed name; (2) xml.children_named / count_named compare local names on both sides; (3) xml.with_namespace renames the element to its LOCAL name when it adds the default xmlns (the prefix is redundant there and may be undeclared), so BR Signature output stays as today; (4) field_name snake-cases the local name, and the two 'choice_' ++# first compositions take xml.local_name first, so BR field names do not churn; (5) generator.spi declares on the example root every xmlns:<p> of the root schema other than the target, XSD and xmldsig namespaces (prefix_declarations). New tests: a_prefixed_target_matches_the_same_local_element, a_default_namespace_drops_the_element_prefix. Known limit: prefixes declared only by an imported schema (sac/sbc/sig, inside UBL extension content) are not declared on the root. Next: node proof = true-baseline regen, BR modules byte-identical or Signature-only moves, then the UBL example validates (validate-example -Resolve) with 0 messages.")
inl note_of_xsd_imported_namespace_elements_4 () = Note ("XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS", 4u32, "2026-10-27T08:47Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 04:47 fiscal: node proof QUEUED: job-1793090714004-fiscal-ns-proof (after the xs:any proof). It also proves the generator's new bench test (FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH n36). Inputs are staged hash-verified: base = the pre-draft tree (xml D55BBB83, xsd_emit DD404B4E, generator 9BA3862A) plus the emptiable and xs:any transforms; candidate = the tree now (xml 321990D4, xsd_emit C6282D52 as landed, generator 2B17149C). PASS rule (pre-written): both regenerations exit 0 with every generator test run and passed (0 memo hits); with each module's new <module>_bench_runs block set aside, ONLY generated_ubl_* modules move (every BR, CFDI, FatturaPA and KSeF module byte-identical, so the ds:Signature handling and the field names are unchanged); every listed family's module carries its bench test, and all 16 print a bench row 'parse_us N write_us N runs 31 bytes N' (UBL included: it reads its own example once the namespaces are right); family-gates exits 0 (every sample validates with 0 messages, the UBL example included); mirror restored hash-verified. Round-trip rows are reported, not gated (UBL's empty required aggregates are a known example-side gap).")
inl note_of_xsd_imported_namespace_elements_5 () = Note ("XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS", 5u32, "2026-10-27T08:50Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 04:50 fiscal: PASS RULE CORRECTED before the run (ns-proof still queued; node copy hash-verified 2C348373). Two defects in note 4's sample claim, found by reading family-gates.ps1: (1) it never sets an exit code from validation results, so 'family-gates exits 0' checked nothing; (2) 'the UBL example validates with 0 messages' also needs the empty required aggregates fixed, a separate example-side gap, not what this item claims. Replaced by: every non-UBL '== <sample>' section reports 'validation messages 0'; and the UBL example, validated directly with every message shown (-Show 2000), has NO message naming a child element in the Invoice namespace (the wrong-namespace symptom). The regex was controlled both ways: it matches the real wrong-namespace message shape and does not match an 'incomplete content' message. The other claims are unchanged.")
inl note_of_xsd_imported_namespace_elements_6 () = Note ("XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS", 6u32, "2026-10-27T10:44Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 06:48 fiscal: ns-proof (job-1793090714004) claim BROKEN, by the rule as written: with each module's bench block set aside, 17 modules moved, not only generated_ubl_*. Every move is explained from the candidate output (the local same-box bench regenerated the same tree, so its generated/ is this candidate): (a) 14 BR families + FatturaPA now emit the ref's qualified name in lookups, e.g. cte_v4 line 16125 'xml.required_child \"ds:Signature\" children' (cte_v4 14 such lines, nfe 4, mdfe_v1 2): same element, since readers now compare local names; behavior evidence: generated_cte_os_v3_00 (12 such lines) passed 3 of 3 tests including its bench test, which reads its own example; (b) CFDI's example root now declares xmlns:catCFDI and xmlns:tdCFDI, prefixes cfdv40.xsd uses only in type= references, never in element names: dead declarations, a real flaw in prefix_declarations. Note 3 of this item had anticipated 'Signature-only moves'; note 4's stricter rule omitted them, so the rule was miscalibrated, not the behavior. NEXT, rule pre-written before the rerun: (1) fix: prefix_declarations declares a prefix only when the root schema text contains ref=\"<prefix>: (UBL's Invoice schema refs cbc:/cac:/ext:, CFDI refs none, so CFDI's root returns to its old bytes); (2) rerun claim: after setting the bench block aside AND normalizing every '\"ds:' to '\"' in both texts, ONLY generated_ubl_* modules differ; plus all the other claims of note 4/5 unchanged. The rest of this run's claims (bench rows, sample gates, UBL namespace messages) are still reported when it ends.")
inl note_of_xsd_imported_namespace_elements_7 () = Note ("XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS", 7u32, "2026-10-27T11:40Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 07:50 fiscal: ns-proof FINISHED (job-1793090714004, exit 1). HOLDS: both regenerations exit 0 with 0 failed / 0 memo hits; every listed family carries its bench test; 15 of 16 families measure a bench row through the generator's new <module>_bench_runs test (node, us parse/write: NF-e v2 1033/773, v3.10 2357/1720, CT-e v2 609/450, v3 717/536, v4 1267/853, CT-e OS v3 753/545, v4 1570/1210, CT-e Simp 1806/1528, GTV-e v3 1432/1081, v4 1483/1102, MDF-e v1 662/526, v3 608/471, CFDI 237/165, FatturaPA 617/465, KSeF 583/391), so the append_bench port is proven; all 15 measured families round-trip EQUAL; every non-UBL sample validates with 0 messages (16 sections). BROKEN: (1) the module-move claim, already explained in note 6 (Signature-only lookups + CFDI's dead prefix declarations; the CFDI fix is in the tree since 06:5x); (2) UBL: its unit timed out again at the 1,200 s cell budget (units build exit 1), so it wrote no sample, so neither its bench row nor the namespace check could run. UBL's compile time is now the blocker for this item and for the seven UBL-based country items (Peppol, ZATCA, MyInvois, SUNAT, DIAN, RO_CIUS, UBL-TR). Next: measure the UBL rust cell alone on the node with a raised budget (phases: target vs compile), then decide between a higher budget and a smaller module (XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS / FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES shrink every module).")
inl note_of_xsd_imported_namespace_elements_8 () = Note ("XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS", 8u32, "2026-10-27T12:51Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 08:51 fiscal: the UBL blocker is resolved by budget, not by code: UBL's unit passes in 2,852 s (rustc 92%), and the generator now scales each module's cell budget with its size (FISCAL-PACKAGE-COVERAGE note of this time). The next regeneration proof (with the CFDI prefix fix) can now check UBL's bench row and its namespace messages.")
inl note_of_xsd_imported_namespace_elements_9 () = Note ("XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS", 9u32, "2026-10-27T15:24Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 11:24 fiscal: LIB TESTS PASS on the node (all-proof job-1793112172864, Cells lib_gate per module, process compiler, memo off, full logs kept): xsd 8/8, xsd_resolve 4/4, xsd_emit 17/17, json_schema 5/5, xml 10/10 (13 rows), every one of today's new tests present and green. xml's a_prefixed_target_matches_the_same_local_element and a_default_namespace_drops_the_element_prefix pass.")
inl note_of_xsd_imported_namespace_elements_10 () = Note ("XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS", 10u32, "2026-10-30T02:02Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 22:02 fiscal: GROOM, END-TO-END EVIDENCE: fiscal-6b-set-ublj2 (pack 6b, mirror ublj6b, 10-29 16:21-20:26) HOLDS 'the UBL Invoice example has no child element in the wrong (Invoice) namespace (0 such messages)' for regenerated generated_ubl_invoice_2_1. That is this story's correctness claim on a real regeneration, not only the 10-27 lib tests. Not closed: the same run's json round trip fails on all 22 UBL-JSON documents (FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS n16-18), which may or may not be namespace-related. Its 7 dependents (Peppol, ZATCA, UBL-TR, MyInvois, SUNAT, DIAN, RO_CIUS) can't close before this one; decide next session whether the JSON size drift belongs here or to MyInvois.")
inl note_of_xsd_imported_namespace_elements_11 () = Note ("XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS", 11u32, "2026-10-30T15:25Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 11:25 fiscal: the namespace claim on the regenerated UBL Invoice is still VOID: fiscal-p7-set-ublj2 timed out in generated_ubl_invoice_2_1 at its 85-min cell budget under node load (details FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS, this time). Rerun fiscal-p7-set-ublj3 (job-1793373950641-fiscal-p7-set-ublj3) gets a mirror-only 3x budget; the 10-29 pack-6b HOLDS (n of 10-29 22:02) stands as the latest real evidence.")
inl note_of_xsd_imported_namespace_elements_12 () = Note ("XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS", 12u32, "2026-10-30T22:53Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 18:52 fiscal: CLOSED. fiscal-p7-set-ublj3 (job-1793373950641, mirror p7ublj2, live lib, pack 7, mirror-only cell budget x3 so the unit could finish): 'HOLDS / the UBL Invoice example has no child element in the wrong (Invoice) namespace (0 such messages)', the same claim as 10-29 pack 6b, now on the live lib. The 10-29 open question is DECIDED: the UBL-JSON drift belongs to FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS. The diagnostic shows the typed JSON path ADDING nodes (408 -> 430 at ID//ExtensionURI), only in the 22 UBL-JSON documents, so it is not a namespace fault; the XML documents read back fine. Dependents unblocked: Peppol, ZATCA, UBL-TR, MyInvois, SUNAT, DIAN, RO_CIUS.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_1 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 1u32, "2026-10-27T10:15Z", "main", "user 2026-10-27 06:0x: \"move everything useful from polyglot to i574n.github so we remove polyglot from the org. also check if there's something in the spiral repo or in the others that could also be moved to i574n.github, that one since already holds agile could also become the examples lab etc. gotta care for drift though, we already dumped a lot of scripts into it recently.\"\nCENSUS 10-27 06:1x (main). polyglot holds:\n- apps: chat (12 files, the NEAR chat contract and its tests, last commit 10-27, live), spiral (37, 10-25), parser 5, ipfs 4, perf 2, scheduler 2, builder 0 (empty, all 10-07 or later)\n- lib: fsharp 18, math 9, rust 97, typescript 121\n- scripts: 17, incl. core.ps1, which most consumer builds dot-source\n- examples 1, .github/workflows 2\n- deps: mostly third-party checkouts (Fable, dotnet-interactive, Paket, The-Spiral-Language, mpmath, hyperui), plus deps/spiral -> C:\\home\\git\\spiral\nCONSUMERS: 662 references to polyglot in 118 script/config files:\n- dice: scripts/init.ps1 x11, publish, build, contract and lib builds, and ui/package.spiproj, whose packageDir resolves lib through deps/polyglot/deps/spiral/lib\n- alphabet: init x7, apps/hangul and apps/documents spiproj and builds\n- vault and tibia: init, workflow, publish, app builds\n- i574n.github's own scripts: workflow, publish, init, build, outdated, pins, remote, pages-sweep\n- dotfiles: dist/appdata/spiral/build.ps1\n- spiral: lab scripts, and compiler tmp scripts env.ps1, parser-corpus-gate, lib-usage-census\n- also an absolute link apps/chat/contract/lib -> C:\\home\\git\\polyglot\\lib\nPLAN (phase rules fixed before any move):\n(1) Inventory every polyglot path into exactly one class: MOVE (unique and useful), ELSEWHERE (an equal or newer copy exists, proven by hash or a diff of the content), THIRD-PARTY (re-fetchable dependency), DROP (empty or history-only). Record it in this item's notes, not a new doc.\n(2) Drift guard before anything lands in i574n.github: grep each moved file's stem across i574n.github/scripts (44 files, incl. the 8 job-runner tools main moved there on 10-26/27), spiral/apps/compiler/tmp/scripts and polyglot/scripts. A second copy is merged into the existing one or dropped, never added beside it (one record per fact).\n(3) Shared build scripts (core.ps1 and what it dot-sources) move first, as i574n.github/scripts/<name>, with the consumer path unchanged until (5).\n(4) Apps and libs: polyglot lib rust/typescript/fsharp/math go to spiral lib where they are Spiral-generated lib code (lib-first), otherwise to i574n.github. chat moves as one unit with its contract tests; its build proof is the existing build.ps1 exit 0 plus the contract tests on a copy.\n(5) Consumers repoint one repo at a time (dice, alphabet, vault, tibia, dotfiles, i574n.github, spiral), each proven by that repo's own build GREEN on a copy. Each repo's team gets its edit.\n(6) Done when grep finds 0 polyglot references outside fc1943s backups and history. Then the repo is ARCHIVED on GitHub by the user (deleting or archiving an org repo is the user's call). fc1943s keeps the dump.\nEXAMPLES LAB (the user's suggestion: i574n.github as the examples lab). Candidates to census next:\n- spiral/lab (107 folders, 1,506 files; LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL): drafts land in their home repo by rule, so only true examples move, never WIP\n- polyglot apps parser/ipfs/perf/scheduler/examples\n- standalone sample apps in other repos that are demos rather than products\nThe compiler's regression fixtures stay in spiral (apps/compiler/tmp/tests and samples: they are the matrix's oracle input). The examples/ top-level folder is a structure decision: the user proposed it here, and its exact name and layout are confirmed with the user before the first move.\nRelated: SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT (spiral's own polyglot references), COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE, LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_2 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 2u32, "2026-10-27T10:18Z", "main", "10-27 06:18 main: planning fields, set by note because kit has no verb for them after add (agile set takes only progress and status; agile add accepts --estimate/--deps only at intake, a gap for EOIE-AGILE-FIELD-COMPLETENESS). ESTIMATE 1,230m, from the plan's milestones: (1) inventory 120m, (2) drift census by stem across the three script homes 60m, (3) shared scripts 120m, (4) apps and libs 480m (chat with its contract tests is most of it), (5) consumer repoints 7 repos x 60m = 420m, (6) final grep 30m. DEPS: SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT (Paused; spiral's own polyglot references, now a sub-goal of this epic's phase 5), soft COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE and LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL (both decide what of spiral is an example, which this epic's examples-lab half needs). LOAD light (it's file moves and builds on copies), ASSIGNEE agent, TEAM main (repoint edits go to each repo's team).")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_3 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 3u32, "2026-10-27T10:28Z", "main", "10-27 06:28 main: phase-5 input from tibia (ack 10-27 06:2x). tibia's polyglot consumers are scripts/build.ps1, init.ps1, workflow.ps1 and publish.ps1, plus apps/arena/build.ps1 and apps/canary/build.ps1. apps/arena/build.ps1 dot-sources deps/polyglot/scripts/core.ps1 and runs first in every tibia gate, so its repoint needs a full tibia gate on a copy; tibia proves each repoint itself when it's due. Also from the 06:2x census: polyglot/scripts/core.ps1 is already a shim that dot-sources deps/spiral/scripts/core.ps1 (spiral's shared helpers). So phase 3 for core.ps1 is a repoint to spiral's scripts/core.ps1 (or a one-line i574n.github shim), not a move of code.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_4 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 4u32, "2026-10-27T10:32Z", "main", "10-27 06:32 main: phase 2 drift census (by file stem and by function definition, PowerShell AST) over the four script homes: i574n.github/scripts 21 scripts, spiral/apps/compiler/tmp/scripts 43, polyglot/scripts 15, spiral/scripts 13. STEMS in more than one home: only the per-repo standard entry points build, init, outdated, publish and workflow (every repo has one by the sibling convention, and all differ), plus core (polyglot's 13-line shim over spiral's 423-line scripts/core.ps1). No script was copied between homes, so tonight's job-runner tools (serial-runner, queue-serial, job-stop, watch-ids and the rest) have no second copy anywhere. FUNCTIONS (123 definitions): CheckToml is byte-identical in polyglot/scripts/outdated.ps1 and spiral/scripts/outdated.ps1, and the polyglot copy goes with polyglot. Get-FileSha256 has two different bodies in compiler-tmp env.ps1 and test.ps1, and Resolve-Results two in ci-classify.ps1 and compare-runs.ps1; both are compiler-internal duplication, flagged to COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE. Verdict: moving polyglot's scripts into i574n.github adds no duplicate as long as each standard entry point merges into i574n.github's own and core.ps1 becomes a repoint to spiral's.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_5 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 5u32, "2026-10-27T12:00Z", "main", "10-27 08:00 main: phase 1, first pass (identity test): 302 polyglot files outside deps and generated folders (target, node_modules, dist, bin, obj, .history), each hashed against byte-identical copies in spiral, dice, alphabet, i574n.github, vault, tibia, kit, blog, dir-tree-html, x and fiscal. Only 9 are ELSEWHERE by identity, all repo config (.editorconfig, .gitattributes, .markdownlint.json, LICENSE, requirements.txt, rust-toolchain.toml, plus one file each in apps/chat and apps/spiral). Everything substantive is unique to polyglot: lib/rust 81, lib/typescript 90, lib/fsharp 18, lib/math 5; apps chat 12, spiral 37, parser 5, ipfs 4, perf 2, scheduler 2; scripts 17 (incl. build.livemd, core.ps1 the shim, dep_hyperui.ps1); workflows 2, devcontainer 2, flake 2. So no substantive file is an exact duplicate; the next pass classifies by content and use (MOVE or DROP), starting with lib/rust and lib/typescript, the two largest. Table: TEMP polyglot-inventory.tsv (Top, Path, Twin).")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_6 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 6u32, "2026-10-27T12:53Z", "main", "10-27 08:53 main: phase 1, second pass (content and use), the two largest folders. lib/rust (81 files: 48 .rs, 20 .fsx) and lib/typescript (90: 54 .ts, 24 .fsx) each hold only a fable/ subfolder: vendored Fable runtime libraries (fable_modules/fable-library-rust and its TS twin) plus generated .fsx. lib/fsharp is 18 files (8 .livemd, 6 .fsx, 3 .rs); lib/math is 9 files, with built .dll/.exe/.pdb under dist/ (generated output). The org dropped Fable, so these classify as DROP once no consumer is left. But two consumers still build against lib/rust's Fable library through a Cargo path dependency: tapas2 (i574n, Cargo.toml:16 fable_library_rust = { path = \"deps/polyglot/lib/rust/fable/fable_modules/fable-library-rust\" }, and its contract/build.ps1 dot-sources deps/polyglot/scripts/core.ps1) and mechahaze album1 (an outside org, apps/album1/Cargo.toml:9, the same path dependency). Both are outside the census's repo list, which covered only i574n's main repos. So (a) phase 5's consumer list gains tapas2 and album1, and (b) lib/rust is blocked on their Fable exit: each either drops Fable (no-Fable direction) or vendors fable-library-rust itself, and that is their teams' call, not a move into i574n.github. The grep found no consumer of lib/typescript's Fable library outside polyglot/deps/Fable itself. Next pass: apps/spiral (37), apps/chat (12), scripts (17).")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_7 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 7u32, "2026-10-27T12:56Z", "main", "10-27 08:56 main: phase 1, third pass: apps and scripts. PROPOSED classes; the examples-lab layout in i574n.github is the user's call before anything moves. apps/chat (12 files, live; last commit 10-27): MOVE as one unit (contract, contract tests, Cargo workspace, .cargo config); its home is the open question (i574n.github examples, or a repo of its own like dice). apps/perf (Perf.spi) and apps/scheduler (Tasks.spi), 2 files each: small Spiral programs, examples-lab candidates. apps/spiral (37 files): all under temp/, experiments (cube in C, .fsx, Lua and Python with a build.ps1; a Blender build.py). The spiral matrix's native_cube_* samples already cover the cube on every backend, so this is ELSEWHERE for the cube and examples or DROP for the rest. apps/parser (5: JsonParser.fs and Parser.fs with their .livemd, last 10-07): F# from the Fable era, DROP under the no-Fable direction unless a consumer appears. apps/ipfs (4: a Bun index.ts with package.json): examples or DROP after a consumer check. scripts (17: build/init in .ps1 and .livemd, core.ps1 = the shim over spiral's core.ps1, dep_hyperui, dep_spiral, dep_spiral_extension and the rest): each standard entry point merges into i574n.github's own (drift census n4), and core.ps1 becomes a repoint. Open user decisions, asked together when phase 3 starts: the examples/ layout, and chat's home.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_8 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 8u32, "2026-10-27T13:22Z", "main", "10-27 09:22 main: examples-lab census, spiral side (the user's 06:0x ask: anything in spiral or other repos that could also move to i574n.github). spiral top level: apps (10,627 files), lib (1,146), lab (289 in 50 folders after tonight's drains), scripts (16), plus config folders. Inside apps: cells, compiler, spiral and zed are products. plot and wasm are referenced by spiral's own CI/scripts, so they stay (CI builds them). lisp (6 files: a Lisp written in Spiral as 3 .spl plus livemd, a Python helper and build.ps1; last 10-19; no CI or script reference) is an examples-lab CANDIDATE. apps/cells-nightpack is an EMPTY folder (0 entries, untracked, named by no script in spiral or i574n.github); it's checked for live owners before removal. lab: drafts land in their home repo by rule, so only folders that are genuinely examples (not WIP) are candidates; LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL judges each one, and none has been classified as an example yet. Compiler fixtures (apps/compiler/tmp/samples and tests) stay: they're the matrix's oracle input. Shortlist so far for the lab, pending the user's layout decision: polyglot apps/perf, apps/scheduler, maybe apps/ipfs (n7), and spiral apps/lisp.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_9 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 9u32, "2026-10-30T22:51Z", "main", "10-30 18:51 main, R4 DECIDED (placement is answered by rules, not left as a user call; BACKLOG-DANGLING-1030): the examples lab is i574n.github/examples/<name>/, one self-contained folder per example (its .spi + build.ps1). build.ps1 reaches the sibling spiral checkout through ../../../spiral (the same relative pattern as i574n.github/scripts/pins), so no deps/ copy. polyglot keeps its copies until the retire step archives the repo (archive, never delete). FIRST SLICE moved (unstaged): examples/perf (Perf.spi 23,420 B, edition 3, byte-identical to polyglot apps/perf) and examples/scheduler (Tasks.spi 5,969 B, edition 3), each with build.ps1 repointed (core.ps1 and run_notebook.ps1 from ../../../spiral; both paths resolve). PROOF next: run each build.ps1 (a Cells notebook run) after main's Cells window 3; pass = notebook exits 0. Still open: apps/chat (a NEAR contract with a Cargo workspace; it stays in polyglot until NEAR-CONTRACT-CRATES decides its home); apps/spiral temp/ experiments (drop or elsewhere, per n-1); apps/parser F# (drop under the no-Fable direction).")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_10 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 10u32, "2026-10-30T23:38Z", "main", "10-30 19:3x main: examples/perf from its new home: the notebook ran (Perf.spi.ipynb written 19:25) but exit 1 after 993 s: cell 22 (binary_search_tests, count = 10,000,000) hit the 300 s Cells cell timeout while the box was at 100% CPU (three main proofs plus fiscal and kit runs). It is a timing workload, so this is a load red, not a move regression; rerun it alone on a quiet box (or inside a short bench window). examples/scheduler passed 4/4 earlier.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_11 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 11u32, "2026-10-31T15:39Z", "main", "10-31 11:39 main, the two open decisions, from the tree (dangling check by stem across C:\\home\\git): (1) apps/parser (F#: Parser.fs, JsonParser.fs, their .livemd, build.ps1) can NOT be dropped yet: dice/scripts/init.ps1:28, alphabet/scripts/init.ps1:28, mechahaze-album1/scripts/init.ps1:29 and tapas2/scripts/init.ps1:22 still build it, and tapas2/contract/build.ps1:18 runs its DibParser to turn the .dib into .spi. i574n.github/scripts/spiral-independent/rewrite-deps.ps1:26 already strips that build line, but the migration hasn't been run in those repos. DECIDED: parser retires right after SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT's rewrite runs in those 4 repos (tapas2's .dib->spi step needs its .spi committed first). (2) apps/spiral/temp: cube (13 files) is referenced only by polyglot itself (scripts/symlinks.ps1:9, README.md:112) and blender (2) and extension (269 files, 25 MB, mostly untracked) by nothing: all three go with the polyglot archive, nothing to move. Still open: examples/perf's timing rerun on a quiet box (after kit's train6).")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_12 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 12u32, "2026-11-01T03:40Z", "main", "main 23:4x WIP groom (user 23:3x: drift/stall, too much waiting): Active -> Planned. apps/parser stays until dice/alphabet/mechahaze init.ps1 stop using it (n11); blocked by SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT (Paused, user batch).")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_13 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 13u32, "2026-11-01T14:35Z", "main", "main 10:3x (user 11-01: 'gotta check for the old tasks checking what's left to retire polyglot'). State: n11 found apps/parser still used by dice/alphabet/mechahaze init.ps1, and the migration waits on SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT (user batch). Also wanted from polyglot before retiring: its Nov-2025 state for CELLS-PLOT-EXPORT and ERL-VS-DIB-BENCH (the dib plotting/export reference), the Blender experiment (BLENDER-SAMPLE) and the Perf notebooks (PERF-FRAMEWORK-STUDY). NEXT STEP: a full census of polyglot's tracked folders by: still used (by whom) / moved / to move (target) / drop, written on this item.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_14 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 14u32, "2026-11-02T19:01Z", "main", "main 11-02 14:5x CENSUS of polyglot's tracked folders, with readers in sibling repos (git grep \"polyglot/<folder>\"; forks excluded). SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT is DONE for spiral and tibia (both deps\\polyglot links removed, tibia's init clones spiral directly; n36/n37), so these are the remaining readers:\n- STILL USED, migrate the reader first:\n  - scripts/ (17 files): build/init dot-sources in alphabet (apps/documents, apps/hangul build.ps1), dice (contract/build.ps1, contract/tests/build.ps1), dotfiles (dist/appdata/spiral/build.ps1), fc1943s.github, mechahaze-album1, tapas2, vault (init/publish), i574n.github (scripts/build.ps1). Fix = point each at deps/spiral/scripts/core.ps1, as tibia and regex do.\n  - apps/parser (5): init.ps1 of alphabet, dice, mechahaze-album1, tapas2; tapas2 contract/build.ps1 (DibParser). Retires once those init.ps1 stop building it (rewrite-deps.ps1 already strips the line).\n  - apps/spiral (36): dotfiles appdata build, mechahaze-album1 (apps/album1 build + init), tapas2 (contract build + init), vault (data/spiral/spiral.md docs).\n  - lib/fsharp (18): dice lib/fsharp (build.ps1 + .livemd), singularity Tidal.dib, tapas2 contract .rs.\n  - lib/math (5): only README mentions (fc1943s, i574n.github profile); its pyo3/mpmath harness is the zeta porting oracle, so it MOVES to lib/spiral/zeta with ZETA-NUMERIC-CORE.\n- ONLY THE BACKLOG MENTIONS IT (move or drop on decision): apps/chat (12), apps/perf (2; PERF-FRAMEWORK-STUDY), apps/scheduler (2).\n- NO READERS (drop at retire): apps/ipfs (4), examples (1), .devcontainer, .github, root files (16), workspace (2; only the .code-workspace files list it).\nORDER: (1) repoint the scripts/core.ps1 dot-sources in dice, alphabet, dotfiles, mechahaze-album1, tapas2, vault, i574n.github (alphabet mirrors dice); (2) their init.ps1 stop building apps/parser; (3) lib/math moves with zeta; (4) archive the rest. fc1943s.* repos are the dump (fc1943s-dump-i574n-destructive): leave them.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_15 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 15u32, "2026-11-02T19:02Z", "main", "main 11-02 15:0x STEP 1 started. polyglot/scripts/core.ps1 is a pure forwarder to spiral/scripts/core.ps1 (SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT n7), so repointing each dot-source at spiral is behaviour-preserving. DONE: dotfiles dist/appdata/spiral/build.ps1 (absolute path -> c:/home/git/spiral/scripts/core.ps1; parse ok; 0 polyglot sites left; unstaged). REMAINING sites (git grep polyglot/scripts/core.ps1): dice 12, alphabet 8 (mirror dice), mechahaze-album1 6, tapas2 6, vault 3 (one reaches it through deps/alphabet/deps/polyglot). Repos WITHOUT a deps/spiral link today: dice, tapas2, vault (alphabet and mechahaze-album1 have one). So each also needs its init.ps1 to clone or link spiral as deps/spiral, the way regex and tibia now do, and a local deps/spiral link for local builds. Prove each with its own build (dice/alphabet on the node). Next heartbeats: dice + alphabet as a pair, then mechahaze-album1, tapas2, vault.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_16 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 16u32, "2026-11-02T21:07Z", "main", "main 11-02 17:1x STEP 1 alphabet PROVEN on the node's real checkout (synced -Force, digest 57736BEE7E55D702, deps/spiral linked): apps/documents compiles (cargo Finished) and runs through the new paths; its one test row fails only because the node lacks crowbook (test.hangul.md + test.md.html come back Ok after main copied the box's hangulize.exe over; before that hangulize.exe was missing too, the node has no Go). apps/hangul: spiral-tests 2/2 passed; its livemd F# cell 'AssertAreEqual(국어, hanjaConvert 國語)' fails, and an in-job A/B with HEAD's build.ps1 + package.spiproj (the polyglot paths) fails IDENTICALLY, so it predates the rewrite (filed as a note here; the hanja table lookup misses, likely an encoding read of the cell source). vault repointed (POLYGLOT-READERS-PORT n2). mechahaze-album1 + tapas2 need a port, not a repoint: POLYGLOT-READERS-PORT.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_17 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 17u32, "2026-11-02T21:15Z", "main", "main 11-02 17:2x STEP 1 dice PROVEN on the node's real checkout (deps/spiral junction, the rewritten tree): contract build exit 0, spiral-tests 7/7 passed, 'RUST-OK dice/contract / the NEAR sandbox tests passed on dist/dice.wasm'. So dice + alphabet are done for step 1 (dice keeps deps/polyglot only for lib/fsharp Common.fs). Side fix in dice contract/build.ps1: ClearCargoTarget '../..' -> '..' (from contract/, '../..' is the folder above the repo, so the CI cleanup never reached dice's workspace target). Readers left after tonight: tapas2 (port in proof, POLYGLOT-READERS-PORT), dice lib/fsharp Common.fs, the docs-only mentions, i574n.github scripts/build.ps1.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_18 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 18u32, "2026-11-02T23:27Z", "main", "main 11-02 19:2x NO CONSUMER CLONES POLYGLOT ANY MORE (unstaged). (1) alphabet scripts/init.ps1: polyglot clone + 'pwsh ../../polyglot/scripts/init.ps1' replaced by spiral's own 'pwsh ../../spiral/scripts/init.ps1', the exact change dice's CI proved green tonight (run 41538911884); git grep polyglot in alphabet = 0. (2) i574n.github umbrella: scripts/build.ps1 no longer runs polyglot's build, outdated.ps1 no longer runs polyglot's outdated, and init.ps1 no longer clones polyglot (all parse; 0 polyglot refs in those 3 + the workflows). Readers left: vault/mechahaze-album1/tapas2 ported (unstaged), docs prose, and the inventory scripts that LIST polyglot as an org repo (pins.ps1, pages-sweep.ps1, recovered-drafts-census.ps1, remote.ps1's route check). Those stay while the repo exists. NEXT (step 3/4): lib/math moves with ZETA-NUMERIC-CORE; then archive polyglot's remaining folders (CELLS-PLOT-EXPORT reference, Blender, Perf notebooks noted in n13). Archiving the GitHub repo is the user's call (n1).")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_19 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 19u32, "2026-11-03T08:49Z", "main", "main 11-03 04:1x ORG EXIT DONE BY THE USER (11-03): polyglot left the i574n org and is now fc1943s/polyglot, with no redirect. The local C:\\home\\git\\polyglot stays as the SOURCE until every folder below is absorbed or ruled out; it is then deleted after a proper check (11-03 rule: hash/tree comparison against the new homes). CI and link fallout is ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT. ABSORPTION MAP (tracked files per folder, then owner):\napps/chat (12; the NEAR chat contract .spi + generated .rs) -> NEAR-CONTRACT-CRATES / NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS, destination i574n.github/apps/chat (this item's examples lab).\nlib/math (5) -> ZETA-NUMERIC-CORE (spiral lib), then ZETA-MEGA-RETIRE.\nlib/fsharp (18; Common.fs and friends, F#-era helpers) -> FSHARP-OUTSIDE-COMPILER decides per file: whatever a live fixture needs (Cells' document_test reads dice's own lib/fsharp, not polyglot's) is copied to its consumer, everything else is ruled out.\napps/perf (2) -> PERF-FRAMEWORK-STUDY (read as a reference, then ruled out).\napps/parser (5; FParsec era) -> FPARSEC-RETIRE / parsing lib, reference only.\napps/spiral (36; the Supervisor / old CLI) -> superseded by spiral's apps; rule out after a stem grep.\napps/ipfs (4), apps/scheduler (2), examples/elixir (1) -> UNOWNED, a triage step: keep as an i574n.github example if it still builds or teaches something, otherwise rule it out.\nscripts (17) -> superseded by spiral/scripts (core.ps1, init, publish); diff for any function that exists only here, then rule out.\nAlso referenced as a source: CELLS-PLOT-EXPORT (old plots), BLENDER-SAMPLE (Blender experiment), DIB-MODERNIZE (.dib remnants), all read from the local copy.\nNEXT: the triage step for ipfs/scheduler/elixir, then the ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT sweep.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_20 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 20u32, "2026-11-03T09:03Z", "tibia", "11-03 05:0x tibia: tibia's polyglot dependency census = NONE in sources. grep over tibia (deps/ excluded) finds polyglot only in README.md:256, which said init.ps1 'clones polyglot (which brings spiral) ... links both under deps/'. scripts/init.ps1 actually clones spiral only and links deps/spiral (plus Lua 5.1 and, via spiral's init-wgsl-run.ps1, Mesa Vulkan on Ubuntu). README fixed to match (unstaged). The local tibia/deps/polyglot link is unused by tibia's build and tests; only the node's consumer3 gate runner links it for spiral's process.spi route check, so tibia is not a blocker for retiring polyglot.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_21 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 21u32, "2026-11-03T09:36Z", "main", "main 11-03 05:4x TRIAGE of the 3 unowned folders. RULE, written first: keep what is Spiral or teaches something no kept repo has; rule out copies of third-party material and code for dead external services. (1) apps/ipfs (index.ts 15 lines + package.json, bun.lockb, build.ps1; last 10-07): a TypeScript uploader to nft.storage, whose classic upload API was sunset in 2024. Not Spiral; the NEAR chat contract computes its own CID (generate_cid). RULED OUT. (2) apps/scheduler (Tasks.spi 214 lines, last 10-25; build.ps1): a typed task-scheduling model (task_id/task_name nominals, recurrency_offset/fixed_recurrency unions over date_time). Typefeatureset-shaped domain code with no equivalent elsewhere. KEEP -> i574n.github/apps/scheduler, respelled to edition 3 with test blocks, proven by a gate, then the polyglot copy is ruled out. (3) examples/elixir/exercism.livemd (433 lines, last 10-07): Exercism's exercise text copied into the retired livemd format. RULED OUT. NEXT: move scheduler, then the per-folder rule-outs for lib/fsharp, apps/perf, apps/parser, apps/spiral and scripts (diff for unique functions first).")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_22 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 22u32, "2026-11-03T09:38Z", "main", "main 11-03 05:5x RULE-OUTS, checked. (a) scripts (17 files): function diff against spiral/scripts + lib/spiral (24 functions). Only 5 exist solely in polyglot: UpdateToml/UpdateJson (update.ps1: thin wrappers over 'cargo update' / 'bun update'), CheckJson (outdated.ps1, the JSON twin of spiral's CheckToml), and Resolve-PolyglotSpiralBundle / Ensure-SpiralRustCompiler (spiral-bundle.ps1, polyglot's own obsolete bundle). Nothing unique worth moving: RULED OUT. (b) lib/fsharp (18): no live reader in any i574n repo (the 11-03 full-repo grep: dice no longer references polyglot; the only hits are the fc1943s dump repos and singularity's playground data), so RULED OUT; FSHARP-OUTSIDE-COMPILER keeps dice's own lib/fsharp. (c) apps/spiral (36; Supervisor, old CLI): superseded by spiral's apps (cells, compiler, spiral) and referenced only in history comments: RULED OUT. STILL READ FROM THE LOCAL COPY, so the local C:\\home\\git\\polyglot is deleted only after these close: ZETA-NUMERIC-CORE (lib/math), NEAR-CONTRACT-CRATES (apps/chat), SCHEDULER-MODEL-MOVE (apps/scheduler), PERF-FRAMEWORK-STUDY (apps/perf, reference), FPARSEC-RETIRE (apps/parser, reference), compiler's extract-corpus 'user' corpus (polyglot@bb856d13), CELLS-PLOT-EXPORT (old plot reference). Progress 60 -> 70.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_23 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 23u32, "2026-11-03T11:37Z", "compiler", "11-03 07:5x compiler: the extract-corpus 'user' corpus no longer reads the local C:\\home\\git\\polyglot (done 05:4x, ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT n3). tmp/formatter/extract-corpus.ps1 clones https://github.com/fc1943s/polyglot bare with --filter=blob:none into LOCALAPPDATA/spiral-bin/corpus-src/polyglot.git on first use, at the same pinned bb856d13 (on fc1943s/main). End-to-end run: 86 files, 577,482 bytes, 0 content mismatches against the local copy, 1 MB clone. Strike it from the list of local-copy readers.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_24 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 24u32, "2026-11-03T12:42Z", "main", "main 11-03 08:5x PATH CORRECTION: the examples lab is i574n.github/examples/<name>/ (R4, 10-30; examples/perf and examples/scheduler already live there), not i574n.github/apps/. n21 and the apps/chat line said apps/; that wording produced a duplicate apps/scheduler, now folded into examples/scheduler (SCHEDULER-MODEL-MOVE n3). So apps/chat's destination is i574n.github/examples/chat when NEAR-CONTRACT-CRATES moves it (X-ON-NEAR is deferred by the user, so it stays in the local polyglot copy until then). SCHEDULER-MODEL-MOVE is closed: strike it from the local-copy readers.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_25 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 25u32, "2026-11-03T13:42Z", "tibia", "11-03 09:2x tibia, CORRECTION to n20 (tibia has no polyglot dependency): its SOURCES do not use polyglot, but tibia CI did bootstrap through polyglot until d4ad52ad (11-02 21:59), and the switch to spiral's init-app-build.ps1 is exactly where tibia's Ubuntu CI went red: 4 unchanged Lua-only test files now report unsupported and a Zig main fails (TIBIA-1-0-DOD n4). So retiring polyglot from tibia is not done until spiral's bootstrap provides what polyglot's did for these targets.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_26 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 26u32, "2026-11-03T13:58Z", "tibia", "11-03 09:5x tibia, follow-up to n25: the gap is exact. Polyglot init.ps1 built the Spiral CLI (deps/spiral/apps/spiral/build.ps1, line 151); spiral scripts/init-app-build.ps1 does not, so every app that switched to it loses its lua target on CI (cells runs lua via spiral lua). Tibia now builds the CLI itself in scripts/init.ps1 (unstaged). Other apps that moved to init-app-build need the same, or init-app-build should build the CLI (spiral-owned script, main lane decision).")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_27 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 27u32, "2026-11-03T14:03Z", "main", "main 11-03 10:0x FIXED IN ONE PLACE (unstaged, spiral): scripts/init-app-build.ps1 now builds the Spiral CLI when workspace/target/release/spiral[.exe] is missing, via apps/spiral/build.ps1 -fast 1 (the canonical release-unwind + mimalloc build; spiral's own workflow.ps1 runs the same call green on ubuntu-24.04 and windows-2025). This restores what polyglot init.ps1:151 did, so every init-app-build app (tibia, fiscal, blog, kit, x, html, regex) gets its lua/cuda cell targets back on CI (tibia n26 root cause). tibia's per-app copy stays harmless (same missing-exe guard). Turns green on the user's spiral push.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_28 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 28u32, "2026-11-03T18:43Z", "main", "main 11-03 14:4x LOCAL COPY CHECKED: C:\\home\\git\\polyglot is an exact mirror of https://github.com/fc1943s/polyglot branch main-i574n (HEAD 2fbb9ee2, 0 ahead / 0 behind after fetch, clean, 0 untracked non-ignored files). So nothing in it is unique: every 'reads the local copy' item can clone fc1943s instead (compiler's corpus already does). Deletion stays gated by n22's owners (ZETA-NUMERIC-CORE, NEAR-CONTRACT-CRATES, PERF-FRAMEWORK-STUDY, FPARSEC-RETIRE, CELLS-PLOT-EXPORT) for workflow continuity, not data loss. DANGER for whoever deletes it: polyglot\\deps\\spiral is a LINK to the live spiral tree (it measures 40 GB if followed) and apps/chat/contract/lib links back into polyglot/lib; never run 'git clean -X' or a following recursive delete there: remove the links first (pwsh 7.6 Remove-Item deletes a junction without following, verified on the box 11-03), then the folder. Disk isn't a reason to hurry: C: has 228 GB free.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_29 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 29u32, "2026-11-05T19:17Z", "main", "main 11-05 15:2x ORPHAN SWEEP: the deletion gate is WIDER than n22's five main items (all still Planned p=0..10). Live references outside polyglot: fc1943s.github/scripts/{build,init,publish,outdated,workflow}.ps1 + workflow.dib dot-source ../../polyglot/scripts/core.ps1 (publish.ps1:80 also runs polyglot/apps/dir-tree-html/dist/DirTreeHtml), fc1943s.code-workspace + fc1943s-deps.code-workspace open ../polyglot/{workspace,deps/*}, and The-Spiral-Language 2.fsproj:56 falls back to ../../polyglot/spiral/clr/clr.fsx. fc1943s.github is the user's dump repo (no destructive edits there), so deleting the local copy breaks the user's own fc1943s build. NEXT before any delete: either the user retires fc1943s.github's tooling or its core.ps1/nbs_header.ps1/dir-tree-html move into i574n.github. Active untouched 54 h -> Planned at 70.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_30 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 30u32, "2026-11-06T12:50Z", "main", "main 11-06 11:0x DoD backfill (kit lint): DoD: everything useful from polyglot has moved (to i574n.github or a descriptive repo), and polyglot is out of the org (done 11-03, user) with 0 dangling references in the own repos. Next step: grep the own repos for polyglot references and classify each.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_31 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 31u32, "2026-11-06T12:51Z", "main", "main 11-06 11:1x reference census (git grep -i polyglot, 11 own repos, backlog and generated graphs excluded): spiral 23, i574n.github 2, others 0. Fixed (unstaged): the org profile README linked https://i574n.github.io/polyglot/lib/math/math.spi.html, a 404 since polyglot left the org, and now links the same notebook's home https://i574n.github.io/spiral/lib/spiral/math.spi.html (200). Legitimate and kept: spiral compiler comments explaining compat with polyglot's Supervisor host, the cells polyglot_root compat option and its tests, sample strings where 'polyglot' is the domain word (contract_*_polyglot_* samples), the formatter's user-corpus clone of fc1943s/polyglot (the user's archive), an example heading. DoD met for references; the move half is done since 11-03. Proof: 0 dangling polyglot links left in the own repos.")
inl note_of_kit_pending_dangling_1 () = Note ("KIT-PENDING-DANGLING", 1u32, "2026-10-27T10:24Z", "kit", "06:2x kit, from main's heal request (user 10-27 06:0x: 'check those pending files dangling, heal what's generating it'). Generator: workspace_primitives/files.spi replace_file_checked wrote <path>.<pid>.pending and then renamed it, so a writer killed between the two (job timeout, tree kill) left a file no later writer ever looked for (every writer has a new pid). Main archived and removed the two found (agile.spi.115112.pending, agile.spi.78508.pending; superseded, verified). Fix, decided against main's suggested sweep of dead-pid siblings, because the lib has no Rust directory listing or process liveness: the temporary becomes the fixed <path>.pending (pending_path). A killed writer now leaves at most one copy per file, and the next replacement overwrites and renames it, so nothing accumulates. It also removes a host macro (std::process::id). Two concurrent writers of one file now meet on the same temporary, and the existing readback check reports ReadbackMismatch; before, both renames succeeded and one update was silently lost. Draft: kit scratch clean/kit-rename/pending-fixed-name.do (files.spi + a test in toolchain.spi: every_writer_of_one_file_shares_one_pending_copy). Proven on a full src copy: applies 2/2; agile_todo_roots compiles, 422 lines against 425 live, process::id references 1 -> 0. workspace_primitives is inlined, so the next release regenerates every crate reaching it. Lands after kit-release-SLICES drops its lease. No .gitignore entry: a dangling copy should stay visible.")
inl note_of_kit_pending_dangling_2 () = Note ("KIT-PENDING-DANGLING", 2u32, "2026-10-27T14:33Z", "kit", "10:3x kit: a bug in my own landed test, caught by the literal-set node run: toolchain.spi's every_writer_of_one_file_shares_one_pending_copy is ETY-UnboundVariable 'files' (a test block cannot reach a sibling module by its bare name; --backend builds skip tests, so only a notebook catches it). Fix staged as clean/kit-rename/pending-test-fix.do: the test moves into files.spi beside pending_path, with a plain failwith check (dry-run 2/2 on the probe). It applies after the SLICES2 rerun, because touching workspace_primitives now would void that rerun's regen-skip freshness proof. toolchain.spi is not in its notebook set.")
inl note_of_kit_pending_dangling_3 () = Note ("KIT-PENDING-DANGLING", 3u32, "2026-10-29T12:53Z", "kit", "10-29 08:5x kit, wipe check: the lost pending-test-fix.do needs no redo, because both halves are in the live tree. workspace_primitives/files.spi:26 has pending_path (the fixed <path>.pending), and replace_file_checked uses it (:33); the test every_writer_of_one_file_shares_one_pending_copy sits beside it in files.spi:29 with a plain failwith check, and toolchain.spi no longer has it. No dangling *.pending files under the backlog or %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit (checked now). Closes once TRAIN3 (job-1793275863025, a full regen of every owner) installs and workspace_primitives/files.spi passes as its own notebook run after the install. Correction 09:0x: it is NOT in TRAIN3's candidate set, which holds only packages with uncommitted changes.")
inl note_of_kit_pending_dangling_4 () = Note ("KIT-PENDING-DANGLING", 4u32, "2026-10-29T15:41Z", "kit", "10-29 11:4x kit: closed. Installed in TRAIN3 (kit.exe CD2F0D1A, 11:35; the full regen republished every crate reaching workspace_primitives). workspace_primitives/files.spi ran as its own notebook (job-1793288400504): 1/1 pass, every_writer_of_one_file_shares_one_pending_copy included. No dangling *.pending under the backlog, before or after today's agile writes (TRAIN3 closeout row). Done.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_1 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 1u32, "2026-10-27T10:51Z", "x", "2026-10-27 06:51 x: the one heavy step the 85% client items wait on. verify15 (job-1793096804459) is running on the tree with the split, Bluesky A/B'/D/S1/R1, defuse wire v3, the perf fix and today's test fixes.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_2 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 2u32, "2026-10-27T12:34Z", "x", "2026-10-27 08:32 x: verify16b sim part (job-1793101238694, x/scripts/verify.ps1 -Part sim -Accept, pinned compiler): the Gleam frames built (11,469 lines -> 15 modules, largest 957), x-compat on the sim 0, and every sim fixture was re-accepted from the fixed split_cell (sim-small/stress/lost/gap world+expected, thread-oauth1, prelude events/final/parity; review pending). mix test 42/45, the same on both passes. Two tests timed out at 60 s (spiral_test 'a corpus run and the scenario facade draw the same deliveries', xsim_test 'evicting withdrawn results...'), and the known load-sensitive 'results assigned to whoever asked ... surface stale revisions' (an 80 ms executor against a 100 ms harvest window) passed where it should flag. The node was saturated (main: 9 jobs, 100% CPU), and verify15 passed 45/45 with the same split_cell code on a quieter node, so contention is the first suspect, per the retry rule. Open question to measure, not assume: the timeout stacks sit in the new defusing path (defused_dots_by -> pieces_from -> run_glyph -> ascii_of inside split_cell, which now posts before splitting), so the sim does more work per cell than before the split. Next: rerun only the sim part when the node is below about 70% CPU; if the timeouts repeat, time Frames.split per cell before and after posting.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_3 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 3u32, "2026-10-27T12:38Z", "x", "2026-10-27 08:38 x: reviewed verify16b's accepted sim fixtures against the tree. Every change comes from links-only defusing: the zero-width spaces are gone (sim-small 6 -> 0, lost 4 -> 0, gap 8 -> 0, stress 518 -> 0, prelude events 17 -> 0; none of the inputs has a known-TLD dot or a sigil), cut points move because posts weigh less (prelude events: '\\n    listm.foldBack' now fits in post 1), and stress world ids shift by one with fewer frames. The shape is OK, but NOT landed: the mirror was synced at 07:37, before prelude.spi step 2 changed spread's text, which these fixtures quote. The next verify re-accepts from the current tree, and those fixtures land after the same review.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_4 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 4u32, "2026-10-27T13:21Z", "x", "2026-10-27 09:20 x: generated outputs LANDED in the tree (unstaged), fixing the CI xc-windows 'couldn't find domains.rs'. x/scripts/verify.ps1 -Part regen (job-1793105792101, first real use of i574n.github/scripts/node-proof.ps1: both syncs REMOTE-SYNC-OK, compiler pinned 4FD712E9E357) regenerated all 28 client crates with 0 failures. Compared with the same-compiler base (proof 7's split tree): api is unchanged and keeps its file; 25 crates CHANGED (the WIP touches prelude, wire and glyphs, which most crates open) and 2 are NEW (domains 334, requests 794); all 27 copied into apps/client/<crate>/<crate>.rs. Sizes: write 875 (the Bluesky with_site fix added about 160; R1's bound is 900), posted 899 (at the bound), xc 969, digest 954; 0 over 1000. Cargo.lock gains only xc_requests and xc_domains (+15 lines, through cargo metadata --offline; no version moved; old lock backed up in x-backup-1027-0355). Note verify16b client's first pass failed on infrastructure, not code: Cells stopped on 'Getting kino (Hex package)' (node network flaky today, like the gh TLS timeouts); its second pass is running. Next: one full verify of exactly this tree when the node frees.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_5 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 5u32, "2026-10-27T14:55Z", "x", "2026-10-27 10:55 x: verify17 verdict (job-1793108152156; the tree as of 09:28, pinned compiler). GREEN parts: client gate (28 crates, 0 over 1000) and x-compat 0 on both passes; e2e 153 requests; sim ExUnit 45/45 on both sim passes (so the 42/45 in verify16b was node load); corpus commute ok (699 s, 350 s per schedule); the real-Cells executor run passed; sim x-compat 0. RED, three causes, none in xc: (1) my e2e check read stdout (.Raw) for an stderr message (fixed in the tree after the sync); (2) verify.ps1 accepted the e2e tutorial BEFORE the sim accept regenerated the sim world fixtures that the tutorial's 'xc thread 3000001' step reads, so the plain pass found that step DIFFERENT (fixed: the sim accept now runs first); (3) apps/sim/build.ps1's tampered-thread negative control silently stopped working when oauth1.spi lost its string asserts in the 10-25 lib move (only '_assert_eq 40i32' is left), so replacing '_assert_eq \"' changed nothing and the tampered thread passed. Fixed: the tamper now appends a test that must fail (1i32 |> _assert_eq 2i32), so thread_run must reject it whatever the file asserts. Nothing landed from verify17's outputs (its README accept preceded its sim accept, and the tree has moved since); verify18 runs on the current tree with the fixed order and lands one consistent set.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_6 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 6u32, "2026-10-27T16:06Z", "x", "2026-10-27 12:06 x: closure rule for the 18 dependents, written before verify19 (job-1793116068742) finishes. GREEN means all of: verify exit 0; sim accept and plain sim build exit 0 (ExUnit 45/45, commute ok, thread_run pass, and the tamper rejected with same_cells=false); client gate with every crate <= 1000; x-compat 0 on both packages; every client notebook total with failed 0; e2e with no FAILED line and no DIFFERENT step on the plain pass. On GREEN, (a) land verify19's outputs with node-proof -Land x-verify19 -From C:\\home\\remote-stage\\xv19-out -Repo x: review the report, then -Apply; any CONFLICT is resolved by hand first. (b) Close at 100: SIM-WORLD-SPIRAL, SIM-RUNNER-CORE-SPIRAL, X-GENERIC-TO-LIB, X-PER-ACCOUNT-MIN-1, X-PROOF-SCRIPTS-IN-REPO, X-NOTEBOOK-ASSERT, X-DEFUSE-EDGE-TESTS (only if defuse, tlds and splitter appear among the notebook totals), X-LIB-FIRST-PRELUDE, X-COMPAT-VS-POSTABLE (then tell main: unblocks tibia), X-STRING-SLICE-SITES, X-SIM-ANYDOT-SWEEP, X-README-WIP-SYNC, X-REQUESTS-REVIEW (with write.rs landed), X-SITE-E2E-REVIEW, X-STUB-WEIGHTED-LIMIT, X-SPLIT-ON-NO-ARRAY, X-E2E-SAYS-HELPER and ORG-NODE-PROOF-LAND (after its first real -Apply). (c) X-TUTORIAL-DEFUSE-STEP closes only after a hand review of the accepted links.txt step: a ZWSP before .com and after @, none in listm.foldBack or x.io. (d) X-DEFUSE-LINKS-ONLY stays open on its other deps (SPIRAL-PATH-SYNTAX, SPIRAL-ZWSP-TRANSPARENT). (e) XSIM-GLEAM-SPLIT-BENCH closes once its generated Gleam lands. NOT GREEN: nothing closes; fix the cause, then a new verify.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_7 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 7u32, "2026-10-27T20:56Z", "x", "2026-10-27 16:56 x: verify20 (job-1793123162251) NOT GREEN: (1) token/token's renewal test failed with memo_hits 0 (verify20 synced before the token fix; this refutes my stale-memo guess, which I retracted to main), and (2) it hit its 3 h cap (exit 124) in the final sim pass on a loaded node. Root cause of the failures surfacing one per verify: Invoke-SpiralTests stopped at the first failing notebook, so later ones were neither passed nor failed (token sits after defuse). Fixed at main's suggestion: every notebook runs, each prints passed/FAILED, and the run throws at the end naming all failures. verify21b (job-1793134676549, 6 h cap, manifest x-verify21b) carries the defuse and token fixes plus the run-all gate; closure follows note 6's rule.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_8 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 8u32, "2026-10-27T23:50Z", "x", "2026-10-27 19:50 x: verify21b (job-1793134676549) NOT GREEN, stopped: the client x-compat found one cell over weight (token.spi:153, 284 > 272), my token test edit, which I hadn't run the real x-compat on. That check precedes the notebooks, so they did not run. Everything else it reached was green: sim accept 45/45, gate 28 crates 0 over, e2e accept 2 of 37, the tampered thread rejected on same_cells. Fixed by moving the CR rendering into a shown_cr helper outside the cell; the real x-compat run locally (same DLL 4FD712E9E357) now reports 0 findings in 42 client and 24 sim files. verify22 (job-1793145082977, 6 h cap, manifest x-verify22) carries everything; closure follows note 6's rule, landing via node-proof -Land x-verify22 -From C:\\home\\remote-stage\\xv22-out -Repo x.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_9 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 9u32, "2026-10-28T00:15Z", "x", "2026-10-27 20:15 x: ADDENDUM to note 6's closure rule, before any verify22 result. Seven more rows close at 100 on the same GREEN: X-INVARIANTS-ROW-KIND, X-SIM-RUNNER-CRASHES, X-PAGING-GUARD, X-TOKEN-REFRESH-SAFE, X-LOOKUP-LIMITS and X-READ-BUDGET (their 'Done =' named 10-24 verify jobs that never went green; deps re-pointed from X-DONE, the epic they roll into, to X-WIP-VERIFY), plus X-READ-BUDGET's own condition: review the README answers that the e2e accept rewrote. X-GRANULAR-HEAL closes only after a verify that includes tonight's wire.spi reply_record heal (verify22 synced before it) and a wire.rs regen. X-SIM-FRAMES-GLEAM-IMPORTS was closed tonight on the existing evidence (frames compiles; sim 45/45 in every run today).")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_10 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 10u32, "2026-10-28T01:50Z", "x", "2026-10-27 21:50 x: verify22 (job-1793145082977) STOPPED at 21:4x before its verdict: it synced before tonight's wire reply_record heal, the CJK/emoji and RT:@ sigil-defuse fixes, and the 900 s cell budgets that the bench showed rust+gleam notebooks need under this load (its splitter/reading/defuse cells would time out at 300 s). verify23 (job-1793152313075, 8 h cap, manifest x-verify23) carries all of it. The closure rule (notes 6 and 9) now applies to verify23, and X-GRANULAR-HEAL and X-DEFUSE-EDGE-TESTS close on it too, since it carries their changes.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_11 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 11u32, "2026-10-28T06:02Z", "x", "2026-10-28 02:02 x: verify23 (job-1793152313075, 14615 s) NOT GREEN on one cause: client gate 'posted 1034 lines OVER 1000' (tonight's sigil-defuse fixes grew it from 899), and the gate runs before the client notebooks, so those did not run. Everything else it reached was green: sim accept 45/45, the e2e accept (2 of 37 tutorial outputs rewritten), plain sim build exit 0 with all 23 sim notebooks passed and the per-module lines working, and the tampered thread rejected on same_cells=false. Fix: X-POSTED-MARGIN's planned split into a new xc_entities crate (note 3 there); regen measuring as job-1793167383150, then verify24 carries it. New untracked folder for the user's commit: apps/client/entities/.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_12 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 12u32, "2026-10-28T08:07Z", "x", "2026-10-28 04:07 x: verify24 (job-1793167893768, 6798 s) NOT GREEN on one notebook: the new entities/entities.spi test used zero_width_space without opening glyphs (Unbound), now fixed. Everything else was green: gate 29 crates 0 over (posted 555 after the X-POSTED-MARGIN split), the e2e accept, 16 client notebooks before entities passed, sim build exit 0 with all 23 sim notebooks passed, and the tamper rejection. It also exposed a second hole in MY run-all gate: the client loop STOPPED at entities, with no FAILED line and no later notebooks run. Spiral's Invoke-Block calls 'exit' (core.ps1 line 100) on a failure when OnError is Stop in a non-interactive host, and no try/catch can catch an exit; my 16:5x stub test modelled the failure as a throw, so it never went through that path. Fixed: Invoke-SpiralTests now runs the notebook runner directly and reads $LASTEXITCODE. Re-proven through the REAL path: a real child pwsh with a stub run_notebook.ps1 that exits 1 for module b ran all of a,b,c,d, marked b FAILED, and threw '1 of 4 notebooks failed: b'. Real x-compat 0 in 43 files. verify25 (job-1793174907446, manifest x-verify25) carries both fixes; closure per notes 6, 9 and 10.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_13 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 13u32, "2026-10-28T10:31Z", "x", "2026-10-28 06:31 x groom: ADDENDUM to the closure rule (notes 6, 9, 10), written before verify25 reports. Also close at 100 on the same GREEN: X-E2E-NON-ASCII, X-EMOJI-WEIGHT and X-THREAD-RESUME (re-pointed from X-DONE today; their e2e steps run in every verify), X-POSTED-MARGIN, and X-E2E-SAYS-HELPER. After the reviewed node-proof -Land x-verify25 -Apply: ORG-NODE-PROOF-LAND (first real apply), XSIM-GLEAM-SPLIT-BENCH (generated Gleam landed), then SIM-GLEAM-PACKAGES. X-GRANULAR-HEAL closes on the verify after verify25 (its 4 lint heals came after verify25's sync).")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_14 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 14u32, "2026-10-28T11:09Z", "x", "2026-10-28 06:50 x: CLOSED by X-WIP-VERIFY's pre-registered rule. verify25 (node job-1793174907446, pinned compiler 4FD712E9E357) GREEN on every clause of X-WIP-VERIFY note 6: exit 0; sim accept and plain sim build exit 0 (ExUnit 45/45, corpus commute ok, thread_run pass, tamper rejected with same_cells=false); client gate 29 crates 0 over 1000; x-compat 0 in 43 client and 24 sim files; all 42 client and 23 sim notebooks passed, 0 failing totals; plain-pass e2e 37 of 37 tutorial steps same, 0 FAILED, 153 stub requests. Outputs landed three-way (node-proof -Land x-verify25: 21 files plus 19 Gleam modules, 0 conflicts; net.rs held back because its source changed after the sync, so verify26 lands it).")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_15 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 15u32, "2026-10-28T11:38Z", "x", "2026-10-28 07:38 x: ADDENDUM before verify27/28 report. verify27 (job-1793185923019; installed compiler A4E480202BD4, pre-respell tree with the lint heals) closes X-GRANULAR-HEAL if GREEN by note 6's clauses and confirms the compiler's three edition-3 features functionally (reported to the compiler team). verify28 (job-1793187520986; the same compiler on the respelled tree) closes X-EDITION3-RESPELL and X-DEFUSE-LINKS-ONLY if GREEN; its outputs land three-way through node-proof -Land x-verify28 (report, review, -Apply). If verify28 is green, verify27's outputs are NOT landed: verify28's are the same compiler on the newer tree.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_16 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 16u32, "2026-10-29T11:44Z", "x", "2026-10-29 07:41 x: verify27/28 (10-28) both hit their 8h cap (exit 124) from NODE OVERLOAD, not a defect. On 10-28 the node carried both verifies plus tibia lib gates (4.6h each) and fiscal jobs. verify28's sim corpus was still running at the cap (verify25 did its 2 schedules in 577 s), and the 42/45 and 38/45 sim accepts were ExUnit 60s timeouts; the later plain mix test passed 45/45, all 42 client notebooks passed, and the e2e accepted 1 of 37 ('xc thread 3000001'). verify29 (node job-1793273389666, mirror xv29, compiler A4E480202BD4, 8h cap) replaces both. It was synced at 07:27 with the respell, the xc :~ headroom edit, and main's cells/dictm fixes. Per main (10-29), X-DEFUSE-LINKS-ONLY closes with it. Closure rule = n6/n9/n10/n13/n15 applied to verify29: GREEN closes X-GRANULAR-HEAL, X-EDITION3-RESPELL and X-DEFUSE-LINKS-ONLY; outputs land three-way via node-proof -Land x-verify29 -From C:\\home\\remote-stage\\xv29-out -Repo x. The manifest was rewritten at 07:28 after a node-proof -LandRepos comma bug, now fixed in i574n.github/scripts/node-proof.ps1.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_17 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 17u32, "2026-10-29T14:14Z", "x", "2026-10-29 10:4x x: ADDENDUM to the closure rule, written BEFORE verify29 reports (pre-registered). Context: verify29 (job-1793273389666) passed sim accept 45/45, the client gate (29 crates, 0 over), x-compat, the e2e accept (1 README answer rewritten: the respell's '.'->'::' inside the prelude-text fixture, benign, reviewed 08:3x) and the plain e2e (153 stub requests, 0 FAILED). It is now in the client notebooks (7 of 42 passed, 0 failed at 2h42m), on a node at 100% CPU with 6 other jobs, while verify25 needed 2.5h end to end. If verify29 hits its 8h cap: the phases it reported green STAND. A follow-up job on the SAME mirror xv29, with the tree unchanged (a re-sync must print the same digest, or the follow-up is void), runs exactly the not-yet-reported clauses: the remaining client notebooks via verify.ps1 -Notebooks <unrun list>, then the plain sim build (ExUnit, corpus commute, sim notebooks) and -Out for the three-way landing. Together they close per n6/n9/n10/n13/n15. A notebook that FAILED in verify29 is not rerun into green: it is a RED, diagnosed first. Asked fiscal (5 of 7 node jobs) to cap at 2 until verify29 reports.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_18 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 18u32, "2026-10-29T16:31Z", "x", "2026-10-29 12:3x x: COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE follow-up (main applied it 12:3x: apps/compiler/tmp/scripts -> apps/compiler/scripts, with forwarding stubs that write a notice to stderr). x had 3 callers of the old env.ps1; all now dot-source apps/compiler/scripts/env.ps1, keeping SPIRAL_WORKSPACE_ROOT = apps/compiler/tmp (the bundle root did not move): scripts/gate.ps1:14 (the client crate gate), apps/sim/build.ps1 (toolchain block) and scripts/sim-shell.ps1. Why not leave the stubs: a stderr line inside 2>&1 pipelines under ErrorActionPreference Stop can turn into a terminating error. Checked: the new path resolves the same package dir and the installed DLL with no stderr; a full scan of x's *.ps1/*.yml (19 files) shows 0 old callers. None of these is a verify output, so verify29's three-way land is unaffected; the NEXT verify runs all three on the real path.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_19 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 19u32, "2026-10-29T17:16Z", "x", "2026-10-29 13:1x x: verify29 GREEN (see X-EDITION3-RESPELL's closing note for every clause); it closed X-GRANULAR-HEAL, X-EDITION3-RESPELL and X-DEFUSE-LINKS-ONLY, and its 20 outputs landed with 0 conflicts. Applied AFTER the land, as pre-registered: LIB-PROCESS-COUNTER's x half (net.spi 48466BA9 -> 4D3AB954) and CELLS-EVERYWHERE's fields.spi program. Both, plus the COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE path updates (n18), are proven by the next x verify, which runs on the installed pack-6b compiler once the node has it.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_20 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 20u32, "2026-10-29T18:38Z", "x", "2026-10-29 14:5x x: verify30 (job-1793295825981, pack-6b 9895730DAE80) RED on two causes, both fixed, neither from the counter or the respell. (1) MINE: the fields.spi test cell I added for CELLS-EVERYWHERE weighed 287 > 272 (one post minus the k/n header), and I had not run x-compat on the draft (the n8 lesson again). Split into two tests (a_payload_keeps_the_blank_defaults, empty_external_text_is_none); the real x-compat on pack-6b now reads 0 findings in 43 files (local, 5 s). Rule for myself from now on: run the installed compiler's --x-compat on apps/client and apps/sim/spi before launching any verify. (2) LOAD: sim accept 43/45, both failures ExUnit.TimeoutError at the 60 s default (XsimTest's correct-runner and eviction tests, async beside 16 cases on a node at 100%), the same as verify27/28. By SIM-IN-SPIRAL n64's rule (a deadline bounding an expected completion is raised; one whose expiry is the asserted outcome stays short), XsimTest gets @moduletag timeout: 300_000; its sleeps simulate slow executors and assert no timing. Everything else verify30 reached was green: 29 crates 0 over, 162 files 0 over. verify31 (job-1793299160741, pack-6b, 8h cap, mirror xv30 re-synced) carries both fixes; closure per n6/n9/n10/n13/n15/n17.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_21 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 21u32, "2026-10-29T19:57Z", "x", "2026-10-29 16:1x x: verify31 (job-1793299160741, pack-6b) went red on a COMPILER defect, not on x: xc_net failed with rustc E0599 (RequestBuilder has no clone). Root cause by the compiler lane (RUST-HOST-MOVE-ONLY): ureq's RequestBuilder was missing from codegen's move-only host types, and the clone-stripping post-pass bailed out of exchange because the compiler's own literal cache line (for the new 'xc_requests' argument of process_counter_add) looks like a closure. Reproduced locally from the exact source (evidence: C:\\home\\data\\x-evidence\\verify31-net-clone). Workaround in x (tree, unstaged): posted's branches now return the http_reply instead of a builder (post_builder_for removed), giving 0 non-Clone branch clones on 6b (scan positive-controlled). x-compat 0 on client (43 files) and sim (29). The compiler fix is verified on x's real failing source with the candidate (2 clones -> 0) and rides pack 8. Earlier in verify31: sim accept 45/45 (the ExUnit deadline fix works), x-compat 0, gate 29 crates 0 over. verify32 (job-1793303169424, 6b, re-synced after main's lib gap) carries the workaround; closure per n6..n17, and it is also the pack-6b re-proof of the three items closed on verify29.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_22 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 22u32, "2026-10-29T23:38Z", "x", "2026-10-29 19:38 x: verify32 (job-1793303169424, running for 3h50m) logged '** (Mix) .../apps/client/posts.spi: Spiral cell timed out after 300s; the process tree was killed', after both release builds finished (5m48s and 5m02s) on a node at 100% CPU. Cause class: LOAD. posts.spi had no budget in its header, so it ran at Cells' 300 s default, while 7 client notebooks (defuse, glyphs, paging, protocol, reading, splitter, tlds) carry --timeout 900000. By SIM-IN-SPIRAL n64 (a deadline bounding an expected completion is raised), posts.spi's header is now '///- --package . --timeout 900000' (unstaged). verify32's final verdict is still pending; if this is its only red, it is a load VOID for posts, not a code finding. verify33 carries the budget, thin16 and the entities dependency cleanup. Because main's pack-7 review rule forbids box compiles, x-compat runs as verify33's FIRST node step instead of locally (rule n20), and its result gates the rest of the job.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_23 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 23u32, "2026-10-30T00:52Z", "x", "2026-10-29 20:52 x: verify33 note: the live posts.spi header (--timeout 900000) changes the sim-stress fixtures (apps/client/e2e/sim-stress.world.json / .expected.json come from posts.spi). verify33 runs verify.ps1 -Accept, so it regenerates them and they land three-way with its outputs. Until then, a non-Accept sim build on the live tree fails Confirm-Fixture for sim-stress, which is expected and not a regression.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_24 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 24u32, "2026-10-30T01:58Z", "x", "2026-10-30T02:00Z groom: reopened Done 100 -> Active 80. The state was stale: verify30-33 (n20-n23) have run on this item since it was marked Done, and none is green yet. Remaining: verify32 (job-1793303169424, live in xv30, in its final sim build at 21:51) and verify33 (launch-x-verify33.ps1 into xv30, -Accept so the sim-stress fixture regenerates). Closes on verify33 green with its outputs landed three-way. LIB-PROCESS-COUNTER (dep) and X-CARGO-BUILD-PROFILE wait on the same run.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_25 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 25u32, "2026-10-30T02:04Z", "x", "2026-10-29 22:04 x: caught before launch: launch-x-verify33.ps1's x-compat gate matched '\\b0 findings\\b', but the installed compiler prints 'x-compat report: 0 finding(s) in N file(s)', so the gate could never pass and verify33 would have refused to start every time. Fixed to '^x-compat report: 0 finding\\(s\\) in [1-9]\\d* file\\(s\\)$'. Controls: clean report TRUE; '29 unchecked without a profile' FALSE; 5 findings FALSE; 0 files FALSE.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_26 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 26u32, "2026-10-30T02:41Z", "x", "2026-10-29 22:3x x: verify32 (job-1793303169424) STOPPED by me at 22:34 after 6.8 h, with kit job stop (exit 143; 0 xv30/xv32 processes left). Verdict RED, cause LOAD (already known): apps/client/posts.spi failed 4 tests (zig targets, slowest 365 s against the 300 s cell budget; verify32 was synced before posts.spi got --timeout 900000). The other 56 notebooks it reached all passed. Stopping freed xv30 about 70 min early for the real proof: verify33 (job-1793328097444, pack 7 core 9C899B30495F7DC5, fixed x-compat gate, -Accept, LandRepos x,spiral) started 22:3x. It writes only to the xv30 mirror (re-synced by digest) and remote-stage\\xv32-out (partial, not landed).")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_27 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 27u32, "2026-10-30T10:26Z", "x", "2026-10-30 06:2x x groom: CLOSED with evidence. verify33 (job-1793328097444, pack 7 core 9C899B30495F7DC5, -Accept, LandRepos x,spiral) finished exit 0: client build, sim build, e2e accept and sim accept all exit 0; 66 notebooks passed.")
inl note_of_x_proof_scripts_in_repo_1 () = Note ("X-PROOF-SCRIPTS-IN-REPO", 1u32, "2026-10-27T10:51Z", "x", "2026-10-27 06:51 x: per the user's 10-27 03:2x rule (deliverables live in their proper repo place from the start). Today's verify11..15, base_regen, land_outputs and measure_* scripts are copies with one changed mirror name each. Fold them into x/scripts/node-verify.ps1 and friends, writing only under their -Out path.")
inl note_of_x_proof_scripts_in_repo_2 () = Note ("X-PROOF-SCRIPTS-IN-REPO", 2u32, "2026-10-27T11:02Z", "x", "2026-10-27 07:02 x: x/scripts/verify.ps1 in the tree (unstaged): -Accept (client build, e2e -Accept with the xc binary, sim -Accept), then client and sim build.ps1 plain, -Out saves .rs/.json/.jsonl/.txt/README.md and Cargo.lock, -Notebooks a,b runs only those notebooks through Assert-SpiralTotals; it prints the SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL hash when one is pinned. It also fixes the E2E-ACCEPT 'no xc binary' skip of verify12-15 (they never dot-sourced core.ps1, so _exe was undefined). Left: the node launcher (mirror sync gated on REMOTE-SYNC-OK, scp, job start, waiter) is cross-repo, so it belongs in i574n.github/scripts next to remote.ps1; land_outputs.ps1 (base-vs-new) goes in as x/scripts/land-outputs.ps1 after its first real use on verify15.")
inl note_of_x_proof_scripts_in_repo_3 () = Note ("X-PROOF-SCRIPTS-IN-REPO", 3u32, "2026-10-27T11:46Z", "x", "2026-10-27 07:46 x: the cross-repo half landed unstaged in i574n.github/scripts/node-proof.ps1 (org tooling, next to remote.ps1). -MirrorName -Label -Command ['{mirror}' expands to C:\\home\\remote\\<MirrorName>] [-Repos spiral,x] [-CompilerDll <node path>]. It writes a job script with the pinned compiler and the erlang/elixir PATH, parse-checks it, scps it to remote-stage\\<MirrorName>\\run.ps1 and checks the hash, syncs each repo to the mirror and throws unless every sync printed REMOTE-SYNC-OK, then starts the job. The command sits inside the staged script, so remote.ps1 never sees -Mirror/-Out-like arguments. Also fixed today in x/scripts/verify.ps1: -Part selected nothing (comma precedence) and exited 0; it now throws when nothing is selected. First real use: the next verify.")
inl note_of_x_proof_scripts_in_repo_4 () = Note ("X-PROOF-SCRIPTS-IN-REPO", 4u32, "2026-10-28T10:44Z", "x", "2026-10-28 06:39 x: CLOSED by X-WIP-VERIFY's pre-registered rule. verify25 (node job-1793174907446, pinned compiler 4FD712E9E357) GREEN on every clause of X-WIP-VERIFY note 6: exit 0; sim accept and plain sim build exit 0 (ExUnit 45/45, corpus commute ok, thread_run pass, tamper rejected with same_cells=false); client gate 29 crates 0 over 1000; x-compat 0 in 43 client and 24 sim files; all 42 client and 23 sim notebooks passed, 0 failing totals; plain-pass e2e 37 of 37 tutorial steps same, 0 FAILED, 153 stub requests. Outputs landed three-way (node-proof -Land x-verify25: 21 files plus 19 Gleam modules, 0 conflicts; net.rs held back because its source changed after the sync, so verify26 lands it).")
inl note_of_x_notebook_assert_1 () = Note ("X-NOTEBOOK-ASSERT", 1u32, "2026-10-27T10:51Z", "x", "2026-10-27 06:51 x: my B'/S1/R1 measure scripts printed NOTEBOOK ok over a test that does not parse (SOCIAL-PROFILES-LOCAL note 23). A small helper used by X-PROOF-SCRIPTS-IN-REPO.")
inl note_of_x_notebook_assert_2 () = Note ("X-NOTEBOOK-ASSERT", 2u32, "2026-10-27T11:02Z", "x", "2026-10-27 07:02 x: in the tree (unstaged): x/scripts/common.ps1 Assert-SpiralTotals throws unless every spiral-tests total line has failed 0, unsupported 0, not_run 0, passed = executed, and executed > 0 when tests were discovered, and throws when no total line exists. Checked against the real data: a good total passes, verify14b's failing wire.spi total throws, an output with no total throws. Root cause of the false NOTEBOOK ok lines: my measure scripts set ErrorActionPreference Continue, so Invoke-Block's failure was non-terminating and the catch never ran.")
inl note_of_x_notebook_assert_3 () = Note ("X-NOTEBOOK-ASSERT", 3u32, "2026-10-27T17:23Z", "x", "2026-10-27 13:23 x: bug in my own Assert-SpiralTotals, found by its first real caller (node job-1793120236416, verify.ps1 -Notebooks defuse, 1004 s of notebook work then 'Cannot bind argument to parameter Lines because it is an empty string'). Its [string[]] parameter had [AllowEmptyCollection()] but not [AllowEmptyString()], and real notebook output always carries blank lines; the build.ps1 path never hit it, but both new verify.ps1 paths (-Notebooks and -ParallelNotebooks) would have thrown every time. My earlier controls passed because they used tidy arrays with no blank line, which is not the real data's shape. Fixed (both attributes) and re-proven locally: blank lines with a good total pass, blank lines with a failing total throw, no total throws. -Notebooks also printed nothing on success or failure; it now echoes the spiral-tests and type-error lines. The stopped bench (job-1793120714727) would have hit the same throw after its first arm; restarted as job-1793121820362, and defuse is rechecked as job-1793121647959.")
inl note_of_x_notebook_assert_4 () = Note ("X-NOTEBOOK-ASSERT", 4u32, "2026-10-28T10:45Z", "x", "2026-10-28 06:39 x: CLOSED by X-WIP-VERIFY's pre-registered rule. verify25 (node job-1793174907446, pinned compiler 4FD712E9E357) GREEN on every clause of X-WIP-VERIFY note 6: exit 0; sim accept and plain sim build exit 0 (ExUnit 45/45, corpus commute ok, thread_run pass, tamper rejected with same_cells=false); client gate 29 crates 0 over 1000; x-compat 0 in 43 client and 24 sim files; all 42 client and 23 sim notebooks passed, 0 failing totals; plain-pass e2e 37 of 37 tutorial steps same, 0 FAILED, 153 stub requests. Outputs landed three-way (node-proof -Land x-verify25: 21 files plus 19 Gleam modules, 0 conflicts; net.rs held back because its source changed after the sync, so verify26 lands it).")
inl note_of_x_defuse_edge_tests_1 () = Note ("X-DEFUSE-EDGE-TESTS", 1u32, "2026-10-27T10:51Z", "x", "2026-10-27 06:51 x: two bugs today lived exactly there: ascii_of \"\" counted text start as non-ASCII, so a leading link stayed live, and the frames split dropped defusing from split_cell, which the sim calls. Draft the tests in the tree, unstaged; X-WIP-VERIFY runs them.")
inl note_of_x_defuse_edge_tests_2 () = Note ("X-DEFUSE-EDGE-TESTS", 2u32, "2026-10-27T11:02Z", "x", "2026-10-27 07:02 x: drafted in the tree (unstaged): defuse.spi a_link_and_a_mention_at_the_start_are_defused (cell.app and @bob at text start, the ascii_of empty-string bug) and a_link_right_after_a_wide_glyph_stays_plain (documents the blocks_domain rule), and splitter.spi split_cell_posts_before_splitting (the sim's contract). Every cell <= 272 and every line <= 120. They run in the next X-WIP-VERIFY (defuse and tlds are in build.ps1's notebook list now).")
inl note_of_x_defuse_edge_tests_3 () = Note ("X-DEFUSE-EDGE-TESTS", 3u32, "2026-10-27T17:31Z", "x", "2026-10-27 13:31 x: PRODUCT BUG found by this item's new tests, the first time defuse.spi ran as a notebook (verify19, then node job-1793121647959): a mention at the very START of a post was never defused. mention_quiet asked sm'.contains prev \"!#$%&*@\", and lib's signature is contains (value) (s), so this tests whether the set contains prev; at the start prev is \"\", and every string contains \"\". So \"@bob hi\" posted with a live mention (expected '@<ZWSP>bob hi', got '@bob hi'; both failing tests start with @). Same class as this morning's ascii_of \"\" fix for dots. Fixed with glyphs.spi's existing one_of \"!#$%&*@\" prev, which requires a single glyph; hashtag_after and cash_quiet compare with =, so \"\" cannot match there, and no other sm'.contains <glyph> \"<set>\" call exists in x/apps. Also moved a_link_and_a_mention_at_the_start_are_defused below defused_entities (it ran before the definition: Unbound). Recheck: node job-1793122349993.")
inl note_of_x_defuse_edge_tests_4 () = Note ("X-DEFUSE-EDGE-TESTS", 4u32, "2026-10-28T00:25Z", "x", "2026-10-27 20:25 x: LEAK found while writing the 'after an emoji or CJK glyph' edge test: the mention and hashtag rules were SUBSETS of X's, against this item's own superset principle (an undefused token corrupts the post for good; an extra ZWSP costs 1 weight). Source, twitter-text master: js/src/regexp/validMentionPrecedingChars.js = (?:^|[^a-zA-Z0-9_!#$%&*@＠]|(?:^|[^a-zA-Z0-9_+~.-])(?:rt|RT|rT|Rt):?), so ANY non-ASCII glyph (CJK or emoji) before @ allows a live mention; js/src/regexp/hashtagBoundary.js = (?:^|︎|️|$|(?!hashtagAlphaNumeric|&)codePoint), so letters, marks and digits of every script block a hashtag but an emoji does not. x's defuse.spi blocked both on wide_letter (any non-ASCII), so '日本@bob' and '🙂@bob' posted live mentions and '🙂#tag' a live hashtag. Fixed (tree, unstaged): mention_quiet blocks only on ASCII word glyphs, !#$%&*@ and fullwidth ＠; hashtag_after only on ASCII word glyphs, & and # (so CJK before # gets an extra, harmless ZWSP: a superset). Cashtags already were a superset (X needs whitespace before $). New test sigils_after_wide_glyphs_are_defused. Known gap, not fixed: X's 'RT:@name' form allows a mention right after RT/rt letters, which needs more than one preceding glyph; recorded here for a follow-up. Real x-compat 0 in 42 files. Proof: node job-1793147170243 (defuse notebook), then the next full verify, whose accept may regenerate fixtures holding such texts. Sources: https://github.com/twitter/twitter-text/blob/master/js/src/regexp/validMentionPrecedingChars.js and https://github.com/twitter/twitter-text/blob/master/js/src/regexp/hashtagBoundary.js")
inl note_of_x_defuse_edge_tests_5 () = Note ("X-DEFUSE-EDGE-TESTS", 5u32, "2026-10-28T01:05Z", "x", "2026-10-27 21:05 x: defuse-nb4 (job-1793147170243): 2/8 passed, and all 6 failures are cell timeouts (300 s budget; one cell took 230 s on rust plus 120 s on gleam; node at 100% cpu), with no assertion failure and no type error. Per the user's no-quiet-machine rule the budget is the fix: defuse.spi's header now carries --timeout 900000, the lib's convention for files whose cells build both rust and gleam. Rerun: job-1793149356415.")
inl note_of_x_defuse_edge_tests_6 () = Note ("X-DEFUSE-EDGE-TESTS", 6u32, "2026-10-28T01:39Z", "x", "2026-10-27 21:39 x: defuse proven under load (job-1793149356415, 2295 s): 8/8, including sigils_after_wide_glyphs_are_defused (a mention after CJK and a hashtag after an emoji now get their ZWSP). Slowest cell 525 s against the new 900 s budget (headroom 0.58); the old 300 s would have failed it, so the budget, not the code, caused nb4's 6 failures. What remains: the full verify that carries the fix (after verify22), where the e2e and sim accepts may regenerate fixtures, and the RT:@name gap from note 4.")
inl note_of_x_defuse_edge_tests_7 () = Note ("X-DEFUSE-EDGE-TESTS", 7u32, "2026-10-28T01:50Z", "x", "2026-10-27 21:50 x: note 4's RT gap closed in the tree. twitter-text also accepts a mention after (?:^|[^a-zA-Z0-9_+~.-])(?:rt|RT|rT|Rt):?, so 'RT@bob' and 'rt:@bob' are live on X. defuse.spi: rt_before looks back through entities_from's accumulated glyphs (an optional ':' then t/T, r/R) and rt_boundary requires nothing from [a-zA-Z0-9_+~.-] or the text start before them; mention_after takes 'mention_quiet prev || rt_before before'. Test a_mention_right_after_rt_is_defused: RT@bob and rt:@bob defused, art@bob plain (as on X). Real x-compat 0 in 42 files. Proof: verify23 (job-1793152313075).")
inl note_of_x_defuse_edge_tests_8 () = Note ("X-DEFUSE-EDGE-TESTS", 8u32, "2026-10-28T10:47Z", "x", "2026-10-28 06:39 x: CLOSED by X-WIP-VERIFY's pre-registered rule. verify25 (node job-1793174907446, pinned compiler 4FD712E9E357) GREEN on every clause of X-WIP-VERIFY note 6: exit 0; sim accept and plain sim build exit 0 (ExUnit 45/45, corpus commute ok, thread_run pass, tamper rejected with same_cells=false); client gate 29 crates 0 over 1000; x-compat 0 in 43 client and 24 sim files; all 42 client and 23 sim notebooks passed, 0 failing totals; plain-pass e2e 37 of 37 tutorial steps same, 0 FAILED, 153 stub requests. Outputs landed three-way (node-proof -Land x-verify25: 21 files plus 19 Gleam modules, 0 conflicts; net.rs held back because its source changed after the sync, so verify26 lands it). Its condition holds: defuse, tlds and splitter are among the 42 client notebooks that passed.")
inl note_of_x_json_collect_dedup_1 () = Note ("X-JSON-COLLECT-DEDUP", 1u32, "2026-10-27T10:52Z", "x", "2026-10-27 06:51 x: census on today's base regen (pinned compiler): digest 165, chain 113, thread 98, refs 79, fetch 67, assemble 58, users 55, locate 55, write 52 and more. Analysis and draft are CPU-free; the measuring round needs a compile slot.")
inl note_of_x_json_collect_dedup_2 () = Note ("X-JSON-COLLECT-DEDUP", 2u32, "2026-10-27T11:18Z", "x", "2026-10-27 07:18 x: analysis, lower value than the census suggested. wire's collect is := with an inner :~ ^ from join point, so every (element type, decoder) pair at a call site emits its own from_N, with the decoder f inlined in the loop. digest's 165 lines are 7 loops of 15, 49, 24, 16, 16, 24 and 21 lines: about 12 lines of fixed loop scaffold each, plus the inlined decoder. Collapsing the scaffold (a host json-array-to-list-of-json call, then listm.map per type) saves at most about 12 lines per instance, and map loops come back per element type. The decoders are the real cost, and they are needed. Recommendation: drop to P3; if a crate nears the bound, turn its biggest inlined decoder (digest from_7, 49 lines) into a :~ join point instead.")
inl note_of_x_json_collect_dedup_3 () = Note ("X-JSON-COLLECT-DEDUP", 3u32, "2026-10-27T15:10Z", "x", "2026-10-27 11:09 x: groomed to Paused, so the light view lists only pullable work. Resume condition (from this item's own analysis): a touched crate's regen nears 900 generated lines, or a change has to grow it. Checked against every regen until then.")
inl note_of_x_json_collect_dedup_4 () = Note ("X-JSON-COLLECT-DEDUP", 4u32, "2026-10-28T12:38Z", "x", "2026-10-28 08:38 x: RESUMED by its own condition (digest regen 954 > 900). Took note 2's lever, not the dedup: reference_as as a :~ join point over ref_kind_of (posts.spi), measured with X-HAND-UNITS' headroom round after ~09:33.")
inl note_of_x_json_collect_dedup_5 () = Note ("X-JSON-COLLECT-DEDUP", 5u32, "2026-10-28T15:05Z", "x", "2026-10-28 11:05 x: note 2's lever measured and FAILED: reference_as as a :~ join point grew digest, jsonl, select and view by +15 each (A/B, same compiler); reverted. digest stays 954 (base on the installed compiler), 4 over the 950 headroom; this item's dedup idea (fewer element types or a host collect) is the remaining route for digest, P3.")
inl note_of_x_json_collect_dedup_6 () = Note ("X-JSON-COLLECT-DEDUP", 6u32, "2026-10-29T12:48Z", "x", "2026-10-29 09:0x x: lever 'classify once' measured and REJECTED. reference_as rewritten as ref_kind_of : string -> option ref_kind plus one list build, so the one-element list is constructed once instead of per branch. Same-compiler A/B on the node (A4E480202BD4; base job-1793276236043 vs candidate job-1793276440367, same tree but posts.spi): digest 954 -> 966, jsonl 639 -> 651, select 785 -> 797, view 748 -> 760 (+12 each), the rest equal. The option construction plus the match cost more than the duplicated Cons arms, which is the n5 lesson again in a third form. Not applied (the candidate only ever existed on the node). digest stays at 954 base. Where it comes from (ranked from the fresh digest.rs): 6 specializations of the JSON-array collect loop (from_N, the same 'v0.get(i)' element fetch block 6x), one per element mapper. This item's real lever stays the dedup itself: fewer collect instantiations (one generic element walk returning json values, then typed maps), still P3.")
inl note_of_x_json_collect_dedup_7 () = Note ("X-JSON-COLLECT-DEDUP", 7u32, "2026-10-29T13:16Z", "x", "2026-10-29 09:5x x: 'walk once' MEASURED and REJECTED. collect f items = elements items |> listm::map f, where elements is ONE json-only walk. Same-compiler A/B vs base2 (job-1793278553809 vs job-1793276236043): 14 crates grew, by 15-26 each (digest 954 -> 973, refs 896 -> 918, users 874 -> 898, fetch 728 -> 754, api 255 -> 274, ...), and none shrank. lib map is its own specialized loop per f, so this ADDS a loop instead of removing one. With n6 that's both dedup shapes measured: the hand-written per-f loop is the smallest form on today's Rust backend. digest stays 954 (4 over the 950 headroom, 46 under the gate). Back to Paused: resume on a compiler change to closure specialization (per-f loops sharing one body), or if a change must grow digest.")
inl note_of_x_json_collect_dedup_8 () = Note ("X-JSON-COLLECT-DEDUP", 8u32, "2026-10-30T16:10Z", "x", "2026-10-30 12:1x x: FOURTH dedup shape, not yet measured: 'dyn the mapper'. The three rejected shapes (n5 join point, n6 classify-once, n7 walk-once) all kept f as a compile-time closure, so Spiral still specializes collect's from loop once per mapper. Draft C:\\home\\data\\x-drafts\\jsondyn\\stage\\wire.spi (live DD9C505D572FA1AB + one line: := f = dyn f inside collect) makes f a runtime closure, so same-t mappers (text_of, at_key \"text\", at_key \"id\", ids_at ...) can share one loop body; different t still monomorphize. Not a hot path (one CLI response per call), so the heap-closure cost tibia's eta-reduction relay warned about does not apply. PRE-REGISTERED (launch-x-jsondyn-ab.ps1, xs4probe, pack 8, same-tree A/B via verify.ps1 -Part regen): ADOPT only if net <= -50 lines AND no crate grows by more than +5 AND no crate goes over 950 AND both arms regen every crate with 0 RUST-FAILED; then the client tests on the node gate the land. Otherwise REJECTED, recorded as the 4th shape.")
inl note_of_x_json_collect_dedup_9 () = Note ("X-JSON-COLLECT-DEDUP", 9u32, "2026-10-30T16:37Z", "x", "2026-10-30 12:3x x: 4th shape 'dyn the mapper' MEASURED and REJECTED by n8's rule. x-jsondyn-ab (job-1793376758171, 25 min, xs4probe, pack 8 core 17DDB2DCEF2A2D52, same-tree A/B via verify.ps1 -Part regen; both arms 30 crates, 0 RUST-FAILED): net +199 lines, 13 crates grew, 1 shrank (write -11). digest 954 -> 1,003 (over the 1,000 gate), chain +28, locate/fetch +22, thread +21. A runtime closure costs more per call site (closure construction plus the boxed call) than the shared loop saves; same-t sharing is too rare. All four dedup shapes are now measured, and the per-f specialized loop stays the smallest on today's Rust backend. Not applied (the candidate only ever existed on the node). Stays Paused; the resume condition (n7) is unchanged. BASE DRIFT seen in the A arm (pack 8 + today's lib): xc 975 (n17 accepted 960), refs 901 (896), digest 954, users 879; xc is 25 lines from the 1,000 gate.")
inl note_of_x_json_collect_dedup_10 () = Note ("X-JSON-COLLECT-DEDUP", 10u32, "2026-10-31T23:03Z", "x", "2026-10-31 19:03 x groom: Paused -> Planned at 40. No written resume condition. The last note rejected shape 4 (dyn mapper, +199 lines). Next is a shape that shares the collect loop through a lib helper, measured with the same A/B rule.")
inl note_of_x_json_collect_dedup_11 () = Note ("X-JSON-COLLECT-DEDUP", 11u32, "2026-11-01T06:35Z", "x", "2026-11-01 02:35 x: CORRECTION of my 10-31 19:03 groom note. It said 'no written resume condition', which was WRONG: n3 (10-27 11:09) set one, 'a touched crate's regen nears 900 generated lines, or a change has to grow it', and it had FIRED. digest was 954 on 10-30's base (n9), and shape 4 pushed it to 1,003, over the gate. So Planned is right but for a different reason: the condition fired, and four loop-sharing shapes (n5 join point, n6 classify-once, n7 walk-once, n9 dyn mapper) are all measured and rejected. The per-mapper specialized loop is smallest on the Rust backend.\nThe remaining lever is n2's own: the cost is the inlined DECODERS, not the loop scaffold. NEXT STEP: from the next regen (verify44's outputs land tonight), read digest's generated crate and rank its from_N loops by inlined decoder size. Turn the biggest decoder into its own ':~' function (a separately emitted fn, so its body exists once and each loop calls it). Pass rule, written now: same-tree A/B through verify.ps1 -Part regen; adopt iff digest shrinks by >= 30 lines AND no crate grows by more than 5 AND 0 RUST-FAILED.")
inl note_of_x_json_collect_dedup_12 () = Note ("X-JSON-COLLECT-DEDUP", 12u32, "2026-11-01T12:37Z", "x", "2026-11-01 08:37 x: ITEM UPGRADE (round 4). Fields: tags gain team:x; 60 / light stand (the A/A regen is one node job). DEFINITION OF DONE is n11's rule (verify.ps1 -Part regen, same-tree A/B: adopt iff digest shrinks >= 30 lines, no crate grows > 5, 0 RUST-FAILED); artifact the per-crate line table. NEXT STEP: rank digest's from_N loops by inlined decoder size in the next landed regen (apps/client/digest/digest.rs, after verify46 lands). TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: the hoisted decoder keeps its typed signature (json -> option post, or json -> result t failure). Hoisting only changes where the body is emitted (a ':~' join point), never the decoder's type into a string or a -1 sentinel. wire.spi's reads r GADT stays the boundary type.")
inl note_of_x_json_collect_dedup_13 () = Note ("X-JSON-COLLECT-DEDUP", 13u32, "2026-11-03T15:18Z", "x", "2026-11-03 11:18 x: n12 NEXT STEP DONE on today's landed regen (core 21D5992EDB80D270, census cli6 land). digest.rs is 954 lines with 7 from_N loops (165 lines in from_*). The biggest is from_7 at 49 lines, and its body is posts.spi reference_as INLINED: three arms (quoted, replied_to, reposted|retweeted) each building the same one-element Cons(kind, id, Nil). from_N counts per crate (lines/loops): digest 954/7, refs 901/4, users 880/3, locate 804/3, timeline 779/1, fetch 745/3, assemble 741/2, write 739/3, thread 728/3, chain 638/4, chunks 582/1, args 565/1, frames 451/1, api 255/1, resume 245/1, preview 188/1. DRAFT (kit drafts x\\X-JSON-COLLECT-DEDUP\\posts.spi, layered on the XDUMPS v1 draft 24A9CE7D74EA -> FFF618DAC26C): reference_as becomes a ':~' join point, so it is emitted once as its own fn and each loop calls it. The typed signature (string -> post_id -> list reference) is unchanged, per the n12 typefeatureset plan. A/B per the n11 rule: A = x-events2's regen outputs (posts v1), B = the same tree plus this one-token change. Adopt iff digest shrinks >= 30 lines, no crate grows > 5, and 0 RUST-FAILED. Runs after x-events2 lands.")
inl note_of_x_json_collect_dedup_14 () = Note ("X-JSON-COLLECT-DEDUP", 14u32, "2026-11-03T17:31Z", "x", "2026-11-03 13:31 x: A/B MADE IN-JOB (rule n13 kept, measurement changed BEFORE the run). The node's installed core moved to 7C49B7A6AFC05D2C after x-events3, so x-events3's outputs (core 21D5992EDB80D270) can't be A. x-next1 (job-1793726940700, pinned 7C49B7A6AFC05D2C) builds the client on the landed tree and prints 'A lines <crate> N', then applies only the dedup posts.spi (reference_as ':~') and rebuilds, printing 'B lines <crate> N'. Same core, same mirror, one change. Adopt iff digest shrinks >= 30, no crate grows > 5, 0 RUST-FAILED. world.spi (sim only, no client crate) rides the run unmeasured.")
inl note_of_x_json_collect_dedup_15 () = Note ("X-JSON-COLLECT-DEDUP", 15u32, "2026-11-03T18:31Z", "x", "2026-11-03 14:31 x: x-next1 VOID (not a verdict on the dedup): the A build, before any dedup change, failed cargo with E0505 at generated refs/refs.rs:879 ('method33(&v41, v42, &v43, &v44, v41, v52)', a borrow and a move of v41 in one call). That is a regression in core 7C49B7A6AFC05D2C (installed ~13:1x). compiler confirmed the cause: the rustMoveOnLastUse text pass cut a .clone() although '&v41' appears earlier on the line; a hotfix is being proven (job compiler-hotfix-e0505). Meanwhile x pins the last-good core: node copy C:\\home\\remote-stage\\x-core-21D5 (21D5992EDB80D270, from x's own xhtml1 pin), wired as -PinFrom in the four queued x launchers. Today's landed outputs came from that core, so the A/B and any land stay consistent. Relaunched as x-next1b (job-1793730677056), same in-job A/B rule (n14).")
inl note_of_x_json_collect_dedup_16 () = Note ("X-JSON-COLLECT-DEDUP", 16u32, "2026-11-03T19:21Z", "x", "2026-11-03 15:21 x: pack27 (compiler's E0505 hotfix, core 6F83B94FE33167CC) is installed on the node (main 15:18). x-next1b keeps its pinned 21D5992EDB80D270 copy to the end, so its in-job A/B stays on one core. The next x launches (x-next2, x-next3, x-replay1, x-cells-mpath1, x-html-gleam6) go back to the latest installed core (-PinFrom '' -Core 6F83B94FE33167CC). The 21D5 fallback copy stays on the node in case kit's E0507 (not in pack27) hits x too.")
inl note_of_x_json_collect_dedup_17 () = Note ("X-JSON-COLLECT-DEDUP", 17u32, "2026-11-03T20:13Z", "x", "2026-11-03 16:13 x: x-next1b VERDICT, by the pre-registered rule (n11/n14): REJECT shape 5. In-job A/B on one pinned core (21D5992EDB80D270), one change (posts.spi reference_as ':=' -> ':~'): every gate green (sim accept 0, sim build 0, client A 0, client B 0, e2e RUST-OK 37 + 5, census SAME), but digest went 954 -> 957 (+3) instead of shrinking >= 30, and jsonl 670 -> 673, select 800 -> 803, view 763 -> 766 grew too (total 19,799 -> 19,811). The join point emitted reference_as once, but each call site's argument plumbing cost about as much as the inlined three-arm body it replaced. This is the fifth loop-sharing shape measured and rejected (n5 join point, n6 classify-once, n7 walk-once, n9 dyn mapper, now a decoder join point). posts.spi stays as landed. CONCLUSION from 5 shapes: on the Rust backend the per-mapper specialized loop is already the smallest form; the 841 lines are the price of specialization, not duplication. Proposing Done-as-measured: no shape meets the bar.")
inl note_of_x_string_slice_sites_1 () = Note ("X-STRING-SLICE-SITES", 1u32, "2026-10-27T10:52Z", "x", "2026-10-27 06:51 x: known sites: wire trimmed base URL (cuts a one-byte /, safe to switch), cli char_at/handle strip, prelude digit check; clipped stays on slice because it cuts UTF-8 server text.")
inl note_of_x_string_slice_sites_2 () = Note ("X-STRING-SLICE-SITES", 2u32, "2026-10-27T11:09Z", "x", "2026-10-27 07:09 x: switched the two cuts at a known one-byte boundary: wire trimmed_base (drops a trailing /) now uses cut 0 (n - 1), and cli without_at (drops a leading @) uses rest_from 1. Kept on sm'.slice, because they cut arbitrary text that may be UTF-8: wire clipped (server problem text), cli char_at (user handles and patterns), prelude's digit check. The line effect is measured in the next verify; string_slice stays emitted in any crate that still reaches clipped.")
inl note_of_x_string_slice_sites_3 () = Note ("X-STRING-SLICE-SITES", 3u32, "2026-10-28T10:49Z", "x", "2026-10-28 06:39 x: CLOSED by X-WIP-VERIFY's pre-registered rule. verify25 (node job-1793174907446, pinned compiler 4FD712E9E357) GREEN on every clause of X-WIP-VERIFY note 6: exit 0; sim accept and plain sim build exit 0 (ExUnit 45/45, corpus commute ok, thread_run pass, tamper rejected with same_cells=false); client gate 29 crates 0 over 1000; x-compat 0 in 43 client and 24 sim files; all 42 client and 23 sim notebooks passed, 0 failing totals; plain-pass e2e 37 of 37 tutorial steps same, 0 FAILED, 153 stub requests. Outputs landed three-way (node-proof -Land x-verify25: 21 files plus 19 Gleam modules, 0 conflicts; net.rs held back because its source changed after the sync, so verify26 lands it).")
inl note_of_x_split_on_no_array_1 () = Note ("X-SPLIT-ON-NO-ARRAY", 1u32, "2026-10-27T10:52Z", "x", "2026-10-27 06:51 x: the array-based draft was reverted on 10-27: 277 > 272 in x-compat, and the sim's Gleam build has no array module.")
inl note_of_x_split_on_no_array_2 () = Note ("X-SPLIT-ON-NO-ARRAY", 2u32, "2026-10-27T11:48Z", "x", "2026-10-27 07:48 x: resolved lib-first instead of a new x algorithm. lib already has sm'.split_list (a :~ ^ join point, tested on rust and gleam, no array module), the same recursive cut as x's split_on, but it honours multi-character separators (x's version cut at i + 1, a latent bug for any separator longer than one character). prelude.split_on now delegates to it; its callers (splitter, token, xc preview, sim world/personas) all pass one-character separators, so their behaviour is unchanged. Any speed-up belongs in lib's split_list, where every project gets it.")
