inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_28 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 28u32, "2026-10-28T14:43Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 10:43 fiscal: MEASURED so far (census job-1793186447028, lib with 05:28 landings): regional_rules_census PASSES, so Peppol reads 93 rules / 159 assertions / 135 fatal; its 'invalid' (unparsed) counts went to console only and that mirror is gone. Rerun queued to print them: job-1793198664040 fiscal-census-rules (one cell, after setall, generic fix-proof-d with -Package fiscal\\src -Show census:). PASS for the 19 sequence-constructor tests = Peppol invalid 0.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_29 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 29u32, "2026-10-29T11:46Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 07:5x fiscal: RULES CENSUS (job-1793198664040-fiscal-census-rules, node, corpus_checks 6C0ADD55, A4E48020): regional_rules_census HOLDS. Printed census (from the notebook output): peppol rules 93 assertions 159 fatal 135 INVALID 4; zatca 50/152 fatal 51 invalid 2; zatca cen 35/105 fatal 41 invalid 0; dian 36/192 fatal 169 invalid 0; ro_cius 19/113 fatal 113 invalid 0; ubl_tr 131/299 fatal 0 INVALID 139. So Peppol is NOT at invalid 0: 4 assertions still fail to parse (DE-R-018, n20, is one). Next: print the ids of the invalid assertions (census only counts them) and fix or record each.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_30 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 30u32, "2026-10-29T12:21Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 08:21 fiscal: the 4 invalid Peppol tests NAMED (new fiscal test, job-1793275999999 on setall, 0 type errors): PEPPOL-EN16931-F001 and IS-R-008 use 'castable as xs:date'; DE-R-019 and DE-R-020 use 'for $cp in string-to-codepoints(...) return (if ... then ... else ...)' inside string-join(...) mod 97 (IBAN check). All 4 stop the parser as 'trailing tokens'. ZATCA's 2 invalid are also 'castable as' (text census). So two lib xpath constructs close Peppol and ZATCA: XCastable (parse + eval: lexical check per xs type) and XFor (for $v in E return E, sequence result). UBL-TR's 139 are different (no XPath 2 constructs; 119 of 304 expressions use variables): fiscal-rules-invalid (job-1793276529141) prints its reasons.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_31 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 31u32, "2026-10-29T12:37Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 08:37 fiscal: held lib program fiscal/lib-programs/xpath-castable-for.kit (xpath B44F8524 -> D100F62C, xpath_eval 866CA0F7 -> 9912A6A5; rehearsed on scratch copies): XFor (for $v in E return E, a sequence of the body per item), XCastable (castable as xs:string/integer/decimal/date/time, optional ?; leap-year date and zoned-time checks), string-to-codepoints, and kind tests after an explicit axis (following::node()). Parse tests + eval test for_and_castable_follow_xpath_2. Node gates on mirror ss: fiscal-xp2-gate-xpath job-1793277491422, -eval job-1793277502711, -schrun job-1793277514647. Expected effect: Peppol invalid 4 -> 0 (F001 + IS-R-008 castable; DE-R-019/020 for). Known limit after it: DE-R-019/020 evaluate an IBAN mod 97 over a 24+ digit xs:integer, which lib decimal (i64 units) cannot hold, so those two rules parse but still break at evaluation for DE sellers using codes 58/59 (needs an arbitrary-precision mod; follow-up).")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_32 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 32u32, "2026-10-29T13:44Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 09:44 fiscal: xpath-castable-for PROVEN on mirror ss (live tree + program; each file's hash = draft + mirror-only --timeout 5400000, A4E48020): xpath 4/4 (67106FCB = D100F62C + header), xpath_eval 5/5 incl for_and_castable_follow_xpath_2 (46BF0F04 = 9912A6A5 + header), schematron_run 2/2 (974372AA), 0 type errors (fiscal-xp2-gate-xpath/-eval/-schrun). Lands after TRAIN3's notebooks end, then a re-census.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_33 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 33u32, "2026-10-29T16:01Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 12:01 fiscal: xpath-castable-for and xpath-following-axes LANDED 11:55:35 and 11:58:41 (xpath B44F8524 -> D100F62C -> C266A60D, xpath_eval 866CA0F7 -> 9912A6A5 -> 1AB4EE5A), via lib-guarded-do (git-a6's pack6b window exempted at its native phase; no live reader), hash equal to the node-proven copy; post-land mirror post1029 reproduces the proof mirrors' hashes exactly; main's document_test (spi -> livemd -> spi) GREEN over it; full live-tree gates queued as the fiscal-post-* chain. Undo = git HEAD. Next: re-census (expected Peppol invalid 4 -> 0).")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_34 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 34u32, "2026-10-29T16:30Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 12:30 fiscal: post-land census (mirror post1029 = live lib after 11:58 + the fiscal tree): regional_rules_name_every_test_that_does_not_parse printed NO invalid line for Peppol, ZATCA or UBL-TR, so every regional context and test now parses; the test failed only because it still required Peppol to have one. Inverted (now: every region has 0, else name the first), and regional_rules_census's UBL-TR Common pins (131/299) changed to 0/0 because Common holds only abstract rules reached through Main's extends. Reruns queued: fiscal-census2-* (jobs 1793291096508, 1793291118346, 1793291134906).")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_35 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 35u32, "2026-10-29T17:26Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 13:26 fiscal: re-census PASSES (fiscal-census2-*, mirror post1029, corpus_checks C3692131): regional_rules_name_every_test_that_does_not_parse passes (every Peppol, ZATCA and UBL-TR context and test parses), and regional_rules_census passes with the UBL-TR Common pins at 0/0. Peppol is at invalid 0, the item's parse criterion. Remaining Peppol gap: DE-R-019/020 evaluate an IBAN mod 97 over a 24+ digit integer that lib decimal (i64) cannot hold.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_36 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 36u32, "2026-10-29T18:14Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 14:14 fiscal: re-proven on PACK 6b (node stage spiral-bin-1029-6b, host 9895730DAE80, core 31CC96520D6B7269), mirrors freshly synced: DE-R-019/020 evaluation fix DRAFTED, held as fiscal/lib-programs/xpath-mod-and-long-integers.kit (decimal 99EB6B29 -> B9AC478A, xpath_eval 1AB4EE5A -> BB243652; rehearsed): XPath 'mod' was entirely unsupported in xpath_eval (every rule using it failed); decimal.parse had no overflow guard (a 24-digit IBAN number overflowed i64, a panic in debug Rust). Now decimal.parse returns None past i64, decimal.modulo (dividend's sign, common scale) backs 'mod', and a too-long all-digit dividend (xs:integer keeps it as its digits) folds digit by digit. Tests: modulo_and_the_i64_bound_follow_xpath; mod_follows_xpath_and_checks_an_iban, including DE-R-019's full for/string-to-codepoints expression on DE89370400440532013000 = 1. 6b gates: decimal 4/4, 0 type errors; xpath_eval running.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_37 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 37u32, "2026-10-29T18:33Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 14:33 fiscal: xpath-mod-and-long-integers PROVEN on pack 6b (mirror mod1029, A4E-free pin 9895730DAE80/31CC9652): decimal 4/4 incl modulo_and_the_i64_bound_follow_xpath; xpath_eval 7/7 incl mod_follows_xpath_and_checks_an_iban (DE-R-019's full IBAN expression on DE89370400440532013000 = 1); 0 type errors. Lands 4th in the post-TRAIN4 slot (main agreed).")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_38 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 38u32, "2026-10-29T19:28Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 15:28 fiscal: xpath-mod-and-long-integers LANDED 15:19:10 (decimal 99EB6B29 -> B9AC478A, xpath_eval 1AB4EE5A -> BB243652), via lib-guarded-do in the 15:18 gap (no exemptions), hash equal to the pack-6b-proven copy (node stage spiral-bin-1029-6b, core 31CC96520D6B7269); main's closing document_test 22/22 over all gap lands. Byte-exact undo copies: C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\land-1029\\{m7,sch2,mod,cells64b}\\base (not git HEAD: other lanes' unstaged lib hunks). XPath mod works, decimal.parse no longer overflows on long digit strings, and DE-R-019/020's IBAN check evaluates (test on DE89370400440532013000 = 1). Next: a full Peppol evaluation run over its samples.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_39 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 39u32, "2026-10-29T22:07Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 18:07 fiscal: PEPPOL ROOT CAUSE (fiscal-6b-eval2-peppol_exa, rule ids now in the failure text): the only Peppol failure left is CEN BR-CO-17 on examples/vat-category-O.xml (peppol rules: none). The category-O disjunct not(exists(cac:TaxCategory[..]/xs:decimal(cbc:Percent))) fails because xpath_eval.mapped_each kept a step's empty result as a nested VSequence [VSequence []], which is_empty_value does not see as empty. Fix drafted as held program fiscal/lib-programs/xpath-path-step-flattens.kit (xpath_eval BB243652 -> 38FCB953: flatten step values via sequence_items, VNodes when nothing remains; 2 regression lines in evaluates_en16931_style_rules), rehearsed hash-equal, proving as fiscal-6b-seqflat-proof. Next: land, then rerun peppol_examples_pass_the_peppol_rules.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_40 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 40u32, "2026-10-29T23:05Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 19:05 fiscal: PEPPOL EVALUATION GREEN on the combined lib drafts (fiscal-6b-zfn2-peppol, mirror zfn6b = live lib + schematron-pattern-lets-shared + xpath-path-step-flattens + xpath-floor-pictures-errors, pack 6b): peppol_examples_pass_the_peppol_rules HOLDS (329.6 s, memo_hits 0). Every Peppol BIS 3.0.20 example passes the Peppol and CEN EN16931 UBL schematrons with zero fatal findings, and the and/or error propagation surfaced no hidden failure. The test turns green in the tree once these programs land (next session's first window, per main).")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_41 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 41u32, "2026-10-29T23:58Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 19:58 fiscal: the lib fixes behind the green Peppol evaluation LANDED in window 4 (schematron_run B9D3079F, xpath_eval BFFB32F6, xpath BD24C126), so peppol_examples_pass_the_peppol_rules should now be green against the live lib.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_42 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 42u32, "2026-10-30T00:49Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 20:49 fiscal: PEPPOL GREEN ON THE POST-WINDOW-4 LIB (fiscal-6b-post4-peppol, job-1793320026890, mirror gate4b: file_system 81140E3E5A74, physics B1A4E84872AD, sm' 2196F9C70148, landed schematron_run B9D3079F / xpath_eval BFFB32F6 / xpath BD24C126 / schematron C36C6296; corpus_checks 6695FADB; pack 6b): peppol_examples_pass_the_peppol_rules HOLDS (374.6 s). This replaces note 41's 'should now be green'.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_43 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 43u32, "2026-10-30T22:53Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 18:52 fiscal: GROOM R1: user-batch. Its only agent dep, XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS, closed today (namespace claim re-proven on the live lib), and its evaluation is green on the post-land lib, so the one open step is your commit of fiscal src/corpus_checks.spi (and the generator changes it reads). No further agent work.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_44 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 44u32, "2026-11-01T03:37Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 23:35 fiscal: CLOSING (groom 10-31 night): its open step is done: peppol_examples_pass_the_peppol_rules is in the committed src/corpus_checks.spi (85274a9) and passed on the box m4 run (10-30); the BIS 3.0.20 structure bindings are now fetched by init.ps1 too (canon).")
inl note_of_fiscal_in_gst_einvoice_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-IN-GST-EINVOICE", 1u32, "2026-10-27T11:32Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 07:32 fiscal (user 10-27 06:3x: add most suggested countries, as generic as possible): Source: the JSON Schema (draft-07) is embedded in https://einv-apisandbox.nic.in/version1.03/generate-irn.html#JSONSchema, verified only through a Wayback snapshot (web.archive.org/web/20241005055248/...); from the review box einvoice1.gst.gov.in does not resolve and the sandbox times out, so 1.1 being current is UNVERIFIED. Plan: init.ps1 extracts the schema from the page (or the snapshot), pinned by hash; generator family source JsonSchema (source union landed 10-27, generator.spi family_schema); example and round trip through json_schema.json_document / json_document_text (writer landed 10-27).")
inl note_of_fiscal_in_gst_einvoice_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-IN-GST-EINVOICE", 2u32, "2026-10-27T12:56Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 08:56 fiscal: IN THE TREE, unstaged (fiscal generator.spi E3FD312C, scripts/init.ps1). (1) Schema source: init.ps1 fetches the NIC sandbox page through the Wayback snapshot of 2024-10-05 (reachable from here; the live NIC hosts are not), extracts the JSON Schema from its <pre> block, and REFUSES unless its sha256 starts 2F53D00F2F754722. The published schema is NOT standard draft-07: its 15 sections sit at the root (no properties/type), the key 'AddlDocDtls ' and an inner 'type ' carry trailing spaces, and ItemList/AddlDocDtls are written as one-element arrays holding the item schema. init keeps the raw copy (deps/corpus/in/gst/inv01_published.json) and writes a standard one (inv01_1.1.json) by three recorded rules: root sections under properties with type object; every key trimmed; a one-schema array inside properties becomes type array + items. Checked: root object, 15 properties, 7 required, ItemList an array of objects with 30 properties, 0 keys with spaces. (2) Generator: family gst_inv01_1_1 (module generated_in_gst_inv01_1_1, root GstInvoice, source JsonSchema) with test generates_gst_inv01_1_1; a JSON family's example test writes <module>_example.json through json_schema.json_document_text (schema read at run time by its repo-relative path) and then ROUND-TRIPS it: json_document -> typed _of_xml -> _to_xml -> json text, failing unless identical; the XML-only bench is skipped for JSON families. Type-checked (generator + probe 0 errors), formatter no-op. Next: node proof (regeneration + the unit's example test).")
inl note_of_fiscal_in_gst_einvoice_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-IN-GST-EINVOICE", 3u32, "2026-10-27T14:54Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 10:54 fiscal: an independent JSON referee FOUND THREE MORE DEFECTS in NIC's published schema, each silently corrupting our generated model: PowerShell's Test-Json (a strict draft-07 validator) refused to even parse the normalized schema, and each refusal led to one: (a) type VALUES with stray spaces ('string ' x2, ' number' x1, 'object ' x1): our front end compares type names exactly, so ' number' became a string field and 'object ' would have flattened a whole section into one string; (b) 'String' with a capital S (the two Ph fields); (c) RefDtls carries a 'required': [InvNo, InvDt] list INSIDE its properties, which our front end would have generated as a bogus field named 'required'. init.ps1's normalization now has 5 recorded rules (sections under properties; keys trimmed; type values trimmed and lowercased; a misplaced required list moved up to its object; one-schema arrays as type array + items); refetched; Test-Json now parses it and correctly rejects a partial document for its 6 missing required sections. family-gates.ps1 now judges India's JSON example with Test-Json against this schema (a '== ...json' section with 'validation messages N', so proofs read it like every XML sample). Known gap, recorded not fixed: 6 of 91 GST patterns use ECMA-262 lookaround ('^(?!0+\\$)...') which XSD's regex dialect lacks; our front end passes JSON patterns into XSD pattern facets, so those 6 need an ECMA->XSD translation or a validated-in-code fallback (next step for this item).")
inl note_of_fiscal_in_gst_einvoice_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-IN-GST-EINVOICE", 4u32, "2026-10-27T15:01Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 11:01 fiscal: the regex-dialect gap is CLOSED at the boundary: every GST pattern is now XSD-expressible (0 patterns with '(?' left), by two more recorded normalization rules in init.ps1 (7 in all), each exact and each refusing what it cannot translate exactly: rule 6, the not-all-zeros idiom '^(?!0+\\$)(<digit runs>)\\$' (Stcd x4, Pos, HsnCd) becomes the union of '0{k}[1-9][0-9]{n-k-1}' over each run length, proven by brute force against .NET's regex: 0 disagreements over 711,134 strings for both shapes ('[0-9]{1,2}' and '[0-9]{4}|[0-9]{6}|[0-9]{8}'); rule 7, a '(?i)' case-insensitive word list (SupTyp, Typ) drops the flag and expands each letter to [xX] (0 disagreements on 14 probes incl. mixed case and near misses); a lookaround or (?i) pattern of any other shape now THROWS in init (that guard caught the (?i) ones on its first run, and the partial-fetch trap removed the half-written folder). Test-Json still parses the result and rejects partial documents. The all-proof running now used the schema from before these fixes; the next proof regenerates India from this one.")
inl note_of_fiscal_in_gst_einvoice_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-IN-GST-EINVOICE", 5u32, "2026-10-27T15:24Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 11:24 fiscal: LIB TESTS PASS on the node (all-proof job-1793112172864, Cells lib_gate per module, process compiler, memo off, full logs kept): xsd 8/8, xsd_resolve 4/4, xsd_emit 17/17, json_schema 5/5, xml 10/10 (13 rows), every one of today's new tests present and green. json_schema's element_trees_write_back_to_the_json_their_schema_describes (the JSON writer) and number_bounds_become_the_xsd_range_facets pass.")
inl note_of_fiscal_in_gst_einvoice_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-IN-GST-EINVOICE", 6u32, "2026-10-27T18:41Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 14:41 fiscal: all-proof GST unit FAILED (writes_its_example panicked: not a valid seller Stcd). Cause: the node's in/gst came via the corpus zip, and init normalized only inside the fetch guard, so the node generated from the raw lookahead schema. FIX IN THE TREE: init guards only the fetch (inv01_published.json), then re-checks the pin and derives inv01_1.1.json every run. Verified: unchanged bytes on a normal run; control (raw file in place) is rewritten to the exact normalized bytes.")
inl note_of_fiscal_in_gst_einvoice_7 () = Note ("FISCAL-IN-GST-EINVOICE", 7u32, "2026-10-27T22:28Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 18:28 fiscal: IN THE TREE: (1) the official NIC sample request was INVALID against our normalized schema, exposing 2 normalization bugs: a stray required list went to the enclosing object (RefDtls) instead of the sibling whose items hold the names (PrecDocDtls), and names inside required lists were not trimmed (' InvStDt '). Fixed in init; all 13 required lists checked, controls rejected. (2) init derives the sample (pinned AB5BC97C, nulls dropped) to in/gst/examples; the family lists it; the generator emits a JSON document cell (json_document_checks) comparing schema-ordered text. Generator type-checks.")
