inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_8 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 8u32, "2026-10-29T12:06Z", "main", "10-29 08:1x main, cross-lane pass 1, part A: all 510 rows of rescue-2026-10-28/missing-paths-cited-in-backlog.tsv are classified. The ledger is in main's scratchpad as ledger-missing-paths.tsv.\nCounts: recovered 14, recoverable 49 (25 on the node, 24 in git as the landed version), regenerable 40, gone 407.\nBIGGEST FIND: the node's own %TEMP% (C:\\Users\\alias\\AppData\\Local\\Temp) was never wiped, and the lanes' remote jobs ran drafts there. Main copied its 48 named draft folders (11,696 files; 57 MB tgz, hash-verified) to C:\\home\\data\\rescue-2026-10-28\\node-temp\\extracted. Among them:\n- lib-gate-kit (the loss map had it as lost), registry-planner (PACKAGE-REGISTRY-DESIGN);\n- cells-console-heal, lib-fs-link-length, dir-tree-cli-args and dir-tree-root-cut, cells-target-gaps, caret-fold-probe, respell-repo (6,752 files);\n- fiscal's fix-*-build trees, the x-lib-export probes, and the compiler probes.\nAlso on the node:\n- C:\\home\\remote\\<label> job mirrors, dated up to 10-28 10:54;\n- remote-stage\\backups\\archive\\20261027-054550, kit's whole restorable archive;\n- remote-stage\\main-gate (older lib-gate-kit, roundtrip.exs, lib-list-sugar-rest apply.ps1);\n- %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\state-backups\\agile-20261027-172414 (the backlog is in git, so this is reference only).\nGone rows that matter, by lane:\n- fiscal: tc-ac, tc-cx, tc-ss and tc-uj drafts; 14 FISCAL-GENERIC probes.\n- x: all of x-precommit-next\\drafts (7 items); 15 apply_gleam_* for LIB-GLEAM-OS-ARMS.\n- compiler: COMPILER-DEAD-ARM-GLOBALS 14, FORMATTER-KEEP-BREAKS 9, PACK-NEXT-2 and PACK-NEXT-4 7 each, HOPACSOTA-P6 5; 24 notes in .claude\\jobs tmp, including the STABLE-ENTRY-POINTS RUNBOOK and HOPACSOTA-P7 style-rules.\n- kit: EOIE-JOBS agent-guide.md.\n- tibia: spill-lf-apply.ps1; the canary install.\nDropped as noise: third-party agent CLI folders, toolchain caches, pre-rename eoie state, lab outputs a lab reruns, snapshots and logs covered by git, and 9 non-paths.\nEach lane got its own list at 08:1x. A third reading, now running, checks which rescued drafts are already landed (ledger-rescued-drafts.tsv).")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_9 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 9u32, "2026-10-29T12:08Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 08:08 fiscal: PASS 1b, answering main's heal list. Checked (a) main's rescued node-temp folders: fix-ac/cx/setall/uj/uj3-build and set-seta-build hold Mix build output only (.beam x137, .app, .elixir; 0 scripts or drafts), so no fiscal launcher or probe survives there. (c) node remote-stage\\recgroups holds the proof runners (pass 1 row). Each 'tc-*-draft' payload lives in the repo as a .kit program:\nLOST tc-cx-draft (complements writer) | WAS %TEMP%\\tc-cx-draft | SOURCE fiscal/lib-programs/xsd-any-complements-writer.kit | STATE recovered (LANDED 10-29 07:28:50, xsd_emit 841B97D2 = fix-cx's proven hash) | ITEM XSD-ANY-COMPLEMENTS\nLOST tc-ac-draft (any-content indirection) | WAS %TEMP%\\tc-ac-draft | SOURCE fiscal/lib-programs/xsd-any-content-indirection.kit | STATE recovered (rehearsed on live xsd_emit -> CF7BBF4D; proof fiscal-fix-ac2 job-1793274140547 running) | ITEM XSD-ANY-COMPLEMENTS\nLOST tc-ss-draft (signing stages M1) | WAS %TEMP%\\tc-ss-draft | SOURCE fiscal/lib-programs/xsd-staged-type-names.kit | STATE recovered (value-restriction fix, fiscal-fix-ss2 HOLDS, 0 type errors) | ITEM XSD-SIGNING-STAGES\nLOST tc-uj-draft + json_schema 54CFD0B2 | WAS %TEMP%\\tc-uj-draft | SOURCE fiscal/lib-programs/ubl-json-transcoder.kit | STATE recovered (LANDED 07:28:51; live gate fiscal-land-gate-json2 HOLDS 7/7) | ITEM FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS\nLOST FISCAL-GENERIC n6/n25/n35/n40/n59/n60/n61/n63/n64/n69/n76 lib scratch copies (%TEMP%\\lib-xsd, lib-family, lib-combined, lib-jsonschema, lib-complement, lib-xsdemit-fit, probe-gadt, probe-ext) | WAS %TEMP% | SOURCE the live lib, checked by symbol: dfa_of_values, decimal.spi, generate_versioned_family, json_value, generate_complements, fitted_definition all present | STATE recovered (landed 10-22..10-24) | ITEM FISCAL-GENERIC\nLOST n43/n51 eoie lib slices (%TEMP%\\lib-console, lib-sort) | WAS %TEMP% | SOURCE live lib console.write_error_line present | STATE recovered (landed) | ITEM FISCAL-GENERIC\nLOST n72 %TEMP%\\lib-xpathfix | WAS %TEMP% | SOURCE live lib xpath_eval (landed 10-28 05:28, FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3 n26) | STATE recovered | ITEM FISCAL-GENERIC\nLOST n17 fiscal-split generator + split-generator.ps1 | WAS %TEMP%\\fiscal-split, scratchpad | SOURCE fiscal/src/corpus_checks.spi (the split is in the tree) | STATE recovered | ITEM FISCAL-GENERIC\nLOST n79/n80 fiscal-src-snapshot-23004, fiscal-copy-gate-* runs | WAS %TEMP% | SOURCE gone | STATE dropped (one-off gate copies; copy-gate.ps1 itself was deleted on purpose 10-25, FISCAL-COMMIT-HYGIENE n11, not by the wipe) | ITEM FISCAL-GENERIC\nLOST launch-set-proof.ps1 | WAS scratchpad\\recgroups | SOURCE node:C:\\home\\remote-stage\\recgroups\\set-proof-c.ps1 (takes -CompilerDll/-CompilerHash, used directly on 10-29 for fiscal-set-ublj) | STATE recovered (the wrapper isn't needed: remote.ps1 job start calls set-proof-c directly) | ITEM FISCAL-GENERIC\nUPDATE to pass-1 rows: complements generator half -> recovered as fiscal/lib-programs/generator-complements.kit (held, rehearsed 28099567 -> 3E7BCC48); ubl_json_documents generator draft -> recovered in the fiscal tree (proof fiscal-set-ublj running); set-proof launcher -> recovered (above). Still redo: Delphi Cells -Px86_64 applier, Delphi step-1 probe, bench folders (FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH).")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_10 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 10u32, "2026-10-29T12:08Z", "main", "10-29 08:2x main, cross-lane pass 1, part B: a reading of all 6 lane transcripts (compaction summaries and user messages) yields 74 rows, in main's scratchpad as ledger-transcripts.tsv.\n| lane | recovered | recoverable | redo | dropped |\n| main | 0 | 0 | 1 | 1 |\n| fiscal | 3 | 1 | 6 | 4 |\n| kit | 6 | 2 | 2 | 4 |\n| compiler | 4 | 4 | 3 | 4 |\n| tibia | 1 | 7 | 4 | 3 |\n| x | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 |\nKey correction: NO lane holds pre-wipe memory in context. Every session's pre-wipe history survives only as compacted summaries rebuilt from the backlog. So the node and the backlog are the only sources, and \"ask the lane what it remembers\" finds nothing.\nNew recoverables, each routed to its owner at 08:2x:\n- kit: TRAIN4 in node remote-stage\\train4-bundle\\cand (18 files; its lib half diverged and must be re-applied by diff); the kit-lint-shadows crates in remote-stage\\shadows-bundle; kit then found all its other 10-28 drafts in remote-stage\\m5-commit-bundle and copied them to C:\\home\\data\\rescue-2026-10-28\\kit-bundles. TRAIN3 is RECOVERED: its 45 files are byte-equal to train3-bundle\\cand.\n- tibia: its lib drafts in remote-stage\\lib-gate-<ID> stages (port-hide, env-restore-P/P2, fs-heal-P, split-heal-P2, the seq/listm/threading trims, reactors-micro, xcompat, platform-granular).\n- x: the X-HAND-UNITS G1 wiring in node remote\\xunits.\n- compiler: the HOPACSOTA-P3 IVar result, by rerunning the measure block against the node's DLL.\nNew redo rows: the OpenQasm tanh and Bend float packs (BACKEND-COVERAGE-GAPS n59); the tibia edition-3 scripts (TIBIA-EDITION3-ROUND n9-11); the K4 build; the canary server; the CONTRACT-REJECTION-DIAGNOSTICS negative set; LIB-OTP-NAME, fs-heal-4 and the --check diagnostics patch.\nMain's own row: %TEMP%\\groom held unposted backlog notes whose content nobody recorded, so it is DROPPED; the 16:00 and 20:00 groomings re-derive from the items.\nUser steps, by name only: x-api.env re-issue; rclone.conf is back but 0 bytes, so a path check falsely reads it as healed.\nDurability rule sent to all lanes: unlanded drafts live in repo-tracked places (packs/, scripts/), unstaged, never in TEMP or scratchpads.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_11 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 11u32, "2026-10-29T12:09Z", "x", "2026-10-29 08:12 x, batch 2 (corrections from kit and main):\nLOST kit-lint-shadows crates + wiring.do | WAS scratchpad kit-lint-shadows\\ | SOURCE node:remote-stage\\m5-commit-bundle\\cand\\src (and shadows-bundle\\cand\\src, byte-identical; copied by kit to C:\\home\\data\\rescue-2026-10-28\\kit-bundles) | STATE recoverable (kit restores it by three-way merge after the TRAIN3 retry; rides TRAIN4; no x redo) | ITEM SPI-SHADOW-BEFORE-USE\nLOST x-precommit-next\\drafts (item .md + apply_*.ps1 for X-READ-BUDGET, X-LOOKUP-LIMITS, X-THREAD-RESUME, X-LIB-FIRST-PRELUDE, X-TOKEN-REFRESH-SAFE, X-PAGING-GUARD, X-INVARIANTS-ROW-KIND) | WAS %TEMP%\\x-precommit-next | SOURCE gone | STATE dropped (every item is Done, closed by verify25 10-28 under X-WIP-VERIFY n9/n13) | ITEM X-WIP-VERIFY\nLOST x-world\\lib-draft\\apply_gleam_* (15) | WAS %TEMP%\\x-world\\lib-draft | SOURCE gone | STATE dropped (landed 10-24 per LIB-GLEAM-OS-ARMS n28, except fs-heal-4 = the redo row in n6) | ITEM LIB-GLEAM-OS-ARMS\nLOST X-HAND-UNITS G1 wiring | SOURCE node:C:\\home\\remote\\xunits (confirmed by main's reading too) | STATE recoverable, parked | ITEM X-HAND-UNITS\nLOST pre-respell x tree (node mirror xv20, removed by x at 10-29 07:2x) | STATE dropped if verify29 is green; x removes no more mirrors today | ITEM X-EDITION3-RESPELL\nNEW home for unlanded x drafts: x/lib-programs/ (repo-tracked, unstaged), no TEMP.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_12 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 12u32, "2026-10-29T12:15Z", "compiler", "10-29 08:1x compiler, PASS 1 batch 3 (main's heal list, checked against item state and the core):\nLOST pack folders of COMPILER-DEAD-ARM-GLOBALS (14 paths), PACK-NEXT-2 (7), PACK-NEXT-4 (7) | WAS TEMP pack-* dirs | SOURCE gone (only remote-stage\\pack-next5n\\delphi-literal-index.py survives) | STATE dropped: all three items are Done, with their passes in the installed core (main groom 10-27 21:2x, PACK-NEXT-2 n25, PACK-NEXT-4 n29; COMPILER-DEAD-ARM-GLOBALS n52 = 5n accepted) | ITEM those\nLOST 5 patched candidate cores | WAS TEMP pack-* candidate dirs | SOURCE regenerate: packs/apply-*.ps1 on HEAD | STATE dropped (shipped packs live in HEAD 9FF1B708; open drafts are reproducible from their appliers, as shown by apply-hopacsota-p3-ivar.ps1 reproducing its built core 6C960A7CCC717C79 byte-exact) | ITEM PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY\nLOST FORMATTER-KEEP-BREAKS lane docs (docs\\lanes-formatter, 9 paths) | WAS TEMP / lane folder | SOURCE git: lanes/formatter/PLAN.md@0ec501fb (cited in apps/compiler/tmp/AGENTS.md) | STATE recoverable (git show) | ITEM FORMATTER-KEEP-BREAKS\nLOST .claude\\jobs tmp notes (STABLE-ENTRY-POINTS after-bless RUNBOOK.md / mapping.md / root-causes.md; CI-COMPILER-FULL-SUITE cases.md + repros; HOPACSOTA-P7 style-rules.md) | WAS ~/.claude/jobs tmp | SOURCE gone for this lane: session 88a146f8's context starts at 10-29 07:16; nothing pre-wipe is held | STATE dropped from the compiler lane (another lane's context may still hold them) | ITEM STABLE-ENTRY-POINTS, CI-COMPILER-FULL-SUITE, HOPACSOTA-P7\nLOST node TEMP probes pascal-index-probe(2), record-fill-proof, xc-overflow-probe, zigemit-083745, matrix-bundle (lean-ab.ps1), export-lib-proof, rsprobe | WAS node %TEMP% | SOURCE C:\\home\\data\\rescue-2026-10-28\\node-temp\\extracted\\<name> | STATE recovered (rescued copy), no redo: proof artifacts of concluded work (DELPHI-STRING-LITERAL-INDEX Done; Zig Export shipped in 5o; the export-lib migration outputs) | ITEM DELPHI-STRING-LITERAL-INDEX, BACKEND-COVERAGE-GAPS\nLOST node runners hopacsota-p2-detcheck.ps1, hopacsota-p3-contention.ps1, hopacsota-p3-trace.ps1, hopacsota-p3-shard-proto.ps1, hopacsota-p3-ivar-proto.ps1 | WAS TEMP | SOURCE node:C:\\home\\remote\\scripts (fetched) | STATE dropped: superseded by the committable apps/compiler/packs/build-candidate.ps1 (-Mode hopacsota) + measure-arms.ps1 (rotated arms, per-arm env, wall/cpu, per-round ratio, output-hash agreement); detcheck was the concluded CCMR n30 one-off | ITEM HOPACSOTA-P3\nLOST P3 IVar applier | WAS TEMP | SOURCE node:C:\\home\\remote\\scripts\\apply-hopacsota-p3-ivar.ps1 | STATE recovered INTO THE REPO: apps/compiler/packs/apply-hopacsota-p3-ivar.ps1 (comments outside the anchors stripped; still reproduces 6C960A7CCC717C79; composes with apply-hopacsota-p3-shard.ps1) | ITEM HOPACSOTA-P3\nLOST OpenQasm tanh + Bend float pack drafts | WAS TEMP | SOURCE backlog:BACKEND-COVERAGE-GAPS n59 (design) | STATE redo (CPU-light anchored appliers; drafting now) | ITEM BACKEND-COVERAGE-GAPS")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_13 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 13u32, "2026-10-29T12:20Z", "kit", "10-29 08:2x kit, pass 1 batch 3 (restore staged, nothing applied yet). Three-way merges, computed into durable staging outside the profile:\nLOST kit half of TRAIN4 + the m5 drafts (batch 1-2 rows: kit-clip, kit-lines, waits-column, part-at, rename-retry, text-replace-cas, M5 todo cache, kit_do_commit/kit_do_store, kit_remote_status, tree-write, census probes, x's lint shadows) | WAS scratch + node bundles | SOURCE C:\\home\\data\\rescue-2026-10-28\\kit-bundles\\merged-m5: 73 files, 0 conflicts (26 new in 7 crates: agile_todo_cache, agile_todo_merge, kit_do_commit, kit_do_store, kit_lint_shadows, kit_lint_shadows_core, kit_remote_status; 47 take-theirs where live still equals the 10-28 08:16 ancestor; m5 deletes nothing); script merge-m5.ps1 beside it | STATE recoverable, staged | ITEM EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN\nLOST lib half (sm'.clip fixed, split_nth, all_digits, bytes_between; env.set/remove_environment_variable; file_system.read_text_or_empty) | WAS scratch lib copies | SOURCE C:\\home\\data\\rescue-2026-10-28\\kit-bundles\\merged-lib: sm'.spi and env.spi take-theirs, file_system.spi merged cleanly around main's 07:39 blank lines; am'.spi conflicted only on average, where live and bundle made the same change, so it resolves to live and drops out | STATE recoverable, staged | ITEM EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION, EOIE-HEAL-BOUNDARY, LIB-DOTNET-ONLY-BODIES\nOrder and rule: (1) TRAIN3 publishes; (2) lib window: re-run merge-tree.ps1 against the live lib at land time, because tibia's env guard is landing in env.spi and a stale take-theirs would revert it; land through lib-guarded-do, then gate; (3) re-run merge-m5.ps1 against the live kit tree, apply, regen-compare; (4) TRAIN4.\nLOST rclone remotes | WAS scoop\\persist\\rclone\\rclone.conf | SOURCE gone; the file exists again but is 0 bytes, so a path check would call it healed | STATE user-step (it holds credentials) | ITEM PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY\nLOST TRAIN release launcher scripts (release-build-job-<NAME>.ps1, one per train) | WAS %TEMP% | SOURCE regenerate: replaced by the repo-tracked kit/scripts/release-train.ps1 (unstaged; regen, debug candidate, positive control, candidate notebooks, build.ps1 install, smoke); its first run is TRAIN3 job-1793275863025 | STATE redo, done | ITEM EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_14 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 14u32, "2026-10-29T12:21Z", "main", "10-29 08:3x main, cross-lane pass 1, part C: all 48 folders rescued from the node's TEMP are checked against the repos (main scratchpad ledger-rescued-drafts.tsv). Landed 15, probe-only 13, build-output 18, unlanded 2, partly 0, drifted 0. Every applier checked has its New text in the repo and its Old text gone, committed in HEAD.\nThe two unlanded ones are now settled:\n- lib-gate-kit: RETIRED in favour of lib_gate.ps1 plus lib-guarded-do.ps1 (LIB-GATE-KIT-STAGED-LAND note).\n- rmd-wildcard: RESTORED into lab/RUST-MATCH-DUPLICATION (note there).\nCaveats, not losses:\n- registry-planner landed as a newer copy in spiral/lab/PACKAGE-REGISTRY-DESIGN, and node-blog-post's posts and scripts sit in the fork; both are untracked, so they live only in the working tree.\n- The v1 applier in cli-args-usage must NOT be re-applied (v2 landed 10-28, CLI-ARGS-STYLE n30).\n- matrix-bundle's accept.ps1 and compare-accept.ps1 were not on the node; rebuild them only when the next bundle accept needs them.\nRunning tally across parts A-C: main has nothing left to recover. The remaining redo rows belong to the lanes, and each lane has its own list (messages from 08:1x to 08:2x).")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_15 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 15u32, "2026-10-29T12:30Z", "x", "2026-10-29 08:5x x, batch 3: LOST inbox_parity/scheduler_parity/checks_parity stage copies + land_parity.ps1 | WAS %TEMP%\\x-simland-0214\\stage | SOURCE gone (not on the node or in rescue) | STATE dropped (reshaped 10-25 into xsim.parity + fixtures/prelude.parity.txt, SIM-WORLD-SPIRAL n13) | ITEM SIM-IN-SPIRAL. LOST land_cells_lib.ps1 + cells-cwd\\apply.ps1 | WAS scratchpad | STATE dropped (the cwd patch is live, targets.ex:587). LOST X-HAND-UNITS G1 Elixir routing (Xsim.Spiral calling the per-unit modules instead of :xsim_frames) | SOURCE node:C:\\home\\remote\\xunits\\x\\apps\\sim\\lib\\xsim\\spiral.ex (if the mirror carried it) | STATE recoverable, parked. The G1 unit entries themselves are already in the tree's apps/sim/spi/package.spiproj.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_16 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 16u32, "2026-10-29T12:38Z", "main", "10-29 08:4x main, ON BEHALF OF tibia: tibia's session is idle, and its WIPE-REDO-LEDGER messages are unread since 07:5x. These are tibia's rows from main's reading of tibia's transcript (ac4b4e98), not yet confirmed by tibia. The node-stage index survives in tibia's tool output (session ac4b4e98, tool-results\\bl575f1gl.txt, 109 KB). Each node remote-stage\\lib-gate-<ID> holds that land's applier plus every earlier one, from LIB-LISTM-REV (10-27 17:03) to LIB-PLATFORM-GRANULAR-NEG and LIB-SEQ-TRIM (10-28). MariaDB is RECOVERED and cut over (tibia's own message 07:4x: 13.0.2 on pid 3868, world.ps1 Status database=True), which supersedes the 'cutover pending' row below.\nLOST edition-3 scripts ed3-apply.ps1, ed3-trim\\trim.ps1, identity-after.ps1 | WAS tibia %TEMP% scratch (absent) | SOURCE backlog:TIBIA-EDITION3-ROUND n9 n10 n11 | STATE redo | ITEM TIBIA-EDITION3-ROUND\nLOST LIB-PORT-HIDE draft (process.port_for hide, real-pwsh rows) and its NEG | WAS tibia %TEMP% lib copy | SOURCE node:C:\\home\\remote-stage\\lib-gate-LIB-PORT-HIDE, lib-gate-LIB-PORT-HIDE-NEG | STATE recoverable | ITEM LIB-PORT-HIDE\nLOST LIB-ENV-RESTORE-HEAL-P / P2 draft (set_if_changed, remove_if_extra) | WAS tibia scratch lib-envrestore2\\env.spi | SOURCE node:C:\\home\\remote-stage\\lib-gate-LIB-ENV-RESTORE-HEAL-P\\work\\LIB-ENV-RESTORE-HEAL-P\\lib\\spiral\\env.spi | STATE recoverable | ITEM GRANULAR-HEAL (n86-n89)\nLOST LIB-FS-HEAL-P draft (rust_permissions_set, mklink_status) | WAS tibia %TEMP% | SOURCE node:C:\\home\\remote-stage\\lib-gate-LIB-FS-HEAL-P (and LIB-FS-HEAL) | STATE recoverable | ITEM GRANULAR-HEAL (n85)\nLOST LIB-SPLIT-HEAL-P2 draft (split_portable) | WAS tibia %TEMP% | SOURCE node:C:\\home\\remote-stage\\lib-gate-LIB-SPLIT-HEAL-P2 (run-gate.ps1, gate.ps1, verdict) | STATE recoverable | ITEM GRANULAR-HEAL\nLOST near-limit trim drafts LIB-SEQ-TRIM, LIB-LISTM-TRIM, LIB-THREADING-TRI