inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_30 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 30u32, "2026-10-29T16:16Z", "main", "10-29 12:1x main, SWEEP 3 (transcripts 15:12Z to ~16:09Z; main scratchpad sweep-3.tsv): 17 rows, 1 new loss, 2 unposted recoveries, 2 contradictions, 3 unanswered nudges, 9 hazards. Closed since sweep 2: x's fs-heal-4 (n28, unblocked by main's diff of tibia's rescued applier) and x's switch off the stale kit copy.\nMain's rows:\n- LOST: 5 scoop apps half-installed since the wipe | WAS ~/scoop/apps/{fork, greenshot, notepadplusplus, systeminformer-nightly, wfc}/current (no manifest.json) | SOURCE regenerate: scoop reinstall | STATE redo, a USER step (4 are running GUI apps; wfc is firewall software) | ITEM PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY n24.\n- SELF-CORRECTION 1: main told kit to land with -ExemptAncestry 'CompilerDaemon\\.serve_app'. That matches EVERY Cells daemon, not just main's TEMP-copy one, so it was too broad; it was WITHDRAWN at 12:1x. It is moot, since main's sm' job has been stopped since 12:09, and x's Test-CopyDaemon (n5 of NODE-MIRROR-CELLS-DEPS) now attributes copy daemons without vouching.\n- SELF-CORRECTION 2: the 16:00Z canonical re-land of env.spi bypassed lib-guarded-do. It ran main's own equivalent guard (a live-erl reader check excluding TEMP copies, and a hash check that live = the proven BB39D5562692 before writing), but future lands go through lib-guarded-do.\n- GAP: the only post-land document_test (16:01Z) predates x's 2 lands, kit's merged-lib, main's file_system guard and fiscal's lander6. One final document_test is scheduled after the last land of the window.\nRouted: git-a6, two checks before the pack-6 install (the 2 Zig build-fails must reproduce baseline-identical at -Parallel 1; and whether any of the 74 recompiled rows import a file landed in between) plus pinning the installed kit, not the newest supervisor exe (8CD04145 looks like kit's TRAIN4 candidate); kit, re-merge and hash-prove at land time, and ledger TRAIN3 published and KIT-PENDING