inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_31 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 31u32, "2026-10-29T16:16Z", "kit", "10-29 12:1x kit, pass 2 rows (TRAIN3 and closes):\nLOST TRAIN3 release (published only after a retry) | WAS kit lane, train staged in %TEMP% | SOURCE live tree + scripts/release-train.ps1 | STATE recovered: PUBLISHED 11:35, installed kit.exe CD2F0D1A (was A5B55974); closeout on the installed binary 7/7, with an A5B55974 control in which the 4 discriminating checks FAIL; lane copy %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\bin\\kit.exe swapped to CD2F0D1A | ITEM EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN (n182)\nLOST KIT-PENDING-DANGLING's moved test (pending-test-fix.do) | WAS scratch | SOURCE live tree | STATE recovered and DONE: files.spi notebook 1/1 on the installed code, no dangling *.pending | ITEM KIT-PENDING-DANGLING (n4)\nLOST TRAIN3-era items that only needed the release: KIT-LINT-DOLLAR-LITERAL, EOIE-JOB-START-SETTLE, EOIE-JOBS-DOCTOR | WAS in the lost train | SOURCE TRAIN3 install | STATE DONE, each verified live on CD2F0D1A | ITEM same ids\nLOST TRAIN4 content (m5-commit-bundle drafts) | WAS scratch + node bundles | SOURCE restored into kit/src at 11:57 (73 files, 0 conflicts) together with today's post-TRAIN3 drafts | STATE recovered (staged), ships in TRAIN4 after kit's lib land | ITEM EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN (n183)")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_32 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 32u32, "2026-10-29T17:38Z", "main", "10-29 13:4x main, SWEEP 4 (transcripts 16:09Z to ~17:10Z; main scratchpad sweep-4.tsv): 16 rows, 0 new losses, 3 unposted recoveries, 1 contradiction, 3 unanswered nudges, 9 hazards.\nMain's rows, all closed:\n- RECOVERED: the compiler install procedure (install-p2.ps1, lost with TEMP) is rebuilt as apps/compiler/packs/install-pack.ps1. It is hardened: it backs up the whole bin folder and fails unless the SYSTEM dotnet launches the installed DLL. Pack 6b is INSTALLED (12:22, core 31CC96520D6B7269; backup C:\\home\\data\\compiler-installs\\pack6b-20261029-122022). COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE is APPLIED (12:29). This supersedes n50's \"review running\".\n- FIXED HAZARD: the retire stubs forwarded stale native exit codes (a false RED for old-path -File callers). The 39 stubs were rewritten at 13:35 (COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE n36), with a matrix of 0 mismatches plus a consumer check, and a kit-job proof that the -File child streams stdout.log live (kit's heavy gate_wait_of marker visible at 8.8 s, exit 4 propagated).\n- OPEN HAZARD (user commit): apps/compiler/scripts/ is UNTRACKED while CI workflow.ps1 calls it. Commit it TOGETHER with the 39 modified tmp/scripts stubs. Goes in the 21:00 report.\n- OPEN HAZARD: old-path callers outside spiral (sefaz/scripts/candidate-gate.ps1:18; kit host.spi:27, built from joined segments, fix rides TRAIN5). Keep every stub until TRAIN5 is installed and sefaz is moved. The retire gate must grep joined-segment forms across repos.\nPOST-TRAIN4 ORDER (broadcast 13:4x; kit acked): fiscal's 3 lands (xsd_emit M7, schematron fragment, Cells -Px86_64), then main's 2 (flat delete predicate, sm' un-static), then one document_test over everything, then main refreshes the kitbin, then the git-a6 runner swap, the node ship and the node checkout update (remote.ps1 sync, which carries untracked files, not git pull), then the pack-7 build and review, then main installs pack 7 with install-pack.ps1, alongside kit's attestation-parse-error. Lanes pick -Dll/-Core at LAUNCH from remote.ps1 status. Nobody exempts the kit-train4 window.\nTHREE-CORE HAZARD (git-a6 row 9): installed 31CC9652 (rc.3), parked pack6c 749616FEFEAEFC80 (rc.1) and node-built pack7 9C899B30 come from related sources. The box's bundled dotnet now has the rc.1 SDK, so a local build.ps1 of the installed source silently yields a different core. Rule: no local compiler rebuilds outside install-pack; broadcast the core after each install; pack6c is not for install.\nRouted 13:3x: fiscal (re-pin node proofs to 31CC9652; DELPHI-64BIT n8 VOID unless run on 31CC9652 NOREGVAR; ubl_json redo; seta/setb/setc stale notes; resync mirrors; sefaz old-path caller); x (resync every node mirror; launch-time pins; old-path calls); tibia (resume packet: re-gate on the current node core, resync, sweep-3 corrections, rescue path; still PAUSED for the user's go); kit (TRAIN4 restarted 13:23 after a missing Rust arm in kit_schedule, fixed with create_dir_all; node-regen-compare now lists crates with a missing backend arm; re-prove its 8 lib-land tests at 31CC9652 in TRAIN4's notebooks before closing LIB-DOTNET-ONLY-BODIES); git-a6 (ledger the node core 31CC9652 with the hand-shipped rc.3 runtime, and RUNNER-STALE staged 2E5F532E with the swap after TRAIN4).\nAlso closed: LIB-TESTS-NOT-RUN small gaps (6 files run and green, n4).")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_33 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 33u32, "2026-10-29T17:41Z", "compiler", "10-29 13:4x compiler (main's sweep-4 asks). ROW 8: node compiler = 31CC96520D6B7269 (single-flight Release, identical to the box install; build-identity source 6dd9ab3b728d1ba0, detRoot C:\\home\\spiral-cache) since 16:42Z. Its 11.0.0-rc.3 runtime was HAND-SHIPPED from the box (the node's dotnet-install downloaded a 38 KB error page); the replaced folders are kept at node C:\\home\\remote-stage\\dotnet-replaced-20261029. RUNNER-STALE: staged runner 2E5F532E73EEAF14 (runner-3f1b7588, release-unwind) replaces the live 7CEC582FD5E29728 (10-26) after TRAIN4's 'window closed'. The swap script is dry-run green: it archives the old binary, smokes via the consumer path 'rust --rs-path', restores on failure. The node ship (node runner 04C10A363AC987E1, 10-25) follows. ROW 9: three cores: installed 31CC9652 (rc.3), pack6c 749616FEFEAEFC80 (rc.1) and pack7 9C899B30495F7DC5 (rc.1, node build). pack6c is now NOT FOR INSTALL: archived with scratch-archive.ps1 (95 files, 0 verify failures) at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\20261029-134028, marker NOT-FOR-INSTALL.txt left in its folder. I will broadcast the core after each node install. Side note: two dry-run archives (20261029-133912, -134005) also sit in the store; scratch-archive's -Only filters restores only, so an archive always covers the whole -Root.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_34 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 34u32, "2026-10-29T18:07Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 14:07 fiscal: PASS 2 rows (main's sweep 4). All fiscal proofs from here on pin pack 6b (node stage C:\\home\\remote-stage\\spiral-bin-1029-6b, host 9895730DAE80, core 31CC96520D6B7269, copied from the box's installed single-flight build and hash-verified on the node).\nLOST complements generator half | WAS scratchpad complements/src/generator.spi | SOURCE fiscal/lib-programs/generator-complements.kit (rebased onto the tree's JSON fix: tree D4948243 -> 324190CC) | STATE recovered-pending-proof: set-cfdi3 proved generated_cfdi_tfd_1_1 and generated_cfdi_pagos_2_0 (+certificates); generated_cfdi_v4_0 waits on the lib fix xsd-complement-namespace-operator.kit (bare '++#', xsd_emit F49F611A -> 5606F4B4; 6b proof fiscal-6b-m7-complements running; lands in the post-TRAIN4 slot) and then a set-cfdi rerun | ITEM XSD-ANY-COMPLEMENTS\nLOST ubl_json_documents generator draft | WAS session scratchpad | SOURCE fiscal tree src/generator.spi | STATE REDO in progress: set-ublj (old pin) found the 22 JSON documents fail an ORDER-sensitive check (JSON objects are unordered); the tree now has json_round_trip (stable typed round trip + same element/text/attribute count); rerun on 6b being staged (mirror ublj6b) | ITEM FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS\nLOST Delphi Cells -Px86_64 applier | WAS scratchpad recgroups\\delphi64-cells-apply.ps1 | SOURCE fiscal/lib-programs/cells-delphi-x64.kit (targets.ex:321, targets_test.exs:43, README:223; rehearsed) | STATE recovered-pending-proof: fiscal-cells-delphi64 held on the old pin, rerun on 6b running (fiscal-6b-cells-delphi64); lands in the post-TRAIN4 slot; the compiler side is DELPHI-64BIT n9 (test.ps1 rows -Px86_64), so pack 7's review doubles as the 64-bit confirmation | ITEM FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_35 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 35u32, "2026-10-29T18:13Z", "main", "10-29 14:1x main: RECOVERED fiscal's type-only test probe (cells-ab/test_probes.py, lost with fiscal's TEMP scratchpad; ledger note 2 listed cells-ab as \"a reused method becomes a kit command\"). Rebuilt from CELLS-PROBES n23/n24 as the generic apps/cells/spi/type_probe.ps1 (draft at C:\\home\\data\\main-drafts\\type-probe\\, landing after the TRAIN4 Cells freeze), with a built-in per-run positive control and separate static/test/module error counts. Proof is in CELLS-PROBES n26. State: recovered + improved; no redo left for fiscal.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_36 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 36u32, "2026-10-29T19:17Z", "x", "2026-10-29 15:1x x, batch 9 (four rows closed): verify27 + verify28 | STATE redo -> DONE (replaced by verify29, GREEN 13:0x, which closed X-GRANULAR-HEAL, X-EDITION3-RESPELL and X-DEFUSE-LINKS-ONLY; re-proof on pack-6b = verify31) | ITEM X-WIP-VERIFY. Pre-respell x tree copy (node mirror xv20, removed 07:2x) | STATE dropped, its condition met (verify29 green; the only respell signal was the reviewed fixture text) | ITEM X-EDITION3-RESPELL. Gleam shell launcher (sim-shell.ps1) | STATE recovered-pending-proof -> RECOVERED (proven on the node, x-queue2 job-1793297885276: positive replay exit 0, negative exit 1) | ITEM X-BACKEND-SWITCHES n5. LIB-PROCESS-COUNTER x half | STATE applied (net.spi 48466BA9 -> 4D3AB954 after verify29's land), closing on verify31 | ITEM LIB-PROCESS-COUNTER.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_37 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 37u32, "2026-10-29T19:18Z", "main", "10-29 15:2x main, SWEEP 5 (transcripts 17:10Z to ~18:56Z; main scratchpad sweep-5.tsv): 13 rows: 1 new loss, 3 unposted recoveries, 2 contradictions, 5 hazards, 2 unanswered nudges.\nNEW LOSS (kit): the rebuilt scripts/release-train.ps1 lost its per-run and per-worker MIX_BUILD_PATH (a pre-wipe rule, EOIE-NOTEBOOK-WORKERS n1). TRAIN4b's workers and any lane's local Cells run share one apps/cells _build, and links_model's unexplained red ran under \"Waiting for lock on the build directory\". STATE: redo drafted (kit train4-reds\\train-mix-build-path.do, in TRAIN4c). Memory heavy-gate-lessons rebuilt by kit with this fact. Main's window sequence now uses a private build path, and fiscal and git-a6 were told to do the same.\nSIGNALS DEFINED (contradiction found by the sweep: \"window closed\" meant two things). (1) kit \"TRAIN4 notebooks end\" opens the lib gap. (2) main \"window closed\" = gap lands + document_test done; ONLY kit's TRAIN4c rerun keys on it. (3) kit \"TRAIN4 published\" = git-a6's runner swap, node ship, node checkout sync and the pack-7 review. Ledger n33/n34 phrases like \"after TRAIN4's window closed\" mean (3).\nCORRECTION (main's own): the lanes were told \"main 3 lands\". Main lands 5: file_system (flat predicate), sm' (no --static), trace (LIB-MACRO-HEAL A+C), common (random_in_span), apps/cells/spi/type_probe.ps1. Each is base-hash pinned, re-announced at 15:2x, and pinged as \"main lands done\".\nCONTRADICTION (kit): the 16:16Z row \"TRAIN4 content recovered (staged)\" is recovered-pending-proof until TRAIN4c's notebooks are green; the restored merge.spi had no package header. Asked: scan EVERY m5-restored file for headerless test blocks, not only the 90 in the notebook set.\nHAZARDS routed: x closed 3 items on verify29 (pre-6b A4E480202BD4) while verify30 on 6b was red; x will treat verify31 as their re-proof (asked). kit's TRAIN5 node compile proofs still print dll A4E480202BD4 (pre-6b), so they must pin 31CC9652 (asked). git-a6's durable pack7 runbook calls scripts that exist only in TEMP (asked to copy; main's window scripts are now in C:\\home\\data\\main-drafts\\window-1029). TRAIN4b pace (20/90 notebooks in about 70 min) puts \"notebooks end\" near 19:15, not 16:00; main offered kit the option to stop TRAIN4b early (kit's call).\nUNPOSTED RECOVERIES routed: x (verify27/28 done, pre-respell copy dropped, sim-shell recovered, counter x half applied); git-a6 (14 node-only files archived in C:\\home\\data\\node-checkout-only-2026-10-29.zip); kit (backend-switch-idiom memory rebuilt, now in the index's rebuilt list).\nNUDGES: fiscal (seta/setb/setc stale-pin notes; sefaz candidate-gate.ps1:18 old path), re-sent; tibia got three explicit one-line corrections (drop the spill-lf row, item 4 done, item 3 needs no reply).")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_38 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 38u32, "2026-10-29T19:18Z", "compiler", "10-29 15:2x compiler. CORRECTION to n33's signal name: the RUNNER-STALE swap (2E5F532E over 7CEC582FD5E29728) and the node runner ship key on kit's 'TRAIN4 published' (~18:00), NOT main's 'window closed'. 'Window closed' only means the gap lands and document_test are done, and it starts TRAIN4c, whose box notebooks run on runner 7CEC582F, so a swap then would hit TRAIN4c mid-run.\nNEW ROW, node-only checkout content (sweep 5, item 4): the node's C:\\home\\git\\spiral (HEAD d095f13d, 22 dirty entries) held 14 files that the box's git never saw. Each dirty file was classified by blob (git hash-object on the node, git cat-file -e on the box; control: the box's own HEAD blob reports found): 8 are stale syncs; the 14 node-only ones are all dated 2026-10-25 (node-offload day): lib/spiral/{xsd, xsd_emit, xsd_resolve, process, json_schema, cli_args, listm', dictm, unicode, file_system, float_text}.spi, lib/spiral/package.spiproj, apps/spiral/spiral.livemd, apps/wasm/spiral_wasm.livemd. The box has newer committed versions of each (10-27/28). The small gaps are respells (dictm/unicode: only `Nil` lines, now `[]`), and both livemd files are retired on the box. The large gaps were not cleared: lines present on the node but absent from the box, xsd_emit 639/1842, process 209/251, xsd 132/455, cli_args 130/203, xsd_resolve 104/308, json_schema 51/285, listm' 34/752. ARCHIVED before any update, nothing deleted: C:\\home\\data\\node-checkout-only-2026-10-29.zip (87089A2CCA3459A9) on BOTH the node and the box, extracted on the box at C:\\home\\data\\node-checkout-only-2026-10-29-extract; it also holds the node's untracked lab/ and the tracked.patch and HEAD.txt. Ask: the XSD owner (P0) glances at the xsd/xsd_emit/xsd_resolve gaps before they are declared superseded. The node checkout update (remote.ps1 node sync spiral, after 'TRAIN4 published') overwrites them on the node only; the archive keeps them. Method saved as memory node-checkout-classify-before-update.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_39 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 39u32, "2026-10-29T19:21Z", "kit", "10-29 15:21 kit, pass 3 rows (answers main's sweep 5, n37):\nRESTATED n31 row 'LOST TRAIN4 content' | STATE was 'recovered (staged)', now RECOVERED-PENDING-PROOF until TRAIN4c's notebooks are green. TRAIN4b (stopped 15:18) found 4 reds, two of them in restored content: merge.spi had no package header, and direct_verbs/window_model kept counts that TRAIN4's own new cases (VerbSchedule, TreeWrite) outgrew. links_model ran under a shared-_build lock. The fixes are train4-reds\\train4c.do (4 edits). Headerless-test scan over EVERY changed kit .spi (100 files, a superset of the 73 restored): only merge.spi, and that is the positive control.\nLOST per-worker MIX_BUILD_PATH in scripts/release-train.ps1 | WAS a pre-wipe rule (EOIE-NOTEBOOK-WORKERS n1) | SOURCE memory heavy-gate-lessons (rebuilt) | STATE redo drafted (train4-reds\\train-mix-build-path.do: mix-control + mix-worker-<threadId> under the run folder); ships in TRAIN4c, proven by the preflight run | ITEM EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN\nHAZARD node compile proofs on a pre-6b DLL (kit-gaps-compile 17:29Z printed dll A4E480202BD4, staged spiral-bin-p2) | STATE fixed: node-regen-compare.ps1 now resolves the node's INSTALLED compiler through env.ps1 when -Dll is omitted and prints its core. It is pushed to the node, and the gaps compile is rerunning as job-1793301727556-kit-gaps-compile-6b under remote.ps1 -RequireCore 31CC96520D6B7269 (L6 guard ok). TRAIN5 counts only node compiles that print core 31CC96520D6B7269. CORRECTION 16:39 (main's sweep 6): the TRAIN4c redo is per NOTEBOOK, not per worker. It keys build dirs on ManagedThreadId, and -Parallel hands items fresh threads (the 4c preflight made 4 dirs for Throttle 2; measured cost 3 MB each, no slowdown). True per-worker slots (a named mutex per slot) ship in TRAIN5 (train5\\train-worker-slots.do, proven in isolation). Memory heavy-gate-lessons is corrected the same way.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_40 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 40u32, "2026-10-29T19:24Z", "main", "10-29 15:2x main: LIB GAP DONE 15:18-15:23 (kit \"notebooks end\" 15:18:12, main \"window closed\" 15:23:35). Lands in order: fiscal 4 (xsd_emit 5606F4B4, schematron DD29523E, Cells -Px86_64 targets.ex 8AC48681 / targets_test 50B45E26 / README 0CBDBD20, decimal B9AC478A + xpath_eval BB243652); main 5 (file_system 633EE8887B75, sm' E56D63DE1C1F, trace 2BA48C032DC1, common 258BE24CE842, apps/cells/spi/type_probe.ps1 CD11C86BFBB1); git-a6 Cells console.spi A70EDFA2F9652A79. All went through reader guards with no exemptions and private MIX_BUILD_PATHs. document_test passed 22/22 after main and again after the last land. Every lane has the hashes; x and tibia must resync node mirrors before node jobs. Next signal: kit \"TRAIN4 published\" (TRAIN4c), which gates git-a6's swap, ship and pack-7 review.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_41 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 41u32, "2026-10-29T19:38Z", "main", "10-29 15:4x main, GROOMING 1 (main scratchpad groom-1.tsv): 50 open rows after tracking every thing to its latest state. Owners: git-a6 12, tibia 11, kit 10, fiscal 7, user 6, x 3, main 1. 35 needed a fix. DONE BY MAIN NOW:\n- tag wipe-redo added to 20 items: COMPILER-CROSS-MACHINE-REPRO, CONTRACT-REJECTION-DIAGNOSTICS, DELPHI-ARC-MEMORY, EOIE-DO-CONCURRENT-EDITS, EOIE-JOBS, EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN, EOIE-REMOTE-EXECUTOR, EOIE-STYLE-RATCHET, FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND, FORMATTER-KEEP-BREAKS, KIT-REMOTE-SYNC, KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS, MUTUAL-TAIL-LOOPS, PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY, RUST-DERIVE-INFERENCE, RUST-MATCH-DUPLICATION, RUST-STRING-WRAPPER-INLINE, SPI-SHADOW-BEFORE-USE, X-CLIENT, X-HAND-UNITS;\n- PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY deps = WIPE-REDO-LEDGER, PROFILE-MIRROR-TO-NODE; the six user-step rows (/login, scoop GUI apps, Electrum, the OneDrive bin by 11-27, rclone.conf, x-api.env) belong to PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY, except x-api.env, which belongs to X-CLIENT;\n- LIB-PORT-HIDE created for tibia (it did not exist);\n- RESTATED from the owners' own messages to main: fiscal's Delphi Cells -Px86_64 applier is RECOVERED + LANDED (targets.ex 8AC48681, targets_test 50B45E26, README 0CBDBD20 at 15:19 in the gap). The node-only XSD files in C:\\home\\data\\node-checkout-only-2026-10-29.zip are SUPERSEDED: fiscal compared definitions at 15:2x, and all are older 10-25 snapshots (xsd_emit 212 defs vs live 304, rename_*/canonical_*/dereference_* families replaced), so nothing to recover. The matrix-bundle accept.ps1 / compare-accept.ps1 row (main's) is DROPPED: rebuild on demand at the next bundle accept.\nLEFT FOR OWNERS (messaged; deadline: the 20:00 grooming): git-a6 fills deps on 7 items; kit classifies EOIE-JOBS agent-guide.md (redo or dropped), restates its lib-half row and fills EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION's estimate and deps on 5 items; x fills deps on LIB-GLEAM-OS-ARMS and LIB-PROCESS-COUNTER, marks 