inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_10 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 10u32, "2026-11-04T05:11Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 01:11 fiscal: corpus_checks.spi pass (in place, output-identical by construction; backup in the session scratchpad corpus_checks.before-granular.spi 63395956 -> FBD411B5): model_census 882 -> 585 (Complex/Derived arms -> complex_census, Element/Attribute inline arms -> inline_census, kind-polymorphic members of the same recursive group; every arm now one line); resolve_corpus 648 -> 332 (the 4-counter record -> resolved_file + one_if); examples_fatal 487 -> 446 and examples_fatal_in 508 -> 468 (shared read-one-root-and-count -> fatal_of (count : xml_node -> i32), each keeping its own validator). europa pack27: --check exit 0, bodies exit 0 (NB: needed --check --timeout-ms 180000; europa load 11-15 tonight makes the 30 s default attestation time out with exit 3 on unchanged code too). RUNTIME PROOF QUEUED: node job-1793769101331-fiscal-corpus-checks2 (after the ds:Object regen job), predicted corpus_checks 28/28 with the same counts (580 files, 12077 elements, 2238 complexTypes, 5389 simpleTypes). Still over the proxy here: multi-parameter signatures and a 9-arm GADT walk (one concept each); generator.spi/families.spi wait until the CII/Facturae draft lands.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_11 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 11u32, "2026-11-04T11:51Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 07:51 fiscal: LINE-WIDTH PASS (kit standards over fiscal src: 17 findings -> 8, all remaining 8 in families.spi/generator.spi, which carry pending drafts and are fixed with those lands). Fixed in place, meaning-preserving (backups in the session scratchpad width-backup): canon x2 (a bound 'terms' sub-expression; the types list one per line), corpus_checks x2 (the counted tuples bound as 'counts') + its missing final newline, generated_runtime x1 (the emitted test line split into two string pieces -- identical concatenated text), lifecycle x4 (cancel's signature wrapped, the Authorized GADT case's '-> document r authorized' on its own line, two test expressions bound to names). Now: canon CDD54AC0, corpus_checks 08330A6D, generated_runtime 10B9A650, lifecycle 811CF253. PROOF europa pack27: --check exit 0 for all four, formatter accepts each unchanged, lifecycle's 5 bodies to Rust exit 0 (canon/corpus_checks read the corpus at test time: type-level only here; corpus_checks' node proof job-1793769101331 runs the pre-width FBD411B5, the width change is binding-only).")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_12 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 12u32, "2026-11-04T14:28Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 10:28 fiscal: CELLS CONFIRMED (node job-1793769101331-fiscal-corpus-checks2, pinned core 0758BAF496AE4E7D start and end, pattern-oracle outputs written first as build.ps1 does, box manifests): corpus_checks discovered 28 executed 28 passed 28 failed 0 -- the prediction (28/28) met, including the 2 rows VOID on 11-03 (NotFound) and the new MyInvois rows; the granular corpus_checks split (complex_census / inline_census / resolved_file / one_if / fatal_of) is proven under Cells. MEASURE now (rules 1+2 applied, tests excluded, my scratch approximation of the counter): fiscal src 423 defs, 68 flat dispatches, 61 over 280 = 14.4%; by file generator 39.4% (13/33), families 45.1% (23/51), corpus_checks 11.8%, canon/document/lifecycle/sunat 12-15%, p2p/reports/profiles ~10%. Largest: generator's emitted-code templates (json_round_trip 3136, family_bench 2593, unit_text 2051, json_document_checks 1613, unit_checks_of 1449) and families' data table family_roots 1615. generator.spi and families.spi carry pending drafts (decode generator 7C315FDB, families F1CF3DDF), so their splits follow those lands.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_13 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 13u32, "2026-11-04T14:42Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 10:42 fiscal: BATCH in place (unstaged; backups in the session scratchpad *.before-granular.spi): canon.spi 4DE1FE49 (business_terms -> is_business_term_reference + reference_terms; visit_element -> term_names + declared_data_type; read_children Include branch -> included_terms (group member); structure_terms -> document_section_terms; term_json -> term_kind_text + ubl_json): canon 11.1% -> 3.8%. PROOF (europa pack27, base with fiscal_paths + json_schema, fiscal tests converted to ':#'): before and after BOTH write en16931-terms.json byte-identical (9DBC4B63), 160 terms / 30 groups; a mutant (BUSINESS_TERM misspelled) FAILS '160 EN 16931 terms and 30 groups'. (The committed canon/en16931-terms.json is the pretty-printed form, 2094 lines; the test writes compact JSON -- a pre-existing gap, unrelated.) generated_runtime.spi 7AFC49F9: unit_text (2017 chars) -> one section per emitted function (sample_root/sample_path, run_count, run_at, insert_run, median, sorted_runs, two test sections); PROVEN by evaluation: one module with the old body renamed old_unit_text and a test unit_text () = old_unit_text () passes in Rust; a one-char mutant FAILS. fiscal_paths.spi ED33DAB9: root -> checkout_root (check exit 0, format 0). MEASURE (rules 1+2, tests excluded): fiscal src 441 defs, 58 over = 13.2%; WITHOUT families.spi + generator.spi (pending drafts) 357 defs, 22 over = 6.2%. The remaining distance to 10% is entirely in those two files and follows the decode land.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_14 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 14u32, "2026-11-04T14:51Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 10:51 fiscal: GRANULAR-GENERATOR draft (kit drafts fiscal\\GRANULAR-GENERATOR\\src\\generator.spi 28372016, on the decode generator 3564751D) PROVEN output-identical on europa pack27: regen of all 69 units, 0 differing vs the decode reference (europa's generator restored after, DA6BE426 = the decode draft + its harness main). Change: typed_round_expression factors the emitted 'T_to_xml root (xml_codec.expect_decoded (T_of_xml<witness> <source>))' text that four sites wrote out by hand (two JSON checks, json_round_trip's once/twice via typed_pass_text). Formatter: the draft adds 0 drift (18 lines, all pre-existing in the base). Further template splits held for the GRANULAR-STATS ruling ask (notes 32-33).")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_15 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 15u32, "2026-11-04T15:02Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 11:02 fiscal: CORRECTION of notes 12-13 (14.4% / 6.2%): scratch approximation. kit's ACTUAL counter (Spiral.Cells.CellBudget.over_budget, default profile, top_level_blocks for the denominator; run on europa's synced Cells, private MIX_BUILD_PATH), test blocks excluded: xsd_emit decode base 145/329 = 44.1%, split draft 7FDA3007 177/432 = 41.0%; live xpath_eval 63/235 = 26.8%; fiscal src: families 56.5, generator 60.0 (granular draft 56.3), canon 28.0, corpus_checks 27.7, generated_runtime 25.0, sunat 22.4, document 17.4, posting 16.7, lifecycle 15.4, p2p 14.3, profiles 11.8, reports 10.9, fiscal_paths 0. Main gap vs my scratch counter: the real weight counts EVERY character incl. leading indentation (mine trimmed it), and the counter does not apply the 11-04 rules (1)/(2).")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_16 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 16u32, "2026-11-04T15:07Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 11:07 fiscal: kit RULED (b) at ~11:0x by message: the DoD is the counter WITH rules (1)/(2); signature-only and flat-dispatch overages count as compliant until kit's CellBudget change lands in apps/cells, then re-measure. Ruled measure meanwhile via my draft Spiral.Cells.CellBudgetRuled (kit drafts cells\\CELLBUDGET-RULES, real weights incl. indentation, tests excluded, run on europa): fiscal src lifecycle 3.8, p2p 4.8, profiles 5.9, reports 6.5, sunat 8.6, document 13.0, corpus_checks 14.9, canon 16.0, generated_runtime 16.7, generator 46.7 (granular draft 43.8), families 52.2 (data records; data/template ruling still open in GRANULAR-STATS 32-33).")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_17 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 17u32, "2026-11-04T16:40Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 12:40 fiscal: canon.spi 6AE6468D (in place, unstaged; backup canon.before-ruled.spi in the session scratchpad) under the RULED measure (kit's CellBudgetRuled, tests excluded): 8/50 -> 5/54 = 9.26%. Splits: add_terms -> term_row_of, cardinality_of -> cardinality_parts, term_id_of -> term_id_from, visit_element -> element_terms. PROVEN on europa (fiscal tests converted to ':#'): before and after write en16931-terms.json byte-identical (9DBC4B63), 160 terms / 30 groups; mutant (BUSINESS_TERM misspelled) FAILS the 160/30 assertion. Fiscal src ruled now: canon 9.3, lifecycle 3.8, p2p 4.8, profiles 5.9, reports 6.5, sunat 8.6, document 13.0 (2 of its 3 are type declarations + one record literal), corpus_checks 14.9, generated_runtime 16.7 (2 template sections), generator 46.7 / families 52.2 (pending drafts; template/data ruling open).")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_18 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 18u32, "2026-11-04T17:47Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 13:47 fiscal: corpus_checks.spi 901E881A (in place, unstaged; backup corpus_checks.before-ruled.spi 08330A6D in the session scratchpad) under the RULED measure (kit's CellBudgetRuled, tests excluded): 7/47 -> 1/53 = 1.9% (the one left is resolved_file, a single record literal). Splits: census_corpus -> schema_census, resolve_corpus -> resolve_file, region_failures -> report_failures, catalog_states -> with_large_catalog, examples_fatal -> en16931_example_fatal, examples_fatal_in -> example_fatal_in. PROVEN on europa pack27 (new base base-fiscal-corpus = base-fiscal + fiscal's corpus module; FISCAL_ROOT dec-gen/fiscal with src/corpus.txt generated as pattern-oracle.ps1 writes it: 580 DFe.NET xsd): module + all 28 tests typed (--check and bodies exit 0); the 5 tests reaching the changed functions (models_the_corpus_census, resolves_the_corpus_like_dotnet, cfdi_catalogs_become_minimal_dfas, cen_examples_pass_the_en16931_rules, ro_cius_examples_keep_their_ro_findings) PASS in Rust; mutant (schema_census drops the element census) FAILS with '12077 modeled elements, got 9662'. Two earlier attempts were VOID harness gaps (corpus module missing; src/corpus.txt is git-ignored), not verdicts.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_19 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 19u32, "2026-11-04T17:49Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 13:49 fiscal: ALL 14 src modules measured with kit's CellBudgetRuled (code-only, europa): canon 9.3, corpus 16.7 (1/6), corpus_checks 1.9, document 13.0, families 52.2, fiscal_paths 0, generated_runtime 16.7 (2/12), generator 46.7, lifecycle 3.8, p2p 4.8, posting 16.7 (1/6), profiles 5.9, reports 6.5, sunat 8.6. Every over-10% file outside generator/families is over ONLY through data literals or type declarations, no logic left to split: corpus add_file (one 6-counter record), posting invoice_lines (a 3-entry ledger list), document (term_value GADT + canon_document record type + canon_record record literal), generated_runtime (2 emitted-text template sections). Open: (a) kit's template/data ruling (GRANULAR-STATS 32-33) decides whether literals/types count; (b) generator + families land first (decode), then their split.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_20 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 20u32, "2026-11-04T18:29Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 14:29 fiscal: kit RULED (msg 14:2x, full text on GRANULAR-STATS): data = a type declaration or a def whose body is ONE record/list/tuple literal of constants + constructor applications only -> exempt, reported as its own row; a template counts per emitted section only if it ONLY concatenates string literals, and a template interpolating logic (match/if/fold/call on a non-constant) is measured whole as CODE. Applied to generator: next-layer draft drafts\\fiscal\\GRANULAR-GENERATOR\\src\\generator.next.spi ECBD351B on top of FC53C8CA (land draft unchanged, frozen): generated_folder + capped_unit_text (write/remove share the folder), is_declared_prefix + prefix_pair (declared_prefixes), json_schema_model (family_schema), family_checks + family_any_content + write_certificates_unit + write_family_module (write_family_modules = recursion only). PROVEN on europa pack27 with the land xsd_emit AB4B0165: compile/rustc/generate as always, 69 units 0 differing vs the decode reference. Ruled code-only 14/32 -> 12/41 (29.3%). The 12 left are interpolating templates (example_document, json_example_check, json_document_checks, document_round_trip, json_round_trip, document_checks, xsd_example_check, family_bench, unit_checks_of, ...): by the ruling they are code and need per-section splitting next. families: its 24 rows call fiscal_paths::under and ++#, so they are NOT data yet; making schema/catalog paths relative constants resolved where read would make all 24 exempt (next layer after the land).")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_21 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 21u32, "2026-11-04T18:48Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 14:48 fiscal: template splits under kit's ruling, next-layer drafts in drafts\\fiscal\\GRANULAR-GENERATOR\\src (land draft generator.spi FC53C8CA untouched): .next2 75916581 PROVEN on europa pack27 (compile/rustc/generate, 69 units 0 differing vs the decode reference): example_document -> root_declaration; document_round_trip -> round_trip_reader/difference/arms; xsd_example_check -> pinned_defect + example_write; json_example_check -> json_example_document/write/round; document_checks -> quoted_paths + both_failures + document_reads; shared emitted lines written ONCE: failures_raise () (was emitted by 2 templates), relative_sample_read () (3); unit_checks_of -> a guard + nfe_model_checks () (pure literal template). Ruled list after .next2 (14 over of 58; pure-literal templates nfe_model_checks 2002 and failures_raise 379 are exempt-per-section under the ruling but CellBudgetRuled does not implement that yet): json_round_trip 3346, family_bench 3255, json_document_checks 784, write_family_module 692, json_member_check 532, json_example_write 488, family_checks 430, document_reads 418, json_example_round 417, example_write 362, example_document 350, write_generated_module_with 275. .next3 CEC6452A (proving): json_round_trip -> json_size_helpers () + json_round_trip_verdict () (pure literal) + json_round_trip_reads; family_bench -> is_measurable, bench_timer/insert_runs/row_tail/folder (literal), bench_parse_line (one line emitted at 2 indents), bench_run_tail/report/sample/write; json_document_checks -> json_documents_head/test + schema_read_line (shared with json_example_write). Ask for kit: CellBudgetRuled could mark a def whose body only joins string literals as a template row, per the ruling.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_22 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 22u32, "2026-11-04T19:00Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 15:00 fiscal: families under kit's data rule, ANALYSIS (no edit): of its 24 overages, only ~12 are single record literals that a path change would turn into data (cfdi_v4_0, nfe_v4_00, fatturapa, ksef, chile x2, facturae, verifactu, saft, mydata, hacienda_factura, nav, gst...): they fail the rule only through fiscal_paths::under / ++# path joins; a nominal ':! repo_path = string' field (constructor application = data) resolved where read (generator: qualifies_children, prefix_declarations, family_schema, json_schema_model; catalog entries likewise; repo_relative(under x) = x so emitted text stays identical) would exempt them. The rest are CODE by the rule and stay so: family_roots / nfe_events / hacienda_documents build rows through a local builder (calls), ubl_* rows read manifests (manifest_documents), cfdi_complement takes parameters -- expanding builders into literal rows would trade a shared shape for repetition. Deferred: it touches families F1CF3DDF + generator, both frozen in the decode land set; do it as a next layer after the land.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_23 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 23u32, "2026-11-04T19:07Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 15:07 fiscal: generator.spi MEETS the GRANULAR DoD in its draft chain. drafts\\fiscal\\GRANULAR-GENERATOR\\src: generator.spi FC53C8CA (land draft: decode + typed_round_expression/typed_pass_text + 3600 s cap) -> .next ECBD351B -> .next2 75916581 -> .next3 CEC6452A -> .next4 585F5F7E -> .next5 48E4A89D; EACH layer PROVEN on europa pack27 with the land xsd_emit AB4B0165: compile/rustc/generate, all 69 regen units 0 differing vs the decode reference. Ruled (kit CellBudgetRuled, tests excluded): 14/32 (43.8%) -> 12/41 -> 14/58 -> 19/74 -> 15/82 -> 8/91 = 8.8% RAW; 6 of the 8 are literal-only templates (failures_raise, json_size_helpers, json_round_trip_verdict, bench_timer, bench_insert_runs, nfe_model_checks) that kit's 11-04 ruling measures per section, so code-only = 2/85 = 2.4% (family_bench 292, write_family_module 360). Every emitted line that two templates shared is now written once (failures_raise, relative_sample_read, sample_folder_line, sample_write_call, single_failures, schema_read_line, bench_parse_line at 2 indents, quoted_paths); write_unit_package is now the one place a unit manifest is written (the TOML migration's hook). Land: the .next5 file replaces the land draft (same base) once the decode set lands; generator tests then run in the node gate.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_24 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 24u32, "2026-11-04T19:21Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 15:21 fiscal: generated_runtime.spi 2F02F888 (in place, unstaged; backup generated_runtime.before-ruled.spi 7AFC49F9 in the session scratchpad): sample_path_text called sample_root_text (code by the ruling) -> split into sample_path_tail () (literal-only) + a one-line composition. Ruled 2/12 -> 1/13 raw; the one left, median_tests_text, is a literal-only template (exempt per section) -> code-only 0/12. PROVEN on europa pack27: the new file swapped into the regen harness with the GRANULAR-GENERATOR .next5 generator regenerates all 69 units 0 differing vs the decode reference, generated_fiscal_runtime included; harness restored (35D02A45). Fiscal src code-only (kit ruling, literal templates + data exempt): canon 9.3, corpus_checks 1.9, generated_runtime 0, lifecycle 3.8, p2p 4.8, profiles 5.9, reports 6.5, sunat 8.6, fiscal_paths 0; document/corpus/posting over only through data defs (document's canon_record calls decimal::add, so it stays code: 1/21 = 4.8% once the two type declarations are exempt); generator 2.4% in its draft chain; families waits on the land (see note 22).")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_25 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 25u32, "2026-11-04T19:21Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 15:21 fiscal: CORRECTION to note 24: corpus add_file (counter arithmetic: totals::x + xml::count_named ...) and posting invoice_lines (ledger::debit/credit calls) make non-constructor calls, so by kit's rule they are CODE, not data: corpus 1/6 and posting 1/6 = 16.7% each stay over 10% (one record-building def in a six-def file; splitting the record would scatter one fact). Only document's two type declarations are data.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_26 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 26u32, "2026-11-04T19:39Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 15:39 fiscal: RE-MEASURED with kit's ruling-aware counter (box apps/cells cell_budget_ruled.ex 79B1FC32, loaded with mix run -r on europa since europa's mirror still has D4E2BEFB; code-only, tests excluded), fiscal src as it will land: canon 5/54 9.3, corpus 1/6 16.7, corpus_checks 1/53 1.9, document 1/23 4.3, fiscal_paths 0/4, generated_runtime 0/13, generator (.next5 draft) 2/91 2.2, lifecycle 0/26, p2p 0/21, posting 1/6 16.7, profiles 1/17 5.9, reports 3/46 6.5, sunat 3/58 5.2, families (land draft F1CF3DDF) 24/47 51.1. AGGREGATE 42/465 = 9.0% (<= 10%); without families 18/418 = 4.3%. Per FILE, three stay over: families (rows built through calls; repo_path plan in note 22, after the land), corpus add_file and posting invoice_lines (one record-building def in a six-def file). Which reading is the DoD -- aggregate or per file?")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_27 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 27u32, "2026-11-04T21:30Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 17:30 fiscal: generator's land file is now drafts\\fiscal\\GRANULAR-GENERATOR\\src\\generator.next6.spi CB407C1C (supersedes .next5 48E4A89D, removed; adds built_in_namespaces for M7); proven identical (69 units), 2/92 = 2.2% with kit's ruling-aware counter.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_28 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 28u32, "2026-11-05T04:02Z", "fiscal", "Rebase fact, 11-05 00:1x local: the user commit bb1ebad (11-04 23:18) put my unstaged 11-04 src into HEAD. Live src/generator.spi 5DB916E8 = the decode base 7C315FDB minus test generates_cii_d16b, which was dropped because live families.spi B59F8A10 has no cii_d16b (). That family exists only in the FISCAL-CII-PROFILES draft F1CF3DDF, which also switches local_xmldsig to w3c_xmldsig and adds the Facturae documents. So generator .next6 CB407C1C (it still has generates_cii_d16b) must land in one window with families F1CF3DDF, or drop the test; it can never land alone over 5DB916E8. Diff each draft against live before -Apply: generator.base-3564751D differs from live by 46 lines, and those are the decode changes that land with XSD-DECODE-RESULT.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_29 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 29u32, "2026-11-05T06:52Z", "fiscal", "REPO_PATH LAYER DRAFTED, but MEASURED 0 gain (11-05 02:5x local). Drafts drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-GRANULAR-280\\src\\families.spi 53B36EFD (base F1CF3DDF) and generator.spi C54163F3 (base = the toml draft 2A9BE918): \":! repo_path = string\" with repo_text / repo_file; schema_path : repo_path; \"Xsd : list (string * repo_path)\" plus catalog_of; every single-family literal spells its paths in full (no fiscal_paths::under, no local ++# joins; long literals joined with ^^); the generator reads repo_file family::schema_path, emits repo_text (so the emitted text is identical to the old repo_relative output) and deletes the now unused repo_relative. Ruled counter (box apps/cells cell_budget_ruled.ex F1489A93, code defs only): families 24/49 before and 24/50 after; generator 2/91 -> 2/90. WHY 0: CellBudgetRuled.data_literal? rejects any lowercase identifier followed by an argument, so nominal constructor applications (module_id \"x\", tag_name \"x\", definition_name \"x\", namespace_uri \"x\", repo_path \"x\") count as calls; only uppercase union constructors pass. So the 11-04 premise (\"constructor application = data\") does not hold for :! nominals under the counter. Options: (a) the counter treats names declared with \":!\" as constructors (asked on GRANULAR-CELLBUDGET-RULES); (b) families become rows of plain strings typed by ONE converter into family_root, which gives up nominal typing at the literal only to satisfy a lexical rule (not done: it would game the metric). The repo_path draft is kept as a cleanup (typed repo-relative paths, no path joins) but is NOT a GRANULAR fix; its identity regen is planned on the node.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_30 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 30u32, "2026-11-05T07:31Z", "fiscal", "TYPE-CHECKS PASS, 11-05 03:30 local, europa pack27 (deps trees built with cp -rL; reference dec-gen xsd_emit 5B274B48 checked before and after; MemAvailable gate >= 2100 MB). Generator --check + bodies exit 0 for all three: (1) repo_path layer, generator C54163F3 + families 53B36EFD over the decode lib; (2) generator.next7t AA09ECE1 (sentinel + toml) + families F1CF3DDF over the sentinel lib D00BE390; (3) facet companion generator.toml A9622AB3 + families 8472AD8B over the sentinel lib. The identity regens (sentinel vs facet, repo_path vs toml base) stay PENDING: both europa attempts went VOID (memcg kill exit 137; rustc timeout exit 124 after 2402 s while the VM was starved). They move to the node after its nfe_v4 gate.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_31 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 31u32, "2026-11-05T07:54Z", "fiscal", "WITH KIT'S NOMINAL RULE (11-05 03:5x local; kit built it unstaged in spiral apps/cells: applications of any :!-declared name count as data constructors): box mix spiral.cell_budget --granular, code defs only. families base F1CF3DDF 24/49 = 49% (unchanged: every literal still calls fiscal_paths::under); repo_path draft 53B36EFD 14/53 = 26.4%. The repo_path layer is now the fix it was planned to be. The 14 left: 8 are CODE by design (cfdi_tfd / cfdi_pagos call cfdi_complement; family_roots, nfe_events and hacienda_document(s) are builders; ubl_invoice / ubl_creditnote / ubl_document_2_1 / mydata / nav read manifest_documents). 3 are pure literals blocked only by the call w3c_xmldsig () (facturae 1282, verifactu 707, hacienda_factura 579). NEXT: make w3c_xmldsig a parameterless value if edition 3 allows it (a bare name counts as data), otherwise inline the one repo_path literal; then 11/53 = 20.8%. The aggregate DoD (fiscal src <= 10%) holds well before that.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_32 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 32u32, "2026-11-05T08:30Z", "fiscal", "repo_path families FINAL, 11-05 04:3x local: drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-GRANULAR-280\\src\\families.spi E91CEC5C = 53B36EFD with w3c_xmldsig () inlined as the repo_path literal at its 5 uses (facturae, verifactu, hacienda_factura, hacienda_document, fatturapa already literal). A parameterless value (:= w3c_xmldsig : repo_path = ...) is NOT valid edition 3: \"Global inl/let statements should all return functions known at parse time\" (europa --check, exit 5). The inline variant --check + bodies exit 0 (with generator C54163F3, decode lib). With kit's nominal rule: 11/52 = 21.2% (base F1CF3DDF 24/49 = 49%); the 11 left are builders, manifest readers and parameterized rows, i.e. code by design. Identity regen (repo_path vs toml base): PENDING on the node. Also VOID on europa, 04:2x: the emitter-level sentinel identity probe. rustc of xsd_emit alone needs more than 1.6 GB (opt-level 1: memcg kill at 1.63 GB RSS; opt-level 0: 1800 s timeout while reclaiming), so every identity proof moves to the node.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_33 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 33u32, "2026-11-05T08:53Z", "fiscal", "sunat.spi GRANULAR, 11-05 04:5x local, in place and unstaged (backup sunat.before-granular.spi AF9FFB8C in the scratchpad): 3/56 -> 0/60 code defs over (box mix spiral.cell_budget --granular with kit's nominal rule). Splits: scheme_verdict out of scheme_finding; category_here plus a shared tallied (also used by line_findings, which had the same tally arms) out of category_findings; price_verdict out of price_finding, rewritten as one guarded arm over optionm::map (same semantics: an unknown reason gives None, a match gives None, otherwise the message). PROOF europa pack27 (dec-gen lib, pe corpus present): --check + bodies exit 0; all 8 bodies run in Rust with exit 0 (corpus rules over the homologation set included); MUTANT (price_verdict <> flipped to =) FAILS 'an onerosa line prices with 01, a free transfer with 02'.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_34 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 34u32, "2026-11-05T08:57Z", "fiscal", "reports.spi GRANULAR, 11-05 05:0x local, in place and unstaged (8987026C; backup reports.before-granular.spi in the scratchpad): 3/45 -> 0/49 code defs over. Splits: count_part (was a local closure) plus main_counts out of status_counts; ci_stamp out of stamp; failing_lines out of tests_section. Nothing pinned the summary text before, so I added test status_counts_cover_every_status ('2 passed, 1 failed, 1 static, 1 skipped, 2 other' from TSV-shaped rows, not_run and an unknown status both counted as other). PROOF europa pack27: --check + bodies exit 0; all 4 bodies run in Rust with exit 0; MUTANT ('passed' relabelled 'pass') FAILS the new test.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_35 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 35u32, "2026-11-05T09:03Z", "fiscal", "canon.spi GRANULAR, 11-05 05:1x local, in place and unstaged (FB518FCA; backup canon.before-granular.spi): 5/51 -> 1/57 code defs over (the one left: read_child, 287 > 272; each arm names one recursive call with the threaded arguments, so it stays). Splits: node_terms out of business_terms; element_data_type and element_cardinality out of element_terms; read_child (joined to the :& group) out of read_children; included_file and parent_folder (above the group) out of included_terms; term_head_fields out of term_json. PROOF europa pack27 (peppol-bis3 structure present): --check + bodies exit 0; both bodies run in Rust with exit 0 (en16931 terms: 160 terms, 30 groups, unchanged). Mutants: breaking included_file's separator CRASHES with NotFound (the corpus includes part/*.xml), so the changed include path is exercised. Two mutants were EQUIVALENT on this corpus, and that is a coverage note, not a pass: dropping the business-term guard in node_terms (no non-Reference element carries BT ids) and breaking parent_folder (no included file includes another).")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_36 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 36u32, "2026-11-05T09:13Z", "fiscal", "corpus / posting / profiles GRANULAR, 11-05 05:2x local, in place and unstaged (backups *.before-granular.spi in the scratchpad). corpus AA8939D1: 1/5 -> 0/7 (add_file built in three record-update steps add_elements -> add_type_counts -> enumeration and pattern). posting 61145219: 1/5 -> 0/6 (the local in_currency is now the top-level amount_as). profiles FDC32F7C: 1/21 -> 0/23 (customization_profile + list_version_profile out of ubl_profile_of). PROOF europa pack27: all three --check + bodies exit 0; Rust bodies run with exit 0 (corpus 1, posting 2, profiles 2). Corpus needed its gitignored src/corpus.txt in the work tree, copied from dec-gen; the first run without it was an environment VOID (NotFound). MUTANTS fail: profiles '2.0' -> '2.1' fails ('SUNAT UBL 2.0'); corpus count_named pattern -> patternX fails ('2055 patterns'). LEFT: document canon_record (1/33, an 8-field record literal; splitting it would need placeholder amounts) and canon read_child (1/57). fiscal src without families/generator: 2/313 code defs over (was 15/301).")
