inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_38 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 38u32, "2026-11-05T09:19Z", "fiscal", "corpus_checks.spi GRANULAR, 11-05 05:3x local, in place and unstaged (9B9D3A66; backup corpus_checks.before-granular2.spi): the block-classifying ruled measure (scratch ruled.exs over CellBudgetRuled; my line probe had read this file as 0 defs because its tests come first) found resolved_file over; now 0/53. Split: unresolved_counts (record update of the two unresolved counters) out of resolved_file. PROOF europa pack27 (src/corpus.txt copied from dec-gen): --check + bodies exit 0; the one test over this code, resolves_the_corpus_like_dotnet, runs in Rust with exit 0 (the whole 580-file corpus, 5 s); MUTANT (with_unresolved counts missing-include files too) FAILS 'no dangling type reference where every include is present'. Fiscal src by the ruled measure (families/generator excluded): 2/343 = 0.58% (canon read_child, document canon_record).")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_39 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 39u32, "2026-11-05T09:24Z", "fiscal", "families ROW SPLIT, 11-05 05:4x local: drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-GRANULAR-280\\src\\families.spi 5A989889 (on E91CEC5C). The row tables are now pure data, each with a top-level converter: signed_family (one data-only record over 5 strings; its constructor applications count as data under kit's rule); dfe_rows (12 tuples with a short portal kind nfe / cte / mdfe) + dfe_root + family_roots = map; nfe_event_rows + nfe_event + nfe_events = map; hacienda_rows + hacienda_documents = map over the unchanged hacienda_document. All values are identical (same strings, same namespace text), so the units stay identical; the identity regen is still PENDING on the node. Measured with the mix task (kit's nominal rule): 11/52 -> 8/58 = 13.8% (base F1CF3DDF 24/49). Note that the older CellBudgetRuled entry point (scratch ruled.exs) does NOT carry kit's nominal rule and reads 22/55, so quote the mix task. The 8 left all call something: cfdi_tfd / cfdi_pagos (catalog lists into cfdi_complement), ubl_document_2_1 and hacienda_document (computed names), and ubl_invoice / ubl_creditnote / mydata / nav (manifest_documents). Making the last four data needs a documents-source union (Listed / Manifest repo_path) resolved in the generator: a model change, filed as the next step, not done here. europa pack27 generator --check + bodies exit 0 with this families draft.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_40 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 40u32, "2026-11-05T09:28Z", "fiscal", "DOCUMENTS AS DATA, 11-05 05:5x local: families.spi 99A8339B + generator.spi B5D81CCA in drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-GRANULAR-280\\src. ':| document_source = Listed : list string | Manifest : repo_path'; family_root documents / ubl_json_documents : document_source; documents_of resolves Listed paths as they are and Manifest m through the existing manifest_documents 'deps/corpus/' (repo_text m) (that prefix was the same at every use). Every literal now says Listed [...] or Manifest (repo_path ...), constructor applications only. The generator's 5 reads go through documents_of. FAMILIES 8/58 -> 4/60 = 6.7% (mix task, kit's nominal rule; base F1CF3DDF was 24/49 = 49%), so the file is under 10% on its own. The 4 left are genuinely parameterized builders: cfdi_tfd_1_1 / cfdi_pagos_2_0 (catalogs into cfdi_complement), ubl_document_2_1, hacienda_document. Generator unchanged at 2 code defs over (family_bench, write_family_module). europa pack27: generator --check + bodies exit 0 with both drafts. The identity regen (units identical to the toml base) is PENDING on the node. The later facet / defect generator layer must take documents_of too (its kept_documents reads family::documents).")
