inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_46 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 46u32, "2026-11-05T12:01Z", "fiscal", "GENERATOR + FAMILIES WINDOW LANDED in fiscal src, 11-05 08:0x local, in place and unstaged (backups generator.before-granular-land-385DD926.spi and families.before-granular-land-B59F8A10.spi in the session scratchpad): src/generator.spi 385DD926 -> 40DE71DF and src/families.spi B59F8A10 -> 99A8339B, in one window. That brings .next6 (decode + GRANULAR split + generates_cii_d16b back), the toml manifests, repo_path, the row split, documents as data, and bench_parts / write_family_parts; identity proven node-side (0 differing). generated/: all 82 unit manifests converted package.spiproj -> spiral.toml exactly as module_package writes them (dependencies in order; CFDI lists runtime, tfd, pagos), and generated_cii_d16b added (C3C111BE, formatter-stable) with its toml. README line 145 now names the per-unit spiral.toml. fiscal working tree: 222 changed paths. PENDING: the CI run after the user commits (generator tests regenerate units and diff; the generator's own CFDI test now checks spiral.toml).")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_47 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 47u32, "2026-11-05T12:23Z", "fiscal", "FORMAT PASS on live fiscal src, 11-05 08:3x local, box installed compiler (format, then format --check exit 0 for each): families 99A8339B -> E6AC72B3, generator 40DE71DF -> 03111A90 (the landed drafts were not formatter-clean: long literals and conditionals unwrapped), canon A9821EE2 -> 8457C66F, corpus_checks 9B9D3A66 -> 2AC1F2A4, posting 61145219 -> CBEE84E5 (line endings only); sunat, reports, corpus, profiles and lifecycle were already clean. The facet companion drafts in src2 were formatted too: families 889D2546 -> 8F72669F, generator 96302219 -> 6ADC38CB (the running node facet gate uses the pre-format text; the format pass is semantics-preserving). Re-verified on europa pack27: generator, canon, corpus_checks and posting --check + bodies exit 0. Pre-format copies are in the session scratchpad.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_48 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 48u32, "2026-11-06T08:17Z", "fiscal", "11-05: generator 3B3D0A0E + families 684AAFF5 drafts split the GRANULAR code overages (helpers example_document_line, read_back_call, unit_checks, json_again_line, bench_*_line; td/cat_cfdi_import, cat_pagos_import, ubl_manifest, hacienda_namespace, xmldsig_import). Remaining: families ubl_document_2_1 575, hacienda_document 471, document.spi canon_record 374. Next step (CPU-light): split ubl_document_2_1 record into named field helpers, count with europa cell-budget --granular.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_49 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 49u32, "2026-11-06T08:24Z", "fiscal", "Star exchange 11-06: (tibia #4) helper splits that move  >= b |> f must parenthesize the comparison, since the pipe binds tighter; (x #9) scripted draft swaps bypass the style hook, so grep each draft for comment lines next to the hash guard; (kit #2) europa cell-budget runs gated on MemAvailable >= cap + 600 MB.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_50 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 50u32, "2026-11-06T12:04Z", "fiscal", "08:0x: the last two code overages (families ubl_document_2_1 575, hacienda_document 471) cannot be closed by helper splits: each is one 10-field family_root literal whose field lines alone exceed 280. Two designs: (a) an edition-3 record update ({ base with f = v }) over a family_defaults () base (known_defect None, documents/ubl_json_documents Listed [], extras [], source Xsd []), which would also shrink every other family; neither fiscal src nor lib uses one today, so asked compiler 08:0x whether edition 3 has it; (b) split family_root into nested records (identity { module_name; schema_path; root_element; root_type; target_namespace } + inputs { source; documents; ubl_json_documents; extras; known_defect }), which touches all 45 families and the generator (one regen-identity proof). Decision waits on compiler's answer; (a) if it exists, else (b). DoD: GRANULAR counter on europa shows 0 code overages in fiscal/src (test blocks excluded), with regen byte-identical.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_51 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 51u32, "2026-11-06T12:16Z", "fiscal", "08:1x: compiler confirmed record update ({ base with f = v }; base = a variable or a parenthesized expression; edition 3 also lexes ?| as with). BOX PROBE (pin a688, eff-stage copy, --check): { (base ()) with b = 'y' }, a bound { p with b = 'y' } and { p ?| b = 'y' } all exit 0; negative controls (b = 1i32; unknown field c) both fail ETY-TermError Unification failure, so the positives are real type-checks. DESIGN (a) chosen: an xsd_family constructor taking the 5 identity fields (module_name, schema_path, root_element, root_type, target_namespace) with the 5 inputs defaulted (source Xsd [], known_defect None, documents/ubl_json_documents Listed [], extras []); each family overrides only its inputs with { base with ... }, never dummy identity values. NEXT: draft families.spi in kit drafts FISCAL-GRANULAR-280 v3 (ubl_document_2_1 and hacienda_document first), then one node regen-identity proof (166 files, 0 differing) + GRANULAR count on europa.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_52 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 52u32, "2026-11-06T12:29Z", "fiscal", "08:2x DRAFT v3 (kit drafts fiscal FISCAL-GRANULAR-280\\v3\\families.spi F8ADA183, base live 684AAFF5): bare_family (5 wrapped identity params, 5 inputs defaulted), ubl_base + ubl_document_2_1 = { base with documents; ubl_json_documents }, hacienda_base + hacienda_document = { base with source = Xsd [ xmldsig_import () ]; extras = [ Signed ] }; no dummy identity values. Box --check (pin a688, eff-stage copy, live generator 3B3D0A0E): families 0, generator 0. PROOF QUEUED on the node: job-1793968119108-fiscal-granular3-identity (after gate3b): live vs draft whole-family regen (harness-main-full 45 families), byte compare. Land only on 0 differing, then count GRANULAR on europa.")
