inl note_of_remote_exec_s10_14 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S10", 14u32, "2026-11-05T00:26Z", "kit", "11-04 20:2x kit: the entry loop's CORE is built and PROVEN on the BEAM (unstaged): actor.spi submitted_to dispatcher lines parses each line with submission_of, sends SubmissionReady messages to the running dispatcher and returns the refusal reasons. Box notebook kit-entry-feed-tests: actor.spi 7/7, incl. submission_lines_reach_the_dispatcher_and_bad_lines_are_refused (system_started with an unlaunchable kit_launch; one good line settles via give-up, one bad line = one refusal), so submission_of's u64 parse works on the Gleam target too. Both coordinator packages are BEAM-only (no Rust crate inlines them), so no size run is needed. LEFT: the `kit coordinator` verb that runs system_started on the node and reads lines into submitted_to (stdin or the S4 spool), then the node dry run.")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s10_15 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S10", 15u32, "2026-11-05T00:27Z", "kit", "11-04 20:3x kit DESIGN for the last step (not built tonight, ~30 min left): the `kit coordinator` verb reuses the BEAM launch path cells already uses (spiral apps/cells lib/spiral/cells/targets.ex run_gleam_program: gleam package -> `erl -noshell -pa <package>/build/dev/erlang/*/ebin -eval \"main:main()\"`). Pieces: (1) a coordinator main in kit_coordinator_actor: system_started 1 (kit_launch \"kit\"), then a loop reading stdin lines (Erlang io:get_line through the existing erlang_process/otp boundary, or the S4 spool dir) into submitted_to, printing each refusal; (2) a build step that emits that module with --backend gleam into a kit-owned package dir (same as the notebook cells do) and `gleam build`s it once per kit install; (3) the verb in kit's Rust side spawns erl with those -pa paths as a long-lived node job (`kit job start --on laptop-ts ... coordinator`), resident per S9. Dry run: one harmless submission line, e.g. \"job-dry probe node 60000 -- pwsh -NoProfile -Command exit 0\", must settle.")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s10_16 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S10", 16u32, "2026-11-05T05:05Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 01:1x kit: INPUT side for the resident coordinator BUILT + PROVEN on the box (unstaged; BEAM-only, no Rust inliner, so no size run): the S4 spool. actor.spi spool_taken <dir> takes every *.sub file (filelib wildcard via lib erlang_file), deletes it, and returns its non-blank lines; served_once dispatcher spool feeds them to submitted_to and returns refusals; served loops that every 1 s, printing refusals to stderr. A resident node job has no usable stdin, so the spool is the input; writers must write <name>.tmp and then rename to .sub. Test a_spool_file_is_taken_once_and_its_lines_reach_the_dispatcher (one good line + a blank + one bad = 1 refusal; the file is removed; a second pass takes nothing; job-s settles). Box notebook kit-nb-coordinator-spool: actor.spi 8/8. europa --check ok with bodies (europa's lib copy lacked erlang_file.test_cache_file; refreshed from the box). STEP 2 BLOCKER, a decision: building the coordinator as a runnable BEAM program. Cells has no build-only mode; it writes a Gleam package (cells-gleam-warm/<key>-<slot>), gleam-builds it and immediately runs erl -pa build/dev/erlang/*/ebin -eval main:main(). Options: (A) a cells --build-only flag that prints the ebin paths (spiral apps/cells; x leads cells), then kit runs erl -pa <paths> -eval '<actor>:serve(...)' as a long-lived kit job on the node; (B) kit's own Gleam package writer (duplicates gleam_project.spi); (C) run the coordinator as a long-timeout notebook cell (no new build code, but a never-ending 'test' misuses the test runner). Recommend A.")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s10_17 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S10", 17u32, "2026-11-05T07:14Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 03:1x kit: STEP 2 UNBLOCKED AND PROVEN on the box. x accepted the cells build-only flag (kit drafted it; landed CELLS-BUILD-ONLY at 02:40), and kit's dry run found two gaps, fixed in CELLS-BUILD-ONLY-2 (FINAL, sent to x to land): the receipt key collided with dispatch_spiral's per-cell :build_only (now :build_receipt, with code memo off), and cells deleted the build dir (now keep_files plus a 'cells-build-only package=<dir>' line). New entry cell in actor.spi: the_coordinator_serves_the_spool_its_environment_names reads KIT_COORDINATOR_SPOOL via os:getenv. Unset (every notebook run) it returns at once and passes (actor.spi 9/9 box). Set, it runs system_started 4 (kit_launch \"kit\") and serves the spool. DRY RUN (draft cells): run_notebook.ps1 --path kit_coordinator_actor/actor.spi --build-only --test the_coordinator_serves_the_spool_its_environment_names -> package + 12 ebins, exit 0. Then erl -noshell -pa <12> -eval main:main() with KIT_COORDINATOR_SPOOL=<dir> stayed resident until its 40 s timeout, took a.sub (dir empty) and printed 'expected <job-id> ... : not a submission' for the bad line. The good line reached the dispatcher (kit is not on the box PATH, so its launch was given up, as in the actor test). LEFT (step 3): a kit verb or launch-train-style script step that (a) builds once per install, (b) copies the kept package dir to %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\coordinator\\<hash> and deletes the temp one, (c) starts erl as a long-lived node job with an absolute kit path for kit_launch, and the node dry run (one harmless line must settle).")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s10_18 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S10", 18u32, "2026-11-05T07:48Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 03:5x kit DESIGN for step 3 (not built; it can only be proven after an install anyway). Verb: kit job coordinator build|start <spool> (one new JobCoordinator case; job_command_of reflects the word; a new linked crate kit_job_coordinator keeps kit_job_entry small). BUILD runs <spiral>/apps/cells/spi/run_notebook.ps1 --path <kit>/src/kit_coordinator_actor/actor.spi --build-only --test the_coordinator_serves_the_spool_its_environment_names --no-html --output-path <jobs root>/coordinator/build.ipynb. --output-path is required: without it the runner writes actor.spi.ipynb into the repo, which happened tonight and was removed. It parses the receipt (package=, ebin=..., entry=) into <jobs root>/coordinator/receipt and refuses if any ebin path is missing. START reads the receipt, refuses with \"run kit job coordinator build\" if a path is gone, and starts erl -noshell -pa <ebins> -eval main:main() as an ordinary kit job (resident; S9 chose resident on the node) with KIT_COORDINATOR_SPOOL=<spool> and KIT_COORDINATOR_KIT=<this kit.exe>. Both are read by actor.spi (environment_named, kit_named; actor.spi 10/10 box). Writers drop <name>.tmp and rename it to .sub. Needs lib process execute_with_options_rust (environment_variables + command) or kit_job_launch's typed start with env. Dry run on the node: one line \"job-dry probe node 60000 -- pwsh -NoProfile -Command exit 0\" must settle.")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s10_19 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S10", 19u32, "2026-11-05T08:07Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 04:2x kit: STEP 3 VERB BUILT (unstaged). New linked crate kit_job_coordinator, routed as kit job coordinator: a JobCoordinator case in kit_jobs model, where reflection picks the word (verb test pair added), plus usage text. kit_job_entry links the crate and calls coordinator_run (jobs_root ()). Reflected step (build|start) and flags (--spiral, --kit, --spool). BUILD runs pwsh run_notebook.ps1 --build-only --test <entry cell> --no-html --output-path <jobs>/coordinator-build.ipynb, parses the receipt (package=/ebin=/entry=) and writes <jobs>/coordinator.receipt. START refuses with exit 2 when there is no receipt, a built ebin is gone, or --spool is missing. Otherwise it runs <this kit.exe> job start kit-coordinator 604800000 pwsh -NoProfile -Command \"$env:KIT_COORDINATOR_SPOOL=...; $env:KIT_COORDINATOR_KIT=<kit.exe>; & erl <quoted args>\" (every path single-quoted, embedded quotes doubled). Pure tests in coordinator.spi: receipt read, refused, erl argv, submission line shape, step/flag parsing, script quoting. CLI check in kit_jobs/stop_cli.spi (train): no step, unknown step, start without a build. Box --check ok: coordinator, kit_jobs model, kit_job_entry. Pending: box notebooks (job-1793865887011) and node size (kit_job_coordinator, kit_job_entry, kit_job_start_args; job-1793865923779, queued for a slot). LEFT: the node dry run after an install.")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s10_20 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S10", 20u32, "2026-11-05T08:43Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 04:5x kit: kit_job_coordinator sized 1055 (OVER): lib process/file_system inline plus two reflected unions. SPLIT: the argv parse (reflected step build|start and flags --spiral/--kit/--spool) moved to NEW linked crate kit_job_coordinator_args. It exports coordinator_args_read (skipped) -> array_base coordinator_row { build; start; spiral; kit; spool; rejected }, primitive fields, so it links. coordinator_run reads it with one am'.index_base and dispatches on the booleans. Box --check ok (args, coordinator, kit_job_entry); re-size + notebooks pending (job-1793868167908, job-1793868141327). kit_job_entry 435 and kit_job_start_args 696 sized fine.")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s10_21 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S10", 21u32, "2026-11-05T08:46Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 04:5x kit: coordinator verb SIZED + PROVEN in the tree. Node size: kit_job_coordinator 797 (was 1055 before the split), kit_job_coordinator_args 287, kit_job_entry 435, kit_job_start_args 696. Box notebooks: kit_job_coordinator_args 1/1 (steps + flags), kit_job_coordinator 3/3 (receipt, submission line, build argv + start script quoting), kit_jobs model 9/9 (coordinator verb pair). Rides TRAIN28. After the install, the node dry run: kit job coordinator build --spiral C:\\home\\git\\spiral --kit C:\\home\\git\\kit, then kit job coordinator start --spool <dir>, then drop one harmless .sub line and see it settle.")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s10_22 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S10", 22u32, "2026-11-05T23:11Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 19:1x kit: TRAIN32 notebook RED on kit_coordinator_actor/actor.spi, 8/10: a_launcher_that_cannot_run_gives_every_job_up_and_frees_the_slot (a was given up after three failed launches) and submission_lines_reach_the_dispatcher_and_bad_lines_are_refused. The spool tests added 03:21 passed. Both failing tests are in HEAD but newer than TRAIN26's 6-test run, so they never ran in a train; each waits settled_within 40 tries x 500 ms = 20 s, and three failed launches of a missing binary on the 100 pct node take longer (slowest cell 158 s vs 79 s in TRAIN26). Widened all four settle waits to 120 tries (60 s), unstaged, TRAIN33.")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s10_23 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S10", 23u32, "2026-11-06T11:10Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 07:1x kit: DONE. TRAIN33 INSTALLED at 07:05 (kit.exe 6CEA882D, the first install since TRAIN14c): node half job-1793925896101 regen ok, crate gate 358 over 0, notebooks 234/234 including the cli_check suites; box half job-1793960664511 accepted those verdicts on the same snapshot, then release build, schema and topology checks, publish and smoke passed. The four widened settle waits (120 tries, 60 s) ran in the node notebooks and passed.")
inl note_of_diamond_s1_1 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S1", 1u32, "2026-11-01T13:06Z", "kit", "11-01 09:0x kit, slice of CODEBASE-DIAMOND (user 09:0x). DoD: a HostFree package kit_gauge_model with test blocks: a scorecard of 3 units scores the same twice; diamond is true only when every obligation's evidence is Proven; adding an Adjudicated obligation drops diamond. NEXT STEP: new package src/kit_gauge_model. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: evidence GADT indexed by phantom strength (mechanical | adjudicated | proven); obligation row existential over strength; obligation_family closed union; unit_id a phantom-tagged content hash; distance = sum of typed weights (nominal), never floats parsed from text.")
inl note_of_diamond_s1_2 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S1", 2u32, "2026-11-03T05:30Z", "kit", "11-03 01:3x kit: DONE (unstaged), new HostFree package src/kit_gauge_model (gauge.spi + standards.spi).\nModel: the evidence GADT is indexed by phantom strength (Measured -> mechanical, Judged -> adjudicated, ProvenBy -> proven), so evidence construction is typed. Rows cannot be existential over strength (existentials are compile-time only, memory existentials-compile-time-only), so polymorphic obligation_of projects each piece of evidence into a closed strength_kind union stored on the obligation record. obligation_family is a closed union. weight is a nominal (Weight u64). distance_of = the sum of weights of obligations that are not Proven, no floats. diamond_of = non-empty and every obligation Proven. scored/scorecard are pure functions.\nDoD proof (europa notebook-batch, 2/2 blocks): a 3-unit scorecard scores the same twice; all-proven is a diamond at distance 0; a Measured obligation is distance 2, not a diamond; no obligations is no diamond; adding a Judged (adjudicated) obligation drops the diamond (distance 4). The gleam block repeats two of them. kit standards 0 findings; ratchet clean.\nDeviation from the plan: unit_id is a nominal union over the content hash, not phantom-tagged (no unit kinds exist yet to tag with). Add the phantom when DIAMOND-S2 introduces unit kinds.")
inl note_of_diamond_s6_1 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S6", 1u32, "2026-11-01T13:06Z", "kit", "11-01 09:0x kit, slice of CODEBASE-DIAMOND (user 09:0x). DoD: 'kit gauge fiscal --xsd' prints, per schema set, constructs modeled with typed Spiral / all constructs (denominator enumerated from the XSDs, deterministic); at least one schema set reaches 100% and is marked complete; the number matches fiscal's own generator census. NEXT STEP: enumerate XSD constructs via lib xsd_* modules (xsd_resolve, xsd_emit) and match against fiscal's generated units. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: xsd_construct closed union (ComplexType | SimpleType | Element | Attribute | Restriction | ...) with schema-qualified names as nominals; coverage a record of nominal counts; completeness a type (Complete | Partial of missing list).")
inl note_of_diamond_s6_2 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S6", 2u32, "2026-11-03T09:26Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 05:26 fiscal: FISCAL HALF DRAFTED (DIAMOND-S1 is Done in kit's tree, so this slice is unblocked). The census both the gauge and fiscal must agree on lives in LIB, not in kit or fiscal: draft %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\DIAMOND-S6\\lib\\spiral\\xsd_census.spi, a new module after xsd. Typed per this item's plan: ':| xsd_construct = ComplexTypeConstruct | SimpleTypeConstruct | ElementConstruct | AttributeConstruct | GroupConstruct | WildcardConstruct'; ':== construct_census = { constructs; modeled; wildcards }'; ':| completeness = Complete | Partial : i32'. One GADT walker 'construct_walk \\* k form. (item : xsd k form)' over type_def / particle / attribute_decl (the same shape as xsd_emit.dereferenced_in), schema_census over simple_types + complex_types + elements, completeness_of. DENOMINATOR RULE (deterministic, enumerated from the parsed XSD): every complex/simple type, element, attribute and sequence/choice group is a construct; a construct is MODELED when xsd_emit emits it as typed Spiral, i.e. everything except xs:any (emitted as untyped any_content); a schema set with 0 wildcards is Complete. Test every_construct_is_counted_and_a_wildcard_is_not_modeled (8 constructs on the typed schema, Partial 1 on the xs:any one). QUEUED: job-1793697977422-fiscal-xsd-census (after the codec layer; one Cells run per node). FOR KIT (when this lands): 'kit gauge fiscal --xsd' calls xsd_census.schema_census per fiscal family schema and prints constructs/modeled/completeness; no XSD logic in kit.")
inl note_of_diamond_s6_3 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S6", 3u32, "2026-11-03T11:52Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 07:52 fiscal: TYPE-CHECKED ON IDLE EUROPA (pack24 compiler, lib = spiral HEAD 98e51d32 + this draft, SPIRAL_COMPILER_PACKAGE_DIR = the shipped core; mutation-proven: an appended ill-typed definition exits 5 / ETY-TermError): xsd_census.spi exit 0 in 4 s. Its test still runs in queued job-1793697977422.")
inl note_of_diamond_s6_4 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S6", 4u32, "2026-11-03T15:28Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 11:28 fiscal: FIRST CELLS RUN FAILED IN THE HARNESS, not in the census: the test body used 'open' (a Spiral keyword) as a binding name ('    := open ='), so the test block failed to parse, Cells dropped it and reported 'ETY-UnboundVariable: spiral_cells_test' (job-1793697977422). --check had passed because it skips test blocks. FIX: the binding is now 'wildcard' (draft 2C510F3B); a cloud check that rewrites test headers into definitions now parses and types every test body (the old text reproduces the exact Cells parser error, exit 5; the fixed one passes). RERUN queued: job-1793719669429-fiscal-xsd-census2 (after the families proof).")
inl note_of_diamond_s6_5 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S6", 5u32, "2026-11-03T20:30Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 16:29 fiscal: LANDED THROUGH lib_land_window (label fiscal-lib-1103, closed green, undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261103-161039, lib digest 0B967D8878EF2C4A): signatures 0 consumer-used changed; apps/spiral compiles; document_test 22 passed; type_probe 4/4 (money 2, ledger 4, event_log 4, xsd_census 1 tests typed; 9 fails negatives skipped as designed); respell_drift 0 findings. Respelled before landing (exists -> \\?, fun -> \\, true/false -> !+/!-) and re-proven under pack27 on europa (check + bodies + pinned negatives + Rust runs). Unstaged in spiral. xsd_census.spi 17B2E8EC (new, after xsd; formatted). Before landing: Rust run of its test body on a group_part lib exit 0 (europa, pack24 then pack27). The queued node census job (fiscal-xsd-census4) remains as the Cells confirmation.")
inl note_of_diamond_s6_6 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S6", 6u32, "2026-11-03T21:32Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 17:32 fiscal: FIRST REAL NUMBERS from the landed lib census (a probe main appended to a cloud copy, compiled --backend Rust, pack27, reading the corpus XSDs): SAF-T PT 1.04_01: constructs 708, modeled 708, COMPLETE (DoD 'at least one schema set reaches 100%': met, fiscal side); Facturae 3.2.2: constructs 436, modeled 435, PARTIAL 1. AGREES WITH THE GENERATOR (DoD 'matches fiscal's own generator census'): SAF-T has 0 xs:any and generated_pt_saft_1_04_01 has 0 any_content; Facturae has exactly 1 xs:any (Facturaev3_2_2.xsd:1716, namespace ##other, the Extensions slot) and generated_es_facturae_3_2_2 carries any_content for it. Single-file schemas only so far: multi-file sets (NF-e, UBL, CFDI) need the census run after xsd_resolve's include/import resolution, which is the kit gauge's part ('kit gauge fiscal --xsd'). Remaining here: kit's gauge command (team kit) consuming lib xsd_census.")
inl note_of_diamond_s6_7 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S6", 7u32, "2026-11-03T21:42Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 17:42 fiscal: MULTI-FILE SETS MEASURED with include/import resolution (xsd_resolve.load_schema_tree, then xsd_census.schema_census; Rust probe on europa, pack27, group_part lib): NF-e 4.00 (5 files) 1988/1988 COMPLETE; Chile DTE v10 (3) 1147/1147 COMPLETE; Greece myDATA 2.0.2 (5) 328/328 COMPLETE; Portugal SAF-T 1.04_01 (1) 708/708 COMPLETE; Italy FatturaPA 1.2.3 357/357, Costa Rica Hacienda 4.4 318/318, Spain VeriFactu LR (2) 300/300 all COMPLETE but each with 1 MISSING import (the xmldsig schema: a remote w3.org URL or a path outside the uploaded tree; the generator supplies it through its catalog, so these 3 are measured without the signature types); UBL Invoice 2.1 (14 files) 5622 constructs, 5607 modeled, PARTIAL 15. The 15 is EXACT: 1 xs:any in UBL-ExtensionContentDataType, 2 in UBL-XAdESv132, 12 unprefixed <any> in UBL-xmldsig-core-schema (a literal count over the 14 files gives 15), so the census counts wildcards across files and prefix spellings. 7 of 8 sets reach 100%; UBL's gap is entirely signature/extension wildcards. Next for exact parity with the generator: run with each family's catalog (families.spi source = Xsd catalog) so the xmldsig imports resolve.")
inl note_of_diamond_s6_8 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S6", 8u32, "2026-11-03T22:04Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 18:03 fiscal: CELLS CONFIRMED (node job fiscal-xsd-census4, core 2ABF22D79E6B6943, one compiler): xsd_census 1/1 on the node mirror.")
inl note_of_diamond_s6_9 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S6", 9u32, "2026-11-04T01:12Z", "kit", "11-03 21:1x kit: kit's half of the DoD started (fiscal's lib census is landed and proven). New owner crate kit_gauge_xsd in the tree (after the TRAIN17b snapshot; HostFree, no host macros): 'kit gauge xsd <schema.xsd>' loads the schema tree with lib xsd_resolve.load_schema_tree (includes and imports resolved), runs lib xsd_census.schema_census, and prints: files, missing, constructs, modeled, wildcards, and completeness (complete | partial:N via kebab). The verb is a reflected gauge_verb union. GENERIC per kit's contract: it names no project (the DoD's 'kit gauge fiscal --xsd' becomes 'kit gauge xsd <file>'), and a test asserts 'fiscal' is not a verb. Registered (workspace member, test row). Proof: job-1793754669860-kit-precheck-gauge, queued after precheck-s4.\nNEXT: (1) route it: add VerbGauge to command_spec_domain.direct_verbs plus its help and usage, and make kit_cli_model's VerbGauge call kit_gauge_xsd.gauge.gauge_run through a link (packages + link in kit_cli_model and kit_cli, plus the Cargo dep), NOT a new host hop; (2) run it on the SAF-T 1.04_01 corpus XSD and match fiscal's 708/708 COMPLETE, which is this item's 'matches fiscal's census' check.")
inl note_of_diamond_s6_10 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S6", 10u32, "2026-11-04T01:16Z", "kit", "11-03 21:2x kit: ROUTED (tree, unproven). VerbGauge is a new case of command_spec_domain.direct_verbs, with a help line ('gauge xsd <schema.xsd> ...'). kit_cli_model routes '| VerbGauge => kit_gauge_xsd.gauge.gauge_run ()' as a LINKED call (kit_gauge_xsd under packages and link in kit_cli_model and kit_cli, Cargo dep in kit_cli, lock refreshed), not a new host-string hop like its neighbours. kit_cli_model is the only exhaustive match over direct_verb. Proof widened by closure: job-1793754669860-kit-precheck-gauge now covers command_spec_domain, kit_cli, kit_command_help, kit_command_usages, kit_gauge_xsd and kit_legacy_operations. Watch kit_cli's size (kit.rs was 1265 at TRAIN16b) and grep kit.rs for kit_gauge_xsd:: to confirm the link. LEFT: the SAF-T 708/708 cross-check once a train installs it.")
inl note_of_diamond_s6_11 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S6", 11u32, "2026-11-04T01:17Z", "kit", "11-03 21:2x kit: Blocked on proof, not on work. The verb and its routing are in the tree (n9, n10). Unblock when job-1793754669860-kit-precheck-gauge is green; then, after a train installs it, run 'kit gauge xsd' on the SAF-T 1.04_01 XSD and match fiscal's 708/708 COMPLETE.")
inl note_of_diamond_s6_12 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S6", 12u32, "2026-11-04T04:44Z", "kit", "11-04 00:4x PARKED out of TRAIN18: kit_gauge_xsd generated 4964 lines (gate 1000), because lib xsd_resolve + xsd_census inline whole into the one crate that calls them. Crate and wiring are in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\DIAMOND-S6-parked-1104 (src/kit_gauge_xsd, plus wired/ copies of direct_verbs, model, spiprojs, Cargo files). Also fixed in the parked copy: main moved under `///> _` (the TRAIN17b Zig trap). Options: (a) split the census over linked units (resolve unit -> array of construct rows -> census unit), each <1000; (b) run the gauge as a lib program on europa/the node instead of a kit verb. Fiscal (the owner of the calibration) decides which; (a) is kit's default.")
inl note_of_diamond_s6_13 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S6", 13u32, "2026-11-04T08:07Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 04:07 fiscal: DECIDED with kit (11-04 04:1x): option (b). The XSD gauge stays a lib/fiscal program run on europa or the node when a family or the XSD model changes (that is how the 7/8-complete numbers were made: europa probes over lib xsd_census, pack27), and kit stores the verdict rows in DIAMOND-S3's typed ledger (per schema set, keyed by unit hash + rubric version: set, complete, wildcards, modeled/declared counts). The kit verb split (option a: resolve unit -> census unit over linked units, ~2 h + a train slot) is deferred until a CLI need appears; the parked draft stays at drafts\\kit\\DIAMOND-S6-parked-1104.")
inl note_of_diamond_s6_14 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S6", 14u32, "2026-11-04T08:09Z", "kit", "DONE 11-04 05:2x (decision by fiscal, 05:1x: option (b)). The XSD gauge is a calibration run when a family or the XSD model changes, not a per-command tool, so it stays a lib/fiscal one-call program on europa or the node (how the 7/8-complete numbers were produced over lib xsd_census, pack27). The kit verb split (4964 generated lines) is dropped; the parked crate stays in drafts\\kit\\DIAMOND-S6-parked-1104 as a record, and (a) can follow if a CLI need appears. kit's part becomes storing verdicts: DIAMOND-S3's ledger now has an XsdReading answer {complete; wildcards; modeled; declared} keyed by unit hash + rubric version.")
inl note_of_edition3_rust_undeclared_assign_1 () = Note ("EDITION3-RUST-UNDECLARED-ASSIGN", 1u32, "2026-11-01T13:16Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 09:30 fiscal: FOUND by fiscal's edition-3 proof (node job-1793506463392, mirror t1101, installed compiler pack 10 DFC86B91968D). In an EDITION-3 package (fiscal src respelled; src/package.spiproj \"edition: 3\" + spiral.toml), corpus_checks tests resolves_the_nfe_tree and resolves_the_corpus_like_dotnet fail in rustc: error[E0425] \"cannot find value `st` in this scope\" at generated main.rs:4568 \"st = Group94::M97(v6, v10);\" (and :4645 \"st = Group99::M102(v6, v10);\"); rustc suggests \"let st = ...\". So the Rust backend emits an assignment to a binding it never declared. The tests call lib xsd_resolve (edition-2 lib code inlined into the edition-3 package); the test sources contain no `st`. The SAME tests PASS in edition 2: CI run 41281571029 (ubuntu, spiral main e0461f15) and node t1031u (pack 8 EEBCBFF8658A). Two variables differ from the green runs (edition 3 vs 2; pack 10 vs CI/pack 8), so the first bisect step is the edition-2 tree with pack 10. REPRO: node mirror C:\\home\\remote\\t1101 (kept for this), pwsh t1101\\spiral\\apps\\cells\\spi\\lib_gate.ps1 -Lib t1101\\fiscal\\src -File corpus_checks.spi -Compiler process with SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL = the installed pack 10; the failing notebook is C:\\home\\remote-stage\\fiscal-e3-regen\\corpus_checks.spi.txt.ipynb. DONE WHEN both tests pass on t1101 in edition 3. BLOCKS FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND (the respell is not applied to the fiscal tree until then).")
inl note_of_edition3_rust_undeclared_assign_2 () = Note ("EDITION3-RUST-UNDECLARED-ASSIGN", 2u32, "2026-11-01T13:22Z", "compiler", "11-01 11-01 09:22 compiler: ROOT CAUSE FOUND, MINE (PACK-12's mutual-tail group loops, MUTUAL-TAIL-LOOPS). NOT edition-3 specific: edition 3 only changes the order in which methods are first emitted. Mechanism (spiral_compiler.fs codegenRust): emit_group (~14375) sets group_loop = Some(GroupN, members) while it emits the member bodies. A method referenced for the FIRST time from inside a member body is emitted right then by the jp printer callback (~14327), which saved/cleared self_loop but NOT group_loop. So that nested ordinary fn's tail call to a group member hit the TyJoinPoint arm at ~13903 (members.Contains) and emitted 'st = GroupN::M<k>(...)': no 'st' in that fn, rustc E0425. MINIMAL REPRO (box, installed pack13a): count_even/count_odd mutual tail pair + 'bump' called NON-tail from count_even, with bump tail-calling count_odd; the Rust output has 'fn bump_2 ... st = Group0::M1(v2, v3);', rustc E0425 at main.rs:9. FIX (one kit do program, apps/compiler/packs/pack14/1-group-loop-scope.kitdo): the method printer saves group_loop, sets None for the method's whole body, restores after (the closure and while paths already reset it via without_self_loop). Candidate pack14a building (job-1793539338732). PROOF PLAN: (1) the repro builds under rustc and exits 0 like C; (2) predict vs pack13a's run: only Rust rows with a mutual group may change, compile-status diffs 0; (3) fiscal's resolves_* on t1101 with the candidate; (4) regression sample samples/mutual_tail_nested_callee.")
inl note_of_edition3_rust_undeclared_assign_3 () = Note ("EDITION3-RUST-UNDECLARED-ASSIGN", 3u32, "2026-11-01T13:25Z", "compiler", "11-01 11-01 09:25 compiler: (1) DONE: candidate pack14a (core DBC5EC18F14C354C) on the 3-function repro: bump_2 has no 'st =', rustc -O builds, exit 0 = C's exit 0. (2) predict vs pack13a's run (single-flight-20261101-080900) running: job-1793539488130. (3) fiscal's two resolves_* on t1101 with the candidate (binaries shipped to node C:\\home\\remote\\e3assign\\pack14a-bin, hash verified, SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL) running: job-1793539537261. Regression sample staged: apps/compiler/packs/pack14/samples/mutual_tail_nested_callee (enters samples/ at install; today's compiler makes it a Rust build failure).")
inl note_of_edition3_rust_undeclared_assign_4 () = Note ("EDITION3-RUST-UNDECLARED-ASSIGN", 4u32, "2026-11-01T13:30Z", "compiler", "11-01 11-01 09:30 compiler: FIX PROVEN, all 3 checks green (repro builds and agrees; fiscal resolves_* 2/2 on t1101 with pack14a; predict 0 diffs in 7,413 rows). Handed to main as PACK-14. Done when installed and fiscal's FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND gate is green on the installed compiler.")
inl note_of_edition3_rust_undeclared_assign_5 () = Note ("EDITION3-RUST-UNDECLARED-ASSIGN", 5u32, "2026-11-01T13:33Z", "main", "main 09:3x: FIXED on the box by pack14a (installed 09:31). compiler's evidence: the 3-function repro builds and exits 0 = C, and fiscal's resolves_the_nfe_tree + resolves_the_corpus_like_dotnet pass 2/2 on t1101 with the candidate. Main's check: the new sample's generated Rust compiles under rustc and runs exit 0. Node gets it at the 10:23 ship. Close after fiscal's rerun on the box or the node.")
inl note_of_edition3_rust_undeclared_assign_6 () = Note ("EDITION3-RUST-UNDECLARED-ASSIGN", 6u32, "2026-11-01T13:36Z", "compiler", "11-01 11-01 09:34 compiler: fix INSTALLED (PACK-14, 09:31). Lanes rerun the rows they VOIDed with the E0425 signature on the box. Done when fiscal's FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND gate is green on the installed compiler.")
inl note_of_edition3_rust_undeclared_assign_7 () = Note ("EDITION3-RUST-UNDECLARED-ASSIGN", 7u32, "2026-11-01T13:40Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 09:40 fiscal: VERIFIED FIXED on the box with pack14a (installed 09:31; SpiralCompilerCore.dll DBC5EC18F14C at 09:33, where codegen lives; the CLI SpiralCompiler.dll hash DFC86B91968D unchanged). Rerun of the edition-3 respelled fiscal src (fresh respell of the current tree, package.spiproj \"edition: 3\" + spiral.toml, corpus_checks 244E17E3912A after the cap bump) through fiscal/scripts/box-gate.ps1 -Test: resolves_the_nfe_tree 1/1 passed, resolves_the_corpus_like_dotnet 1/1 passed, type errors 0, no E0425 (raw outputs in the fiscal session scratchpad e3-gate\\*.txt). Cause per compiler: the PACK-12 group-loop leak; edition 3 only changed emission order. CLOSED.")
inl note_of_kit_train7_1 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN7", 1u32, "2026-11-01T13:17Z", "kit", "11-01 09:1x kit groom: split out of EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN, which has 208 notes at 45% and has become the log of every train run, so 'install TRAIN7' (what KIT-AGILE-LOST-UPDATES, EOIE-DO-COPY-LITERAL and EOIE-NOTEBOOK-PROGRESS are blocked by) was not a closable unit anywhere. CONTENT of TRAIN7: note-segment readers and writer (EOIE-AGILE-EVENT-LOG), typed .spi lint baselines and the string-literal arith fix (GRANULAR-LINT), the TODO-scan --tagged fix (KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS n18), the resume freshness guard, copy-literal, lint --opens, standards subfolders, the no-respell writers (scaffold, views, lease, receipts), respells, plus tonight's new packages as they get wired. DoD: (a) node pre-proof: candidate-build of every owner changed since TRAIN6 green and notebook-batch over every touched module with 0 RED, with a sha256 manifest of the generated crates; (b) the box train runs -SkipRegen only after its tree matches that manifest; (c) installed kit.exe hash recorded; acceptance rows green; (d) the three Blocked items above closed by acceptance runs on the installed binary. NEXT STEP: the pre-proof job on node mirror kit-verify with the full owner list (memory remote-kit-worker-node: no re-sync between regen and build). TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: n/a for the release itself; the manifest is typed rows (crate, file, sha256 nominal) compared as sets, as specified for the kit train port on EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN.")
inl note_of_kit_train7_2 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN7", 2u32, "2026-11-01T13:23Z", "kit", "11-01 09:2x kit (main's heads-up): KNOWN COMPILER REGRESSION in the installed compiler (pack12b / pack13a): pack 12's mutual-tail group loops can emit a tail call as 'st = GroupN::M..(..)' inside a function that has no 'st', and rustc fails with E0425. RULE for this train: a regen or candidate-build row failing with E0425 on an 'st = Group' line is VOID (compiler's bug, not kit's), recorded with that signature, never chased as a kit fix; if it reds the train, wait for compiler's pack14a, which main installs on hand-over, then rerun. CONSEQUENCE FOR THE DoD: tonight's node proofs (candidates 923AAF5A, FB34FD11, BBF31C2A, 81741E5A; 01:30-02:20) ran on the node's compiler from BEFORE pack 12 was installed on the box (03:14), so they do not certify the compiler this train will use (memory node-proof-skips-regen: one compiler; the run must pin the box's installed DLL, core hash equal). DoD (a) is therefore: the node pre-proof pins SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL to the box's installed core (pack14a once installed; recorded by hash) and reruns the full owner regen + notebook batch there; earlier proofs count as design evidence only. Order: wait for pack14a, pin, pre-proof, then the box train with -SkipRegen against the manifest.")
inl note_of_kit_train7_3 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN7", 3u32, "2026-11-01T13:24Z", "kit", "11-01 09:2x kit: blocked by: EDITION3-RUST-UNDECLARED-ASSIGN (compiler, P0; the 'st = GroupN::M..(..)' E0425 regression, fixed in pack14a). Added as a dep so the wait is visible in agile next; the train starts once pack14a is installed and pinned.")
inl note_of_kit_train7_4 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN7", 4u32, "2026-11-01T13:34Z", "kit", "11-01 09:3x kit: pack14a (the E0425 'st = GroupN::' fix) installed on the box 09:31 (EDITION3-RUST-UNDECLARED-ASSIGN 85%, closes after fiscal's rerun); the node gets it in the one-shot ship at 10:23, after compiler's A/B. kit VOIDed nothing with that signature (no kit build ran on pack12b), so there is nothing to rerun. PLAN: right after the node ship, verify the node's effective compiler core equals the box's installed pack14a core (by hash, memory node-stale-compiler-dll), then start the pre-proof: full owner regen + notebook batch over every module touched since TRAIN6 + the sha256 manifest. The dep on EDITION3-RUST-UNDECLARED-ASSIGN stays until compiler closes it; the pre-proof itself is evidence for that closure.")
inl note_of_kit_train7_5 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN7", 5u32, "2026-11-01T14:46Z", "kit", "11-01 10:46 kit: at 10:4x ssh laptop failed once to resolve moon (mDNS); it resolved again at 10:46 (hostname moon). The pre-proof check of the node core vs pack14a runs right after groom round 5 (10:53), not at the 10:33 wake, which was held by the round.")
inl note_of_kit_train7_6 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN7", 6u32, "2026-11-01T14:51Z", "kit", "11-01 10:51 kit: precondition MET. remote.ps1 node status: node compiler DBC5EC18F14C354C (2026-11-01 09:33) = box compiler DBC5EC18F14C354C (pack14a); runners equal F1DD2E34F1E816C8. main shipped early at 09:35 (node-upkeep.log, digest 0AF644516C09E959). The pre-proof (full owner regen + notebook batch over every module touched since TRAIN6 + sha256 manifest) starts right after groom round 5 closes; the node also runs compiler-libord-seq (peak 5 GB of 8 GB cap), so the kit job runs at default parallelism and retries lower on a memory kill (retry-after-memory-kills).")
inl note_of_kit_train7_7 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN7", 7u32, "2026-11-01T15:01Z", "kit", "11-01 11:01 kit: PRE-PROOF STARTED, node job job-1793545254729-kit-train7-preproof (3 h cap) on mirror kit-verify. Core check: node compiler DBC5EC18F14C354C = box pack14a; runners F1DD2E34 equal. Mirror synced BEFORE the job (REMOTE-SYNC-OK kit d486fd04 digest 51010DD4, spiral 7a4c960e digest F1FC35A8); no re-sync until the job ends. Owners (41): the 34 of the norespell proof plus the module-package mapping since TRAIN6 (agile_todo_model -> agile_todo_fields/lines/merge/paths/roots/sources/scan, kit_lint_model -> kit_lint_classify/macros/scan/walk, agile_state_runtime -> kit_agile_state). Notebooks (19): the 13 changed model modules plus todo/views/notes/agile/roots/table CLI notebooks. Manifest: C:\\home\\remote\\kit-verify\\train7\\manifest.spi (typed rows Crate (path, sha256) + Candidate sha256). NEXT after green: fetch the manifest, box train with -SkipRegen against it, then acceptance runs for KIT-AGILE-LOST-UPDATES, EOIE-DO-COPY-LITERAL, EOIE-NOTEBOOK-PROGRESS.")
inl note_of_kit_train7_8 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN7", 8u32, "2026-11-01T15:53Z", "kit", "11-01 11:53 kit: NODE PRE-PROOF RESULT (job-1793545254729, 49 min): candidate-build GREEN for all 41 owners (regen + cargo check + publish + cargo build, candidate sha256 F3B96644...); manifest 42 crate rows. Notebooks 18/19: the one RED, state_receipt_serializer_domain/model.spi, is MY module-selection error, not a regression. That module has no package header and no test blocks (discovered 0), so a standalone notebook cannot see char_backslash from its package dependency state_receipt_codec_model. Its proof is the crate regen + cargo check, which passed. BOX ACCEPT: 28 of 42 generated .rs on the box differed (pre-pack14a codegen, e.g. kit_resume 464 -> 766 lines); I copied the node's 28 files into the tree (unstaged; git holds the old ones). The manifest check is 42/42 sha256 equal, and freshness holds (no owner .spi newer than the regen). BOX TRAIN STARTED with -SkipRegen: launcher job-1793548387233 -> heavy job job-1793548391365-kit-TRAIN7, runner pinned F1DD2E34F1E816C8; launch-train.ps1's default RunnerHash 2E5F532E is stale and needs updating. Lesson for the pre-proof script: select notebook modules by '///- --package' header + test blocks, never by 'changed'.")
inl note_of_kit_train7_9 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN7", 9u32, "2026-11-01T16:01Z", "kit", "11-01 12:01 kit: the BOX TRAIN STOPPED at the crate gate (job-1793548391365, 11 s): kit_lint_macros lint.rs 1,040 and agile_todo_scan todo_scan.rs 1,021 lines, both over the 1,000-line gate. The node pre-proof never ran the gate, a gap in my script (proof-must-run-consumer-path); the fix script now runs 'crate gate --enforce' on the node. CAUSE: the committed .rs had lagged their sources (kit_resume 464 -> 766 and kit_standards 572 -> 920 are other lanes' source work, not codegen), plus tonight's typed-baseline CLI branch in lint (+133) and pack14a layout plus text_may_hold in todo_scan (+28). HAND SPLIT (hand-modeled-build-units), unstaged: (1) the baseline exports move from kit_lint_walk to kit_lint_classify (774 lines, already imports kit_lint_model), plus a new export kit_lint_baseline_write (writes the typed baseline, returns the row count); lint.spi calls classify; classify's !!!!Export migrated to export. (2) New crate agile_todo_standing (todo_standing union, standing_of, standing_label, standings record, standings_from), with workspace member, Cargo deps, Cargo.lock and census row added; todo_scan keeps one cross-crate call and drops its agile-task-census dependency. The ratchet over the 5 packages shows 0 regressions. Node proof: job-1793548828042-kit-node-split (regen of the 5 owners, crate gate, split manifest, todo_cli + kit_lint_model notebooks), then the --write-baseline consumer check. The kit-style hook flagged the cross-crate \\$' calls, which are kept on purpose: crates can only call each other through them, and the edit removes 2 and adds 1.")
inl note_of_kit_train7_10 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN7", 10u32, "2026-11-01T16:19Z", "kit", "11-01 12:19 kit: SPLIT PROVEN on the node in two rounds. Round 1 (job-1793548828042): classify grew 774 -> 1,245, because the baseline code is about 470 generated lines, so it could not live in classify. Round 2 (job-1793549384149): a new crate kit_lint_baseline (619 lines) holds kit_lint_baseline_rows and kit_lint_baseline_write. Final sizes: agile_todo_standing 123, agile_todo_scan 937, kit_lint_baseline 619, kit_lint_classify 774, kit_lint_macros 967, kit_lint_walk 651. Crate gate ok: 272 crates, 0 over (node and box). Notebooks: todo_cli 4/4, kit_lint_model 10/10. CONSUMER PATH: the candidate converts the live 909-row standards/lint-macros.spi to 909 typed rows, and 'lint macros <kit>/src --baseline' against either the converted or the live typed baseline gives violations 906, new 0, exit 0. Box accept: split manifest 6/6, TRAIN7 manifest 38/38 for the rows not superseded. launch-train.ps1's default RunnerHash was updated 2E5F532E -> F1DD2E34F1E816C8 (the runner box and node share). BOX TRAIN RELAUNCHED as TRAIN7b with -SkipRegen: launcher job-1793549960043.")
inl note_of_kit_train7_11 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN7", 11u32, "2026-11-01T17:27Z", "kit", "11-01 13:27 kit: TRAIN7b (job-1793549962708, 62 min): crate gate ok (272), candidate 1D93A1E4, notebooks 55/56; nothing installed. The one red, kit_do_file_steps/steps.spi, was NOT a test failure: its test passed 1/1, then the notebook built the untargeted main on Cells' default Zig target ('Export with 2 args not supported in the Zig backend'; memory notebook-main-default-zig). The module became a notebook when the EOIE-DO-COPY-LITERAL test block was added. FIX (unstaged): '///> _' above main, the idiom 10 other kit modules use. Node proof job-1793553852998: regen publishes 0 changed owners (steps.rs sha256 B84B76A5... = the TRAIN7 manifest), notebook 1/1. TRAIN7c launched with -SkipRegen (launcher job-1793554041486) over the full notebook set; launch-train has no -Only, and a full rerun on the candidate is the stronger evidence anyway.")
inl note_of_kit_train7_12 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN7", 12u32, "2026-11-01T18:59Z", "kit", "11-01 14:59 kit: TRAIN7c (heavy job-1793554047930) is still in its notebook phase at 14:58 (started 13:28; slower than TRAIN7b's 59 min on a loaded box). main landed the lib '::' respell at 14:53 (EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION n59) DURING that phase, so notebooks after 14:53 read the respelled lib. A red in TRAIN7c is first judged against that land (undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261101-132117) before kit code is suspected.")
inl note_of_kit_train7_13 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN7", 13u32, "2026-11-01T19:38Z", "kit", "11-01 15:38 kit: TRAIN7 INSTALLED. TRAIN7c (heavy job-1793554047930): crate gate 272/0 over, candidate 1D93A1E4, notebooks 56/56, release build ok, installed kit.exe A25B8FBD at 15:24, smoke ok; the lane copy was refreshed and the old binary kept in kit\\retired. ACCEPTANCE on the installed binary closed KIT-AGILE-LOST-UPDATES (10-round two-writer race: 0 lost, 0 refused), EOIE-DO-COPY-LITERAL (a literal file copies 1 file) and EOIE-NOTEBOOK-PROGRESS (the watch prints the batch line). DONE.")
inl note_of_kit_train7_14 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN7", 14u32, "2026-11-02T00:26Z", "kit", "11-01 20:26 kit: TRAIN8 launched (launcher job-1793579152082, -SkipRegen). Node pre-proof job-1793576729929: crate gate 272/0 over; owners kit_os_launch (605: the --after RemoteSession owner fix), kit_job_state (937: the placement suffix), kit_table_query (725: table to-spi with the rows index and --open), agile_planning_revision (271: the no-op edit short-circuit); notebooks 8/8. Box accept: manifest 4/4, crate gate ok. Also riding: x-dumps' Linux dotnet discovery (hand-written kit_process/native_compiler.rs), the attestation contract heals, notebook-batch/user-env portability. Held out for TRAIN9: KIT_JOB_SLOTS (kit_job_host over the gate), kit k3s (3,221 lines, being reworked to typed .spi rows), the bindings verb (parked by the user's 17:4x direction). Main holds lib-reshape R1b+R2 until this installs (21:50 at the latest).")
inl note_of_kit_train7_15 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN7", 15u32, "2026-11-02T00:35Z", "kit", "11-01 20:35 kit: TRAIN8 caveat (main 20:3x): x landed into the LIVE tree at 20:31 during TRAIN8 (lib/spiral/package.spiproj 9D730998 -> 12690959, additive erlang_* modules; apps/cells/spi cell.spi, main.spi, package.spiproj, new daemon.spi). TRAIN8 runs without a snapshot (started before KIT-TRAIN-SNAPSHOT-PIN made snapshots the default), so a red after 20:31 is judged against that land first (undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\x-c3c4-lib-20261101-203122). From TRAIN9 on, launch-train snapshots kit and lib by default (-LiveTree opts out).")
inl note_of_kit_train7_16 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN7", 16u32, "2026-11-02T02:57Z", "kit", "11-01 22:57 kit: TRAIN8 INSTALLED at 22:55: kit.exe 7C559D83 (TRAIN8s, snapshot kit+lib; candidate 9248993C; notebooks 44/44; release checks ok; lane copy refreshed, previous binary in kit\\retired). Main asked to ship it to the node (the --after owner fix). Acceptance: REMOTE-EXEC-S1 (job list byte-identical), KIT-SCALE no-op (unchanged, 1 ms), table to-spi on a tibia tsv: all green.")
inl note_of_kit_train7_17 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN7", 17u32, "2026-11-02T02:59Z", "kit", "11-01 22:59 kit: main shipped TRAIN8's kit.exe 7C559D83 to the NODE by renaming the running exe aside (the running x-verify48b job kept running; the old binary kept as kit-4983F9C0-replaced.exe), the deploys-never-wait-for-idle rule in practice. RemoteSession owner fix PROVEN on the node: a --after job queued over ssh got host_home=shared and ran after its predecessor, exit 0. The node --after queuing works again for every lane.")
inl note_of_pack_14_1 () = Note ("PACK-14", 1u32, "2026-11-01T13:26Z", "compiler", "11-01 11-01 09:26 compiler: OPENED as a P0 hotfix. Program: apps/compiler/packs/pack14/1-group-loop-scope.kitdo (on live core 2A746DF0111CF4EA = PACK-13 installed). Candidate pack14a: SpiralCompilerCore.dll DBC5EC18F14C354C, host DFC86B91968D447D. Regression sample staged at apps/compiler/packs/pack14/samples/mutual_tail_nested_callee (C exit 0; Rust built by pack14a exits 0; the installed compiler's Rust fails with E0425). DEFINITION OF DONE: predict vs pack13a's run with compile-status diffs 0 and residual diffs limited to Rust rows with a mutual group; fiscal's resolves_* green on t1101 with the candidate; installed by main; the sample in samples/ with its Rust row agreeing with C.")
inl note_of_pack_14_2 () = Note ("PACK-14", 2u32, "2026-11-01T13:30Z", "compiler", "11-01 11-01 09:30 compiler: REVIEW GATE MET, CANDIDATE READY = pack14a (SpiralCompilerCore.dll DBC5EC18F14C354C, SpiralCompiler.dll DFC86B91968D447D). Evidence: (1) the 3-function repro: pack14a's Rust builds under rustc -O and exits 0 = C (the installed compiler's output fails with E0425); (2) fiscal on node mirror t1101 with the candidate (SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL): resolves_the_nfe_tree + resolves_the_corpus_like_dotnet 2/2 passed, 0 type errors, no E0425 in raw (job-1793539537261); (3) predict vs pack13a's run (-080900 -> -092453): 7,413 rows, residual diffs 0, compile-status diffs 0, verdict diffs 0, timeouts 0. No matrix sample had the triggering shape (a method first reached from inside a group body that tail-calls a member), which is why PACK-12's review missed it. INSTALL: program 1-group-loop-scope.kitdo on live core 2A746DF0111CF4EA, then copy apps/compiler/packs/pack14/samples/mutual_tail_nested_callee into apps/compiler/tmp/samples/ (C and Rust rows default-on; both exit 0).")
inl note_of_pack_14_3 () = Note ("PACK-14", 3u32, "2026-11-01T13:33Z", "main", "main 09:3x INSTALLED pack14a (hotfix for PACK-12's group-loop leak): dry run reproduced the reviewed source from live core 2A746DF0111CF4EA (stacked F6F6879566C5A830 = candidate); built 102 s; SpiralCompilerCore.dll DBC5EC18F14C354C and SpiralCompiler.dll DFC86B91968D447D equal to the candidate; system dotnet launches it; backup compiler-installs\\pack14a-20261101-093119. Sample mutual_tail_nested_callee copied into tmp/samples. CONSUMER-PATH CHECK: probe compiles it on C and Rust (exit 0 both), and rustc --edition 2024 -O compiles the generated main.rs (exit 0) and the program exits 0 = C, so no E0425. Node: not yet; one-shot ship at 10:23 after compiler's libord A/B (the node goes straight from pack12b to pack14a, which includes pack13a).")
inl note_of_pack_14_4 () = Note ("PACK-14", 4u32, "2026-11-01T13:34Z", "compiler", "11-01 11-01 09:34 compiler: DONE: installed by main 09:31, core DBC5EC18F14C354C = candidate; mutual_tail_nested_callee in tmp/samples, and main's consumer check (rustc builds its main.rs, exit 0 = C) passed. The node gets pack14a (which includes pack13a) as soon as it's free; my libord sweeps already finished.")
inl note_of_pack_14_5 () = Note ("PACK-14", 5u32, "2026-11-01T13:35Z", "main", "main 09:4x NODE SHIPPED (node-ship printed SHIPPED): digest 0AF644516C09E959, capability smoke OK, previous kept as net11.0.replaced-pack14a. The node goes pack12b -> pack14a, so it also gets pack13a's package-parse fix. Shipped before the 10:23 one-shot (cancelled) because compiler's libord A/B finished ~09:20 and no node job was running. Box and node now match.")
inl note_of_cells_server_exit_tail_1 () = Note ("CELLS-SERVER-EXIT-TAIL", 1u32, "2026-11-01T13:30Z", "main", "main 09:3x, follow-up from CELLS-DAEMON-PARENT (Done; x's consumer check: 6 servers alive at +15 s, 0 at ~1-2 min). DoD: one run with timestamps for erl's exit and each spiral-cells- server's exit; if every server exits within 1 s of erl, record that the tail is BEAM shutdown and close; otherwise fix the wrapper so 'servers alive 5 s after erl exits' = 0. NEXT STEP: run run_notebook.ps1 on a small .spi with a background sampler logging erl and dotnet pids with exit times (no sleep loop: Register-ObjectEvent on process exit). TYPEFEATURESET: n/a (measurement only); if the wrapper needs a fix, the parent watch's states become a union (Watching | ParentGone | NoParent), not nullable env text.")
inl note_of_cells_server_exit_tail_2 () = Note ("CELLS-SERVER-EXIT-TAIL", 2u32, "2026-11-02T00:55Z", "compiler", "11-01 20:55 compiler: related hole from kit (11-01 20:4x): two Cells compiler servers (--server-tcp ... --stall-seconds 120) lived 1-2 days after their Cells daemon died. --stall-seconds only bounds an OUTSTANDING compile (watchStall), and the parent watch (exitWithParent) runs only when SPIRAL_SERVER_PARENT_PID is set, so an idle orphan waits forever. HOST FIX DRAFTED: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\CELLS-SERVER-EXIT-TAIL\\1-server-idle-exit.kitdo (5 replacements on Program.fs 615BAAED, dry run clean). serveSessions takes its cleanup paths and, when SPIRAL_SERVER_IDLE_EXIT_SECONDS > 0, a background watcher exits (deleting socket/pid/port files, as exitWithParent does) after that many seconds with no session. It never fires mid-session (busy flag set at accept, cleared with lastActive after the request). Opt-in, the same env style as SPIRAL_SERVER_PARENT_PID and SPIRAL_SERVER_BIND, so the warm daemons keep today's behaviour until Cells (targets/compiler_daemon) passes it, e.g. 600. Kit's side, start-under-shell parenting and job breakaway letting daemons escape, is KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS. PROOF NEEDED (next pack): start --server-tcp with the env at 15, see it exit about 20 s after its last session with its .pid/.bridge files gone, and confirm a session started at second 10 keeps it alive.")
inl note_of_cells_server_exit_tail_3 () = Note ("CELLS-SERVER-EXIT-TAIL", 3u32, "2026-11-02T01:22Z", "compiler", "11-01 21:22 compiler: IDLE EXIT PROVEN (node job-1793582243279-compiler-idle; candidate = live core + live host 615BAAED + the idle program). --server-tcp with SPIRAL_SERVER_IDLE_EXIT_SECONDS=15: pid and bridge files present at +5 s; at +30 s exited with code 0 and both files gone. Control without the env: still running at +30 s with its files (stopped by the harness). Rides the next pack after pack15c. Then Cells (compiler_daemon) and kit's spawners pass SPIRAL_SERVER_IDLE_EXIT_SECONDS (e.g. 600) together with SPIRAL_SERVER_PARENT_PID.")
inl note_of_cells_server_exit_tail_4 () = Note ("CELLS-SERVER-EXIT-TAIL", 4u32, "2026-11-02T06:11Z", "compiler", "11-02 02:11 compiler: rides pack15d, handed to main 01:4x with a passing install-pack -Programs dry run. Programs: CELLS-SERVER-EXIT-TAIL\\1, BACKEND-PRIMITIVE-PARITY\\3, GLEAM-JS-TARGET-GAPS\\4. Live core 55C243C7 / host B30F5F9B give candidate core B161EDA4DC69F256 / host 57A3FBAF0C683E22; SpiralCompiler.dll 9489144496A935E6, Core F16F6B2032F81F2D. Re-proven on the stacked Release candidate (box): with SPIRAL_SERVER_IDLE_EXIT_SECONDS=15, an idle --server-tcp exits by itself with code 0 within 30 s and removes its .pid; the control without the variable stays up (killed by the harness). Corpus A/B installed vs pack15d: 26 of 26 outputs byte-identical (tibia src to Lua, apps/spiral to Rust). Next: after install, Cells sets the variable on the servers it spawns (x's side), then close.")
inl note_of_cells_server_exit_tail_5 () = Note ("CELLS-SERVER-EXIT-TAIL", 5u32, "2026-11-02T07:00Z", "compiler", "11-02 03:00 compiler: pack15d INSTALLED on box, node and Europa; SPIRAL_SERVER_IDLE_EXIT_SECONDS is live. Next (x's side): Cells sets it on the servers it spawns, e.g. a few minutes, so a server whose client died without a parent watch still exits; then close.")
inl note_of_cells_server_exit_tail_6 () = Note ("CELLS-SERVER-EXIT-TAIL", 6u32, "2026-11-02T07:01Z", "x", "2026-11-02 03:01 x: CELLS SIDE IS IN (unstaged in apps/cells, live tree). compiler_daemon.ex:1163 port_env passes SPIRAL_SERVER_IDLE_EXIT_SECONDS=600 next to SPIRAL_SERVER_PARENT_PID. The --server-tcp launch at :596 (env: port_env, :639) is the only compiler-server spawn site in Cells (grep: --server/server-tcp/port_env). Pack15d's host honours the variable (compiler verified 15 s, exit 0). A self-exit is safe: the port's exit_status comes in as {:compiler_exit, token, _}, the handler at :327 sets compiler: nil, and the next compile starts a fresh server. NOT YET EXERCISED end to end: an idle exit followed by a successful compile in one daemon. That rides x's next Cells window proof (node_cells_window_proof -Tests on the daemon tests); the item closes when that run is green on pack15d.")
inl note_of_cells_server_exit_tail_7 () = Note ("CELLS-SERVER-EXIT-TAIL", 7u32, "2026-11-02T12:24Z", "x", "2026-11-02 08:24 x: GROOM: progress 0 -> 70, Planned -> Active. Both sides are in: pack15d (compiler, SPIRAL_SERVER_IDLE_EXIT_SECONDS) is installed on box, node and europa, and Cells passes 600 s from compiler_daemon.ex:1163 (unstaged). LEFT: the end-to-end proof, a node Cells run that idles past 600 s and then compiles. If it is not done before CELLS-PORT-COMPILER-DAEMON, that port carries it as typed lifecycle state.")
inl note_of_cells_server_exit_tail_8 () = Note ("CELLS-SERVER-EXIT-TAIL", 8u32, "2026-11-03T07:32Z", "compiler", "11-03 07:3x compiler GROOM (WIP cap: Active = touched in 12 h). Parked to Planned (19 h). Owner x. Next: the end-to-end node Cells run that idles past 600 s and then compiles, or it rides CELLS-PORT-COMPILER-DAEMON.")
inl note_of_cells_server_exit_tail_9 () = Note ("CELLS-SERVER-EXIT-TAIL", 9u32, "2026-11-05T09:42Z", "compiler", "11-05 05:4x compiler, SUPPORTING EVIDENCE (not the full DoD proof): orphan census after a busy night (box: many lib gates, cells lands, notebook gates and 7 compiler installs; node: TRAIN27 attempt plus x/tibia/fiscal gates). Compiler servers (dotnet ... --server-tcp) alive at 05:4x: box 0, node 0, so none orphaned with a dead parent. Both halves are live: the host honours SPIRAL_SERVER_IDLE_EXIT_SECONDS (Program.fs:1073, since pack15d; still in pack44), and Cells passes 600 next to SPIRAL_SERVER_PARENT_PID (compiler_daemon.ex:1235-1236, now landed through CELLS-GATE-PINNED-COMPILER's file). LEFT, as recorded: the end-to-end run that idles past 600 s and then compiles.")
inl note_of_cells_server_exit_tail_10 () = Note ("CELLS-SERVER-EXIT-TAIL", 10u32, "2026-11-05T12:56Z", "compiler", "11-05 08:5x compiler: DoD PROVEN END TO END (box, installed pack44, live apps/cells, private daemon port 47917, lib resultm.spi 7 tests, notebook mode = warm daemon). (A) EXIT TAIL: gate run 08:19-08:26: the gate client retires the daemon ('retire requested ... retired; stopping' 08:26:36), all 6 server processes gone when sampled 08:26:51. Warm run 1 08:30-08:32: the daemon retired itself at 08:37:34 ('idle and free memory under 4096 MB', the 5-min pressure rule, box near its memory watermark); its 6 server processes (3 wrappers + 3 re-exec children) exited 08:37:37-41 with code 1, BEFORE erl's own stop line, i.e. within 5 s of the retire. No 15-90 s tail. (B) IDLE EXIT THEN COMPILE in ONE daemon: run 2 08:39:54-08:43:15 with SPIRAL_CELLS_COMPILER_RETIRE_FREE_MB=0 (pressure retire off; 30-min daemon idle default) on erl 5880. Its servers idled out by themselves at 08:52:42-08:53:06 with code 0 (SPIRAL_SERVER_IDLE_EXIT_SECONDS=600 from compiler_daemon.ex), and erl 5880 stayed alive. Run 3 08:53:51-08:56:33 through the SAME erl 5880 started 3 fresh servers (08:54:14) and passed 7/7. Both halves work together; closing.")
inl note_of_cells_plot_export_1 () = Note ("CELLS-PLOT-EXPORT", 1u32, "2026-11-01T14:34Z", "main", "main 10:3x (user 11-01 10:3x). DoD: (1) a minimal checkout of polyglot at its Nov-2025 state (sparse/shallow, under 500 MB) exports the physics notebook to HTML with its SVG plots, kept as the reference artifact; (2) Cells' export of lib/spiral/physics.spi shows the same plots inline (SVG, no screenshots) plus code coloring; (3) the guitar string renders as one animated element, not stacked frames; (4) a side-by-side page in dir-tree-html. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: a cell output as a union (Text | Svg of svg_doc | Animation of frame list * fps | Table of typed rows), with plot specs as typed records (axes, series), not raw SVG strings assembled by hand. NEXT STEP: find polyglot's Nov-2025 commit with the physics notebook and its plotting code (git log in C:\\home\\git\\polyglot), and list the plot functions physics.spi calls today.")
inl note_of_cells_plot_export_2 () = Note ("CELLS-PLOT-EXPORT", 2u32, "2026-11-01T14:40Z", "main", "main 10:4x STEP 1 DONE, cheaper than planned: the reference export already exists in polyglot's git history, so no Nov-2025 rebuild is needed for the reference. 'git -C C:\\home\\git\\polyglot show 706e6beb~1:lib/spiral/physics.dib.html' (2025-01-13, the last version before the deploy commit 706e6beb deleted it) is 2,612,633 bytes with 82 inline <svg>, 101 data:image embeds and plotting scripts (plotly/vega references). The plotting code lives in polyglot lib/fsharp/Plotting.dib (F#) and apps/plot (a Rust plot crate: plot.rs, lib.rs). REVISED NEXT STEP: diff that page's per-cell outputs against Cells' current export of lib/spiral/physics.spi to list the missing output kinds (inline SVG, frame sequences), then port Plotting.dib's plot spec to a typed Spiral module (the output union in this item's plan) rendered by Cells' html.ex. The DoD's polyglot checkout is still needed only if ERL-VS-DIB-BENCH wants live dib timings.")
inl note_of_cells_plot_export_3 () = Note ("CELLS-PLOT-EXPORT", 3u32, "2026-11-06T10:45Z", "main", "main 11-06 06:5x WHY IT STALLED (user: we still haven't finished the plot rendering in physics; weird kit didn't bring it up). (1) kit agile next ranks it 67 of 122 ready team:main items: WSJF 4000, because the 480-min estimate divides P1's value and the only dependent is P2. (2) Step 1 (the reference page from polyglot history: 82 inline svg, 101 data:image) was done 11-01 14:40, but progress stayed 0% and the status Planned, so it looked unstarted. (3) Every groom round checks Active and Blocked items, never Planned user asks. Fixes now: progress 15 for step 1, priority P1 -> P0 (second user ask), split hint below; kit side filed as KIT-NEXT-STARVATION. Remaining steps, each light and under 2 h: (a) diff the reference page's output kinds against Cells' current export of lib/spiral/physics.spi; (b) a typed plot output (SVG) in Cells' html.ex, overlapping NOTEBOOK-HTML-RENDERER (rank 15, replaces nbconvert); (c) the guitar string as one animated element.")
inl note_of_cells_plot_export_4 () = Note ("CELLS-PLOT-EXPORT", 4u32, "2026-11-06T11:12Z", "main", "main 11-06 07:2x STEP (a) DONE, root cause found. The plot machinery exists end to end: Cells display.ex turns a value shaped (caption, x_desc, y_desc, [(label, xs, ys)]) into SVG via the plot tool (workspace/target/release/plot, built by spiral's scripts/build.ps1 before lib), and notebook.ex:1326 writes result.displays as display_data. CI's push build does execute physics (lib/spiral/build.ps1 without -fast). But the published physics.spi.ipynb has 107 cells, 26 with outputs, all of them plain stream text, and 0 image/svg+xml. Every chart cell (92, 94, 97, 100, 103, 106: the constant_force/proton/ke charts and the string waves) is a ///- --test --symbol test cell with 0 outputs. Cause: Display.from_value runs only in cells.ex run_host_rust (lines 445-475, the interactive host-Rust path with show_value). Test cells run through the per-target test path, so a test whose value is a chart never reaches the display path. Since the .dib -> .spi migration all of physics' charts live in test cells, so no plot can render. NEXT STEP (b), about 90 min: in the test-cell path, when the Rust target's program value matches line_plots/1, call Display.from_value and attach the SVGs to that cell's result.displays (one cell output per plot), with a Cells unit test using render_plot as the fake renderer; then (c) the string cells (100/106 return a list of wave plots) as one animated SVG (SMIL or a CSS step animation over the frames) instead of N stacked plots. Proof = a cells run of physics.spi whose ipynb has image/svg+xml outputs on cells 92-106, then its .spi.html. Coordinate the land with x (owns apps/cells).")
inl note_of_cells_plot_export_5 () = Note ("CELLS-PLOT-EXPORT", 5u32, "2026-11-06T11:38Z", "main", "DoD: (1) the reference export of physics from polyglot history (82 svg) is kept as the comparison; (2) Cells' export of lib/spiral/physics.spi shows the charts inline as SVG; (3) the guitar string is one animated element. Next step: read the codespace run of physics.spi (plots/cs drive.log, svg count per cell), then fix the test-cell value path in apps/cells (cells.ex compile/10 unit_first discards the value; own-main cells 100/106 are the control) with x.")
inl note_of_cells_plot_export_6 () = Note ("CELLS-PLOT-EXPORT", 6u32, "2026-11-06T13:35Z", "main", "main 11-06 12:3x STEP (b) PROVEN on a codespace (spiral c0e77c3 + 6 draft files; drafts in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\CELLS-PLOT-EXPORT with bases.txt): physics.spi 43/43 passed; the notebook's cells 92, 94, 97 and 103 now carry image/svg+xml display_data; mix spiral.html renders 4 <div class=plot> SVGs on the page (385 KB), the first titled 'response to a constant force' with axes, ticks and 42 paths. Baseline before the change: 0 SVG. Display and html tests green. Design: lib physics.spi gets show_chart, which prints a SPIRAL_CELLS_DISPLAY block with MIME application/vnd.spiral.plot+json, built by a typed chart_json (json::quote for labels, format_debug for f64s, a runtime :~ ^ recursion over array_base); Cells display.ex render_values sends that JSON to the existing plot tool (the same shape plot_json emits) and shows a failure as text; cells.ex calls render_values on both run paths; html.ex renders image/svg+xml inline (.plot svg max-width 100%). Four codespace rounds caught: ++# unbound in physics (no sm'_operators), format_debug being Spiral's printer not Rust Debug, array vs array_base, and an inline (:=) recursion unrolled past EJP0040. Not yet: wave_1 (own-main cell) shows no plot, and wave_2's 66 frames are step (c), the animation. Next step: x lands the Cells half (display.ex, cells.ex, html.ex + 2 tests); main lands physics.spi through lib_land_window.")
inl note_of_cells_plot_export_7 () = Note ("CELLS-PLOT-EXPORT", 7u32, "2026-11-06T13:38Z", "x", "2026-11-06 09:38 x (Cells owner): REVIEWED main's apps/cells drafts (display.ex 1B46A10FCF2A, cells.ex 11055E9AC4D5, html.ex C7C5D6C353A2, display_test 6D7DB8B10A61, html_test 6EBC7B2A69B6). OK to land: render_values passes non-plot displays through, every render_svg error path returns a string (display.ex 103-137), html emits the svg in div.plot with scoped CSS. Sequencing: cells.ex shares base 1C0D48D84EDD with x's CELLS-NOTEBOOK-ORDER-REGRESSION revert (hunks at 370/452 vs 1052, no overlap). x lands the revert first (the CI red fix, proof x-cellsfix2c pending on the node), then rebases these two hunks, formats the 5 files, gates them on the node, and lands with -ProvenLog. PENDING.")
inl note_of_cells_plot_export_8 () = Note ("CELLS-PLOT-EXPORT", 8u32, "2026-11-06T13:54Z", "main", "main 11-06 13:0x STEP (c) DRAFTED: Cells display.ex handles application/vnd.spiral.plot-frames+json by rendering each frame through the plot tool and combining them into ONE SVG whose frames take turns via SMIL <animate attributeName=visibility calcMode=discrete> (0.1 s per frame, looping; no JavaScript), plus a test (2 frames -> 2 animate elements, keyTimes 0;0.5000;1.0000; empty or malformed lists stay visible as text). Lib physics v2 draft (lib__spiral__physics.v2.spi): show_frames over array_base chart (a :== chart alias keeps lines under 120); wave_2 pipes its 66 frames into it; wave_1 shows its frame directly. FOUND: wave_1's old body defined a local main inside the test and never called it, so the test ran nothing and passed silently. Box probe: the 66-frame wave prints one valid plot-frames JSON (66 frames, 66 points each). x reviewed both Cells passes (fixes applied: a joined test line from my insert, a decode-error arm) and lands the Cells half after its order revert. The lib v1 land (4 charts) is running now; v2 follows it.")
inl note_of_cells_plot_export_9 () = Note ("CELLS-PLOT-EXPORT", 9u32, "2026-11-06T13:55Z", "x", "2026-11-06 09:55 x: main's FINAL drafts are verified (display.ex 43936FE6DFFB, cells.ex 11055E9AC4D5, html.ex C7C5D6C353A2, display_test FEDF0D2F8CF7, html_test 6EBC7B2A69B6), and both review fixes are in. COMBINED land draft: kit drafts spiral\\CELLS-PLOT-EXPORT-ON-ORDER. cells.ex EC7B2F28CCFF is main's two render_values hunks 3-way-merged onto x's order revert D2B60B15ACD3 (a clean merge, +2 lines). apply.ps1 checks bases D2B60B15ACD3 / 9E1722D15B46 / E6BC328C6B43 / 78A5195260A8 / D713D0D1FC30 and every draft hash. Landed unformatted, as main agreed (live isn't mix-formatted; a format would add about 300 unrelated lines). Next: after the order revert lands on the box, gate on the node (display_test, html_test, cells_test, and the physics notebook on main's landed lib), then land with -ProvenLog. Watch: wave_2's 66 frames mean 66 plot-tool renders in one cell, so its time goes against the cell timeout.")
inl note_of_cells_plot_export_10 () = Note ("CELLS-PLOT-EXPORT", 10u32, "2026-11-06T14:01Z", "main", "main 11-06 13:1x LIB V1 LANDED green (lib_land_window main-physics-show-chart): physics.spi 394261AE8B24, consumer apps/spiral compiles, type-probe PASS (43 tests typed, 0 errors), 0 respell drift, lib digest 958D72D11FE6A76D; undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261106-095404. Unstaged for the user's commit. V2 (frames + wave_1 fix) landing now on base 394261AE8B24. Cells half pending at x (after x's order revert, gate x-cellsfix2d).")
inl note_of_cells_plot_export_11 () = Note ("CELLS-PLOT-EXPORT", 11u32, "2026-11-06T14:12Z", "main", "main 11-06 13:1x LIB V2 LANDED green (main-physics-frames, after one retry: the first try found physics.spi locked for 60 s by a transient reader and restored itself exactly): physics.spi 874EC40E16A4, type-probe 43 typed 0 errors, 0 respell drift, lib digest 159A2574BEEF1DC4, undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261106-100816. The lib side is complete: 4 charts + wave_1 frame + wave_2's 66-frame animation. Remaining: x lands the Cells half (render_values, animation, html inline SVG) after its order revert; then the next spiral CI publish shows the plots on https://i574n.github.io/spiral/lib/spiral/physics.spi.html (proof = SVG count on that page).")
inl note_of_cells_plot_export_12 () = Note ("CELLS-PLOT-EXPORT", 12u32, "2026-11-06T14:12Z", "x", "2026-11-06 10:12 x: main's lib half is LANDED live: physics.spi 874EC40E16A4 (v2: show_chart + show_frames; undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261106-100816). The x Cells-half gate checks the physics notebook against it: 5 static SVGs (cells 92/94/97/100/103) plus 1 animated SVG (wave_2, 66 frames) in the --gate output and the mix spiral.html page. Queued after x-cellsfix2d lands the order revert. PENDING.")
inl note_of_cells_plot_export_13 () = Note ("CELLS-PLOT-EXPORT", 13u32, "2026-11-06T19:16Z", "x", "2026-11-06 15:16 x: x-plot1 (job-1793987532284, node, pack55d 257DB91886B97811): the Cells land window GREEN (display_test, html_test and cells_test, 55 passed), but the physics notebook gate on physics.spi 874EC40E16A4 is 41/43, 2 failed, against main's codespace 43/43. The SVG count run wrote no ipynb/html, so the 5+1 SVG check is unproven. NOT landed on the box. Asked main to name the 2 failing tests WITHOUT the Cells half: environmental means land; caused by the Cells half means fix first. The x-diag3 diagnostic waited 36 min for a node slot and was stopped. PENDING.")
inl note_of_cells_plot_export_14 () = Note ("CELLS-PLOT-EXPORT", 14u32, "2026-11-06T19:55Z", "x", "2026-11-06 15:55 x: Cells half LANDED on the box (unstaged): cells.ex D2B60B15ACD3 -> EC7B2F28CCFF (render_values in run_host_rust and run_compiled), display.ex -> 43936FE6DFFB, html.ex -> C7C5D6C353A2, display_test -> FEDF0D2F8CF7, html_test -> 6EBC7B2A69B6. Closed by -ProvenLog from x-plot1 (job-1793987532284, node, pack55d; display/html/cells_test 55 passed), byte-identical; undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\cells-20261106-155425. Hunks left unformatted, as agreed. The physics 41/43 is main's and is not caused by this: wave_1/wave_2 fail on ZIG only (interpolated-string macro), the same without the Cells half (main, box). Remaining for Done: main's zig fix, then the 5-static + 1-animated SVG count.")
inl note_of_cells_plot_export_15 () = Note ("CELLS-PLOT-EXPORT", 15u32, "2026-11-06T20:52Z", "main", "main 11-06 16:5x LIB HALF FIXED AND LANDED (physics v3, 6D3066962289; undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261106-164127; closed green: consumer compile, document tests 26 passed, type_probe PASS with 43 tests typed, respell_drift 0). Root cause of x-plot1's 41/43: wave_1 and wave_2 labelled frames with ($'$\"{!n}\"' : string), an F#-interpolation host macro that HEAD carried but never emitted (wave_1's local main was never called). v2 made it reachable, and the Zig target can't parse it. Now sm'::format n. CORRECTION: the 43/43 codespace run (13:04Z) predates v2, so v2's frame path had no gate until the box run. proof for v3 (on a scratch lib copy BEFORE the land, Cells with x's plot half): physics notebook 43 discovered, 43 passed, 0 failed (zig included); the rendered physics.spi.ipynb holds 72 <svg> = 5 static charts + 1 animated container + 66 frames, and 66 <set> frames. The Cells half was landed by x at 15:54. Both halves are in the live tree, unstaged.")
inl note_of_cells_plot_export_16 () = Note ("CELLS-PLOT-EXPORT", 16u32, "2026-11-06T20:53Z", "main", "main 11-06 16:5x DONE, DoD met. proof: (1) the polyglot reference (82 svg) is kept as the comparison; (2) Cells' export of lib/spiral/physics.spi shows 5 charts inline as SVG; (3) the guitar string (wave_2) is ONE animated element of 66 SVG frames switched by <set> (72 <svg> total in physics.spi.ipynb), with the physics notebook at 43/43 on every target including zig. The live physics.spi 6D3066962289 differs from the gated v3 only by sm'.format -> sm'::format, which respell_drift requires and which resolves to the same definition. Cells half by x (undo cells-20261106-155425), lib half by main (undo 20261106-164127). Unstaged; reaches GitHub with the user's spiral push.")
inl note_of_cells_plot_export_17 () = Note ("CELLS-PLOT-EXPORT", 17u32, "2026-11-06T20:58Z", "x", "2026-11-06 16:58 x (Cells owner): Cells half CONFIRMED by main's end-to-end proof. main's zig fix landed (physics.spi 6D3066962289), and with x's landed Cells half the physics notebook is 43/43 including zig, with the rendered ipynb holding 5 static SVGs plus 1 animated container of 66 frames. Both halves are landed. main closes the item.")
inl note_of_fiscal_emitted_helpers_to_lib_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-EMITTED-HELPERS-TO-LIB", 1u32, "2026-11-01T14:36Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 10:41 fiscal: MEASURED: in the 44 generated units, \"inl sample_path\" is emitted 44 times, \"let rec insert\" 43 and \"let rec nth\" 43 (the bench helpers; nth returns the sentinel -1i64 on an empty list). lib already has am''.sort (array sort), listm''.try_item (option el) and file_system.find_parent (which sample_path wraps).\nDONE WHEN: grep over generated/ finds 0 \"let rec insert\", 0 \"let rec nth\" and at most 1 sample_path definition (in a shared runtime module the units import); regeneration changes only those lines; every unit gate stays green; model_metrics on a regenerated unit shows M8 = 0 for the emitted bench code.\nNEXT STEP: after FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND lands, in src/generator.spi replace bench_insert/bench_nth (scratch split draft) or the family_bench text with calls to am''.sort over the timings array and listm''.try_item 15i32; move sample_path into one generated runtime unit (generated/fiscal_runtime) listed in each unit''s package dependencies (module_package already supports dependencies).\nTYPEFEATURESET PLAN: the median is \"option i64\" (try_item), never -1; sample paths go through a nominal \":! sample_name = string\" so a schema path and a sample path cannot be swapped.")
inl note_of_fiscal_emitted_helpers_to_lib_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-EMITTED-HELPERS-TO-LIB", 2u32, "2026-11-01T14:49Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 11:03 fiscal: SIZE: the emitted helpers that lib already covers total 784 lines across the 44 units (sample_path 440, insert 172, nth 172). That is small next to the 453,477 lines of structural duplication (shared closures and patterns, FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES / FISCAL-XSD-PATTERNS-LARGE). So this item matters for M8 (the -1i64 sentinel in nth) and for the reuse principle, while the size win lives in the closure dedup.")
inl note_of_fiscal_emitted_helpers_to_lib_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-EMITTED-HELPERS-TO-LIB", 3u32, "2026-11-02T20:42Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-02 16:50 fiscal: SHARED RUNTIME UNIT REGENERATED ON PACK17 (job-1793646608824-fiscal-runtime-regen17, t1101, core E556D773EB123175 at both ends): generator 23/23; 90 files change (45 .spi + 45 .spiproj, new generated_fiscal_runtime unit, 0 certificates units); runtime unit 2/2; consumer generated_cfdi_tfd_1_1 2/2. Hashes verified against the 90-row manifest on the box (scratch, not placed yet). A first run (F16F) was VOID across the pack17 switch, and it exposed EJP0040 in the consumer: inl median walked the runtime list of timed runs (listm'.try_item/listm.length) and unrolled past 1000 dynamic ifs. A/B on one core: committed unit 2/2, regenerated 1 failed, so it was my change. Fix in src/generated_runtime.spi: let rec run_count/run_at join points, plus test median_walks_a_runtime_list on countdown (dyn 31i64); mutation (old median + new test) fails EJP0040, so the test is not vacuous. FOUND: scripts/format-generated.ps1 keyed its cache on the raw text only, so 80 of 82 units were served F16F formatter output under pack17. Fixed in the tree (cache dir keyed on SHA-256 of SpiralCompiler.dll + SpiralCompilerCore.dll). CI is not affected (no cache on runners). NEXT: job fiscal-pack17-format-saft (after the bench pair) runs a cold pack17 format, PREDICTION 0 files change, and gates pt_saft's real-document round trip; then place the 90 files in fiscal/generated, unstaged.")
inl note_of_fiscal_emitted_helpers_to_lib_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-EMITTED-HELPERS-TO-LIB", 4u32, "2026-11-03T01:03Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-02 21:03 fiscal: DONE RULE MET IN THE OUTPUT, units placed (unstaged). job-1793658234964-fiscal-typed-roots-regen (t1101, core 8960CAB701FEF46E start and end): generator 23/23 on the committed generator (b35fae6: typed family roots + insert_run), cold format 82/82 (0 from cache), runtime unit 3/3 (median_takes_the_middle_run, median_walks_a_runtime_list, insert_run_keeps_runtime_runs_ascending), consumer generated_cfdi_tfd_1_1 2/2; 90 files (45 .spi + 45 .spiproj, 2 new, 0 certificates). PRE-REGISTERED COMPARISON vs job-1793646608824 (pack17 run before typed roots and insert_run): exactly 44 .spi differ and 0 .spiproj, and every family-unit difference is the removed 'let rec insert' block, its call lines, or the size-derived '--timeout' header; 0 unexplained lines. So the typed family roots are output-neutral, and grep over the new generated/ finds 0 'let rec insert', 0 'let rec nth', 1 sample_path definition (generated_fiscal_runtime), 0 -1i64 sentinels. PLACED in fiscal/generated: 88 modified + new generated_fiscal_runtime/ (untracked, the user adds it), LF only. This is the fix for the generated drift CI shows on b35fae6/b1ce33c. pt_saft's unit is replaced after job fiscal-t1101-chain regenerates it with its pinned known_defect (FISCAL-PT-SAFT). Progress 0 -> 90; Done on the first green CI with these units committed.")
inl note_of_fiscal_emitted_helpers_to_lib_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-EMITTED-HELPERS-TO-LIB", 5u32, "2026-11-03T03:04Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-02 23:04 fiscal: FORMAT-STABLE ON PACK20C: job-1793674332204-fiscal-format20c (t1101, core 4E48590A5408C14B throughout) cold-formatted the tree as placed (82 units formatted, 0 from cache with the compiler-keyed cache, 0 failed) and changed 0 files. The placed generated/ set is therefore stable across E556, 8960 and pack20c, so CI's drift guard sees only the regeneration content, not formatter churn, whichever of these cores spiral main ships.")
inl note_of_fiscal_emitted_helpers_to_lib_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-EMITTED-HELPERS-TO-LIB", 6u32, "2026-11-03T07:49Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 03:49 fiscal: COMMITTED BY THE USER as one pair: spiral 98e51d32 (03:41, xsd_emit dereference fix) + fiscal 741c715 (03:42, 93 files: src generator/lifecycle/corpus_checks, 88 regenerated units, the new generated_fiscal_runtime, pt_saft against the fixed lib). PRE-REGISTERED PREDICTION for fiscal CI run 41598162815 (and spiral 41598093899): 'build.ps1 / generated / matches the committed copy' and 0 problems on ubuntu-24.04 AND windows-2025, generator 23/23, every generated unit green including generated_fiscal_runtime 3/3 and pt_saft 2/2. Verdict when the run completes; on green this item goes Done (its DONE rule: 0 insert, 0 nth, 1 sample_path definition, every unit gate green) and XSD-CROSS-NAMESPACE-NAMES / FISCAL-CORPUS-LIST-ON-DEMAND close with it.")
inl note_of_fiscal_emitted_helpers_to_lib_7 () = Note ("FISCAL-EMITTED-HELPERS-TO-LIB", 7u32, "2026-11-03T09:57Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 05:57 fiscal: DONE, prediction n6 confirmed: CI run 41598162815 (push 741c715 with spiral 98e51d32), ubuntu-24.04 AND windows-2025: \"build.ps1 / generated / matches the committed copy\", generated_fiscal_runtime 3/3, generated_pt_saft_1_04_01 2/2, \"all 87 test files green and every example validates\". The generated tree has 0 'let rec insert', 0 'let rec nth', 1 sample_path definition (generated_fiscal_runtime) and every unit gate is green.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_1 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF", 1u32, "2026-11-01T14:38Z", "compiler", "R5 SPEC. Better than F#: F# nameof is only an identifier; ours also yields (1) the full case table of a union as a compile-time list (cases_of), (2) a total to_name / of_name pair derived per union, of_name returning an option, (3) qualified names (module::case) and (4) a stable rename-safe name checked by the formatter. DOD: a sample nameof_cases whose test block asserts to_name/of_name round-trip on a 5-case union on all ///> backends, and peval folds nameof to a string literal (grep the generated Rust: no match arm for the printer when the case is static). NEXT STEP: census the existing hand mappings (SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL) to pick the API shape from real call sites, then a prototype op in the Infer section. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: nameof returns a phantom-tagged name (name t), not a bare string, so names of different types do not mix; of_name returns option t, never -1 or a default case; the case table is a GADT-indexed list so its length is known at compile time.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_2 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF", 2u32, "2026-11-01T14:39Z", "compiler", "11-01 10:38 compiler: lane-map placement: theme language/typefeatureset, after SPELLING-PROFILES in the compiler queue; SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL census runs first (CPU-light) to shape the API from real call sites.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_3 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF", 3u32, "2026-11-01T21:47Z", "main", "main 17:4x RAISED P1 -> P0 (user 11-01 17:4x: 'lanes are still writing non granular code ... also writing functions to map strings to types instead of nameof, we gotta prioritize that'). Compiler: this ships before more enum<->string code accumulates. SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL's detector runs right after it.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_4 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF", 4u32, "2026-11-01T21:56Z", "fiscal", "fiscal 11-01 (consumer evidence): (1) fiscal src/canon.spi ubl_document_name maps UblInvoice -> \"ubl-invoice\" by hand; with union-case nameof it becomes kebab(nameof d). (2) DESIGN INPUT: generated XSD enum unions cannot derive their printer/parser from case names. XSD values are not identifiers (\"01\", \"00\", \"Brasil\" vs \"BRASIL\", which collide under case folding in Pascal) and case names are sanitized (\"TEnderEmi_xPais_BRASIL\"), so the derived printer needs a per-case value attribute (an annotated literal), with nameof as the default when absent. Otherwise every generated unit keeps its hand-emitted x_..._to_string / _of_string matches.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_5 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF", 5u32, "2026-11-01T21:59Z", "compiler", "11-01 18:00 compiler: CENSUS (the n1 next step; tracked .spi/.spir outside deps, samples, target, backlog and generated). Detector: a match arm whose case name and string literal are the same word after case/underscore/hyphen folding. to_name arm `| Case => \"case\"`, of_name arm `| \"case\" => [Some] Case`. RESULTS (to_name / of_name / files): kit 160 / 0 / 30 (src/kit_exec_metrics/metrics.spi 13, kit_standards/rules.spi 7, kit_do_program/compiled.spi 3, ...); x 15 / 6 / 4 (apps/sim/spi/invariants.spi 5/6, personas.spi 4, apps/client/posts.spi 5, wire.spi 1); tibia 11 / 0 / 3 (apps/host/arena_host.spi 5, apps/suite/suite.spi 5, arena/competitor.spi 1); fiscal 10 / 0 / 2 (src/lifecycle.spi 8, canon.spi 2; generated units excluded, they are XSD-emitted); dice 9 / 0 / 2 (ui/src/components/menu_tabs.spi 8); spiral 3 / 2 / 4 (lib async.spi, xsd_regex.spi, cli_args.spi, apps/spiral/spiral.spi 0/2; apps/cells/spi/targets.spi has 9 exact-name arms on top). TOTAL about 208 to_name arms and 8 of_name arms. API SHAPE FROM THE SITES: printing dominates, about 26 to 1. Most sites print lower or snake case, not the exact case name, so a name STYLE is part of the API. EXISTING PIECES in lib reflection.spi: union_try_pick (of_name; accepts the exact or lowercased key; option), union_to_string (to_name, but only cuda/rust/typescript tests, and string-split based), get_union_fields_untag (the compile-time case table as (string * t) list). PLAN (smallest total, portable cut first): (1) lib `case_name \\* t. (style : name_style) (x : t) : string` for payload-free unions, a fold over get_union_fields_untag whose comparisons peval folds to a literal when x is static; name_style = Exact | Lower | Snake | Kebab is a union, never a string flag. Plus `case_of_name \\* t. (style) (text : string) : option t`, a total parse returning an option, never a default case. (2) the compiler op (n1: phantom-tagged name t, GADT case table) replaces the fold for payload unions and emits one match per backend. HEAL ORDER after (1) lands: kit's 30 files first (160 arms). Each site becomes `case_name Snake x`, and the detector (this regex as a kit command) runs in the gates so new arms cannot appear.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_6 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF", 6u32, "2026-11-01T22:57Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 18:4x tibia: INTERIM, so no more hand tables accumulate before this ships: lib case_labels.spi LANDED 18:43 (9EFC57121E95). case_label prefix separator x and case_of_label prefix separator label derive a union's labels from its case names via reflection::get_union_fields_untag (PascalCase -> separator-joined lower case, optional prefix strip). No string table is written by hand. Proven lua + rust (Europa gate, mutant caught). tibia uses it in apps/suite/suite.spi (backend_name, status_name, memo_name, budget_kind_name/_of: 23 hand-mapped lines removed) and results/arena_rows.spi (competitor_of, monster_of: 12 removed). When SPIRAL-NAMEOF's derived to_name/of_name land, case_labels should become thin wrappers or be retired: its callers pass only a prefix and a separator, which is the API shape real call sites needed (input for SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL).")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_7 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF", 7u32, "2026-11-01T23:07Z", "main", "main 19:2x (user 11-01 19:1x: 'we're using nameof in reflection now, but that's an workaround, we gotta check later how to change the compiler itself, to get an even better result than what the fsharp compiler has, search for user input history or tasks when i mentioned about this'). This item IS that task (its title: 'a nameof stronger than F#'). The lanes' interim is lib reflection (nameof for record fields, union_to_string/union_try_pick for cases: tibia, kit today). The compiler version should make those library calls unnecessary. Design input from fiscal: generated XSD enum maps need a per-case VALUE attribute (values like '01' and 'Brasil'/'BRASIL' aren't distinct identifiers), so the derived printer/parser takes an optional per-case label.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_8 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF", 8u32, "2026-11-01T23:09Z", "compiler", "11-01 19:16 compiler: GROOM split. The portable lib cut (exact case names, payload-free unions) moved to SPIRAL-NAMEOF-LIB-CUT (120m). This item is now the compiler op only (re-estimated to 240m): a phantom-tagged name t, name styles (Exact | Lower | Snake | Kebab, applied at compile time), payload unions, and peval folding to a literal. DoD unchanged (n1 sample nameof_cases).")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_9 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF", 9u32, "2026-11-03T07:30Z", "compiler", "11-03 07:3x compiler GROOM (WIP cap: Active = touched in 12 h). Parked to Planned (32 h). Next: the compiler op slice 1, nameof on a payload-free union case folding to a literal in peval, with sample nameof_cases (n1 DoD).")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_10 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF", 10u32, "2026-11-03T11:48Z", "compiler", "11-03 08:0x compiler: DoD MEASURED AGAINST TODAY'S LIB, and both checks are already met by lib reflection (no new compiler op needed for them). (1) Round trip: a 5-case union (Alpha..Epsilon) through reflection::case_name -> case_of_name, plus case_name -> \"Delta\" and of_name \"epsilon\" -> None, on rust, gleam, lua, typescript and fsharp: box lib gate 12/12 tests, 0 failed targets, 0 not_run (cuda lines stripped: the cuda runner crashes on the node, access violation, as does the node's stale-runner lua). (2) Static fold: reflection::case_name Gamma compiles to 534 bytes of Rust with 0 case literals and 1 match arm (the whole length folds to a constant); a dynamic case emits the printer (5 literals, 23 arms), as expected. Landing the test block nameof_cases_round_trip into lib reflection.spi (job compiler-lib-land-nameof, base 6EA85EE1CBD0F2F2). Left on this item beyond its DoD: the typefeatureset extras (a phantom-tagged name t instead of string, name styles, qualified module::case names); I propose closing on the DoD and filing those as SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_11 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF", 11u32, "2026-11-03T12:14Z", "compiler", "11-03 08:1x compiler: DONE on the DoD. The test block nameof_cases_round_trip (5-case union nameof_probe through reflection::case_name / case_of_name, plus an unknown name -> None) LANDED in lib reflection.spi (closed green: document_test 22 passed, type_probe 12 typed tests; reflection.spi EA0F566D6A274B80; undo 20261103-080849; the first land attempt was undone for a missing final newline, landed from lib_roundtrip's canonical form). Static fold measured: reflection::case_name Gamma compiles to 534 bytes of Rust with no case literal. The typed extras (phantom name t, name styles, module::case) move to SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_1 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 1u32, "2026-11-01T14:38Z", "compiler", "R5 SPEC. DOD: a kit command (kit heal nameof, Spiral, not .ps1) that lists every match whose arms map N>=3 nullary cases to string literals equal (case-insensitively) to the case name, with repo/file/line and a count per repo; run once on spiral, kit, x, tibia, fiscal, dice, alphabet, recorded here; zero false positives on a hand-checked sample of 20. NEXT STEP: write the detector over the compiler tokens command output (lexemes), no regex over source text. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: a finding is a record { site : site; cases : list case_name; kind : HealKind } with HealKind = NameMapping | ReverseMapping | Partial, never a string kind.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_2 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 2u32, "2026-11-01T14:47Z", "compiler", "11-01 10:46 compiler, DESIGN FINDING from a first regex probe: exact equality (| Foo => \"Foo\") finds 0 arms in spiral, yet lib has the spam in other shapes: json_schema.spi:112 and :455 | JsonNull => \"null\" (type prefix stripped and lowercased, mapping written twice in one file), async.spi:411 | Error _ => \"error\" (payload ignored). So the detector must normalize the case name before comparing: strip the union-name prefix, case-fold, and accept snake/kebab joins, and count payload-ignoring arms (Case _) too. Duplicated mappings of one union across files are the strongest heal signal. The probe was a regex over text, a throwaway; the DOD detector stays token-based (kit heal nameof).")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_3 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 3u32, "2026-11-01T21:54Z", "x", "2026-11-01 17:54 x: x's AUDIT of its last day's diffs (user 17:4x). Multi-line host macros: 0. Case<->string mappings: 12 functions, triaged.\n- TRUE nameof case (1): Cells C4 draft daemon.spi request_line, where Hello/Status/Pool/Retire become \"hello\"/\"status\"/\"pool\"/\"retire\" (the lowercased case names). It switches to the derived printer when SPIRAL-NAMEOF ships. The draft is in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\CELLS-IN-SPIRAL-C4, not landed yet.\n- NEAR-name, a wire/log vocabulary (2): x sim_serve.spi:269 caller_word (AppBearer -> \"app\", ...) and sim_run.spi:180 status_word (Done -> \"ok\", ...). Both feed request-log/outcome rows that tests compare byte for byte. They become derivable only if the cases are renamed to their words, so it's a decision for the detector's rules.\n- WIRE ENCODINGS, not names (9): Cells cell.spi main_text (\"0\"/\"1\"/\"2\", read by cell.ex/notebook.ex), shown_of (\"1\"), run_output_text ('0\\n'/'1\\n' prefixes), directives.spi timeout_text (\"-\"), daemon.spi wait_text/wait_of (\"-1\"), retiring_text/retiring_of (\"false\"), free_text (\"-\"). Each mirrors an existing Elixir or daemon protocol, so a nameof printer can't produce them. They go away when the Elixir readers are ported (CELLS-IN-SPIRAL C5+), not through nameof.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_4 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 4u32, "2026-11-01T21:59Z", "compiler", "11-01 18:00 compiler: census done; numbers, method and heal order recorded on SPIRAL-NAMEOF n5 (one record per fact). Detector regex: to_name '\\|\\s*([A-Z]\\w*)\\s*(?:\\w+\\s*)?=>\\s*\"([\\w\\-]+)\"' and of_name '\\|\\s*\"([\\w\\-]+)\"\\s*=>\\s*(?:Some\\s+)?([A-Z]\\w*)', keeping only pairs equal after removing _ and - and lowercasing. About 208 + 8 arms in 47 files; kit holds 160.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_5 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 5u32, "2026-11-03T12:40Z", "compiler", "11-03 08:4x compiler: DETECTOR BUILT AND RUN. lib nameof_heal.spi (token-based, no regex over source): parses SpiralCompiler tokens rows (line, from, nearTo, class) into typed token records, groups them by line in one pass (join point over the token array, no per-line rescans), matches arm shapes on the token list (| Case => \"lit\", | Case _ => \"lit\", | \"lit\" => Case, | \"lit\" => Some Case; same-length shapes tried in order inside one case, after a first draft lost the OfName shapes to an earlier same-length pattern), compares case and literal after lowercasing and dropping _ and -, and reports runs of >=3 consecutive same-kind arms as finding records { kind : ToName | OfName; first_line; arms; cases : list string }. Node gate 1/1 on rust + gleam vs the box lib tree, round trip canonical. Landing queued (job compiler-lib-land-heal: nameof_heal.spi new + package.spiproj F2B334FD -> 8FB24F8A). CENSUS (git-tracked hand-written .spi of spiral, kit, x, tibia, fiscal, dice, alphabet; samples/state/deps skipped; 163 pre-filtered files, tokens via the installed compiler): 30 findings, 144 arms. kit 20 findings / 108 arms / 13 files (largest: kit_adoption_habits 17 arms, command_spec_domain and toolchain receipt 8 each, window_model 9), x 4 / 13, spiral 3 / 12 (cells daemon request_line, lib metrics suite_label + suite_of), dice 2 / 8 (menu_tabs twice), tibia 1 / 3, fiscal 0, alphabet 0. Kinds: ToName 28, OfName 2. Hand check of 22 first arms: 0 false positives (all case -> lower/upper/kebab name, some with a -- flag prefix). Not yet caught by design: prefix-stripped names (BackendC => \"c\", JsonNull => \"null\"); kit_style_probes is untracked so it was skipped (probe_word, 19 arms, will count once committed). Left for the DoD: the kit command wiring (kit heal nameof: list files, run tokens, call nameof_heal::findings), which is kit's to land; then rewrite sites to reflection::case_name.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_6 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 6u32, "2026-11-03T12:50Z", "compiler", "11-03 08:5x compiler: nameof_heal LANDED (closed green: document_test 22 passed, type_probe 1 typed test; nameof_heal.spi BC4D16D71E48923D, package.spiproj 8FB24F8AD13A2580; undo 20261103-083954). First rewrite done in my own lane: lib metrics suite_label = sm'::to_lower (reflection::case_name s) and suite_of = reflection::union_cases_find (suite_label s = name), replacing 2 hand maps of 4 arms each (node gate 14/14 rust + gleam; landing queued, job compiler-lib-land-metrics12). kit asked to wire kit heal nameof (its call); remaining sites per lane: kit 20, x 4, cells daemon 1, dice 2, tibia 1.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_7 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 7u32, "2026-11-04T04:16Z", "compiler", "11-04 00:1x compiler groom: stays Active (user 11-04 00:2x: Active = a note within 48 h). The lib side is landed (nameof_heal.spi, metrics rewrite). Next concrete step is kit's: wire kit heal nameof (list files, tokens, nameof_heal::findings). Then each lane rewrites its own sites (kit 20, x 4, cells daemon 1, dice 2, tibia 1).")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_8 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 8u32, "2026-11-04T04:35Z", "kit", "11-04 00:4x kit: `kit heal nameof <dir>...` wired, unstaged and not yet built: the new crate kit_heal_nameof (heal.spi). Typed verb union HealNameof, read back by reflection. It walks .spi files, skipping target/.git/.cache/node_modules/deps/_build, runs `dotnet <SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL or the deployed single-flight dll> tokens <file>` per file through lib process, and feeds lib nameof_heal.findings. Output: one `nameof <file>:<line> to-name|of-name arms=N cases=A,B,C` line per finding, then per root `files= unreadable= findings= arms=`, then `kit heal nameof ok roots= arms=`. It exits 0 (a census, not a gate). Type-checked on europa with pack31 (exit 0 in 6 s; an injected field error was rejected with ETY-RecordIndexFailed, exit 5). Registered as VerbHeal in direct_verbs with a help line, routed in kit_cli_model, link: in kit_cli_model and kit_cli, a Cargo dep, a workspace member and Cargo.lock. Next: rides TRAIN18, then the census on spiral, kit, x, tibia, fiscal, dice and alphabet gets recorded here. Cost note: one dotnet start per file; `tokens --stdin` batching is the follow-up if a root takes minutes.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_9 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 9u32, "2026-11-04T05:31Z", "kit", "11-04 01:3x kit: kit's own sites. A local census with compiler's to-name regex (suffix matches counted) found 82 arms in 17 places. First rewrites, unstaged; europa pack31 --check exit 0 as-is and test bodies:\n(1) kit_mirror drift_word = union_case_kebab \"\" drift. The case SameOnBoth -> Same, so \"same\" comes from the name; its 6 uses are in kit_mirror only, and the existing test pins \"same\".\n(2) kit_job_start_args start_flag_word = kit_flag_words.flag_word (union_case_suffix \"Start\" flag). All 9 cases prefixed Start*, with QuietStart -> StartQuiet and FrontStart -> StartFront, so --quiet and --front come from the names. New test start_flag_words_come_from_the_case_names pins all 9 words.\nSKIPPED (need a decision, not a mechanical rewrite): exec_metrics phase_word is snake_case (\"slot_wait\"), CBackend -> \"c\", machine-watch Healthy -> \"ok\" (an Ok case would clash with result), ci tools ToolRebar -> \"rebar3\" (spans 3 crates), payload cases (mirror state_word, task_query filters), and the GADT-indexed query_flag. Next batch after TRAIN19: field_rendering, todo content_label, kit_do_model query verbs, habits (17 arms).")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_10 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 10u32, "2026-11-04T05:44Z", "kit", "11-04 01:5x PARKED out of TRAIN19: kit_heal_nameof generated 2120 lines (arms_from_21 = 1111) because lib nameof_heal's arm matchers are all `:=` and inline into each of arms_from's two push_arm calls. Proposed to compiler: push_arm, arm_of, to_name_arm, of_name_arm and named become `:~` (behaviour-identical, each emitted once). The crate and wiring are in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL-parked-1104 (src + wired copies). They come back when the lib change lands. kit's own rewrites (kit_mirror drift_word, kit_job_start_args flags) stay in the tree; they don't depend on the heal crate.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_11 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 11u32, "2026-11-04T06:01Z", "compiler", "11-04 01:5x compiler: LIB FIX LANDED for kit's crate gate (kit 11-04: kit heal nameof stopped TRAIN18; heal.rs was 2120 lines, arms_from_21 alone 1111, because everything arms_from reaches was := and inlined). named, to_name_arm, of_name_arm, arm_of and push_arm became :~ (emitted once, called by name), behaviour-identical. Proof on box, installed pack33, a Rust consumer counting findings over the fixture: 1,620 -> 861 lines, arms_from 1,111 -> under 86 (largest now arm_of 111); both builds exit 2 under rustc -O. Lib land window closed green: 0 consumer-used signatures changed, apps/spiral compiles, document_test 22 passed, type_probe pass, 0 respell-drift. nameof_heal.spi BC4D16D7 -> 0CA4C9B0, lib digest 67ABD08F69EA1D44, undo 20261104-015609. kit un-parks its crate (drafts kit SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL-parked-1104) for TRAIN19.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_12 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 12u32, "2026-11-04T06:36Z", "kit", "11-04 02:2x kit: compiler landed the emit-once change (nameof_heal.spi 0CA4C9B0: named, to_name_arm, of_name_arm, arm_of and push_arm are :~; a findings consumer went 1620 -> 861 lines). kit now SPLITS the verb so lib's detector never shares a crate with the CLI. New linked crate kit_nameof_findings exports kit_nameof_finding_rows ((source, tokens) : string * string -> array_base finding_row {kind; first_line; arms; cases}): records in an array cross. kit_heal_nameof keeps the walk, the dotnet tokens calls and the printing, and links it. Both are back in the tree and wired again (VerbHeal, kit_cli/kit_cli_model link, workspace members, Cargo.lock). europa --check exit 0 for both, as-is and test bodies. Not in TRAIN19 (snapshot taken before the restore); rides TRAIN20 after a node size precheck.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_13 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 13u32, "2026-11-04T07:21Z", "kit", "11-04 03:2x kit batch 2 (unstaged; europa --check exit 0): (3) agile_todo_model content_label = union_case_kebab \"Content\" verdict; the cases are renamed ScanContent/SkipBinary/SkipLarge/SkipUnreadable -> ContentScan/ContentBinary/ContentLarge/ContentUnreadable across agile_todo_model, agile_todo_scan and agile_todo_merge; the existing test pins \"large\"/\"binary\". (4) agile_field_rendering edit_field_name = union_case_kebab \"Edit\" field; AppendTitle -> EditTitleAppend (local only), so \"title-append\" comes from the name; it stays inline `:=` because unknown_field_rule joins the words with union_cases_joined (StaticStringConcat needs static strings). NOTE: union_case_kebab/union_case_suffix strip the prefix by LENGTH without checking it, so every case of a union needs the same prefix before reflection replaces a mapping.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_14 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 14u32, "2026-11-04T11:20Z", "compiler", "11-04 07:2x compiler: FIX DRAFTED for kit's 03:2x NOTE (union_case_kebab/union_case_suffix strip the prefix by LENGTH without checking it). Draft %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL\\1-checked-case-prefix.kitdo, against kit/src/union_reflection/cases.spi at C8AB33236DB2DAB9. It adds 'prefixed_at name prefix', which returns the prefix length when the case name starts with it and otherwise raises !!!!ErrorType(\"the case <Name> does not start with the prefix <P>\") at compile time; both helpers call it. Proof (box, installed pack34, kit-shaped packages |core- + union_reflection, Zig): a union ContentScan/ContentBinary/ContentLarge gives union_case_suffix \"Content\" ContentBinary = \"Binary\" and union_case_kebab \"Content\" ContentScan = \"scan\", exit 0; generated main.zig is BYTE-IDENTICAL to the unchecked version (D36EFA080ECA9C73), so the check costs nothing at runtime. A SkipLarge case under prefix \"Content\" now fails the compile with 'TracedError: the case SkipLarge does not start with the prefix Content' instead of yielding \"arge\". CAUTION for kit: when a RUNTIME union value is passed, Unbox expands every case, so each existing call site whose union mixes prefixes now stops compiling; that is the bug surfacing, but kit should europa --check every union_reflection consumer before applying (kit owns the crate, so I did not edit it).")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_15 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 15u32, "2026-11-04T12:35Z", "kit", "11-04 08:3x kit: compiler's draft 1-checked-case-prefix VERIFIED and APPLIED. europa pack34 --check of every kit package that uses union_case_kebab/union_case_suffix (52, staged with their 98-package closure and the drafted cases.spi): 52/52 green, so no kit union mixes prefixes. Applied with `kit do src/union_reflection -` (cases.spi C8AB33236DB2DAB9 -> 126F3DAC902E80A8, unstaged); in TRAIN22.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_16 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 16u32, "2026-11-04T12:36Z", "compiler", "11-04 08:4x compiler (relaying kit's verdict): the checked-prefix draft passed pack34 --check on europa for all 52 kit packages that call union_case_kebab/suffix plus their 98-package closure, 0 failures, so no consumer mixes prefixes. kit APPLIED it to kit/src/union_reflection/cases.spi (C8AB33236DB2DAB9 -> 126F3DAC902E80A8, unstaged); it rides TRAIN22. A mismatched prefix is now a compile-time error ('the case X does not start with the prefix P').")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_17 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 17u32, "2026-11-04T19:57Z", "compiler", "11-04 16:0x compiler: spiral-side census rows re-checked against the tree. lib metrics suite_label/suite_of: HEALED (suite_label = sm'::to_lower (reflection::case_name s); suite_of = reflection::union_cases_find over suite_label). cells daemon request_line: NOT healable yet. request is GADT-indexed (Hello :: request hello_reply, ... Compile :: compile_ask -> request compile_reply), and case_name/union_cases_find over a GADT is the open 'GADT-indexed case table' slice of SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED; once that lands, the four nullary arms become one default arm over sm'::to_lower (reflection::case_name q), keeping Compile explicit for its fields (the daemon test pins 'compile\\\\trust\\\\t...'). The rest of the spiral rows (wait_text '-1', retiring_text 'false', free_text '-') are wire encodings, already listed as such. Kit's batches (habits, query verbs) are kit's to apply in its trains. No spiral rewrite is open until the GADT slice.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_18 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 18u32, "2026-11-05T06:42Z", "compiler", "11-05 02:3x compiler: cells daemon request_line HEALED (unstaged), the last spiral nameof-heal site from the 11-04 census. apps/cells/spi/daemon.spi: the four nullary arms (Hello => 'hello', Status, Pool, Retire) are one default arm over sm'::to_lower (reflection::case_name q); Compile keeps its explicit arm for its fields: 'tabbed (sm'::to_lower (reflection::case_name q) :: ask_fields a)'. Draft round-tripped canonical before the edit; live base unchanged since 11-02 (7 diff lines = the edit); undo copy kept (D843CD720633 -> 987D73D85ADA). Proof (box, installed pack40 with the op, daemon compiler): lib_gate -Lib apps/cells/spi -File daemon.spi 'tests: passed 6 failed 0 of 6', type errors 0, including the pinned request_line (Compile (sample_ask ())) = 'compile\\trust\\ta.spi\\ta.rs\\t900000\\t17\\t42'. Depends on reflection.spi's case_name over !!!!UnionCaseName (landed and green 11-05 01:1x/02:1x). The Elixir twin (lib/spiral/cells/compiler_client.ex request_line) is hand-written Elixir and out of this census.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_19 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 19u32, "2026-11-05T07:18Z", "compiler", "11-05 03:2x compiler: PERIODIC CENSUS (the item's DoD report), all repos, with compiler's to-name detector: arms '| Case [binder] => \"<case name>\"' whose literal is the case name exact, lower, kebab or snake, counted as a place when 2+ such arms sit within 3 lines; .cache/ and other hidden trees excluded (kit's .cache/cold-renewal copies alone gave 107 false places). RESULT: kit 0 places (fully healed since 11-04's 82 arms in 17 places); spiral 7 places / 26 arms = 6 contract-test fixtures (samples/contract_*: test text, kept as written) + 1 lib site doc_blocks.spi:50 level_tag (6 arms); i574n.github 4 / 19 (apps/graphs/agile.spi:60 8 arms, graph.spi:83/93/99 6+2+3); tibia 2 / 5 (apps/host/arena_host.spi:91, :105); x 2 / 5 (apps/client/posts.spi:217, :279); fiscal 1 / 2 (src/reports.spi:117). Healed tonight: cells daemon request_line (5 arms -> 2, green 6/6). Drafted + proven for its owner x: doc_blocks level_tag -> sm'::to_lower (reflection::case_name l) (kit drafts SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL\\doc_blocks, canonical; lib_gate on a lib copy 1/1 rust + gleam, 0 type errors); offered to x. The other repos' sites are their owners' (asks to follow with the next groom). Raw candidate list: compiler scratchpad nameof-census.txt (25964 candidate lines before filtering).")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_20 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 20u32, "2026-11-05T07:40Z", "compiler", "11-05 03:4x compiler: doc_blocks level_tag HEAL LANDED (x asked compiler to land it, after x's lib window). lib_land_window -BaseHash A7B00A03CE59 closed GREEN at 03:3x: consumers compile (apps/spiral), document_test 26 passed, type_probe PASS, 0 respell drift; live doc_blocks.spi = draft ECF33DAF4A7EC63B, lib digest CEF6365B3FB3F2F6, undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261105-033347 (unstaged). Behaviour proven before the land (lib copy gate 1/1 rust + gleam). With the cells daemon heal (02:3x), spiral's application code now has 0 to-name sites; the 6 contract fixtures stay as test text. Left, owned elsewhere: x posts.spi:217/279 (on x's list), tibia arena_host.spi:91/105, fiscal reports.spi:117, i574n.github apps/graphs (agile.spi:60, graph.spi:83/93/99). The node has pack41 (op present) since main's 03:10 ship, so owners can prove their heals there.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_21 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 21u32, "2026-11-05T12:03Z", "compiler", "11-05 08:0x compiler: DONE. DoD met: (1) token-based detector lib nameof_heal.spi (landed 11-03, emit-once fix 11-04) and kit's 'kit heal nameof' verb; (2) census on spiral, kit, x, tibia, fiscal, dice and alphabet recorded (n5 of SPIRAL-NAMEOF, 11-03 08:4x here, periodic rerun 11-05 03:2x); hand check of 22 first arms recorded; (3) every compiler- and spiral-owned site healed: lib metrics suite_label/suite_of, cells daemon request_line, lib doc_blocks level_tag; kit 0 places. The remaining sites are other lanes' own work in their trees (x posts.spi:217/279 on x's list, tibia's 1, i574n.github graphs agile.spi/graph.spi); the 6 spiral contract fixtures stay as test text. Periodic reruns go through 'kit heal nameof'.")
inl note_of_agile_concurrent_write_battletest_1 () = Note ("AGILE-CONCURRENT-WRITE-BATTLETEST", 1u32, "2026-11-01T14:39Z", "resilience", "2026-11-01 ~10:4x resilience (git-51), ROUND-5 (user: \"concurrent agile writes battle-tested\"). RESULT: PASS, no lost updates at process-level contention. Method: scratch backlog ($TEMP\\...\\scratchpad\\concwrite), real kit.exe processes fired via Start-Process (true OS concurrency, not threads).\nROUND A: 16 concurrent `agile note` on one task -> 16/16 exit 0, 16/16 distinct notes persisted. Since each note reports bytes_before/after (a WHOLE-FILE rewrite of agile.spi), 16 un-serialized rewrites would have clobbered down to 1-2 survivors; all 16 landing proves kit lock-serializes writes.\nROUND B (the real RMW test): 26 MIXED concurrent ops on overlapping targets -- 10 `note` (append) on one task + 8 `set <progress> <status>` + 8 `edit title` on 8 sibling tasks (set and edit hit the SAME tasks = read-modify-write contention). RESULT: 26/26 exit 0; all 26 notes persisted; 8/8 siblings set to Active AND 8/8 titles edited. BOTH mutation kinds survived on every task -- no last-writer-wins clobber.\nVERDICT: kit agile mutations are concurrency-safe under concurrent processes (a global lock serializes the whole-file rewrite; note/set/edit all survive). The memory agile-status-lost-updates risk is NOT at the process level.\nRESIDUAL (not a kit bug, a usage rule): a SESSION-level stale-read race remains possible -- an agent reads state, deliberates for minutes, then writes based on the stale snapshot. kit re-reads current state at each op's exec time, so this only bites if an agent caches state across a long gap. Guard = snapshot-before-bulk-groom (agile-edit-tags-replaces) and small, late mutations. Recommend keeping that memory but narrowing it to the stale-read case.")
inl note_of_migrate_tibia_tsv_1 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TIBIA-TSV", 1u32, "2026-11-01T14:45Z", "kit", "11-01 10:4x kit census (git ls-files): tibia 61 .tsv, 0 in other own repos. Runs as main-thread light work in the tibia lane plus kit jobs, no subagents (user round 5 item 8). DoD: 0 tracked .tsv in tibia; each former tsv has a .spi rows module with a round-trip test; PR-1 and PR-12 analyses give identical numbers before and after (tibia's acceptance). NEXT: install kit table to-spi (kit_table_rows node-proven 1/1), convert the 5 largest files first. TYPEFEATURES: one row union per table family, not list string.")
inl note_of_migrate_tibia_tsv_2 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TIBIA-TSV", 2u32, "2026-11-01T18:18Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 14:2x tibia: SCOPE EXTENDED by the junk census (TIBIA-HARVEST, same time): besides the 61 .tsv, the 4 results/*.txt (path-check-pc1/pc2, arena-spot-scan-r12, arena-region-r45) become typed rows, and the 4 analysis/*.ps1 become Spiral functions over the typed rows; the DoD's PR-1/PR-12 identical-numbers check runs those ports against the old scripts before the .ps1 and the text tables are archived (scratch-archive.ps1, never deleted). This item IS DATA-ROWS-TYPED part 3 (n9's arena_rows.spi GADT reader plan); work happens here. Merges with main's incoming Pages-HTML item: the HTML view is generated from the typed rows, so .tsv never comes back as the published form. Next step: unchanged, kit table to-spi on results/*.tsv when kit reports it installed.")
inl note_of_migrate_tibia_tsv_3 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TIBIA-TSV", 3u32, "2026-11-01T18:38Z", "main", "main 14:4x (user 11-01 14:0x: 'for ci-only results, tsvs need to be abandoned asap from all repos, change to something gh pages readable like maybe html itself, so it can be enriched indefinitely'). Per tibia's census (TIBIA-HARVEST n6), this item carries tibia's 61 .tsv, 4 results/*.txt and 4 analysis/*.ps1: typed Spiral rows first, an HTML view generated from them in CI, then the old files archived. The generic pieces are separate items: PAGES-FILE-VIEWERS, DIR-TREE-MARKDOWN-GFM, PAGES-NOTEBOOK-PUBLISH, DIR-TREE-LANE-METRICS. Other repos' CI-only .tsv follow this pattern under DATA-ROWS-TYPED.")
inl note_of_migrate_tibia_tsv_4 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TIBIA-TSV", 4u32, "2026-11-01T22:06Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 18:1x tibia: READER WRITTEN, unstaged in tibia/results (new package: package.spiproj + spiral.toml with lib; modules table_rows, arena_rows). DATA CENSUS (all 61 files): 4 shapes: 10 cols (1 file, 10 rows), 13 (2, 75), 15 (42, 990) = 1,075 arena rows; 5-col arm steps (16 files, 284 rows). No width mismatches. 398 rows have empty cells, all meaningful, so the reader types them: cleared_ms empty (174) = NotCleared; experience/lowest_health/actions_* empty together (12, nexbot check/diagnostic) = NoClientData; foreign_* empty (242) = NotRecorded (spiral rows record 0 0, so empty means not recorded, not 'not foreign'). TYPES (n9 plan, refined): phantom v10/v13/v15; ':| arena_row v = Base :: base_run -> arena_row v10 | WithEconomy :: base_run * economy -> arena_row v13 | WithForeign :: base_run * economy * foreign -> arena_row v15'; existential 'some_arena_row = \\? v. arena_row v'; closed competitor (8 cases) and monster (4) plus monster_spec = Lone | Mix (list (monster * i32)) for 'cyclops:1,troll:2'; row_rejection = WrongWidth | NotANumber column | UnknownCompetitor | UnknownMonster; decoding chains a 'decoded t = Decoded | Rejected' through 'then'. Names go through lib case_labels (case_of_label, derived from the union's case names; no hand-written string table, per user 17:4x), which is gating now. KIT SIDE (kit 17:4x): to-spi now emits 'rows ()' and takes '--open <module>'; tibia owns 'table_rows' (union table_row = Columns | Row), row_of_table adapts. Tests: 3 schema summaries, 2 rejections, the mixed camp (lua + rust); format clean, budget 0. Next: case_labels land, then a local run of results/, then to-spi over the 61 files with --open table_rows once kit's TRAIN8 installs, and the recount test.")
inl note_of_migrate_tibia_tsv_5 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TIBIA-TSV", 5u32, "2026-11-02T00:04Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 20:0x tibia: CITATION INVENTORY for the BENCHMARK.md rewrite (DoD item), done now so the rewrite is mechanical once to-spi installs. docs/BENCHMARK.md holds 42 citations of result files (38 distinct): 35 .tsv, 2 .txt, 5 analysis .ps1. One cited path never existed: results/arena-results-cyclops-pr3.tsv (L124, L126) is PR-3's PRE-REGISTERED output path, and the run happened as PR-3a (L138, arena-results-cyclops-pr3a.tsv). The rewrite keeps that citation as the plan's text and points nowhere new; no module is invented for a run that didn't happen. 30 of the 61 .tsv are cited by no doc (only by backlog notes): they still convert, and the recount test covers them. Rewrite rule: each results/<name>.tsv citation becomes results/<name>.spi, read through results/arena_rows.spi; the 5 analysis/*.ps1 citations become the Spiral function names once those ports exist.")
inl note_of_migrate_tibia_tsv_6 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TIBIA-TSV", 6u32, "2026-11-02T00:06Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 20:1x tibia: the 4 analysis/*.ps1 are LOG analyses, not .tsv readers. pc3-analysis.ps1 parses raw OTClient arena logs (knight hits 'due to your attack', 'step away from', 'You gained N experience points', each with @t+ms) into the 2000 ms swing-grid residual check of PC-3 (BENCHMARK L224, re-used for PR-12 at L511). Their documented inputs are gone: %USERPROFILE%\\tibia-local\\arena-logs holds 4 logs (three 10-14 runs plus one diagnose log), not PC-3's 5 or PR-12's 40, presumably lost in the 10-28 wipe. So 'identical numbers on the original inputs' is no longer checkable for these four. Their ports are pinned on synthetic fixtures plus a parity run against the .ps1 on the 4 remaining logs, and BENCHMARK keeps the published numbers as historical, citing the ported function. The PR-1/PR-12 .tsv analyses (kit experiment analyze) are unaffected; their inputs are the committed .tsv. Port home: apps/canary, beside lead_trace/ground_trace, which already parse these logs.")
inl note_of_migrate_tibia_tsv_7 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TIBIA-TSV", 7u32, "2026-11-02T00:24Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 20:2x tibia: analysis port 1 of 4 WRITTEN (unstaged): results/hit_grid.spi ports analysis/pc3-analysis.ps1. It has typed events (event_kind = Hit | Step | Kill with the @t+ms stamp), a grid record ({ grid_ms; tolerance_ms; think_ms }, pc3_grid () = 2000/60/1000 as in PC-3), a stable insertion sort by stamp (the script sorts), and a fold with the script's exact pairing rules: a kill between two hits drops the pair, a step sends it to the step buckets (on grid / inside think+tolerance / other), else plain (on / off grid); residual = gap mod grid. Test (lua + rust) on a synthetic 7-line log pins (1, 1, 0, 1, 0), hand-checked against the script's rules. Registered in results/package.spiproj and spiral.toml; format clean; budget 0 over (6 'mention' findings are the @t stamps, non-blocking). Next: a parity run against the .ps1 on the 4 surviving logs (needs a small file-reading entry), then the other 3 ports (pc4, pr12-secondary, pz-in-traces), then archive analysis/*.ps1. UPDATE 20:3x: the parity run is VACUOUS. pc3-analysis.ps1 over the 4 surviving logs prints all zeros, because those logs contain no hit/step/kill lines at all (counted per log: hit 0, step 0, kill 0). So the port's evidence is by construction: a second test (step on grid, step far off it) joins the first, and together they drive every branch of the script (plain on/off grid, step on grid / in window / other, kill exclusion). BENCHMARK's PC-3/PR-12 numbers stay as published history. No log-reading entry is needed for these ports until new arena logs exist.")
inl note_of_migrate_tibia_tsv_8 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TIBIA-TSV", 8u32, "2026-11-02T00:39Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 20:4x tibia: analysis port 2 of 4 WRITTEN (unstaged): results/walk_pace.spi ports analysis/pc4-analysis.ps1. It parses 'knight-straight step x,y,z -> x2,y2,z; interval after its KIND step N ms' lines into typed straight_step { direction = sign dx + 10 * sign dy; after_straight; interval }, keeps an interval only when the previous step was knight-straight in the same direction (else counts a turn; direction resets per log, as the script does), takes the median of the kept intervals, and maps it to a closed pace_verdict = FormulaSpeed | BaseSpeed | NeitherBand with PC-4's bands (486+60, 702+-30) as a record. The median is kept DOUBLED (an exact integer even when the script's even-count median is x.5) and compared to doubled bands. Test (lua + rust): straight, straight, turn -> 1 kept, 2 turns, FormulaSpeed. Format clean, budget 0 over. Parity run vacuous here too (no surviving logs hold these lines). Next: pr12-secondary and pz-in-traces, then archive analysis/*.ps1.")
inl note_of_migrate_tibia_tsv_9 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TIBIA-TSV", 9u32, "2026-11-02T01:01Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 21:0x tibia: analysis ports DECIDED for all 4. WRITTEN (unstaged, results/ package): hit_grid.spi (pc3-analysis), walk_pace.spi (pc4-analysis), secondary_hits.spi (pr12-secondary: per-run start marker, 10 s early/late hit split, floor-6 flag; the summary keeps exact integer sums plus run counts, so the script's 2-decimal mean rounding is derived, not stored). KEPT AS GLUE: pz-in-traces.ps1. Its counting already lives in a kit verb ('kit table sequences' with --count/--in-set over the protection-zone listing), and the script is ~30 lines of argument glue around one tool call, the junk census's glue class; it moves with live/ when PS1-TO-SPIRAL ports the runners. The 3 .ps1 with Spiral ports get archived after their ports are green in CI. A node test run of the whole results package (with the 'then' -> 'and_then' fix) is in flight.")
inl note_of_migrate_tibia_tsv_10 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TIBIA-TSV", 10u32, "2026-11-02T01:38Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 21:4x tibia: results/ package node runs. hit_grid 2/2, walk_pace 1/1, secondary_hits 1/1, table_rows 1/1 PASS (job-1793582213350). arena_rows needed two fixes found by the node: (1) the existential 'some_arena_row = \\? v. arena_row v' can't be built at runtime ('Cannot dyn an existential into a runtime var'; existentials are compile-time only), so it's now a runtime union 'AtV10 (arena_row v10) | AtV13 (arena_row v13) | AtV15 (arena_row v15)'; the version-indexed GADT stays, and code holding an arena_row v15 still reads foreign without an option; (2) on Lua, the generated decoder hit Lua's limit of 60 upvalues per function ('function at line 503 has more than 60 upvalues', from the chained partial applications in base_of), so arena_rows' tests are pinned to rust: it's a host-side analysis that never runs inside the Lua client. Rust re-run in flight (job tibia-arena-rows-4). A backend note for the compiler lane: deep and_then chains can exceed Lua 5.1's 60-upvalue cap; a codegen that lifts captured cells into a table would avoid it.")
inl note_of_migrate_tibia_tsv_11 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TIBIA-TSV", 11u32, "2026-11-02T01:48Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 21:4x tibia: results/ package ALL GREEN on the node. arena_rows 4/4 on rust (job-1793583861151, build exit 0), after the runtime-union fix and one fixture fix: the mixed-camp line had experience=90 with the other four client columns empty, a partial client block the decoder correctly rejects (the census's 12 real no-client rows have all five empty), so the fixture now matches the data. With hit_grid 2/2, walk_pace 1/1, secondary_hits 1/1 and table_rows 1/1 earlier. Unstaged. Next: to-spi over the 61 .tsv with --open table_rows once TRAIN8 installs, then the recount test.")
inl note_of_migrate_tibia_tsv_12 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TIBIA-TSV", 12u32, "2026-11-02T02:59Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 23:0x tibia: CONVERSION DONE, verified (unstaged, untracked): kit table to-spi (kit.exe 7C559D83) ran over all 61 results/*.tsv with --open table_rows into results/rows/<name with _ for ->.spi. Per file, kit's rows= and columns= equal the .tsv's data lines and header width: 61 of 61, 0 mismatches, 1,359 rows total = the census's 1,075 arena + 284 arm-step rows. CONTENT CHECK: every generated Row [ ... ] literal, unescaped and tab-joined, equals its .tsv line byte for byte: 1,359 compared, 0 differing (empty cells kept as \\\"\\\"). Placement: results/rows/, a subfolder, because generated lines exceed the cell budget and build.ps1 lists results/*.spi non-recursively (budget and tests skip rows/); the modules are NOT yet registered in results/package.spiproj, so no build compiles them until the next step proves them. NEXT (one step, node-proven before it lands in the package): add a 'rows/' folder block to results/package.spiproj and spiral.toml, a recount test in arena_rows (decoded rows per module = the counts above, 0 rejections, via row_of_table over each module's rows ()), then the BENCHMARK citation rewrite (inventory n5) and archive of the .tsv.")
inl note_of_migrate_tibia_tsv_13 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TIBIA-TSV", 13u32, "2026-11-02T14:26Z", "tibia", "11-02 tibia, step 2 (unstaged). results/package.spiproj and spiral.toml now register a rows/ folder block (61 modules, after table_rows) and a new module results/row_census.spi. Census: the 284 arm-step rows over 16 tables decode with 0 rejections (green on the node, job tibia-row-census-2). The 1,075 arena rows over 45 tables cannot compile as one Rust test: each row is a 15-string list literal, rustc peaked at 10.4 GB with 0.1 GB left free on the node, and the cell timed out at 300 s even after the decoders became join points. That half is parked at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\tibia\\MIGRATE-TIBIA-TSV\\row_census.full.spi (sha D77BCDD575CA). It returns once kit table to-spi can emit one string literal per row (requested from kit 11-02), plus a Line case in table_rows. arena_rows stays green 4/4 with rows/ registered. Next: re-emit rows/ in the compact form, restore the arena census, then the BENCHMARK citation rewrite and the .tsv archive.")
inl note_of_migrate_tibia_tsv_14 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TIBIA-TSV", 14u32, "2026-11-02T14:33Z", "tibia", "11-02 tibia: the format question with kit is settled. kit declined per-row joined strings (EncodedRow drift, banned by AGENTS.md) and suggested reading the TSV at test time. tibia declined that, since this item archives the .tsv files out of the repo. Asked instead for kit's typed whole-table literal (one string per table, decoded once at runtime, counted by kit's census). Plan: regenerate all 61 tables in that form, replacing the per-row Row lists, and restore the arena census from the draft. Fallback if kit declines: per-table census tests (CPU-heavy).")
inl note_of_migrate_tibia_tsv_15 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TIBIA-TSV", 15u32, "2026-11-02T15:48Z", "tibia", "11-02 tibia: results/*.txt decided by a rule fixed before looking (a file only cited by docs becomes an .md evidence page; a file a tool reads moves to its real format together with its reader). Done now, unstaged: results/path-check-pc1.txt and results/path-check-pc2.txt are DELETED, replaced by results/path-check-pc1.md and path-check-pc2.md (a heading plus the verbatim log in a text fence, body byte-identical, 76 and 48 lines), and docs/BENCHMARK.md:153 and :203 now cite the .md files. Kept for now: results/arena-region-r45.txt and results/arena-spot-scan-r12.txt, because apps/map/run.ps1:39-49 reads and rewrites them (map golden and live-scan agreement); they move with that logic in TIBIA-MAP-GRIDS-TYPED. ALSO: kit implemented to-spi --whole (one Table string per table, ships in TRAIN12; node candidate at C:\\home\\remote\\kit-verify\\kit\\src\\target\\debug\\kit.exe). Next: add | Table :: string -> table_row to results/table_rows.spi, regenerate the 61 tables with --whole, restore the arena census from the draft.")
inl note_of_migrate_tibia_tsv_16 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TIBIA-TSV", 16u32, "2026-11-02T16:40Z", "tibia", "11-02 tibia, step 3 (unstaged). All 61 tables were regenerated with kit table to-spi --whole --open table_rows (the node candidate kit, TRAIN12 pending); each round-trips byte-identical to its .tsv (61/61, checked locally). results/table_rows.spi is now one case, Table : string, with text_of and a typed fold_data that skips the header and blank lines, plus a test. The unused Row/Columns cases, line_of and arena_rows.row_of_table are removed. results/row_census.spi folds every table through arena_rows.row_of_line / arm_step_of_line. Node proof (job tibia-census-whole): row_census 2/2, all 1,075 arena rows and 284 arm-step rows decode with 0 rejections, in 45 s (was a 10 GB rustc and a timeout); table_rows 1/1; arena_rows 4/4. The .tsv files are NOT deleted yet: live/run-arena.ps1 and live/block.ps1 still write them, and scripts/score.ps1:39 and live/arena-summary.ps1 read them. Asked kit (11-02) for kit table query/logs/append to read and write whole-table .spi, so the live harness writes results/rows/*.spi directly. Then: retarget the 4 scripts and BENCHMARK's 53 citations, delete the 61 .tsv files (deletion rule: unstaged, paths listed), and the item is done.")
inl note_of_migrate_tibia_tsv_17 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TIBIA-TSV", 17u32, "2026-11-02T19:43Z", "tibia", "11-02 tibia: kit's .spi table I/O is done and proven (europa candidate), and it ships in TRAIN13. The format is chosen by extension: kit table query/diff read .spi; kit table logs --out x.spi writes one Table literal with open table_rows; and the new kit table append <x.spi> <cells...> | --row-tsv appends one row atomically (via .pending plus a rename), refusing width mismatches and tab/newline cells. PLAN once TRAIN13 is installed (not before, or the scripts break against the current kit): live/run-arena.ps1 appends to results/rows/<name>.spi; live/block.ps1 runs table logs --out results/rows/<name>_secondary.spi; live/arena-summary.ps1 and scripts/score.ps1:39 query the .spi; then BENCHMARK.md's 53 citations move to results/rows/*.spi and the 61 .tsv files are deleted (unstaged, paths listed); publish.ps1 drops *.tsv from -Include.")
inl note_of_migrate_tibia_tsv_18 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TIBIA-TSV", 18u32, "2026-11-03T03:53Z", "tibia", "11-02 23:5x tibia, MIGRATION DONE in the tree (unstaged), right after kit's TRAIN13c install (AF229BEC). Readers/writers retargeted through new helpers in live/paths.ps1 ($TibiaKit, Read-ResultRows = kit table query --cols --quiet parsed as TSV, New-ResultTable = header-only table via kit table to-spi --whole --open table_rows, Add-ResultRow = kit table append --row-tsv, atomic and width-checked): live/run-arena.ps1 (new tables and rows are whole-table .spi), live/block.ps1 (reads rows through Read-ResultRows; secondary table <name>_secondary.spi beside it via kit table logs --out), live/arena-summary.ps1 (default results/rows/arena_results_cyclops.spi), scripts/score.ps1 (Get-RetreatLogs reads rows/arena_results_cyclops_pr12/pr16.spi), scripts/publish.ps1 (*.tsv dropped from -Include), README's example -Out path, and docs/BENCHMARK.md (all 47 arena-results citations plus the -cyclops-*/-hunter-* shorthands now cite results/rows/arena_results_*.spi; only target/ scratch tables keep .tsv; the one cited module that does not exist, arena_results_cyclops_pr3, is PR-3's registered output path that was never run, pr3a ran). PROOFS (local, installed kit): kit table query on arena_results_cyclops_pc10 prints identical output from .tsv and .spi; experiment analyze PR-1 reports identical row counts from both (spiral-retreat 31/60, vbot 30/60, interim refusal) and PR-12 refuses identically (verdict exists, one analysis per registration, so no ledger write was forced); score.ps1's inputs pr12/pr16 give identical spiral-retreat rows (40, 20); a scratch New-ResultTable + 2 Add-ResultRow + Read-ResultRows round trip works and matches the existing module format. DELETED from the worktree, unstaged: all 61 results/*.tsv (no reference left in tibia or any sibling repo outside backlog history; content in git and in the round-trip-verified rows/*.spi modules). Left: a live block run (box, live world) to exercise run-arena/block end to end; new live tables also need a rows/ manifest entry to join row_census.")
inl note_of_migrate_tibia_tsv_19 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TIBIA-TSV", 19u32, "2026-11-03T10:26Z", "tibia", "11-03 06:2x tibia, LIVE BLOCK ATTEMPT BLOCKED BY MEMORY, not code: a one-hunt smoke block (live/block.ps1 -Results rows/arena_results_smoke_1103.spi -Runs 1 -Competitors spiral-policy -Monster troll, 30-min window, StartBy +15 min) asked kit for a live-gui window, and kit refused it for 14 min: 'reason=low-memory free_mb=2394..2483 need_mb=4096'; the block exited cleanly with no table written. Box: 15.9 GB total, 2.6 GB free; the largest holders are 8 Claude lane sessions (about 4.1 GB together) plus browsers, none tibia's to stop. kit window run takes --min-free-mb, but DECIDED not to lower it: the live world's footprint (MariaDB + Canary + one OTClient) is unmeasured, and running with about 1 GB left risks the low-RAM state that has killed lane sessions (main-crash-transcript-size). NEXT: retry when free memory is >= 4 GB (fewer sessions open), or measure the world's peak RSS on the node first and request a window sized from that. This live run is the last step for both MIGRATE-TIBIA-TSV (run-arena writing typed .spi rows end to end) and TIBIA-MAP-GRIDS-TYPED.")
inl note_of_migrate_tibia_tsv_20 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TIBIA-TSV", 20u32, "2026-11-04T04:17Z", "tibia", "11-04 00:17 tibia GROOM: parked to Planned (no note in 12 h). The migration is done in the tree. NEXT: one-hunt smoke block (live/block.ps1 -Runs 1 -Monster troll) once kit grants a live-gui window (needs 4096 MB free; refused 11-03 at about 2.4 GB).")
inl note_of_migrate_tibia_tsv_21 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TIBIA-TSV", 21u32, "2026-11-04T04:21Z", "tibia", "11-04 00:21 tibia: back to Active, percent kept. User 11-04 00:2x moved the stale-Active window from 12 h to 48 h, and this item has a note within 48 h, so this morning's parking (12 h rule) is undone. The next step in the 00:2x note still holds.")
inl note_of_migrate_tibia_tsv_22 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TIBIA-TSV", 22u32, "2026-11-04T07:35Z", "tibia", "11-04 03:3x tibia: DONE, LIVE SMOKE PASSED. The box had about 5.1 GB free, so kit granted the live-gui window at once (win-...-1504, 30 min). live/block.ps1 -Results rows/arena_results_smoke_1104.spi -Runs 1 -Competitors spiral-policy -Monster troll ran one live hunt against the Canary world: row 2026-11-04T03:34:29 spiral-policy run 1 troll, count 3, experience 90, cleared_ms 121543, lowest_health 181, deaths 0. It was written through kit's .spi table I/O (New-ResultTable as a header-only open table_rows Table literal, then Add-ResultRow = kit table append --row-tsv, atomic and width-checked), and kit table query reads it back with the right columns. The secondary path also ran on .spi: kit table logs wrote arena_results_smoke_1104_secondary.spi (1 log, arm spiral-policy) and kit table query grouped it. Boosted creature was Defiler, not a spawned kind, so the run is comparable. So the migrated readers and writers work live end to end, not only in node regression suites. tibia has no tracked .tsv left (part 3 of DATA-ROWS-TYPED, now Done). The two smoke tables stay unstaged in tibia/results/rows.")
inl note_of_migrate_txt_files_1 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TXT-FILES", 1u32, "2026-11-01T14:45Z", "kit", "11-01 10:4x kit census (git ls-files). fiscal's src/corpus.txt is already tracked in FISCAL-CORPUS-LIST-ON-DEMAND (90%), so fiscal is done when that lands. DoD: each listed file has a decision (typed module | derived | allowlisted license/upstream text) recorded here; NoUntypedRows refuses new ones. NEXT: list the 17 paths with their first line, decide each (CPU-light).")
inl note_of_migrate_txt_files_2 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TXT-FILES", 2u32, "2026-11-03T08:58Z", "main", "main 11-03 04:3x SCOPE: polyglot's 1 tracked .txt drops out, since polyglot left the org 11-03 and is absorbed, not maintained (POLYGLOT-RETIRE). Remaining: spiral 10, tibia 4, fiscal 1, x 1.")
inl note_of_migrate_txt_files_3 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TXT-FILES", 3u32, "2026-11-04T22:18Z", "kit", "11-04 18:3x kit: CENSUS RE-RUN + DECISIONS (git ls-files *.txt): kit 0, i574n.github 0, tibia 0, fiscal 0 (corpus.txt gone), polyglot out of scope; 7 remain. DECIDED: (1) spiral/apps/zed/tree-sitter-spiral/test/corpus/{definitions,symbols,test_headers,test_symbol}.txt -> ALLOWLIST: tree-sitter's test runner requires its corpus as .txt under test/corpus (tool format, not our rows). (2) spiral/requirements.txt (mpmath) -> ALLOWLIST: pip's fixed manifest name. (3) spiral/apps/cells/data/tlds.txt and x/postability/tlds.txt -> byte-identical 7516 B IANA TLD lists (upstream data): ALLOWLIST one copy as upstream text with its source and date in the allowlist reason, and x reads it from the spiral copy (or both derive it from the IANA list on demand) so the duplicate goes. NEXT: write the 3 allowlist entries where NoUntypedRows reads them (owner of the census probe), and hand the tlds dedupe to x (their repo).")
inl note_of_migrate_txt_files_4 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TXT-FILES", 4u32, "2026-11-04T22:20Z", "kit", "11-04 18:4x kit: found that the NoUntypedRows refusal this item's DoD leans on is NOT implemented anywhere (the name appears only in backlog notes; no .spi in kit, spiral or lib defines it), so there is no allowlist file to write the 3 decisions into yet. They stay recorded here (tree-sitter corpus x4, pip requirements.txt, one IANA tlds.txt with source + date) for whoever builds the probe. What is DONE for this item: every tracked .txt in the org has a decision; kit, i574n.github, tibia and fiscal track none. LEFT: the probe itself (or fold it into the census as a \"tracked-txt\" count with these exemptions) and x's tlds dedupe.")
inl note_of_migrate_txt_files_5 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TXT-FILES", 5u32, "2026-11-04T22:25Z", "x", "2026-11-04 18:25 x: x's SHARE PLANNED and drafted (rides x-next7, which follows x-next6d): x/postability/tlds.txt is byte-identical (cmp) to spiral/apps/cells/data/tlds.txt. Readers in x: (1) apps/client/tlds.spi's parity test now reads ../../../spiral/apps/cells/data/tlds.txt (x builds with spiral cloned beside it, scripts/common.ps1 SpiralRoot; node mirrors use the same sibling layout) and is renamed the_list_matches_cells_data_tlds_txt (draft 16879E85697F); (2) postability/x.json top_level_domains_file -> ../../spiral/apps/cells/data/tlds.txt (no code reads that key today; CD95B0C1D176 -> CCD8A70C597E); (3) scripts/gate.ps1 drops it from dataFiles (6487C87D09A5 -> BFAFFC5C7967); (4) apps/client/README.md names the shared IANA copy (9FB6AD176816 -> F6BA371E172E). land-x-next7 deletes x/postability/tlds.txt only if still byte-identical to the spiral copy. No other repo reads x's copy (grep over x, spiral/apps, i574n.github/scripts, kit/src).")
inl note_of_migrate_txt_files_6 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TXT-FILES", 6u32, "2026-11-04T23:16Z", "kit", "11-04 19:2x kit: the PROBE is written and parked as a known-good draft in the kit store (%LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\MIGRATE-TXT-FILES-tracked-text\\kit_tracked_text, linked-crate shape): `standards --tracked-text <repo>...` runs `git -C <repo> ls-files *.txt`, exempts only this item's decisions through a typed text_allowance (ToolCorpus = tree-sitter test/corpus, ToolManifest = requirements.txt, UpstreamData = spiral apps/cells/data/tlds.txt), prints each other path and \"kit standards tracked-text ok repos=N untyped=M\", exit 1 when M > 0. Test: x's postability/tlds.txt duplicate is NOT allowed, CRLF and blank rows ignored. europa --check ok with bodies. WHY PARKED, not routed: the natural route is a FlagTrackedText case in kit_style_census, but that package already fails its own typed-density ratchet (forall 1/227 at baseline -> 1/335 now; its only \"forall\" is a fixture string), so the style hook refuses ANY edit there, and \"baselines only shrink\" forbids re-recording. NEXT: either add real typefeatureset use to kit_style_census (restoring the ratchet) and route it, or give it its own verb.")
inl note_of_migrate_txt_files_7 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TXT-FILES", 7u32, "2026-11-04T23:36Z", "kit", "11-04 19:4x kit: the probe is ROUTED after all, not through kit standards (blocked by kit_style_census's own ratchet) but as `kit lint tracked-text <repo>...`: LintTrackedText case in kit_lint_cli (precheck's shape: rest -> array_base string), kit_tracked_text restored from the draft store as a linked crate (output lines now \"kit lint tracked-text ...\"), workspace member + lock (cargo metadata --offline --locked exit 0). europa --check ok with bodies on text.spi and cli.spi. Size + notebooks pending (kit-size-hookverbs / kit-hookverbs-tests). After install: `kit lint tracked-text C:\\home\\git\\spiral C:\\home\\git\\x` should list only x's postability/tlds.txt until x-next7 lands.")
inl note_of_migrate_txt_files_8 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TXT-FILES", 8u32, "2026-11-04T23:37Z", "kit", "11-04 19:4x kit: usage gap, deliberately NOT fixed tonight: command_spec_domain/direct_verbs.spi VerbLint usage names only `lint macros` and `lint shadows` (already missing growth and precheck, now tracked-text too). That domain feeds kit_cli, last measured at 995 generated lines, so adding usage text needs a size run on kit_cli first. Do it with the next size batch.")
inl note_of_migrate_txt_files_9 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TXT-FILES", 9u32, "2026-11-04T23:45Z", "kit", "11-04 19:4x kit: `kit lint tracked-text` GREEN: node size kit_lint_cli 226, kit_tracked_text 469; box notebooks cli 1/1, text 1/1. Rides TRAIN27. The VerbLint usage text stays as is (command_spec_domain is below its typed-density baseline, so the style hook refuses edits; see TYPEFEATURESET-ENFORCEMENT n44).")
inl note_of_migrate_txt_files_10 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TXT-FILES", 10u32, "2026-11-05T20:22Z", "main", "main 11-05 16:2x CLOSE: DoD met. Box recount (git index, 11 repos: spiral, kit, x, fiscal, tibia, regex, html, dice, alphabet, i574n.github, blog): tracked .txt = 0 apart from the reasoned allowlist (tree-sitter test/corpus = tool-mandated; spiral cells/data/tlds.txt and x postability/tlds.txt = external IANA data read by name; LICENSE/requirements), 0 new untracked .txt, 0 tracked-but-ignored (TSV-TXT-GITIGNORE-HEAL n6). polyglot's 1 goes with POLYGLOT-RETIRE. The Write hook now advises on any new .txt in a repo. kit's 'lint tracked-text' (n of 11-04 19:4x) is NOT in the installed kit yet: 'kit lint tracked-text <root>' falls through to 'lint macros' (usage lists only macros), so the CI-side ratchet waits for kit's install and is tracked on TSV-TXT-GITIGNORE-HEAL.")
inl note_of_migrate_spiral_py_classify_1 () = Note ("MIGRATE-SPIRAL-PY-CLASSIFY", 1u32, "2026-11-01T14:45Z", "kit", "11-01 10:4x kit census (git ls-files): spiral 907 .py, dice 2, polyglot 3, every other own repo 0. Most are likely backend samples/generated oracles (Python is a Spiral target), which are legitimate outputs, not tools. DoD: a typed census row per directory (class union Sample|Oracle|Script|Vendored, count); Script-class files get one port item each under PS1-TO-SPIRAL rules; Sample/Oracle classes allowlisted in KIT-STANDARDS-ECOSYSTEM NoUntypedRows. NEXT: group by top directory (git ls-files | split path), CPU-light. TYPEFEATURES: py_class union.")
inl note_of_migrate_spiral_py_classify_2 () = Note ("MIGRATE-SPIRAL-PY-CLASSIFY", 2u32, "2026-11-01T14:54Z", "kit", "11-01 11:0x kit: SHRUNK per main (classification already done in compiler round 2 and PS1-TO-SPIRAL n24), verified against git ls-files: 907 total, 902 under apps/compiler/tmp/samples (generated outputs, keep, allowlisted for NoUntypedRows). DECISION PER FILE: (1) apps/compiler/runtime/corelib.py (46 lines, static_array etc.): KEEP, it is the Python backend's runtime emitted beside outputs, part of the target, not a tool. (2) apps/compiler/tmp/tests/native-shims/run_main.py (25): KEEP, it loads a generated main.py and calls main() for the Python native tier, which has to run in Python; allowlist with that reason. (3) apps/compiler/tmp/tests/native-shims/cpp_native.py (64): PORT, it is a process-spawn wrapper (compile main.cpp/main.cu to an exe) and becomes a Spiral step in the native-probe runner over workspace primitives (spawn + exit code); drop the .py once test.ps1 -Native Cpp rows pass through it. (4) apps/compiler/tmp/tests/native-shims/openqasm-run/run.py (1,502): PORT, a classical OpenQASM simulator is a strong typed-Spiral program (gate/instruction union, width-indexed integers with wrap semantics as phantom widths); scheduled under OPENQASM3-BACKEND, D5, since it is the oracle of that backend's matrix rows and must agree row for row before the .py goes. (5) apps/spiral/test_json_protocol.py (108): PORT, the CLI JSON-protocol test becomes a Spiral test block that spawns the rebuilt CLI; the child-Python-process clients stay only if the protocol's Python client is itself under test (check the spiral CLI caller first). DoD: 2 allowlist rows with reasons, 3 port items (cpp_native, openqasm-run under OPENQASM3-BACKEND, json-protocol test), each closes when its .py is archived via scratch-archive.ps1 with the replacement green. NEXT: file the 3 port items (CPU-light).")
inl note_of_migrate_spiral_py_classify_3 () = Note ("MIGRATE-SPIRAL-PY-CLASSIFY", 3u32, "2026-11-01T19:26Z", "main", "main 15:3x CLOSED, every one of the 5 hand-written .py decided (compiler 11-01 14:3x, PS1-TO-SPIRAL n49; main for the fifth): (1) apps/compiler/runtime/corelib.py KEEP: the Python backend's codegen runtime, read by spiral_compiler.fs:27858 and copied into every Python output, so it is part of the target. (2) apps/compiler/tmp/tests/native-shims/run_main.py DROPPED: inlined as python -c in test.ps1/bench-native.ps1, identical stdout and exit on 11/11 samples. (3) native-shims/cpp_native.py DROPPED: test.ps1's Cpp arm calls g++/clang++ directly; the C++ old-vs-new proof was waiting for the kit-TRAIN7c window (compiler archives both .py after it). (4) openqasm-run/run.py PORT: OPENQASM-SIM-SPIRAL (P2). (5) apps/spiral/test_json_protocol.py PORT: moved to the kit drafts store with its own item (main's call: it checks the CLI's SPIRAL_JSON envelope at every trace level). The other 902 are generated Python-backend sample outputs under apps/compiler/tmp/samples, kept and allowlisted as Sample class.")
inl note_of_zig_expected_semicolon_regression_1 () = Note ("ZIG-EXPECTED-SEMICOLON-REGRESSION", 1u32, "2026-11-01T14:47Z", "compiler", "11-01 10:48 compiler, reported by tibia. DOD: tibia scripts/build.ps1 -Files ground_trace compiles and runs on Zig with the installed core, and a minimal regression sample (one per bug) reproduces main.zig:160 shape on the matrix with ///> zig and passes; the culprit pack edit is named by bisecting the PACK-12, 13, 14 programs on scratch cores. NEXT STEP: on the box (window check first), compile ground_trace to Zig with installed pack14a, read main.zig:150-165 and zig ast-check it; if the line is a statement emitted by the PACK-12 mutual-tail loop or group-loop code (Rust-only appliers, but shared helpers), compare against a PACK-11-era core. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: Zig statement emission typed as a union ZigStmt = Expr of expr | Decl of decl | Block of list ZigStmt, with the printer adding the terminator per case, so no call site concatenates ; by hand.")
inl note_of_zig_expected_semicolon_regression_2 () = Note ("ZIG-EXPECTED-SEMICOLON-REGRESSION", 2u32, "2026-11-01T15:04Z", "compiler", "11-01 11:04 compiler, BISECT 1: (a) the main.zig:160 text is const v4: any = (v3):getPosition(); a Lua-only macro (canary.spi:24 creature_position) reached through ground_trace's unpinned := main, which Cells builds on the default target Zig. The box gives that SAME Zig error with pack11 (pre-window), pack12b, pack13a and pack14a, and still passes 2/2 tests on every one, so this zig message is old and not the regression. (b) The CI diff is elsewhere: in red run 41314129444 combat_text is 0/5 executed, 5 unsupported and game_calls 0/3, 3 unsupported, on BOTH OS jobs; green 41281548884 had 5/5 and 3/3. combat_text's tests are pinned ///> lua, not default Zig, and lua5.1 installs identically in both runs, so this is a Lua-cell unsupported verdict, not Zig. (c) Range: spiral e0461f15 (06:36Z) to 7a4c960e (13:48Z); in it, Cells changed only cell_budget's walk, SPIRAL_SERVER_PARENT_PID and the gleam maths dep; lib changed convert.spi and json_schema.spi; plus PACK-12/13/14 in the compiler. NEXT: combat_text on the box with pack14a vs pack11 (running) to see whether the unsupported verdict reproduces and which arm flips.")
inl note_of_zig_expected_semicolon_regression_3 () = Note ("ZIG-EXPECTED-SEMICOLON-REGRESSION", 3u32, "2026-11-01T15:17Z", "compiler", "11-01 11:17 compiler, ROOT CAUSE: tibia's CI builds the spiral CLI from deps/spiral (apps/spiral/build.ps1:27 RUST-FAILED) and it fails: TracedError Cannot convert i64 to the following type: time_span, at convert.spi:75 (numeric_conv's conv) from try_convert's Zig arm :346, which CONVERT-ZIG-UNATIVEINT (main, landed 08:42, convert 36C910747663) changed from a retag (x |> to) to x |> numeric_conv. numeric_conv tests only the SOURCE type for numeric, so a nominal target like date_time's time_span (i64 on Zig) hits conv. With no spiral tool, Cells returns :tool_missing -> unsupported (notebook.ex:1150) for every cell that needs it. The box hid it because workspace/target/release/spiral.exe was built before the land. REPRO: dotnet SpiralCompiler.dll --backend Rust spiral.spi on the live tree: exit 5, the same TracedError. FIX (program scratchpad zigsemi/convert-numeric-target.kitdo, 1 replacement): numeric_conv's condition also requires the target u to be a numeric prim, else the old retag; 36C9107476637EBF -> 9035FB80D406E22D, byte-identical to the formatter's own layout (canonical). The fixed scratch lib compiles the CLI (exit 0, 1,476,452 B .rs). Lib tests (convert.spi, date_time.spi) on the scratch lib are running; land through land-lib-program when green. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: replace the two copy-pasted typecases with a type-level numeric class (a {number} constraint check at the type level, or a prototype numeric_prim t) so conv is only reachable when both sides carry the constraint; a target that is not numeric is a separate Retag path, not a fallthrough.")
inl note_of_zig_expected_semicolon_regression_4 () = Note ("ZIG-EXPECTED-SEMICOLON-REGRESSION", 4u32, "2026-11-01T15:29Z", "compiler", "11-01 11:29 compiler, PROOF on the scratch lib (pack14a = installed core DBC5EC18F14C354C): apps/spiral --backend Rust exit 0 (live lib: exit 5); convert.spi 4/4 (includes main's zig+rust unativeint round trip), 0 type errors; date_time.spi 43 passed 0 failed of 44, 0 type errors; the box BASE arm on the live lib is running to account for the 44th row before landing. GATE GAP CLOSED (main's ask): a consumer signature row could not have caught this, because try_convert's signature never changed; the break only shows when a consumer specializes it (i64 -> time_span). So lib_land_window.ps1 gains a close step '=== consumers': -Consumer (default apps/spiral/spiral.spi) is compiled --backend Rust with the installed compiler against the just-copied lib, output to spiral-bin/mix-builds/lib-land-consumers; a nonzero exit fails the close and undoes the land, like the other checks. It parses clean, and this convert fix will be its first land.")
inl note_of_zig_expected_semicolon_regression_5 () = Note ("ZIG-EXPECTED-SEMICOLON-REGRESSION", 5u32, "2026-11-01T15:35Z", "compiler", "11-01 11:35 compiler, LANDED and closed green via lib_land_window (window win-1793547273785, label compiler-convert-numeric-target): convert.spi 36C9107476637EBF -> 9035FB80D406E22D, unstaged. Close: 14 signatures unchanged; NEW consumers step: apps/spiral/spiral.spi compiles; document_test 22 passed; type_probe PASS (4 tests typed, control ok). Undo: spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261101-113433. BASE vs EDIT on the box (installed core): date_time.spi base 10 passed 33 failed of 44, edit 43 passed 0 failed of 44, so the same bug was also breaking 33 date_time tests (time_span paths on rust/zig/fsharp/lua/cuda), and the node control arm's 10/33 date_time row was this bug, not load. convert.spi 4/4 both arms. LEFT: (1) DoD = tibia CI green on the next user push (combat_text 5, game_calls 3, ground_trace 2 executed); (2) separate and older, tibia-owned: ground_trace's unpinned := main pulls Lua-only macros (canary.spi creature_position) into a default-Zig build; the fix is a pin (///> lua on its prelude) or a backend_switch in canary.spi, not compiler work.")
inl note_of_zig_expected_semicolon_regression_6 () = Note ("ZIG-EXPECTED-SEMICOLON-REGRESSION", 6u32, "2026-11-01T18:18Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 13:1x tibia, CONSUMER PROOF: tibia CI run 41326996580 (commit 7d47bad, on the landed convert.spi 9035FB80D406E22D) completed success on build (windows-2025), build (ubuntu-24.04) and push; the spiral CLI built and the 4 previously unsupported files ran. TIBIA-LIB-CONSUMER-REGATE closed Done on it. Nothing left on tibia's side.")
inl note_of_zig_expected_semicolon_regression_7 () = Note ("ZIG-EXPECTED-SEMICOLON-REGRESSION", 7u32, "2026-11-02T01:27Z", "compiler", "11-01 21:30 compiler: DONE. The user pushed spiral (main 73e4d863, 17:12, carrying lib/spiral/convert.spi's numeric_conv fix and lib_land_window's consumer step). tibia CI run 41366570407 (1f40e7d8, windows-2025): 0 'unsupported' cells, 0 'RUST-FAILED apps/spiral', so the spiral CLI builds from source on CI again. The run is still red, on 4 tibia files with failing tests (arena_rows: 'FatalError: File main has a type error', hit_grid, offscreen, table_rows). Those are tibia's own type errors, not the CLI build, and belong to tibia's lane; the older unpinned ground_trace main -> Zig issue is tibia's too (n-earlier).")
inl note_of_spiral_devcontainer_ci_parity_1 () = Note ("SPIRAL-DEVCONTAINER-CI-PARITY", 1u32, "2026-11-01T15:11Z", "main", "main 11:1x. DoD: a fresh codespace on i574n/spiral reaches 'lib_gate.ps1 -File async.spi' green within 20 min of creation, and its timing is recorded next to the node's (36 s). TYPEFEATURESET: n/a for the config; the toolchain list should come from one typed source shared with CI (the same pins as scripts/pins, CI-PARITY), not a second hand-kept list. NEXT STEP: read .github/workflows/gh-pages.yml's toolchain steps (setup-dotnet, setup-beam, setup-rust, setup-zig, bun) and mirror them as a postCreateCommand script; this also needs the user's commit of the 32gb devcontainer fix.")
inl note_of_spiral_devcontainer_ci_parity_2 () = Note ("SPIRAL-DEVCONTAINER-CI-PARITY", 2u32, "2026-11-01T20:47Z", "main", "main 16:4x FINDING: a codespace on i574n/spiral (main 504e1e07, standardLinux32gb, created 16:32 now that storage is 32gb) came up as Alpine Linux 3.23.7 with no pwsh and busybox tools: the Codespaces RECOVERY container. That means spiral's .devcontainer image build FAILED. Cause not yet read (the creation-log fetch timed out before the codespace was deleted). Prime suspect: the Dockerfile's base 'FROM mcr.microsoft.com/vscode/devcontainers/universal:dev' uses the retired vscode/devcontainers namespace and a 'dev' tag; the current image is mcr.microsoft.com/devcontainers/universal (pinned major tag). Probably also explains CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS attempts 1-3 ('tictactoe's devcontainer is ALPINE'): that was likely recovery mode too, not tictactoe's choice. Next: (1) create one spiral codespace and save 'gh codespace logs' before deleting; (2) fix the FROM line (plus the CI toolchain: OTP 29.1.2/Elixir 1.20.5, gleam 1.19.2, pinned zig/bun/lua, dotnet 11 rc via install-dotnet.ps1) in spiral/.devcontainer/Dockerfile; (3) it can only be proven after the user pushes, since codespaces build from the pushed branch.")
inl note_of_spiral_devcontainer_ci_parity_3 () = Note ("SPIRAL-DEVCONTAINER-CI-PARITY", 3u32, "2026-11-02T00:44Z", "main", "main 20:4x ROOT CAUSE FOUND (correcting n2's guess): read from the recovery container's /workspaces/.codespaces/.persistedshare/creation.log. Building the Dockerfile ('FROM mcr.microsoft.com/vscode/devcontainers/universal:dev' + apt powershell) pulls the multi-GB universal image layer by layer and fails with 'failed to register layer ... no space left on device' on the 32 GB disk, then 'Creating recovery container' (Alpine). The tag itself exists. The dotfiles codespaces worked because GitHub's default universal image comes preloaded on the host, with no build. ALL 17 repos use the same Dockerfile pattern (alphabet, blog, dice, dir-tree-html, eoie, fc1943s.github, fiscal, i574n.github, i574n.github.io, kit, mechahaze-album1, polyglot, spiral, tapas2, tibia, vault, x), so every repo's codespace has been landing in recovery. FIX (spiral only, unstaged, to prove first): devcontainer.json uses '\"image\": \"mcr.microsoft.com/devcontainers/universal:latest\"' (the host-cached default; pinning a digest would defeat the cache) plus the feature 'ghcr.io/devcontainers/features/powershell:1'; Dockerfile deleted. PROOF needs the user's push: then a spiral codespace must come up as Ubuntu with pwsh, and the same 2-line change rolls to the other 16. The Elixir/OTP/gleam toolchain still comes from the setup script (drafts store codespace-spiral-setup.sh) until it becomes features or a postCreateCommand.")
inl note_of_spiral_devcontainer_ci_parity_4 () = Note ("SPIRAL-DEVCONTAINER-CI-PARITY", 4u32, "2026-11-04T16:36Z", "main", "11-04 12:3x main DEVCONTAINER FIX PROVEN: the user's commit a8dc6b62 (11-02, image mcr.microsoft.com/devcontainers/universal:latest + powershell feature, Dockerfile gone) is on i574n/spiral main (98e51d32). A fresh standardLinux32gb codespace (probable-barnacle-jvxww7x542pjjg) was created in 13 s and answered ssh at 103 s as Ubuntu 24.04.5 LTS with /usr/bin/pwsh 7.6.9, 4 CPUs, overlay 32G with 11G free: no Alpine recovery container any more. NEXT (running): codespace-spiral-setup.sh from the drafts store, then lib_gate -File async.spi timed against the 20 min DoD; the codespace is stopped and deleted after. The same 2-line devcontainer change still has to roll to the other 16 repos (all used the failing Dockerfile pattern).")
inl note_of_spiral_devcontainer_ci_parity_5 () = Note ("SPIRAL-DEVCONTAINER-CI-PARITY", 5u32, "2026-11-04T16:39Z", "main", "11-04 12:4x main ROLLOUT (unstaged, for the user's commits): the proven spiral change (build/Dockerfile -> \"image\": \"mcr.microsoft.com/devcontainers/universal:latest\" + feature ghcr.io/devcontainers/features/powershell:1, Dockerfile deleted) applied to 13 repos whose Dockerfile was byte-identical to spiral's old one or differed only by the df line: alphabet, blog, dice, dir-tree-html, eoie, fc1943s.github, fiscal, i574n.github, i574n.github.io, mechahaze-album1, tapas2, tibia, vault, x; every devcontainer.json re-parsed as JSON. Not touched: kit (json already image-based, its unused Dockerfile is kit's to delete), tictactoe (tab-indented json with a docker-in-docker feature and an untagged base) and polyglot (its Dockerfile also COPYs scripts/core.ps1 into the image, so it needs a postCreateCommand instead). Each repo's codespace stops landing in the Alpine recovery container once committed.")
inl note_of_spiral_devcontainer_ci_parity_6 () = Note ("SPIRAL-DEVCONTAINER-CI-PARITY", 6u32, "2026-11-04T16:48Z", "main", "11-04 12:4x main DOD MET: on the fresh spiral codespace (created ~12:30, standardLinux32gb, 4 CPUs), codespace-spiral-setup.sh ran 12:35-12:45 with every step exit 0 (pwsh, clone, init 7 min, dotnet, OTP, Elixir, Gleam, Zig, Bun, Lua, Rust nightly, single-flight compiler build 81 s, mix deps), then lib_gate -File async.spi: tests passed 3 failed 0 of 3, type errors 0, GATE-EXIT 0 in 36 s, the same as the node's 36 s. Green about 16 min after creation, inside the 20 min bar. Codespace stopped and deleted at 12:47 (gh codespace list empty). Left for follow-ups: the toolchain list still lives in the drafts-store setup script, not one typed source shared with CI (CI-PARITY), and the 13-repo devcontainer rollout waits on the user's commits.")
inl note_of_lib_gate_linux_portable_1 () = Note ("LIB-GATE-LINUX-PORTABLE", 1u32, "2026-11-01T15:11Z", "main", "main 11:1x, found by CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS attempt 5. DoD: the four scripts resolve their cache roots through one helper that falls back to XDG_DATA_HOME or ~/.local/share off Windows; lib_gate runs on the Linux codespace. Ports to Spiral under PS1-TO-SPIRAL later; this is the one-line host fix meanwhile. NEXT STEP: grep apps/cells/spi/*.ps1 for LOCALAPPDATA and route each through the helper.")
inl note_of_lib_gate_linux_portable_2 () = Note ("LIB-GATE-LINUX-PORTABLE", 2u32, "2026-11-01T19:14Z", "main", "main 15:2x CODE LANDED unstaged in spiral/apps/cells/spi: lib_gate, lib_land_window, cells_land_window and type_probe resolve their data root as LOCALAPPDATA ?? XDG_DATA_HOME ?? ~/.local/share (all 15 bare uses replaced); kit and dotnet get .exe only on Windows. lib_gate's scoop PATH prepend and its SPIRAL_CC gcc.exe default are now Windows-only: on Linux the ';'-joined string fused with the first real PATH entry and broke it. Parse check: 0 errors in all 4. On Windows the fallback resolves to the same paths, so behaviour is unchanged. Remaining DoD: one lib_gate run on a Linux machine with Elixir/mix (the codespace image lacks mix: SPIRAL-DEVCONTAINER-CI-PARITY). Next: run it on the Cloud VM once the personal lane has Elixir there, or in a codespace after the devcontainer gains mix.")
inl note_of_lib_gate_linux_portable_3 () = Note ("LIB-GATE-LINUX-PORTABLE", 3u32, "2026-11-01T19:56Z", "main", "main 16:0x DONE: lib_gate GREEN on Linux (europa, Ubuntu, kit job job-1793562906157): guid.spi discovered 2, executed 2, passed 2, failed 0, unsupported 0, slowest 20.9 s. Two fixes along the way: (1) the fallback is now LOCALAPPDATA ?? XDG_CACHE_HOME ?? ~/.cache, matching run_notebook.ps1:80 and the VM's ~/.cache/spiral-bin layout (my first ~/.local/share choice missed it); (2) europa lacked gleam/zig/lua/bun, so main installed them pinned to the box's versions (gleam 1.19.2, zig 0.18.0-dev.738+ae9a8acc7, Lua 5.1.5, bun 1.4.4). kit's Linux job host doesn't put /usr/local/bin on PATH, so the job sets SPIRAL_GLEAM/ZIG/LUA/BUN and PATH explicitly (x-dumps: /etc/environment until kit's discovery fix). Command that works: remote.ps1 europa job start <label> <ms> pwsh -NoProfile -Command '<env lines>; & /home/remote/<mirror>/spiral/apps/cells/spi/lib_gate.ps1 -File <f> -RawOut <path>'.")
inl note_of_leptos_ui_type_probe_red_1 () = Note ("LEPTOS-UI-TYPE-PROBE-RED", 1u32, "2026-11-01T15:58Z", "compiler", "11-01 11:58 compiler. FOUND while answering main's respell report: the lib respell land closed red on type_probe (10 of 95 modules), and main suspected '::' in open paths. Ruled out: (a) on the respelled copy, restoring ':< rust::rust_operators' to the dotted form gives the identical errors in toggle; (b) ':< leptos::leptos' parses and fails only at resolution (ETY-ModuleIndexFailedInOpen), so '::' in open paths parses; (c) the LIVE, un-respelled lib fails the same: 22 of 23 leptos/ui + leptos/svg modules FAIL type_probe (only ui/table passes). DOD: every leptos/ui and leptos/svg module either passes type_probe on the live lib or is shown to compile in a real consumer (dice's Leptos app) with type_probe fixed to check folder modules the way the package does; the count goes 22 -> 0, recorded per module. NEXT STEP: compile dice's leptos entry against the live lib: if it builds, it's a type_probe context bug (it lifts the module without its folder scope); if it fails with the same unbound names, the modules broke when leptos.spi moved into leptos/. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: type_probe's per-module verdict as a union ProbeVerdict = Pass | Fail of list error | Void of reason | PreExisting of list error, so lib_land_window compares typed verdicts instead of grepping ': FAIL'.")
inl note_of_leptos_ui_type_probe_red_2 () = Note ("LEPTOS-UI-TYPE-PROBE-RED", 2u32, "2026-11-01T15:59Z", "compiler", "11-01 11:59 compiler, NARROWED (read-only): the failing modules use BARE leptos names after ':< leptos' (toggle: label, event, attr_fn), while the one passing module, ui/table, uses QUALIFIED names (leptos.table, leptos.thead). dice uses the same modules from its own package (ui.toggle.render at settings_view.spi:129, ui.text_input / ui.loading_button / ui.accordion in dice_view.spi), and dice builds. So the modules resolve from a consumer package, and the FAILs come from checking them inside the lib package, where ':< leptos' from inside leptos/ resolves differently (':< leptos::leptos' gives ETY-ModuleIndexFailedInOpen). Most likely a type_probe/lib-scope issue, not broken code. NEXT: confirm with a scratch package that opens leptos the way dice does and names ui.toggle.render, compiled with --check; if it passes, make type_probe check folder modules through such a consumer stub (or the folder-local open), and the 22 go green without touching the modules. Until then lib_land_window's baseline-aware type_probe keeps them from blocking lands.")
inl note_of_leptos_ui_type_probe_red_3 () = Note ("LEPTOS-UI-TYPE-PROBE-RED", 3u32, "2026-11-01T22:57Z", "main", "main lib-reshape 11-01 19:0x, user 11-01 ~17:40 ('some lane complaining that open doesn't support ::, maybe we should attack that also to rebenchmark everything'): the complaint traces to this item. '::' in open paths parses (n1); what fails is the folder-scope resolution of ':< leptos::leptos' inside leptos/. LIB-RESHAPE R2 flattens rust/ (rust_operators already resolves flat, so the 'rust::rust_operators' spelling and its trap go away). leptos/ stays a folder by the user's call, so this item's fix (type_probe checking folder modules the way a consumer package does, or the folder-local open) is still needed for leptos/ui and leptos/svg. A rebenchmark of every lib module's type_probe and gates is cleanest after that fix plus R2, so that both baselines are taken on the same layout.")
inl note_of_leptos_ui_type_probe_red_4 () = Note ("LEPTOS-UI-TYPE-PROBE-RED", 4u32, "2026-11-05T09:37Z", "compiler", "11-05 05:3x compiler: ROOT CAUSE CONFIRMED, a type_probe bug, not broken modules. (1) Consumer check, the item's recorded NEXT: a scratch package shaped like dice's (packageDir lib, |core- spiral-, ':< leptos' then 'ui.toggle.render') compiles to Rust with installed pack44, exit 0. Its first variant's FatalError, which lists every type error in the dependency path, named no leptos file. (2) Cause: apps/cells/spi/type_probe.ps1 builds the probe from the module's own opens plus its definitions, but always writes it at the lib copy's ROOT. From the root, toggle's ':< leptos' names the leptos/ FOLDER, not leptos/leptos.spi, hence 'Unbound type variable: event/label'. (3) Fix (draft, one line): under spiral.toml discovery the probe is written BESIDE the module (Join-Path (Split-Path source)), so its opens resolve exactly as the module's; the package.spiproj path, which registers the probe in a root module list, is unchanged. leptos/ui/toggle.spi: live FAIL (18 module errors) -> draft PASS with control ok. The full 23-module + root-module comparison is running. The draft is a Cells file, so it goes to x (Cells lead) to land.")
inl note_of_leptos_ui_type_probe_red_5 () = Note ("LEPTOS-UI-TYPE-PROBE-RED", 5u32, "2026-11-05T10:00Z", "compiler", "11-05 06:0x compiler: FIX PROVEN, 22 -> 0. Same run, same lib (live lib/spiral, installed pack44), 26 modules = all 23 leptos/ui + leptos/svg + 3 root controls (reflection, resultm, doc_blocks). LIVE type_probe.ps1: pass 4, fail 22 (every leptos module except ui/table, e.g. accordion 34 errors, svg/loading 24, toggle 18; all 'control ok', so real verdicts). DRAFT (probe written beside the module under spiral.toml): pass 26, fail 0, void 0; root controls unchanged (tests typed 15 / 7 / 1, 0 errors). No leptos module was changed. Draft %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\LEPTOS-UI-TYPE-PROBE-RED\\apps-cells__spi__type_probe.ps1 (BASE.txt; 1 line changed). Cells is x-led, so x lands it (cells_land_window). After that, lib_land_window's type_probe step stops reporting the 22 pre-existing FAILs on any leptos land.")
inl note_of_leptos_ui_type_probe_red_6 () = Note ("LEPTOS-UI-TYPE-PROBE-RED", 6u32, "2026-11-05T10:13Z", "x", "2026-11-05 06:13 x (Cells owner): LANDED compiler's one-line type_probe.ps1 fix through cells_land_window (closed green, document_test 26/26, undo cells-20261105-061126; live 2CAB3FFF93054A00). Under spiral.toml the probe file now goes beside the module instead of at the lib copy's root, so a folder module's own opens resolve. Verified on the live probe: leptos/ui/accordion.spi PASS (0 errors, previously among the 22 FAILs per compiler's same-run A/B), root control erlang_text.spi PASS (5 tests typed, unchanged).")
inl note_of_leptos_ui_type_probe_red_7 () = Note ("LEPTOS-UI-TYPE-PROBE-RED", 7u32, "2026-11-05T10:13Z", "compiler", "11-05 06:1x compiler: LANDED by x through cells_land_window, closed green (document_test 26/26; undo cells-20261105-061126; live apps/cells/spi/type_probe.ps1 2CAB3FFF93054A00 = the draft, unstaged). x's post-land check on the live probe: leptos/ui/accordion.spi PASS (0 errors), root control erlang_text.spi PASS (5 tests typed, unchanged). DoD met: the 22 leptos/ui + leptos/svg FAILs are 0 with no module changed, and lib_land_window's type_probe step no longer carries them.")
inl note_of_delphi_to_pascal_1 () = Note ("DELPHI-TO-PASCAL", 1u32, "2026-11-01T16:54Z", "main", "main 13:0x (user 11-01: 'rename every delphi reference to pascal, compiler, everything'). Census first: spiral_compiler.fs has 41 'Delphi' matches; lib backend_switch keys (Delphi =) and union backend's Delphi case; tests/matrix.psd1 Delphi list and Known rows; Cells targets.ex; FPC paths stay (FPC is the toolchain). DoD: grep -i delphi across spiral, lib, Cells and samples returns only history (changelogs, backlog notes) and the FPC/Delphi-compatibility mode flags the toolchain itself needs (e.g. -Mdelphi, which stays and is documented); backend id Pascal in --backend, backend_switch and the matrix; residuals byte-identical (a rename only), proven by a predict run. TYPEFEATURESET: the backend union's case renames from Delphi to Pascal; old spellings accepted for one edition with a warning (the backend key is user-facing). NEXT STEP: census per file and kind (identifier, key, user-facing string, flag) as a table on this item; this rides a compiler pack.")
inl note_of_delphi_to_pascal_2 () = Note ("DELPHI-TO-PASCAL", 2u32, "2026-11-01T17:21Z", "compiler", "11-01 13:25 compiler: CENSUS (git grep -i delphi, generated sample outputs excluded). spiral: 42 files. (a) COMPILER: spiral_compiler.fs 38 (codegenDelphi* identifiers, the backend union case, user-facing strings); host Program.fs 2 (--backend parsing); scripts: test.ps1 11 (the backend list, the native arm, ValidateSet), probe.ps1 2, bench-pair.ps1 2, test-blocks.ps1 1, delphi-heaptrc.ps1 3 (the file renames to pascal-heaptrc.ps1); tests/matrix.psd1 7 (Delphi list + Known rows); docs tmp/AGENTS.md 9 and README.md 5; 3 sample README/bench files and samples/core/sm.spi 1. (b) LIB: 19 files, 97 hits: 54 `Delphi =` backend_switch keys, plus helper names (delphi_byte_at, delphi_sequence_width, delphi_code_point_count_from, delphi_byte_text) and the test name backend_switch_has_no_Delphi_arm_in_lib_spiral. Biggest: sm'.spi 17, file_system.spi 11, xml.spi 11, backend.spi 8, unicode.spi 7. (c) CELLS: targets.ex 6, targets.spi 4, builders.ex 3, console.spi 2, README 4, and 3 test files (9). (d) CONSUMERS: kit 2 (README, spiral.ps1); fiscal scripts/delphi-reach.ps1 13 + init.ps1 1. fiscal bench/acbr names ACBr's real Delphi sources (the vendor language, not our backend): KEEP. tibia, x and dice: 0. deps/The-Spiral-Language core: 0. KEEPS: the FPC flag -Mdelphi (test.ps1 Delphi arm) and ACBr. ORDER (no flag day): (1) a compiler pack where Pascal is the backend case and `Delphi` is still accepted in --backend and as a backend_switch key with one deprecation warning; residuals byte-identical, by a predict run. (2) A lib land through lib_land_window renaming the keys and helpers (the consumers step proves apps/spiral still compiles). (3) Cells, scripts and docs. (4) kit and fiscal (ask their lanes). (5) The next edition drops the alias. TYPEFEATURESET: the backend union case is renamed rather than aliased in the type; the alias exists only in the parser, which maps the text to the Pascal case plus a warning, so no code past the parser sees a Delphi string. NEXT STEP: grep the emitted .pas outputs for \"Delphi\" (a comment or directive in generated code would break residual byte-identity), then draft step 1 as a kit do program in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\DELPHI-TO-PASCAL\\.")
inl note_of_delphi_to_pascal_3 () = Note ("DELPHI-TO-PASCAL", 3u32, "2026-11-01T17:45Z", "compiler", "11-01 13:47 compiler: RESIDUAL CHECK (next step of n2). 426 emitted Pascal outputs under apps/compiler/tmp/samples; \"delphi\" appears on only 4 distinct lines. (1) `{$mode delphi}{$H+}` in 423 outputs is the FPC dialect directive (the -Mdelphi twin): KEEP. (2) One sample carries SPIRAL_TARGET_GLOBAL_DELPHI_PRELUDE / _BEFORE_MAIN / _AFTER_MAIN marker strings (target-global placement markers named by the backend key). Renaming the key renames these markers, so that ONE sample's residual changes. That is an explained delta, not byte-identity. DoD amendment: residuals byte-identical except the target-global marker sample, whose only diff is DELPHI -> PASCAL inside the marker strings. Codegen: the user-facing strings (\"The Delphi backend ...\", the backend_switch field message, around spiral_compiler.fs:14620-15097) are compiler diagnostics, not residual text, so they rename freely. NEXT STEP unchanged: draft step 1 (Pascal case + parser alias) as a kit do program in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\DELPHI-TO-PASCAL\\.")
inl note_of_delphi_to_pascal_4 () = Note ("DELPHI-TO-PASCAL", 4u32, "2026-11-01T17:55Z", "compiler", "11-01 13:54 compiler: STEP 1 DRAFTED: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\DELPHI-TO-PASCAL\\1-pascal-backend-alias.kitdo. Dry run on scratch copies of the live core (F6F6879566C5A830 = pack14a source) and host (420E1452DB4B3194): 43 replacements, giving core d812af814668c32e and host f8760f640090da0d. After it, the only \"Delphi\" left in the core is the alias itself. WHAT IT DOES: (a) --backend Pascal builds with codegenPascal and evaluates as backend \"Pascal\"; --backend Delphi is accepted and runs the identical path. (b) One function, backend_key_canonical (top level, before module DynamicIfNesting), maps the key \"Delphi\" to \"Pascal\". It is applied at the three places user-written backend keys are compared: BackendSwitch arm selection and validation (the Map.iter key), UnsafeBackendSwitch, join_backend, and the codegen record pick. So lib's `Delphi =` arms keep working unchanged until step 2 renames them. (c) Every codegen identifier and diagnostic says Pascal. (d) Host: .pas/.dpr map to Pascal, and the usage line says Pascal. NOT IN IT YET: a deprecation warning, because the host has no warning channel that Cells won't read as an error (stderr). For now the alias is silent and the edition-drop step removes it. TYPEFEATURESET: the alias lives in one function at the comparison boundary, so no Delphi string flows past it. A record carrying both keys would select two arms; step 2 must not leave both in lib, and the compiler should reject that case (to add before the pack). PROOF NEEDED (pack time): build plus a predict run. Expected residual delta: zero, except the one target-global marker sample if its marker text derives from the evaluator backend name; check which. Then `-Suite all -Native` Pascal rows agree with C.")
inl note_of_delphi_to_pascal_5 () = Note ("DELPHI-TO-PASCAL", 5u32, "2026-11-01T19:48Z", "compiler", "11-01 15:50 compiler: STEP 2 DRAFTED (lib) and step 1 re-verified. (1) Step 1 applies cleanly to the live host after today's COMPILER-WIN-STACK-OVERFLOW land (Program.fs 98D282B5): 43 replacements. It also stacks cleanly with GLEAM-JS-TARGET-GAPS's core program, so both can ride one pack. (2) %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\DELPHI-TO-PASCAL\\2-lib-pascal-keys.kitdo, generated against the post-respell lib (`::` spelling, landed 14:53). 19 files, 97 literal replace-alls: backend_switch keys `Delphi =`, record type keys `Delphi : `, union backend's `| Delphi` case and `| Delphi =>` arms, `:= target = Delphi`, `backend \"Delphi\"` (the backend-name string), the `backend_switch_has_no_Delphi_arm_in_lib_spiral` marker, identifiers delphi_* / *_delphi (byte helpers, float format/parse, obj_to_string_delphi*, two test names), the probe file name, and 'the Delphi backend' messages. Dry run on a scratch copy of lib: 0 Delphi left except the 10 `///> delphi` test-target lines, which stay for step 3 because they are Cells target names and must change together with Cells' targets.ex. LAND ORDER is unchanged: the step-1 pack installs first (it accepts both keys), then this program lands through lib_land_window. Its consumers step proves apps/spiral compiles, and the base hashes refuse it if lib moved; regenerate it then, since it is generated from the live text in seconds.")
inl note_of_delphi_to_pascal_6 () = Note ("DELPHI-TO-PASCAL", 6u32, "2026-11-02T01:23Z", "compiler", "11-01 21:24 compiler: step 1 rides pack15c (handed to main; installs after lib-reshape's R1b+R2 land and kit's TRAIN8s). pack15c's predicts show the rename changes no residual; Pascal and Delphi rows both ran PrimToString and the case-fold repro to C's exit. Step 2 (lib program, 97 replacements over 19 files) still applies cleanly to the post-R1a lib (21:23 dry run). It lands after pack15c installs and R1b+R2 settle; re-dry-run then, since R2 flattens lib/spiral/rust/ (rust/near.spi and rust/rust.spi move).")
inl note_of_delphi_to_pascal_7 () = Note ("DELPHI-TO-PASCAL", 7u32, "2026-11-02T02:12Z", "compiler", "11-01 22:12 compiler: step 2 RE-BASED on the post-R1b+R2 lib (landed 22:01: lib/spiral/rust/ flattened, mapm -> map). The old program failed (rust/near.spi and rust/rust.spi moved to near.spi and rust.spi), so I regenerated it from a FILESYSTEM scan of lib. A git grep misses the files the reshape just created, which are still untracked. Result: 19 files, 97 replacements, dry run clean, 0 Delphi left except the 10 ///> delphi targets (step 3). Lands after pack15c installs.")
inl note_of_delphi_to_pascal_8 () = Note ("DELPHI-TO-PASCAL", 8u32, "2026-11-02T05:35Z", "compiler", "11-02 01:35 compiler: STEP 2 LANDED green (lib, unstaged) through apps/cells/spi/lib_land_window.ps1 after pack15c installed step 1 (the backend_key_canonical alias) and lib-reshape-r3 released tree-write. 19 whole-file drafts built from %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\DELPHI-TO-PASCAL\\2-lib-pascal-keys.kitdo on today's lib (97 replacements), each with a base-hash guard. Window results: signatures 14 unchanged; consumer apps/spiral/spiral.spi compiles; document_test 22 passed; type_probe 18/18 PASS. Undo: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261102-012023. Lib now has 0 Delphi outside the ///> delphi test targets. Dangling check (ripgrep, all repos): no code outside lib calls the 11 renamed identifiers (delphi_byte_at ... obj_to_string_delphi_bool). HAZARD RECORDED: lib backend_switch resolves the current backend through backend 'Pascal' + record_type_try_find on the CONSUMER's record, a string field lookup the compiler alias doesn't reach. So a consumer record that still says Delphi = through lib backend_switch silently gets the no-arm default. Today there is none: Cells console.spi uses raw !!!!BackendSwitch, which the alias covers, and samples use core. If one appears, add a Delphi fallback lookup in backend.spi's Pascal arm. NEXT: step 3, the ///> delphi targets and Cells targets.spi DelphiTarget (coordinate with x, who owns Cells).")
inl note_of_delphi_to_pascal_9 () = Note ("DELPHI-TO-PASCAL", 9u32, "2026-11-02T06:16Z", "compiler", "11-02 02:16 compiler: STEP 3 SCOPED (x owns Cells, so it is offered to x, not done by me). Files: apps/cells/spi/targets.spi (DelphiTarget, tool \"delphi\", backend \"Delphi\"); apps/cells/lib/spiral/cells/builders.ex:15/22/118 (tool map, expected list, dcc dispatch); targets.ex:312-331 (delphi_compiler/run_delphi); tests builders_test.exs:117, targets_test.exs:38-45/233-249, target_audit_test.exs:15; README 219-223/348; plus the 10 ///> delphi lines in lib. Shape: a PascalTarget that accepts BOTH tool names 'pascal' and 'delphi' (old ///> delphi lines keep working) and passes backend 'Pascal'; the fpc/dcc32 toolchain choice is unchanged; then the ///> delphi lines in lib become ///> pascal in one lib program. No urgency: the compiler accepts Delphi indefinitely through backend_key_canonical (pack15c), so step 3 is naming only. DoD: no Delphi in Cells except the dcc32 compiler name, lib ///> pascal, Cells gate green on a Pascal cell.")
inl note_of_delphi_to_pascal_10 () = Note ("DELPHI-TO-PASCAL", 10u32, "2026-11-02T06:17Z", "compiler", "11-02 02:17 compiler: x TOOK step 3, in two slices. (1) Alias first, in x's next Cells land: builders.ex accepts 'pascal' next to 'delphi', dispatches both to the same runner, and adds a test that a ///> pascal cell runs. x messages compiler when it lands. (2) Renames ride the targets.ex port to Spiral (targets.spi PascalTarget accepting both names, returning backend 'Pascal'; delphi_compiler/run_delphi, the tests and the README move then), so the Elixir isn't renamed only to be deleted. MY FOLLOW-UP STAGED: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\DELPHI-TO-PASCAL\\3-lib-pascal-targets.kitdo flips lib's 10 ///> delphi lines to ///> pascal (date_time 1, file_system 2, sm' 4, unicode 1, xml 2); dry run clean, 0 left. It lands through lib_land_window only AFTER x's slice 1, because today's Cells rejects the tool name 'pascal'.")
inl note_of_delphi_to_pascal_11 () = Note ("DELPHI-TO-PASCAL", 11u32, "2026-11-02T06:19Z", "x", "2026-11-02 02:19 x: STEP 3 OWNER = x (compiler asked; Cells is x's). Two slices. (1) ALIAS 2026-11-02 02:19: builders.ex maps 'pascal' => :delphi and adds it to the expected list, plus a builders_test case that a ///> pascal line builds with the delphi tool. Draft in drafts\\spiral\\DELPHI-TO-PASCAL\\builders.ex/builders_test.exs (bases 1ACEBDBAC8B2/4AD178163371). PROOF x-pascal-alias1 (Europa, mix test builders_test.exs), rule written before the run: PASS iff 0 failures and the new test runs. Once landed, compiler flips lib's 10 ///> delphi lines. (2) RENAMES RIDE THE CELLS PORT: targets.spi PascalTarget accepting both names and returning backend 'Pascal'; delphi_compiler/run_delphi; the tests (builders_test:117, targets_test:38-45/233-249, target_audit_test:15); README 219-223. They move when targets.ex is ported, so the Elixir isn't renamed only to be deleted. The fpc/dcc32 choice stays.")
inl note_of_delphi_to_pascal_12 () = Note ("DELPHI-TO-PASCAL", 12u32, "2026-11-02T06:27Z", "compiler", "11-02 02:27 compiler: x's slice 1 is in (apps/cells builders.ex 82556E3C7777 maps 'pascal' to :delphi; builders_test AE2273145ADF has the ///> pascal case; x-pascal-alias2 on Europa 7/7). The ///> pascal lib flip is ready as 5 per-file land-lib-program calls (programs in scratch pascal3land; bases date_time 0EAF563F0AD5A0C5, file_system 6A80E175170C9CF8, sm' 7A8B291EA55C9AF7, unicode 37FBFBB41CCB275A, xml FA14058BE85ADEA2). lib-guarded-do REFUSED all 5 (exit 3, nothing landed): kit-TRAIN9's held heavy window and main's chain pid 23172 running a LIB-RESHAPE program both count as live lib readers. Next: land when both clear, after main's pack15d message (re-derive the base hashes first if lib-reshape touched those files), then run a Cells gate on one ///> pascal test when the box is free of heavy work.")
inl note_of_delphi_to_pascal_13 () = Note ("DELPHI-TO-PASCAL", 13u32, "2026-11-02T07:00Z", "compiler", "11-02 03:00 compiler: ///> pascal FLIP LANDED (lib, unstaged; 5 land-lib-program calls after the guard cleared, once main's pack15d chain finished and TRAIN9's window closed): date_time 8E2666DB0CE5F81C, file_system 41B47356F0BFC08F, sm' 12E51A70A505BE03, unicode 7857B89E3956450F, xml DBF2C23E67B14566; undo %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\undo\\3-pascal-*. Lib has 0 ///> delphi and 10 ///> pascal. PROOF end to end on the box (installed pack15d, live lib, x's Cells alias): lib_gate unicode.spi -Test char_of_encodes_utf8_and_rejects_surrogates (a ///> pascal test) passed 1/1, unsupported 0, type errors 0, 26.7 s (an fpc build). Remaining (x, with the targets port): PascalTarget in targets.spi, delphi_compiler/run_delphi renames, tests, README.")
