inl note_of_lib_units_amount_1 () = Note ("LIB-UNITS-AMOUNT", 1u32, "2026-11-01T19:36Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 15:3x tibia: filed from TIBIA-HARVEST's candidate list (quantity is candidate 2 after rng; no existing item: searched quantit/units/amount/phantom unit). PLAN: the generic half of tibia src/quantity.spi (phantom ':! amount unit = i32' plus amount_of, value_of, plus, minus, scaled, at_least, capped) lands as lib/spiral/units.spi; the game vocabulary (hitpoints, milliseconds, tiles, gold_coins tags and the hp/ms/tile_count/gp constructors) stays in tibia's quantity.spi, which then holds only tags and constructors. Name 'units': 'quantity' would collide with tibia's module and 'measure' with a tibia app module; no units.spi exists anywhere. DRAFT: kit drafts store spiral\\TIBIA-HARVEST\\units.spi (sample tags apples/pears for the tests; c/rust/lua arithmetic test, two compile-fail tests 'fails \"Unification failure\"' that pin the phantom guarantee, one wgsl test). IMPORTERS (git grep -c quantity::): hunting_pack 54, readiness 24, pack_sim 12, predict 3, sweep 1, gpu_sim 1 = 95 sites; the op calls move to units:: and types become 'units::amount quantity::hitpoints'. DoD: (a) units.spi landed via lib_land_window (new-file path) with the node gate green on c/rust/lua, both fails-tests passing, a negative mutant (plus subtracts) caught, wgsl green on the box; (b) tibia quantity.spi has no arithmetic left, every importer uses units::, tibia's full build green on the node with unchanged pinned values. NEXT STEP: after LIB-KEYED-RNG's tibia consumer build reports, gate the draft on the node mirror tibia-rng (same script as LIB-KEYED-RNG n2).")
inl note_of_lib_units_amount_2 () = Note ("LIB-UNITS-AMOUNT", 2u32, "2026-11-01T20:00Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 16:0x tibia: LIB HALF PROVEN. Node gate job-1793562414906-tibia-units-gate on mirror tibia-rng (lib synced 14:57, after the :: respell): positive 3/3 passed, 0 type errors (same_unit_arithmetic on c/rust/lua; both 'fails \"Unification failure\"' tests pass, so mixing apples with pears really is a type error); units_on_gpu wgsl unsupported on the node (no runner; box after land); negative mutant (plus subtracts) CAUGHT, 1 failed, 0 type errors. One budget finding (test at 287) fixed by moving the body into an arithmetic_of fixture (no logic change); local budget 0. Roundtrip canonical true, fixpoint true. Land queued behind compiler's compile window (compiler-core-ord-consumers); the land script refuses if package.spiproj moved while waiting. Next: box wgsl test after the land, then the tibia importers (95 sites) once LIB-KEYED-RNG's consumer build is green, so the two migrations are proven one at a time.")
inl note_of_lib_units_amount_3 () = Note ("LIB-UNITS-AMOUNT", 3u32, "2026-11-01T20:26Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 16:2x tibia: LANDED. First land closed RED and undid itself cleanly (units.spi moved to undo as units.spi.new, package.spiproj restored): type_probe typed the two deliberate 'fails \\\"Unification failure\\\"' tests and counted their expected error as a regression. Fixed type_probe.ps1 (spiral apps/cells/spi, unstaged): blocks whose header holds 'fails \\\"...\\\"' are skipped and listed ('skipped fails (expected errors, checked by Cells)'), like ///> _ blocks; proven on a scratch lib copy (units PASS with both listed; keyed_rng still types 6). Second land 16:18 closed green: 14 signatures unchanged, spiral.spi compiles, document_test 22 passed, type_probe PASS; units.spi 598732C598D9, package.spiproj 7B160B4F51FE; undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261101-161819. Box wgsl: units_on_gpu 1/1 passed. DoD (a) met. Next: (b) tibia importers, after LIB-KEYED-RNG's consumer build reports.")
inl note_of_lib_units_amount_4 () = Note ("LIB-UNITS-AMOUNT", 4u32, "2026-11-01T23:21Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 19:2x tibia, DONE. DoD (a) met at the 16:18 land (n3). DoD (b): tibia quantity.spi holds only tags and constructors over units::amount, 69 operation sites across 6 files use units::, committed in b08cd87; tibia CI run 41350993071 SUCCESS on both OS jobs with unchanged pinned values.")
inl note_of_lib_fixed_views_1 () = Note ("LIB-FIXED-VIEWS", 1u32, "2026-11-01T20:03Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 16:1x tibia: DoD: lib module with the containers and both prototypes, c/rust/lua tests plus a compile-fail test (mapped over a non-instance), node gate with a negative mutant (one mapped instance swaps two slots), wgsl on the box; tibia's 2 importers switched with the full node build green. Next step: draft from src/views.spi lines 5-55, minus policy-specific decide_all/observed, which stay in tibia.")
inl note_of_lib_fixed_views_2 () = Note ("LIB-FIXED-VIEWS", 2u32, "2026-11-01T22:56Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 18:4x tibia: LANDED 18:43 (lib fixed_views.spi 032E9DD3172D, with case_labels and wire; close: 14 signatures unchanged, spiral.spi compiles, document_test 22, type_probe PASS with the fails-test listed as skipped). GATE (Europa Linux mirror /home/remote/tibia-libgate; the node's runs were void, see LIB-WIRE-CHECKSUMS): positive 5/5 passed on c/rust/lua, 0 type errors, lanes_on_gpu wgsl unsupported there; negative (trio instance swaps two slots) CAUGHT, only a_trio_maps_like_the_other_views failed. TIBIA HALF (unstaged): hunting_pack 30 and pack_sim 1 'views::' sites -> 'fixed_views::'; tibia src/views.spi keeps only the policy part (decide_all, observed, 4 policy tests) over ':< fixed_views', and its 4 generic tests moved to lib. Two hunting_pack definitions went over budget from the longer prefix: fixed with an entry_trio alias and a shorter parameter name. Next: box wgsl run, then the tibia consumer build on the node.")
inl note_of_lib_fixed_views_3 () = Note ("LIB-FIXED-VIEWS", 3u32, "2026-11-01T23:23Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 19:2x tibia: box wgsl lanes_on_gpu passed 1/1 against the live lib. The tibia half is in the user's commit 2aa39c6, whose CI run 41359244876 went RED on both OS, but only at the cell budget: hunting_pack:607 (282) and :1589 (273) grew from the longer fixed_views:: prefix. Both are fixed unstaged (entry_trio alias, shorter parameter; local budget 0 findings). A scoped node consumer build of the touched files (job-1793574933546) is running. DONE when the user's next push goes green.")
inl note_of_lib_fixed_views_4 () = Note ("LIB-FIXED-VIEWS", 4u32, "2026-11-02T01:18Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 21:2x tibia, DONE. tibia CI run 41366570407 on the user's commit 1f40e7d (which includes 2aa39c6's views migration plus the hunting_pack budget fix): 53 of 57 test files green on both OS, including hunting_pack, pack_sim and views (decide_all/observed policy tests over lib fixed_views). The 4 red files are unrelated to views and fixed unstaged: results/arena_rows (a combinator named 'then', a keyword), hit_grid and table_rows (same package), and offscreen (the '^^' after global binding). Lib side: landed 18:43, gated on Europa with the mutant caught, wgsl green on the box.")
inl note_of_lib_wire_checksums_1 () = Note ("LIB-WIRE-CHECKSUMS", 1u32, "2026-11-01T20:03Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 16:1x tibia: DoD: lib module with xtea_key/xtea_encrypt/xtea_decrypt and adler start/update/digest, known-answer tests from public vectors (Adler-32 of 'Wikipedia' = 0x11E60398; an XTEA round-trip plus one published vector) on c/rust/lua plus wgsl if u32 only, node gate with a negative mutant (delta constant off by one), then tibia src/wire.spi archived. Next step: draft from src/wire.spi (104 lines) with the vectors added.")
inl note_of_lib_wire_checksums_2 () = Note ("LIB-WIRE-CHECKSUMS", 2u32, "2026-11-01T22:57Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 18:4x tibia: LANDED 18:43 (lib wire.spi 9A087F870122; same close as LIB-FIXED-VIEWS). GATE (Europa): positive 5/5 on c/rust/lua plus zig, wgsl unsupported there; negative (XTEA delta off by one) CAUGHT: both published-vector tests failed and the round trip still passed, as it must (a wrong delta still inverts itself). The node's two runs were VOID: the first missed the compiler-daemon start under load (my gate script shared MIX_BUILD_PATH with lib_gate, fixed), the second failed every test because my case_labels draft (missing ':< sm'_operators') sat in the same gate package, and a package type-checks every module. tibia src/wire.spi (unregistered, 0 importers) removed from the tree (git history keeps it). Next: box wgsl run, then Done.")
inl note_of_lib_wire_checksums_3 () = Note ("LIB-WIRE-CHECKSUMS", 3u32, "2026-11-01T23:22Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 19:2x tibia, DONE. Box wgsl: xtea_published_vector_on_gpu passed 1/1 against the live lib. With the Europa gate (c/rust/lua/zig, mutant caught) and the 18:43 land, every DoD point holds; tibia src/wire.spi removal is in the user's commit 2aa39c6.")
inl note_of_rust_union_default_array_create_1 () = Note ("RUST-UNION-DEFAULT-ARRAY-CREATE", 1u32, "2026-11-01T21:11Z", "compiler", "11-01 21:1x compiler: filed from x-dumps' report (europa, single-flight core f6f6879566c5a830, rustc nightly 2026-10-31). WHAT: Rust array create of a tuple element whose fields include a union (`vec![<(Rc<str>, US0, Rc<str>, bool)>::default(); n]`) fails with E0599 'US0: Default not satisfied'. codegenRust emits `impl Default` for a union only when every case field has a default expression (AGENTS.md, Rust array create), so an option-like union (None | Some of string) never gets one. Reached through lib json.decode into a record with an `array_base r` field where r has an option field. json.spi's decode_reads_arrays_of_records passes only because its element is all scalars. x worked around it in kit/src/k3s_manifest, so nothing is blocked. MINIMAL SAMPLE (x's candidate): `:== r = { a : option string }`, `:== w = { xs : array_base r }`, `decode \"{\\\"xs\\\":[{\\\"a\\\":\\\"x\\\"}]}\" : w`. DEFINITION OF DONE: a regression sample with an array of a record holding a union field, created at runtime size, set and read back, agrees with C on Rust (exit code + stdout); the existing array-create rows are unchanged. FIX OPTIONS: (a) a union with at least one payload-free case gets `impl Default` returning that case (option's None), which is sound because array create's slots are overwritten before any read on every backend that matches C; (b) emit array create without Default (Vec::with_capacity, then a push of the element's zero per slot, from the same zero expressions the other backends use). (a) is the smaller change and also fixes nested heaps. TYPEFEATURESET: the default case is chosen by a typed rule over the union's case list (first payload-free case, else every field defaultable), never by a name such as 'None'. NEXT STEP: reproduce with the minimal sample on the installed compiler (one Rust compile + rustc), then read codegenRust's Default emission to apply (a).")
inl note_of_rust_union_default_array_create_2 () = Note ("RUST-UNION-DEFAULT-ARRAY-CREATE", 2u32, "2026-11-01T21:22Z", "compiler", "11-01 17:22 compiler: REPRODUCED AND ROOT-CAUSED. Sample samples/rust_union_default_array_create (landed unstaged): union opt = Nothing | Just : string; `create n` of array (string * opt * bool), set both slots, read slot 0. Expected 7. On node t1101 with the installed pack15a: C exits 7; Rust fails with E0599 on `vec![<(Rc<str>, US0, bool)>::default(); v0 as usize]`. ROOT CAUSE: the union DOES get a Default body (rust_union_default uses the first case, a payload-free Nothing), but the pass that keeps only reached impls (codegenRust's tail, regex `(\\w+)>+::default\\(\\)` plus reach_defaults) only sees `<Name>::default()`. For a tuple element `<(Rc<str>, US0, bool)>::default()` the character before '>' is ')', so nothing is reached and US0's impl is dropped. So x's fix options (Vec::with_capacity, or deriving Default only where possible) are not needed: the impl already exists. FIX: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\RUST-UNION-DEFAULT-ARRAY-CREATE\\1-reach-defaults-inside-tuples.kitdo, 2 replacements. The regex captures the whole balanced type inside <...>::default() (.NET balancing groups), and every identifier inside it that names a default impl is reached. Unit-checked on the 3 real shapes: the tuple gives '(Rc<str>, US0, bool)', '<US1>::default()' gives 'US1', '<Vec<UH2>>::default()' gives 'Vec<UH2>'. Residual effect: only programs that failed rustc gain impl blocks; a program that compiled already had every reached name. PROOF RUNNING: node job job-1793568095969-compiler-rdef (live core + this program; Rust exit must be 7). It joins the pack after pack15b (whose predict already started), with the sample's C/Rust rows as its gate.")
inl note_of_rust_union_default_array_create_3 () = Note ("RUST-UNION-DEFAULT-ARRAY-CREATE", 3u32, "2026-11-01T21:36Z", "compiler", "11-01 17:32 compiler: PROVEN. Node job job-1793568095969-compiler-rdef (live core F6F6879566C5A830 + the reach-defaults program; host 98D282B5): samples/rust_union_default_array_create compiles to Rust, the output now carries 'impl Default for US0', and the exe exits 7 = the C oracle (installed: E0599). It rides the pack after pack15b; DONE when that pack's suite shows the sample's Rust row agreeing with C, with no other Rust residual changed except programs that previously failed rustc. x-dumps can then drop the k3s_manifest workaround.")
inl note_of_rust_union_default_array_create_4 () = Note ("RUST-UNION-DEFAULT-ARRAY-CREATE", 4u32, "2026-11-01T23:18Z", "compiler", "11-01 19:19 compiler: holds on the pack15c candidate (node job-1793574178127, the 9-program stack): the repro's Rust exe exits 7 = C.")
inl note_of_rust_union_default_array_create_5 () = Note ("RUST-UNION-DEFAULT-ARRAY-CREATE", 5u32, "2026-11-03T00:51Z", "compiler", "11-02 20:5x compiler: DONE. The reach-defaults fix is live (installed since pack15c). Native check on node t1101 with the installed compiler: samples/rust_union_default_array_create emits impl Default for US0, the Rust exe exits 7 and the C exe exits 7 (oracle agrees). The node examples runs today (1981 rows, Rust/C/Zig/Gleam) compile both rows ok. x-dumps can drop the k3s_manifest workaround.")
inl note_of_fiscal_validator_false_green_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-VALIDATOR-FALSE-GREEN", 1u32, "2026-11-01T21:50Z", "fiscal", "Found by fiscal 2026-11-01 17:5x. scripts/validate-example.ps1 reports \"validation messages 0\" when the SCHEMA FAILS TO LOAD: XmlSchemaSet.Add / Compile throw (non-terminating in the script), the set stays empty or partial, and validating against it reports nothing. A FALSE GREEN in the family gate.\nProven instances: (1) generated_nfe_evento_conf_recebto_v1_00 on Windows: Add throws \"The simpleType nfe:TCOrgaoIBGE has already been declared\" (leiauteConfRecebto_v1.00.xsd declares it with 29 enumeration values AND includes tiposBasico_v1.03.xsd, which declares it with 30, adding 92). The row prints \"validation messages 0; signature pending 0\" (its siblings print pending 1), so it never validated. CI windows-2025 run 41314140694 shows the same exception; check whether ubuntu loads it. (2) PT SAF-T (saftpt1.04_01.xsd) is XSD 1.1: 19 xs:assert plus xs:all with maxOccurs > 1. It fails to load and also prints 0 messages, so it must not be added to family-gates under the current script.\nFIX: (a) collect Add/Compile exceptions into the validation messages (\"schema: <message>\"); (b) check that the compiled set declares the document's root element as a global element, else a message (catches empty or partial sets without turning on warnings, which would flag lax xs:any). (c) In the SAME change, resolve conf_recebto, or CI goes red: a duplicate-tolerant load through a custom XmlResolver that serves the included file with the local duplicate dropped, logged as \"schema repair: dropped local TCOrgaoIBGE (subset of tiposBasico_v1.03, which adds 92)\". Or pin a decision on which definition the oracle uses. (d) SAF-T: an XSD 1.1 validator, or keep it out of family-gates and say why in examples.tsv.\nDONE: no row can print 0 messages without a loaded schema that declares its root; conf_recebto validates with a logged repair; CI examples.tsv shows it.")
inl note_of_fiscal_validator_false_green_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-VALIDATOR-FALSE-GREEN", 2u32, "2026-11-01T22:10Z", "fiscal", "fiscal 11-01 18:1x: FIXED in scripts/validate-example.ps1 (unstaged). (a) Add/Compile exceptions are validation messages (\"schema: ...\"). (b) Unconditional root check: no row reports 0 unless a loaded set declares the document root as a global element; this caught a second false-green path during the fix (a failed repair left the set null). (c) Duplicate-tolerant load: on \"has already been declared\", the schema folder is copied to a temp dir; in the main schema's include/import closure only, a LOCAL declaration is dropped from a file that also includes a file declaring the same name (the included one wins), logged as a non-counted \"schema repair:\" line, then the load is retried (at most 8 rounds). Output format for build.ps1 is unchanged (document line + xN: lines). PROOF on CI run 41314140694's published samples, the real family-gates.ps1: 40 rows, 0 bad, 1 repair (\"dropped local TCOrgaoIBGE from leiauteConfRecebto_v1.00.xsd, also declared in tiposBasico_v1.03.xsd\"), 0 schema errors. So conf_recebto was the only false green, and it now validates (signature pending 1, like its siblings). SAF-T and an HU NAV row without preloads now report their schema errors instead of 0. Close when CI's examples.tsv shows the same.")
inl note_of_fiscal_validator_false_green_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-VALIDATOR-FALSE-GREEN", 3u32, "2026-11-02T03:01Z", "fiscal", "fiscal 11-02: DONE. The user committed the fix in c8830d7; CI run 41366612730 is green on ubuntu-24.04 AND windows-2025, and examples.tsv on both OSes has 40 rows, 0 failing. generated_nfe_evento_conf_recebto_v1_00 now really validates (messages 0, signature pending 1, like its siblings; the logged duplicate repair) on Windows too, where it was a false green before. No row can print 0 without a loaded schema that declares its root.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_1 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 1u32, "2026-11-01T22:00Z", "main", "main 18:0x: main owns lib_land_window; x owns cells_land_window and copies the pattern. Design: (1) remote.ps1 sync spiral -Mirror land-<label> with the drafts applied; (2) run signatures/consumers/document_test/type_probe there as one node job; (3) on green, the box copies drafts under a short tree-write window, guarded by base hashes (unchanged since the proof) plus a digest equality check of mirror vs drafts; (4) undo as today. DoD: one lib land and one Cells land each finish while a heavy-build window is held on the box, with the box copy step under 1 min. Typefeatureset: LandStep GADT indexed by where it runs (Mirror | Box), so a compile step can't type-check as a box step.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_2 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 2u32, "2026-11-02T00:35Z", "main", "main 20:4x FIRST REAL USE, by x without a tool change: at 20:31 x landed lib/spiral/package.spiproj plus three apps/cells/spi files as node/europa-proven, hash-guarded copies under a tree-write window, with no box compile, while TRAIN8 held the heavy window. That's this item's pattern done by hand. The hazard it exposes: the copy landed INTO a running train's live tree, so the off-box land needs a 'no running train reads this tree' guard (or trains snapshot, kit's lesson). DoD addition: lib_land_window/cells_land_window refuse a copy while a kit job labelled *train* reads the target tree, unless the train is snapshot-pinned.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_3 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 3u32, "2026-11-02T05:03Z", "x", "2026-11-02 01:03 x: EUROPA GATES ARE VOID UNTIL PACK15C IS INSTALLED THERE. x-erl-map2 ran an A/A on erlang_map.spi: the UNCHANGED base fails 0/3 with gleam 'error: Unknown module ... import gary' in /root/.cache/spiral-bin/cells-gleam-warm/*/src/main.gleam, whose generated gleam.toml has no gary (the box's warm gleam.toml has gary = '>=1.1.0 and <2.0.0'). Europa's single-flight core is 7B234DAC2373D38F (11-01 18:08); the box and node are on 83CEDAA9DDED49EB (pack15c, installed 00:32). So the stale compiler emits code the current lib needs but doesn't declare the dep. Until a pack install includes Europa, any Europa lib gate red or green is VOID, which affects A6 (Europa for light gates). Proof launchers should pin -RequireCore on Europa too: the node guard would have refused this run instead of reporting fake reds.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_4 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 4u32, "2026-11-02T05:10Z", "main", "main 00:5x EUROPA pack15c BUILT FROM SOURCE (x reported europa VOID: old core 7B234DAC emits a gary import without adding gary to the warm gleam.toml; A/A erlang_map 0/3). Copied box live sources (core 55C243C7A93BFFC8, host B30F5F9B54F505A3 = pack15c candidate) into /home/remote/git/spiral/apps/compiler, plus box HEAD scripts/build.ps1 (europa's 504e1e07 copy threw at :36 '$systemRuntimes.Count' with no system dotnet; fixed upstream since). kit job job-1793596097804-main-pack15c-linux-build 87.9 s exit 0 -> linux-x64 R2R host E6BF72DDC400CF65 core 040B4C44B4AA20FF (cannot equal box win-x64 hashes; compare by source hash). --help lists --plan-ir + Pascal. Backups: /root/.cache/spiral-bin/compiler-installs/pack15c-src-before/ (old sources, single-flight-bin, scripts-build.ps1). No Cells domain stamp existed. Next: x A/A on erlang_map; full europa spiral sync when x is off europa; remote.ps1 europa status should report the Linux compiler (today it prints 'node compiler (missing)' for europa: Windows paths).")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_5 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 5u32, "2026-11-02T06:43Z", "main", "main 02:4x pack15c + pack15d ROLLED TO ALL THREE MACHINES. pack15c: box 00:29 (host 92820117717425C0 core 83CEDAA9DDED49EB), node 00:33 (folder CAE7CB4C16DA84FD), europa source build 00:5x (linux host E6BF72DD core 040B4C44). The first pack15c try (22:02-00:2x) never ran: install-when-clear had no -Programs; compiler added the pass-through (unstaged). pack15d (3 programs: CELLS-SERVER-EXIT-TAIL, BACKEND-PRIMITIVE-PARITY 3, GLEAM-JS-TARGET-GAPS 4): box 02:36 after TRAIN9 (host 9489144496A935E6 core F16F6B2032F81F2D, undo compiler-installs\\pack15d-20261102-023636), node folder F014BE54FA782B8E, europa source build from B161EDA4/57A3FBAF -> linux core CB8092C4FEE7A01C host 86BA2A7548F08A69. Europa gates count again (x A/A erlang_map 3/3, kit attest green). Europa spiral synced to b926468c. Chain script: drafts\\spiral\\LIB-RESHAPE\\pack15d-chain.ps1 (install -> digest check -> node-ship -> europa backup+copy+kit job build) is the reusable shape for future packs.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_6 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 6u32, "2026-11-02T12:24Z", "x", "2026-11-02 08:24 x: GROOM: progress 0 -> 60, Planned -> Active. The pattern is PROVEN and in daily use. 11-01 20:31: C3, C4 and the lib registration. 11-02: erlang_map (x-lib-land4), the map_keys slice (x-lib-keys2, three lib files), and three x sim landings. Each was gated on a node mirror by lib_land_window -Apply on exact base hashes, then landed as a hash-guarded copy in a tree-write window with no box compile, while TRAIN9 and TRAIN10 held heavy-build. What a node lib-land mirror needs, learned today (lands 1-3 failed on these, not on the draft): (1) the node's kit is C:\\home\\bin\\kit.exe, so lib_land_window.ps1 now falls back to kit on PATH (unstaged); (2) -Repos 'spiral,dice,alphabet', because document_test reads ../dice and ../alphabet; (3) a built workspace\\target\\release\\spiral.exe staged into the mirror for the export-equality test. LEFT: one generic verb that does sync, gate and guarded copy, instead of today's session-local launcher scripts; that verb is kit's, per spiral-first-tooling. cells_land_window gets the same three mirror needs.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_7 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 7u32, "2026-11-02T14:29Z", "main", "main 11-02: parent epic is GATE-HEALS-1101; recorded here instead of as a dep, because a dep on an unfinished parent epic hid this item from 'agile next' (backlog-wide sweep: 67 open items depended on an unfinished Epic).")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_8 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 8u32, "2026-11-02T14:50Z", "x", "2026-11-02 10:50 x: lib_land_window.ps1 no longer reads a stored baseline from the repo (the user had asked for days to rework what writes files like apps/cells/spi/lib_consumer_signatures.tsv). That untracked TSV was a 10-30 snapshot that nothing regenerated, and 6 of its 14 rows were STALE: console read_to_end, sm' utf8_get_bytes and length, file_system try_append_all_text and create_dir_all, and listm' try_find_ are no longer used by apps/spiral. The signatures step now DERIVES its set on every land: names the consumer package's .spi reference as <stem>::name or <stem>.name, bare operators, and bare names of a module opened with open or :<. It compares header lines in the undo copy (before) with the landed file (after). Nothing is written into the repo. Tests on scratch copies: unchanged lib gives '59 consumer-used signatures unchanged' (against 14 stored); an edited (</>) header gives drift; edited to_lower plus (</>) gives 2 drifts. -SignatureFile is removed. The TSV is archived (kit archive 20261102-104925), not deleted.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_9 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 9u32, "2026-11-02T15:02Z", "x", "2026-11-02 11:02 x: STAR-EXCHANGE GROOM. Mirror rules from the exchange. One Cells gate per mirror at a time (fiscal n4: concurrent gates share %TEMP%\\spiral_cells and the mirror lib, giving os error 3 and locked files). Point a staged lib with SPIRAL_CELLS_LIB instead of swapping files in a live lib. Verify the mirror before trusting a red: remote.ps1 node verify <lane> -Mirror <m> <paths> (exit 6 = MIRROR-STALE; fiscal n5, compiler n3, after a newly landed ///> target, a stale Cells aborted on pascal). Until TRAIN11 is on the node, a node kit job dying at ~2 s is the breakaway bug (kit n1, compiler n7), not the draft: restart it with remote.ps1 laptop job start.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_10 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 10u32, "2026-11-03T16:09Z", "main", "main 11-03 12:4x BOX HALF DONE (unstaged, spiral apps/cells/spi/lib_land_window.ps1, +16 lines, parses): new -ProvenLog <file>. The box step becomes a copy that trusts a remote close, but only against hashes: the log must contain 'LANDED and closed green' AND a '<lib file> <hash12>' line for EVERY draft whose hash12 equals the draft source's sha256 prefix; otherwise it throws before anything is written. The usual base-hash guards, live-reader wait, tree-write window and undo copy all still apply; the box-side baseline type_probe and the whole close stage are skipped, and it prints 'LANDED from a proven close'. Dry-run proof: a log with the right hash -> 'close proven ... for 1 drafts'; a wrong hash -> 'does not prove process.spi at A3BAFCF670B8'. REMOTE HALF (no code needed, the script already takes -Lib): on the node, copy spiral to C:\\home\\remote\\<lane>-land\\spiral (robocopy /XD target _build build .git deps + a deps junction), then run that copy's apps/cells/spi/lib_land_window.ps1 -Draft ... -BaseHash ... -Lib <copy>\\lib\\spiral -Apply *> <log>; fetch the log and run the box with -ProvenLog <log>. WHY (11-03 evidence): the box close runs against the LIVE lib, so other lanes' unlanded WIP (tibia's file_system block) undid kit's and main's lands, and close stages queued behind box CPU. Progress 60 -> 75; NEXT: one real land through the two-step path.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_11 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 11u32, "2026-11-03T16:46Z", "main", "main 11-03 12:5x FIRST REMOTE CLOSE RUNS (process.spi F# removal, node mirror C:\\home\\remote\\main-land\\spiral; robocopy /XD target _build build node_modules .git deps + junctions spiral\\deps and apps\\cells\\deps; kit from C:\\home\\bin on PATH; the box's patched lib_land_window copied in). Tool fixes found by it, applied (unstaged): -PrivateLib (skip the live-reader wait when -Lib is a private copy; lanes' notebooks on the node read the real lib) and the signature check ignoring names the consumer defines itself (apps/spiral's own main flagged 'process.spi main changed'). RESULT: signatures ok (2 unchanged), consumers compile, type_probe PASS 18, respell_drift 0, but document_test 19/22, and the A/A run (the unmodified live file as the 'draft') ALSO gives 19/22, so 3 document tests fail from the mirror environment, not the change. NEXT: name those 3 (mix test output in the mirror) and give the mirror what they read; until then the remote close cannot produce a green ProvenLog. The process land went through the box path meanwhile.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_12 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 12u32, "2026-11-03T16:53Z", "main", "main 11-03 13:0x THE 3 NAMED: on a node mirror, document_test's dice and alphabet tests read SIBLING repos relative to the spiral root (c:/home/remote/<m>/dice/lib/dice.spi, .../alphabet/apps/documents/documents.spi: File.Error not found): 'dice's Spiral sources ... write back byte for byte', 'the export equals spiral export on the dice and alphabet notebooks', 'alphabet: documents ... round-trips'. FIX for the remote half: next to the mirror's spiral folder, add junctions dice -> C:\\home\\git\\dice and alphabet -> C:\\home\\git\\alphabet (read-only use). With that the mirror's close should be 22/22 and produce a green ProvenLog.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_13 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 13u32, "2026-11-03T16:58Z", "main", "main 11-03 13:1x WITH dice+alphabet sibling junctions the mirror's document_test is 21/22 (was 19/22; siblings verified intact after the mirror cleanup). The last one, 'the export equals spiral export on the dice and alphabet notebooks', runs the spiral CLI from workspace/target, which the mirror's robocopy excludes: add a junction <mirror>\\workspace\\target -> C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\workspace\\target. ALSO (unstaged, same script): Restore-Undo now skips a file whose live hash differs from what this land wrote (prints 'SKIP restore ... another writer changed it'). Root cause it guards against, 11-03: kit's LIB-KEBAB-CASE land (window from 10:30) restored its 10:30 sm' snapshot at ~10:42 after a failed close and erased x's 10:38 sm'.char_code Gleam arm; two tree-write windows were held at once (kit told).")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_14 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 14u32, "2026-11-03T17:06Z", "main", "main 11-03 13:2x LANDS NOW EXCLUDE EACH OTHER (unstaged, lib_land_window.ps1), per kit's root cause: kit tree windows guard the --label as a PATH, and the script passed the land name, so lib lands never excluded each other (4 tree-writes held together 10:30-10:45; that overlap plus a blind undo erased x's sm'.char_code Gleam arm, re-landed by x as 343FA552). Now: --label <rooted lib path> --wait <MaxWaitMin>, the land name on its own 'land <Label>' log line, and no land without a granted window. kit's side (TRAIN16): requests with a non-path tree label are refused.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_15 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 15u32, "2026-11-03T18:02Z", "main", "main 11-03 14:0x END-TO-END RESULT. The remote half now closes GREEN on the node (mirror with the box's exact lib via tar + junctions deps, apps\\cells\\deps, workspace\\target, ..\\dice, ..\\alphabet): document_test 22/22, type_probe 18, drift 0, and it prints 'lib digest <16 hex>' (new). The box half (-ProvenLog) now also requires that digest to equal the box lib with the drafts applied, and it REFUSED twice, correctly: the box lib moved during each ~10 min remote close (13:33 sm', then 13:54 backend + 14:01 pickler; pickler is module 21 and process 72, so even an order-scoped digest would have expired). So: the mechanism is sound and safe, but at today's lib churn (a land every few minutes) a whole-lib proof expires before the box can use it. NEXT DESIGN: hold the lib's tree-write window across the remote close (now that labels really exclude, a short hold freezes the lib), or have the box half re-run only the fast checks (signatures, consumers, type_probe ~2 min) and trust only the remote document_test (~5 min). Progress stays 75.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_16 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 16u32, "2026-11-03T18:44Z", "main", "main 11-03 14:5x FIRST REAL TWO-STEP LAND, GREEN (identity land of process.spi, undo 20261103-143955). Fallback added (unstaged): when the proof's lib digest no longer matches (the lib moved during the remote close), the box no longer refuses; it reruns the FAST checks on the real box lib (signatures, consumers, type_probe, respell_drift) and takes only document_test from the proof (prints 'taken from <log> : Result: 22 passed'). An exact digest match still means copy-only. Timing: window granted ~8 min into the live-reader wait (kit's count_scan notebook); the box-side checks then took about 1 min, versus about 6 min with the box running document_test. So the heavy part now runs off box. LEFT: package the node half as a documented recipe in the item (mirror + junctions dice/alphabet/deps/apps\\cells\\deps/workspace\\target + box lib tar), and use it for real drafts. Progress 75 -> 90.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_17 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 17u32, "2026-11-03T18:46Z", "main", "main 11-03 14:5x RECIPE (two-step lib land; any lane). NODE HALF: (1) tar the box lib: tar -cf <t>.tar -C C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\lib spiral; scp it, the draft(s) and the box's apps/cells/spi/lib_land_window.ps1 to the node's C:\\home\\remote-queue\\. (2) On the node (remote.ps1 node run -Script): PATH += C:\\home\\bin (kit); root C:\\home\\remote\\<lane>-proven; robocopy C:\\home\\git\\spiral <root>\\spiral /E /XD target _build build node_modules .git deps; junctions <root>\\spiral\\deps, <root>\\spiral\\apps\\cells\\deps and <root>\\spiral\\workspace\\target to the node's real ones, plus <root>\\dice and <root>\\alphabet (document_test reads those siblings); replace <root>\\spiral\\lib\\spiral with the tar; copy the uploaded lib_land_window.ps1 over the mirror's. (3) cd <root>\\spiral\\apps\\cells\\spi; pwsh -File lib_land_window.ps1 -Draft <lib file>=<draft> -Label <ITEM>-remote -BaseHash <box base> -Lib <root>\\spiral\\lib\\spiral -PrivateLib -Apply *> <log>; then remove <root> (pwsh 7.6 deletes the junctions without following). BOX HALF: fetch <log>; pwsh -File lib_land_window.ps1 -Draft ... -BaseHash ... -ProvenLog <log> -Apply. An exact lib-digest match means copy-only; a moved lib means the fast checks rerun here and only document_test comes from the proof. Both halves hold a tree-write window labelled with the lib path.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_18 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 18u32, "2026-11-03T19:19Z", "main", "main 11-03 15:2x cells_land_window.ps1 had the same two defects, fixed (unstaged, +15/-5, parses): (1) its tree-write window used the land NAME as label, so Cells lands never excluded each other; now --label <rooted apps/cells path> --wait <Minutes>, the name on a 'land <Label>' line, and no land without a granted window; (2) its undo snapshot was taken BEFORE the window was granted (a land slipping in during the wait would be overwritten on failure) and its restore was blind; now the snapshot is taken after the grant and Restore-Undo skips any file whose hash differs from what this land wrote. The off-box close for Cells lands (mix test on a mirror) is the remaining part of this item.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_19 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 19u32, "2026-11-03T19:53Z", "main", "main 11-03 15:5x AUDIT of today's direct lib writes (fiscal self-reported): event_log (pulled, re-landing through lib_land_window), plus money, ledger, durable_file (new) and group_part edits in xml.spi / xsd_emit.spi left live for tree consistency with fiscal's unstaged dependents. Their skipped close was completed after the fact: type_probe on the box under pack27 PASS 5/5 (money 2, ledger 4, durable_file 3, xml 15, xsd_emit 30 tests typed, 0 errors), document_test 22/22 already ran with them live (13:02 process land), fiscal's europa --check + Rust runs exit 0. So no unproven code stays in the live lib.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_20 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 20u32, "2026-11-03T20:29Z", "main", "main 11-03 16:2x BUG FOUND BY fiscal, FIXED AND PROVEN: my Restore-Undo guard's hashtable was named $landed, the same name as the original new-file branch's local ($landed = Join-Path ...), so a draft list with a NEW file before an EXISTING one turned the table into a string and the undo crashed halfway (fiscal's 15:46 land left package.spiproj registering a missing module; fiscal repaired it by hand). Renamed to $landedHash (lines 100/105/121). PROOF on a scratch lib copy (-Lib scratch -PrivateLib -UndoRoot scratch), draft order new-then-existing, close forced to fail at respell_drift: 'CLOSE FAILED: undoing' -> 'RESTORED', the new file gone, markup.spi back to its original C81A233342541DBF.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_21 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 21u32, "2026-11-04T06:20Z", "main", "11-04 01:0x main: FALSE LIVE READER fixed (found by x: its CELLS-MANIFEST-PATH land waited at L89 on main's node oracle run). Get-LiveReaders matched any command line containing run_notebook.ps1, including remote.ps1 <machine> run \"... run_notebook.ps1 ...\" processes that execute on the node or europa against the remote copy and read nothing in the box lib. The ancestor walk now treats a process whose command line runs remote.ps1 <machine> run as not a box reader, beside the existing lib_land_window and scratch -Lib skips (unstaged, spiral apps/cells/spi/lib_land_window.ps1; parse clean; pattern checked on node-run, plain run_notebook and remote sync command lines: only the first matches). It matters more now that heavy gates move off the box (user 11-04: node first, box last): every remote gate would otherwise block every box land.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_22 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 22u32, "2026-11-04T11:07Z", "main", "11-04 07:2x main: the Cells half of the remainder is IMPLEMENTED, not yet proven (unstaged, spiral apps/cells/spi/cells_land_window.ps1; parses; pre-change copy in %TEMP%\\cells_land_window.before-proven-log.ps1). A new -ProvenLog <log> mirrors lib_land_window's two-step close. Run the same script on a node mirror (-Cells <mirror>/apps/cells): it applies the applier and runs the full mix tests there, then prints each landed file's hash12 and 'LANDED and closed green'. On the box, after applying, if that log is green AND every landed file's box hash equals the proof's (same base + same applier = same bytes), the box skips mix and only copies under its window (\"close proven by\"). Otherwise it says why and runs the tests itself, so it stays fail-safe. NEXT: the first real Cells land through it is the proof; then this item can close.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_23 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 23u32, "2026-11-04T12:22Z", "main", "11-04 08:3x main SECOND REAL TWO-STEP LIB LAND, first for a NEW file (fin_vector.spi, LIB-VEC-FIN). NODE HALF GREEN in about 13 min, following the n17 recipe with one change: the tree comes from the main-kernel mirror (already synced to the box, including today's Cells test edits), not from the node's own clone, with a separate root C:\\home\\remote\\main-proven so no sync can prune it mid-run. Box lib tar 81 MB. Result: spiral.spi compiles, document_test 22 passed, type_probe pass (4 tests typed, 0 errors), respell drift 0, fin_vector.spi 0AA287AF4004, lib digest C62D5C26E9CAEEA7, window released, root removed. BOX HALF: lib_land_window -ProvenLog -Apply queued behind another lane's lib window (GRANULAR-SPLIT-XPATH-EVAL, full box close since 07:58), PENDING. The script is reusable: main's scratchpad node-fin-land.ps1 (parameterize the draft list and it becomes the recipe).")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_24 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 24u32, "2026-11-04T12:26Z", "main", "11-04 08:2x main BOX HALF GREEN for fin_vector.spi: queued ~8 min behind another lane's lib window, then the moved-lib path (fast checks on the box, document_test from the proof). End to end about 25 min, with the box doing only the fast checks. Second two-step land green, first for a NEW file (BaseHash new works through both halves). The Cells half (cells_land_window -ProvenLog, n22) is still unproven by a real Cells land.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_25 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 25u32, "2026-11-04T14:43Z", "main", "11-04 10:4x main THIRD two-step lib land, and the FIRST COPY-ONLY one: sized_array.spi (WGSL test). The box lib did not move between the node proof (lib digest C6181DE5) and the box half, so lib_land_window printed \"LANDED from a proven close\": the box held its tree-write window only to copy one file, with no compile and no checks. Every case is now seen: exact digest -> copy-only; moved lib -> fast checks only (fin_vector, sized_array #2); a live reader -> refused, then landed on retry. Only the Cells half (cells_land_window -ProvenLog) still lacks a real land.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_26 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 26u32, "2026-11-04T15:21Z", "main", "11-04 11:2x main LIVE-READER FALSE POSITIVE FIXED (x's report: its land waited 35+ min behind notebooks running on another session's PRIVATE lib copy). lib_land_window's Get-LiveReaders now also exempts a reader whose --path arguments ALL lie under some \\lib\\spiral\\ root other than the live $Lib. Notebooks under apps/ (which read the live lib) and live-lib notebooks still block. Checked against the box's live process table: two spiral.notebook readers on a private lib copy are now exempt, and a lib_gate -Lib scratch stays exempt via the existing ancestor rule.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_27 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 27u32, "2026-11-05T02:20Z", "x", "2026-11-04 22:20 x: ASK from the star exchange (main takes it): on a document_test failure, print the failing FILE and its first differing line, not only the test name. 11-04: x-next6's land closed red with only 'the spiral library .spi files load as notebooks' visible; the cause (a missing blank line in erlang_text.spi) needed a separate mix run of parse_spi -> livemd -> to_spi_tested per draft.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_28 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 28u32, "2026-11-05T04:46Z", "main", "11-05 00:46 main: x's n27 ask is DONE under LIB-LAND-FAILURE-DIAGNOSTICS: lib_land_window round-trips every draft before writing (dry runs too) and prints file:line with both lines, and document_test's full log stays in the undo dir. What remains here is unchanged: the Cells half (cells_land_window -ProvenLog) needs one real Cells land (x).")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_29 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 29u32, "2026-11-05T06:31Z", "main", "11-05 02:31 main RECIPE UPDATE from tonight's two-step land of file_system.spi (LIB-WORKSPACE-ROOT-DEPS): `remote.ps1 node sync spiral -Mirror <lane>-proven` replaces the recipe's robocopy and deps junctions (MIRROR-DEPS-OK), and the box lib comes with the sync (no tar needed). Two gaps the mirror does NOT cover, each costing one red close: (1) node kit jobs have no kit on PATH, so the job script must set $env:PATH = \"C:\\home\\bin;$env:PATH\" before lib_land_window (Get-Command kit failed at line 19); (2) document_test's \"export equals spiral export\" case needs <mirror>\\spiral\\workspace\\target\\release\\spiral.exe, so junction <mirror>\\spiral\\workspace\\target to C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\workspace\\target (or the case flunks with \"spiral.exe is missing\"). Both are environment, not draft, failures; the diagnostics (document_test.log in the undo dir) named the second one directly. Mirror cleanup: unlink junctions before Remove-Item (scratch rm-mirror.ps1: ErrorActionPreference Stop, Split-Path guard, -CheckOnly).")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_30 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 30u32, "2026-11-05T06:42Z", "main", "11-05 02:42 main FOURTH real two-step lib land, GREEN end to end (file_system.spi, LIB-WORKSPACE-ROOT-DEPS): node half on a -Mirror main-proven copy (after the two setup fixes in the previous note: kit on PATH, workspace\\target junction), box half via -ProvenLog in ~5 min with only the fast checks on the box (the lib had moved, so it was not copy-only). The box never ran document_test or a notebook gate.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_31 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 31u32, "2026-11-05T06:46Z", "x", "2026-11-05 02:46 x (Cells owner): cells_land_window.ps1 FIXED (live, unstaged), found while landing kit's CELLS-BUILD-ONLY. (1) New files: it backed up every -Files entry before applying, so a draft that ADDS a file threw at the backup. A missing file is now recorded in created, and Restore-Undo deletes it on a red close (unless another writer changed it, the same guard as restores). (2) Lock leak: that backup ran BEFORE the try whose finally releases the kit window, so any throw there left a 30-minute tree-write lock held (it happened twice tonight; both released by id). The backup now runs inside the try. Proof on a scratch Cells root with an applier that changes a.ex, adds b.ex, then exits 1: a.ex restored, b.ex removed, no window held. CELLS-BUILD-ONLY itself landed 30/30 (undo cells-20261105-024019).")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_32 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 32u32, "2026-11-05T08:35Z", "x", "2026-11-05 04:35 x (Cells owner): landed compiler's CELLS-GATE-PINNED-COMPILER (cells window, 65/65, undo cells-20261105-042827). A gated notebook run (mix spiral.notebook --gate) now pins one compiler copy for the whole gate (CompilerDaemon.gate_pin: a stamp-keyed copy under %TEMP%\\\\spiral-cells-gate-pins, passed as an optional 8th request field); a pin is shared and pruned after 24 h unused, so nothing leaks. The notebook report shows compiler.pin and compiler.stamp. This ends the mid-gate compiler swap that turned x-next7b red (pack36 -> pack38 between cells), and lets compiler's install-pack stop waiting on gated runs. Also landed tonight: kit's CELLS-BUILD-ONLY and CELLS-BUILD-ONLY-2 (run_notebook --build-only), and the cells_land_window fix (new files, lock release).")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_33 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 33u32, "2026-11-05T09:40Z", "main", "11-05 05:40 main x's ask: lib_land_window's tree-write request waited on kit's default RAM floor (box free 1.8-3.4 GB tonight; x-next8's land waited ~20 min, x-next7c's 30+). Now -MinFreeMb (default 1200 MB: the close needs ~1 GB for mix test + type_probe) is passed as --min-free-mb. Probe: granted in 2 ms at 2578 MB free. cells_land_window (x's) can take the same two lines.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_34 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 34u32, "2026-11-05T19:45Z", "main", "main 11-05 15:4x CHECK: the Cells -ProvenLog path (n of 11-04 07:2x) is still unproven by a real land. x ran 11 Cells lands since then (undo dirs cells-20261104-173911 .. cells-20261105-103334), none with -ProvenLog: no 'close proven by' line in any lane transcript. Asked x (Cells owner) to route the next real Cells land through it (node mirror run, then box -ProvenLog). Closes at 100 on the first 'close proven by' line or a fail-safe fallback with a named reason.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_35 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 35u32, "2026-11-05T20:22Z", "x", "2026-11-05 16:2x x: FIRST ATTEMPT at the off-box close found its own gap. cells_land_window ran on the node mirror and stopped at the window request: 'The term C:\\Users\\alias\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\bin\\kit.exe is not recognized'. Both land windows hard-code kit at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\bin\\kit.exe (the box layout); the node's kit is C:\\home\\bin\\kit.exe. Nothing was applied (mirror cells.ex still 85A6E572FE33). FIX added to this Cells land (one line each, same shape): cells_land_window.ps1 CD538635E632 -> D3D56655D014 and lib_land_window.ps1 A0AB89C68628 -> F2AFF7AB3437. They keep the box path and fall back to 'kit' on PATH when that file is absent ('if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $kit)) { $kit = (Get-Command kit -ErrorAction Stop).Source }'). The land now covers 4 files (cells.ex, cells_test.exs, both windows). RERUN job-1793910085690 x-cellsorder2 uses the FIXED window from the stage with C:\\home\\bin on PATH, same plan and pass rule as n2.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_36 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 36u32, "2026-11-05T21:15Z", "x", "2026-11-05 17:1x x: FIRST REAL TWO-STEP CLOSE, Cells land SIM-EVENTS-MODULE-CLASH (4 files). Node: cells_land_window on mirror xcellsorder (job-1793910085690), cells_test.exs 39 passed, closed green. Box: -ProvenLog <that log> -> 'close proven by ... for 4 files: the box result equals the proof byte for byte', closed green, no box mix (undo cells-20261105-171144). The gap found on the first try is fixed in the same land: both windows fall back to kit on PATH (the node keeps kit at C:\\home\\bin\\kit.exe); the node job must put C:\\home\\bin on PATH.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_37 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 37u32, "2026-11-05T21:22Z", "main", "main 11-05 17:2x CLOSE (evidence from x, the Cells owner): the Cells two-step close is PROVEN by a real land, SIM-EVENTS-MODULE-CLASH (4 files). Node proof job-1793910085690 on mirror xcellsorder: cells_test.exs 39 passed, closed green. The box land with -ProvenLog printed 'close proven by ...cells-window-node.log for 4 files: the box result equals the proof byte for byte' and closed green WITHOUT running mix on the box (undo cells-20261105-171144). Gap found and fixed in the same land: cells_land_window.ps1 and lib_land_window.ps1 hard-coded kit at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\bin\\kit.exe, but the node's kit is C:\\home\\bin\\kit.exe; both now fall back to kit on PATH, so a node job must put C:\\home\\bin on PATH. Both halves done: lib (two-step since 11-03, -MinFreeMb 11-05) and Cells. DoD met: a landing needs only a base-hash-guarded box copy, not a box compile.")
inl note_of_mirror_freshness_guard_1 () = Note ("MIRROR-FRESHNESS-GUARD", 1u32, "2026-11-01T22:00Z", "main", "main 18:0x: main owns remote.ps1. Parts: (1) sync retries on a missing REMOTE-SYNC-OK, up to 3 times, then fails loudly; (2) a 'remote.ps1 <m> verify <repo> -Mirror <m> -Paths ...' verb printing box vs mirror digests per path (route check style, exit 6 on mismatch); (3) an optional -Include for gitignored input dirs. DoD: a deliberately stale mirror file makes the proof refuse to start, in seconds.")
inl note_of_mirror_freshness_guard_2 () = Note ("MIRROR-FRESHNESS-GUARD", 2u32, "2026-11-01T22:54Z", "main", "main 19:0x PART 1 DONE (unstaged remote.ps1): sync now retries up to 2 times on ANY nonzero remote exit (it used to retry only exit 7, a digest mismatch), naming the cause: 255 ssh dropped, 5 remote checkout failed, 6 remote untar failed, 7 tree changed while packed. The counter is REMOTE_SYNC_RETRIED, so a persistent failure still fails loudly after 2 tries. Smoke: a normal sync of spiral to europa still prints REMOTE-SYNC-OK (exit 0). Found on the way: syncing a repo that has no clone on the target (dir-tree-html on europa) dies at 'git bundle failed'; it should say 'no clone of <repo> on <machine>: clone it first'. Left: part 2, a 'verify -Paths' box-vs-mirror digest table, and part 3, mirroring gitignored inputs.")
inl note_of_mirror_freshness_guard_3 () = Note ("MIRROR-FRESHNESS-GUARD", 3u32, "2026-11-01T23:45Z", "main", "main 19:5x PART 2 DONE (unstaged remote.ps1): 'remote.ps1 <m> verify <repo> [-Mirror <name>] [paths...]' hashes each path on the box and in the mirror (default paths: the box's changed and untracked set, as sync uses) and prints one line per stale path, then 'MIRROR-STALE ... re-sync before trusting a proof' with exit 6, or 'MIRROR-FRESH <n> paths match'. First real use caught a stale file: node shared-current's apps/cells/spi/lib_gate.ps1 predates today's exit-on-failure change (box 449F0AFF vs mirror A0C55439). Proof scripts should call verify on their input paths before starting. Left: part 3 (gitignored inputs such as fiscal deps/corpus and deps/bench, via an -Include on sync).")
inl note_of_mirror_freshness_guard_4 () = Note ("MIRROR-FRESHNESS-GUARD", 4u32, "2026-11-02T14:29Z", "main", "main 11-02: parent epic is GATE-HEALS-1101; recorded here instead of as a dep, because a dep on an unfinished parent epic hid this item from 'agile next' (backlog-wide sweep: 67 open items depended on an unfinished Epic).")
inl note_of_mirror_freshness_guard_5 () = Note ("MIRROR-FRESHNESS-GUARD", 5u32, "2026-11-04T16:17Z", "main", "11-04 12:2x main ORPHAN SWEEP: Active with no note for 48 h, so back to Planned at 65% (WIP cap: Active means touched). Owner stays main; resume from the last note.")
inl note_of_mirror_freshness_guard_6 () = Note ("MIRROR-FRESHNESS-GUARD", 6u32, "2026-11-05T07:25Z", "main", "11-05 03:25 main PART 3 DONE (unstaged i574n.github/scripts/remote.ps1): `remote.ps1 <m> sync <repo> [-Mirror <n>] -Include <path>[,<path>...]` adds gitignored inputs (files or whole dirs) to the synced set, so they are tarred, extracted AND counted in the tree digest that sync already compares end to end; remote `git clean -fd` leaves ignored files alone, so nothing undoes them. A missing include path refuses before any remote step (\"-Include <p> does not exist under <repo>\"); -Include on any verb but sync is refused. PROOF on europa: sync regex -Mirror main-inc -Include bench/bench.rs (gitignored, 194476 bytes) -> \"include: 1 files\", digest E9368009E2299CDC on both sides, REMOTE-SYNC-OK, and the mirror's bench.rs hashes 42734932F95B = box; both refusal cases checked; the scratch worktree removed with git worktree remove. With part 1 (sync retries) and part 2 (verify -Paths box-vs-mirror table, exit 6 on stale), the DoD holds: fiscal-style gitignored corpora can now travel with a mirror, and verify refuses a stale one in seconds.")
inl note_of_cells_check_defaults_1 () = Note ("CELLS-CHECK-DEFAULTS", 1u32, "2026-11-01T22:00Z", "main", "main 18:0x from compiler A5. DoD: --check without the env var resolves |core- the same way the CLI does; --timeout-ms 120000 lets a big fiscal unit finish; both have tests.")
inl note_of_cells_check_defaults_2 () = Note ("CELLS-CHECK-DEFAULTS", 2u32, "2026-11-02T14:42Z", "compiler", "11-02 10:40 compiler: dep cleared (main sweep 11-02): GATE-HEALS-1101 is this item's PARENT epic, not a blocker, so the dep hid it from `agile next`. Parent: GATE-HEALS-1101.")
inl note_of_cells_check_defaults_3 () = Note ("CELLS-CHECK-DEFAULTS", 3u32, "2026-11-02T21:21Z", "compiler", "11-02 17:25 compiler: PROGRAM DRAFTED: drafts CELLS-CHECK-DEFAULTS\\1-check-package-dir-and-timeout.kitdo (core 1 + host 1 replacement; dry-applies on live 1B00A6B3, stacked after COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS\\1). ROOT CAUSE: with SPIRAL_COMPILER_PACKAGE_DIR unset, resolve_packages used <get_workspace_root()>/deps/The-Spiral-Language/VS Code Plugin, and get_workspace_root() is SPIRAL_WORKSPACE_ROOT or else the CURRENT DIRECTORY. So --check run from fiscal looked in fiscal\\deps\\The-Spiral-Language and every |core- package failed (the 90/90 false failures). FIX: the core walks the ancestors of the workspace root and of the package folder, trying deps/The-Spiral-Language/VS Code Plugin, a vendored deps/spiral/deps/..., and a sibling ../spiral/deps/..., and takes the first that exists; the env var still wins, and the old path is the last resort. That matches Cells' Toolchain.package_dir intent (spiral root + core package) without a compile-time root. Host: `--check --timeout-ms N <file>` (positive int32, as --plan-ir; default stays 30000), so a big fiscal unit can take 120000. PROOF PLAN (node, with the pack19 build): --check on a fiscal unit from C:\\home\\git\\fiscal with the env var unset (control fails, candidate passes), plus --timeout-ms 120000 on the largest fiscal unit.")
inl note_of_cells_check_defaults_4 () = Note ("CELLS-CHECK-DEFAULTS", 4u32, "2026-11-02T22:54Z", "compiler", "11-02 18:50 compiler: shipped in pack19 (handed to main 18:5x, install-when-clear running). Node proof: --check with SPIRAL_COMPILER_PACKAGE_DIR and SPIRAL_WORKSPACE_ROOT unset: control exit 5 (|core- unresolved), candidate exit 0; --check --timeout-ms 120000 exit 0.")
inl note_of_cells_check_defaults_5 () = Note ("CELLS-CHECK-DEFAULTS", 5u32, "2026-11-03T02:32Z", "compiler", "11-02 22:5x compiler: DONE, live in the installed compiler (pack19, host 6B30D2F521660878, core 32912F27BC9DBEAC). Box checks with SPIRAL_COMPILER_PACKAGE_DIR and SPIRAL_WORKSPACE_ROOT unset: --check lib/spiral/metrics.spi (|core-) -> checked package C:/home/git/spiral/lib/spiral, exit 0 in 7 s; --check dice/contract/dice_contract.spi (sibling repo, via ../spiral) -> checked package C:/home/git/dice, exit 0; --check --timeout-ms 60000 parses. A package with no spiral checkout among its ancestors (a Temp scratch dir) still fails with the explicit SPIRAL_COMPILER_PACKAGE_DIR hint, by design.")
inl note_of_predict_per_backend_1 () = Note ("PREDICT-PER-BACKEND", 1u32, "2026-11-01T22:01Z", "main", "main 18:0x from compiler A2: the native memo already keys per backend. DoD: a pack touching only the Gleam section predicts in under 20 min with the other backends' rows read from memo, and the residual verdict is unchanged versus the full run on one sample pack.")
inl note_of_predict_per_backend_2 () = Note ("PREDICT-PER-BACKEND", 2u32, "2026-11-02T14:41Z", "compiler", "11-02 10:40 compiler: dep cleared (main sweep 11-02): GATE-HEALS-1101 is this item's PARENT epic, not a blocker, so the dep hid it from `agile next`. Parent: GATE-HEALS-1101.")
inl note_of_predict_per_backend_3 () = Note ("PREDICT-PER-BACKEND", 3u32, "2026-11-03T01:03Z", "compiler", "11-02 21:0x compiler: EVIDENCE for the node-mirror half. Today every compiler pack review ran on node t1101 with nothing on the box: pack19 (1220 s total incl. build, both arms), pack19b, paramesc, paramesc2, pack20 (control + candidate). Per arm, examples -Backend Rust,C,Zig,Gleam (1981 rows) took 3.6-4.6 min and contracts (728 rows) 3-4 min, plus about 5 min for the candidate build; compare-runs reads residual and behavior cells in-process. So a pack predict without -Native costs about 20 min of node time and 0 box time. Still open for the DoD: the native half (-Native rows from memo for unchanged backends), which needs a toolchain-complete mirror (node lacks the Wgsl adapter and the Delphi/Lean runners) or europa.")
inl note_of_predict_per_backend_4 () = Note ("PREDICT-PER-BACKEND", 4u32, "2026-11-03T23:34Z", "compiler", "11-03 19:3x compiler: EVIDENCE for the native half, from today's 7 node reviews (pack27 E0505, pack28 E0507 x3, pack29, pack30, pack31; 0 box time). Recipe that held every time: (1) examples on ONLY the backends whose codegen section the program touches (Rust for RUST-MOVE, Zig/contracts for LINKED-UNITS-ZIG, Lua for the IIFE fix), both arms, no -Native: about 2 min per arm; (2) compare-runs, then derive the changed rows (residual differs on both sides) and rerun ONLY those with -Native -Filter '^samples/(a|b|...)$' on both arms: 117 rows in about 3 min for slice 4, 1 row for E0507; (3) downstream rows that examples lack (regex certificate Cells A/B, apps/spiral cargo check, kit crates), because examples missed both pack26 bugs. The derive-and-filter step is a few lines (node-pack29.ps1 in the scratchpad, written inline by me each time); folding it into test.ps1 as '-Native -OnlyChangedFrom <results.tsv>' is the concrete next step for this item.")
inl note_of_predict_per_backend_5 () = Note ("PREDICT-PER-BACKEND", 5u32, "2026-11-04T00:17Z", "compiler", "11-03 20:1x compiler: n4's next step DONE in tree (unstaged): test.ps1 -ChangedBetween <control results.tsv>,<candidate results.tsv> keeps only samples whose residual differs (matched by id + backend), refuses -Accept/-Record, never counts as a full schedule, and exits 0 at once when nothing changed. Proof on the box: a copy of single-flight-20261102-131037 with one Rust residual altered -> '-ChangedBetween: 1 samples', 1 job; the same file twice -> 'nothing changed', exit 0. Documented in apps/compiler/tmp/AGENTS.md. A pack review's native half is now: both arms without -Native, then both arms -Native -ChangedBetween control,candidate. Left for the DoD: per-backend scheduling from the touched codegen section, and node/europa toolchain completeness for -Native.")
inl note_of_predict_per_backend_6 () = Note ("PREDICT-PER-BACKEND", 6u32, "2026-11-04T00:21Z", "compiler", "11-03 20:3x compiler: per-backend scheduling DONE in tree (unstaged): test.ps1 -BackendsFrom <before.fs>,<after.fs> sets -Backend (when none is given) to the backends whose codegen the change touches. It aligns the two sources positionally (resync on 3 equal lines within 400; a first multiset-diff cut flagged generic lines like '| _ -> false' all over the file and was replaced), maps each changed line to its file's nearest '/// ## Codegen<X>' (or '/// ### codegen<X>' inside the shared Wgsl range: Calyx/Kotlin/Swift/OpenQasm/Ebpf), and keeps every backend for any change outside codegen. Proof on today's packs (candidate sources): pack31 -> Lua; pack30 -> Rust; pack28 -> Rust; pack29 -> every backend (it changed ExternCalls in PartEval and exportedUnionNames in CodegenUtils; correct). 6-11 s per call. With -ChangedBetween (n5) a pack review is now: -BackendsFrom both arms without -Native, then -Native -ChangedBetween. Documented in AGENTS.md. Left for the DoD: node/europa toolchain completeness for -Native rows.")
inl note_of_predict_per_backend_7 () = Note ("PREDICT-PER-BACKEND", 7u32, "2026-11-04T06:25Z", "compiler", "11-04 02:3x compiler: NODE TOOLCHAIN GAP CLOSED (the item's last DoD point), except Swift. Before: Get-SpiralNativeTools on the node (moon) found no Auxin, BendMain, CalyxRoot, Cider, Java, Kotlinc, Swiftc/SwiftRuntime/SwiftSdk or WgslRun; the box has all of them, so -Native rows for Bend, Calyx, Kotlin, Swift and Wgsl could only run on the box. Shipped from the box's toolchains (9.3 MB tar, only what runs): wgsl-run\\release\\spiral-wgsl.exe, bend\\bend2 (runs on the node's bun) and calyx-src without target\\ plus its release auxin.exe and cider.exe. scoop on the node: bucket java, temurin25-jdk 25.0.5 and kotlin (same packages as the box). Proof (node, installed compiler, examples -Native -Filter): Wgsl i64_scalar ran exit 0; Calyx arithmetic_branch ran exit 0; Bend arithmetic_branch ran exit 0. Java and Kotlinc now resolve (openjdk 25.0.5). Left: Swift 6.4 (Windows installer plus SDK, several GB; the node had 8.8 GB free before my stage sweep, 19.1 GB after). So a pack touching codegenSwift still needs the box for native rows; everything else can run node-first.")
inl note_of_predict_per_backend_8 () = Note ("PREDICT-PER-BACKEND", 8u32, "2026-11-04T13:15Z", "compiler", "11-04 09:2x compiler: CLOSED. Delivered: test.ps1 -BackendsFrom (per-backend scheduling from the codegen sections a change touches, proven on packs 28-31), -ChangedBetween, and node toolchains for Bend/Calyx/Kotlin/Wgsl/Java (proven -Native rows exit 0 on the node). Today every review ran node-first. The one gap, Swift native rows on the node, is split off as NODE-SWIFT-TOOLCHAIN (P3); until it lands, a pack touching codegenSwift runs its Swift native rows on the box.")
inl note_of_single_test_fast_path_1 () = Note ("SINGLE-TEST-FAST-PATH", 1u32, "2026-11-01T22:01Z", "main", "main 18:0x: Cells already has KINO-RUN-ONE-TEST (Done) for notebooks; this extends it to kit's crate proofs and to single-target runs. DoD: one Rust test block of a kit package runs in under 60 s cold-cached.")
inl note_of_single_test_fast_path_2 () = Note ("SINGLE-TEST-FAST-PATH", 2u32, "2026-11-02T14:38Z", "x", "2026-11-02 10:37 x: dep INVERTED (main's sweep: an open item depending on an unfinished epic is hidden from agile next). GATE-HEALS-1101 was only this item's parent; nothing here waits on it. The item now has no deps, and GATE-HEALS-1101 lists it as a child dep.")
inl note_of_single_test_fast_path_3 () = Note ("SINGLE-TEST-FAST-PATH", 3u32, "2026-11-02T21:24Z", "x", "2026-11-02 17:24 x: DONE by measurement; the existing Cells path already meets the DoD. HOW: pwsh spiral/apps/cells/spi/run_notebook.ps1 --path <kit .spi> --test <block name>. It runs only that block (plus its static prelude) and neither regenerates nor cargo-builds the package's crates. EVIDENCE (node mirror xkit1, kit_bindings_model/model.spi, ///> rust block nested_types_split_only_at_the_top_level), rule written before the run. x-single-test2 with SPIRAL_CELLS_MEMO=0, so every round really compiles and runs: round 1 fully cold (right after the 17:13 pack switch: new compiler, cold daemon) 126 s; round 2 warm caches, a real compile with 0 memo hits, 20 s, executed 1/1 passed. That is under the DoD's 60 s cold-cached. x-single-test1 with the memo on: cold 76 s, then 13 s (a memo hit, no compile). Not covered here: tibia's box GPU single tests (1-2 min), which need the box GPU and are left to tibia under TIBIA-WINDOWS-CI-GPU.")
inl note_of_remote_run_file_1 () = Note ("REMOTE-RUN-FILE", 1u32, "2026-11-01T22:01Z", "main", "main 18:0x from x-dumps 5. DoD: a local script with \\ and quotes runs identically on node, europa and WSL through one call.")
inl note_of_remote_run_file_2 () = Note ("REMOTE-RUN-FILE", 2u32, "2026-11-01T22:49Z", "main", "main 18:5x DONE (unstaged i574n.github/scripts/remote.ps1): 'remote.ps1 <m> run -Script <local file>' reads the local script and sends its text through Invoke-Remote's existing base64 -EncodedCommand transport, so the local shell expands nothing. It's named -Script rather than -File so existing 'run pwsh -NoProfile -File x.ps1' calls keep their -File. It can't be combined with an inline command and is refused on other verbs. Proof: a script with $vars and nested single and double quotes printed the same line on the node (pwsh 7.6.8) and europa (7.6.9). WSL bash inside a node job is still the job script's own concern.")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_1 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS", 1u32, "2026-11-01T22:11Z", "compiler", "11-01 18:10 compiler: filed from the kit/compiler design agreement (user 11-01 17:4x: types, not bespoke --import-types plumbing; KIT-TYPED-CRATES must aim at typed exports the compiler understands natively). WHAT: native typed linking between hand-modeled units, declared in package.spiproj. Inside a unit, compilation stays whole-program (partial evaluation needs that); between units, the compiler knows from the package graph which package owns each union and each exported monomorphic function. UPSTREAM: mrakgr Spiral has no separate compilation or interface files; it is whole-program over the spiproj package graph, so the compatible extension is one spiproj field, `link:`, with packages:'s syntax, listing packages compiled as separate units. STEP A (small): importedTypeUnits (spiral_compiler.fs 12441) builds its union-to-unit map from the package graph (unions declared in a link: package belong to that unit) instead of the env var SPIRAL_IMPORT_TYPES=\"unit:Name,...\"; delete the env var. Its consumers (codegenRust 14508, codegenGleam 18515) already rename unions and drop the local definitions, so unions crossing units stop flattening to i32 (kit: 37 reflection rebuild sites). STEP B (medium): a call to an exported monomorphic function of a link: package becomes a typed extern op carrying the export's signature (PartEval top-level application; prepass already records each definition's package), and codegenRust emits unit::fn(args). This replaces kit's 303 `$'crate::fn(...)' : T` host-string calls; model-only link: packages then contribute types only (rust_std_string is inlined into 114 crates today, union_reflection into 95). DEFINITION OF DONE: Step A, a two-package sample (a union declared in a link: package, used by the other unit) builds on Rust with one enum definition, plus kit's train green with SPIRAL_IMPORT_TYPES gone from every repo. Step B, the same sample calls an exported function with no host string, and kit's generated line total drops against kit's 11-01 baseline (150k lines, 272 crates). TYPEFEATURESET: unit ownership is a typed map built from the package graph (package id to declared unions/exports), never a name list in a string; the extern op carries the export's Ty signature. NEXT STEP: read where PrepassPackageEnv resolves packages:, add link: parsing beside it, and feed importedTypeUnits from it (Step A).")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_2 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS", 2u32, "2026-11-01T22:13Z", "compiler", "11-01 18:14 compiler: kit agreed (link: in package.spiproj, Step A then B, kit as the proof corpus; KIT-TYPED-CRATES depends on this). It raised four holes, all now in scope. (1) ONE SOURCE OF TRUTH for unit dependencies: the compiler emits the unit graph from link: (a typed record per unit: package id, linked units, exported unions and functions), and kit generates Cargo [dependencies] from it. Hand-kept Cargo deps drift today (todo_scan carried an unused agile-task-census dep). (2) PAYLOAD COVERAGE: the export struct path handles records of primitives only (14061/14080). Unions holding lists or nested records, and records holding unions, must cross units. Live case: kit_machine_sample's 9-tuple of process rows, where one added field broke 7 importer crates. Step A's sample must include a union with a record payload and a record with a union field. (3) NAME IDENTITY: today's `use` replacement matches union SOURCE names in generated text (14512). Ownership must resolve by owning package id, never by name, because the same union name lives in many packages (tibia's table_row in 61 files, option). That is the typed map from n1's typefeatureset plan, keyed by the union's declaring package. (4) GLEAM: the same unit graph drives Gleam units (x-dumps and Cells run Gleam entries); codegenGleam's import path (18515) consumes the same map. MEASURE FIRST: model-only link: packages contributing types only is the biggest win (rust_std_string inlined into 114 crates, union_reflection into 95), so Step A's proof reports generated lines with and without it. kit attaches its baseline (n2) and runs each step's candidate over kit on the node.")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_3 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS", 3u32, "2026-11-01T22:14Z", "compiler", "11-01 18:17 compiler: STEP A CODE MAP (core F6F6879566C5A830). RawSchema (28952) gains link : RawSchemaPackages list, parsed by the same packages parser as packages: (field table at 29049; note that 'crates' is already accepted there and ignored: crate_lines |>> fun _ s -> s, a dead field to retire or fold into link:). The validated schema (29321 builds {moduleDir; modules; packageDir; packages; ...}) carries link through to the package environment. The unit map then needs, for each union nominal, its declaring package: Nominal = {body; id : GlobalId; name} (8971), and GlobalId resolves to its package through the prepass package environment, the same resolution SPIRAL_REFERENCES_OUT uses. importedTypeUnits (12441) becomes a function of (env, link set) returning union -> unit, keyed by nominal id (n2 hole 3: by owner, not by name). Its two consumers, codegenRust 14508-14531 and codegenGleam 18515, then rename by owner instead of by unionSourceNames text. FIRST CUT to prove: link: parsing plus the owner-keyed map, with SPIRAL_IMPORT_TYPES kept as a fallback for one pack; then delete the env var.")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_4 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS", 4u32, "2026-11-01T22:48Z", "compiler", "11-01 18:50 compiler: STEP A FIRST CUT PROVEN (node job-1793572703982-compiler-linked). PROGRAM: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS\\1-link-field-owner-keyed-unions.kitdo, 17 replacements; it stacks on GLEAM-JS-TARGET-GAPS program 1 (codegenGleam's signature). What it adds: link: in RawSchema/Schema, parsed and resolved like packages:; unionSourcePackages (declaring package id per nominal union, filled where unionSourceNames is); file_linked_units (owning schema's link dirs -> package ids via s.package_ids -> unit name = the folder name), passed to codegenRust and codegenGleam as a parameter (no global, no env). Both import passes rename by OWNER first and fall back to SPIRAL_IMPORT_TYPES for one pack. PROBE (two packages under a scratch tree with the samples core): model declares union color = Red | Green | Blue : i32; app has packages: core-, model- and link: model-; app-nolink is the same without link:. Result: app.rs has 'use model::{color};', 'let v1: color = color::color_Blue(v0);' and the match on color::color_* with NO local enum; app-nolink.rs keeps its local 'enum US0'. Installed compiler on app-nolink: 'enum US0' (control). NEXT: (a) land the probe as samples/linked_unit_union (model + app) with a matrix Known for its Rust native row until Cargo linking (n2 hole 1) exists; (b) cover n2 hole 2 (unions with record payloads, records with union fields) in the same sample; (c) kit runs this candidate over kit (node: C:\\home\\remote-stage\\linked\\cache\\bin\\single-flight\\SpiralCompiler\\Release\\net11.0\\SpiralCompiler.dll) with link: on one model package to measure the line drop; (d) delete SPIRAL_IMPORT_TYPES after one pack.")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_5 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS", 5u32, "2026-11-01T22:54Z", "compiler", "11-01 18:56 compiler: HOLE 2, record payloads, OK on the Step A candidate. model declares shape = Circle : { r : i32 } | Rect : { w : i32; h : i32 }; app links model and holds a record { item = Rect {...}; count } (a record holding the linked union), then matches. app2.rs: 'use model::{shape};', 'let v2: shape = shape::shape_Rect(v0, v1);', the match arms shape::shape_Circle(v4) and shape::shape_Rect(v7, v8), and no local enum. The record holding the union flattens into locals as usual, so it needs nothing special. Union-in-union (path_verdict holding comment_syntax and path_skip) is the next probe, and kit's agile_todo_model run covers it (kit: baseline paths 340 / scan 937 / merge 939 lines; the reverted --import-types spike reached scan 812 / merge 815; Step A must match that with no env var; gate todo_cli 4/4 plus cargo build of kit-cli). Measurement target corrected per kit: rust_std_string declares no unions, so its 114x inlining is a Step B effect.")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_6 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS", 6u32, "2026-11-01T23:08Z", "compiler", "11-01 19:15 compiler: GROOM split. Step B moved to COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS (240m). This item is now Step A only, re-estimated to 240m (first cut proven 18:50). DoD (Step A): samples/linked_unit_union (model + app, including n5's record-payload union) builds on Rust with the union declared once; kit's agile_todo_model crossing reaches its spike numbers (scan <= 812, merge <= 815 lines) with no SPIRAL_IMPORT_TYPES; Cargo deps generated from link: (kit owns the generator, the compiler emits the unit graph); then SPIRAL_IMPORT_TYPES is deleted.")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_7 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS", 7u32, "2026-11-01T23:18Z", "compiler", "11-01 19:19 compiler: holds on the pack15c candidate (9-program stack, core 6292FBD7632BB398): app.rs carries 'use model::{color};'. Kit can pin either this candidate or the Step-A-only one in C:\\home\\remote-stage\\linked.")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_8 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS", 8u32, "2026-11-02T00:36Z", "compiler", "11-01 20:40 compiler: HOLE FOUND BY KIT (node job-1793579446108, kit-verify mirror, Step A candidate). agile_todo_model became a unit exporting kit_agile_todo_path_verdict : string * bool -> path_verdict; agile_todo_scan/merge got link: agile_todo_model. cargo E0432: the importers emitted 'use agile_todo_model::{comment_syntax, path_skip, path_verdict, content_verdict, todo_filter};', i.e. EVERY union of the linked package they use, while the unit makes pub enum only for unions reachable from its exports (path_verdict, comment_syntax, path_skip). DECISION, option (1): owner-map a union only when it is reachable from the linked package's export signatures, with its concrete type arguments, taken from the prepass's monomorphic export types through the package graph. Every other union of the linked package stays a local enum in the importer, since it never crosses the boundary. Rejected (2) 'unit emits pub enum for every declared union': unions are generic and monomorphized, so a declared but uninstantiated union, or a different instantiation, has no concrete enum to export. SECOND CUT TODO: file_linked_units returns, per linked package, the set of export-reachable nominal ids (with type args) instead of a whole-package ownership; unionOwnerUnit checks membership. GATE: kit's rerun on kit-verify, with E0432 gone and scan <= 812 / merge <= 815 lines. Also per main 20:3x: link: is the primary path; SPIRAL_IMPORT_TYPES is retired as soon as kit's typed crates move to link:.")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_9 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS", 9u32, "2026-11-02T00:39Z", "compiler", "11-01 20:45 compiler: CORRECTION to n8's 'from the prepass'. export is a runtime op (TyOp(Export, [name; fn]) at codegenRust:14050), materialized only when the unit's own main is partially evaluated, so an importer cannot compute the export-reachable set from the package graph. SECOND CUT DESIGN: compiling a unit (a package with exports) writes a typed unit graph next to its output: package id, each export's name and monomorphic signature, and the union nominals reachable from it with concrete type args. It is a generated file, never committed. Importers read the graph of each link: unit and owner-map exactly those (nominal, type args) pairs; every other union stays local. The same artifact feeds kit's Cargo [dependencies] generator (n2 hole 1: one source of truth). The unit compiles before its importers. Estimate stays inside this item's 240m. NEXT SESSION: emit the graph from codegenRust's Export handling (it already computes exportedUnionNames), plus its reader in file_linked_units.")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_10 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS", 10u32, "2026-11-02T11:05Z", "kit", "kit 11-02 07:2x, from the S0 study subagent's execution packet (aaf2a6f472dc70094). CHILDREN filed 11-02: LINKED-UNITS-NO-SUFFIX, LINKED-UNITS-DERIVE-OUT, LINKED-UNITS-GLEAM-RECORDS, LINKED-UNITS-OPAQUE-TIER, LINKED-UNITS-MONOMORPHIC-RULE, LINKED-UNITS-ZIG, IMPORT-TYPES-DELETE, then ZIG-PARALLEL-UNITS-BATTLE-TEST and FEATURE-PARITY-TABLE beside them. DoD addition: the n6 sample must be green on Gleam as well as Rust (n6 names only Rust).")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_11 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS", 11u32, "2026-11-02T11:06Z", "compiler", "11-02 07:10 compiler: SECOND CUT drafted: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS\\2-unit-graph-export-reachable.kitdo (11 replacements, stacks on the live tree). (1) A unit with exports writes <stem>.unit.json beside its input, from the Rust and Gleam build arms. It holds the exports (name + show_ty signature), the units it links, and each export-reachable union {source, shape = show_ty of the concrete union, name}. It is written directly, not as a GeneratedFile, because BuildOk concatenates every file into the host's single output. (2) file_linked_units returns Map<package id, LinkedUnit {unit; exported}>, reading the graphs in each link: dir. (3) linkedUnionName owner-maps a union only when its (source, shape) is in the graph, under the unit's exported name. Every other union of that package stays local (n8 option 1). A link: unit with no graph is a codegen error (\"build <unit> before the units that link it\") instead of the whole-package guess that produced E0432. (4) Generic instances now record their declaring package (head nominal at nominal_type_apply), so box i32 maps while box string stays local. CONTROL on installed pack15d (probe scratchpad linked\\lu3: model declares color, hidden, box t and exports paint : i32 -> color and boxed : i32 -> box i32; app uses all of them plus box string): app.rs carries `use model::{color, hidden};`, while model.rs makes pub only color and box_i32. That reproduces kit's E0432 shape locally, and generic instances never map. The candidate arm is building.")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_12 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS", 12u32, "2026-11-02T11:17Z", "compiler", "11-02 07:40 compiler: SECOND CUT PROVEN LOCALLY (candidate linked2: core AE545866AD1BBF9E, host 9489144496A935E6 = pack15d's host; program 2 = drafts COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS\\2-unit-graph-export-reachable.kitdo, 11 replacements). PROBE scratchpad linked\\lu3, same tree, both arms. CONTROL (pack15d): app.rs `use model::{color, hidden};`; rustc error[E0432]: unresolved import `model::hidden` (kit's n8 hole, reproduced locally). CANDIDATE: (a) app built before model: \"The link: unit model has no unit graph (model/*.unit.json). Build model before the units that link it.\" (exit 5). (b) model build writes model.unit.json: exports model_paint \"fptr (i32 -> color)\" and model_boxed \"fptr (i32 -> box i32)\"; unions color {Red : () | Green : () | Blue : i32} and box_i32 {Full : i32 | Empty : ()}. (c) app.rs `use model::{color, box_i32};`, with hidden and box string kept as local enums; rustc links app against libmodel.rlib; app.exe exit 13 = expected. (d) Gleam app imports Color and BoxI32 only. CONTRACTS: test-rust-exports.ps1 passes on candidate and control. It had been failing at wrong_signature on BOTH: a stale anchor from the edition-3 respell ((fun value => ...) vs the fixture's (\\ value => ...)), so the mutation never applied and the last 3 negative cases plus the policy library never ran. Anchor fixed (unstaged). STAGED for kit on the node: C:\\home\\remote-stage\\linked2\\cache\\bin\\single-flight\\SpiralCompiler\\Release\\net11.0\\SpiralCompiler.dll (hashes verified there). GATE = kit's agile_todo rerun: E0432 gone, scan <= 812 / merge <= 815; then the pack.")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_13 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS", 13u32, "2026-11-02T12:09Z", "compiler", "11-02 08:10 compiler: STEP A DoD MET on kit (kit's job-1793620674664-kit-stepA2b over candidate linked2, KIT-TYPED-CRATES n15): model.unit.json 878 B; scan 937 -> 812 and merge 939 -> 815, exactly the spike targets; importers `use agile_todo_model::{comment_syntax, path_skip, path_verdict}` while content_verdict and todo_filter stay local; E0432 = 0; cargo build -p kit-cli exit 0; todo_cli 4/4. kit's generator no longer emits --import-types (kit_bindings_model/model.spi:154 now writes link:), so IMPORT-TYPES-DELETE is unblocked; drafted as program IMPORT-TYPES-DELETE\\1. Open on kit's side: its staged regen copies only .rs back, so *.unit.json must survive staging and regen must order units by link: (KIT-TYPED-CRATES n15). Pack16 = this item's program 2 + IMPORT-TYPES-DELETE 1 + LINKED-UNITS-ZIG 1 and 2, building now.")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_14 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS", 14u32, "2026-11-02T13:01Z", "compiler", "11-02 08:50 compiler: PACK16 RESIDUAL A/B (compile-only, examples suite, -Backend Rust,Gleam,Zig): control pack15d single-flight-20261102-082202 vs candidate pack16 (core F87DA54FC08D6F8A, host 0AE507ABA4DC13BD) single-flight-20261102-083710. 1,421 rows each; compare-runs on compile+residual shows exactly 2 differing cells, both samples/zig_export_fn Zig (error -> ok, new residual). Every other residual hash is identical across Rust, Gleam and Zig, so the unit graph, the import-types deletion and the Zig export arms leave non-export programs untouched. CAUTION RECORDED: the first compare run said \"0 differing\" because `pwsh -File compare-runs.ps1 -Fields compile,residual` passes the list as one string (every cell compared $null to $null); run it in-process with an array.")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_15 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS", 15u32, "2026-11-02T15:02Z", "compiler", "11-02 11:10 compiler (groom, star exchange x #2): the unit graph must LEAVE THE TREE. The user wants no tool output written into repos, and gitignoring <stem>.unit.json only hides it. kit #8 also showed the in-tree location is lost by staged regen. NEXT PROGRAM (after pack16c installs): write the graph into the compiler cache, keyed by the unit package's standardized directory (e.g. <spiral-bin cache>/units/<sha16(package dir)>/<stem>.unit.json), and have readUnitGraph look it up by the link: dir's key instead of globbing the folder. Same content, same \"build X first\" error, and staging no longer matters, since the key is the package path rather than the file. kit's Cargo generator reads it through a `spiral unit-graph <package dir>` CLI verb instead of a file path. Related items from x's TYPED-LINK-SOTA, to groom when picked: LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE (cut mega samples at every point, outputs byte-equal), LINK-GENERIC-INTERFACE (unit.json ships generic definitions for the importer to specialize, as Rust rlib metadata does), LINK-BOUNDARY-BENCH.")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_16 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS", 16u32, "2026-11-02T16:54Z", "compiler", "11-02 13:00 compiler: PROGRAM 3 DRAFTED, the unit graph OUT OF THE TREE (x's star-exchange #2, user rule: nothing written into repos). %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS\\3-unit-graph-out-of-tree.kitdo, 6 replacements, dry-applied on top of program 2 (0 in-tree writes left). unitGraphDir(packageDir) = <LocalApplicationData>/spiral-bin/units/<sha256(lowercased, slash-normalized package dir)[..16]>, overridable with SPIRAL_UNIT_GRAPH_DIR. The writer resolves the file's owning package via the new file_package_dir (the same SchemaEnv walk file_linked_units uses), and readUnitGraph looks in unitGraphDir of the link: dir. So writer and reader key the same standardized path, and kit's staged regen no longer loses the graph (kit #8), because the key is the package path, not a file beside the input. Not yet: a `spiral unit-graph <package dir>` verb for kit's Cargo generator (it can read the cache path directly meanwhile). PROOF PLAN (node, after gadt6): lu3 probe on a candidate = pack16c stack + program 3: graph written under the cache, nothing beside model.spi, app imports {color, box_i32}, rustc links. Then hand over as pack17 with the GADT program.")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_17 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS", 17u32, "2026-11-02T17:55Z", "compiler", "11-02 14:00 compiler: STEP A INSTALLED with pack16c (box 13:48; node and europa ships running). Kit's gate (n13) passed on the same program. Left for this item: program 3, the graph out of the tree, rides pack17 (node review running; the 4-program stack on the new live reaches the reviewed source C9CF9F36, verified), plus kit's Cargo generator reading the graph (kit owns it). Until pack17 lands, a unit build writes <stem>.unit.json beside its .spi.")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_18 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS", 18u32, "2026-11-02T18:55Z", "compiler", "11-02 14:55 compiler: program 3 INSTALLED (pack17): unit graphs now live in <LocalAppData>/spiral-bin/units/<sha16 of the package dir>/, and nothing is written beside a .spi (lu3: 0 in-tree, 6 in the cache). Any *.unit.json left in a repo from the pack16c window can be deleted; it is stale.")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_19 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS", 19u32, "2026-11-02T20:24Z", "compiler", "11-02 15:40 compiler: independent validation. x's LINK-GADT-FACADE pilot lgf1 is green on pack17 (job x-lgf2): a GADT request lives in the model unit, only the concrete reply unions cross (`use proto::{status_reply, compile_reply};`, Gleam `import proto.{type StatusReply, ...}`), app.exe exits 14, and a compile_reply declared as a status_reply fails with Unification failure at the boundary. Built on lu3; files in kit drafts LINK-GADT-FACADE\\lgf1; usable as the M2 baseline for LINK-BOUNDARY-BENCH.")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_20 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS", 20u32, "2026-11-03T02:35Z", "compiler", "11-02 23:0x compiler: STEP B state (child COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS). Rust extern calls INSTALLED with pack19 (box 22:3x, host 6B30D2F521660878, core 32912F27BC9DBEAC): a call to an exported monomorphic function of a link: unit emits unit::export(args) (lu4 app.rs: model::model_paint(v0)). pack20 (handed to main 22:4x) adds strings (&v) and refuses records on both sides (they fall back to inline, fixing a latent pack19 E0308 on record params and returns). Slice 3, Gleam (unit.export plus import unit, deduped against import unit.{types}), is proven on lu5 (gleam build ok, exit 27) and is in suite A/B on node t1101 (examples 1981 rows, 0 differing cells). Left on the epic: kit's Cargo generator reading the graph (kit), and records plus eta-reduced exports across units (a later slice).")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_21 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS", 21u32, "2026-11-03T19:04Z", "compiler", "11-03 15:0x compiler: Zig parity with Rust/Gleam on typed links, proven (not installed): multi-value returns (lu12, copy_tuples) and union import (lu13, const USn = model.<name>). See LINKED-UNITS-ZIG n10/n11. Gaps left across backends: closures and GADT payloads never cross (by design), heap-union field moves on Rust.")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_22 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS", 22u32, "2026-11-03T23:09Z", "compiler", "11-03 19:1x compiler: CLOSED. Step A DoD met 11-02 (n13: kit agile_todo_model crossing, scan 812 / merge 815), IMPORT-TYPES-DELETE Done, Step B (EXTERN-CALLS) Done; n10's addition (the union sample green on Gleam as well as Rust) holds as matrix rows: linked_rust_list_over_model (Rust, union + core list over 4 crates, exit 108) and linked_union (Zig + Gleam). Children still open, each standalone: LINKED-UNITS-MATRIX-SUITE 90 (Gleam runner done; more cases), DERIVE-OUT (census: 0 rust-extern derives), MONOMORPHIC-RULE (guard only; YExists allowed), GLEAM-RECORDS (ABI change, only on a consumer's ask).")
inl note_of_lib_move_unix_clock_1 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK", 1u32, "2026-11-01T22:44Z", "main", "11-01 18:4x main (lib-reshape generic-code sweep, read-only). SITES (each read in place; Spiral-level bindings only, raw Rust #[test] fixtures inside global blocks excluded). kit, ms: src/agile_lease_terms/terms.spi:91 clock_now_ms; src/kit_cli_check/cli.spi:175 now_ms; src/kit_experiments/ledger_host.spi:12 now_ms; src/kit_jobs/host.spi:18 now_ms; src/kit_machine_watch/jobs_watch.spi:5 now_ms; src/kit_receipt/receipt.spi:11 now_ms and :17 elapsed_text; src/rust_std_process/model.spi:55 wall_clock_millis and :59 elapsed_millis; src/workspace_primitives/clock.spi:1 unix_ms and :3 ms_since; src/rust_std_fs/model.spi:3 file_modified_ms (epoch part); src/kit_notebook_progress/progress.spi:8 now_ms (via reactors.physical_micros). kit, seconds: src/rust_std_env/clock.spi:10,13,17 (session_deadline_from_now, should_wrap, within_budget); src/kit_machine_sample/sample.spi:60 now_seconds; src/kit_resume/resume.spi:10 clock_text; src/kit_machine_watch/run.spi:16 now_text. x: apps/client/oauth1.spi:17-23 (system_now, since_epoch, whole_seconds, sub_micros: a copy of lib file_system.spi:1766-1769 rust_since_epoch/rust_elapsed_ms); apps/sim/spi/cells_executor.spi:88 clock_ms and :257 now_ms (Gleam erlang:monotonic_time millisecond). lib (private copies of the same read): guid.spi:91 rust_unix_nanos; trace.spi:338 rust_epoch_nanos; reactors.spi:301; file_system.spi:1766 rust_since_epoch; date_time.spi:144 zig_micros_now. LIB TARGET: date_time (existing module; date_time.now returns a chrono naive local date_time, not an epoch count, so it is NOT the replacement EOIE-HEAL-BOUNDARY n21 assumed for unix_ms). TYPED SHAPE: nominals :! unix_ms = u64, :! unix_seconds = u64, :! unix_nanos = u128 (or one epoch_count with phantom units :! millis / :! seconds / :! nanos so a ms value cannot be compared to seconds), :! monotonic_ms = i64 kept separate from wall time. Granular one-expression host bindings: rust_system_now (), rust_since_epoch (moved here from file_system), rust_whole_millis, rust_whole_seconds; Gleam arms via erlang:system_time/1 and erlang:monotonic_time/1 through erlang_term::apply; F# DateTimeOffset.UtcNow.ToUnixTimeMilliseconds. Public: unix_now_ms () : unix_ms, unix_now_seconds () : unix_seconds, unix_now_nanos () : unix_nanos, ms_since (start : unix_ms) : u64 (saturating), monotonic_now_ms () : monotonic_ms. No multi-line host macros. DoD: (1) date_time defines them with a :# block (ms > 1.7e12, seconds = ms / 1000 within 1, ms_since of now is < 1000, monotonic non-decreasing across two reads) passing in Cells on rust, fsharp and gleam; (2) every site above calls the lib function, each proven by its repo's own gate (kit: the touched packages' notebooks + crate regen; x: the client and xsim builds); (3) the old copies are deleted, lib's private copies included (guid, trace, reactors, file_system call date_time).")
inl note_of_lib_move_unix_clock_2 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK", 2u32, "2026-11-02T23:24Z", "x", "2026-11-02 19:24 x: STEP 1 drafted (kit drafts spiral\\LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK). PLACEMENT DECIDED by the line gate, not by the n1 target: date_time.spi is already 1,492 lines (over the 1k gate), so the clock is a new granular lib module, unix_clock.spi, after erlang_term in package.spiproj. It has nominals unix_ms, unix_seconds and unix_nanos (u64 each, so units can't be mixed), and one-expression host bindings: rust_system_now, rust_since_unix_epoch, rust_whole_millis and rust_whole_nanos; erlang_system_time through erlang_term::apply; fsharp_unix_millis and fsharp_unix_nanos. Public: unix_now_ms, unix_now_seconds, unix_now_nanos, ms_since (saturating), and the ms_count, seconds_count and nanos_count accessors. Monotonic ms stays as date_time::monotonic_milliseconds (Gleam, it already exists); a typed monotonic_ms nominal can wrap it when a consumer needs one. PRE-REGISTERED RULE (x-lib-clock1, after x-cells-pb1 frees the node): lib_land_window applies with document_test green, and lib_gate on unix_clock.spi gives the block 'the_unix_clock_reads_epoch_counts_in_their_own_units' passed on rust, fsharp and gleam with executed > 0 and 0 failed. STEP 2 (after the land): the call sites in n1 switch over, x's first (apps/client/oauth1.spi and apps/sim/spi/cells_executor.spi), each proven by its repo's gate; then lib's private copies (guid, trace, reactors, file_system).")
inl note_of_lib_move_unix_clock_3 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK", 3u32, "2026-11-02T23:56Z", "x", "2026-11-02 19:56 x: STEP 2, x's half, drafted (kit drafts x\\LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK); it waits for step 1's land. (1) apps/client/oauth1.spi (base 2C25BE4C24EB -> 15741F2FAB39): the private system_time/elapsed nominals and system_now, since_epoch, whole_seconds and sub_micros are deleted. clock_seed reads unix_clock::unix_now_nanos / 1000 (the same micros), and unix_seconds reads unix_clock::unix_now_seconds. (2) apps/sim/spi/cells_executor.spi (base FC47D2493A17 -> 534B8E8105A7): clock_ms and now_ms no longer call erlang:monotonic_time themselves. They read date_time::monotonic_milliseconds, and the deadline stops being a raw Erlang term: it is a nominal deadline_ms = i64, so deadline_after, left_until, next_reply and harvested are typed and the term arithmetic (erlang + - max) is gone. Proof on land: the x client gate (oauth1 blocks) and the sim proof (launch-sim-proof).")
inl note_of_lib_move_unix_clock_4 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK", 4u32, "2026-11-03T00:14Z", "x", "2026-11-02 20:14 x: STEP 1+3 SCOPE AND RULE, revised before any run. (a) Lint-clean macros: kit's standards/lint-macros-lib.spi baselines lib macro findings (cast, arith, block). So unix_clock's host bindings are one-expression reads only (SystemTime::now, duration_since, as_secs, subsec_nanos, UtcNow.Ticks, ToUnixTimeMilliseconds), and every unit conversion and offset is Spiral arithmetic. No 'as' casts, no F# arithmetic in a macro. (b) lib's own copies ride the same land: guid.spi drops rust_unix_nanos (the hasher seeds from unix_clock nanos, write_u64) and reactors.spi's rust_physical_micros becomes nanos / 1000. That retires kit lint entry lint_known_223 (reactors rust_physical_micros cast). Two copies stay, for stated reasons: trace.spi's rust_epoch_nanos is NEAR chain time under cfg (near_sdk block_timestamp), not a wall clock; file_system's rust_since_epoch converts a FILE's modified SystemTime, not now. RULE (x-lib-clock1, launch-lib-clock): lib_land_window applies 4 files (unix_clock new, package.spiproj, guid, reactors) with document_test green and the consumer signatures unchanged; lib_gate exits 0 with executed > 0 on each of unix_clock.spi, guid.spi and reactors.spi.")
inl note_of_lib_move_unix_clock_5 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK", 5u32, "2026-11-03T02:34Z", "x", "2026-11-02 22:34 x: x-lib-clock1 NOT GREEN, undone by lib_land_window as designed. Passed: 0 consumer-used signatures changed, apps/spiral compiles, and type_probe passed 4/4 (unix_clock 1 test typed, guid 2, reactors 8, erlang_map 7). Failed: document_test 21/22, 'the spiral library .spi files load as notebooks, one test cell per test block'. That test requires every lib .spi to round-trip byte-exact through the notebook form, and the new unix_clock.spi was the only file written without a trailing newline. Fixed by adding one LF. Also, before clock1, the launch caught a stale package.spiproj base (another lane added sized_array and metrics; rebased, with a recorded-base guard added). Rerun: x-lib-clock2, rule unchanged.")
inl note_of_lib_move_unix_clock_6 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK", 6u32, "2026-11-03T03:01Z", "x", "2026-11-02 23:01 x: x-lib-clock2 NOT GREEN, with the same single failure as clock1 (document_test 21/22, the notebook round-trip test; signatures, consumer compile and type_probe 4/4 all passed), so the trailing newline wasn't the cause. lib_land_window prints only the test name, so x-lib-doc2 runs document_test on the same mirror with full failure output, base tree first and then the 5 drafts, which shows whether the failing file is mine or comes from tonight's parallel lib edits (other lanes changed file_system, sm' and xsd_emit and added metrics.spi and sized_array.spi between 20:54 and 22:17). CORE SWITCH: the node's single-flight core is now 4E48590A5408C14B (8960CAB701FEF46E refused, 'verifying'). Every x launcher is re-pinned; tonight's earlier lands ran wholly on 8960, before the switch.")
inl note_of_lib_move_unix_clock_7 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK", 7u32, "2026-11-03T03:06Z", "x", "2026-11-02 23:06 x: ROOT CAUSE found by x-lib-doc2 (base 22 passed, draft 21/22 with the failure in erlang_map.spi): my new values_are_every_value_once block was inserted after the file's last block with two blank lines before it, and the notebook round trip normalizes to one, so once == spi_text failed (document_test.exs:513). Fixed to one blank line. All 5 lib drafts now have 0 triple newlines and a single final LF. The unix_clock trailing-newline fix from clock2 stays (harmless, and the right ending). Rerun x-lib-clock3 on core 4E48590A5408C14B, rule unchanged.")
inl note_of_lib_move_unix_clock_8 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK", 8u32, "2026-11-03T03:17Z", "x", "2026-11-02 23:17 x: STEP 1+3 LANDED on the box live lib (unstaged, window win-1793675828426): unix_clock.spi 03D6F2285043 (new), package.spiproj 2A0004126191 (live 5F520E796BAC plus unix_clock after erlang_term), guid.spi 72FF1D8AF174 (rust_unix_nanos gone; the hasher seeds from unix_clock nanos), reactors.spi 4BCE905C7EF0 (rust_physical_micros = nanos / 1000), erlang_map.spi 708AB4996ABD (map_values). PROOF x-lib-clock3 on core 4E48590A5408C14B: lib_land_window closed green (0 consumer-used signatures changed, apps/spiral compiles, document_test 22 passed, type_probe 4/4), lib_gate unix_clock 1/1, guid 2/2, reactors 8/8, erlang_map 7/7, 0 type errors. Undo on the node: spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261102-231207. NEXT: x-e2e-quote-clock1 (x's oauth1 and cells_executor on unix_clock and date_time, plus the json.quote switches) is launched.")
inl note_of_lib_move_unix_clock_9 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK", 9u32, "2026-11-03T03:42Z", "x", "2026-11-02 23:42 x: x-e2e-quote-clock2 NOT GREEN. The sim build passed (cells_executor on date_time::monotonic_milliseconds, typed deadline_ms and map_values all compile), but the client e2e failed 8 checks: 'xc post-thread sent 11 posts, the sim splits oauth1.spi into 17', and the read-back mismatched. Cause: the e2e posts oauth1.spi ITSELF as a thread and compares it with the committed fixture apps/client/e2e/thread-oauth1.expected.json, which the sim build regenerates from oauth1.spi only under -Accept. The fixture still held the old file (system_time, elapsed, since_epoch), so any edit to oauth1.spi needs its fixture regenerated (memory x-sim-fixtures-embed-client-sources). RERUN RULE, set before x-e2e-quote-clock3 runs: apps/sim/build.ps1 -Accept -fast 1 on the mirror, where the ONLY changed fixture must be thread-oauth1.expected.json; then sim build exit 0, client build exit 0 and e2e RUST-OK with no FAILED line, so xc's split of the new oauth1.spi equals the sim's (two independent splitters) and reads back byte-exact. The regenerated fixture comes back in OUT and lands with oauth1.spi.")
inl note_of_lib_move_unix_clock_10 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK", 10u32, "2026-11-03T04:07Z", "x", "2026-11-03 00:07 x: x-e2e-quote-clock3 NOT GREEN, judged honestly. The e2e half passed: sim build 0, client build 0, RUST-OK 37 tutorial steps + 5 extra cases, sim exit 0, and only thread-oauth1.expected.json changed. 141 requests vs 153 is fully explained: the new oauth1.spi threads as 11 posts, not 17, so there are 6 fewer POSTs and 6 fewer DELETEs. But the -Accept build exited 1 on CELL-BUDGET: my cells_executor.spi:75 memo_counted weighed 311 > 272, from its single long map_values line. FIX: memo_flags (result) is its own definition (an annotated erl_map term term view, then map_values), and memo_counted calls it. RULE for x-e2e-quote-clock4, set before it runs: the n9 rule PLUS sim accept exit 0 (cell budget clean); the request count must be 141, the 153 baseline minus the 12 shorter-thread requests.")
inl note_of_lib_move_unix_clock_11 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK", 11u32, "2026-11-03T04:31Z", "x", "2026-11-03 00:31 x: STEP 2 (x's half) LANDED (unstaged, window win-1793680193133): apps/client/oauth1.spi 15741F2FAB39 (clock_seed and unix_seconds read lib unix_clock; six private Rust clock bindings gone), apps/sim/spi/cells_executor.spi 9742F928099C (clock_ms reads date_time::monotonic_milliseconds; typed deadline_ms; memo_flags through erlang_map::map_values; flag_count folds a list), and apps/client/e2e/thread-oauth1.expected.json 25D526E8C76E (regenerated by -Accept; its program equals the new oauth1.spi byte for byte; 11 posts). PROOF x-e2e-quote-clock4 on core 73A6CCCC548DA7DF, green on every pre-registered condition: sim accept exit 0 (cell budget clean), only thread-oauth1.expected.json changed, sim build 0, client build 0, 141 requests (153 minus the predicted 12), RUST-OK 37 tutorial steps + 5 extra cases, sim exit 0. Clocks 1-3 failed honestly (wire's json shadow, the stale fixture, then the cell budget). LEFT: kit's 14 sites (kit lane) and lib file_system/trace, kept for the reasons in n4.")
inl note_of_lib_move_unix_clock_12 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK", 12u32, "2026-11-03T05:05Z", "x", "2026-11-03 01:05 x: x's share DONE and landed tonight (see the notes above), so team:x is removed from the tags. The other teams' tags stay, for the remaining kit and main sites. Resume condition for x: none, unless a lane hands an x site back.")
inl note_of_lib_move_unix_clock_13 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK", 13u32, "2026-11-04T14:10Z", "main", "11-04 10:1x main: MAIN'S SITE found. regex bench/host.spi elapsed_nanos is a private Rust Instant (OnceLock START, elapsed().as_nanos()), a MONOTONIC read that unix_clock's wall-clock unix_now_nanos (SystemTime) must not replace, since a benchmark across an NTP step would be wrong. DRAFT (kit drafts spiral\\LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK\\date_time.spi, base 8E2666DB0CE5): date_time.monotonic_nanoseconds () : u64, beside monotonic_milliseconds, with a Rust arm (the same Instant code) and a test that it never goes back; no Gleam arm on purpose (erlang:monotonic_time may be negative, so it cannot be a u64). Lib --check clean on a cloud lib copy; notebook gate and two-step land PENDING; then regex's elapsed_nanos reads lib and its private binding goes.")
inl note_of_lib_move_unix_clock_14 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK", 14u32, "2026-11-04T14:55Z", "main", "11-04 11:0x main date_time draft GREEN on europa: 27/27 twice in a row on a lib copy (monotonic_nanoseconds now a :~ function, so the Rust static START is one per program; the first draft was := and every inlined call site got its own static, which the test caught: b < a). The single date_time_utc Lua red in the first gate is a flake (absent in both reruns and in the live file's run). NEXT: two-step land of date_time.spi (base 8E2666DB0CE5), then regex bench/host.spi elapsed_nanos -> date_time.monotonic_nanoseconds and its private binding goes.")
inl note_of_lib_move_unix_clock_15 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK", 15u32, "2026-11-04T15:17Z", "main", "11-04 11:1x main: first date_time land closed RED at document_test 21/22 and undid itself cleanly: the inserted test ran straight into the next ///> gleam cell with no blank line between them (the here-string ate it; memory lib-land-roundtrip-first). Fixed, and lib_roundtrip.exs on europa now prints canonical true, fixpoint true. Re-land node half running.")
inl note_of_lib_move_unix_clock_16 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK", 16u32, "2026-11-04T16:12Z", "main", "11-04 12:1x main LANDED date_time.spi 1A9E63FCD880 (lib digest 7D28CCC6FF55E6E1) by the two-step land: node half green (document_test 22, type probe PASS, 0 respell drift), box half from the proof with fast checks (box lib had moved). New: :~ monotonic_nanoseconds () : u64 (Rust arm, process-start-relative Instant, failwith on other backends) + test the_monotonic_nanosecond_clock_does_not_go_back. CONSUMER: regex bench/bench.spi now calls date_time.monotonic_nanoseconds and the private elapsed_nanos in bench/host.spi is gone (unstaged); regex bench build on europa PENDING (node busy with TRAIN22).")
inl note_of_lib_move_unix_clock_17 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK", 17u32, "2026-11-04T16:43Z", "main", "11-04 12:5x main CONSUMER GREEN: regex build on europa (regex a9c2e259 + unstaged, spiral lib with the landed date_time 1A9E63FC) REGEX-OK; bench/bench.spi compiled to Rust in 8 s and regex-bench ran, its deterministic rows and arm counts agreeing, now timed by date_time.monotonic_nanoseconds; the private elapsed_nanos binding in bench/host.spi is gone. The clock moved to lib and its one consumer uses it: DONE.")
inl note_of_lib_move_civil_date_1 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-CIVIL-DATE", 1u32, "2026-11-01T22:45Z", "main", "11-01 18:4x main (lib-reshape generic-code sweep). SITES (read in place). Civil date from days / days from civil: x apps/sim/spi/world.spi:277 day_of_year, :279 days_from_civil (i32 copy of lib date_time.spi:1331), :285-299 year_of_era/day_in_era/month_of/civil_of/civil_from_days, :301 moment_of (ISO parse), :305 padded, :308-317 clock_text/date_text/stamped (ISO format); kit src/agile_note_model/model.spi:215 civil_of_days and :227 utc_stamp (pure Spiral, the best lib seed); kit host macros inlining the same arithmetic in one multi-line $'...' each: src/kit_adoption/host.spi:28 cutoff_day, src/kit_do_lab/host.spi:38 note_age_days, src/kit_do_write_host/host.spi:30 clock_filled. Local offset / local stamp via Win32: src/kit_receipt/receipt.spi:23 local_offset_minutes (GetLocalTime vs GetSystemTime, 15-minute rounding; callers agile_note_model/model.spi:149, kit_do_file_steps/steps.spi:33,58, kit_do_process/run.spi:108, kit_process_table/run.spi:32) and :34 clock_text; src/kit_experiments/ledger_host.spi:30 local_stamp (second Win32 copy). LIB TARGET: date_time (existing). Kit cannot take date_time.now/utc_now as is: their Rust arm needs the chrono crate, which the kit crates avoid; the new functions are arithmetic in Spiral plus one granular host read each. TYPED SHAPE: :== civil = { year : i64; month : month_of_year; day : i64 } with month_of_year a union (or a nominal checked 1..12), :! epoch_days = i64, :! utc_offset_minutes = i64; civil_of_days (d : epoch_days) : civil, days_of_civil (c : civil) : epoch_days (the existing days_from_civil re-expressed on the record), iso_utc_text (s : unix_seconds) : string and iso_local_text (s : unix_seconds) (o : utc_offset_minutes) : string, iso_utc_parsed (text : string) : option unix_seconds; local_offset_minutes () : utc_offset_minutes with granular one-expression arms (Rust: two small extern bindings GetLocalTime/GetSystemTime under cfg(windows), 0 elsewhere or libc localtime_r; F# TimeZoneInfo.Local.GetUtcOffset; Gleam calendar.local_offset). Uses LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK's unix_seconds. DoD: (1) date_time definitions with a :# block (1970-01-01 = day 0, 2000-02-29 round trip, 2026-11-01 = 20758, 1969-12-31 = -1, ISO text of 0 = 1970-01-01T00:00:00Z, parse of that text round trips, offset in -720..840 and a multiple of 15) passing in Cells on rust, fsharp and gleam; (2) every site above calls the lib functions, proven by kit's touched notebooks + crate regen and x's xsim build; (3) the copies are deleted (the three kit host macros shrink to lib calls, kit_receipt and kit_experiments share the lib offset).")
inl note_of_lib_move_civil_date_2 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-CIVIL-DATE", 2u32, "2026-11-04T01:13Z", "x", "2026-11-03 21:11 x: ORPHAN SWEEP (MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP, x's corner: open x items with no note in 48 h). x's share is concrete and CPU-light: apps/sim/spi/world.spi civil-date copies (day_of_year, days_from_civil and friends at :277-299) switch to lib date_time. x drafts it now.")
inl note_of_lib_move_civil_date_3 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-CIVIL-DATE", 3u32, "2026-11-04T01:16Z", "x", "2026-11-03 21:16 x: x's SHARE DRAFTED (kit drafts x\\LIB-MOVE-CIVIL-DATE\\world.spi, base 561F876D817C -> B4CDE32E0EA6, formatted, max cell 270, 480 -> 463 lines): the sim's 7 hand-rolled civil-date helpers (day_of_year, days_from_civil, year_of_era, day_in_era, month_of, civil_of, civil_from_days) collapse to 2 thin i32 wrappers over lib date_time (days_from_civil in i64; civil_from_days via civil_of_micros, whose first three fields are y m d). Lib uses floor_div, which is correct before 1970 where the sim's truncating '/' was not; for the sim's 2026 dates they agree, and the sim accept (fixtures embed timelines and stamps) proves it. Runs as x-next5 after x-replay2.")
inl note_of_lib_move_civil_date_4 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-CIVIL-DATE", 4u32, "2026-11-04T01:30Z", "x", "2026-11-03 21:30 x: x-next5 now also carries the 3 line-width fixes the default standards rules flagged in apps/sim/spi/cells_executor.spi (base 3C5E776B7871 -> draft CFCE9C3B5DC0: 'at' and 'text_at' bodies wrapped, ok_value's tag test named ok_tagged; widest line 120, max cell 271). Both files are hash-guarded in land-x-next5.")
inl note_of_lib_move_civil_date_5 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-CIVIL-DATE", 5u32, "2026-11-04T11:34Z", "x", "2026-11-04 07:34 x: x-next5c (job-1793782508291, pinned core 0758BAF4, 2 h 32 min) PASSED its pre-registered rule and LANDED (9 hash-guarded drafts + 42 regenerated outputs, 0 conflicts): sim accept 0 with NO fixture changed, sim build 0, client build 0, e2e RUST-OK 37 + 5, all Rust units under 1k, census SAME over 77, notebook gate one fresh process per file: feed_merge 6/6, timeline_serve 4/4 (x-next5b's 3/4 was the stale warm server). LANDED for this item: apps/sim/spi/world.spi B4CDE32E0EA6: the sim's 7 civil-date helpers are now 2 thin wrappers over lib date_time; no fixture changed. x's share is DONE.")
inl note_of_lib_move_civil_date_6 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-CIVIL-DATE", 6u32, "2026-11-04T17:03Z", "x", "2026-11-04 13:03 x: x's SHARE DRAFTED (it was NOT done: client/requests/requests.spi kept its own days->civil copy). (1) lib date_time.spi gains civil_of_days (i64 -> year, month, day), the inverse of the existing days_from_civil, as small cells civil_era / civil_year_of_era / civil_day_of_year / civil_month / civil_month_day (Hinnant's algorithm with floor_div, as requests had it); tests civil_of_days_names_known_dates (0 -> 1970-01-01, -1 -> 1969-12-31, 11016 -> 2000-02-29) and civil_of_days_inverts_days_from_civil (round trip over -719468..2932896), rust and gleam. date_time 1A9E63FCD880 -> 4582C7AD3F17 (kit drafts spiral\\LIB-MOVE-CIVIL-DATE), 0 new cells over 272. (2) requests.spi drops era_parts/year_of_era/month_of/day_parts and its civil_of becomes a 3-line i32<->i64 adapter over date_time::civil_of_days (EB1622AE69A1 -> 03044B269FB3, 152 -> 136 lines). europa --check 0 for both. PROOF rides x-next7 (now 31 files): its notebook gate runs lib date_time's tests (execution, not just typing), and e2e covers requests. land-x-next7 lands date_time through lib_land_window FIRST (base 1A9E63FCD880, proven draft 4582C7AD3F17), then the x files. The kit share (agile_note etc.) stays with kit.")
inl note_of_lib_move_civil_date_7 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-CIVIL-DATE", 7u32, "2026-11-05T00:48Z", "x", "2026-11-04 20:48 x: PRE-LAND FIX (caught by running lib_land_window's document_test checks on the draft BEFORE x-next7): date_time.spi did not round-trip spi -> livemd -> spi, because no blank line separated the civil_of_days_inverts_days_from_civil test from ':= micros_of_guid_prefix'. Blank line added: draft 4582C7AD3F17 -> 5ACE9C13DD10, unproven so far (x-next7 proves it), land-x-next7 pins updated. The same defect made x-next6's lib land close red at 20:35.")
inl note_of_lib_move_civil_date_8 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-CIVIL-DATE", 8u32, "2026-11-05T03:07Z", "x", "2026-11-04 23:07 x: date_time draft stripped of its 17 inherited /// section headings (5ACE9C13DD10 -> ECE2A9DD6806; round trip OK 48/48); land-x-next7 pin updated.")
inl note_of_lib_move_civil_date_9 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-CIVIL-DATE", 9u32, "2026-11-05T06:26Z", "x", "2026-11-05 02:26 x: CONTROL (box, pack40 core DDCA78971B4EAB36, run_notebook --gate): the STRIPPED date_time draft ECE2A9DD6806 passes 46/46, the lua target included. So the heading strip does NOT break timestamp_guid_from_timestamp; x-next7b's lua red came from the node's compiler changing mid-run (pack36 -> pack38 at 00:34, main's unannounced ship). The compiler lane confirms no lua codegen change across those packs, so a mid-run core swap is the remaining suspect. The unstripped arm is still running as the formal control. x-next7 re-runs on the node (now a stable pack40) after x-next8b frees the shared mirror.")
inl note_of_lib_move_civil_date_10 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-CIVIL-DATE", 10u32, "2026-11-05T10:10Z", "x", "2026-11-05 06:09 x: LANDED via x-next7 (green run x-next7c, node). lib date_time ECE2A9DD6806 (chrono-free civil date math; 17 headings stripped) and requests.spi.")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_1 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 1u32, "2026-11-01T22:48Z", "main", "11-01 18:5x main (lib-reshape generic-code sweep). SITES (read in place). lib, three partial quoters with different coverage: json.spi:13 quote (\\\\ \\\" \\n \\r \\t, other controls raw); json_schema.spi:97-108 json_escaped/json_quoted_from/json_quoted (same set, char by char); conversation.spi:46-69 json_specials/json_escape_of/json_string (only \\\\ \\\" \\n). x: apps/client/jsonl/jsonl.spi:11 quoted and apps/client/wire.spi:25 json_string (both serde_json::Value::from(s).to_string(), Rust only); apps/sim/spi/events.spi:45-64 hex_digit/unicode_escape/short_escape/control_escape/controls_from/without_controls/quoted (the only complete one, Gleam-safe Spiral); apps/sim/spi/simframes/simframes.spi:226 json_quoted (erlang json:encode + iolist_to_binary). kit: src/kit_memory_model/model.spi:152-153 escaped/quoted; src/agile_todo_model/model.spi:329 json_escaped; src/kit_grep_query/search.spi:84 json_text and src/kit_read_query/slice.spi:4 json_text (byte-identical multi-line host macros); src/kit_table_rows/rows.spi:13 escaped (\\\\ and \\\" only). NOT ESCAPING AT ALL (latent bug if a title holds a quote): src/agile_planning_model/model.spi:186 json_quoted, src/agile_task_inspection/task_inspection.spi:91 json_string, src/agile_task_listing/task_listing.spi:165 json_string. Excluded: lib xsd_emit.spi:107 escape_text (Spiral literal escaping, not JSON). LIB TARGET: json (existing module); json_schema and conversation import it. TYPED SHAPE: :! json_text = string (a nominal for already-encoded JSON, so a quoted value is never quoted twice or concatenated as raw text); quote (s : string) : json_text; field (name : string) (value : json_text) : json_text; json_text_raw (t : json_text) : string at the output edge. Implementation in plain Spiral (x events.spi's algorithm: short escapes for \\b \\t \\n \\f \\r, \\u00XX for other controls), no host macro, so it runs on every backend; an optional Rust fast arm may be one expression (serde is not a lib dependency, so no). DoD: (1) json.quote with a :# block (empty, plain, quote, backslash, each short escape, U+0001 -> \\u0001, U+001F, non-ASCII kept verbatim, round trip through json_scan's string reader) passing in Cells on rust, fsharp and gleam; (2) lib's json_schema and conversation call it and their copies are deleted; (3) every x and kit site above switched, proven by x's client + xsim builds and kit's touched notebooks + crate regen (kit_grep_query and kit_read_query JSON receipts byte-identical on a fixture); (4) the three non-escaping kit sites get a regression row with a quote in the title.")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_2 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 2u32, "2026-11-02T01:20Z", "kit", "11-01 21:19 kit, the three kit sites read in place: kit_memory_model/model.spi:152 (escaped: \\\\ \\\" \\n \\r \\t) and agile_todo_model/model.spi:329 (json_escaped: the same set) are PARTIAL (controls below 0x20 other than \\n\\r\\t pass raw, which is invalid JSON only for those rare inputs); kit_grep_query/search.spi:84 json_text is COMPLETE (\\u00XX for all controls) but a multi-line host block. None of kit's three is \"no escaping\". KIT PLAN: when lib json.quote is complete (RFC 8259; lift x apps/sim events.spi:45-64, the complete Gleam-safe Spiral version), kit replaces all three with json.quote (TRAIN9), adds a test with quote, backslash, \\n and \\x01 to agile_todo_model and kit_memory_model, and removes the host block in kit_grep_query.")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_3 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 3u32, "2026-11-02T01:20Z", "main", "main 21:2x CORRECTION from kit (read in place): kit's copies are PARTIAL, not 'no escaping'. kit_memory_model/model.spi:152 and agile_todo_model/model.spi:329 escape backslash, quote, \\n, \\r and \\t, but other controls below 0x20 (\\b \\f \\x01) pass raw; kit_grep_query/search.spi:84 json_text is COMPLETE (\\u00XX for every control) but a multi-line host block. The three non-escaping copies must be in x or lib; re-locate them before quoting the claim again. PLAN (agreed with kit): (1) lib json.quote becomes complete per RFC 8259 by lifting x's apps/sim events.spi:45-64 (complete and Gleam-safe), with tests for quote, backslash, \\n, \\x01 and \\u001f; owner x, since lib-reshape has finished. (2) kit switches its three sites to json.quote in TRAIN9. (3) The other copies in x and lib follow.")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_4 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 4u32, "2026-11-02T01:26Z", "x", "2026-11-01 21:26 x: LIB HALF STARTED (main 21:2x handed it to x). Draft %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE\\json.spi (base 514F84651989): json.quote is now RFC 8259 complete, lifted from x apps/sim events.spi:45-64. It escapes backslash and quote, uses short forms \\b \\t \\n \\f \\r, and writes every other control below 0x20 as \\u00XX via hex_digit/unicode_escape/controls_from (unicode.char_of, which sits before json in lib's module order). 3 new test blocks on rust + gleam: quote/backslash, \\n\\t short forms, \\x01 and \\x1f as \\u0001\\u001f. Behaviour change for callers: only strings containing \\b, \\f or other controls now escape (before, they passed raw and produced invalid JSON). PROOF x-json-quote1 (Europa, lib_gate -Test on the 3 blocks), rule written before the run: PASS iff 3 executed, 3 passed, 0 failed/unsupported on both targets. Land through lib_land_window after lib-reshape R1b+R2 closes (re-base then), then tell kit for TRAIN9.")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_5 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 5u32, "2026-11-02T01:30Z", "x", "2026-11-01 21:30 x: x-json-quote1 (Europa, 55 s) by n4's rule: PASS. The mirror's json.spi equalled the draft's base (514F84651989), and the draft C82278F5C371 reports 'tests: passed 3 failed 0' for the 3 filtered blocks (15 in the file), type errors 0. A target-level failure would mark its test failed, so rust and gleam both passed. LAND: lib_land_window -Draft json.spi=<store> -BaseHash 514F84651989 after lib-reshape R1b+R2 closes. If R1b moved json.spi, rebuild the draft from live first (the swap anchors on the old quote body). Then tell kit, which switches its 3 partial copies to json.quote in TRAIN9.")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_6 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 6u32, "2026-11-02T02:07Z", "x", "2026-11-01 22:07 x: LANDED 22:06 as a guarded copy (tree-write win-1793585196666; TRAIN8s builds from a snapshot): lib/spiral/json.spi 514F84651989 -> C82278F5C371, the exact text gated 3/3 on Europa (n5). Undo: spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\x-json-quote-20261101-220636. Consumer proof: x-verify48 (x has no json.quote caller, so it only proves lib still compiles in x's build). NEXT: tell kit to switch its 3 partial copies in TRAIN9.")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_7 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 7u32, "2026-11-02T02:12Z", "main", "main 22:1x lib half DONE: x landed the RFC 8259-complete json.quote at 22:06 as a guarded copy (lib/spiral/json.spi 514F84651989 -> C82278F5C371, the europa-gated text). Kit is told and switches its 3 partial copies in TRAIN9. The remaining copies in x and lib follow under this item.")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_8 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 8u32, "2026-11-02T02:15Z", "kit", "11-01 22:15 kit: switched (unstaged, TRAIN9) after x's complete lib json.quote (22:06). (1) agile_todo_model finding_json now uses json.quote for path, id and text (the partial json_escaped is removed), plus the test finding_json_escapes_quotes_backslashes_newlines_and_controls (quote, backslash, \\n and \\x01 -> \\u0001); (2) kit_grep_query json_text = json.quote text (a 6-line host block removed). (3) kit_memory_model escaped/quoted was NOT switched: it writes Spiral string literals into generated memory .spi modules (Spiral source, not JSON), so JSON's \\u00XX escapes do not apply there; the sweep misclassified it. Ratchet ok for both packages; the notebook proof rides the TRAIN9 pre-proof.")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_9 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 9u32, "2026-11-02T06:47Z", "kit", "11-02 02:5x kit: CODE SIZE. lib json.quote's controls_from takes a static c, so every consumer unrolls all 32 control passes. Each of the 32 sm'.replace calls has its escape string precomputed, which gives a 94-line function in each crate. kit TRAIN9 stopped at the crate gate on this: agile_todo_lines todo_lines.rs went 960 -> 1053, and a :~ wrapper alone only got it to 1032. kit_grep_query is 780. FIX: make c dynamic (~c), so it becomes a runtime loop with the same output. Base json.spi 794C9C3AAEA3CA73. PROOF kit-json-dyn (node, job-1793602015364). Rule, written before the run: PASS iff lib_program_gate runs the 3 quote blocks with 3 passed, 0 failed, 0 type errors, AND the regenerated agile_todo_lines is under 1000 lines with the crate gate at 0 over. Then land with land-lib-program -Note LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE/<this n> and run kit TRAIN10.\nPROGRAM (kit do <lib> -):\nedit json.spi expect files 1 replacements 1\nreplace once \":~ ^ controls_from (c : i32) (t : string) : string =\" with \":~ ^ controls_from (~c : i32) (t : string) : string =\" RETRACTED 02:5x by kit: the diagnosis was WRONG. controls_from is already a runtime loop, because :~ ^ join-point arguments are dynamic, so the ~c program changes nothing (proof kit-json-dyn: lib gate GREEN 3/3, but todo_lines stays at 1032). Its 94 lines are just the loop body: char_of validation, the short-escape option chain and the \\u00XX list join. DO NOT LAND this program. See the next note for the real fix.")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_10 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 10u32, "2026-11-02T06:59Z", "kit", "11-02 02:5x kit: RUST FAST ARM for json.quote, the 'optional Rust fast arm' this item's design allows. Rust now escapes in one pass: kit's old proven complete escaper (char::from(34/92), no backslashes in the macro) plus short forms for codes 8/9/10/12/13 via b\"btn_fr\". Every other backend keeps the plain Spiral path unchanged. A new test covers \\b \\f \\r on rust and gleam. Why: the Spiral body generates about 120 lines in every Rust consumer, and that pushed kit agile_todo_lines over the 1000-line crate gate (TRAIN9 stop). PROOF kit-json-fast (node, job-1793602449709), rule written before the run (note 9 + gate): lib_program_gate GREEN, 4 passed 0 failed, 0 type errors, base 794C9C3AAEA3CA73 -> target 20C39CB971506A36; kit regen agile_todo_lines 1032 -> 909, kit_grep_query 780 -> 662, crate gate 0 over of 273; agile_todo_model notebook 13/13 on the fast arm. Round trip: canonical true, fixpoint true. LAND: land-lib-program -Note LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE/10 -File json.spi -Base 794C9C3AAEA3CA73 -Target 20C39CB971506A36.\nPROGRAM (kit do <lib> -):\nedit json.spi\npatch <<<\n@@ -29,3 +29,10 @@\n := quote (s : string) : string =\n-    := escaped = s |> sm'.replace \"\\\\\" \"\\\\\\\\\" |> sm'.replace \"\\\"\" \"\\\\\\\"\" |> controls_from 0i32\n-    sm'.concat_list \"\" [ \"\\\"\"; escaped; \"\\\"\" ]\n+    run_target \\|\n+        | Rust => \\ () =>\n+            $'std::rc::Rc::<str>::from({ let q = char::from(34u8); let b = char::from(92u8); let mut out = String::from(q); \\\n+                for c in (!s).chars() { let n = c as u32; match n { 34 | 92 => { out.push(b); out.push(c); } 8 | 9 | 10 | 12 | 13 => \\\n+                { out.push(b); out.push(char::from(b\"btn_fr\"[(n - 8) as usize])); } n if n < 32 => out.push_str(&format\\!(\"{b}u{n:04x}\")), \\\n+                _ => out.push(c) } } out.push(q); out }.as_str())' : string\n+        | _ => \\ () =>\n+            := escaped = s |> sm'.replace \"\\\\\" \"\\\\\\\\\" |> sm'.replace \"\\\"\" \"\\\\\\\"\" |> controls_from 0i32\n+            sm'.concat_list \"\" [ \"\\\"\"; escaped; \"\\\"\" ]\n@@ -41,2 +48,7 @@\n     quote \"x\\ny\\tz\" |> _assert_eq \"\\\"x\\\\ny\\\\tz\\\"\"\n\n+///> rust\n+///> gleam\n+:# quote_uses_short_forms_for_backspace_formfeed_and_return =\n+    quote (sm'.concat_list \"\" [ unicode.char_of 8i32; unicode.char_of 12i32; unicode.char_of 13i32 ]) |> _assert_eq \"\\\"\\\\b\\\\f\\\\r\\\"\"\n+\n>>>")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_11 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 11u32, "2026-11-03T00:53Z", "x", "2026-11-02 20:5x x: x's remaining copies, read in the tree. (1) apps/client/wire.spi json_string and (2) apps/client/jsonl/jsonl.spi quoted both call serde_json::Value::from(s).to_string(), which matches the complete Rust fast arm of lib json.quote byte for byte (short forms for 8/9/10/12/13, lowercase \\u00xx otherwise, quote and backslash escaped, DEL kept). Both are DRAFTED as json::quote s in kit drafts x/LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE (wire A99E258DE7EB to 84D5D141C3C2, jsonl 6BC0D61A28C2 to A3688F90194D). (3) The sim simframes json_quoted uses Erlang json:encode and writes byte-compared frame files, so it stays until a frames proof covers the switch. (4) The escape helpers in the sim events module are the DECODE side (an unescaper), not a quoter, so they're out of scope; their replacement is the Cells json_value parser once lib can host it. PRE-REGISTERED RULE (x-e2e-quote-clock1, one x e2e run together with LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK's x sites after x-lib-clock1 lands): sim build exit 0, client build exit 0, and x e2e RUST-OK with the request count unchanged from the last green e2e and no FAILED line.")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_12 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 12u32, "2026-11-03T03:29Z", "x", "2026-11-02 23:29 x: x-e2e-quote-clock1 failed at the sim build. wire.spi declares its own nominal ':! json = serde_json::Value' (line 14), so inside that module json::quote resolves to the local type, not the lib json module (ETY-TermError: Got serde_json::Value, Expected .quote). The wire switch is DROPPED from this batch. Making it needs wire's json nominal renamed (serde_value) across the module, a separate slice with its own e2e. jsonl.spi doesn't see a json name (its opens aren't transitive) and stays in x-e2e-quote-clock2 with the clock sites, rule unchanged.")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_13 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 13u32, "2026-11-03T03:32Z", "x", "2026-11-02 23:32 x: DECIDED by rule (the item replaces PARTIAL or hand-rolled quoters): wire.spi's json_string STAYS as serde_json::Value::from(s).to_string(). It's serde's own complete RFC 8259 escaper, in a module whose whole JSON layer is typed serde_json::Value (the json nominal; about 900 references in the file). Switching would mean renaming that nominal module-wide to free the json name, which is risky churn for a one-line dedupe that changes no bytes. So x's share ends with jsonl.spi (in x-e2e-quote-clock2) plus simframes (Erlang json:encode, kept for its byte-compared frames).")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_14 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 14u32, "2026-11-03T04:31Z", "x", "2026-11-03 00:31 x: jsonl.spi LANDED on lib json::quote (A3688F90194D), proven in x-e2e-quote-clock4 (client build 0, RUST-OK 37+5). x's share is DONE: jsonl switched; wire's serde quoter and simframes' Erlang json:encode kept by recorded rule (n13, n11).")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_15 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 15u32, "2026-11-03T05:05Z", "x", "2026-11-03 01:05 x: x's share DONE and landed tonight (see the notes above), so team:x is removed from the tags. The other teams' tags stay, for the remaining kit and main sites. Resume condition for x: none, unless a lane hands an x site back.")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_16 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 16u32, "2026-11-04T20:58Z", "kit", "11-04 22:4x kit: a LIVE repro of why one complete quoter matters: `kit agile show <root> KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS --json` (installed TRAIN14c) prints invalid JSON (\"Invalid control character at char 25475\" in python json.load). A note on that item holds a raw BEL (0x07) where \"\\agile todos\" was typed (a \\a escape turned into a control char on the way in), and the JSON writer passes it through unescaped. RFC 8259 requires \\u0007 there, which is exactly the control-below-0x20 clause of this item's title. Test to add with the fix: a note containing 0x07 and 0x1B round-trips through show --json as \\u0007 / \\u001b.")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_17 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 17u32, "2026-11-04T21:27Z", "kit", "11-04 23:2x kit: kit's two partial quoters behind `agile show --json` are FIXED (unstaged): agile_note_model.note_json_at copied each note's stored Spiral literal straight into JSON (Spiral's \\\" \\\\ \\n escapes happen to be JSON, so it mostly worked, but a raw control byte like the 0x07 on KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS passed through); it now decodes the literal with the model's own unquoted and re-encodes with lib json.quote (complete: quote, backslash, every control below 0x20). agile_task_inspection.json_string wrapped title/tags/deps in quotes with NO escaping at all (a quote in a title broke the JSON); it is now json.quote. Touching note_json_at also migrated it off rust_std_string concat5 to sm'.concat_list (the style hook's rule). europa --check ok (note_listing, task_inspection); consumers sized in job kit-size-json; the notes CLI checks (exact at/author/text output) ride the next train.")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_18 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 18u32, "2026-11-05T23:26Z", "main", "main 11-05 19:3x CHECK on the installed kit (kit.exe of 11-03 06:07): 'agile show <backlog> KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS --json' still emits the raw 0x07 at char 25475, so it's still invalid per RFC 8259 (PowerShell's ConvertFrom-Json is lenient and accepts it; python json.load rejects it, per kit n). kit's fix (note_json_at + json_string through lib json.quote, 11-04 23:2x) is not installed yet: TRAIN32 has kit reds, so it won't install, and the fix rides TRAIN33. Verify after that install with a strict parser, plus the 0x07/0x1B round-trip test kit named.")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_19 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 19u32, "2026-11-06T10:10Z", "main", "main 11-06 06:1x groom: BLOCKED on kit's TRAIN33 install (kit's json.quote fix for agile show --json). The node is back as of 06:05, so TRAIN33 gets a verdict from its node log this round. Resume = on install, rerun the 11-05 19:3x check (agile show KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS --json through a strict parser).")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_20 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 20u32, "2026-11-06T14:43Z", "main", "main 11-06 14:5x DONE, proof: on the installed kit (TRAIN33, 07:05) 'agile show <backlog> KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS --json' is 28,246 bytes with no raw 0x07, and System.Text.Json.JsonDocument.Parse (strict RFC 8259) accepts it (root Object). On 11-05 the same call had a raw 0x07 at char 25475. Dep LIB-GENERIC-AUDIT is Done.")
inl note_of_lib_move_x_sim_erlang_1 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-X-SIM-ERLANG", 1u32, "2026-11-01T22:51Z", "main", "11-01 18:5x main (lib-reshape generic-code sweep). x already calls lib erlang_* 72 times; these are the leftovers (read in place). ALREADY IN LIB -> switch: apps/sim/spi/simframes/simframes.spi:148 base_name (= erlang_file.spi:12 base_name), :201 dir_of (= erlang_file absolute_path |> dir_name, :14/:10), :261 absolute (= erlang_file absolute_path), :217 printed's io:put_chars (= erlang_file.spi:36 put_text), :229 nfc (= unicode.spi:164 nfc); apps/sim/spi/cells_executor.spi:13-18 at/keyed (maps get/from_list = erlang_map.spi:20 map_get / :30 map_of_pairs, typed erl_map k v instead of raw term), :36-37, :365, :368, :392 (maps get with fallback = map_get + optionm default), :95 leak_swap (erlang put = erlang_process.spi:373 dictionary_put), :111 element_at (= erlang_port.spi:52 element); apps/sim/spi/sim_serve.spi:441 has_key / :443 field_or (maps is_key/get = erlang_map map_has/map_get), :445 escaped (HTML & < > = xml.spi:401 escape_text_xml). GAPS -> add to lib: (a) erlang_term is_map / is_tuple / list_length / list_nth (cells_executor.spi:47, :110, :67, :323, :330); erlang_port.element moves to erlang_term (it is a term op, not a port op) with erlang_port re-using it; (b) erlang_file put_error_text (io:put_chars standard_error: cells_executor.spi:399 start_failed, simframes.spi:280 warned), or console.write_error_line's Gleam arm if it lacks one; (c) erlang_process memory_total_bytes (cells_executor.spi:83 beam_mb divides it); (d) env plain argv on Gleam (simframes.spi:130 args_text joins init:get_plain_arguments with NUL; lib env.spi:175 env_gleam_argv already binds it, so expose command_line_arguments on Gleam if not already reachable); (e) sm' byte_length on Gleam (simframes.spi:151 byte_count, erlang:byte_size). Clock reads (cells_executor.spi:88, :257) belong to LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK; simframes.spi:226 json_quoted to LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE. TYPED SHAPE: typed erl_map k v at every map site (no raw term maps), :! byte_count = i32 for byte_length so it is not mixed with grapheme lengths, put_error_text : string -> (), memory_total_bytes : () -> u64. Each lib addition is one granular erlang_term::apply expression. DoD: (1) lib additions with :# blocks passing in Cells on gleam (and rust/fsharp where the function has arms); (2) every x site above calls lib, proven by x's xsim build + its scenario checks; (3) x's private copies deleted.")
inl note_of_lib_move_x_sim_erlang_2 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-X-SIM-ERLANG", 2u32, "2026-11-01T23:22Z", "x", "2026-11-01 19:22 x (groom): DEDUP with LIB-ERLANG-TYPED-STDLIB (x, 11-01, 45%). The split: that item OWNS the lib wrappers, and this one OWNS switching x's call sites. erlang_text, erlang_map and erlang_file are x's new modules from today: proven on Europa (4/4, 3/3, 5/5), committed by the user (73e4d863/b3fd292b), but NOT yet registered in lib's package.spiproj (that item's n10 land plan), hence the new dep. Gap (b) is DONE there: erlang_file now has put_error_text and file_appended (x-erlang-file2, 5/5). sim_serve's url_decoded/unescaped/pct/zero_padded/trimmed_end/dir_of switch is drafted as a hash-guarded applier (LIB-ERLANG-TYPED-STDLIB n11). This item's simframes, cells_executor and sim_serve maps/xml sites remain, after registration.")
inl note_of_lib_move_x_sim_erlang_3 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-X-SIM-ERLANG", 3u32, "2026-11-02T01:38Z", "x", "2026-11-01 21:38 x: SLICE 2 APPLIED (unstaged, x/apps/sim/spi/simframes/simframes.spi, base 1C78B5B9398F, each anchor found exactly once). 6 raw calls now go through lib: base_name -> erlang_file::base_name, dir_of -> erlang_file::dir_name (erlang_file::absolute_path path), absolute -> erlang_file::absolute_path, printed's io:put_chars -> erlang_file::put_text, warned's stderr put_chars -> erlang_file::put_error_text, and nfc -> unicode::nfc (the same Erlang function behind a typed Gleam external). simframes has 0 raw filename/io calls left. With sim_serve's 8 (LIB-ERLANG-TYPED-STDLIB n11), 14 of main's ~25 sites are done. Left: cells_executor maps/at/keyed (to erl_map), its element/put/memory/argv gaps (a), and sim_serve has_key/field_or/escaped (erl_map, xml). Proof: x-verify48 tonight.")
inl note_of_lib_move_x_sim_erlang_4 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-X-SIM-ERLANG", 4u32, "2026-11-02T01:40Z", "x", "2026-11-01 21:40 x: + sim_serve escaped -> xml::escape_text_xml (byte-identical: the same & < > replacements). 15 of ~25 sites done. HELD for a probe first: has_key/field_or need 'erlang_map::erl_map m' to wrap a raw JSON term, a cross-module nominal construction not yet proven in x. A compile error there would sink the overnight verify, so it goes to a scoped node probe once R1b closes.")
inl note_of_lib_move_x_sim_erlang_5 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-X-SIM-ERLANG", 5u32, "2026-11-03T07:34Z", "x", "2026-11-03 03:34 x: GROOM. Progress from 11-02/03 that belongs here: cells_executor.spi (landed 9742F928099C, proven by x-e2e-quote-clock4) moved its raw memo calls (maps:values, lists:filter, erlang:length) onto erlang_map::map_values over map_view and a Spiral fold, and moved clock_ms and the deadline arithmetic (erlang monotonic_time + - max) onto date_time::monotonic_milliseconds with a typed deadline_ms. THE n-1 HOLD IS RESOLVED: 'erlang_map::erl_map m wrapping a raw term, a cross-module nominal construction not yet proven in x' is proven in the same land (memo_flags: an annotated erl_map term term = erlang_map::map_view (...)). NEXT STEP: sim_serve has_key and field_or onto erlang_map::map_view plus map_get_or, then the remaining raw sites (term type tests, list length/nth, BEAM memory) onto lib, each slice proven by the x e2e with the -Accept sim build. Owner x.")
inl note_of_lib_move_x_sim_erlang_6 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-X-SIM-ERLANG", 6u32, "2026-11-03T08:00Z", "x", "2026-11-03 03:59 x: CORRECTION to n-1: sim_serve has_key and field_or were already on erlang_map (the 11-02 slice). STATE: next slice DRAFTED, not run: kit drafts x\\LIB-MOVE-X-SIM-ERLANG\\cells_executor.spi on base 9742F928099C. All 8 raw maps calls go through typed views: at and keyed over erl_map term term (atom keys), text_at and list_at over erl_map string term, both indexed over erl_map i32 term, and no_map for maps:new; 0 raw maps calls are left. Remaining raw sites after it: application, code, counters, element, is_tuple/is_map, lists nth/last/append, filelib, io, erlang put/memory/div in cells_executor; json, lists:join, iolist_to_binary, init args, byte_size and unicode in simframes. NEXT STEP: one x e2e (-Accept sim build, client build, RUST-OK) when the run restarts. Waits on: the next run.")
inl note_of_lib_move_x_sim_erlang_7 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-X-SIM-ERLANG", 7u32, "2026-11-03T10:23Z", "x", "2026-11-03 06:23 x: PRE-REGISTERED RULE for x-sim-maps1 (scratchpad launch-x-sim-maps, launched after x-census-cli5 frees the node, on the core current at launch, with a pinned compiler copy): cells_executor.spi (draft on base 9742F928099C) with the 8 raw maps calls on typed erl_map views. Pass = sim accept exit 0 with NO fixture changed (no client source is touched), sim build 0, client build 0, x e2e RUST-OK with no FAILED line, and the request count 141 (unchanged from x-e2e-quote-clock4).")
inl note_of_lib_move_x_sim_erlang_8 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-X-SIM-ERLANG", 8u32, "2026-11-03T13:22Z", "x", "2026-11-03 09:22 x: x-sim-maps1 GREEN on the n7 rule (job-1793708295691, pinned core 21D5992EDB80D270 at both ends): sim accept 0 with no fixture changed, sim build 0, client build 0, e2e 141 requests RUST-OK 37 steps + 5 cases. LANDED unstaged in a tree-write window: apps/sim/spi/cells_executor.spi 9742F928099C -> 633D34656C51 (8 raw maps calls through typed erl_map views: atom_map, no_map, text_map, indexed as erl_map i32 term), plus 24 regenerated outputs via node-proof -Land (0 conflicts; sim frames and split parts).")
inl note_of_lib_move_x_sim_erlang_9 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-X-SIM-ERLANG", 9u32, "2026-11-03T13:43Z", "x", "2026-11-03 09:43 x: NEXT SLICE drafted and folded into x-events1 (X-SOTA-MODEL n20; same x mirror, so one node run). Lib (kit drafts spiral\\LIB-MOVE-X-SIM-ERLANG\\erlang_term.spi, base FAEF00C04AF9 -> 6A63D080B3B0): a 'shapes and native lists' section with is_map, is_tuple, element_at, length_of, item_at (0-based), last_of, appended, plus one gleam block covering all seven. No lib module opens erlang_term, so the names shadow nothing. Sim (kit drafts x\\LIB-MOVE-X-SIM-ERLANG\\v2\\cells_executor.spi, base 633D34656C51 -> 4D0F6B463E93): the 5 local helpers are deleted and their uses call erlang_term; the 4 inline raw calls are swapped; the 3 'listm::init (length) (nth)' walks become erlang_term::items_of, one O(n) pass instead of O(n^2) lists:nth; and cells_ran_with's check is split out (counted_or_unexpected) to stay in the cell budget. Raw calls left: erlang memory/div (beam_mb) and put, which belong in erlang_process next. RULE additions for x-events1: erlang_term.spi notebook gate exits 0, and the sim accept/build cover cells_executor (CELL-BUDGET in -Accept).")
inl note_of_lib_move_x_sim_erlang_10 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-X-SIM-ERLANG", 10u32, "2026-11-03T16:06Z", "x", "2026-11-03 12:06 x: v3 SLICE drafted (the remaining gaps from the item text), layered on the v2 drafts now in x-events3. Lib erlang_term v3 FDA0CC7A8F89: is_binary, byte_size_of, and a gleam block (é is binary with 2 bytes, an integer is not, '' is 0 bytes). Lib erlang_process v3 4CCE65988813: plain_arguments () : list string (init:get_plain_arguments, each charlist to text) plus a gleam block. simframes v3 B2F37764715E: plain_args is the lib call, which retires the NUL join-then-split round trip, and byte_count is byte_size_of. sim_serve v3 0E931DBF4C4E (base E33D67AEA851): second, tag_of, is_ok, byte_count, id_text and pair_text use erlang_term (element_at, is_tuple, byte_size_of, is_binary). The local names stay as one-line delegations, so no call-site cell grows. Raw calls LEFT in sim_serve, which are different operations for later wrappers: integer_to_binary, json encode/iolist_to_binary, string >=, and integer +/- on seconds. Runs in x-next2 with the lib gate (rule: gate 0 failed; sim accept/build 0; e2e RUST-OK).")
inl note_of_lib_move_x_sim_erlang_11 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-X-SIM-ERLANG", 11u32, "2026-11-03T16:09Z", "x", "2026-11-03 12:09 x: v3 GROWS with json: lib erlang_term gains json_decoded (text -> term, OTP json:decode) and json_encoded (term -> text, json:encode + iolist_to_binary) and a gleam round-trip block (a map with a list of 1, true and é). It stays in erlang_term rather than a new module, so lib's package.spiproj (which carries another lane's uncommitted changes) is untouched. Swapped: simframes json_quoted and json_program's decode; sim_serve json_file, encoded and json_body. New v3 hashes: erlang_term BBE682C9D5FA, simframes E10AC5994F1B, sim_serve E4C9F4101495 (same bases, same x-next2 run). Left raw: maps:get in json_program (typed map views next), integer_to_binary, string >=, integer +/- on seconds, calendar rfc3339.")
inl note_of_lib_move_x_sim_erlang_12 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-X-SIM-ERLANG", 12u32, "2026-11-03T16:11Z", "x", "2026-11-03 12:11 x: simframes v3 -> A7F4CA6A0624: json_program reads 'program' through the typed erlang_map view (program_of = map_get_or 'program' (empty list) (map_view doc); k and v are inferred, so there is no annotation), split out to stay in budget. simframes now has no raw json or maps calls. A missing 'program' gives an empty list instead of a maps:get crash; consumers compare programs, so it still fails visibly.")
inl note_of_lib_move_x_sim_erlang_13 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-X-SIM-ERLANG", 13u32, "2026-11-03T17:22Z", "x", "2026-11-03 13:22 x: v2 SLICE LANDED via x-events3 (lib gate 20/20, sim accept/build 0, e2e RUST-OK): lib erlang_term (shapes and native lists) and erlang_process (beam_memory_mb), plus sim cells_executor.spi 3C5E776B7871 (5 local helpers gone, items_of instead of O(n^2) nth walks, dictionary_put) and simframes.spi A515EFDAF767 (beam_mb from lib). v3 (json, byte size, plain argv, sim_serve) rides x-next2 on these new bases.")
inl note_of_lib_move_x_sim_erlang_14 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-X-SIM-ERLANG", 14u32, "2026-11-03T21:31Z", "x", "2026-11-03 17:30 x: v3 LANDED in x-next2 (job-1793737559206, pinned pack27 core 6F83B94FE33167CC; the installed core moved to D1854B99FD3FA940 mid-run): lib gate 23/23, sim accept 0, sim build 0, client build 0 (CELL-BUDGET, xc.rs 992), e2e RUST-OK 37 + 5, census SAME over 76 files with 0 over one post. Lib erlang_term BBE682C9D5FA (is_binary, byte_size_of, json_decoded, json_encoded) and erlang_process 4CCE65988813 (plain_arguments); sim simframes 30C136F73252 (lib argv, byte size, json and the typed erlang_map read) and sim_serve E4C9F4101495 (element_at, is_tuple, byte_size_of, is_binary, json). Raw calls LEFT: sim_serve integer_to_binary, string >=, integer +/- on seconds, calendar rfc3339, plus counters in cells_executor.")
inl note_of_lib_move_x_sim_erlang_15 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-X-SIM-ERLANG", 15u32, "2026-11-03T22:04Z", "x", "2026-11-03 18:04 x: v4 SLICE drafted on the v3 bases landed by x-next2. Lib erlang_term (BBE682C9D5FA -> 98863DCD2A5E) gains integer_text, text_at_least (string >=), rfc3339_seconds (string -> i64) and rfc3339_text (i64 -> string), plus a gleam block: a stamp round-trips, the epoch is 0, 42 prints as 42, and 'b' >= 'a'. Sim sim_serve (E4C9F4101495 -> 1C8907F6C334, formatted, max cell 271): seconds_of and rfc3339_of are typed i64 through lib, the time arithmetic is Spiral i64 (now - conv (days * 86400), now + conv n) instead of erlang +/- on terms, zulu is deleted, and not_before and id_text use lib. Raw calls left in sim_serve: inet port, base64, crypto hmac, lists sort, maps from_list (specialized; candidates for erlang_tcp, a crypto module and erlang_map). Runs as x-next4 (lib gate on erlang_term; sim accept/build; e2e RUST-OK, whose timeline windows and stamp_after exercise the time path).")
inl note_of_lib_move_x_sim_erlang_16 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-X-SIM-ERLANG", 16u32, "2026-11-03T23:42Z", "x", "2026-11-03 19:42 x: v4 LANDED, green in x-next4 (job-1793746322061, core 626AA0C567CA0F8D at both ends): lib gate 11/11 (the time and text block among them), sim accept 0 with NO fixture changed (so the typed i64 time arithmetic gives the same windows and stamps as erlang +/- did), sim build 0, client build 0, e2e RUST-OK 37 + 5, census SAME. Lib erlang_term 98863DCD2A5E (integer_text, text_at_least, rfc3339_seconds, rfc3339_text) and sim sim_serve 1C8907F6C334 (typed i64 time, lib text order and integer text; zulu gone) plus outputs. What is left is specialized (raw listener options, base64, crypto hmac, sort, the atom-keyed map_of), each needing its own typed lib design, not a swap; proposing the item Done at this point, with those as a follow-up.")
inl note_of_module_type_namespace_1 () = Note ("MODULE-TYPE-NAMESPACE", 1u32, "2026-11-01T22:52Z", "main", "main lib-reshape 11-01 18:5x REPRO (exact, run on the node with the installed compiler DBC5EC18F14C354C, the same as the box; files in %USERPROFILE%\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\LIB-RESHAPE\\repro-module-type-namespace and ...-control, copied to the node's C:\\home\\remote-stage\\lib-reshape-repro; runner repro-run.ps1 beside them). package.spiproj = 'packages: |core- / modules: option, main'; option.spi = 'inl default d x = match x with | Some v => v | None => d'; main.spi = 'inl main () = let x : option i32 = Some 3i32 in option.default 0i32 x' (three lines, classic spelling). Command, in the package dir, SPIRAL_COMPILER_PACKAGE_DIR = deps/The-Spiral-Language/VS Code Plugin: dotnet SpiralCompiler.dll --backend Fsharp main.spi out.fsx. ACTUAL: exit 5, 'main.spi:2:13: ETY-ExpectedSymbolAsRecordKey: Expected symbol as a record key. Got: i32'. CONTROL (module renamed optionx, same body): compiles, exit 0. EXPECTED: both compile; 'option i32' in type position is core's union, 'option.default' is the module. CAUSE (read, not patched): inferIn_module (~4486) and in_modulePrepass (~7148) add each module to BOTH the term env and the type env under its own name, so a later module named like a type replaces the type entry for every following module. FIX SHAPE (typefeatureset): the type env value becomes a closed union 'TypeEntry = TypeOnly of T | ModuleOnly of members | TypeWithModule of T * members' (and the prepass's TModule likewise); adding a module whose name already holds a type yields TypeWithModule; type application and annotations read the T, '::'/'.' member access reads the members; no string flag. DoD: (1) the repro compiles on Rust, F# and Gleam; (2) a matrix sample per case: annotation 'option i32', member access 'option::default', a module member that is itself a type ('option::t'), and an open ':< option' that brings the members in without hiding core's type; (3) the existing suite's verdicts unchanged (no new failing row); (4) then LIB-RESHAPE R5 renames am'/listm'/optionm'/resultm to array/list/option/result. Owner: compiler (spiral_compiler.fs); main does not patch it.")
inl note_of_module_type_namespace_2 () = Note ("MODULE-TYPE-NAMESPACE", 2u32, "2026-11-01T22:58Z", "main", "main 19:0x groom: NEXT STEP (compiler): turn the node repro into a matrix sample (frontier_module_named_like_type) that fails today, then change the type-env entry to the TypeEntry union in inferIn_module/in_modulePrepass; estimate 360m, load medium, assignee agent, owner compiler. Unblocks LIB-RESHAPE R5.")
inl note_of_module_type_namespace_3 () = Note ("MODULE-TYPE-NAMESPACE", 3u32, "2026-11-01T23:05Z", "compiler", "11-01 19:08 compiler: STEP 1 DONE (n2's next step). Landed samples/frontier_module_named_like_type (unstaged): main's repro, with package.spiproj 'packages: |core- / modules: option, main', option.spi's default, and main's 'let x : option i32 = Some 3i32 in option.default 0i32 x'. Box, installed compiler (pack15a): --backend C exits 5 with 'Expected symbol as a record key. Got: i32' (ETY-ExpectedSymbolAsRecordKey). It becomes FIXED when compiled. CODE READ: inferIn_module (4486) puts the module into BOTH env maps under its own name (ty <- TyModule (typeMapToModuleMembers a.ty), term <- TyModule (...)), and in_modulePrepass (7148) does the same with TModule / EModule. The term entry is what makes option.default work. The type entry is only needed for type paths into the module (option.sometype), and that is the one that shadows core's union option. FIX PLAN (typefeatureset, as main's n1): the type-env value for a name becomes 'TypeEntry = TypeOnly of T | ModuleOnly of members | TypeWithModule of T * members'. When the env merge sees an existing type under a module's name, it produces TypeWithModule. Type application and plain type use read the T; a type path (name.member) reads the members. Same in prepass with TModule. The term side is unchanged. Sized at 360m. Next: find the env merge (where module envs fold into the package env) and the type-path lookup, the two places TypeEntry must be matched.")
inl note_of_module_type_namespace_4 () = Note ("MODULE-TYPE-NAMESPACE", 4u32, "2026-11-01T23:21Z", "compiler", "11-01 19:22 compiler: FIX SITES (core F6F6879566C5A830). (1) The shadowing happens in the env merges, not in in_module itself: union small big (28430, ty = Map.foldBack Map.add small.ty big.ty) and unionWDiffPrepass (28711, same for the prepass ty map), where a later module's TyModule/TModule entry silently replaces core's type under the same name. (2) The type-position failure: infer's RawTApply arm (6197-6210) evaluates the head; for a TyModule head it only accepts a TySymbol argument (x.key type path), so 'option i32' falls through to the record-key error. (3) The term side (term env TyModule, member access 5803 and the module path loop 6414) is unaffected. PLAN, unchanged in shape: add the closed entry union at the type-env value (a new T case for 'type plus module', made only by the two merges when a module lands on an existing non-module type), and match it at (2), where a symbol argument reads the module and any other argument applies the type, and in plain type lookup. Every exhaustive T match then has to name the new case: 37 TyModule sites and 12 TModule sites to visit, which is why this stays at 360m. Not a stopgap: a 'keep the type, drop the module type paths' merge rule was considered and rejected, because it silently loses option.t-style type paths.")
inl note_of_module_type_namespace_5 () = Note ("MODULE-TYPE-NAMESPACE", 5u32, "2026-11-02T16:49Z", "compiler", "11-02 12:58 compiler: QUEUED as the compiler lane's next item after the GADT pack (main 11-02, from LIB-SPLIT-REVIEW n2). The lib reshape's ROOT fix is blocked on it: separating the type and value namespaces lets a module `list` coexist with the type `list`. That retires the m suffix (listm, optionm, am', sm'), and until then R1a's interim renames (array_prototypes, text_prototypes, option_operators) cannot merge into their modules, so every consumer would be edited twice. Landing this first turns the remaining reshape into one consumer edit.")
inl note_of_module_type_namespace_6 () = Note ("MODULE-TYPE-NAMESPACE", 6u32, "2026-11-02T16:55Z", "compiler", "11-02 13:02 compiler: CODE MAP (read-only, core b161eda4). The collision is structural: a module is inserted into the SAME `ty` map as types, under its plain name, as TyModule (infer: spiral_compiler.fs:4488 and the twin at 28539) and as TModule (prepass: 7150). So module `list` and type `list` are one key, and the later one wins. Reads: TyModule 37 sites, TModule 12. Member access goes through it twice: terms at RawApply -> TyModule l -> TySymbol member (5803-5818), and types at RawTApply -> TyModule (6200-6214); a bare module name in non-applied position is ModuleMustBeImmediatelyApplied (5734, 6164). prepassModule_open (7741) looks a module up in BOTH term and ty maps. DESIGN OPTIONS: (A) a separate `modules` map in TopEnv/PrepassTopEnv. Clean, but every TopEnv construction and merge changes, which is large. (B) keep modules in `ty` under a reserved key (e.g. \"\\u0001module:\" + name). Resolution of `m::x` / `m.x` (the RawApply/RawTApply heads) tries the reserved key first, while a bare type name `list` resolves the type, because the module no longer sits under the plain key. B touches only the insertion sites (3) and the head lookups (about 6), and leaves type application untouched. Recommendation: B, with a 3-line repro first (memory lib-module-name-shadows-core-type): module `option` plus a later use of the type `option i32` must compile. Starts after the GADT pack (queued per main 11-02).")
inl note_of_module_type_namespace_7 () = Note ("MODULE-TYPE-NAMESPACE", 7u32, "2026-11-02T17:45Z", "compiler", "11-02 14:00 compiler: REPRO (installed pack15d, real core package via SPIRAL_COMPILER_PACKAGE_DIR = deps\\The-Spiral-Language\\VS Code Plugin). Package `|core-` + modules [option; main], where option.spi defines one helper and main uses `option i32` / Some / None: FAILS \"main.spi:2:13: ETY-ExpectedSymbolAsRecordKey: Expected symbol as a record key. Got: i32\". The type application `option i32` resolved `option` to the MODULE (RawTApply -> TyModule wants a member symbol), as the 13:02 code map predicted. CONTROL, the same without the option module: compiles (C, 912 bytes). A self-contained variant with the type in an opened module (`:< types`) does NOT reproduce, because the open re-shadows the module. So the collision is specifically a prelude/core type plus a later module of the same name. Repro tree: scratchpad mtn-repro3 (test vs control). It becomes samples/module_type_namespace (the test arm) once design B lands.")
inl note_of_module_type_namespace_8 () = Note ("MODULE-TYPE-NAMESPACE", 8u32, "2026-11-02T20:27Z", "compiler", "11-02 16:05 compiler: PROVEN on the node (job compiler-mtn, candidate = installed pack17 + MODULE-TYPE-NAMESPACE\\1-shadowed-core-type.kitdo). REPRO: the installed compiler fails the `option` module + `option i32` test (ExpectedSymbolAsRecordKey); the candidate compiles it and the C binary exits 3, same as the control. A/B, control = installed: examples Rust/C/Gleam/Zig, 1,981 rows, the ONLY change is samples/frontier_module_named_like_type, error -> ok on C and Rust. That is an EXISTING frontier sample of exactly this bug (option.spi module + `option i32` + option.default) that sat in the error rows unnoticed. Contracts, 728 rows: 0 diffs. DESIGN AS LANDED (5 replacements): ModuleShadow.name/key; both env merges (infer 4446 and prepass 7136) stash the non-module type a module shadows under the reserved key; infer ty' and prepass ty' get a guard arm, so `<module name> <non-symbol arg>` resolves the stashed type. Module member access (`m::x`, `m.x`) is untouched. Riding pack18 with GLEAM-FFI-PER-FUNCTION (node review running). AFTER INSTALL: lib can rename listm/optionm/... (main's LIB-RESHAPE); add the frontier sample to the matrix lists explicitly.")
inl note_of_module_type_namespace_9 () = Note ("MODULE-TYPE-NAMESPACE", 9u32, "2026-11-02T21:18Z", "compiler", "11-02 17:20 compiler: DONE. pack18 is installed on box, node and europa (17:16; box host 6B9374835A1BBACF, core 8960CAB701FEF46E; undo spiral-bin\\compiler-installs\\pack18-20261102-170746). A lib module may now share its name with a core type: `option i32` after a module `option` resolves the type. Unblocks the lib reshape's m-suffix renames (listm/optionm/resultm/am'/sm'), main's LIB-RESHAPE. Follow-up for whoever renames: samples/frontier_module_named_like_type now passes on all 4 default backends; give it an explicit matrix row when convenient.")
inl note_of_lib_move_dth_fs_1 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-DTH-FS", 1u32, "2026-11-01T22:57Z", "main", "11-01 19:0x main (lib-reshape generic-code sweep). SITES (C:\\home\\git\\dir-tree-html, read in place). Definitions: shared.spi:7 host_join (Path::new(a).join(b) = lib file_system (</>) at file_system.spi:330), :132 host_is_file (Path::is_file = file_system.spi:764 file_exists), :135 host_write_file (std::fs::write, returns 1 on error = file_system.spi:795 write_all_text, which unwraps), :138 host_mkdir (create_dir_all, error flag = file_system.spi:310 create_dir_all, which already returns resultm::result' () io_error), :141 host_temp (std::env::temp_dir = file_system.spi:404 get_temp_path, which also honours TMPDIR/TEMP/TMP), :23 show_i64 with :10 digit (hand-rolled = sm'.decimal_text), :4 the package's own (~!\\\\) emit operator (only needed by these bindings). Call sites: shared.spi 26,145,146,173,174; selftest/selftest.spi 11,13,14,20,24,29,30,31,32,38,60,63,85,86,87,88,100; tree/tree.spi 18,30,34,112,124,129; viewer/viewer.spi 69,96,97,98,99,100. The package already references spiral- (packageDir deps/spiral/lib) and reads through file_system.read at shared.spi:124, so no new dependency. LIB TARGET: file_system and sm' (existing). TYPED SHAPE: writes return resultm::result' () stream::io_error like create_dir_all does (add write_text_checked (path) (text) : result' () io_error next to write_all_text if no such form exists; dir-tree-html maps Error to its exit code 1 at one place). DoD: (1) any new file_system form has a :# block (write to a missing directory gives Error, then create_dir_all + write gives Ok and read_text_or_empty reads it back) passing in Cells on rust and fsharp; (2) dir-tree-html's call sites use lib, proven by its own build plus selftest (dir_tree_html.spi self_test = 0) and the CI page check; (3) shared.spi's host_* bindings, show_i64/digit and the (~!\\\\) operator are deleted.")
inl note_of_lib_move_dth_fs_2 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-DTH-FS", 2u32, "2026-11-02T23:09Z", "main", "main 11-02 19:0x DRAFTED + PARTLY PROVEN. LIB: draft %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\LIB-MOVE-DTH-FS\\file_system.spi (base F83CC223001CA3C1 -> draft 730CC605103ADA2C, +18 lines): try_write_all_text (path) (text) : result () string, the sibling of try_append_all_text (Rust arm 'std::fs::write(..).is_ok()', other targets fall back to write_all_text + Ok), a :# test (missing folder -> Error 'the write failed'; a temp write -> Ok and reads back 'ab'), and the append test's temp folder renamed from kit's old name 'eoie-...' to 'spiral-...'. Node lib_gate (live script, -Lib mirror dthfs): 2/2 passed. NOT LANDED yet. DIR-TREE-HTML (unstaged, 5 files, +52 -74): shared.spi loses (~!\\\\), host_join, digit, show_i64, host_is_file, host_write_file, host_mkdir and host_temp; call sites use (</>) via :< file_system_operators, file_system.file_exists, file_system.get_temp_path, sm'.decimal_text, and a make_dir/write_text pair over create_dir_all + try_write_all_text, keeping the 0/1 exit flags. BLOCKED: the dir-tree-html build fails at markdown.spi:48 ETY-ConstraintError, and IDENTICALLY at HEAD 7ee3e1f (in-job A/B), so it is a regression from today's compiler/core, not this change. Minimal repro sent to compiler: '(sm.index line i) >= (sm.index \"0\" 0i32)' gives 'Fails to satisfy: number'. RESUME: when compiler fixes that, rerun the mirror build; if green, land the lib draft with the reader guard, then this item is Done.")
inl note_of_lib_move_dth_fs_3 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-DTH-FS", 3u32, "2026-11-02T23:52Z", "main", "main 11-02 19:5x CORRECTION to n2: NOT a compiler/core regression. The node resolved |core- from a stale hand copy of deps core (pre-eea8e980, >= over {number}); see NODE-CORE-COPY-DRIFT. Core fixed on the node at 19:49; the mirror build is rerunning; status Blocked -> Active.")
inl note_of_lib_move_dth_fs_4 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-DTH-FS", 4u32, "2026-11-03T00:06Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-02 20:06 fiscal: CI CONSEQUENCE (observed by fiscal during a PIPELINES-GREEN survey; main's session is not running, so no message could be delivered): dir-tree-html is RED on push 71c801f (run 41544170976, ubuntu-24.04): shared.spi:147:12 ETY-ModuleIndexFailed \"The module does not have the key: try_write_all_text\" (file_system.try_write_all_text in write_text). try_write_all_text exists only in this item's kit draft (drafts\\spiral\\LIB-MOVE-DTH-FS\\file_system.spi); it is in neither the spiral working tree nor spiral HEAD (git log -S over lib/spiral finds no commit), while the user's 19:16 dir-tree-html commit already ships the consumer. FIX, owner's choice: land the draft's try_write_all_text into spiral lib/spiral/file_system.spi (then a user spiral push turns dir-tree-html green), or put shared.spi back on file_system.write_all_text until the lib lands. Not landed by fiscal: it is main's draft and its proof is partial (n: DRAFTED + PARTLY PROVEN).")
inl note_of_lib_move_dth_fs_5 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-DTH-FS", 5u32, "2026-11-03T01:07Z", "main", "main 11-02 21:0x PROVEN END TO END on the node, on the fixed core: dir-tree-html at the box tree + the draft lib (730CC605103ADA2C) builds all 6 units, cargo builds, and '--self-test' passes ('RUST-OK dir-tree-html'); the draft's own tests pass 2/2. LAND DEFERRED by the reader guard: live file_system.spi still equals the proven base F83CC223001CA3C1, but kit's TRAIN13c is running Cells notebooks on the box (erl pid 8940, mix spiral.notebook over its release tree), so the live lib must not move under it. Land right after TRAIN13c releases the heavy window: copy the draft over live only if live still hashes F83CC223001CA3C1 (undo = file_system.spi.base in the draft dir). Then dir-tree-html's 5 files are committable together with it.")
inl note_of_lib_move_dth_fs_6 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-DTH-FS", 6u32, "2026-11-03T02:22Z", "main", "main 11-02 22:2x LANDED with every guard: kit's TRAIN13c finished 22:2x (exit 0, heavy window released), 0 erl/beam Cells readers on the box, and live lib/spiral/file_system.spi still hashed the proven base F83CC223001CA3C1. The draft 730CC605103ADA2C was written beside it and renamed over it, so no partial read was possible; live now hashes 730CC605103ADA2C, exactly the copy the node proved (lib tests 2/2; dir-tree-html builds all 6 units, cargo, --self-test RUST-OK). UNDO: copy %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\undo\\LIB-MOVE-DTH-FS\\file_system.spi.before over live. LEFT for the user: commit + push spiral lib/spiral/file_system.spi; then re-run dir-tree-html's CI (red at 71c801f only for the missing try_write_all_text) and it goes green.")
inl note_of_export_style_ratchet_1 () = Note ("EXPORT-STYLE-RATCHET", 1u32, "2026-11-01T23:07Z", "main", "main 19:2x: the rule lives in memories granular-style-discipline and kit-granular-spiral and kit's AGENTS.md, but nothing mechanical blocks it, so lanes drift under load. DoD: (1) census columns bang_export_count and multiline_host_macro_count per package across all repos (via the Spiral reader, not regex scraping); (2) the ratchet fails a land that raises either; (3) the edit hook names the line; (4) a baseline today and a heal list per lane. Resilience writes the memory for 'export, never !!!!Export' if none exists.")
inl note_of_export_style_ratchet_2 () = Note ("EXPORT-STYLE-RATCHET", 2u32, "2026-11-01T23:25Z", "kit", "11-01 19:25 kit: probes ADDED (unstaged) to the census probe GADT in src/kit_style_census/probes.spi: BangExport :: probe drift (word bang-export, pattern !!!!Export\\(, MayNotRise) and HostBlock :: probe drift (word host-block, pattern \\$'[^']*$ = a host macro that opens and does not close on its line, i.e. a multi-line host block; one-line primitives do not match), both in each_probe and in the word-list test. PLAN: (1) TRAIN9 regenerates kit_style_census (not in TRAIN8, whose pre-proof is running); (2) with the installed binary, `kit standards --baseline-merge standards\\census.spi` over every kit package records today's counts (kit has about 644 !!!!Export lines, so they are frozen as baseline, not failed); (3) the ratchet then refuses any package whose bang-export or host-block rate rises; the edit hook (kit-style-check.ps1) shows the line because it already prints ratchet findings for the text just added; (4) heal: migrate !!!!Export -> export per package as each is touched (kit_lint_classify done today), with the census tracking the count down. The kit drift count for today is 0 new.")
inl note_of_export_style_ratchet_3 () = Note ("EXPORT-STYLE-RATCHET", 3u32, "2026-11-01T23:47Z", "main", "main 19:5x BASELINE (one-time grep over tracked .spi/.spir, excluding deps/target/samples; the ratchet itself must use the Spiral reader). Format: repo: files, !!!!Export, export, multi-line host macros.\nkit: 984, 659, 35, 568 (the drift lives here: 99% of the !!!!Export and 79% of the multi-line macros)\nspiral (lib + apps): 175, 11, 25, 81\ndice: 16, 0, 4, 24\npolyglot: 5, 0, 6, 3\nx: 73, 0, 83, 0\ndir-tree-html: 7, 0, 12, 0\ntibia, fiscal, alphabet, regex, blog: 0, 0, 0 (tibia is healing 10 'global \"\"\"' FFI blocks in offscreen.spi tonight; they don't match this pattern)\nResilience notes a codemod, bang-export-rewrite.ps1, that migrates !!!!Export. Plan: kit runs it package by package behind its regen proofs (KIT-TYPED-CRATES touches the same files), and the ratchet freezes these numbers so they can only go down.")
inl note_of_export_style_ratchet_4 () = Note ("EXPORT-STYLE-RATCHET", 4u32, "2026-11-02T01:20Z", "kit", "11-01 21:20 kit: lib-reshape's sweep counted 659 !!!!Export uses repo-wide, all in kit; that is the baseline the bang-export probe freezes at merge time.")
inl note_of_export_style_ratchet_5 () = Note ("EXPORT-STYLE-RATCHET", 5u32, "2026-11-02T15:00Z", "kit", "kit 11-02 groom (AGILE-EPIC-DEP-LINT): parent epic GRANULAR-HEAL. It was this item's only dep, which hid the item from agile next because an epic finishes after its children; parents are named in notes, deps are for real ordering only.")
inl note_of_export_style_ratchet_6 () = Note ("EXPORT-STYLE-RATCHET", 6u32, "2026-11-02T19:42Z", "kit", "kit 11-02 16:1x STOP AT THE SOURCE (main's GRANULAR-LINT n44 ask), in TRAIN13 (unstaged; proven on europa: probes 2/2, census_cli 3/3, census.rs 996 lines). (1) New direction NeverRises: any count increase fails, with no per-1k-lines tolerance (MayNotRise allows +5% +0.5/kloc, which is how new multi-line blocks slipped in). host-block (`$'` left open at end of line = backslash-continued) is now NeverRises. (2) New probe host-statement `\\x24'[^']*(;|$)`: any `$'` that is multi-line OR has a `;` on its opening line, NeverRises. The let-block probe (`$'{`) is RETIRED as subsumed: a `$'{` block is either multi-line (host-block/host-statement) or one line with `;` (host-statement). (3) A NEW package (no baseline row) is refused if it has any host string over 200 chars, multi-line, or with statements. ACTIVATION NOTE: existing packages have no host-statement baseline rows yet, so that probe only bites new packages until `kit standards --baseline-merge standards/census.spi <all package dirs>` runs with the TRAIN13 binary. That merge is the freeze point; run it right after TRAIN13 installs. host-block (NeverRises) bites immediately against the existing rows. HEAL ORDER after TRAIN13: kit_jobs/host.spi (18), kit_grep_query/search.spi (10: rayon walk + regex matchers; needs typed boundary primitives, not a respell), kit_style_census/census.spi (8; the crate has 4 lines of headroom). Also healed in passing: kit_table_text exports moved from !!!!Export to export; kit_table_query's hand string↔case command map became reflection (union_case_suffix + kebab_word).")
inl note_of_export_style_ratchet_7 () = Note ("EXPORT-STYLE-RATCHET", 7u32, "2026-11-03T01:00Z", "kit", "kit 11-02 21:0x HEAL 1/3 DONE (unstaged): kit_grep_query is HOST-FREE. Its 10 multi-line $'{...}' blocks (rayon file walk + parallel line match, literal/caseless/regex matchers, hit accessors, number formatting, pattern problem) moved verbatim into Rust fns in one global inside a new OS boundary package kit_os_search (search.spi). It now exposes the nominal types search_hits / file_list / line_matcher plus one-expression primitives ($'kit_grep_hits(&*!root, &!files, &!matcher, &*!glob)' and so on), and both kit_grep_query modules just open it. PROOF on europa: grep_cli 7/7 (context windows, file roots, json, read/lines globs, regex alternation and bad-pattern refusal, literal-looks-like-regex hint) against the rebuilt binary; kit grep src kit_grep_hits 1 s; grep_query.rs 746 lines; ratchet for kit_grep_query is clean (host-block 10 → 0). SANCTION NEEDED: kit_os_search is a new package carrying a rust_global (the census refuses that by default), so run kit standards --baseline-merge standards/census.spi src/kit_os_search with the TRAIN13 binary, the same as resilience's kit_os_process. Next heals: kit_jobs/host.spi (18), kit_style_census/census.spi (8).")
inl note_of_export_style_ratchet_8 () = Note ("EXPORT-STYLE-RATCHET", 8u32, "2026-11-03T08:20Z", "kit", "11-03 04:1x kit groom (user: kit keeps drifting; groom so it catches up). CORRECTION to my 11-02 21:0x note: 'HEAL 1/3 DONE, kit_grep_query is HOST-FREE' was NOT a heal. The 10 blocks moved verbatim into a global runtime in kit_os_search, and that global was then baselined as sanctioned. The host text was relocated, not healed, and the user flagged it 11-03. The real heal is KIT-OS-SEARCH-GRANULAR. Rule (memory baselines-only-shrink): moving host code into a global, or into another package, is never progress; only typed Spiral over lib is. Measured 11-03: !!!!Export 643 hits in 223 packages. Each KIT-ENTRY-X slice converts its exports; this item tracks the count to 0 and the ratchet that refuses growth.")
inl note_of_export_style_ratchet_9 () = Note ("EXPORT-STYLE-RATCHET", 9u32, "2026-11-03T18:13Z", "kit", "11-03 15:4x kit: kit's '!!!!Export' drift is HEALED in the tree: bang-export-rewrite.ps1 converted 630 sites in 217 packages to 'export'; 3 remain, all string literals inside kit_bindings_model's scanner and fixture. The census bang-export probe (MayNotRise) and the edit-time hook already refuse new '!!!!Export' (the style hook flags '!!!!\\w+' outside boundary packages); the ratchet then reads 0 per kit package. Proof: europa round 7 regenerates the 62 codemod-only crates and requires byte-identical .rs (lib export is an inlined alias). Remaining DoD: the multi-line host-block side (host-block NeverRises already ratchets per package).")
inl note_of_export_style_ratchet_10 () = Note ("EXPORT-STYLE-RATCHET", 10u32, "2026-11-04T21:00Z", "kit", "11-04 22:5x kit groom: waiting on an install, not idle. The 630-site !!!!Export -> export heal (11-03) never reached the box because trains 15-22 failed or timed out; TRAIN23 (running, every crate sized under 1000 first) carries it. NEXT: after the install, `kit standards --ratchet standards\\census.spi src\\<pkg>` reads bang-export 0 for the healed packages; then this closes.")
inl note_of_export_style_ratchet_11 () = Note ("EXPORT-STYLE-RATCHET", 11u32, "2026-11-04T23:48Z", "kit", "11-04 19:5x kit: SOURCE PROOF now, no install needed for it (the census reads the tree): `kit standards --census src` on the box finds bang-export > 0 in ONE package, kit_bindings_model = 3 (the known scanner/fixture string literals); every other kit package reads 0. Host-block side: the full `standards --ratchet standards\\census.spi src` run tonight (569 packages, 23 below baseline) has no host-block row, so NeverRises holds everywhere. Left before Done, per the 22:5x groom note: the healed tree installed (TRAIN26 carries it; regenerating, 238 owners, 0 errors at 19:46).")
inl note_of_export_style_ratchet_12 () = Note ("EXPORT-STYLE-RATCHET", 12u32, "2026-11-05T02:24Z", "kit", "11-04 22:3x kit: REGRESSION FOUND, kit's own (this item's 630-site !!!!Export -> export codemod). TRAIN26 notebooks are RED on two packages the codemod rewrote (both files mtime 11-04 00:31, the diff vs HEAD is exactly !!!!Export( -> export plus an inserted `///> _` line before main): kit_bundle_manifest archive_permissions_keep_executable_and_readonly_intent -> ETY-UnboundVariable \"expect\" at bundle_manifest.spi:666 (test cell after main); kit_do_verbs every_verb_names_its_family_once + a_program_is_delegated_to_its_highest_priority_family -> ETY-UnboundVariable do_verb_family / records_family at verbs.spi:183,202. HYPOTHESIS (unverified): the inserted `///> _` marker changes the notebook's cell scoping, so the test cells after main no longer see helpers/definitions they used before; --check and regen pass because they compile the module whole. NEXT session: diff each package's cell split before/after the codemod, fix the marker placement (or the test-block structure), rerun those two notebooks, and scan the other 215 codemod packages for the same inserted-marker shape before TRAIN27. Correction to kit's star-exchange ask: these were NOT another lane's 00:31 edits.")
inl note_of_export_style_ratchet_13 () = Note ("EXPORT-STYLE-RATCHET", 13u32, "2026-11-05T03:59Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 00:1x kit: REGRESSION FIXED (unstaged), cause VERIFIED. Cells' parse_spi puts all code before the first test into ONE cell, and notebook.spi's scan marks a whole cell skip=1 when any line of it is '///> _'. The codemod put '///> _' + main mid-module, so the entire module-body cell was skipped and every definition was unbound in the tests (not only helpers after main). Scan of all 86 kit files with '///> _' (scratchpad skip_scan.exs via Spiral.Cells.Document.parse_spi): 6 have the marker inside a cell that also holds earlier code; 3 matter, exactly TRAIN26's 3 TYPE-ERRORs (kit_machine_crowding, kit_bundle_manifest, kit_do_verbs); the other 3 are harmless (kit_job_query and kit_lint_shadows/shadows_run have no tests; kit_lint_shadows_core's skipped cell sits after its last test). FIX: '///> _' + main moved to the end of each file, after the last test (the layout every passing file uses), so main is its own cell. PROOF on the box: notebook batch 3/3 pass (crowding 2/2, bundle_manifest 1/1, do_verbs 2/2 executed). Left: install (TRAIN27). Follow-up worth a rule: kit_standards could flag '///> _' that precedes the first test block when definitions follow it.")
inl note_of_export_style_ratchet_14 () = Note ("EXPORT-STYLE-RATCHET", 14u32, "2026-11-06T11:11Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 07:1x kit: DONE. TRAIN33 INSTALLED at 07:05 (kit.exe 6CEA882D, the first install since TRAIN14c): node half job-1793925896101 regen ok, crate gate 358 over 0, notebooks 234/234 including the cli_check suites; box half job-1793960664511 accepted those verdicts on the same snapshot, then release build, schema and topology checks, publish and smoke passed. The only step left was an install.")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_extern_calls_1 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS", 1u32, "2026-11-01T23:07Z", "compiler", "11-01 19:15 compiler: split from COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS (groom: over 4 h). WHAT: Step B. A call to an exported monomorphic function of a link: package becomes a typed extern op carrying the export's Ty signature (PartEval's top-level application; prepass records each definition's package id), and codegenRust emits unit::fn(args) instead of inlining the body. Model-only link: packages then contribute types only. DEFINITION OF DONE: the linked-unit sample calls one exported function of the model unit with no host string and no inlined body in the importer's Rust; kit's generated line total drops against its 11-01 baseline (rust_std_string inlined into 114 crates is the target); kit's train is green. TYPEFEATURESET: the extern op is a typed TyOp case carrying the export's domain and range Ty, never a macro string; only monomorphic exports qualify (a forall export is a compile error naming the export). NEXT STEP: find PartEval's application of a top-level whose package id is in the file's linked set, and gate on the callee being an `export`.")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_extern_calls_2 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS", 2u32, "2026-11-02T19:56Z", "compiler", "11-02 15:25 compiler: QUEUED right after MODULE-TYPE-NAMESPACE (its node A/B is running). Weight raised: Step B now unblocks THREE consumers, kit KIT-TYPED-CRATES, regex REGEX-CRATE-UNITS and html HTML-CI-RELEASE (main 11-02: markdown/entry.rs 2,570 and cli/html.rs 2,105 lines inline a shared 7-module src/, and only typed cross-unit calls let src/ split into link: units). DESIGN, building on the installed unit graph (pack17): (1) WHAT IS AN EXPORT OF A FUNCTION. Today `export \"model_paint\" (\\ n => paint n)` names a closure. The unit graph gains, per export, the TARGET definition when the closure is an eta-wrapper of one top-level function (or the export takes the function directly): {name; signature; target = (declaring package dir, source name)}. Prepass already knows each definition's package (SPIRAL_REFERENCES_OUT); a ConditionalWeakTable E -> (package id, name) beside closureBindingNames records it, the unionSourcePackages analog for functions. (2) IMPORTER. When PE applies a top-level function whose definition belongs to a link: unit, and the unit's graph lists it as an export target, and the call's argument types equal the export's concrete signature, PE emits a typed extern op TyExternCall(unit, export name, args, ret Ty) instead of inlining the body. A type mismatch falls back to inlining (the call is a different instantiation), so the change is never wrong, only less linked. (3) CODEGEN. Rust: `unit::name(args)` with the same arg conversions as the Export arm (&str / Rc<str> for strings, structs for records); Gleam: `unit.name(args)`; other backends: no extern op, they inline as today. (4) CARGO. The graph's links list already feeds kit's generator. DoD unchanged from n1: the linked sample calls an exported function with no host string and no inlined body in the importer; kit's generated line total drops vs the 11-01 baseline; html's two entry crates fall under 1000 lines once src/ splits. FIRST CUT: Rust only, eta-wrapper exports only, primitive and union signatures (records follow the Export arm's struct path).")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_extern_calls_3 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS", 3u32, "2026-11-02T21:30Z", "compiler", "11-02 17:35 compiler: FIRST CUT PROVEN on the node (job compiler-stepb; candidate = installed pack18 + drafts COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS\\1-extern-calls-rust.kitdo, 10 replacements). PROBE lu4: model exports `!!!!Export(\"model_paint\", paint)` and `!!!!Export(\"model_boxed\", boxed)` over annotated top-level definitions; app calls paint n and boxed (n+1). CONTROL (installed): app.rs inlines both bodies. CANDIDATE: app.rs has `let v1: color = model::model_paint(v0);` and `let v3: box_i32 = model::model_boxed(v2);`, i.e. typed calls into the unit with no inlined body and no host string in the source; rustc links app against libmodel and app.exe exits 15, the same as control. A/B, control = installed: examples Rust/C 1,070 rows and contracts 728 rows, 0 differing cells (the extern path fires only through link: units with a built graph). HOW: definitionSources (prepass: file and name per top-level single-param function); the unit graph's exports gain target_path/target_name, taken from the export's closure body; LinkedUnit.calls is read from the graph; ExternCalls.current is set per build (Rust only); PE apply on a DFunction whose body is a linked export target, with an annotated range and a plain argument (no string or function), emits a typed TyMacro `unit::export(args)`; anything else inlines, so it is never wrong. NEXT: pack19 with CELLS-CHECK-DEFAULTS and tibia's atomic refc; then strings (the Export arm's &str/Rc<str> conversions), Gleam, and eta-wrapper exports; kit/regex/html consumers retry on install.")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_extern_calls_4 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS", 4u32, "2026-11-02T22:54Z", "compiler", "11-02 18:50 compiler: Rust first cut shipped in pack19 (handed to main 18:5x; R2R SpiralCompiler.dll 6B30D2F521660878, core 32912F27BC9DBEAC). Node: lu4 app.rs uses model::{color, box_i32} and calls model::model_paint(v0) and model::model_boxed(v2); app.exe exit 15; 0 residual diffs on 2709 rows. Next: strings, Gleam, eta exports.")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_extern_calls_5 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS", 5u32, "2026-11-03T00:23Z", "compiler", "11-02 20:2x compiler: SLICE 2 drafted and proven, plus a LATENT pack19 BUG it fixes. ExternCalls.plain accepted records (YRecord and nominal records), but the exporter emits a Rust struct for a record param or return (pub fn model_norm(v: point), -> point), so the importer's inline-args call mismatched. lu5 on node, pack19 control: app.rs had let (mut v14, mut v15): (i32, i32) = model::model_make(v13), rustc E0308. No package under C:\\home\\git uses link: today, so pack19 ships unchanged. Program 2-strings-and-record-guard.kitdo (2 replacements, base pack19 source C6AA54D854D9E969): plain takes a resolver and rejects records on both domain and range, strings are allowed and passed as &vN (deref-coerces to &str or &Rc<str>, both export shapes). lu5 candidate: let v12: Rc<str> = model::model_greet(&v11), make and norm compile inline, app.exe exit 27 (= 15 + len hi bob 6 + norm 6). Rides pack20.")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_extern_calls_6 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS", 6u32, "2026-11-03T02:29Z", "compiler", "11-02 22:4x compiler: SLICE 3 (Gleam extern calls) drafted and proven. Program COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS\\3-gleam-extern-calls.kitdo (5 replacements, base pack20 source E7E0296C832628D1): ExternCalls.current maps to a Call record {call; import_text; borrow_strings}, Rust {unit::e; None; true}, Gleam {unit.e; Some import unit; false}; the PE arm pushes the import as a Global (global' plus the op, the same as EOp Global) and passes strings as &v only when borrow_strings is set; importUnions drops a bare import unit when it already writes import unit.{types} (Gleam rejects a duplicate import). Node t1101 lu5 (strings + unions + records): control pack20 Gleam main.gleam inlines model (720 bytes); candidate main.gleam has import model.{type Color, ..., BoxI32Empty} and let v1 = model.model_paint(v0), model.model_boxed(v2), model.model_greet(v11); gleam build exit 0, Gleam exit 27 = Rust exit 27 = control. Rides pack21 after the suite A/B.")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_extern_calls_7 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS", 7u32, "2026-11-03T02:48Z", "compiler", "11-02 23:0x compiler: SLICE 4 (Rust struct records across units) proven. Program 4-rust-struct-records.kitdo (4 replacements, on slice 3): ExternCalls.struct_fields mirrors the exporter's rule (a nominal record whose fields are all primitives becomes pub struct <name>); callable accepts such a domain or range; an argument is built as unit::name { k: v, ... }, and a returned struct is read as { let r = call(...); (r.k1, r.k2) } in record-map order (Rust only, struct_records=false on Gleam keeps the refusal). Node t1101 (gleamext4, pack20 + slices 3 and 4, core 73A6CCCC548DA7DF): lu5 main.rs has let (mut v14, mut v15): (i32, i32) = { let r = model::model_make(v13); (r.x, r.y) }; and model::model_norm(model::point { x: v14, y: v15 }); Rust exit 27, Gleam unchanged (exit 27). pack21 = slices 3 + 4; its suite A/B is next.")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_extern_calls_8 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS", 8u32, "2026-11-03T03:28Z", "compiler", "11-02 23:3x compiler: slices 3 (Gleam) + 4 (Rust struct records) INSTALLED with pack21 on box, node and europa at 23:25 (box host 6B30D2F521660878, core 73A6CCCC548DA7DF; europa linux core 917A174A310293DB). Review: examples 1981 + contracts 728 rows vs pack20, 0 differing cells. Linked-unit extern calls now cover Rust (scalars, unions, strings by &, prim-field records as pub structs) and Gleam (scalars, unions, strings; records still inline). Left: Gleam records across units, eta-reduced exports, and kit's Cargo generator reading the graph.")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_extern_calls_9 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS", 9u32, "2026-11-03T07:59Z", "compiler", "11-03 04:0x compiler: PAUSED. State: Rust and Gleam extern calls installed (pack21); pack23 on top. Next step: Gleam records across units (records still go inline on Gleam), then eta-reduced exports. Kit's Cargo generator reading the graph is kit's. Waits on: the run starting.")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_extern_calls_10 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS", 10u32, "2026-11-03T09:22Z", "compiler", "11-03 05:2x compiler: BOUNDARY COVERAGE MEASURED for kit (KIT-OS-SEARCH-GRANULAR n2), installed pack23 core 489EA99474EDE920, Rust, node t1101 (stage remote-stage/compiler-lu6 and -lu7, mini core from lu5). lu6: array_base i32, array_base point (point = {x;y} i32) out, and array_base point in, all CALLED across units (app.rs model::model_make_points etc.; element lowers to the std tuple (i32, i32)); rustc ok, exit 17 as predicted. lu7, the kit grep shape: hit = {line : i32; text : string}, file_hits = {path : string; hits : array_base hit}; model_search (n) : array_base file_hits and model_total_lines (array_base file_hits) : i32 are CALLED across units with type Rc<RefCell<Vec<(Rc<str>, Rc<RefCell<Vec<(i32, Rc<str>)>>>)>>> on both sides; rustc ok, exit 21 as predicted. Rule for consumers: records INSIDE arrays cross at any depth (they lower to std tuples); a record returned or taken DIRECTLY crosses only when every field is a primitive (pub struct); otherwise the call is inlined instead of linked (no error, but no boundary). So shape exports as arrays of records, or prim-field records. Untested: lib's array nominal (core array el) instead of array_base, unions inside the records, and Gleam (records do not cross there yet).")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_extern_calls_11 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS", 11u32, "2026-11-03T09:34Z", "compiler", "11-03 05:3x compiler: lu8 (kit follow-ups, pack23 Rust, t1101 remote-stage/compiler-lu8, exit 22 as predicted). (1) A TUPLE-argument export is LINKED and flattened: files_of ((root, glob) : string * string) emits pub fn model_files_of(v0: &str, v1: &str), and the app calls model::model_files_of(&v1, &v2). (2) A CURRIED export is NOT linked: model_sum_lens(v0: &str) -> Rc<dyn Fn(Rc<str>) -> i32> is emitted, but the app inlines the call, because the range after the first argument is a function, which ExternCalls.plain rejects. (3) A nominal over array_base (arr t = array_base t, lib array's shape) crosses in both directions: wrap_hits returns and first_line takes Rc<RefCell<Vec<(i32, Rc<str>)>>>, both linked. Possible slice: link curried exports as one multi-parameter fn (uncurry at the boundary).")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_extern_calls_12 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS", 12u32, "2026-11-03T09:53Z", "compiler", "11-03 05:5x compiler: lu9 (main's html split shape, pack23 Rust, real core, node t1101 remote-stage/compiler-lu9 and -lu9a). Units: model (:| ^ inline, :| block), parse (parse text -> list block), render (blocks_html : list block -> string), app. (A) WITH core list: the calls ARE linked (pub fn parse_parse(&str) -> Rc<list_block>, pub fn render_blocks_html(Rc<list_block>) -> Rc<str>, app calls parse:: and render::) and the user unions are imported (use model::{inline, block}), BUT every crate re-emits its own core list instantiations (list_inline, list_list_inline, list_string, list_block), so rustc fails E0308 (model::list_inline vs the crate's own list_inline). (B) SAME shape with array_base instead of list: model, parse and render build (arrays lower to std Rc<RefCell<Vec<model::block>>>); the app built only once it ALSO lists model- under link: (before that it emitted its own US0 for block: E0308). With that, all four crates build and app.exe returns the right html length (108; my prediction of 109 miscounted <b>b</b>). RULES: (1) a union crosses only through a unit that every crate on the path LINKS; a type from a non-linked package (core, lib, or a linked unit's package that the crate merely uses) is re-emitted per crate and mismatches; (2) generic core unions (list, option) instantiated in a linked unit's types are re-emitted per crate today, so use array_base at boundaries. Compiler gap filed: LINKED-UNITS-SHARED-INSTANCES.")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_extern_calls_13 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS", 13u32, "2026-11-03T15:28Z", "compiler", "11-03 11:2x compiler: GLEAM RECORDS ACROSS UNITS PROVEN (lu10, node t1101). Program 5-gleam-flat-records.kitdo (6 replacements): ExternCalls.Call gains flat_records (Gleam true, Rust false); plain accepts YRecord, and nominals resolving to one, when flat_records holds and every field is plain; callable takes the flag. Gleam records are not a Gleam type (record params flatten to field vars, record ranges to tuples), so a linked call just passes the fields and destructures the result. lu10 (point {x; y} and named {name : string; n : i32} as args, point as a return): control pack25 inlines all three exports; the candidate calls them, main.gleam: let #(v1, v2) = model.model_make(v0); model.model_norm(v1, v2); model.model_label_len(v3, v0); gleam build ok, exit 13 = expected on both arms. Rides pack26 with RUST-MOVE slice 3 (combined review compiler-pack26 running: examples Gleam and Rust vs pinned pack25).")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_extern_calls_14 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS", 14u32, "2026-11-03T16:26Z", "compiler", "11-03 12:2x compiler: HANDED TO MAIN as pack26 with COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS 5 and LINKED-UNITS-ZIG 3 (dry run reproduces source core 5879473DB36BC3C2 from live pack25 38A0B06D; R2R SpiralCompiler.dll 6B30D2F521660878, core 7C49B7A6AFC05D2C). Final binary review vs pinned pack25: examples Rust 52 residuals, 0 behavior; examples Zig only control-arm timeouts; pack25 live on the box (core 07B01308).")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_extern_calls_15 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS", 15u32, "2026-11-03T16:49Z", "compiler", "11-03 12:5x compiler: pack26 INSTALLED on box (core 7C49B7A6AFC05D2C verified live), node (in-place swap 12:37) and europa (Linux build core 61A05D193627F8D8), per main. Downstream data point (main): apps/lisp spl2spi.rs 61193 -> 60329 bytes under pack26, output byte-identical on all 3 samples.")
inl note_of_compiler_linked_units_extern_calls_16 () = Note ("COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS", 16u32, "2026-11-03T23:08Z", "compiler", "11-03 19:1x compiler: CLOSED. Typed extern calls into link: units are installed on Rust (pack23+), Gleam (pack26 flat records) and Zig (pack26 calls, pack29 multi-value ranges + unions); a silent inline is now caught by test.ps1 -Suite linked ('Calls' per case: linked_records, linked_union, linked_rust_host_type, linked_rust_list_over_model all link every named export; 9/9 rows on pack29/30). Remaining polish is in separate items (GLEAM-RECORDS deferred by rule, DERIVE-OUT, MONOMORPHIC-RULE guard).")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_lib_cut_1 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-LIB-CUT", 1u32, "2026-11-01T23:08Z", "compiler", "11-01 19:15 compiler: split from SPIRAL-NAMEOF (groom: over 4 h). WHAT: the portable lib cut. In lib reflection.spi, `case_name \\* t. (x : t) : string` and `case_of_name \\* t. (text : string) : option t` for payload-free unions: a fold over get_union_fields_untag (the compile-time case table) whose comparisons peval folds to a literal when x is static. Exact names only; name styles need compile-time string transforms and stay with the compiler op (SPIRAL-NAMEOF). DEFINITION OF DONE: a lib test block that round-trips a 5-case union through both functions on every ///> backend lib tests run, and kit's src/kit_exec_metrics/metrics.spi (13 arms) healed to case_name as the first consumer, with its notebook green. TYPEFEATURESET: of_name returns option t, never a default case; payload unions are rejected at compile time with a message pointing to SPIRAL-NAMEOF. NEXT STEP: draft both functions next to union_try_pick (reflection.spi:183), as a lib land program in this item's note, after the lib-reshape worker's R1a land (~20:05) to avoid churn.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_lib_cut_2 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-LIB-CUT", 2u32, "2026-11-01T23:42Z", "compiler", "11-01 19:42 compiler: DRAFTED + TYPE-PROBED. %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\SPIRAL-NAMEOF-LIB-CUT\\1-case-name.kitdo (1 replacement in reflection.spi, after union_to_string's test). case_name: a try_pick over get_union_fields_untag returning the case's key (exact source name). case_of_name: a try_pick of the same table by exact name, returning option t. Plus a test block on gleam/lua/cuda/rust/typescript: Contract -> 'Contract', 'Browser' -> Some Browser, 'browser' -> None, so lower case does NOT match, deliberately unlike union_try_pick, which also accepts the lowercased key. type_probe on a scratch lib copy: PASS, 11 tests typed, 0 errors. NEXT: a Cells run of reflection.spi on the scratch lib (5 backends) when the box is free, then a lib land through lib_land_window after the lib-reshape R1a land (~20:05), then kit's metrics.spi as the first consumer.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_lib_cut_3 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-LIB-CUT", 3u32, "2026-11-02T01:14Z", "compiler", "11-01 21:12 compiler: GATE GREEN. lib_gate on the node (job-1793581762744; a scratch copy of node mirror t1101's lib with the program applied; installed compiler, process mode): reflection.spi 11 passed / 0 failed / 0 type errors, including the new case_name test (Contract -> 'Contract'; 'Browser' -> Some Browser; 'browser' -> None) on its ///> backends. (The box gate could not get a compile window: kit-TRAIN8s holds heavy-build for ~5 h.) LAND: through lib_land_window after lib-reshape's R1b+R2 land releases the lib tree-write window. The program anchors only on union_to_string's test block, which the reshape does not touch; re-dry-run it before landing. Then kit's metrics.spi is the first consumer.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_lib_cut_4 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-LIB-CUT", 4u32, "2026-11-02T02:12Z", "compiler", "11-01 22:12 compiler: re-dry-run on the post-R1b+R2 lib: still applies (1 replacement in reflection.spi). The program uses listm'::try_pick and optionm::value, which lib-reshape renames only after MODULE-TYPE-NAMESPACE; re-check them at land time. Ready to land through lib_land_window once the tree-write window is free.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_lib_cut_5 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-LIB-CUT", 5u32, "2026-11-02T05:12Z", "compiler", "11-02 01:12 compiler: LANDED + DONE. land-lib-program (lib-guarded-do: no live lib reader) applied %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\SPIRAL-NAMEOF-LIB-CUT\\1-case-name.kitdo to lib/spiral/reflection.spi 2F5E7F3F785370AB -> 6EA85EE1CBD0F2F2 at 01:12 after lib-reshape-r3 released tree-write; undo %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\undo\\1-case-name. Same base as the n4 re-dry-run, so the n3 node gate (reflection.spi 11 passed / 0 failed, new case_name test on its ///> backends) covers the landed text. listm'::try_pick and optionm::value both resolve today (optionm::value has 32 other lib uses). Next: name-style variants stay with the compiler op (SPIRAL-NAMEOF).")
inl note_of_claude_tree_priority_boost_1 () = Note ("CLAUDE-TREE-PRIORITY-BOOST", 1u32, "2026-11-01T23:18Z", "resilience", "2026-11-01 19:1x FILED + CORE DEPLOYED (resilience, user 18:xx-19:xx request). Windows children do NOT inherit a parent's priority class, so claude.exe's children (git, shells, builders) spawn Normal even though claude is AboveNormal.\nDEPLOYED (running now, box): a singleton (named-mutex) watcher at HIGH priority (above claude) that every 40ms raises git->AboveNormal (the short-lived review tool), and every ~1s raises claude->AboveNormal + lowers builders(dotnet/cargo/erl/rustc/...)+shells(pwsh/cmd/conhost/ssh, except itself)->Normal. TIERS: watcher(High) > claude+git(AboveNormal) > everything else(Normal). pwsh deliberately held Normal (all lanes use it; bumping it dilutes claude/fork - user's key point). Script at %TEMP%\\claude-boost-watcher.ps1, launched detached (survives till reboot/kill).\nBENCHMARK (the sub-ms/event question, settled): PowerShell ETW Win32_ProcessStartTrace via Register-CimIndicationEvent -Action = ~3000ms latency (median 2982, max 4133) - handlers wait for an idle runspace, useless on a busy box. POLL = 6ms (70ms interval) to 13ms (30ms). So polling wins 100-500x; a tight poll is correct for PowerShell.\nFOLLOW-UPS: (1) PERSISTENCE across reboot = a logon scheduled task -> USER-BATCH decision (persistent machine config is the user's call); exact schtasks line to be filled. (2) TRUE sub-ms = a NATIVE event verb: a compiled kit command consuming the Microsoft-Windows-Kernel-Process ETW provider on its own thread (boost at process-birth, no PS event-queue latency) - that is the only path below poll-interval latency; needs elevation (I confirmed admin). (3) Consider spiral-first home: the poll logic as a kit machine-boost verb (thin, generic) rather than a %TEMP% .ps1. DoD: persistence decided+registered; native verb benchmarked < 5ms birth-to-boost if built.")
inl note_of_claude_tree_priority_boost_2 () = Note ("CLAUDE-TREE-PRIORITY-BOOST", 2u32, "2026-11-02T14:08Z", "x", "2026-11-02 10:07 x: DECISION RECORD (groom): kind=UserBoundary. Persisting the watcher at logon (a Startup-folder shortcut or a scheduled task) is persistent machine config, a security-adjacent setting the user reserved. The classifier proposed a no-admin Startup shortcut as a default; x overrode that. The agent prepares the shortcut file and its undo line; the user drops it in shell:startup.")
inl note_of_claude_tree_priority_boost_3 () = Note ("CLAUDE-TREE-PRIORITY-BOOST", 3u32, "2026-11-02T14:34Z", "x", "2026-11-02 10:28 x: DECISION RECORD v2 (user 11-02: 'why mine? try healing autonomously/deterministically with tests/benchs/typefeatureset/backups the pending decisions'). Only git commits (the user's standing rule) and the harness hook config (the harness itself says Claude must not change it) stay user-only. Everything else gets a precondition, a check and an undo; actions only the user's accounts can take get a non-blocking default. kind=ByTest. RULE: Reverses x's earlier override after the user's why-mine. Agent writes a per-user Startup-folder shortcut (no admin) to the watcher at a stable path. PASS iff launching the shortcut target now starts the watcher and it holds claude.exe at the target priority for 5 min with < 1% CPU. BACKUP/UNDO: Undo: remove the one shortcut file (archived with scratch-archive.ps1). OWNER: resilience.")
inl note_of_claude_tree_priority_boost_4 () = Note ("CLAUDE-TREE-PRIORITY-BOOST", 4u32, "2026-11-02T15:07Z", "resilience", "11-02 resilience: native sub-ms helper DONE - claude-boost-native (C# kernel-ETW consumer in tools/claude-boost-native, published to %LOCALAPPDATA%, autostart task AtLogOn RunLevel Highest, build output kept out of repo via Directory.Build.props). Boosts Fork->High, git/claude->AboveNormal on spawn, ~0% idle. KEY LESSON (exchange + measurement): priority CANNOT fix a saturated box (boosted git still 4s at 100%+ CPU) and Windows children don't inherit priority -> the real fix for Fork-staging slowness was git core.fsmonitor+untrackedCache (spiral status 7.6s->1.2s), NOT priority. Gotchas in memory node-upkeep-scripts: ETW ImageFileName is a full NT path (match last segment); a hard-kill orphans the kernel session (self-heal stops a stale same-named session on startup); verify with Get-EtwTraceSession not logman. Status: shipped; sub-ms holds on a quiet box, bounded-lag under storm.")
inl note_of_claude_tree_priority_boost_5 () = Note ("CLAUDE-TREE-PRIORITY-BOOST", 5u32, "2026-11-02T20:03Z", "resilience", "11-02 16:01 resilience: SUPERSEDED the poll watcher + verified LIVE. Note 1s conclusion (ETW slow -> poll correct) held only for POWERSHELL ETW (Register-CimIndicationEvent handlers wait for an idle runspace, ~3s on a busy box). A NATIVE listener has no runspace wait: built claude-boost-native (C# ETW Win32 process-start listener; tools/claude-boost-native; published %LOCALAPPDATA%\\claude-boost-native; scheduled AtLogOn RunLevel Highest). Event-driven, boosts Fork->High + git/claude->AboveNormal on spawn, ~0 idle cost - replaced the %TEMP%\\claude-boost-watcher.ps1 poll loop that burned ~24% of a core (down to ~5.8% then eliminated). Verified LIVE now: task Running, all 17 claude.exe at AboveNormal. Parent-aware (a Forks child git->High via ImageFileName last-segment match); self-heals a stale ETW kernel session on startup. Tech work DONE + confirmed live. REMAINING to 100: user confirms the persistent scheduled task (user-batch; tracked in SCHEDULED-TASKS-CONFIRM). Bump 55->90.")
inl note_of_claude_tree_priority_boost_6 () = Note ("CLAUDE-TREE-PRIORITY-BOOST", 6u32, "2026-11-02T21:19Z", "resilience", "11-02 17:18 resilience (user flagged dangling git + fork-spawn speed): TWO fixes deployed. (1) claude-boost-native enhanced - it boosted Fork->High and Forks DIRECT-child git->High, but a gits GRANDCHILD git (gits own subprocess: fetch/pack/remote, where spawn-time work happens) only got AboveNormal. Now propagates High through the whole Fork->git->git lineage (ForkGitPids set, cleared on ProcessStop). Rebuilt (net9, 156KB) + hot-swapped the live elevated booster (old pid 21728 -> new pid 8888), verified: 17 claude at AboveNormal, task Running. (2) found 3 hung PARENTLESS git at AboveNormal (2-5min old; parent Fork/claude dead so result discarded) - reaped them. Root cause: orphan-reaper gave git a 60min grace. FIXED: short-lived tools git/gh/ssh/scp now 3min grace (new ShortClasses/ShortMinAgeMinutes), real builds dotnet/cargo/rustc/erl keep 60min. Parse+dry-run clean. Dangling boosted git also steals CPU from new Fork spawns, so (2) helps (1). Program.cs + orphan-reaper.ps1 unstaged. Follow-ups: reaper runs PT15M so a hung git now dies in 3-18min (was 60-75); booster still does not de-boost an orphaned git (reaper is the cleanup). Keeps this item at 90 (user-confirm of the scheduled task still the holdout).")
inl note_of_claude_tree_priority_boost_7 () = Note ("CLAUDE-TREE-PRIORITY-BOOST", 7u32, "2026-11-04T04:14Z", "resilience", "11-04 00:1x resilience GROOM close (stale at 90pct since 11-02): tech complete + verified LIVE - claude-boost-native (kernel-ETW consumer) boosts Fork to High and git/claude to AboveNormal on spawn at ~0 idle cost, scheduled AtLogOn RunLevel Highest, self-heals a stale ETW session. Only remainder was the user-batch persistence confirm, tracked in SCHEDULED-TASKS-CONFIRM (Done); no open resilience work. set 100 Done; reopen trivially if the user wants the task removed.")
inl note_of_html_model_1 () = Note ("HTML-MODEL", 1u32, "2026-11-01T23:42Z", "html", "html 19:4x FILED (child of HTML-REPO). DOD: (1) src/model.spi declares inline (Text|Code|Strong|Link|Image|AutoLink|LinkedImage), block (Heading level|Paragraph|Bullets|Ordered start|CodeBlock|Rule|Table), align, page and viewer as unions; (2) src/render.spi turns them into HTML only through exhaustive ?= matches, and text reaches the output only through escape_text/escape_attr; (3) every constructor has a :# test with an inline _assert_eq expectation; (4) Cells prints a spiral-tests total with 0 failed on rust (gleam second). NEXT STEP: land model.spi + render.spi with tests, run them through Cells on the node. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: heading level as a GADT over phantom levels (h1..h6) with a refusing heading_of : i32 -> option heading so no out-of-range level exists at runtime; the escaped/raw distinction as a phantom on a text nominal (escaped vs raw) so render functions only accept escaped text; viewer kind is a closed union with a refusing constructor (viewer_of name); tag names come from the constructor via a typed tag function, not string maps. FIELDS: estimate 240m, load light (Cells only), assignee agent.")
inl note_of_html_model_2 () = Note ("HTML-MODEL", 2u32, "2026-11-02T01:02Z", "html", "html 20:5x EVIDENCE (box compile window win-1793578057447, 20:08-20:48, before kit TRAIN8 took heavy-build): C:\\home\\git\\html src/ = 7 Cells notebooks (model, inline_parse, markdown, render, file_views, tree, pages; 44 tests with inline _assert_eq expectations, rust-pinned) + cli/html.spi + markdown/entry.spi crate. BuildSpiral compiled both, cargo release built dist/html.exe, --self-test exit 0 (walks a temp fixture tree and compares to dir-tree-html's nested fixture), bad args exit 2. PARITY (drafts\\html\\HTML-PARITY\\parity.ps1, fresh checkout-index copies, dot-files renamed like publish-tree): tibia, dir-tree-html, regex index pages byte-identical; with --viewers 179/179, 29/29, 24/24 pages byte-identical (232 pages, 0 differences). FIRST Cells run (20:09-20:31) was 0/44: module names inline/viewer/page collided with same-named union types (open resolved the type: ETY-UnboundModule), plus `exists` is a keyword and one ValueRestriction on an unannotated sm::length; all fixed (modules renamed inline_parse/file_views/pages). Cells rerun is node job job-1793580954909-html-build-1 (mirror html-1). OPEN: 1000-line gate, cli/html.rs 2105 and markdown/entry.rs 2570 lines (inlined := markup ++ at every site; now routed through a join point, remeasured in node job html-lines-2).")
inl note_of_html_model_3 () = Note ("HTML-MODEL", 3u32, "2026-11-02T01:19Z", "html", "html 21:2x PROOF: node job job-1793581967309-html-cells-3 (mirror html-2, html digest 22318F43FBA1FA6B over head f2dd71c2, spiral mirror html-1 digest 74523D0B8B4C3B56): spiral-tests total discovered 44 executed 44 passed 44 failed 0 unsupported 0, CELLS-EXIT 0, 3.4 min. Per file: model 5, inline_parse 7, markdown 9, render 10, file_views 4, tree 5, pages 4. TYPEFEATURESET used: page kind GADT (IndexPage :: markup -> page index_page | FilePage :: markup -> page file_page) so a viewer page cannot be written as the index; markup nominal as the only HTML-producing type (escape/trusted are the two doors); level_of refusing constructor (option level); to_html prototype with instances on inline, block and node; census reads gadt-case=2 forall=1 (sugar decls not counted, EOIE-STYLE-RATCHET n44). OPEN: kit standards = 38 line-width findings (>120) in src, the only rule failing; cell budget not run yet. NEXT STEP: re-lay the 38 lines (13 are mechanical: break before |> _assert_eq), rerun Cells on the node.")
