inl note_of_html_viewers_3 () = Note ("HTML-VIEWERS", 3u32, "2026-11-02T11:24Z", "yed", "Ask from yed lane (11-02, user wants i574n.github/apps/graphs results to look good in the pages): per-file viewers for .png/.svg (inline <img>, fit to width, click for full size) and .mmd (a page that loads mermaid.js with maxEdges>=5000 and maxTextSize>=2000000: backlog.mmd has ~790 edges and 238 KB, over mermaid's defaults of 500 and 50000; spiral-compiler.mmd renders with defaults). dir-tree-html has neither today; the html repo has only markdown images. Note: dir-tree-html cannot be deleted yet: publish-tree.ps1 still uses its pinned binary (HTML-ADOPT-REPOS 0%, HTML-PARITY 50%).")
inl note_of_html_viewers_4 () = Note ("HTML-VIEWERS", 4u32, "2026-11-04T13:44Z", "main", "11-04 09:4x main yed's ask (n3) IMPLEMENTED, unstaged, gate PENDING: viewer gains Picture (png/svg/jpg/jpeg/gif/webp: <p><a href=name><img src=name alt=name style=max-width:100%></a></p>, attributes escaped through lib markup's attributes) and Diagram (.mmd: <pre class=\"mermaid\"> with the source escaped, then a module script importing mermaid@11 and initializing with maxEdges 5000 and maxTextSize 2000000, enough for backlog.mmd's ~790 edges / 238 KB). viewer_body now takes the file name; the CLI's page_source never reads a Picture as text (a binary .png would not be valid UTF-8). Tests: extension table (e.png -> Picture, f.mmd -> Diagram), picture markup with an & in the name, mermaid escaping, raised limits. Cell budget 0 over in every touched file. WATCH: cli html.rs was at 998/1000 lines before page_source.")
inl note_of_html_viewers_5 () = Note ("HTML-VIEWERS", 5u32, "2026-11-04T14:35Z", "main", "11-04 10:4x main EUROPA GREEN: html build.ps1 HTML-OK, Cells 49/49 (incl. picture markup, mermaid escaping, raised limits, extension table), generated cli/html.rs 994 lines. The first try (1009 lines) failed the 1000-line gate because of a new page_source in the CLI; replaced by making the existing slurp read LOSSILY (read_lossy: String::from_utf8_lossy over std::fs::read), so a binary .png page never panics and the CLI shrank. yed's ask (n3) is DONE; item closes.")
inl note_of_html_cli_1 () = Note ("HTML-CLI", 1u32, "2026-11-01T23:42Z", "html", "html 19:4x FILED. DOD: dist/html(.exe) accepts exactly dir-tree-html flags (--dir <d> --html <f> [--viewers], --self-test) with the same exit codes (0 ok, 1 write failure, 2 bad args); build.ps1 runs Cells (requires the spiral-tests total line), then BuildSpiral per crate, cargo build --release, the binary self-test, and prints the largest generated .rs (gate 1000); kit standards + kit crate gate --enforce clean. NEXT STEP: crates core (model+markdown+render, pure) and cli (walk, I/O, args), typed single-argument exports only. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: options as a record parsed by cli_args.parse_operands into a typed mode union (Render options | SelfTest), the exit status as a union mapped to i32 once at main; I/O helpers as one-expression host bindings returning the host result type (granular-style), local :~ ^ wrappers per helper. FIELDS: estimate 180m, load medium (cargo), assignee agent.")
inl note_of_html_cli_2 () = Note ("HTML-CLI", 2u32, "2026-11-02T01:17Z", "html", "html 21:1x EVIDENCE: cli/html.spi (walk, I/O, args, self-test; typed mode union Render|SelfTest|BadArgs and outcome union Wrote|Mismatch|Refused mapped to the exit code once) + markdown/entry.spi crate (export \"html_markdown\" : string -> string, called from the cli through one typed macro binding). Box build 20:4x: dist/html.exe --self-test exit 0, bad args exit 2, flags --dir/--html/--viewers/--self-test as dir-tree-html. 1000-LINE GATE OPEN: first build cli/html.rs 4330 lines (one crate); split out markdown -> markdown/entry.rs 2570 + cli/html.rs 2105; routing the markup ++ operator through a join point (node job html-lines-2) -> 2155 + 1701. Profile of entry.rs: 114 small functions, no single hog (largest are the two mutual-recursion groups, 149/121 lines), so the remaining cut is crates, not join points. NEXT STEP (decided): split markdown/ into an inline crate (inline_parse + inline render, export html_inline : string -> string) and a block crate, and cli/ into walk+args vs pages (head/CSS, tree render, viewer bodies); measure each by regen on the node; the build.ps1 gate throws above 1000. Write failures still panic (exit 101 from lib write_all_text) instead of dir-tree-html's exit 1: replace with a one-expression host binding returning the io result.")
inl note_of_html_cli_3 () = Note ("HTML-CLI", 3u32, "2026-11-03T16:33Z", "main", "main 11-03 12:3x STATE: every open point from n(21:1x) is closed in the unstaged tree. The 1000-line gate is met by HTML-CI-RELEASE's 8-crate split (cli/html.rs 962 lines, the largest; markdown/entry.rs 12). The cli self-test covers the nested fixture byte for byte, the viewer/no-overwrite fixture (one page written, an existing .html kept, .txt skipped) and, since 11:1x, an unreadable root refused with exit 2 and no page (HTML-TREE slice). kit standards 0 across all 8 packages; x's gleam target lines landed on top (hash-guarded). Europa fast build HTML-OK. LEFT: CI green on GitHub after the user's html push (HTML-CI-RELEASE). Progress 50 -> 90.")
inl note_of_html_cli_4 () = Note ("HTML-CLI", 4u32, "2026-11-03T18:28Z", "main", "main 11-03 14:4x DROP-IN PROVEN through the real path: spiral/scripts/publish-tree.ps1 -Tool <exe> on fresh clones of regex and dice, once with today's html.exe (box build.ps1 -fast: HTML-OK, cli/html.rs 962) and once with dir-tree-html.exe: every generated page is BYTE-IDENTICAL (regex index.html; dice index.html + ui/index.html), both exit 0. So switching the shim changes no published page for these repos (tibia's README differs by design: the GFM code-span fix). Only LEFT: CI green after the user's html push.")
