inl note_of_html_lib_candidates_6 () = Note ("HTML-LIB-CANDIDATES", 6u32, "2026-11-03T14:31Z", "main", "main 11-03 10:3x CONSUMERS MOVED (unstaged): (a) regex bench/bench.spi renders its page through lib markup: escaped cells via markup::escape, markup::table for the arm table, element h1/h2/p, markup::document for the page; report.html is now typed markup::markup. Europa run: page renders, 55 rows (5 workloads x header+10 arms). (b) blog engine/html.spi escape delegates to markup.escape |> markup.markup_text (same 4 entities, & first = single pass, so pages are unchanged); its 22 call sites stay. Europa blog gate 29/29 executed passed, 1 unsupported (the chrono -d test, as before). Also LANDING a lint heal of markup.spi itself (10 non-recursive ^ dropped, 4 rewraps, ///- --package . header; europa 5/5, round-trip canonical). LEFT: kit agile_report_model (kit) and Cells html_markdown.spi (x).")
inl note_of_html_lib_candidates_7 () = Note ("HTML-LIB-CANDIDATES", 7u32, "2026-11-03T15:12Z", "main", "main 11-03 11:2x markup.spi LINT HEAL LANDED (live C81A2333 = draft; base 40397C40, undo 20261103-104522). The 10:45 land was cut off by main stopping its wrapper shell after apply and before close (memory stopping-jobs-that-mutate, 11-03 slip). The close stage was then run by hand once LIB-KEBAB-CASE's land had exited: type_probe markup PASS (5 tests), respell_drift 0, consumer apps/spiral/spiral.spi compiles, document_test 22 passed. Window released. kit standards on the file: 0 (was 15).")
inl note_of_html_lib_candidates_8 () = Note ("HTML-LIB-CANDIDATES", 8u32, "2026-11-04T06:28Z", "main", "11-04 02:2x main DECISION (by this item's reuse rule): the html block model and renderer move into spiral lib. x's X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND is the second real consumer (x's client package sees only core and spiral). Options weighed: (a) x depends on the html repo (CI checks out html; rejected, app-to-app checkouts don't scale); (b) lib move (chosen); (c) x emits its own minimal HTML (rejected, duplicate renderer). x does the move via lib_land_window with html's tests as the gate (europa pack33: tree 5/5, pages 5/5, HTML-OK). Then html's model/render units import the lib modules, with no copies left. Generic names only.")
inl note_of_html_lib_candidates_9 () = Note ("HTML-LIB-CANDIDATES", 9u32, "2026-11-04T06:38Z", "x", "2026-11-04 02:37 x: MOVE (b) under way, decided by main 02:3x (x's timeline page is the 2nd consumer). FINDING first: lib/spiral/markup.spi ALREADY holds html model's markup core (markup type, markup_text, trusted, entity, run_of, escape, plus element/attribute/table/document) with the escape tests, and NO consumer uses it yet; html_model keeps a duplicate. So the move builds ON lib markup, with no second markup type. DRAFTED (kit drafts spiral\\HTML-LIB-CANDIDATES): lib doc_blocks.spi (3AD47CC53B37: level, align, inline, block, level_of, level_tag, 1 test) and lib doc_render.spi (17B8B227EE9D: render lines 10-120 verbatim, plus local (++) = joined; wrap = element t [] and anchor = element 'a' [(href, h)], byte-identical to html's forms; quoted; digit and show_i64; 3 render tests), registered after markup in lib package.spiproj (DF7923212DBB -> draft). Generic names (no repo names). Europa pack33 --check: both exit 0. STAYS in html: the markdown front-end (markdown_html, md and the md-driven tests in render; markdown, inline_parse) and the dir-tree types in model (viewer, node, page kinds). NEXT: a node notebook gate on both modules (rust + gleam) plus html build.ps1 -fast 1 still HTML-OK, then lib_land_window. html's side (model and render import lib's markup + doc_blocks + doc_render and delete their copies; linked units regen) is main's after the land, as offered.")
inl note_of_html_lib_candidates_10 () = Note ("HTML-LIB-CANDIDATES", 10u32, "2026-11-04T07:18Z", "x", "2026-11-04 03:18 x: x-libdoc1 PREPARED (scratchpad launch-libdoc.ps1; node mirror xcells1 with html; staged and cleaned in the mirror only). Proves the lib batch: doc_blocks, doc_render and list_sort (LIB-LIST-SORT, a merge sort for x's sim and route), plus one package.spiproj registering all three after markup (base DF7923212DBB). PRE-REGISTERED RULE: notebook gate exit 0 with spiral-tests failed=0 over doc_blocks (1 test), doc_render (3) and list_sort (2), each on rust + gleam; AND html build.ps1 -fast 1 exit 0 with an HTML-OK line, against the mirror lib with the new modules (html's own units are unchanged, so this proves the addition is non-breaking). Else FAIL. LAND: lib_land_window with the 4 files ('new' for the 3 modules), then message main the landed hashes for html's switch. It launches when the node queue reaches it (x-next5b is running; x-next6/7 come first).")
inl note_of_html_lib_candidates_11 () = Note ("HTML-LIB-CANDIDATES", 11u32, "2026-11-04T08:50Z", "x", "2026-11-04 04:50 x: ADAPTED to LIB-SPIRAL-TOML-MIGRATION (main, 04:49): lib/spiral now has a prelude-only spiral.toml and derives its modules from the files, and package.spiproj is gone. x-libdoc1 no longer stages or guards a lib package.spiproj; it stages only doc_blocks, doc_render and list_sort (new files, guarded as 'must not exist'). The HTML-LIB-CANDIDATES and LIB-LIST-SORT package.spiproj drafts are obsolete (kept in drafts, never landed). The lib land (lib_land_window) takes just the 3 new .spi files. x's europa check stage gets re-staged from the new lib layout before the next lib check.")
