inl note_of_linked_units_zig_1 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-ZIG", 1u32, "2026-11-02T10:49Z", "main", "main 11-02 07:0x filed from kit-session Explore subagent aaf2a6f472dc70094 (11-02, read-only; report relayed by kit to main). Parent per the report: extend, don't fork the plan.")
inl note_of_linked_units_zig_2 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-ZIG", 2u32, "2026-11-02T10:53Z", "compiler", "11-02 06:55 compiler: GROOM. SCOPE IS BIGGER THAN THE TITLE: Zig has no Export arm at all. TyOp(Export ..) is handled by F# 12939, Rust 14073, Gleam 18283 and TypeScript 24558; codegenZig (15461) has none. So step 0 is `export` on Zig (a `pub fn` wrapper calling the closure, as Gleam does at 18296), with a single-unit sample. Then Step A: union owner map, where the importer emits `const m = @import(\"model\"); ... m.color` and drops its local union. Step B: direct calls. Zig unions are tagged unions (`union(enum)`), so a renamed export also needs `pub`. Zig modules link via build.zig `addModule`, and the unit graph (n9) feeds that the same way it feeds Cargo deps. Estimate 600m stands if step 0 is ~120m. Order: after the second cut and LINKED-UNITS-NO-SUFFIX (naming rule shared by all three backends).")
inl note_of_linked_units_zig_3 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-ZIG", 3u32, "2026-11-02T11:11Z", "compiler", "11-02 07:30 compiler: STEP 0 MADE PRECISE (main asked). What is missing is FUNCTION export itself, so union export is missing too, since unions cross only through export signatures. Installed pack15d on scratchpad linked\\lu3\\model (export \"model_paint\" : i32 -> color) with --backend Zig: \"Compiler error: Export with 2 args not supported in the Zig backend\". It is a REGRESSION: pack 5o (10-27, BACKEND-COVERAGE-GAPS n55/n56) shipped a Zig Export arm, mirroring codegenRust's builder and keeping spiralMain; export_add(40,2)=42 was green on the node. The live codegenZig (spiral_compiler.fs 15461-16061) has no Export case, so a later core rewrite dropped it. Its applier packs/apply-zig-export-pack.ps1 was archived on 10-31 (PS1-TO-SPIRAL n16, main's file). Nothing caught it because tests/families/export_family.spi is UNWIRED (not in the families package.spiproj, not in matrix.psd1). STEP 0 = (a) re-derive the Zig fn Export arm as a kitdo program (no archive restore of the .ps1); (b) wire export_family into the matrix Zig list so the regression gates; (c) then union export: `pub const` for unions reachable from exports, named by exportedUnionNames like Rust/Gleam. The report's export_family citation was the regression sample, not live support.")
inl note_of_linked_units_zig_4 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-ZIG", 4u32, "2026-11-02T11:46Z", "compiler", "11-02 07:50 compiler: STEP 0(a)+(b) PROVEN. Program %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\LINKED-UNITS-ZIG\\1-zig-fn-export.kitdo (3 replacements, all inside codegenZig; candidate zigexp). (1) closure_of_var and export_names in codegenZig. (2) The generic TyJoinPoint arm records a capture-free closure bound to a single local (the Gleam/Rust rule). (3) The Export arm emits `pub fn <name>(v..: T) R { return <closure>(@ptrCast(&spiral_export_env<tag>), v..); }` over a top-level `var spiral_export_env<tag>: ClosureEnv<tag> = .{};`. A global env sidesteps zigConstLocals and Zig's never-mutated rule, and spiralMain is kept, so the program still runs standalone. PROOF: (i) a standalone zig build-exe exits 0; (ii) a separate consumer.zig doing @import(\"main.zig\") and fam.spiral_add(40, 2) == 42 exits 0, which is the linked-unit call shape. MATRIX: new samples/zig_export_fn (Fsharp set + Zig list, since C has no Export arm and Rust's export emits a library crate). Candidate: Fsharp exit 0, Zig exit 0, agree 1, DISAGREE 0. Control pack15d: the Zig row errors (\"Export with 2 args not supported\"). Residual risk: only the TyJoinPoint arm touches non-export programs, and it only fills a dictionary, so emitted text is unchanged; the full Zig list runs at pack review. NEXT, step 0(c): union export (`pub` on export-reachable unions, named by exportedUnionNames), then Step A importer (`const m = @import(\"model.zig\")`).")
inl note_of_linked_units_zig_5 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-ZIG", 5u32, "2026-11-02T12:09Z", "compiler", "11-02 08:10 compiler: STEP 0(c) union export PROVEN. Program LINKED-UNITS-ZIG\\2-zig-union-export.kitdo (1 replacement, end of codegenZig). Unions reachable from exports (exportedUnionNames, the same map Rust and Gleam use) are renamed from US<tag>/UH<tag> to their exported name, made `pub const`, and their constructors made `pub fn`. Candidate zigexp2 on lu3's model: `pub const color = struct {...}`, `pub const box_i32`, pub color_Red/Green/Blue and box_i32_Full/Empty, plus the two export fns. consumer.zig (@import(\"model.zig\")) reads model_paint(7) as color tag 2 payload 7 and model_boxed(3) as box_i32 tag 0 payload 3: exit 0. The standalone model program still exits 0. KNOWN LIMIT: heap unions are built with spiralCreate on the unit's spiral_gpa, which only the unit's own main() sets, so an importer calling an export that builds a heap union needs a unit init hook (library mode). That belongs with Step A on Zig. NEXT: Step A importer (`const m = @import(...)`, drop the local union, map by the unit graph).")
inl note_of_linked_units_zig_6 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-ZIG", 6u32, "2026-11-03T07:31Z", "compiler", "11-03 07:3x compiler GROOM (WIP cap: Active = touched in 12 h). Parked to Planned (19 h). Next: ride program 2 (zig union export) and the zig_export_fn sample in the next pack, then Step B direct calls.")
inl note_of_linked_units_zig_7 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-ZIG", 7u32, "2026-11-03T16:12Z", "compiler", "11-03 12:1x compiler: STEP B PROVEN (scalars, strings, flattened records; lu11 on node t1101). Programs 1-2 (fn export, union export) are already installed (their replacement text is in pack25). Program LINKED-UNITS-ZIG\\3-zig-extern-calls.kitdo (6 replacements on pack25 + RUST-MOVE 3 + COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS 5): ExternCalls.Call gains multi_ranges (Rust and Gleam true: their tuples are structural; Zig false: Zig tuples are per-file structs, main.Tuple0 vs model.Tuple0); a Zig branch builds calls as unit.e(args) with const unit = @import(\"unit.zig\"), flat records, unborrowed strings; and the Zig build path now writes the unit graph (build_many + writeUnitGraph, like Rust and Gleam), without which no Zig call was ever linked. lu11: the candidate calls model.model_norm(v0, @as(i32, 2)) and model.model_label_len(v1, v0), inlines model_make (record range), zig build-exe ok, exit 13 = expected on both arms. Left: multi-value ranges and unions across Zig units (an import step like import_rust_unions). Rides pack26; final review compiler-pack26b running.")
inl note_of_linked_units_zig_8 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-ZIG", 8u32, "2026-11-03T16:26Z", "compiler", "11-03 12:2x compiler: HANDED TO MAIN as pack26 with COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS 5 and LINKED-UNITS-ZIG 3 (dry run reproduces source core 5879473DB36BC3C2 from live pack25 38A0B06D; R2R SpiralCompiler.dll 6B30D2F521660878, core 7C49B7A6AFC05D2C). Final binary review vs pinned pack25: examples Rust 52 residuals, 0 behavior; examples Zig only control-arm timeouts; pack25 live on the box (core 07B01308).")
inl note_of_linked_units_zig_9 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-ZIG", 9u32, "2026-11-03T16:49Z", "compiler", "11-03 12:5x compiler: pack26 INSTALLED on box (core 7C49B7A6AFC05D2C verified live), node (in-place swap 12:37) and europa (Linux build core 61A05D193627F8D8), per main. Downstream data point (main): apps/lisp spl2spi.rs 61193 -> 60329 bytes under pack26, output byte-identical on all 3 samples.")
inl note_of_linked_units_zig_10 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-ZIG", 10u32, "2026-11-03T18:27Z", "compiler", "11-03 14:1x compiler: MULTI-VALUE RETURNS cross (lu12, node). Program LINKED-UNITS-ZIG\\4-zig-multi-value-returns.kitdo (5 replacements; source 5879473D -> 78AECF78): ExternCalls.Call gains copy_tuples (Zig only; Zig multi_ranges false -> true). A linked call whose range flattens to 2+ values is emitted as 'blk: { const r = model.f(..); break :blk .{ .f0 = r.f0, .f1 = r.f1 }; }', so the anonymous literal coerces to the caller's own TupleN (Zig tuples are per-file structs; every file names fields f0..fN). Fixture: model exports norm (record arg), make (record range), pair (i32 * i32 range), label_len (string record arg). Control pack26 links norm/label_len and inlines make/pair; candidate calls model.model_make and model.model_pair through the copy; zig build-exe ok, exit 13 on both arms; contracts Zig 620 rows: 0 differing cells. Left: Zig unions crossing.")
inl note_of_linked_units_zig_11 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-ZIG", 11u32, "2026-11-03T19:04Z", "compiler", "11-03 15:0x compiler: UNIONS cross (lu13, node). Program LINKED-UNITS-ZIG\\5-zig-union-import.kitdo (3 replacements): codegenZig takes linked_units (like Rust/Gleam); import_zig_unions replaces each linked union's local 'const USn = struct {...};' line with 'const USn = <unit>.<name>;' (adding the @import when no linked call did), so local constructors and matches keep working on the aliased type. Fixture: model ':| shape = | Circle : i32 | Square : i32', exports area (shape arg) and make_sq (shape range); main matches the returned shape locally. Control (pack26 + program 4): zig build-exe fails 'expected type main.US0, found model.shape'. Candidate: const US0 = model.shape; zig build-exe ok, exit 13; contracts Zig 620 rows vs control: 0 differing cells. With n10, Zig links now carry scalars, strings, records (flattened), multi-value ranges and unions. Ships in the next feature pack with RUST-MOVE slice 4 (after the E0505/E0507 hotfixes).")
inl note_of_linked_units_zig_12 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-ZIG", 12u32, "2026-11-03T23:05Z", "compiler", "11-03 19:0x compiler: INSTALLED in pack29 (box/node/europa; downstream green). Zig links now carry scalars, strings, records (flattened), multi-value ranges (copy_tuples) and unions (const USn = model.<name>); matrix rows samples/linked_records and samples/linked_union pass on Zig AND Gleam under test.ps1 -Suite linked. DoD met.")
inl note_of_subagent_hold_hook_1 () = Note ("SUBAGENT-HOLD-HOOK", 1u32, "2026-11-02T10:50Z", "main", "main 11-02 07:0x: USER DECISION (settings.json is the user's call; nothing installed). Unverified: the largest hook timeout Claude Code accepts, and whether SendMessage reaches a caller blocked on a foreground subagent. Simulation steps are in the report. Rec: yes for background forks/general-purpose only (types.txt), 60 min cap.")
inl note_of_subagent_hold_hook_2 () = Note ("SUBAGENT-HOLD-HOOK", 2u32, "2026-11-02T10:50Z", "main", "main 11-02: section 1 of the report verbatim (hook script, settings.json entry, simulation):\n## 1. Keeping subagents open (SubagentStop hook, version 2)\n\nWhat the binary confirms:\n- A `SubagentStop` hook can return `{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"SubagentStop\",\"additionalContext\":\"...\"}}`. The subagent then continues and acts on that text.\n- Your `Stop` hook (`autonomous-gate.ps1`) never fired inside a subagent. I checked this session's transcripts.\n\nThe hook works in two phases:\n1. **First stop:** it tells the subagent to send its full report to main with `SendMessage`, then end. That costs one short extra turn, and main gets the report immediately.\n2. **Second stop:** it waits without using any tokens until you release it or the time limit passes. The subagent stays open to browse the whole time.\n\n`%USERPROFILE%\\.claude\\hooks\\subagent-hold.ps1`:\n```powershell\n$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'\n$dir = Join-Path $HOME '.claude\\subagent-hold'\n$p = try { [Console]::In.ReadToEnd() | ConvertFrom-Json } catch { $null }\nif (-not $p -or -not (Test-Path (Join-Path $dir 'armed'))) { exit 0 }\n$types = Join-Path $dir 'types.txt'\nif ((Test-Path $types) -and \"$($p.agent_type)\" -notin @(Get-Content $types | ForEach-Object Trim | Where-Object { $_ })) { exit 0 }\n$id = \"$($p.agent_id)\"; $reported = Join-Path $dir \"$id.reported\"\nif (-not (Test-Path $reported)) {\n    Set-Content $reported (Get-Date -Format o)\n    @{ hookSpecificOutput = @{ hookEventName = 'SubagentStop'; additionalContext =\n        \"Before ending: send your complete final report to the agent that spawned you (main unless told otherwise) with SendMessage, verbatim, then end with one line. Do not start new work.\" } } | ConvertTo-Json -Compress -Depth 4\n    exit 0\n}\n$held = Join-Path $dir \"$id.held\"; $release = Join-Path $dir \"$id.release\"; $all = Join-Path $dir 'release-all'\n$max = 60; $m = Join-Path $dir 'max-minutes.txt'; if (Test-Path $m) { $max = [int](Get-Content $m -TotalCount 1) }\n\"$(Get-Date -Format o) $($p.agent_type) $($p.agent_transcript_path)\" | Set-Content $held\n$start = (Get-Item $held).LastWriteTime\nwhile ((Get-Date) -lt $start.AddMinutes($max) -and -not (Test-Path $release) -and -not ((Test-Path $all) -and (Get-Item $all).LastWriteTime -gt $start)) { Start-Sleep -Seconds 10 }\nRemove-Item $held, $release, $reported -ErrorAction Ignore\nexit 0\n```\n\nAdd this under `hooks` in `settings.json`, next to your existing `Stop` entry:\n```json\n\"SubagentStop\": [{ \"hooks\": [{ \"type\": \"command\",\n  \"command\": \"%USERPROFILE%\\\\scoop\\\\apps\\\\pwsh\\\\current\\\\pwsh.exe\",\n  \"args\": [\"-NoProfile\",\"-NonInteractive\",\"-File\",\"%USERPROFILE%\\\\.claude\\\\hooks\\\\subagent-hold.ps1\"],\n  \"timeout\": 3720, \"statusMessage\": \"held: create ~/.claude/subagent-hold/<agent_id>.release\" }] }]\n```\n\nTo use it:\n- Create `~/.claude/subagent-hold/armed` to switch it on. Optionally list agent types in `types.txt`, one per line (for example `fork`, `general-purpose`, `Explore`).\n- Release one subagent with `<agent_id>.release`, or all of them with `release-all`.\n\nTo simulate it (in a fork):\n```powershell\n$h='%USERPROFILE%\\.claude\\hooks\\subagent-hold.ps1'; $d=\"$HOME\\.claude\\subagent-hold\"; New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force $d | Out-Null\n'1' | Set-Content \"$d\\max-minutes.txt\"; '' | Set-Content \"$d\\armed\"\n$j='{\"agent_id\":\"sim1\",\"agent_type\":\"fork\",\"stop_hook_active\":false}'\n$j | pwsh -NoProfile -File $h          # expect JSON with additionalContext, instantly\n$t=Measure-Command { $j | pwsh -NoProfile -File $h }; \"held $([int]$t.TotalSeconds) s (expect ~60)\"\nStart-Job { Start-Sleep 5; '' | Set-Content \"$using:d\\sim1.release\" } | Out-Null\n$j | pwsh -NoProfile -File $h          # phase 1 again (marker was cleared)\n$t=Measure-Command { $j | pwsh -NoProfile -File $h }; \"released in $([int]$t.TotalSeconds) s (expect ~5-10)\"\n```\n\nThen one real check: start a background fork that answers \"ok\", and confirm main receives the `SendMessage` while the fork shows as held. Two things are unverified: the largest `timeout` Claude Code accepts, and whether a `SendMessage` reaches a caller that is blocked waiting on a foreground subagent.")
inl note_of_subagent_hold_hook_3 () = Note ("SUBAGENT-HOLD-HOOK", 3u32, "2026-11-02T11:04Z", "kit", "kit 11-02 07:2x, from the S0 study subagent's execution packet (aaf2a6f472dc70094). INSTALLED on the USER's direct order (11-02 07:2x: 'also change the damn settings, it was me who asked'). Files: %USERPROFILE%\\.claude\\hooks\\subagent-hold.ps1 (the n2 script, version 2: phase 1 tells the subagent to SendMessage its report to its spawner, phase 2 holds with no tokens until <agent_id>.release / release-all / max-minutes); settings.json gains hooks.SubagentStop (exec form, pwsh -File, timeout 3720 s, statusMessage), every other hook unchanged, JSON re-parsed OK. ARMED: ~/.claude/subagent-hold/armed, max-minutes.txt = 60, no types.txt (all agent types). SIMULATED (pipe-test): unarmed -> exit 0, no output; armed phase 1 -> the additionalContext JSON at once; phase 2 with a release file written after 6 s -> returned in 13 s (10 s poll), markers cleaned. LEFT for DoD: one live check (a background fork answering 'ok' must SendMessage its spawner and show as held), the largest timeout Claude Code accepts, and whether SendMessage reaches a caller blocked on a foreground subagent. Hooks load per session: sessions started before 07:2x may need /hooks or a restart to pick it up.")
inl note_of_subagent_hold_hook_4 () = Note ("SUBAGENT-HOLD-HOOK", 4u32, "2026-11-02T11:06Z", "kit", "kit 11-02 07:06 LIVE CHECK GREEN (real subagent, not a pipe-test): the S0 Explore subagent aaf2a6f472dc70094 hit its first stop at 07:05:36 (.reported marker), the hook's additionalContext made it SendMessage its full final report to its spawner (kit) before ending, and at 07:05:47 it went into the token-free hold (.held marker naming its transcript). The running session picked up the settings.json change without /hooks or a restart. Still open: the largest timeout Claude Code accepts (3720 s set), and SendMessage to a caller blocked on a FOREGROUND subagent (this one was background).")
inl note_of_subagent_hold_hook_5 () = Note ("SUBAGENT-HOLD-HOOK", 5u32, "2026-11-02T11:25Z", "kit", "kit 11-02 07:2x REDESIGN after a real failure. INCIDENT: the v2 hold BLOCKS inside SubagentStop; Claude Code's stream watchdog killed the held S0 subagent after 600 s ('Agent stalled: no progress for 600s', interrupted 07:15:47), and while held it could not receive the user's queued message (it never reached the transcript). It also held Claude Code's internal helper agents (empty agent_type). USER requirements (07:1x): must be able to send messages, 24 h limit, no spinning, no token burn. NEW DESIGN (v3, installed): the hook never blocks (timeout 30 s). First stop of a typed subagent -> additionalContext: SendMessage the report, then run 'waitfor /t <=86400 subagent<id>' with run_in_background, then end the turn. The subagent then sits 'waiting on its own background work': no tokens, no watchdog, and messages resume it normally. Later stops pass through while a waitfor with that signal is alive (found by command line); asked once per agent (<id>.asked). Release = stop that waitfor.exe (Get-CimInstance Win32_Process -Filter \\")
inl note_of_subagent_hold_hook_6 () = Note ("SUBAGENT-HOLD-HOOK", 6u32, "2026-11-02T13:43Z", "x", "2026-11-02 09:43 x: v4 HOLD IS OPT-IN (the user's direction to x, verbatim in memory subagents-on-request-only). Holding exists so a subagent the USER asked for stays reachable instead of vanishing as idle. Agents a lane spawns for its own needs must not be held, and lanes spawn only when the user asks. CHANGE to ~/.claude/hooks/subagent-hold.ps1 (backup subagent-hold.ps1.before-opt-in-20261102.bak, sha 626F3A5AC197): after the release check, the hook exits 0 (pass-through, the agent ends normally) unless line 1 of agent_transcript_path, the spawn prompt, contains the literal '[hold-for-user]', or ~/.claude/subagent-hold/<agent_id>.keep exists (retroactive opt-in). Only line 1 is read, so a marker that shows up later in files the agent read can't trigger a hold. PIPE-TEST (fake ids, armed): untagged -> no output, exit 0; tagged -> hold additionalContext; untagged plus .keep -> hold. LIVE DRAIN TEST: x's three lane-spawned classifiers (a3af5691, a1a09e3e, ab98dab0) were released with <id>.release plus stopping their waitfor. All three ended their turn and stopped with no re-ask, which proves the release path. Seven other holds remain, owned by other lanes; each lane drains its own. RULE FOR LANES: when the user asks for a subagent, put [hold-for-user] in its prompt; never otherwise.")
inl note_of_subagent_hold_hook_7 () = Note ("SUBAGENT-HOLD-HOOK", 7u32, "2026-11-02T14:15Z", "add9e665535617d64", "add9e665535617d64 11-02 10:2x v3 INCIDENT, then v4 installed (user 11-02 ~08:4x: \"why this subagent failed instead of waiting? ... fix the hook and what's around it\").\nEVIDENCE:\n- Agent add9e665535617d64 reached \"completed: waiting on its own background work\" at 12:14:19Z, so the hold registered.\n- By 12:41:59Z its `waitfor /t 86400 subagentadd9e665535617d64` (task bjcmcn2rw) was gone. No completion notification reached the agent or main.\n- v3 asks only once per agent (<id>.asked), so the agent's next stop would have ended it for good.\n- After the 07:55 crash, six old waitfors (a6ba2b, a78218, a7601c, a47d386, a68d3a, a30fa65) are orphans whose parent shells are dead. The harness no longer tracks them: a6ba2b was reported \"finished\" at 12:15:30Z while its waitfor pid 5552 still ran. v3's command-line check still counted them as held.\n- What killed the 12:14 waitfor is UNKNOWN. A SendMessage resume does not kill holds: a6ba2b stayed waiting across three main resumes at 11:25-11:31Z.\nv4 (~/.claude/hooks/subagent-hold.ps1; v3 kept as subagent-hold.ps1.before-self-heal-20261102.bak):\n(1) A waitfor counts as live only when it sits under this session's claude.exe. Orphans are stopped on the agent's next stop.\n(2) The hook re-asks whenever no live hold exists, at most max-asks.txt times (default 6). It skips when stop_hook_active is set (loop guard), when <id>.release exists, or when the last ask is older than max-minutes.\n(3) It writes <id>.json (type, transcript, session, root pid, asks), a registry for resuming agents after a crash.\n(4) The agent ends with one line that names its id. A re-ask tells it not to resend an earlier report.\n(5) The settings.json SubagentStop timeout went from 30 to 90 s, because pwsh startup alone measured 5-15 s on the loaded box.\nPIPE TESTS 6/6: first ask, loop guard, re-ask, live under root (skip), orphan stopped then re-ask, release (skip).\nLIVE: x then added the opt-in on top: only agents whose prompt contains [hold-for-user], or that have <id>.keep, are held (memory subagents-on-request-only).\nThis agent got a .keep because the user resumed it, and the v4 hook then gave it the first-ask text live at about 10:0x.\nOPEN:\n- the 12:14 killer;\n- a hold that dies while the agent is idle is only healed at the agent's next stop;\n- a 24 h live check.")
inl note_of_subagent_hold_hook_8 () = Note ("SUBAGENT-HOLD-HOOK", 8u32, "2026-11-02T14:49Z", "add9e665535617d64", "add9e665535617d64 11-02 10:48 NEW EVIDENCE on the killer: my v4 hold (waitfor pid 8392, started 09:53 under this session's claude.exe) ended with exit code 255, which means it was terminated by force.\n- It wasn't a release: there is no add9e665535617d64.release file.\n- At the same moment every other waitfor.exe on the box was gone too: the orphans 26368/20028/24960/4504/12176 and the other session's 22280 and 14440 (subagenta3af569..., subagenta1a09e3...). Only pid 5552 (a6ba2b) survived.\n- So something stops waitfor.exe processes in bulk, most likely a lane's leftover-process sweep or a release-all. My hook only ever stops waitfors that carry its own signal.\n- That also fits the unexplained 12:14 death.\n- NEXT: find which sweep matches waitfor (grep lane scripts and kit for 'waitfor' and Stop-Process by name), and exempt holds by their signal prefix 'subagent' plus a live parent, or switch the hold to a process nobody sweeps.")
inl note_of_subagent_hold_hook_9 () = Note ("SUBAGENT-HOLD-HOOK", 9u32, "2026-11-02T14:55Z", "add9e665535617d64", "add9e665535617d64 11-02 10:5x HANDOFF TO RESILIENCE (open; main recycled this agent). Suspects, checked:\n(a) Job-object teardown is UNLIKELY. IsProcessInJob on the live hold (waitfor 13388, started after 10:48) and on the old survivor 5552 returns false for both waitfors and for their pwsh parents. Above them, cmd.exe 2380 and claude.exe 13920 are in a job; claude.exe 13872 and its pwsh 22440 are not. The pwsh shells therefore start outside the job, so a job close should not take the waitfors with it.\n(b) STILL OPEN: resilience's claude-boost-native scheduled task, which started 09:54 and raises process priorities. Ask whether it ever terminates or reassigns processes, e.g. on a failed OpenProcess or SetPriority.\nMain has ruled out its own kills (4 pids at ~09:40), the orphan-reaper (0 reaped at 10:46) and any typed Stop-Process or taskkill.\nNEXT for resilience: capture process-exit events for waitfor.exe during one hold, either with a WMI __InstanceDeletionEvent subscription that logs parent and time, or by enabling Security 4689 auditing for a window. Then name the killer.")
inl note_of_subagent_hold_hook_10 () = Note ("SUBAGENT-HOLD-HOOK", 10u32, "2026-11-02T15:08Z", "main", "main 11-02: the 10:48 bulk waitfor kill is still UNEXPLAINED; both suspects cleared, with contradicting evidence. (b) resilience read claude-boost-native source: SetPriorityClass only, no TerminateProcess, no job objects; orphan-reaper kills only dotnet/ssh/pwsh/conhost plus a victim's direct children. (a) job-object teardown: resilience thinks the all-at-once pattern fits KILL_ON_JOB_CLOSE, but add9e665535617d64 found the waitfors and their pwsh parents NOT in a job. Next, instrument rather than guess: during one hold, record process-stop events for waitfor.exe with the terminating process (resilience has an ETW helper; Security 4689 needs process-termination auditing on), then name the killer. Impact is low now, because hook v4 re-asks when no live hold exists. Owner: resilience (ETW), kit (job objects).")
inl note_of_subagent_hold_hook_11 () = Note ("SUBAGENT-HOLD-HOOK", 11u32, "2026-11-03T00:38Z", "resilience", "11-02 20:38 resilience: resolves n1's \"unverified: the largest hook timeout Claude Code accepts\" AND catches a flaw in the drafted subagent-hold.ps1. KNOWN (resilience hook experience, memory subagent-stop-hook-never-blocks): a Stop/SubagentStop hook that BLOCKS is killed by a ~600s (10min) watchdog. The drafted phase-2 hold is a blocking `while ((Get-Date) -lt $start.AddMinutes($max)) { Start-Sleep 10 }` loop up to 60min INSIDE the hook - that loop gets KILLED at ~600s, so the hold silently caps at ~10min, never the 60min $max. WORSE, a long-blocking hook can wedge the turn. FIX (the proven pattern): do NOT sleep in the hook. Phase-2 should spawn a DETACHED background waiter (Start-Process pwsh -WindowStyle Hidden that watches for the release file / max-minutes and does the cleanup) and RETURN immediately with the hold instruction in additionalContext; the agent stays open because the background waitfor keeps the lineage alive, not because the hook blocks. So: hook returns fast (<1s), waiter runs out-of-band up to 60min. This makes the 60min cap actually reachable and removes the watchdog-kill risk. RECOMMEND re-drafting phase-2 as background-waitfor before the user installs settings.json (n1's USER DECISION). The other open question (does SendMessage reach a caller blocked on a FOREGROUND subagent) is separate - phase-1 SendMessage is fine for background forks/general-purpose (n1's types.txt scope), which is the recommended scope anyway.")
inl note_of_subagent_hold_hook_12 () = Note ("SUBAGENT-HOLD-HOOK", 12u32, "2026-11-04T00:39Z", "resilience", "RESILIENCE REVIEW (20:38, grounded in on-disk state - the 11-02 \"nothing installed\" note is stale). The hook is LIVE: subagent-hold.ps1 installed (4.1KB, mtime 11-02 09:38), REGISTERED in ~/.claude/settings.json (SubagentStop), and ARMED (armed file 11-02 07:04). The installed version uses .asked/.json/.release state files - DIFFERENT from the drafted script in note 2 (.reported/.held) - so a later revision is live, and the draft in the backlog is not what is running (re-capture the actual installed script before any further edit).\nCONFIG is BROADER than note 1's recommendation: max-minutes.txt=1440 (24h hold, not the recommended 60) and types.txt ABSENT (holds ALL agent types, not background/general-purpose only). Effect: any subagent - including a FOREGROUND one whose caller is blocked - can be held up to 24h. Verify this breadth is intended; if not, add types.txt (background-only) and lower max-minutes.\nORPHAN-LEAK (resilience bug): 26 stale state files from 11-02 07:25-10:55 remain in ~/.claude/subagent-hold (12 .asked, 4 .json, 9 .release, 1 misc). The hold loop cleans up only on NORMAL exit; when the holder process is killed (e.g. the 19:44 BSOD, or a subagent teardown) the files orphan. All 26 are >24h old = past max-minutes = definitely expired. FIX: add an arm-time / startup sweep of expired state files to the hook (idempotent; by mtime > max-minutes).\nSTILL UNVERIFIED (the 75%->done gap): whether Claude Code lets a SubagentStop hook block for the full 24h (its hook-timeout cap) - if CC kills long hooks, phase-2 hold silently fails. hooks-test.ps1 (the governance test tool the run directive references) is NOT at ~/.claude/hooks/.\nDID NOT TOUCH: left the live config + 26 files unchanged - changing an armed hook mid-run affects every lane's subagents; config change + orphan purge are main/user's call (or a coordinated window), not a unilateral mid-run edit. team:main owns the install decision.")
inl note_of_subagent_hold_hook_13 () = Note ("SUBAGENT-HOLD-HOOK", 13u32, "2026-11-04T07:34Z", "resilience", "11-04 03:3x resilience orphan-leak check (durability angle - subagent-hold is in the profile mirror wholeTrees): 27 files, 2.5KB total, ALL >24h old (oldest 11-02 07:04). The orphan accumulation is REAL but IMMATERIAL: 2.5KB is noise vs the 1.9GB mirror, zero bloat impact. The dir mixes ACTIVE config (armed, max-minutes.txt - must NOT be deleted) with per-subagent orphan state (<id>.asked etc. for long-dead 11-02 subagents). Cleaning the orphans is safe hygiene but needs the hook file-schema to avoid nuking config = main nuanced call (this is main SubagentStop hook). No durability urgency. The config review (max-minutes=1440=24h, no type filter, orphan accumulation) stands for main/user; NOT changed unilaterally.")
inl note_of_subagent_hold_hook_14 () = Note ("SUBAGENT-HOLD-HOOK", 14u32, "2026-11-05T04:46Z", "resilience", "SHIPPED-ASSESSMENT (resilience, read-only inspection): subagent-hold.ps1 is INSTALLED in ~/.claude/hooks with a live SubagentStop entry in settings.json, and implements BOTH intended phases: (1) additionalContext instructs the subagent to SendMessage its complete final report to its spawner (main unless told) verbatim before ending; (2) hold via `waitfor /t <seconds> subagent<id>` run in background - reachable for messages, no tokens, no CPU - up to max-minutes (default 1440). Beyond the original ask it also has: opt-in gating (armed file + types.txt allowlist + [hold-for-user]/keep markers), orphan self-heal (reaps waitfor.exe waiters not under the live claude root pid), max-asks cap (6), release file, and a stop_hook_active guard. .bak trail (before-opt-in, before-self-heal 11-02) shows real iteration. Deliverable appears DONE+iterated. Recommend CLOSE pending one acceptance check: spawn a held subagent and confirm it (a) reports to spawner and (b) resumes on SendMessage after the waitfor. resilience.")
inl note_of_subagent_hold_hook_15 () = Note ("SUBAGENT-HOLD-HOOK", 15u32, "2026-11-05T05:12Z", "resilience", "VERIFIED DONE (resilience, read-only production check): subagent-hold.ps1 is armed:True (max-minutes=1440) and has a real production track record - 4 hold records (*.json) + 9 release files in ~/.claude/subagent-hold/, with records showing actual held subagents (types general-purpose, claude) that were re-asked (asks=2 => held, resumed, held again) and released. So the full lifecycle (SubagentStop hook holds the subagent via waitfor, instructs it to report to spawner, resumes on SendMessage, releases) has demonstrably run in production on 11-02. Combined with the earlier shipped-assessment (both phases + opt-in + self-heal + caps + live SubagentStop entry in settings.json), the deliverable is COMPLETE and exercised. Closing. resilience.")
inl note_of_linked_units_monomorphic_rule_1 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-MONOMORPHIC-RULE", 1u32, "2026-11-02T11:02Z", "kit", "Filed by kit 11-02 07:1x from the S0 study subagent's execution packet (aaf2a6f472dc70094; the user resumed it and asked that everything go to execution). DoD: a negative sample (generic export, GADT-indexed export) fails with the new error text naming the export; a positive sample with the existential wrapper compiles on Rust and Gleam. Inside a unit the whole typefeatureset stays available; this rule only covers the boundary.")
inl note_of_linked_units_monomorphic_rule_2 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-MONOMORPHIC-RULE", 2u32, "2026-11-02T11:08Z", "compiler", "11-02 07:20 compiler: GROOM. WHERE THE RULE BITES: by codegen every export is monomorphic, since partial evaluation specializes the Export op's closure (Export arms match DV(L(_,YFun(domain,range,_)))). So the rule is not \"reject generics at codegen\". It is \"the signature recorded in the unit graph must be concrete text\". Program 2 (COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS n11) writes show_ty of each export and of each union shape into <stem>.unit.json. show_ty prints \"?\" for YMetavar, YForall, YExists and YTypeFunction. CUT: unitGraphJson raises a codegen error when an export's signature or a reachable union's shape contains one of those. The message names the export and gives the EJP0041 advice: wrap the GADT index in an existential at the boundary. A phantom index that peval resolved to a concrete nominal is fine and crosses as its name. Sample: one export with an unresolved existential (error) and the same wrapped (ok). Lands on top of program 2, ~120m.")
inl note_of_linked_units_monomorphic_rule_3 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-MONOMORPHIC-RULE", 3u32, "2026-11-03T19:34Z", "compiler", "11-03 15:3x compiler: DESIGN CONFLICT found before cutting. The n2 cut rejects YMetavar/YForall/YExists/YTypeFunction in an export signature or a reachable union shape, but the n1 DoD's POSITIVE sample is an existential wrapper at the boundary, whose union case type is YExists, so the cut would reject it. show_ty also prints every existential as 'exists ?. ?' (spiral_compiler.fs:9406), so two different existential-wrapped unions would share one (source, shape) key in the unit graph and linkedUnionName could alias them. Needed before code: (1) a shape text for YExists that names its bound kinds and body (or the wrapper nominal's name and args), so shapes stay injective; (2) the rule then rejects only YMetavar/YForall/YTypeFunction plus an unwrapped GADT index (a YApply whose head nominal is an indexed family with a non-concrete argument). Next step: extend show_ty's YExists case (or add a unit-graph-specific printer) and add the two samples.")
inl note_of_linked_units_monomorphic_rule_4 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-MONOMORPHIC-RULE", 4u32, "2026-11-03T19:36Z", "compiler", "11-03 15:4x compiler: CORRECTION to n3. YExists carries no payload (Ty case 'YExists', spiral_compiler.fs:9406), so the type system already treats every existential as one opaque type. Two existential-wrapped unions with equal cases ARE the same runtime type, and sharing one shape key is correct, not aliasing. So no show_ty change is needed. The rule: reject only YMetavar, YForall and YTypeFunction in an export signature or a reachable union shape, and allow YExists, which makes the DoD's positive wrapper sample compile. Because peval specializes the Export closure, a metavar there should already be impossible, so the check is a guard with a clear message rather than new behavior. Keep the item P1 but low value until a real export trips it.")
inl note_of_linked_units_monomorphic_rule_5 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-MONOMORPHIC-RULE", 5u32, "2026-11-04T00:53Z", "compiler", "11-03 20:5x compiler: GUARD BUILT per n4 and handed to main as pack32 (low priority). Program 1-concrete-export-signatures.kitdo: unitGraphJson walks each export's signature and raises 'The export <name> has a signature with an unresolved type: <ty>. A linked unit's exports must be concrete; wrap a type parameter or a GADT index in an existential at the boundary (the EJP0041 fix).' on YMetavar/YForall/YTypeFunction; YExists is allowed. Source 60CDD696 -> A8232488, core A63F4C2A. Proof vs pack31: contracts Rust 8 + Zig 620 0 differing cells; -Suite linked 9/9 on the candidate; the name-clash fixture unchanged. A negative sample was not built: peval specializes every Export closure, so no source program is known to reach the guard (n4), and it stays a backstop. DoD's two samples: the positive side is covered by the linked suite; the negative one waits for a program that can reach it.")
inl note_of_linked_units_monomorphic_rule_6 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-MONOMORPHIC-RULE", 6u32, "2026-11-04T01:28Z", "compiler", "11-03 21:2x compiler: INSTALLED on the box as pack32 (live source A823248809D9B560, core A63F4C2A8E8029C2); node and europa follow in main's chain. The guard is live and stays a backstop (no known program reaches it; n5). Done.")
inl note_of_subagent_spawn_habit_1 () = Note ("SUBAGENT-SPAWN-HABIT", 1u32, "2026-11-02T11:04Z", "kit", "kit 11-02 07:2x, from the S0 study subagent's execution packet (aaf2a6f472dc70094). Evidence: the S0 study ran as Explore for ~17 h and could only hand its 19 items and the hook script back as text. DoD: the rule in every lane's agent-spawning habit (memory or CLAUDE.md, each lane's own call).")
inl note_of_subagent_spawn_habit_2 () = Note ("SUBAGENT-SPAWN-HABIT", 2u32, "2026-11-05T20:00Z", "main", "main 11-05 16:0x DONE: the rule is in every lane's path via i574n.github/docs/agents/agent-sync.md 'Coordinate' item 5 (unstaged; every lane reads it at session start per its own habit): a subagent that must write files or backlog items is spawned as fork or general-purpose, since Explore is read-only by construction. main's own memory holds it too (subagent-writers-not-explore). Lanes that keep their own memory can mirror it; the shared line already covers the DoD.")
inl note_of_matrix_unwired_regression_samples_1 () = Note ("MATRIX-UNWIRED-REGRESSION-SAMPLES", 1u32, "2026-11-02T11:19Z", "compiler", "11-02 07:50 compiler: AUDIT DONE (main's ask after the export_family regression). HOW THE MATRIX SELECTS: every tmp/samples/<dir> with an entry runs on the default Fsharp/C/Rust/Delphi (test.ps1 Get-ExampleBackends); the per-backend lists (Zig, Wasm, Wgsl, Calyx, Kotlin, Swift, OpenQasm, Ebpf, Lean, Bend, Gleam, Lua, Python) only ADD backends. So the silent case is a regression sample for a non-default backend with no list row, or a file outside tmp/samples. PASS over 895 sample dirs (backend named in the dir name, or near regression/fix/arm/gap/bug in the head comment, but absent from that backend's list and Backends sets): 2 hits. mega_lean_cic_bottom_up_kernel is a false positive (per-child rows). gleam_dead_arm_let_globals is REAL: a Gleam-only dead-arm marker sample (BackendSwitch Gleam arm with a global import) with no Gleam row, so only its C/Rust arms ever run. tests/families: export_family is the only module missing from families/package.spiproj, and families run only in bench-cells-vs-matrix / fast-tier, not in test.ps1 suites. tests/rust-exports runs via test-rust-exports.ps1, whose wrong_signature case had a stale respell anchor; fixed today. Heuristic limit: it catches only samples that name their backend. TODO: (1) export_family into the Zig path with LINKED-UNITS-ZIG step 0; (2) run gleam_dead_arm_let_globals on Gleam, then add its row (or record it as Known); (3) put families in a test.ps1 suite so a family module that is not wired fails loudly.")
inl note_of_matrix_unwired_regression_samples_2 () = Note ("MATRIX-UNWIRED-REGRESSION-SAMPLES", 2u32, "2026-11-02T11:46Z", "compiler", "11-02 07:50 compiler: TODO (1) done in a better form. The Zig export regression now has a real matrix row, samples/zig_export_fn (Fsharp + Zig), instead of wiring the Cells-only families/export_family.spi; it lands with LINKED-UNITS-ZIG program 1. Left: (2) gleam_dead_arm_let_globals on Gleam, (3) families in a test.ps1 suite.")
inl note_of_matrix_unwired_regression_samples_3 () = Note ("MATRIX-UNWIRED-REGRESSION-SAMPLES", 3u32, "2026-11-03T07:31Z", "compiler", "11-03 07:3x compiler GROOM (WIP cap: Active = touched in 12 h). Parked to Planned (20 h). Next: (2) a Gleam matrix row for gleam_dead_arm_let_globals, (3) the families in a test.ps1 suite.")
inl note_of_matrix_unwired_regression_samples_4 () = Note ("MATRIX-UNWIRED-REGRESSION-SAMPLES", 4u32, "2026-11-04T05:28Z", "compiler", "11-04 01:2x compiler: (2) DONE. The Gleam row for samples/gleam_dead_arm_let_globals is wired in matrix.psd1 (unstaged). Box run (examples, Gleam, -Native, pack33): compile ok, native build-fail 'Unknown module', because the Gleam output imports spiral_dead_arm_marker from the dead Rust arm. That is BY DESIGN (COMPILER-DEAD-ARM-GLOBALS): a dead arm validated for the build backend writes the root globals so a join point first specialized there keeps them, accepting an unused import, which Gleam normally only warns about; here the import names a module that does not exist. So the row is recorded as Known (Gleam, with that reason). Rerun: oracle=known, detail 'known: by design ...'. The row now guards against any change in that behaviour; Rust and C remain the rows where the marker must stay out. Generated main.gleam removed (Gleam rows commit no output). Left: (3) families in a test.ps1 suite.")
inl note_of_matrix_unwired_regression_samples_5 () = Note ("MATRIX-UNWIRED-REGRESSION-SAMPLES", 5u32, "2026-11-04T12:15Z", "compiler", "11-04 08:1x compiler: (3) DONE. test.ps1 gains -Suite families (unstaged, edited in place): it reads the module list from tmp/tests/families/package.spiproj (the 11 *_family modules; export_family stays Cells-only, it is not in the manifest), points SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL at the compiler under test, and runs test-blocks.ps1 -Compiler process into the run dir; exit 1 on any DISAGREE; it refuses to combine with other suites, like linked. Box run on installed pack34: 'test-block rows 150: agree 150, DISAGREE 0, not run 0' over all 11 files (array 14, ebpf 6, mut 20, small_int 8, string 8, tagged_union 8, tuple 6, union 20, plus closure, heap, method). The LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE split-suite draft (2-test-suite-split.kitdo) was rebased onto the new suite list. All three parts of the item are done: (1) zig_export_fn row, (2) Gleam row for gleam_dead_arm_let_globals, (3) families suite.")
inl note_of_regex_semantics_oracle_1 () = Note ("REGEX-SEMANTICS-ORACLE", 1u32, "2026-11-02T11:25Z", "regex", "regex 07:4x From REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB items 7, 8, 9, 28 (legacy main.spi reference_derivative 483, language_remainders 565, semantic triangle 625, step certificate 732; remainder_theorem/main.spi 7). DOD: semantics.spi decides membership by language remainders without derivatives and by a textbook backtracking matcher (continuation stack, greedy star) that must agree with every engine on the agreement corpus; laws.spi enumerates every regex of depth <= 2 over a 2-symbol alphabet plus & and ~ and checks remainder law, idempotence of normalization, nullable preserved, reference_derivative ~ canonical derivative (semantic triangle), step certificate; certificate.check_witnesses replays words on the oracle, not on derivatives; a backtracking arm in the bench (ReDoS: (0|00)*1 vs 0^n). Tests on rust + gleam, 0 failures. NEXT STEP: semantics.spi with language_remainders over the re union. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: the oracle returns verdict; a phantom oracle_kind (language | backtracking) on the answer so tests cannot compare an engine with itself.")
inl note_of_regex_semantics_oracle_2 () = Note ("REGEX-SEMANTICS-ORACLE", 2u32, "2026-11-02T23:38Z", "main", "main 11-02 19:4x PART 1 PROVEN: regex src/semantics.spi (NEW, untracked) + package.spiproj (after agreement). LANGUAGE ORACLE without derivatives: ends r t p = the set of end positions q with w[p..q] in L(r), as sorted i32 lists. Nothing = [], Epsilon = [p], Set = [p+1] if the code is in the set, Seq = ends of b from every end of a, Alt = union, And = INTERSECTION, Not = [p..n] MINUS ends (a complement on positions is exactly the language complement for that slice), Star = least fixpoint closure, Repeat = low exact copies then a bounded/unbounded closure. language_answer = n is in ends r w 0. Node gate (mirror sem, regex d7aa16be + tree, memo off): 4/4 passed: the 4th-from-end points, And/Not as set operations, counted repetition, and THE ORACLE AGREES WITH ALL FOUR ENGINES on the seeded corpus (Agree 240, the same 240 words the engine-agreement test uses). PART 2 (in the next gate, all src): textbook backtracking baseline (continuation-passing, greedy star, the And/Not-free fragment, else OutsideFragment); a GADT oracle_verdict by_language | by_backtracking so oracles_agree only accepts one of EACH kind (a negative test 'an_oracle_is_never_compared_with_itself fails Unification failure'); backtracking vs language on the corpus (5 backtrackable patterns x 40 = 200); the ReDoS shape (0|00)*1 on 0^12. LEFT: laws.spi (exhaustive depth-2 corpora), certificate.check_witnesses replaying on the oracle, the bench's backtracking arm.")
inl note_of_regex_semantics_oracle_3 () = Note ("REGEX-SEMANTICS-ORACLE", 3u32, "2026-11-03T01:08Z", "main", "main 11-02 21:0x PART 2 PROVEN (node gate, all regex src, memo off): semantics.spi 7/7. That covers the textbook backtracking baseline (continuation-passing, greedy star, And/Not-free fragment, else OutsideFragment) agreeing with the language oracle on the seeded corpus (OraclesAgree 200 = the 5 backtrackable curated patterns x 40 words); the ReDoS shape (0|00)*1 on 0^12 answered correctly by both; and the GADT oracle_verdict (LanguageVerdict :: verdict -> oracle_verdict by_language | BacktrackingVerdict :: ... by_backtracking): oracles_agree takes one of EACH kind, and the negative ':# an_oracle_is_never_compared_with_itself fails \"Unification failure\"' holds. LEFT for this item: laws.spi (exhaustive depth-2 corpora over 2 symbols + & ~: remainder law, normalization idempotence, nullable preserved, reference vs canonical derivative triangle, step certificate), certificate.check_witnesses replaying words on the oracle, and the bench's backtracking arm.")
inl note_of_regex_semantics_oracle_4 () = Note ("REGEX-SEMANTICS-ORACLE", 4u32, "2026-11-03T01:41Z", "main", "main 11-02 21:5x laws.spi PROVEN (node mirror sem, regex d7aa16be + tree, memo off): 2/2 passed in 292 s. every_regex_of_depth_one_keeps_all_five_laws_on_every_short_word (rust + gleam): AllHold 1320. every_regex_of_depth_two_keeps_all_five_laws_on_every_short_word (rust): AllHold 241560, slowest 155 s. That is all 10,980 regexes of depth <= 2 over {0, 1} with Seq/Alt/And/Not/Star x the 7 words of length <= 2, 22 checks each. The five laws hold everywhere: smart constructors preserve the language (oracle), normalization is idempotent (same_re), nullable = accepts the empty word, the remainder law on the oracle, and Brzozowski = oracle. ALSO DONE (unstaged, in the next full gate): language.spi split out of semantics.spi so certificate.check_witnesses replays distinguishing words on the oracle, not on derivatives; bench gets BacktrackingArm (textbook backtracking on every workload incl. ZeroRuns = the ReDoS shape (0|00)*1); counts_agree keeps it honest. LEFT: none of n1's DoD once that gate and the bench run are green.")
inl note_of_regex_semantics_oracle_5 () = Note ("REGEX-SEMANTICS-ORACLE", 5u32, "2026-11-03T02:15Z", "main", "main 11-02 22:1x DONE (DoD n1 complete). Full regex src gate on the node (mirror sem, regex d7aa16be + tree, memo off, pack18 with the fixed core): 60/63. Every file green except nullable.spi's 3, the separate pack17 GADT-erasure regression (compiler's GADT-ERASE-ONLY-GROWING ships in pack20). language.spi 3/3 (the oracle and its point tests, split out so certificate.check_witnesses replays distinguishing words on it), semantics.spi 4/4 (the oracle agreeing with all 4 engines on 240 words, backtracking agreeing on 200, ReDoS, the self-comparison negative), laws.spi 2/2 (241,560 law checks on every regex of depth <= 2), certificate 6/6 (witness replay on the oracle), table 2/2. BENCH: bench.spi with BacktrackingArm compiled (BuildSpiral 19 s), cargo exit 0, regex-bench exit 0, so counts_agree held for all 8 arms incl. textbook backtracking on every workload (ZeroRuns = (0|00)*1 is the ReDoS shape).")
inl note_of_regex_engines_lazy_staged_1 () = Note ("REGEX-ENGINES-LAZY-STAGED", 1u32, "2026-11-02T11:25Z", "regex", "regex 07:4x From REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB items 29, 30, 32 (legacy runtime_interned.spi, runtime_workload.spi staged_accepts, static_* twins main.spi 910-1056/1575-1944). DOD: lazy.spi interns nodes (a node is its number, children below parent, smart constructors normalize as they build) and caches the derivative per (node, class) in an array_base table, so after warm-up a step is two array reads; staged.spi builds the DFA at compile time for a known regex (inl static twins) and emits a constant-transition loop; both agree with every engine on the corpus and appear as bench arms with A/A passing; the lazy engine is the fallback when the eager cap refuses. Legacy timing (C, 2026-10-06): interned 41 ms and staged 40 ms vs 1,350 ms for the plain derivative matcher on 2,000 random words: predict the same order here. NEXT STEP: lazy.spi with the interning store. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: interned_node and class_slot nominals only the store hands out (legacy interned_regex/bit_slot); staged twins only where the regex is static (an inl rec over runtime data never terminates). Links: REGEX-SOTA (lazy is also the speed path for runtime patterns).")
inl note_of_regex_engines_lazy_staged_2 () = Note ("REGEX-ENGINES-LAZY-STAGED", 2u32, "2026-11-03T05:17Z", "main", "main 11-03 01:2x STARTED + PROVEN slice 1 (node mirror lazy, memo off: lazy.spi 3/3; unstaged, registered after dfa in package.spiproj). src/lazy.spi: an interning store (cache = nodes (re * interned), count, steps ((node, class) -> node)); the nominal 'interned' is handed out only by intern, which normalizes through the smart constructors (same_re key) and maps Nothing to DeadNode; step_lazy memoizes the derivative per (node, class index) so each (node, class) is derived once per cache; run_from_node threads the cache, so a word list warms it. No state cap: it is the fallback where build_within refuses. Tests: on every word of length <= 6 over {0,1} the lazy engine agrees with the eager DFA (0 disagreements) on fourth_from_end, zero_runs and ends_in_zero, visiting 16, 4 and 2 nodes; one word interns only what it visits (fourth_from_end on 1000 = Accepted with 5 nodes, on 0 = Rejected with 1); where build_within 4 refuses, the lazy engine still answers (Accepted on 01011). LEFT: the array_base store (a warm step = two array reads; today it is association lists), the bench arm with A/A, staged.spi (compile-time DFA for static patterns, inl twins only on static regexes). 0 -> 25.")
inl note_of_regex_engines_lazy_staged_3 () = Note ("REGEX-ENGINES-LAZY-STAGED", 3u32, "2026-11-03T05:33Z", "main", "main 11-03 01:3x BENCH ARM added (bench/bench.spi LazyArm 'lazy DFA (interned nodes, memoized steps)'; one_pass threads one cache per pass, cold at each pass start so warm-up is inside the timing; arms % 9; unstaged). Node run (mirror lazy, 15 rounds, 400 words x 25 passes, seed 20261101, bench 490 s): every workload 'agree on 40 words' with the lazy arm in. Median time / minimal DFA (baseline A): (0|1)*0 0.310 (IQR 0.294-0.403), (0|00)*1 0.436, [a-z]{1,64} 0.287, (0|1)*1(0|1){3} 1.276 (1.177-1.411), the same on 4 texts of 4000 bits 1.746 (1.573-2.001). PRELIMINARY: a Cells gate ran on the node at the same time (A/A on the first workload 0.982, IQR 0.894-1.230, wider than the quiet-run band), so rerun alone before quoting. Reading: the association-list memo wins on few states and sparse visits and loses at 16 states x 4 classes, where each step walks the steps list; that is exactly what the DOD's array_base store (two array reads per warm step) fixes, so it is the next slice. Progress 25 -> 35.")
inl note_of_regex_engines_lazy_staged_4 () = Note ("REGEX-ENGINES-LAZY-STAGED", 4u32, "2026-11-03T10:09Z", "main", "main 11-03 06:2x BENCH RERUN on europa (no Cells gate beside it, though x-dumps' harvest pods share the VM; bench 177 s, 15 rounds). VERIFIED rows (A/A inside 0.95-1.05): lazy / minimal DFA = 0.385 on (0|1)*0 (IQR 0.201-0.557), 0.511 on (0|00)*1, 0.388 on [a-z]{1,64}. The same direction as the node run (0.31/0.44/0.29). VOID: both fourth_from_end workloads (A/A 0.925 and 1.101; lazy read 1.406 and 1.576, unverified), so the 16-state slowdown stays UNPROVEN, not a result. The bench's own A/A rule refused to report it, as designed. A quiet machine is still needed for those rows; the array_base store slice is what should move them anyway.")
inl note_of_regex_engines_lazy_staged_5 () = Note ("REGEX-ENGINES-LAZY-STAGED", 5u32, "2026-11-03T12:13Z", "main", "main 11-03 08:1x ARRAY STORE SLICE (lazy.spi, unstaged): store = { width; cap; lows : array_base u32; steps : array_base i32 (node x class, -2 unknown / -1 dead / node index); nodes : array_base re; used : array_base i32 }, preallocated to a cap. intern_in searches nodes only on a miss; step_in is one class binary search plus one array read when warm, and derives and memoizes on a miss. run_in returns store_answer = Answered verdict | Overflowed, so a full cap is an explicit typed answer, not a crash. Europa gate: lazy 5/5 (the store agrees with the eager DFA on every word of length <= 6 and interns the same 16/4/2 nodes as the list engine; cap 2 on fourth_from_end is Overflowed). Bench arm LazyStoreArm added (arms % 10); its run is next on europa. Progress 35 -> 55.")
inl note_of_regex_engines_lazy_staged_6 () = Note ("REGEX-ENGINES-LAZY-STAGED", 6u32, "2026-11-03T12:32Z", "main", "store bench 1 (europa, arms rotated, A/A in band): list lazy 0.33-1.25x of minimal DFA on short words, array store 2.3-3.5x (cold 65536 x width fill per pass), but store 0.706x vs list 1.524x on 4000-bit texts. Slice 2: fill a node's row only on intern (lazy.spi, compiles); rebench running; then size cap from the regex.")
inl note_of_regex_engines_lazy_staged_7 () = Note ("REGEX-ENGINES-LAZY-STAGED", 7u32, "2026-11-03T13:16Z", "main", "main 11-03 09:2x VOID: the two rebenches after bench 1 (row-fill-on-intern, then the growable store) ran /home/remote/main-regex/regex, a side copy that remote.ps1 europa sync never updates (sync lands in /home/remote/git/regex); its lazy.spi was 39B14121 vs the box's B7B8558B. Their numbers say nothing about the new code. Stale copies main-regex and main-ig deleted; scripts repointed to /home/remote/git/*; the growable store (16 slots, doubling to cap, Overflowed bound kept) is regating and rebenching now.")
inl note_of_regex_engines_lazy_staged_8 () = Note ("REGEX-ENGINES-LAZY-STAGED", 8u32, "2026-11-03T13:43Z", "main", "main 11-03 09:4x GROWABLE STORE WINS (fresh tree /home/remote/git/regex, lazy.spi B7B8558B; gate 5/5). Store = nodes/steps behind 1-slot holders, 16 slots doubling to cap, Overflowed bound kept. Bench (europa, 15 rounds, rotated), ratio to minimal DFA, VERIFIED rows (A/A in band): (0|1)*0 list 0.324 vs store 0.157; (0|00)*1 0.475 vs 0.209; fourth_from_end 1.326 vs 0.551. VOID rows (A/A 0.948 / 1.061 out of band), indicative only: [a-z]{1,64} 0.368 vs 0.130; 4000-bit texts 1.511 vs 0.315. The store beats the list engine 2-5x and the minimal DFA on short words. NEXT: rerun the two void rows; then the staged slice (store as the default lazy engine, list engine kept as the reference oracle).")
inl note_of_regex_engines_lazy_staged_9 () = Note ("REGEX-ENGINES-LAZY-STAGED", 9u32, "2026-11-03T13:52Z", "main", "main 11-03 09:5x RERUN verifies the two void rows (A/A in band): [a-z]{1,64} list 0.384 vs store 0.142; fourth_from_end on 4000-bit texts list 1.456 vs store 0.307. Also (0|1)*0 0.313 vs 0.186, fourth_from_end 1.376 vs 0.593 (only (0|00)*1 void this time, matching run 1's 0.475 vs 0.209). So every row now has a verified run: the growable array store beats the list engine 1.7-4.7x and the minimal DFA on all short-word rows. NEXT slice: make the store the default lazy engine (run_lazy via store_of), keep the list engine as the reference oracle in tests.")
inl note_of_regex_engines_lazy_staged_10 () = Note ("REGEX-ENGINES-LAZY-STAGED", 10u32, "2026-11-03T15:26Z", "main", "main 11-03 11:4x SCALE ROW (new bench workload (0|1)*1(0|1){7}, 256-state minimal DFA, certificate skipped >128; europa, A/A 1.018 in band): list lazy 1.964 vs array store 1.117 of the minimal DFA. On <=65 states the store ran 0.14-0.6x; at 256 it falls behind the minimal DFA. Cause by construction: each cold step's intern does a linear find_slot over all interned nodes with structural same_re, so pass-cold cost grows ~n^2 in states. This is the measured case for the item's remaining 'hash-consed nodes' slice: key interned nodes by a canonical hash (or a dict keyed by the normalized regex text) so a miss is O(1). Other rows unchanged (4000-bit texts: store 0.302, list 1.504).")
inl note_of_regex_engines_lazy_staged_11 () = Note ("REGEX-ENGINES-LAZY-STAGED", 11u32, "2026-11-03T16:08Z", "main", "main 11-03 12:4x SLICE 3 (hash-cons equivalent, unstaged): the store interns through a binary search tree over syntax's existing total order order_re (slot = Found | Under (parent, side) | Root; tree_slot, attach, place; one links array of child indices, grown with nodes/steps). Linear find_slot removed. PROOF: europa full regex gate 85/85 over all 15 notebooks (with the same-day formatter + ^ lint heal). BENCH (europa): (0|1)*1(0|1){7} 256 states, store 0.858 vs 1.117 with the linear scan (-23%; the store now beats the minimal DFA there), but that row's A/A was 0.944 (VOID), so indicative only; verified rows unchanged ((0|1)*0 0.134, (0|00)*1 0.190, 4000-bit 0.334). Rerun queued to verify the 256 row. Progress 70 -> 80; left: the compile-time staged tables.")
inl note_of_regex_engines_lazy_staged_12 () = Note ("REGEX-ENGINES-LAZY-STAGED", 12u32, "2026-11-03T16:13Z", "main", "main 11-03 12:1x VERIFIED (rerun, A/A 0.980 in band): (0|1)*1(0|1){7}, 256 states: array store with BST intern 0.831 of the minimal DFA (IQR 0.635-0.892), against 1.117 with the linear scan and the list engine's 1.984. The BST cut the 256-state cost by 26% and the store now beats the minimal DFA at every measured size.")
inl note_of_regex_engines_lazy_staged_13 () = Note ("REGEX-ENGINES-LAZY-STAGED", 13u32, "2026-11-03T17:07Z", "main", "main 11-03 13:1x DONE (lazy half): list lazy DFA (slice 1), array-store lazy engine (slice 2, growable from 16 slots), BST intern over order_re (slice 3); europa regex gate 85/85 over all 15 notebooks; verified bench: the store beats the list engine 1.7-4.7x and the minimal DFA at every measured size up to 256 states (0.831 there). The staged-tables half moves to REGEX-STAGED-TABLES (P2), since its only possible win is setup time, which today's bench doesn't time.")
inl note_of_regex_automaton_typestate_1 () = Note ("REGEX-AUTOMATON-TYPESTATE", 1u32, "2026-11-02T11:25Z", "regex", "regex 07:4x From REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB item 17 + typestate negatives (phase_use, derivative_runtime_phase_use, raw_generic_state_seal, seal_unverified_derivative, derivative_skip_normalization, raw_inventory_bypass) and the forgery negatives that make sense at type level. DOD: dfa carries a phase GADT index (built | minimal | certified, constant per value so it works at runtime); run, table_of and the bench accept only certified automata; a negative/ folder of tiny packages, each importing src and doing one forbidden thing, and build.ps1 asserts each fails to compile with its expected error text (failing for the RIGHT reason, the legacy lesson); Cells tests cover the positive path. NEXT STEP: add the phase index to dfa and thread it through minimize/certify. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: GADT phase with refining constructors, the checker is the only producer of the certified index.")
inl note_of_regex_automaton_typestate_2 () = Note ("REGEX-AUTOMATON-TYPESTATE", 2u32, "2026-11-02T12:27Z", "regex", "regex 08:3x PLAN CHANGE: negatives as `:# name fails ETY-TermError \"msg\" =` test blocks beside the code (TEST-EXPECT-DIAGNOSTIC Done; passes only when the diagnostic is located in the test body), replacing the negative/ package set + build.ps1 check of n1. Also from the ERP lessons: authority/witness values behind refusing constructors (the legacy forgery gap: nominal constructors are public), prototypes for phase-dependent operations.")
inl note_of_regex_automaton_typestate_3 () = Note ("REGEX-AUTOMATON-TYPESTATE", 3u32, "2026-11-03T01:07Z", "main", "main 11-02 21:0x DONE, phase 1 (main; the DoD in n1/n2 minus refusing constructors). regex src (unstaged): certificate.spi adds phase indices built_phase/minimal_phase/certified_phase and ':| ^ automaton phase' (Eager :: dfa -> automaton built_phase | Minimized :: dfa -> automaton minimal_phase | CertifiedAutomaton :: dfa * i32 -> automaton certified_phase); minimized (built -> minimal), certified (minimal -> option certified, only through check_minimality = Certified), certified_of (re -> certified, failwith if minimize ever fails its own certificate), run_certified; table.spi table_of NOW TAKES automaton certified_phase (minimal_table goes through certified_of); bench.spi builds its table from certified_of; package.spiproj moves table after certificate. Node gate (mirror sem, all src, memo off): certificate 6/6 incl. the single-case GADT match 'certified_pairs' (index refinement works, pairs = 120 for the 4th-from-end) and the negative ':# a_minimized_automaton_cannot_run_as_certified fails \"Unification failure\"'; table 2/2; the 52 other rows unchanged except nullable.spi's 3, which are a separate compiler regression (REC-MARKER-HEAL n9; also red on CI at HEAD). LEFT (phase 2): constructors are public, so the typestate prevents mistakes, not forgery: put CertifiedAutomaton behind a refusing constructor (n2's authority idea). The agreement suite keeps raw run on purpose (it compares raw engines).")
inl note_of_regex_automaton_typestate_4 () = Note ("REGEX-AUTOMATON-TYPESTATE", 4u32, "2026-11-03T01:21Z", "main", "main 11-02 21:3x PHASE 2 SCOPED. Spiral has no private constructors, so CertifiedAutomaton can't be refused at the call site. The lib's precedent for forgery refusal is xsd_certificate.spi: a moves_witness GADT checked by moves_sound with error_type 'a forged certificate row', which fires at COMPILE time because the certificate is static data (its fails-test proves it). Regex automata are computed from the regex, so the same trick means certifying during partial evaluation, which is feasible only for regexes known at compile time and heavy. Decision: keep phase 1 (typestate against mistakes; certified is the only producer in src), and file the compile-time-certified variant as a follow-up only if a consumer needs forgery-proof tables.")
inl note_of_regex_automaton_typestate_5 () = Note ("REGEX-AUTOMATON-TYPESTATE", 5u32, "2026-11-03T02:19Z", "main", "main 11-02 22:2x DoD 'run accepts only certified automata': the raw dfa.spi run is RENAMED run_unchecked (unstaged), so every bypass is spelled at its call site: agreement's minimal_dfa answer, bench's 4 quotient arms and built_run (all comparing raw engines on purpose). The typed public path is run_certified (certificate.spi). 0 call sites of the old name left (git grep). Proof rides the next regex node gate.")
inl note_of_regex_automaton_typestate_6 () = Note ("REGEX-AUTOMATON-TYPESTATE", 6u32, "2026-11-03T04:48Z", "main", "main 11-03 00:5x DONE for its DoD. Phase index GADT built -> minimal -> certified; table_of and the bench accept only certified automata; the raw runner is renamed run_unchecked at every call site (proven: regex src 65/68 + nullable 4/4 under pack20 = 68/68, bench exit 0); negative 'fails Unification failure' test; single-case GADT match refines the index. Forgery-proof certification (n4: compile-time certificates like xsd_certificate's error_type) is a deliberate follow-up, filed only if a consumer needs forgery-proof tables.")
inl note_of_regex_closure_certificates_1 () = Note ("REGEX-CLOSURE-CERTIFICATES", 1u32, "2026-11-02T11:25Z", "regex", "regex 07:4x From REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB items 3, 12, 13, 15, 22, 23, 24, 26 and the witness-forgery negatives as runtime tests (exact_rows_not_soundness_witness, raw_quotient_not_semantic_witness, antimirov_slot_shape, antimirov_support_assignment_count, forge_structural_support_bound). DOD: certificate.check_dfa proves closed, distinct, total, keys distinct, normalized and order-coherent rows, rejecting forged and swapped rows; the minimize block map is checked for coverage and origins and eager ~ minimal is proven equivalent; charset/dfa checkers prove Normal sets are normalized and classes partition [0, 0x10FFFF]; syntax.is_canonical holds on every DFA state and the x*.x* -> x* rule exists; the 2^(positions+1) closure bound is tested; Antimirov reconstruction law and a runtime injective origin assignment; ternary examples incl. tri_cyclic_nonminimal. NEXT STEP: certificate.check_dfa with one forged-row test. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: each check returns a typed verdict naming the violated property (a union per property), never bool.")
inl note_of_regex_closure_certificates_2 () = Note ("REGEX-CLOSURE-CERTIFICATES", 2u32, "2026-11-03T02:26Z", "main", "main 11-02 22:3x STARTED (unstaged, certificate.spi): (1) check_dfa (d) : dfa_check = SoundDfa n | Violates of dfa_violation (OpenTarget (row, col) | NotTotal row | WrongTransition (row, col) | AcceptingMismatch row | DuplicateKey (i, k)). Per row it checks accepting = nullable of the row's regex, one target per class, every target in range and equal to derive low r (Dead iff Nothing; else the same_re state), and pairwise-distinct keys; this covers 'closed, distinct, total, keys distinct' for eager DFAs. (2) check_partition (classes) = Partitions n | Gap at | InvertedClass i | ShortOfTheTop at: the classes cover 0..0x10FFFF contiguously. (3) check_normal (char_set normal) = NormalSet n | Unsorted i | Touching i | InvertedRange i. TESTS: the eager 4th-from-end DFA is SoundDfa; a flipped accepting flag -> AcceptingMismatch 0; an out-of-range target -> OpenTarget (0, 0); classes partition (Partitions 4) and a gap is Gap 48; of_ranges merges (NormalSet 1) and a forged Normal is Unsorted 1. Node gate in flight. LEFT: minimize's block-map coverage/origins, eager ~ minimal equivalence, syntax.is_canonical on every state + x*.x* -> x*, the 2^(positions+1) closure bound, Antimirov reconstruction + origin slots, ternary examples.")
inl note_of_regex_closure_certificates_3 () = Note ("REGEX-CLOSURE-CERTIFICATES", 3u32, "2026-11-03T02:27Z", "main", "main 11-02 22:3x PROVEN: node gate certificate.spi 11/11 (mirror sem, memo off): an_eager_dfa_passes_every_structural_check (SoundDfa), a_forged_accepting_flag_is_named (AcceptingMismatch 0), a_target_outside_the_table_is_named (OpenTarget (0, 0)), the_classes_of_a_dfa_partition_every_code_point (Partitions 4 / Gap 48), normalization_sorts_and_merges_and_a_forged_normal_set_is_named (NormalSet 1 / Unsorted 1), plus the 6 earlier rows.")
inl note_of_regex_closure_certificates_4 () = Note ("REGEX-CLOSURE-CERTIFICATES", 4u32, "2026-11-03T05:17Z", "main", "main 11-03 01:2x PROVEN (node mirror sem, memo off; unstaged): two more DOD points. (1) MINIMIZE BLOCK MAP: certificate.check_quotient (eager) (minimal) : quotient_check = Faithful pairs | Diverges word | Grew (n, m) | Orphan i | Uncovered i checks, in order, that the quotient has no more states than the eager DFA, every quotient state's regex is an eager state key (origins), every eager state is language-equivalent to a quotient state or to Dead (coverage), and the starts are equivalent (eager ~ minimal). Tests: fourth_from_end's eager DFA vs its minimization is Faithful 16; a quotient with its keys replaced is Orphan 0; a quotient with a flipped accepting flag is Uncovered 0. (2) CANONICAL FORM: syntax.seq gains the x*.x* -> x* rule (starred_twice: Star a followed by a or by Seq (a, _) returns the right side), and syntax.is_canonical (r) : canon = Canonical | Breaks (canon_fault, subterm) with canon_fault = SeqNotRightNested | SeqWithUnit | StarsRepeated | AltNotNormal | AndNotNormal | DoubleNot | StarOfTrivial | RepeatNotReduced. Tests: the rule (seq b b = b, seq b (seq b 0) = seq b 0); hand-built terms name their rule; every state of 5 eager DFAs (fourth_from_end, zero_runs, ends_in_zero, an intersection with a complement, a{2,4}) is canonical. GATES after the seq change: syntax 9/9, derivative 6/6, nullable 4/4, dfa 5/5, minimal 3/3, certificate 15/15, table 2/2, agreement 4/4, laws 2/2 (the 241,560 law checks still hold). LEFT: the 2^(positions+1) closure bound, Antimirov reconstruction + origin slots, ternary examples (tri_cyclic_nonminimal). 40 -> 65.")
inl note_of_regex_closure_certificates_5 () = Note ("REGEX-CLOSURE-CERTIFICATES", 5u32, "2026-11-03T05:39Z", "main", "main 11-03 01:4x PROVEN (node mirror sem, memo off; unstaged): minimal 4/4, certificate 16/16, partial 6/6. (1) CLOSURE BOUND: certificate.check_closure (r) : closure_check = WithinBound (n, bound) | PastBound (n, bound), bound = 2^(positions+1) with positions = Set leaves; fourth_from_end 16 <= 64, zero_runs 4 <= 32, ends_in_zero 2 <= 16, (0|1)* & ~ends_in_zero 2 <= 64. (2) ANTIMIROV RECONSTRUCTION LAW: partial.reconstruction_by (split) (r) : reconstruction = Reconstructs classes | SplitsDiffer (class low, word): for every class, the union of the split's terms and the Brzozowski derivative answer alike on every word of length <= 4, judged by language.spi's oracle (no derivatives, no partials). partials reconstructs on fourth_from_end, zero_runs, ends_in_zero (4 classes each); a forged split that drops its first term is caught. (3) TERNARY: minimal.tri_cyclic_nonminimal = (a|aa)*(b|c) has 4 derivative states (r0, (e|a).r0, r0|(e|a).r0, e) and 2 minimal ones, matching the hand derivation. LEFT: only the runtime injective origin assignment for Antimirov terms (each support term mapped to a distinct position). 65 -> 85.")
inl note_of_regex_closure_certificates_6 () = Note ("REGEX-CLOSURE-CERTIFICATES", 6u32, "2026-11-03T05:43Z", "main", "main 11-03 01:4x DEBT recorded: kit standards on regex src = 73 line-width findings (HEAD 42, so ~31 are from tonight's certificate/lazy/partial/syntax/minimal edits, mostly long test tuples). regex does not enforce line-width yet; rewrap tonight's lines (each file re-gated) before regex adopts the html-style standards gate.")
inl note_of_regex_closure_certificates_7 () = Note ("REGEX-CLOSURE-CERTIFICATES", 7u32, "2026-11-03T12:00Z", "main", "main 11-03 08:0x DONE. Europa gate (idle machine, pack24, memo off, one Cells run): syntax 9/9, minimal 4/4, lazy 3/3, certificate 16/16, partial 8/8, dfa 5/5 = 45/45. The last point, ANTIMIROV ORIGIN SLOTS: partial.origins (r) : origins = Injective n | Orphaned k | OutsideFragment maps every support term to a distinct position whose continuation (conts_of: Set -> tail; Seq a b -> a with tail b.tail; Alt -> both; Star a -> a with tail Star a.tail) equals the term (same_re), greedily, over the seq/alt/star/set fragment. zero_runs Injective 3, ends_in_zero Injective 2, (a|b)*abb Injective 4 (r, bb, b, e), all derived by hand first and right on the first run; a forged term no position continues is Orphaned 1; a complement is OutsideFragment. Earlier gates for the line-width rewraps (certificate/partial/syntax/minimal/lazy) are in this 45/45 too. ALL DOD POINTS MET: check_dfa (closed, distinct, total, keys distinct, normalized rows; forged rows named), the minimize block map (origins + coverage) and eager ~ minimal (check_quotient), the classes partition and Normal sets, is_canonical on every state plus the x*.x* -> x* rule, the 2^(positions+1) closure bound, the Antimirov reconstruction law plus origin slots, and ternary examples incl. tri_cyclic_nonminimal; every check returns a typed verdict, never a bool.")
inl note_of_lib_vec_fin_1 () = Note ("LIB-VEC-FIN", 1u32, "2026-11-02T11:25Z", "regex", "regex 07:4x From REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB item 2 (b) (legacy main.spi finite_length 75, finite_symbol_vector 78, finite_symbol_index 84; probes existential_helper_control, recursive_indexed_definition, finite_vector_rank become its unit tests) and tibia's request (ML-LABS n11, TIBIA-AGENT M3 typed_network.spi: sizes as type indices, raw/planned/frozen typestate). DOD: a lib module with type-level naturals, length-indexed vectors with no fallback arm, bounded indices with a total lookup, C/Rust/WGSL(/Gleam) arms and a generic element type; compile-time only where the index grows (GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX; the FOR-D runtime index bug); its tests are the three legacy probes; the 3-line shadowing repro (memory lib-module-name-shadows-core-type) run before choosing the module name; consumers: REGEX-TYPED-CORES, TIBIA-AGENT follow-up, TYPED-TRANSFORMER-LAB. NEXT STEP: read tibia's M3 draft and the legacy vec/fin code, then the naming repro. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: GADT naturals, prototypes for dimension arithmetic, existentials only for compile-time chosen sizes.")
inl note_of_lib_vec_fin_2 () = Note ("LIB-VEC-FIN", 2u32, "2026-11-02T11:31Z", "main", "main 11-02 07:3x CORRECTION to the absorption map's constraint (REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB n1, \"items 2/20/21 must stay compile-time because of the open FOR-D bug\"): the uninhabited-payload runtime GADT bug is GADT-UNINHABITED-PAYLOAD-RUNTIME, DONE since 10-12. compiler's new standalone sample samples/gadt_uninhabited_payload_runtime PASSES today on Fsharp/C/Rust/Delphi (4 ran, 0 disagree), and gadt_rank_matrix passes on 7 backends incl. Cpp. The runtime-index blocker that is still OPEN is GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX (P0, 45%): a let rec join point over a runtime GADT whose recursion GROWS the index (term n -> term (succ n)) hangs the compiler. So a runtime Fin/Vec index is fine as long as recursion does not grow the index; length-growing recursion (cons building a vec n -> vec (succ n) at run time) stays compile-time or on i32 until that item lands. Re-check the typed-core design against this before choosing i32 rows.")
inl note_of_lib_vec_fin_3 () = Note ("LIB-VEC-FIN", 3u32, "2026-11-02T14:44Z", "regex", "regex 10:2x MINGLED with tibia's 11-02 groom: LIB-TYPE-SHAPES (type_arith over type literals, length-indexed static arrays sa n el with scan/tree-reduce/merge, tuple_list n el, C/Rust/WGSL/Lua arms, dim_of witness; from the ML-library nugget inventory) covers the length-indexed vector half of this item. ONE RECORD PER FACT: this item keeps only what LIB-TYPE-SHAPES lacks, the bounded index (finite_symbol_index / Fin n with a total lookup) and the three legacy probes as its tests (existential_helper_control, recursive_indexed_definition, finite_vector_rank), built ON LIB-TYPE-SHAPES' naturals. Deps now LIB-TYPE-SHAPES. The naming repro (memory lib-module-name-shadows-core-type) is shared.")
inl note_of_lib_vec_fin_4 () = Note ("LIB-VEC-FIN", 4u32, "2026-11-04T11:48Z", "main", "11-04 08:3x main DRAFT (drafts store spiral\\LIB-VEC-FIN\\fin_vector.spi, a new lib module; not landed). Peano naturals nat_zero/nat_succ (phantom nominals, xsd_certificate style), vector n el (VectorEnd | VectorCons), fin n (FinFirst at nat_succ n | FinNext), and item : fin n -> vector n el -> el as a TOTAL two-arm match (fin nat_zero is uninhabited, so no fallback; legacy finite_symbol_vector_lookup). Also rank, fin_value, mapped (index-preserving recursion = recursive_indexed_definition), to_list, and the existential some_vector el = SomeVector (\\? n. vector n el) with of_list (the index GROWS at run time, so it also regression-guards GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX), some_rank and some_list = existential_helper_control and finite_vector_rank. 4 tests on c/rust/lua. Names checked against lib, no collisions (memory lib-module-name-shadows-core-type). Bridge to sized_array (fin n -> index into sized n el) is the next step once green. Gate PENDING on the node.")
inl note_of_lib_vec_fin_5 () = Note ("LIB-VEC-FIN", 5u32, "2026-11-04T11:57Z", "main", "11-04 09:2x main NODE (spiral 98e51d32, digest C80CFA10, draft placed in the mirror's lib/spiral and removed after): fin_vector.spi notebook gate 4/4 passed, 0 failed. Covered: the total two-arm lookup through all three indices; rank and fin_value; index-preserving mapped; the existential of_list (growing index at run time, no compiler hang) with some_rank/some_list round-tripping a 4-list and the empty list. FINDING: the planned bridge to sized_array does not type as-is. sized n el is indexed by TYPE LITERALS (sized 3) and fin n by Peano nominals (nat_succ ...), so fin can index sized only through a type-level literal <-> Peano conversion. Either (a) fin_vector grows a literal-indexed fin (FinLit n carrying an i32 checked once at construction against type_lit_to_lit n), or (b) type_arith gains a to_peano. (a) is smaller; it can follow the land. NEXT: land fin_vector.spi through lib_land_window (new file, no consumers).")
inl note_of_lib_vec_fin_6 () = Note ("LIB-VEC-FIN", 6u32, "2026-11-04T12:26Z", "main", "11-04 08:2x main LANDED (box, lib_land_window two-step): lib/spiral/fin_vector.spi 0AA287AF4004 is IN LIB, unstaged; closed green, undo 20261104-081754. Node proof: document_test 22, type_probe pass, consumer compiles. Box: lib had moved (digest 45EB077C vs the proof's C62D5C26), so signatures, consumer, type_probe (4 tests typed, 0 errors) and respell drift reran on the box, with document_test taken from the proof. NEXT (drafted): sized_array's literal-indexed bounded n (bounded_of checked once, at total), gate PENDING on the node.")
inl note_of_lib_vec_fin_7 () = Note ("LIB-VEC-FIN", 7u32, "2026-11-04T13:09Z", "main", "11-04 09:0x main LANDED #2 (box, two-step, unstaged): lib/spiral/sized_array.spi F9B2C0B3ADC4 (base BA3E5993) gains bounded n = i32, the literal-indexed bounded index: bounded_of checks once against type_lit_to_lit n and returns option, then at : bounded n -> sized n el -> el reads with NO check (bounded_value exposes it). Test: both ends in range, past-the-end and negative refused (c/rust/lua). Node proof: 14/14 notebook, document_test 22, type_probe 13 typed; box: fast checks on the moved lib, first attempt refused for a live kit notebook reader (guard), retry landed. DoD status: Peano naturals + length-indexed vector + total fin lookup + existential + three legacy probes (fin_vector) DONE; literal-indexed bounded index (sized_array) DONE; generic element type DONE; arms C/Rust/Lua DONE. LEFT: a WGSL arm for at (sized_array's gpu test pattern).")
inl note_of_lib_vec_fin_8 () = Note ("LIB-VEC-FIN", 8u32, "2026-11-04T14:43Z", "main", "11-04 10:4x main LANDED #3: sized_array.spi 878BA9B92082 adds a ///> wgsl test (a_bounded_index_reads_on_the_gpu: bounded_of + at on the GPU backend). Node notebook 15/15 (a first run showed 4 unrelated reds from main's own mirror sync mid-run; the clean rerun was 15/15), node proof document_test 22 and type_probe 14 typed, box copy-only (exact lib digest). DoD MET: Peano naturals, length-indexed vectors with no fallback arm, bounded indices with a total lookup, C/Rust/Lua/WGSL arms, generic element type, the three legacy probes as tests. Item closes.")
inl note_of_regex_typed_cores_1 () = Note ("REGEX-TYPED-CORES", 1u32, "2026-11-02T11:25Z", "regex", "regex 07:4x From REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB items 20, 21 and negatives truncated_canonical_vector, indexed_row_length, finite_index_out_of_range, inventory_length_mix, indexed_dfa_quotient_coverage_count, indexed_dfa_representative_origin_count (legacy indexed_dfa_state_cardinality/main.spi state vector 4, coverage 188, origins 248, acceptance vector 402, target matrix 415). DOD: typed.spi builds, for a static regex, a compiled core whose rows and targets are length/Fin indexed (compile time), replayed against the runtime engines; runtime cores stay on i32 state until the FOR-D GADT runtime-index bug is fixed; the negatives live in the REGEX-AUTOMATON-TYPESTATE negative/ set and fail for the right reason. DEPENDS ON LIB-VEC-FIN. NEXT STEP: after LIB-VEC-FIN, port the indexed core for (0|1)*1(0|1){3}. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: GADT-indexed vectors, compile-time only.")
inl note_of_regex_typed_cores_2 () = Note ("REGEX-TYPED-CORES", 2u32, "2026-11-02T11:31Z", "main", "main 11-02 07:3x CORRECTION to the absorption map's constraint (REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB n1, \"items 2/20/21 must stay compile-time because of the open FOR-D bug\"): the uninhabited-payload runtime GADT bug is GADT-UNINHABITED-PAYLOAD-RUNTIME, DONE since 10-12. compiler's new standalone sample samples/gadt_uninhabited_payload_runtime PASSES today on Fsharp/C/Rust/Delphi (4 ran, 0 disagree), and gadt_rank_matrix passes on 7 backends incl. Cpp. The runtime-index blocker that is still OPEN is GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX (P0, 45%): a let rec join point over a runtime GADT whose recursion GROWS the index (term n -> term (succ n)) hangs the compiler. So a runtime Fin/Vec index is fine as long as recursion does not grow the index; length-growing recursion (cons building a vec n -> vec (succ n) at run time) stays compile-time or on i32 until that item lands. Re-check the typed-core design against this before choosing i32 rows.")
inl note_of_regex_typed_cores_3 () = Note ("REGEX-TYPED-CORES", 3u32, "2026-11-04T13:59Z", "main", "11-04 10:0x main IMPLEMENTED (unstaged, regex src/typed.spi, last module; uses lib fin_vector landed today): the static pattern (0|1)*1(0|1){3} as a COMPILE-TIME-CHECKED core, 16 states = the last four bits read: row s accepts iff s >= 8, and on bit b goes to (2s+b) mod 16. Types: n1..n16 Peano aliases, bit_row = verdict * fin n16 * fin n16, q0..q15 : fin n16, r0..r15, and v1..v16 each typed vector nK bit_row, so a wrong length or a target past the last state is a TYPE error. run_core (generic in n, :& with run_step) reads rows through fin_vector's total item (no bounds check, no fallback); a non-bit symbol rejects. TEST: replayed against the derivative matcher on all 127 words of length 0..6 (0 misses), plus 1000 accepted and the symbol 2 rejected. NEGATIVES (legacy truncated_canonical_vector / finite_index_out_of_range): a core one row short typed as n16, and a fin n2 target two past FinFirst, both fails \"Unification failure\". 76 cells, 0 over budget; package --check clean on europa; Cells gate PENDING.")
inl note_of_regex_typed_cores_4 () = Note ("REGEX-TYPED-CORES", 4u32, "2026-11-04T14:35Z", "main", "11-04 10:4x main EUROPA GREEN: typed.spi 3/3. The 16-state compile-time core replays the derivative matcher on all 127 words of length 0..6 with 0 misses; a_core_one_row_short_does_not_type and a_target_past_the_last_state_does_not_type both fail with \"Unification failure\" as required. DoD met for the static pattern: compiled core, rows and targets length/Fin indexed at compile time, replayed against the runtime engine, legacy negatives as fails blocks. Item closes.")
inl note_of_cic_app_scaffold_1 () = Note ("CIC-APP-SCAFFOLD", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:19Z", "regex", "regex 08:2x User 11-02 07:46: \"file backlog items to fully rewrite the lean mega sample in spiral/apps/kernel, drawing every templating lesson from the lanes plus the typefeatureset to properly start the full bottom up implementation, now we have the lean backend to test against\". SOURCE: read-only research by subagent add9e665535617d64 (11-02), copy at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\cic-sps-report.md. STATE: spiral/apps/kernel does not exist; spiral scripts/workflow.ps1 runs only apps/spiral/build.ps1 and the root build.ps1 (lines 39-47); apps/cells/spi/ci_gate.ps1 gates only lib/spiral/*.spi, so a new app needs its own build.ps1 wired into workflow.ps1. DOD: the app builds and its Cells gate prints a spiral-tests total line in CI on ubuntu and windows. First draft: restore the archived lab kernel.spi (%LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\20261030-232045, -Only 'LEAN-KERNEL-NOTEBOOKS/*': intrinsic term, existential Apply, substitute_top/beta_top context-polymorphic, gate 8/8) or record why it starts over. SHARED TYPEFEATURESET RULE: the runtime term is a closed `:| ^ term` with a de Bruijn depth as a runtime u32 (no growing phantom, so no wait on GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX); scope typestate is a two-value phantom (loose | closed, constant indices compile today); judgements are GADT-indexed certificates (cert has_type | cert defeq | cert whnf) with refusals as a reason union; prototypes for environment and reduction-strategy dispatch (forall prototype lists explicit, dispatch once at the boundary); existentials only for the static fixture/corpus registry; names are nominals, strings only at the Lean printer boundary. TEMPLATE: regex repo (src notebooks with `///- --package . --timeout N`, a `:# <file> static =` prelude, `///> rust`/`///> gleam`/`///> lean` pinned tests with one-line _assert_eq bodies, :~ join points for multi-use helpers, build.ps1 reading the spiral-tests total line, the Windows event-log crash reader, the 1000-line gate, cell budget 272) and kit's link: units for crate splits (not --import-types, deleted by IMPORT-TYPES-DELETE).")
inl note_of_cic_app_scaffold_2 () = Note ("CIC-APP-SCAFFOLD", 2u32, "2026-11-02T14:13Z", "add9e665535617d64", "add9e665535617d64 11-02 10:1x discoveries for the scaffold that weren't on file yet:\n(1) LEAN TEST BUDGET: Lean elaboration takes median 3.45 s, p90 10.2 s and max 23.5 s per row (LEAN-BACKEND n5). Set a raised `--timeout` on each notebook's FIRST `///-` line once it has `///> lean` tests. A later line is ignored (memory cells-test-block-structure).\n(2) LEAN IN CELLS: `///> lean` runs `lean --run` on leanprover/lean4:v4.35.0. The binary resolves from SPIRAL_LEAN, then that toolchain under ELAN_HOME / ~/.elan / scoop elan, then PATH (apps/cells/README.md:224-226). The box has scoop elan. CI needs an elan install step, and actions.lock must be regenerated if that step adds a `uses:`.\n(3) The old sample's Lean row in tests/matrix.psd1 (runtime_native) builds a main.lean that returns 0, because everything in it is staged at compile time. It proves nothing about CIC, so don't count it as Lean coverage.\n(4) NEGATIVES: use `:# name fails ETY-TermError \"...\" =` (TEST-EXPECT-DIAGNOSTIC). The diagnostic must be located in the test's own body, so a broken module can't make a negative pass. tibia/src/readiness.spi:81 is a working example.\n(5) DEP: I removed the dep on the parent LEAN-KERNEL-NOTEBOOKS (fill-all-task-fields trap 1).")
inl note_of_cic_app_scaffold_3 () = Note ("CIC-APP-SCAFFOLD", 3u32, "2026-11-03T20:14Z", "main", "main 11-03 16:1x DONE (unstaged, spiral): apps/kernel/src/package.spiproj (packageDir ../../../lib) + src/syntax.spi (the first CIC-SYNTAX slice: universe level = Zero | Succ | Max | Param, term = Var (de Bruijn) | Sort | Const | App | Lam | Pi | Let, level_text / sort_text (Prop, Type, Sort (l)) / term_text, and loose_range = Lean's loose bound-variable range with is_closed; 3 rust tests) + apps/kernel/build.ps1 (cloned from regex's notebook gate: requires a 'spiral-tests total' line, prints KERNEL-OK). Wired into spiral scripts/build.ps1 (CI on both OSes), together with apps/lisp/build.ps1, which wasn't in CI either. kit standards 0. EUROPA: apps/kernel/build.ps1 exit 0, spiral-tests total 3/3, KERNEL-OK. Next: CIC-SYNTAX continues (names/universe params), then CIC-SCOPE and CIC-SUBST.")
inl note_of_cic_syntax_1 () = Note ("CIC-SYNTAX", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:19Z", "regex", "regex 08:2x SOURCE: read-only research by subagent add9e665535617d64 (11-02), copy at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\cic-sps-report.md. DOD: rust + gleam + lean test targets agree (T1 target agreement: the kernel computes at RUN time, which the old sample never did; its runtime_native/main.lean is 32 lines returning 0). SHARED TYPEFEATURESET RULE: the runtime term is a closed `:| ^ term` with a de Bruijn depth as a runtime u32 (no growing phantom, so no wait on GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX); scope typestate is a two-value phantom (loose | closed, constant indices compile today); judgements are GADT-indexed certificates (cert has_type | cert defeq | cert whnf) with refusals as a reason union; prototypes for environment and reduction-strategy dispatch (forall prototype lists explicit, dispatch once at the boundary); existentials only for the static fixture/corpus registry; names are nominals, strings only at the Lean printer boundary. TEMPLATE: regex repo (src notebooks with `///- --package . --timeout N`, a `:# <file> static =` prelude, `///> rust`/`///> gleam`/`///> lean` pinned tests with one-line _assert_eq bodies, :~ join points for multi-use helpers, build.ps1 reading the spiral-tests total line, the Windows event-log crash reader, the 1000-line gate, cell budget 272) and kit's link: units for crate splits (not --import-types, deleted by IMPORT-TYPES-DELETE).")
inl note_of_cic_syntax_2 () = Note ("CIC-SYNTAX", 2u32, "2026-11-03T20:29Z", "main", "main 11-03 16:3x FIRST SLICE to spec (unstaged, spiral apps/kernel/src/syntax.spi): name nominal (:! name = string); level = Zero | Succ | Max | IMax | Param name; binder = Default | Implicit | StrictImplicit | InstImplicit (Lean-style printing (x : T) {x : T} ⦃x : T⦄ [x : T]); term = BVar | FVar | Sort | Const (name, levels) | App | Lam | Pi | Let; level_text, sort_text (Prop / Type / Sort (l)), term_text, loose_range (Lean's looseBVarRange) + is_closed, term_size, and structural equality through a prototype :? same_as with level and term instances (alpha-equivalence: binder names and info ignored, as Lean's Expr.eqv). 4 rust tests; kit standards 0 (formatter applied); europa apps/kernel/build.ps1 4/4, KERNEL-OK. LEFT: hash. Progress 0 -> 80.")
inl note_of_cic_syntax_3 () = Note ("CIC-SYNTAX", 3u32, "2026-11-04T10:24Z", "main", "11-04 06:2x main DONE by its title's DoD: name nominal, level union, term union (Sort/BVar/FVar/Const/App/Lam/Pi/Let, plus Proj for structures), binder info, structural equality through the same_as prototype, size, and now a structural HASH: term_hash/level_hash, polynomial mod 1000000007 so every backend agrees, names hashed by char codes. It ignores binder names and info exactly like same_as. Test: equal-up-to-names terms hash equal; different sorts, projection indices and anagram names differ. europa: kernel 55/55 KERNEL-OK.")
inl note_of_cic_scope_1 () = Note ("CIC-SCOPE", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:19Z", "regex", "regex 08:2x SOURCE: read-only research by subagent add9e665535617d64 (11-02), copy at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\cic-sps-report.md. DOD: round-trip laws as tests; diagnostic-expect blocks (:# name fails ETY-TermError ''msg'' =, TEST-EXPECT-DIAGNOSTIC) for instantiating a closed term with a loose one. SHARED TYPEFEATURESET RULE: the runtime term is a closed `:| ^ term` with a de Bruijn depth as a runtime u32 (no growing phantom, so no wait on GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX); scope typestate is a two-value phantom (loose | closed, constant indices compile today); judgements are GADT-indexed certificates (cert has_type | cert defeq | cert whnf) with refusals as a reason union; prototypes for environment and reduction-strategy dispatch (forall prototype lists explicit, dispatch once at the boundary); existentials only for the static fixture/corpus registry; names are nominals, strings only at the Lean printer boundary. TEMPLATE: regex repo (src notebooks with `///- --package . --timeout N`, a `:# <file> static =` prelude, `///> rust`/`///> gleam`/`///> lean` pinned tests with one-line _assert_eq bodies, :~ join points for multi-use helpers, build.ps1 reading the spiral-tests total line, the Windows event-log crash reader, the 1000-line gate, cell budget 272) and kit's link: units for crate splits (not --import-types, deleted by IMPORT-TYPES-DELETE).")
inl note_of_cic_scope_2 () = Note ("CIC-SCOPE", 2u32, "2026-11-03T20:37Z", "main", "main 11-03 16:4x FIRST SLICE (unstaged, spiral apps/kernel/src/scope.spi, registered after syntax): Lean's locally nameless operations: shift_from / lift / lower (BVar index shifting above a depth), instantiate_at / instantiate (the outer bound var becomes a value lifted to its depth, higher indices drop by one), abstract_at / abstract_fvar (a free var becomes a bound var; existing loose indices move up), open_with. Round-trip laws as rust tests: open then abstract the same fvar gives the body back and the opened term is closed; instantiate leaves closed terms alone and fills BVar 0 ('(a a)'); lower (lift t k) k = t. Europa apps/kernel/build.ps1: 7/7 (scope 3, syntax 4), KERNEL-OK; kit standards 0. LEFT: the loose|closed phantom on term so open/close are checked by type. Progress 0 -> 60.")
inl note_of_cic_scope_3 () = Note ("CIC-SCOPE", 3u32, "2026-11-03T22:59Z", "main", "18:40 main: closed-term nominal landed. scope.spi ':! closed = term'; as_closed (option, only when loose_range = 0) is the sole constructor; typing.infer_top takes closed, so top-level inference cannot see a loose BVar by construction. Chose a nominal over a full phantom index on term: the index would ripple through all 8 modules for the same guarantee at the one boundary that needs it. Europa pack30: kernel 30/30 KERNEL-OK, kit standards 0 findings.")
inl note_of_cic_scope_4 () = Note ("CIC-SCOPE", 4u32, "2026-11-04T10:40Z", "main", "11-04 06:5x main DONE by its title's DoD: locally nameless open/close/instantiate/abstract, lift/lower, the closed nominal as the loose|closed boundary (only as_closed builds it; infer_top takes it), and round-trip laws as tests. New: every term shape round-trips through open+abstract and lift+lower, including Let and the new Proj former (a 4-term family). europa: kernel 56/56 KERNEL-OK.")
inl note_of_cic_subst_1 () = Note ("CIC-SUBST", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:19Z", "regex", "regex 08:2x SOURCE: read-only research by subagent add9e665535617d64 (11-02), copy at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\cic-sps-report.md. DOD: the legacy renaming/lifting/two-cell-swap/one-binder-substitution laws as test blocks on rust, gleam, lean. SHARED TYPEFEATURESET RULE: the runtime term is a closed `:| ^ term` with a de Bruijn depth as a runtime u32 (no growing phantom, so no wait on GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX); scope typestate is a two-value phantom (loose | closed, constant indices compile today); judgements are GADT-indexed certificates (cert has_type | cert defeq | cert whnf) with refusals as a reason union; prototypes for environment and reduction-strategy dispatch (forall prototype lists explicit, dispatch once at the boundary); existentials only for the static fixture/corpus registry; names are nominals, strings only at the Lean printer boundary. TEMPLATE: regex repo (src notebooks with `///- --package . --timeout N`, a `:# <file> static =` prelude, `///> rust`/`///> gleam`/`///> lean` pinned tests with one-line _assert_eq bodies, :~ join points for multi-use helpers, build.ps1 reading the spiral-tests total line, the Windows event-log crash reader, the 1000-line gate, cell budget 272) and kit's link: units for crate splits (not --import-types, deleted by IMPORT-TYPES-DELETE).")
inl note_of_cic_subst_2 () = Note ("CIC-SUBST", 2u32, "2026-11-03T21:33Z", "main", "main 11-03 17:3x FIRST SLICE (unstaged, spiral apps/kernel/src/subst.spi, registered after scope): the renaming/lifting laws as tests, each checked over a 7-term family (bound vars inside and outside binders, free vars, App, Lam, nested implicit Pi, Let) rather than one example: (1) identity: instantiate (lift t 1) v = t; (2) composition: lift (lift t 2) 3 = lift t 5; (3) commutation: lift (t[0:=v]) 1 = (shift_from t 1 1)[0 := lift v 1]. All hold (alpha-equality via same_as). Europa apps/kernel/build.ps1 25/25 over 8 modules, KERNEL-OK; kit standards 0. LEFT: associativity of substitution composition and the legacy sample's exact law set. Progress 0 -> 50.")
inl note_of_cic_subst_3 () = Note ("CIC-SUBST", 3u32, "2026-11-04T01:34Z", "main", "21:3x main: the substitution lemma as a law test over the 7-term family: instantiate (instantiate t u) v == instantiate (instantiate_at t 1 v) (instantiate u v), with u and v both carrying loose variables (u = (u #0), v = (w #1)), so it exercises instantiate_at's lift-by-depth and the outer instantiate's lowering. Passes; europa kernel 47/47.")
inl note_of_cic_subst_4 () = Note ("CIC-SUBST", 4u32, "2026-11-06T08:21Z", "main", "main 11-06 04:2x groom (untouched >12 h): PAUSED by the WIP cap; last touched 11-04 (substitution lemma law test, kernel 47/47 on europa). Resume = the next lemma in the item plan.")
inl note_of_cic_subst_5 () = Note ("CIC-SUBST", 5u32, "2026-11-06T11:39Z", "main", "main 11-06 08:4x re-decided (run start, user: pull Planned/0% items): stays Paused. Reason: kernel 47/47 with the substitution lemma; the kernel lane's current work is CIC-NOCONFUSION-BLOWUP. Resume when that closes, from the next lemma in the item plan.")
inl note_of_cic_subst_6 () = Note ("CIC-SUBST", 6u32, "2026-11-06T18:53Z", "main", "main 11-06 15:0x RESUMED (its condition fired: CIC-NOCONFUSION-BLOWUP is Done). Added the two missing laws from the title to spiral/apps/kernel/src/subst.spi (unstaged): lifting_by_zero_is_the_identity (lift t 0 == t over the 7-term family) and shifts_compose_by_adding_their_amounts_at_every_cutoff (shift_from (shift_from t c 2) c 3 == shift_from t c 5 for c = 0, 1, 2; the old test covered only cutoff 0 via lift). proof: europa Cells gate on the subst notebook, 6 discovered, 6 executed, 6 passed, 0 failed (europa pack57; syntax/scope/package.spiproj byte-equal to the box; europa's subst.spi restored after). A first run failed 6/6 on 'zig failed (exit 134) DWARF NoSpaceLeft' because europa's /tmp tmpfs was 100% full; it passed after main archived 692 MB of stale /tmp items. Laws now covered: identity, composition at every cutoff, and associativity (the substitution lemma). Next step: commutation of instantiate with shift at a deeper cutoff (shift_from (instantiate_at t d v) c k vs instantiate_at (shift_from t (c+1) k) d (shift_from v c k) for c >= d), then the full kernel build on a synced mirror. DoD: the substitution/renaming law family green in the full kernel gate.")
inl note_of_cic_subst_7 () = Note ("CIC-SUBST", 7u32, "2026-11-06T18:58Z", "main", "main 11-06 15:1x ADDED instantiation_commutes_with_shifting_at_or_above_its_depth to subst.spi (unstaged). The law, for c >= d: shift_from (instantiate_at t d v) c k == instantiate_at (shift_from t (c+1) k) d (shift_from v (c-d) k). It is derived by cases (i<d, i=d, i>d; binders raise d and c together), and the i=d case forces the c-d cutoff on v, because instantiate_at lifts v by d. It is tested at (d,c) = (0,0), (0,2), (1,1), (1,3) with v = App (App (w, #0), #2). proof: europa subst notebook, 8 discovered, 7 passed, and the 1 failure was the deliberate mutant_naive_value_cutoff (v shifted at c instead of c-d), which was not kept in the box file. So the law passes AND distinguishes the right cutoff. A first try with v = App (w, #1) let the mutant pass too (#1 shifts alike at cutoffs 0 and 1): a law test needs a value with loose indices between the competing cutoffs. Next step: the full kernel build on a synced mirror (europa's checkout is stale at faf422c9), then close at the DoD.")
inl note_of_cic_subst_8 () = Note ("CIC-SUBST", 8u32, "2026-11-06T19:35Z", "main", "main 11-06 15:3x FULL KERNEL GATE on europa (box tree synced, head d86fd005 digest 0E5C547436ED90FA; pack57; MemoryMax=1400M): 78 discovered, 67 passed, 11 failed. subst.spi passed every test, including the 3 new laws. The 11 failures are VOID, not red: inductive 1, reduce 4, typing 1 and universes 1 died on System.OutOfMemoryException in the compiler under the cap, and scope 4 ran in the same starved window. fiscal's rustc (690 MB) was running beside it, and MemAvailable fell to 1581 MB. A per-file rerun was stopped to leave europa to fiscal. None of those files changed (byte-equal to the box). Next step: rerun scope/inductive/reduce/typing/universes one notebook at a time when europa has MemAvailable >= 2000 MB, or run the full gate on the node once TRAIN34 ends.")
inl note_of_cic_subst_9 () = Note ("CIC-SUBST", 9u32, "2026-11-06T20:10Z", "main", "main 11-06 16:1x DONE. proof: the kernel is 78/78 on europa (box tree synced at d86fd005 / digest 0E5C547436ED90FA, pack57, MemoryMax=1400M). The full gate passed 33 tests in conversion, env, export, lean, nested, oracle, subst and syntax. Its 5 OOM-VOID files, rerun one notebook at a time with MemAvailable 2168 MB and no other job, gave scope 5/5, inductive 20/20, reduce 4/4, typing 10/10 and universes 6/6, with 0 OutOfMemory. subst.spi now holds the whole law family: instantiate after lift is the identity; lifting by zero is the identity; shifts compose at every cutoff; lifts compose; substitution commutes with lifting; instantiation commutes with shifting at or above its depth (proven discriminating with a mutant); and the substitution lemma. Unstaged in spiral/apps/kernel/src/subst.spi. Note for the kernel gate: the 13-notebook gate needs more than 1.4 GB of compiler heap on Linux, so run it per file on europa, or whole on the node.")
inl note_of_cic_reduce_1 () = Note ("CIC-REDUCE", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:19Z", "regex", "regex 08:2x SOURCE: read-only research by subagent add9e665535617d64 (11-02), copy at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\cic-sps-report.md. DOD: WHNF tests incl. let/delta/spine from the legacy sample; fuel exhaustion is a Rejected reason, never a hang. BEND2-IN-SPIRAL shares this layer (its archived nbe.spi: levels NbE + Pi/Typ + conversion). SHARED TYPEFEATURESET RULE: the runtime term is a closed `:| ^ term` with a de Bruijn depth as a runtime u32 (no growing phantom, so no wait on GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX); scope typestate is a two-value phantom (loose | closed, constant indices compile today); judgements are GADT-indexed certificates (cert has_type | cert defeq | cert whnf) with refusals as a reason union; prototypes for environment and reduction-strategy dispatch (forall prototype lists explicit, dispatch once at the boundary); existentials only for the static fixture/corpus registry; names are nominals, strings only at the Lean printer boundary. TEMPLATE: regex repo (src notebooks with `///- --package . --timeout N`, a `:# <file> static =` prelude, `///> rust`/`///> gleam`/`///> lean` pinned tests with one-line _assert_eq bodies, :~ join points for multi-use helpers, build.ps1 reading the spiral-tests total line, the Windows event-log crash reader, the 1000-line gate, cell budget 272) and kit's link: units for crate splits (not --import-types, deleted by IMPORT-TYPES-DELETE).")
inl note_of_cic_reduce_2 () = Note ("CIC-REDUCE", 2u32, "2026-11-03T20:53Z", "main", "main 11-03 17:0x FIRST SLICE (unstaged, spiral apps/kernel/src/reduce.spi, registered after universes): weak-head normalization by spine (head + argument list) with beta (a Lam head consumes the first argument through scope's instantiate) and zeta (a Let head unfolds its value), FUEL AS A TYPED REFUSAL (whnf_result = Whnf (term, trace) | OutOfFuel (term, trace); fuel is spent per step, so a term already in WHNF needs none) and a STEP TRACE (step = Beta | Zeta). Tests: (fun x => x) a -> Whnf (a, [Beta]); let f := id; f b -> b in 2 steps (zeta then beta); omega = (fun x => x x)(fun x => x x) -> 'out of fuel after 5' instead of looping. Europa apps/kernel/build.ps1 13/13 (syntax 4, scope 3, universes 3, reduce 3), KERNEL-OK; formatter applied, kit standards 0. LEFT: delta (needs the constants environment), iota (inductives). Progress 0 -> 35.")
inl note_of_cic_reduce_3 () = Note ("CIC-REDUCE", 3u32, "2026-11-03T21:27Z", "main", "main 11-03 17:2x DELTA ADDED: new apps/kernel/src/env.spi (decl = Axiom (name, type) | Def (name, type, value); find_decl, unfold) and an env parameter threaded through whnf; a Const head with a Def unfolds (step Delta name in the trace), an axiom stays in WHNF. Test: with id := fun x => x, 'id a' -> Whnf (a, [Delta id; Beta]). Universe-parameter instantiation of constants is not done yet (levels on Const are ignored). Europa kernel 22/22 over 7 modules under pack28. Progress 35 -> 55; LEFT: iota (inductives), level instantiation.")
inl note_of_cic_reduce_4 () = Note ("CIC-REDUCE", 4u32, "2026-11-04T10:11Z", "main", "11-04 06:1x main DONE by its title's DoD: WHNF with beta, delta (with universe-level instantiation, unfold_at), zeta, and iota through generated recursors (rule RHS terms, one Iota step); plus quotient lift/ind and structure projection steps (Project); fuel is a typed result (OutOfFuel); every step is traced. Lean oracle 188/188 exercises iota, quotient and projection reduction. Box kernel 54/54.")
inl note_of_cic_reduce_5 () = Note ("CIC-REDUCE", 5u32, "2026-11-04T15:03Z", "main", "11-04 11:0x main K-LIKE REDUCTION (Lean's toCtorWhenK; unstaged reduce.spi, package --check clean on a cloud scratch copy). When iota finds a major that is not a constructor and the recursor is K-like (family in Prop: k_family checks its type ends in Sort 0; exactly one rule: single_rule; the constructor has zero fields after the parameters: k_ctor), the major is replaced by the constructor applied to the recursor's parameters. That is sound only when the recursor's index arguments equal the constructor's indices under those parameters (Lean's check), done here as indices_agree: same_as, else both sides to whnf then same_as (sound, incomplete vs Lean's full defeq). Tests: kernel a_proof_of_an_equation_reduces_by_k_only_at_matching_indices (Eq.rec on a free h reduces at index zero, stays stuck at index one); oracle k_like_corpus probe (transport along an arbitrary h : K.Eq Type K.T K.T), Lean comparison pending. Europa kernel gate PENDING (the run may have seen a mixed tree after main's mid-run sync; a red there gets rerun before it is trusted).")
inl note_of_cic_reduce_6 () = Note ("CIC-REDUCE", 6u32, "2026-11-04T15:14Z", "main", "11-04 11:1x main K-LIKE REDUCTION AGREES WITH LEAN: both oracle probes (direct index, and an index equal only after delta-unfolding K.id, which needs the whnf step in indices_agree) are accepted by the kernel and by Lean; box oracle 225/225. The europa kernel gate earlier showed 63/64 with only the oracle pin list red (it predated the flipped K pin and saw main's mid-run sync). The kernel unit test for K (reduces at matching index, stuck at index one) still needs a clean inductive.spi run.")
inl note_of_cic_reduce_7 () = Note ("CIC-REDUCE", 7u32, "2026-11-04T15:35Z", "main", "11-04 11:3x main CLEAN EUROPA KERNEL GATE: KERNEL-OK 65/65 (spiral 98e51d32 + unstaged, synced 11:15 with no sync during the run, compiler pack36 on europa). Includes a_proof_of_an_equation_reduces_by_k_only_at_matching_indices, nested inductives, universe equivalence and the oracle pins (K probes accepted). K-like reduction is DONE: kernel test + Lean agreement (box oracle 225/225).")
inl note_of_cic_universes_1 () = Note ("CIC-UNIVERSES", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:19Z", "regex", "regex 08:2x SOURCE: read-only research by subagent add9e665535617d64 (11-02), copy at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\cic-sps-report.md. DOD: level law tests and Lean agreement on a level corpus. SHARED TYPEFEATURESET RULE: the runtime term is a closed `:| ^ term` with a de Bruijn depth as a runtime u32 (no growing phantom, so no wait on GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX); scope typestate is a two-value phantom (loose | closed, constant indices compile today); judgements are GADT-indexed certificates (cert has_type | cert defeq | cert whnf) with refusals as a reason union; prototypes for environment and reduction-strategy dispatch (forall prototype lists explicit, dispatch once at the boundary); existentials only for the static fixture/corpus registry; names are nominals, strings only at the Lean printer boundary. TEMPLATE: regex repo (src notebooks with `///- --package . --timeout N`, a `:# <file> static =` prelude, `///> rust`/`///> gleam`/`///> lean` pinned tests with one-line _assert_eq bodies, :~ join points for multi-use helpers, build.ps1 reading the spiral-tests total line, the Windows event-log crash reader, the 1000-line gate, cell budget 272) and kit's link: units for crate splits (not --import-types, deleted by IMPORT-TYPES-DELETE).")
inl note_of_cic_universes_2 () = Note ("CIC-UNIVERSES", 2u32, "2026-11-03T20:46Z", "main", "main 11-03 16:5x FIRST SLICE (unstaged, spiral apps/kernel/src/universes.spi, registered after scope): the semantic definition of levels: level_value under an assignment of parameters to naturals, with imax a b = 0 when b = 0 (Prop impredicativity); params_into; leq_upto / eq_upto check the relation over EVERY assignment of the levels' parameters up to a bound (a :& every_assignment/every_value group). Named 'upto' on purpose: it refutes by search but is not the complete decision procedure; Lean's normalization-based leq comes next and must agree with it on these tests. pi_level domain codomain = imax. Tests: a Pi into Prop lives in Prop for every domain (imax u 0 = 0), imax u 1 = max u 1; u <= max u v, not u+1 <= u, max u (u+1) = u+1; closed values with imax dropping to 0. Europa apps/kernel/build.ps1 10/10 (syntax 4, scope 3, universes 3), KERNEL-OK; formatter applied, kit standards 0. Progress 0 -> 40.")
inl note_of_cic_universes_3 () = Note ("CIC-UNIVERSES", 3u32, "2026-11-03T21:53Z", "main", "main 11-03 17:5x DECISION PROCEDURE for the imax-free fragment: atoms_of normalizes a level to atoms (base = 0 or a parameter, plus an offset); leq_decide a b : option bool says a <= b iff every atom of a is dominated by an atom of b (same parameter with offset >= k, or a constant atom against any atom with offset >= k, since parameters are >= 0), and returns None when either side has imax (outside the complete fragment). TEST: on a 15-level family (grown from 0, 1, u, v, max u 1 by succ and max _ v) the decision agrees with the semantic leq_upto on all 225 ordered pairs. Europa kernel 26/26 over 8 modules under pack29. LEFT: imax normalization (Lean's case split on the imax's right side), then eq via mutual leq. Progress 40 -> 60.")
inl note_of_cic_universes_4 () = Note ("CIC-UNIVERSES", 4u32, "2026-11-03T22:12Z", "main", "main 11-03 18:1x IMAX DECIDED: simplify (imax a 0 = 0; imax a (succ _) = max; imax distributes over a max or a nested imax on its right), imax_param finds an imax whose right side is a bare parameter, and leq_full splits that parameter p into p := 0 and p := p+1 (sound and complete: p ranges over {0} and {q+1}); each case simplifies the imax away, then the imax-free decision applies. TEST: on a 15-level family with imax (imax u v, imax v u, imax u 0, imax (u+1) (max u v), u, grown by succ and max _ v) leq_full agrees with the semantic leq_upto on all 225 ordered pairs. Europa kernel 27/27 over 8 modules. LEFT: eq via mutual leq in conversion (sorts currently use eq_upto), level instantiation of constants. Progress 60 -> 80.")
inl note_of_cic_universes_5 () = Note ("CIC-UNIVERSES", 5u32, "2026-11-04T13:40Z", "main", "11-04 09:4x main GAP FOUND AND FIXED (unstaged, conversion.spi, gate PENDING): Sort comparison already used leq_full both ways, but constants compared their universe arguments syntactically (same_constant = same_as), so @c.{max u v} and @c.{max v u} were DIFFERENT to the kernel while Lean's is_def_eq treats equivalent level arguments as equal. Now same_constant = same name and equivalent_levels (leq_full both ways per argument), used by lazy_delta's same-head path and by compare_whnf's fallback arm. Test a_constant_matches_itself_at_equivalent_universe_levels: max u v ~ max v u, imax u (v+1) ~ max u (v+1), and u vs v stays different.")
inl note_of_cic_universes_6 () = Note ("CIC-UNIVERSES", 6u32, "2026-11-04T14:18Z", "main", "11-04 10:2x main EUROPA kernel gate (spiral 98e51d32 + unstaged): 63/64; a_constant_matches_itself_at_equivalent_universe_levels PASSED (max u v ~ max v u, imax u (v+1) ~ max u (v+1), u vs v different), and every older conversion/typing test still passes with constants now compared up to level equivalence. The one red is nested.spi's, not this. Progress 80 -> 95; left: a Lean oracle entry once the oracle can state universe-polymorphic examples.")
inl note_of_cic_universes_7 () = Note ("CIC-UNIVERSES", 7u32, "2026-11-04T14:43Z", "main", "11-04 10:5x main ORACLE ENTRIES ADDED (unstaged oracle.spi, package --check clean on europa): a Poly entry (universe params + type + value, printed as one line \"section universe u v example : T := v end\" so each entry scopes its own universes), and universe_corpus: axioms K.Pp.{a} : Type and K.pp.{a} : K.Pp.{a}, then K.pp.{max v u} checked against K.Pp.{max u v} (equivalent levels: kernel and Lean should both accept) and K.pp.{v} against K.Pp.{u} (both refuse). Pins !+ !+ !+ !-. Lean comparison PENDING on the node.")
inl note_of_cic_universes_8 () = Note ("CIC-UNIVERSES", 8u32, "2026-11-04T15:14Z", "main", "11-04 11:1x main LEAN AGREES on the universe entries (box oracle 225/225): K.pp.{max v u} : K.Pp.{max u v} accepted by both, K.pp.{v} : K.Pp.{u} refused by both. Item at 100: level normalization, leq/eq with imax, Prop impredicativity, and conversion up to level equivalence, Lean-checked.")
inl note_of_cic_conversion_1 () = Note ("CIC-CONVERSION", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:19Z", "regex", "regex 08:2x SOURCE: read-only research by subagent add9e665535617d64 (11-02), copy at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\cic-sps-report.md. DOD: defeq certificate checked independently; legacy structural defeq + conversion-constraint solver behaviours as tests. SHARED TYPEFEATURESET RULE: the runtime term is a closed `:| ^ term` with a de Bruijn depth as a runtime u32 (no growing phantom, so no wait on GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX); scope typestate is a two-value phantom (loose | closed, constant indices compile today); judgements are GADT-indexed certificates (cert has_type | cert defeq | cert whnf) with refusals as a reason union; prototypes for environment and reduction-strategy dispatch (forall prototype lists explicit, dispatch once at the boundary); existentials only for the static fixture/corpus registry; names are nominals, strings only at the Lean printer boundary. TEMPLATE: regex repo (src notebooks with `///- --package . --timeout N`, a `:# <file> static =` prelude, `///> rust`/`///> gleam`/`///> lean` pinned tests with one-line _assert_eq bodies, :~ join points for multi-use helpers, build.ps1 reading the spiral-tests total line, the Windows event-log crash reader, the 1000-line gate, cell budget 272) and kit's link: units for crate splits (not --import-types, deleted by IMPORT-TYPES-DELETE).")
inl note_of_cic_conversion_2 () = Note ("CIC-CONVERSION", 2u32, "2026-11-03T21:02Z", "main", "main 11-03 17:1x FIRST SLICE (unstaged, spiral apps/kernel/src/conversion.spi, registered after reduce): definitional equality as a TYPED VERDICT defeq = Same (list step) | Different string | NoFuel, where Same carries the reduction steps used as its certificate. Both sides go to WHNF (reduce), then compare_whnf recurses structurally (Lam/Pi: domain then body; App: head then argument, through a lazy 'both'), sorts compare through universes' eq_upto, and ETA in both orientations (fun x => f x ~ f, a Lam against a non-Lam via App (lift other 1, BVar 0)). Tests: (fun x => x) a ~ a is Same [Beta]; eta equal both ways; Prop vs Type is 'different: Prop vs Type'; omega vs f reports 'no fuel'. Europa apps/kernel/build.ps1 16/16 over 5 modules, KERNEL-OK; formatter applied, kit standards 0. LEFT: lazy delta (needs the constants environment), proof irrelevance, the certificate checker. Progress 0 -> 35.")
inl note_of_cic_conversion_3 () = Note ("CIC-CONVERSION", 3u32, "2026-11-03T22:19Z", "main", "main 11-03 18:2x sorts now compare with the COMPLETE level decision (leq_full both ways, CIC-UNIVERSES n4), replacing the bounded eq_upto, so Sort u ~ Sort v is decided for all assignments, imax included. Europa kernel 27/27. Progress 35 -> 40.")
inl note_of_cic_conversion_4 () = Note ("CIC-CONVERSION", 4u32, "2026-11-04T00:53Z", "main", "20:5x main: lazy delta. defeq_with first tries syntactic equality (same_as -> Same []), then, when both sides share a constant head with equal levels, compares the arguments pairwise (args_defeq) before unfolding anything; only on disagreement does it whnf both sides (unfold_both). id (identity a) vs id a = Same [Beta] (was Delta id; Beta; Beta; Delta id; Beta). Sound by congruence, complete because disagreement falls back to unfolding. Europa kernel 44/44.")
inl note_of_cic_conversion_5 () = Note ("CIC-CONVERSION", 5u32, "2026-11-04T05:43Z", "main", "11-04 01:4x main: DEFINITIONAL PROOF IRRELEVANCE (Lean's is_def_eq_proof_irrel), placed like Lean's: after the syntactic check, before lazy delta. conversion.spi gains constant_type, a closed type inference for Const and App spines over the env (instantiate_levels on the declared type, whnf the function type to a Pi, instantiate the codomain), plus is_proposition (the type's type whnfs to Sort 0) and proof_type. Two terms whose types are the same proposition are Same. Test: p1, p2 : P : Prop compare 'same in 0'; q1, q2 : T : Type stay 'different: q1 vs q2'. The oracle corpus gains conversion entries (eta through Eq, proof irrelevance through Eq.refl, distinct Type inhabitants refused). europa kernel 50/50 KERNEL-OK across 11 modules. The Lean side of the new entries runs on the node after the pack33 swap.")
inl note_of_cic_conversion_6 () = Note ("CIC-CONVERSION", 6u32, "2026-11-04T08:44Z", "main", "11-04 04:3x main: Lean confirms the conversion entries (oracle 146/146): eta through Eq and definitional proof irrelevance (two proofs of one Prop equal), while two distinct Type inhabitants stay unequal.")
inl note_of_cic_conversion_7 () = Note ("CIC-CONVERSION", 7u32, "2026-11-04T10:12Z", "main", "11-04 06:1x main: lazy delta, function eta, struct eta and definitional proof irrelevance are in; Lean agrees on every conversion entry (188/188). Left for the title's 'typed defeq certificate': Same carries the step trace today, not a checkable certificate term.")
inl note_of_cic_conversion_8 () = Note ("CIC-CONVERSION", 8u32, "2026-11-04T15:23Z", "main", "11-04 11:2x main GAP vs Lean (found while planning unit-like eta): conversion has NO LOCAL CONTEXT. defeq_with env a b fuel infers types only through constant_type (Const/App/Sort), so a free variable's type is unknown. Consequences: (1) definitional proof irrelevance works for closed proofs (constants) but NOT for hypotheses, so (p q : P) -> p = q is refused while Lean accepts it; (2) Lean's unit-like eta (any two values of a one-constructor, zero-field type are defeq, e.g. x y : PUnit) cannot be expressed at all. PLAN: thread the typing context (list (string * term)) through defeq_with and its group (callers: typing's check/infer, inductive's positivity/eliminates_large uses), extend constant_type with an FVar arm via lookup, then add the unit-like rule beside proofs_or_delta. Oracle probes to add with it: (p q : P) -> K.Eq p q, and (x y : K.Unit) -> K.Eq x y (Lean accepts both). Est. 2 h with gates. Not started.")
inl note_of_cic_conversion_9 () = Note ("CIC-CONVERSION", 9u32, "2026-11-04T15:28Z", "main", "11-04 11:3x main IMPLEMENTED (unstaged, package --check clean on a cloud scratch copy), more simply than the threading plan in n8: typing's check now calls defeq_with on context_env ctx env, which projects the local context into the environment as axioms named fvar:<name> (the colon cannot collide with a constant), and constant_type gained an FVar arm that reads them. Every conversion function keeps its signature. Effects: (1) proof irrelevance now covers hypotheses; (2) a new unit_or_delta step: two values whose types are the same one-constructor, zero-field, index-free family (unit_like/unit_family, reusing reduce's single_rule/axiom_of/through_params/is_pi) are equal after their types are. Tests: kernel two_hypotheses_proving_one_proposition_are_definitionally_equal; oracle probes forall (P : Prop) (p q : P), K.Eq p q, and forall (x y : K.Unit), K.Eq x y (Lean accepts both). Box Lean run and europa kernel gate PENDING. Limitation kept: comparisons UNDER binders inside conversion still see bound variables, not fvars.")
inl note_of_cic_conversion_10 () = Note ("CIC-CONVERSION", 10u32, "2026-11-04T15:55Z", "main", "11-04 11:5x main EUROPA KERNEL GATE KERNEL-OK 66/66 (sync 11:3x included context_env + unit_or_delta + the new bodies_defeq: binder bodies of Lam/Pi are now compared after opening both with one fresh fvar axiom typed by the domain, so proof irrelevance and unit eta also hold under binders). First box oracle with the probes was 230/234: all 4 reds were kernel=False lean=True on the new probes, which compare under the binders of the example; that motivated bodies_defeq. Box oracle rerun PENDING. Scratch copy also has CIC-LITERALS work (NatLit), package --check clean on europa; not yet in the live tree.")
inl note_of_cic_conversion_11 () = Note ("CIC-CONVERSION", 11u32, "2026-11-04T16:04Z", "main", "11-04 12:0x main BOX LEAN ORACLE 234/234 agree (pins green, cells 1/1) with context_env + unit_or_delta + bodies_defeq in the live tree; the 4 earlier reds (proof irrelevance and unit eta under the binders of an example) now agree. With the europa kernel gate 66/66 on the same code, context-aware conversion is DONE: hypotheses and binder-bound variables are typed during conversion, proof irrelevance and unit-like eta hold there.")
inl note_of_cic_typing_1 () = Note ("CIC-TYPING", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:19Z", "regex", "regex 08:2x SOURCE: read-only research by subagent add9e665535617d64 (11-02), copy at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\cic-sps-report.md. DOD: the 40 legacy negatives (matrix.psd1 ExpectedErrors 291-330) each mapped to a fails block or a runtime Rejected test; subject reduction checked on the corpus. SHARED TYPEFEATURESET RULE: the runtime term is a closed `:| ^ term` with a de Bruijn depth as a runtime u32 (no growing phantom, so no wait on GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX); scope typestate is a two-value phantom (loose | closed, constant indices compile today); judgements are GADT-indexed certificates (cert has_type | cert defeq | cert whnf) with refusals as a reason union; prototypes for environment and reduction-strategy dispatch (forall prototype lists explicit, dispatch once at the boundary); existentials only for the static fixture/corpus registry; names are nominals, strings only at the Lean printer boundary. TEMPLATE: regex repo (src notebooks with `///- --package . --timeout N`, a `:# <file> static =` prelude, `///> rust`/`///> gleam`/`///> lean` pinned tests with one-line _assert_eq bodies, :~ join points for multi-use helpers, build.ps1 reading the spiral-tests total line, the Windows event-log crash reader, the 1000-line gate, cell budget 272) and kit's link: units for crate splits (not --import-types, deleted by IMPORT-TYPES-DELETE).")
inl note_of_cic_typing_2 () = Note ("CIC-TYPING", 2u32, "2026-11-03T21:13Z", "main", "main 11-03 17:1x FIRST SLICE (unstaged, spiral apps/kernel/src/typing.spi, registered last): infer / sort_of / check / apply_type as one :& group over a local context (list of fvar name * type). Binders open with fresh names (scope's open_with) and close with abstract_fvar. Pi : Sort (imax l1 l2); Lam : Pi of its body's type; App: the function type goes to WHNF, must be a Pi, and the argument is CHECKED by conversion (defeq), then the codomain is instantiated; Let checks its value, then unfolds. TYPED REFUSALS: refusal = UnknownVar | NotAFunction | NotAType | Mismatch | LooseBound | NoConstants | TooDeep, wrapped as inferred = Typed | Rejected. Tests: the identity on Prop : (x : Prop) -> Prop and the polymorphic identity : (A : Type) -> (a : #0) -> #1; poly_id Prop p : Prop; rejected with named refusals: 'not a function: Prop : Type', 'unknown q', 'mismatch: Type vs Prop'. Europa apps/kernel/build.ps1 19/19 over 6 modules (syntax 4, scope 3, universes 3, reduce 3, conversion 3, typing 3), KERNEL-OK; formatter applied, kit standards 0. LEFT: the environment (constants with delta), inductives, the legacy negative families as fails blocks. Progress 0 -> 30.")
inl note_of_cic_typing_3 () = Note ("CIC-TYPING", 3u32, "2026-11-03T21:27Z", "main", "main 11-03 17:2x CONSTANTS: env threaded through infer/sort_of/check/apply_type (and conversion's defeq_with, so lazy unfolding comes from reduce's delta); Const takes its declared type from the environment, an unknown name is refused ('unknown constant foo'). Test: nat : Type (axiom), id p : Prop (def applied), foo refused. Europa kernel 22/22. Progress 30 -> 40.")
inl note_of_cic_typing_4 () = Note ("CIC-TYPING", 4u32, "2026-11-03T22:28Z", "main", "main 11-03 18:3x UNIVERSE-POLYMORPHIC CONSTANTS: decl now carries its universe parameters (Axiom (name, params, type) | Def (name, params, type, value)); env gains instantiate_level / instantiate_levels (Param -> the use's level, through Sort and nested Const levels) and unfold_at. Typing instantiates a constant's declared type with the levels at its use and refuses a wrong count ('wrong number of universe levels for id'); reduce's delta instantiates the value. Test: id.{u} : (A : Sort u) -> A -> A used at u := 1 has type (A : Type) -> (a : #0) -> #1; 'id' with no levels is refused. Europa kernel 28/28 over 8 modules. Progress 40 -> 50.")
inl note_of_cic_typing_5 () = Note ("CIC-TYPING", 5u32, "2026-11-03T23:20Z", "main", "19:1x main: declaration admission (Lean add_decl shape). typing.admit refuses a duplicate name (AlreadyDeclared), a universe Param the decl does not declare (UndeclaredLevel, via env.stray_in_decl), a type that is not a sort, and a Def whose value does not check against its type; admit_all threads the env. Europa pack30: kernel 33/33 KERNEL-OK, kit standards 0. Next: inductive types (CIC-INDUCTIVE) need admit as their entry point.")
inl note_of_cic_typing_6 () = Note ("CIC-TYPING", 6u32, "2026-11-04T10:12Z", "main", "11-04 06:1x main: infer/check with typed refusals now cover constants, quotients, projections (incl. the Prop-structure rule) and declaration admission; Lean agrees 188/188. Left by the title: port the legacy mega sample's negative families as fails blocks plus runtime Rejected cases (CIC-MEGA-ABSORB).")
inl note_of_cic_typing_7 () = Note ("CIC-TYPING", 7u32, "2026-11-05T02:15Z", "main", "11-04 22:1x main GROOM: typing now admits 18857 Lean 4.35 library declarations with 0 refusals across five replayed modules (CIC-REPLAY-OPAQUE-VALUES), and today's typing changes (context-aware check, opaque values checked, semantic Prop test in prop_guard) are oracle-checked 364/364. Progress 80 -> 90. Left by the title, unchanged: port the legacy mega sample's negative families as fails blocks plus runtime Rejected cases.")
inl note_of_cic_typing_8 () = Note ("CIC-TYPING", 8u32, "2026-11-05T04:44Z", "main", "11-05 00:44 main LEGACY NEGATIVES PORTED (the title's last piece). All 40 mega_lean_cic_bottom_up_kernel negatives are mapped by error class. Runtime Rejected tests: argument mismatch (legacy_application_codomain, general_dependent_application_argument, dependent_cross_pair, total_substitution_domain) -> existing ill_typed_terms_are_rejected_with_a_named_refusal. NEW test the_legacy_negative_families_are_refused_at_runtime (typing.spi, unstaged) covers binder/domain not a type (dependent_pi_domain, general_pi_binder_body, general_dependent_lambda_binder_body), let value vs declared type (legacy_let_codomain), capture/loose variable (capture), dependent result mismatch (dependent_result_type, indexed_dependent_application_result, indexed_unary_constructor_application_result, programmed_dependent_application_result, programmed_endpoint_cross_codomain, recursive_codomain_application_depth) and sort mismatch through whnf/defeq (whnf_sort, atomic_defeq_sort, conversion_constraint_sort, ordinary_identity_beta_source/target_sort, unification_constraint_context): a beta-equal sort is accepted, a beta-unequal one refused. Iota cross-category (3 iota_indexed_*) -> inductive.spi recursor tests plus the replay's recursor-vs-Lean defeq check. NO KERNEL ANALOGUE, by design: 9 metavariable families (meta_*, two_meta_*, unification_assignment, membership_identity_authority, typed_meta_identity_decision); Lean's kernel has no metavariables either, they are elaborator-level. 7 \"authority\" families (*_authority, intrinsic/scalar/obstruction): proof-carrying types of the old encoding, whose content (non-defeq is not defeq) the conversion tests cover. 4+3+1+1+6+6+3+9+7 = 40. Proof: typing.spi 9/9 on europa (run_notebook --gate). Also today: Init.Data.Array.Basic replays 6875 decls with 0 refusals (new replay test, 475 s on europa) after the universe simplify fix (CIC-NOCONFUSION-BLOWUP).")
inl note_of_cic_typing_9 () = Note ("CIC-TYPING", 9u32, "2026-11-05T07:35Z", "main", "11-05 03:35 main CROSS-OS: the whole kernel (apps/kernel/src, 12 modules: conversion env export inductive lean nested reduce scope subst syntax typing universes; oracle excluded, it needs the Lean toolchain) passes 74/74 on WINDOWS (box, one run_notebook --gate holding a test-suite window, 0 failed, 0 unsupported), with tonight's universes.simplify fix, the legacy-negatives, context-exchange and beta-zeta-diamond tests; the same modules were green on Linux (europa) earlier tonight.")
inl note_of_cic_typing_10 () = Note ("CIC-TYPING", 10u32, "2026-11-05T10:38Z", "main", "11-05 06:38 main WINDOWS REPLAY attempt 1 (node mirror, pack44): VOID, not red. The first cell over the 300 s default (headroom 1.25, slowest 375 s on the busy node) killed the notebook's whole process tree, so every later replay 'failed' with it, Array.Basic included despite its own header. Real data point: Init.Prelude replays on WINDOWS with 0 refusals (1837, 0, 0). FIX (unstaged apps/kernel/replay/replay.spi): ///- --timeout 1200000 on the Core, Nat, List and WF replay tests (Array keeps 1800000, Prelude the default); the notebook still round-trips canonical + fixpoint. Rerun queued on the node (job main-replay2).")
inl note_of_cic_typing_11 () = Note ("CIC-TYPING", 11u32, "2026-11-05T11:18Z", "main", "11-05 07:18 main WINDOWS REPLAYS (node mirror, pack44, rerun with the per-test timeouts): Init.Prelude (1837, 0, 0), Init.Core (3479, 0, 0), Init.Data.Nat.Basic (4281, 0, 0), Init.Data.List.Basic (4868, 0, 0), Init.WF (4392, 0, 0): five of six replay on WINDOWS with 0 refusals and EXACTLY the Linux declaration counts. Init.Data.Array.Basic hit its own 1800 s budget (headroom 1.0) on the loaded node (europa: 475 s): VOID, not red; its header is now ///- --timeout 3600000 (unstaged; replay.spi still canonical). So the kernel's Lean replay is cross-OS for 18857 declarations; Array.Basic's 6875 are proven on Linux.")
inl note_of_cic_typing_12 () = Note ("CIC-TYPING", 12u32, "2026-11-05T11:55Z", "main", "11-05 07:55 main CROSS-OS COMPLETE: Init.Data.Array.Basic replays on WINDOWS (node mirror, pack44, alone, ///- --timeout 3600000): (6875, 0, 0), 1902 s, headroom 0.53. With the earlier rerun, all six Lean 4.35 modules (Prelude 1837, Core 3479, Nat.Basic 4281, List.Basic 4868, WF 4392, Array.Basic 6875 = 25732 declarations) replay through the kernel with 0 refusals on BOTH Linux and Windows, with identical counts. replay.spi carries per-test timeouts (unstaged) so a loaded machine can't turn them into VOIDs.")
inl note_of_cic_inductives_1 () = Note ("CIC-INDUCTIVES", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:19Z", "regex", "regex 08:2x SOURCE: read-only research by subagent add9e665535617d64 (11-02), copy at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\cic-sps-report.md. DOD: the legacy strict-positivity certificates and verified eliminators/iota as tests; Lean agrees on every declaration of the corpus. SHARED TYPEFEATURESET RULE: the runtime term is a closed `:| ^ term` with a de Bruijn depth as a runtime u32 (no growing phantom, so no wait on GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX); scope typestate is a two-value phantom (loose | closed, constant indices compile today); judgements are GADT-indexed certificates (cert has_type | cert defeq | cert whnf) with refusals as a reason union; prototypes for environment and reduction-strategy dispatch (forall prototype lists explicit, dispatch once at the boundary); existentials only for the static fixture/corpus registry; names are nominals, strings only at the Lean printer boundary. TEMPLATE: regex repo (src notebooks with `///- --package . --timeout N`, a `:# <file> static =` prelude, `///> rust`/`///> gleam`/`///> lean` pinned tests with one-line _assert_eq bodies, :~ join points for multi-use helpers, build.ps1 reading the spiral-tests total line, the Windows event-log crash reader, the 1000-line gate, cell budget 272) and kit's link: units for crate splits (not --import-types, deleted by IMPORT-TYPES-DELETE).")
inl note_of_cic_inductives_2 () = Note ("CIC-INDUCTIVES", 2u32, "2026-11-04T00:27Z", "main", "20:3x main: first two slices. (1) inductive.spi: Inductive decl (name, level params, former type, constructors); admit_inductive refuses a former that does not end in a Sort, a constructor whose conclusion is not the family (NotConstructorOf), and a non-strictly-positive occurrence (NotPositive: the family inside a binder domain of an argument). (2) Generated recursor + iota: env gains Recursor decls (admit refuses hand-written ones: GeneratedOnly); recursor_type builds motive/minors/major over FVars closed with abstract_fvar, with an IH binder for each direct recursive argument; reduce.iota whnf's the major, picks the constructor's minor and applies args + IHs (step Iota). Nat: Nat.rec pred (succ (succ zero)) whnf = succ zero in [Iota; Beta; Beta], and the application checks against Nat. Scope limits: no inductive parameters/indices yet (recursor only for a former that is exactly Sort (Succ _)), Prop families get no recursor yet, IHs only for direct (not Pi-typed) recursive args. Europa: kernel 37/37 across 9 modules, KERNEL-OK, kit standards 0.")
inl note_of_cic_inductives_3 () = Note ("CIC-INDUCTIVES", 3u32, "2026-11-04T00:43Z", "main", "20:4x main: DESIGN DECISION on structure eta (deferred, not dropped). Doing it through the generated recursor (proj_i x := S.rec params (fun _ => A_i) (fun a.. => a_i) x) makes eta depend on the exact motive/minor spelling a user's projection Def unfolds to, so 'x == mk (fst x) (snd x)' would hold or fail on spelling. The sound route is Lean 4's: a Proj term former (struct name, field index, term) with its own whnf rule (Proj i (mk ps as) -> a_i) and eta in compare_whnf (t vs mk ps as when the ctor is a structure's only ctor: each a_i == Proj i t). That adds a term variant to syntax.spi and every exhaustive match (term_text, same_as, shift_from, instantiate_at, abstract_at, loose_range, instantiate_levels, stray_in_term, mentions). Slice it after indices, as its own story.")
inl note_of_cic_inductives_4 () = Note ("CIC-INDUCTIVES", 4u32, "2026-11-04T00:53Z", "main", "20:5x main: two more slices, europa kernel 44/44 across 10 modules. (3) Prop families get a recursor that eliminates only into Prop (no rec_u level, motive : I -> Prop); True.rec on intro iotas to the minor, and a large motive (True -> Type) is refused with 'mismatch: Type vs Prop'. (4) PARAMETERS: Inductive carries np; params_of opens the former's and every constructor's first np binders with shared FVars p0..; a constructor must conclude in exactly I p0..p(np-1) (uniformity, else NotConstructorOf); the recursor binds params, then motive : (t : I ps) -> Sort u, minors, major; Recursor decls carry np and iota skips np args on both the recursor spine and the constructor spine. List (A : Type): List.rec head-or-zero on cons Nat 1 (nil Nat) = 1 in [Iota; Beta; Beta; Beta] and checks against Nat; a ctor returning Odd Prop is refused. LEFT: indices (Eq), structure eta (Proj former, n3), Pi-typed recursive args' IHs, nested/mutual.")
inl note_of_cic_inductives_5 () = Note ("CIC-INDUCTIVES", 5u32, "2026-11-04T01:16Z", "main", "21:0x main: INDEXED FAMILIES + Lean-style recursor rules; europa kernel 45/45 on pack32. The former's binders after the np params are indices (indices_of opens them as FVars i0..); a constructor must conclude in I p0..p(np-1) j1..jni with index args free of I (concludes_uniformly). The motive abstracts the indices, (i : idx) -> (t : I ps i) -> Sort u; each minor ends in motive (its conclusion's index args) (c ps args); each induction hypothesis uses its recursive argument's own indices. Recursor decls now store (np, ni) and, per constructor, a closed RULE TERM (Lean's RecursorRule.rhs): fun params motive minors args => minor args (rec params motive minors idx_a a)..., built over FVars and closed with lams. Iota instantiates the rule's levels with the recursor's actual levels and substitutes [params, motive, minors] ++ the constructor's non-param args (beta_all), as one Iota step; the per-arg flags and hyps are gone. Test: Eq.{u} (A : Sort u) (a : A) : A -> Prop with refl; Eq.rec Nat zero (fun b h => True) intro zero (Eq.refl Nat zero) = intro in [Iota] and checks against True. LEFT: structure eta (n3), Pi-typed recursive args' IHs, mutual/nested, large elimination for subsingletons like Eq.")
inl note_of_cic_inductives_6 () = Note ("CIC-INDUCTIVES", 6u32, "2026-11-04T01:34Z", "main", "21:3x main: Pi-TYPED RECURSIVE ARGUMENTS. An argument a : (xs) -> I ps js (positivity already allowed it) now gets the function hypothesis ih_a : (xs) -> motive js (a xs), and its rule term passes fun xs => rec .. js (a xs) (branches_of opens the argument's own Pi chain as a_x0..; direct arguments are the xs = [] case). Tree with node : (Nat -> Tree) -> Tree: Tree.rec (fun _ => Nat) zero (fun f ih => ih zero) (node (fun _ => leaf)) = zero in [Iota; Beta; Beta; Beta; Beta; Iota] and checks against Nat. Europa kernel 47/47 on pack32.")
inl note_of_cic_inductives_7 () = Note ("CIC-INDUCTIVES", 7u32, "2026-11-04T05:18Z", "main", "11-04 01:2x main: SUBSINGLETON ELIMINATION (Lean's rule). A Prop family eliminates into any universe if it has no constructors, or exactly one constructor whose every field is a proof (its type's sort is Prop, checked with params and earlier fields in context) or appears among the conclusion's index arguments (Eq). Otherwise Prop only. Such recursors take rec_u first, like Lean's True.rec.{u} / Eq.rec.{u, u_1}. Tests: True.rec at [Zero] and [Succ Zero]; a two-constructor Either refuses large elimination ('mismatch: Type vs Prop'); Eq.rec now takes [Zero; Succ Zero]. europa kernel 49/49. Found by planning the Lean oracle: the kernel refused True's large elimination, which Lean accepts.")
inl note_of_cic_inductives_8 () = Note ("CIC-INDUCTIVES", 8u32, "2026-11-04T09:35Z", "main", "11-04 05:3x main: STRUCTURES + STRUCT ETA. New term former Proj (structure, field index, value), Lean's Expr.proj, handled in every term traversal (syntax text/size/equality/loose range, scope shift/instantiate/abstract, env level instantiation and stray check, positivity mentions, oracle mutants, Lean printer as (e).k). reduce: Proj of a value whnf-ing to the structure's single constructor gives field np+i (step Project). typing: a projection's type is the ctor's i-th field type with params from the value's type and earlier fields replaced by their own projections (Lean's dependent rule); out-of-range or non-structure refuses 'not a structure projection'. env: structure_ctor / structure_of_ctor (one ctor, no indices). conversion: Proj vs Proj componentwise, and STRUCT ETA: a constructor application equals x when every field equals Proj x, tried wherever a mismatch would be reported (or_eta / eta_either). Tests: Pair.1 of mk reduces in one Project step, field types Nat, p equals mk (p.0) (p.1) 'same in 0', index 2 refused. europa pack34 + toml lib: kernel 53/53 KERNEL-OK. Oracle on the node: 172/172 agree (K.Pair projection typing and reduction, struct eta through Lean's Eq, out-of-range refused). Not yet: mutual/nested inductives; Lean's rule restricting projections out of Prop structures to Prop fields; an explicit structure-type check in struct eta.")
inl note_of_cic_inductives_9 () = Note ("CIC-INDUCTIVES", 9u32, "2026-11-04T10:11Z", "main", "11-04 06:1x main: PROP-STRUCTURE PROJECTIONS (Lean's infer_proj rule). A projection out of a value whose type is a proposition must itself be a proof: prop_guard refuses 'a proposition projects only proofs' when the structure's sort is Prop and the field's sort is not. Because a later field's type is instantiated with earlier projections, a proof whose type depends on a non-proof field (Ex's h : P w) is refused too, matching Lean, which rejected (K.e).2. My first expectation there was wrong and the oracle corrected it. And-like structures (K.Both : Prop with two True fields) project their proofs. Kernel test covers all three. Oracle on the node: 188/188 agree. Box kernel: 54/54 KERNEL-OK across 11 modules. CIC-INDUCTIVES remainder: mutual and nested inductives; a structure-type check inside struct eta.")
inl note_of_cic_inductives_10 () = Note ("CIC-INDUCTIVES", 10u32, "2026-11-04T11:30Z", "main", "11-04 07:5x main MUTUAL INDUCTIVES landed in the unstaged kernel (admit_mutual: shared parameter front, one motive per member, group minors, cross-family positivity; admit_inductive = admit_mutual [ ind ]). EUROPA kernel gate 58/58 KERNEL-OK (head 98e51d32 + unstaged), which includes a_mutual_pair_recurses_through_both_families and the new subject-reduction law test (beta, delta and iota redexes keep their type after whnf). NODE Lean oracle: the group declaration MTree/MForest is accepted by both sides, and the negative group (BTree/BForest, renamed so it no longer redeclares MTree) is refused by both with Lean's \"non positive occurrence\". 192/198: the 6 disagreements were a PRINTER bug, not kernel. A binder named \"if\" (a Lean keyword) was printed bare. Fixed: fresh_name wraps keywords as «if» and checks shadowing on the quoted form, with a lean.spi test. That rerun is PENDING on the node.")
inl note_of_cic_inductives_11 () = Note ("CIC-INDUCTIVES", 11u32, "2026-11-04T11:45Z", "main", "11-04 08:1x main: the node oracle rerun with the printer fix is GREEN, 198/198 (n10 pending resolved). Mutual inductives are proven by the europa kernel gate 58/58 plus Lean agreement. Kernel coverage: single, parameterized, indexed and infinitely-branching families; Prop elimination with subsingleton/large elimination; quotients; structures with projections and eta; mutual groups. Still open vs Lean: nested inductives (a family under another, e.g. List Tree) and structure-eta for Prop structures. Commit suggestion for the user when they stage: spiral apps/kernel (env, reduce, conversion, typing, syntax, scope, inductive, lean, oracle).")
inl note_of_cic_inductives_12 () = Note ("CIC-INDUCTIVES", 12u32, "2026-11-04T14:18Z", "main", "11-04 10:2x main NESTED INDUCTIVES (unstaged nested.spi, Lean-style elimination into an auxiliary mutual group, then back-translation; recursor Tree.rec_1 as in Lean). EUROPA kernel gate 63/64: admission (admitted 12, node : List Tree -> Tree), translation (Tree._aux1 and its constructors gone, Tree.rec and Tree.rec_1 present), a container negative in its parameter refused as \"not strictly positive: T._aux1.negmk\", and the unchanged non-nested path all PASS; the oracle test with the nested corpus pins also passes. The single red was MY TEST: iota through Tree.rec / Tree.rec_1 reduced correctly (both defeq checks true: 2 and 3 children counted), but I compared the inferred type's TEXT with \"Nat\" while infer returns the unreduced motive application (fun t => Nat) major. Test now asserts the inferred type is definitionally Nat; rerun PENDING on europa. The Lean oracle run for nested (node) failed before writing its file, cause unknown; it reruns once the kernel is fully green.")
inl note_of_cic_inductives_13 () = Note ("CIC-INDUCTIVES", 13u32, "2026-11-04T14:35Z", "main", "11-04 10:4x main NESTED INDUCTIVES GREEN on europa: nested.spi 5/5 after the test fix (the inferred recursor type is checked definitionally equal to Nat), on top of the full kernel gate's 63 other passes. Nested families are admitted the way Lean does it: aux mutual group, back-translation, Tree.rec_1. Still to do: the Lean oracle comparison for the nested corpus (oracle test pins already pass in the kernel gate; the node Lean run needs a rerun).")
inl note_of_cic_inductives_14 () = Note ("CIC-INDUCTIVES", 14u32, "2026-11-04T14:51Z", "main", "11-04 10:5x main LEAN AGREEMENT FOR NESTED: on the box oracle run (214/217, the 3 reds being an unrelated universe-probe mistake) every nested entry agrees with Lean. Nested inductives are DONE end to end: kernel tests 5/5 + 63 others on europa, Lean agreement on the oracle. Open vs Lean: K-like reduction (probe added).")
inl note_of_cic_inductives_15 () = Note ("CIC-INDUCTIVES", 15u32, "2026-11-04T15:36Z", "main", "11-04 11:3x main CLEAN EUROPA KERNEL GATE 65/65 KERNEL-OK covers mutual + nested inductives (nested.spi 5/5 within). With Lean agreement on every nested/mutual oracle entry, this item's scope (declarations, positivity, recursors, iota, structure eta, mutual, nested) is complete against Lean. Remaining CIC gaps live on their own items (CIC-CONVERSION context, CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY).")
inl note_of_cic_lean_oracle_1 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-ORACLE", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:19Z", "regex", "regex 08:2x SOURCE: read-only research by subagent add9e665535617d64 (11-02), copy at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\cic-sps-report.md. DOD: 100% verdict agreement (Accepted cert | Rejected reason vs lean accept/reject) on the pinned corpus and mutations generated from accepted terms (fiscal''s lesson: positives from the model, mutations expected to fail); disagreements listed as typed rows on the page. LEAN-BACKEND: 442/443 rows agree with C, elaboration median 3.45 s, lean4 v4.35.0 via elan. SHARED TYPEFEATURESET RULE: the runtime term is a closed `:| ^ term` with a de Bruijn depth as a runtime u32 (no growing phantom, so no wait on GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX); scope typestate is a two-value phantom (loose | closed, constant indices compile today); judgements are GADT-indexed certificates (cert has_type | cert defeq | cert whnf) with refusals as a reason union; prototypes for environment and reduction-strategy dispatch (forall prototype lists explicit, dispatch once at the boundary); existentials only for the static fixture/corpus registry; names are nominals, strings only at the Lean printer boundary. TEMPLATE: regex repo (src notebooks with `///- --package . --timeout N`, a `:# <file> static =` prelude, `///> rust`/`///> gleam`/`///> lean` pinned tests with one-line _assert_eq bodies, :~ join points for multi-use helpers, build.ps1 reading the spiral-tests total line, the Windows event-log crash reader, the 1000-line gate, cell budget 272) and kit's link: units for crate splits (not --import-types, deleted by IMPORT-TYPES-DELETE).")
inl note_of_cic_lean_oracle_2 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-ORACLE", 2u32, "2026-11-04T00:53Z", "main", "20:5x main: slice 1, the printer (apps/kernel/src/lean.spi). lean_term prints kernel terms as Lean 4 source: bound variables get their binder names, a shadowed name gets _1, _2..; binders keep their kind ((x : A), {x : A}, {{x : A}}, [x : A]); Sort 0/1 print as Prop/Type, others as Sort with Lean level syntax (u+1, max u v, imax u v, numerals); constants print as @c.{levels} so Lean does not re-elaborate implicits. lean_decl prints axiom/def with .{params}; recursors are skipped (Lean generates them from the inductive). 3 tests, europa kernel 44/44. NEXT: lean is not installed on europa (no elan); install elan + the pinned lean4 v4.35.0 there, then emit a corpus file of decls + 'example : T := t' judgements and compare accept/reject with the kernel's verdicts.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_oracle_3 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-ORACLE", 3u32, "2026-11-04T04:17Z", "main", "11-04 00:1x main CORRECTION to note 2 and the 11-03 report: Lean IS installed. Box: lean 4.35.0 via scoop elan (restored 10-30 in PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY). Node (laptop-ts): scoop elan lean. Only europa lacks it (no ~/.elan; disk 94% full). The oracle does NOT need CI. NEXT: run the T2 comparison on the NODE (node-first rule), emitting decls plus example judgements from lean.spi and comparing accept/reject with the kernel.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_oracle_4 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-ORACLE", 4u32, "2026-11-04T05:18Z", "main", "11-04 01:2x main: slice 2+3 of the ORACLE, run on the NODE (lean 4.35.0). New apps/kernel/src/oracle.spi: entry = Declare decl | Judge (ty, value) | Family inductive; the kernel's verdict per entry (admit / admit_inductive, env grown only by admitted entries) is written beside its Lean source, '-- oracle N kernel_accepts=B', into one file (set_option autoImplicit false + noncomputable section). One lean run, error line numbers map to cases. lean.spi gained lean_inductive (params printed once as binders, constructor types without them, short ctor names). First node run 16/19: the 3 misses were Lean's code generator ('K.t not supported by code generator'), not typing; noncomputable section fixed it. Corpus: 20 judgements (identity, Prop impredicativity, universe errors, let, beta in the expected type, universe-polymorphic K.id at .{1} and .{0}) plus 8 inductive entries (K.Nat recursor, iota in an expected type, K.True subsingleton elimination, K.Either refused large elimination). with_mutants adds 3 per judgement: (ty, ty), (bumped ty, v), (ty, bumped v). europa: kernel 49/49 KERNEL-OK. Lean comparison of the full corpus is running on the node mirror.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_oracle_5 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-ORACLE", 5u32, "2026-11-04T05:27Z", "main", "11-04 01:3x main ORACLE AGREE 94/94 on the node (lean 4.35.0, mirror main-kernel, private MIX_BUILD_PATH, cells 1/1): 28 corpus entries (20 judgements + 8 declarations/families: K.Nat recursor and iota, K.True subsingleton large elimination, K.Either refused large elimination) plus 66 generated mutants (3 per judgement). Every kernel accept/refuse matches lean's. Method: the oracle test writes %TEMP%\\kernel-lean-oracle.lean with '-- oracle N kernel_accepts=B' on each line; `lean <file>`; a line is lean-refused iff an 'error' diagnostic sits on it; compare. NEXT: (1) widen the corpus (List with a parameter, Eq/indexed, Pi-typed Tree, let/zeta, universe-polymorphic families, definitional unfolding through K.id); (2) mutants beyond bump/self (swap arguments, drop an application, wrong recursor level); (3) move the line comparison out of ad-hoc glue into Spiral (the test reads lean's output when lean is on PATH), so the oracle reruns in one call.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_oracle_6 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-ORACLE", 6u32, "2026-11-04T08:44Z", "main", "11-04 04:3x main ORACLE AGREE 146/146 on the node (lean 4.35.0): the 50-entry corpus (20 core judgements; K.Nat/K.True/K.Either; K.List with a parameter, K.Eq indexed and universe-polymorphic, K.Tree with a function-typed recursive argument; eta through Eq, definitional proof irrelevance, distinct inhabitants refused; Lean's prelude Eq + Quot with Quot.lift typing and a lift REDUCTION inside Eq.refl) plus 96 generated mutants. All of tonight's disagreements were printer or harness artifacts, never kernel verdicts, each fixed in lean.spi/oracle.spi: (1) codegen errors on axioms -> noncomputable section; (2) Lean's maxErrors 100 cut off verdicts (set_option has no effect) -> lean -DmaxErrors=100000; (3) curried ((@f a) b) lets Lean instantiate implicit binders after a -> flat spines (@f a b c); (4) an inductive's own universes in its ctor types -> stripped; (5) `axiom K.h : ... Eq` resolved to K.Eq inside namespace K -> every reference printed @_root_.<name>. Lessons in memory lean-oracle-printing. NEXT: move the line comparison from glue into Spiral (a process call to lean when it is on PATH), and widen with mutual/nested inductives and structure projections once the kernel has them.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_oracle_7 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-ORACLE", 7u32, "2026-11-04T09:16Z", "main", "11-04 05:1x main: 155/155 with Quot.sound + Quot.ind entries (53 hand-written + 102 mutants). Kernel 52/52 on pack34 + toml lib.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_oracle_8 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-ORACLE", 8u32, "2026-11-04T09:35Z", "main", "11-04 05:3x main: 172/172 with the structure entries (K.Pair projections, struct eta, out-of-range refusal).")
inl note_of_cic_lean_oracle_9 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-ORACLE", 9u32, "2026-11-04T10:11Z", "main", "11-04 06:1x main: 188/188 (adds K.Ex witness/proof projections and K.Both proof projections). Agreement has held at 100% across 7 corpus extensions since the printer fixes.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_oracle_10 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-ORACLE", 10u32, "2026-11-04T11:45Z", "main", "11-04 08:1x main NODE (spiral head 98e51d32 + unstaged, digest C80CFA10): ORACLE agree 198/198 (was 188/188 before mutual entries). lean.spi + oracle.spi notebooks 5/5, including the new keyword-binder test (fun («if» : Prop) => (fun (if_1 : Prop) => «if»)). The printer now quotes Lean keywords (fresh_name -> quoted, shadowing checked on the quoted form). The 10 entries the mutual group added all agree, with the negative group (K.BForest.bad) refused by both sides for non-positivity.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_oracle_11 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-ORACLE", 11u32, "2026-11-04T14:51Z", "main", "11-04 10:5x main BOX run (Lean on the box; tree = 98e51d32 + unstaged incl. nested + universe entries): ORACLE agree 214/217. All NESTED entries agree with Lean (K.Neg nesting refused by both; K.NTree admitted by both; K.NTree.rec and K.NTree.rec_1 judgments and the Eq.refl count agree). The 3 disagreements were MY universe probe: Lean refuses axiom K.Pp.{a} : Type for an \"unused universe parameter\" (an elaborator policy; the kernel may stay permissive), and the other two only followed from K.Pp being undeclared. Fixed: K.Pp.{a} : Sort (a+1). Also added a K-like reduction probe (transport along an arbitrary h : K.Eq Type K.T K.T must reduce to K.v; Lean accepts by K, and the kernel pin is !- because it has no K-like rule yet). Rerun PENDING (after pack36 frees the box compiler, or on the node).")
inl note_of_cic_lean_oracle_12 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-ORACLE", 12u32, "2026-11-04T15:14Z", "main", "11-04 11:1x main BOX (Lean on the box; installed compiler pack36; tree 98e51d32 + unstaged): ORACLE agree 225/225, and the kernel's pin test passes. New since 188: mutual groups, nested families (K.NTree in K.List, K.Neg refusal, K.NTree.rec_1), universe-polymorphic examples (constants equal up to level equivalence; an unused-universe axiom is Lean front-end policy, fixed in the corpus), and K-like reduction (transport along an arbitrary h : K.Eq Type K.T K.T, plus the same through the definition K.id, both accepted by kernel and Lean).")
inl note_of_cic_lean_oracle_13 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-ORACLE", 13u32, "2026-11-04T16:05Z", "main", "11-04 12:0x main BOX ORACLE 234/234 (was 225/225 at 11:0x): +K.Unit family, proof irrelevance between hypotheses, unit-like eta, each with mutants. Next corpus growth: literals (CIC-LITERALS, scratch run pending).")
inl note_of_cic_lean_oracle_14 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-ORACLE", 14u32, "2026-11-04T18:55Z", "main", "11-04 14:5x main NODE LEAN ORACLE 355/355 agree (cells 1/1, pins green; run on the node mirror main-kernel while kit splits TRAIN22's crates) with every kernel change the Prelude replay forced: Lean's never-zero elimination rule (families in Sort u / Sort (max ..) get recursors), structure eta in iota (struct_iota), fuel 20000, BigNat literals (3 probes around 2^64), Nat.succ <lit> read as a literal by the accelerated ops (probe Nat.ble (Nat.succ 55296) 4294967296 = true). No regression on the earlier 339 entries.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_oracle_15 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-ORACLE", 15u32, "2026-11-04T21:41Z", "main", "11-04 17:4x main NODE LEAN ORACLE 364/364 agree (cells 1/1, pins green; node mirror main-kernel synced 17:34, run with --no-memo --no-html --output-dir instead of --gate because of the warm-path bug x is fixing) on the tree with decimal bignum arithmetic (big_arith/small_or_big) and the 3 new probes: Builtin Nat.sub, Nat.pow 2 64 = 18446744073709551616, Nat.sub 2^64 1 = 18446744073709551615. No regression on the earlier 361 entries.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_oracle_16 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-ORACLE", 16u32, "2026-11-05T02:15Z", "main", "11-04 22:1x main GROOM -> DONE: the DoD (kernel verdicts agree with Lean on a pinned corpus plus generated mutations) holds at 364/364 on Lean 4.35.0 (node, final kernel, mutants via with_mutants). Beyond it, Lean's own library is the oracle now: apps/kernel/replay replays Init.Prelude, Init.Core, Init.Data.Nat.Basic, Init.Data.List.Basic and Init.WF with 0 refusals (CIC-REPLAY-OPAQUE-VALUES). Growth continues there; CIC-BENCH (Planned) depends on this item.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_export_replay_1 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:20Z", "regex", "regex 08:2x SOURCE: read-only research by subagent add9e665535617d64 (11-02), copy at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\cic-sps-report.md. External names UNVERIFIED: confirm the current export format and whether a Lean kernel test corpus exists before filing details; downloads are a standing OK, pin the source. DOD: a pinned export replays with 0 kernel disagreements. SHARED TYPEFEATURESET RULE: the runtime term is a closed `:| ^ term` with a de Bruijn depth as a runtime u32 (no growing phantom, so no wait on GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX); scope typestate is a two-value phantom (loose | closed, constant indices compile today); judgements are GADT-indexed certificates (cert has_type | cert defeq | cert whnf) with refusals as a reason union; prototypes for environment and reduction-strategy dispatch (forall prototype lists explicit, dispatch once at the boundary); existentials only for the static fixture/corpus registry; names are nominals, strings only at the Lean printer boundary. TEMPLATE: regex repo (src notebooks with `///- --package . --timeout N`, a `:# <file> static =` prelude, `///> rust`/`///> gleam`/`///> lean` pinned tests with one-line _assert_eq bodies, :~ join points for multi-use helpers, build.ps1 reading the spiral-tests total line, the Windows event-log crash reader, the 1000-line gate, cell budget 272) and kit's link: units for crate splits (not --import-types, deleted by IMPORT-TYPES-DELETE).")
inl note_of_cic_lean_export_replay_2 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY", 2u32, "2026-11-04T15:43Z", "main", "11-04 11:4x main READINESS: the kernel side this item needs is now in place: inductives incl. mutual and nested (CIC-INDUCTIVES Done), quotients, structures/projections, K-like reduction (CIC-REDUCE Done), universes up to equivalence (CIC-UNIVERSES Done), proof irrelevance (context-aware conversion in progress), and the Lean oracle at 225/225. The FIRST BLOCKER for replaying Init/Prelude is literals: Lean's kernel has Nat literals (Nat.lit plus the GMP-accelerated Nat.add/mul/sub/div/mod/beq/ble/land/lor/xor/shiftLeft/shiftRight/pow/gcd/log2) and String literals (String.mk of a List Char), which appear from Prelude's first screens. NEXT STEP (proposed): a CIC-LITERALS item, Nat literals as a term former with whnf to Nat.succ on demand and the accelerated ops, oracle-checked, before any export tooling. Then fetch lean4export pinned to the installed Lean (downloads standing OK) and build on the node.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_export_replay_3 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY", 3u32, "2026-11-04T17:11Z", "main", "11-04 13:1x main SOURCE PINNED: leanprover/lean4export tag v4.35.0 matches the installed Lean 4.35.0 (box and node); master is already on v4.36.0-rc1, so pin the tag, not master. FORMAT (format_ndjson.md at that tag): \"Lean 4 export format: version 3.1.0\", NDJSON. A meta object, then hash-consed integer tables: names (str/num with \"in\"), levels (succ/max/imax/param with \"il\"), expressions with \"ie\" (bvar, sort, const{name,us}, app{fn,arg}, lam/forallE{name,type,body,binderInfo}, letE, proj, natVal, strVal, mdata, dropped by default). Then declarations: axiom, definition, opaque, theorem, quot, and inductive groups {types[InductiveVal], ctors[ConstructorVal], recs[RecursorVal]} with numParams/numIndices/numNested/all. Every expression form maps 1:1 onto the kernel's term union, now that natVal/strVal have NatLit/StrLit (CIC-LITERALS); the inductive groups map to admit_mutual / admit_nested, and recs can be checked against the kernel's own derivation. PLAN: (1) lake build lean4export@v4.35.0 on the node, export Init.Prelude only (module filter), store the .ndjson pinned by hash in the kit drafts store; (2) export.spi: an NDJSON reader into the three tables (lib json_scan) plus a decoder to term/decl; (3) replay in file order, a disagreement = a refusal Lean accepted; DoD stays: 0 disagreements on Init.Prelude. Bignum Nat literals will be needed (Prelude has USize/UInt64 bounds such as 2^64): a NatLit beyond u64 must be refused, not wrapped.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_export_replay_4 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY", 4u32, "2026-11-04T17:15Z", "main", "11-04 13:2x main STEP 1 DONE (box, the only free machine with Lean): lean4export v4.35.0 (5a9a355, no deps) built in 106 s with lake; Init.Prelude exported in 7 s: 65406 NDJSON lines, 3811816 bytes, sha256 C0BF61671862BCCF..., stored at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY\\init-prelude-lean4.35.0.ndjson (meta: exporter 3.1.0, lean 4.35.0 eb6cafb7). Line census: app 31030, ie-first exprs 12189, forallE 10374, names 7491, const 2320, def 1536, thm 161, inductive groups 126, levels 113, bvar 48, opaque 10, quot 4, axiom 3. FINDINGS for step 2: (a) the largest natVal is 18446744073709551616 = 2^64 (UInt64.size), one past u64, so NatLit needs bignums before the replay (others: 4294967296, 1114112); (b) lib json.decode (typed, options -> None) can read each line into a record of options, but `in` and `type` are reserved words and cannot be field names (probe: \"Expected: }\"), while `fn` works; renaming the keys \"in\": and \"type\": textually before decode is safe because a JSON string value is never followed by a colon. Field access is r::field.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_export_replay_5 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY", 5u32, "2026-11-04T17:29Z", "main", "11-04 13:3x main STEP 2 GREEN on europa: new kernel module src/export.spi (unstaged, in package.spiproj) reads lean4export NDJSON into kernel terms. Rows decode through lib json.decode into one record of options (keys in/type renamed in_/type_), names/levels/terms fill core arrays indexed by id (each row refers only to lower ids, so one pass builds the DAG with sharing), declarations become items: axiom -> Axiom, safe def/thm -> Def, partial def and opaque -> Axiom (value not checked yet), unsafe -> Skipped, inductive groups -> Group (nested if any numNested > 0), quot -> one QuotPackage. natVal beyond u64 becomes a visibly unknown constant bignum-literal:<digits>, never a wrapped value. Tests 2/2: the opening lines of the real export decode to decl Bool.true/Bool.false + an unsafe skip; natural_of keeps 2^64 apart. STEP 3 (running): apps/kernel/replay/replay.spi, a package outside the gate's src glob that replays the pinned export (staged at /tmp/init-prelude.ndjson, sha C0BF6167) through admit/admit_mutual/admit_nested/admit_quotients and tallies accepted/refused/skipped with the first 20 refusals.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_export_replay_6 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY", 6u32, "2026-11-04T17:36Z", "main", "11-04 13:4x main FIRST FULL REPLAY of Init.Prelude (europa, ~1837 items): 774 accepted, 1063 refused, 0 skipped. The refusals cascade from two roots seen in the first 20: (a) Pow.casesOn -> NoConstants(Pow.rec) although the Pow group was not refused, and (b) Nat.brecOn / Nat.add._f / Nat.beq._f -> NotAStructure(PProd); everything after (Nat.add, Nat.mul, Nat.pow, instHPow, noConfusion_of_Nat...) fails on those missing names. Both point at structure-like inductives (Pow, PProd, HPow: one constructor, universe-polymorphic) whose recursor is not in the environment after admission. Rerunning with a check that reports every admitted group lacking <family>.rec.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_export_replay_7 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY", 7u32, "2026-11-04T17:42Z", "main", "11-04 13:4x main FIRST REAL KERNEL BUG FROM THE REPLAY: PUnit, Pow, PProd and HPow were admitted WITHOUT a recursor. group_recursors (inductive.spi) built one only when the family's sort was literally Sort 0 or Sort (Succ _); Sort u (PUnit), Sort (max 1 u v) (PProd), Type (max u v) exported as Sort (max (u+1) (v+1)) (Pow/HPow) fell to \"| _ => Admitted env\". Fixed with Lean's elim_only_at_universe_zero rule: never_zero l (succ; max with a never-zero side; imax with a never-zero right side) -> large elimination, otherwise the same subsingleton criteria as Prop. New kernel test a_family_in_a_universe_variable_still_gets_its_recursor (PUnit.{u} : Sort u and a Box in Sort (max 1 u)). That one gap cascaded into most of the 1063 refusals (casesOn, noConfusion, brecOn via PProd, Nat.add/mul/pow/beq...). Replay rerun PENDING.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_export_replay_8 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY", 8u32, "2026-11-04T17:50Z", "main", "11-04 14:0x main REPLAY AFTER THE RECURSOR FIX: 1766 accepted, 71 refused, 0 skipped (was 774/1063). Two roots left: (1) BitVec.decEq._proof_1 NotAFunction: BitVec.noConfusion's type stayed BitVec.rec ... x_1 on a variable major; Lean's kernel reduces that by STRUCTURE ETA IN IOTA (to_cnstr_when_structure: a major whose type is a one-constructor, index-free, non-Prop family is read as ctor params (proj 0 x) ... (proj k x)). Implemented as struct_iota after k_iota in reduce.spi (structure_fields/ctor_fields/projections; Prop families excluded via ends_in_prop), test a_recursor_on_a_structure_variable_reduces_through_its_projections. The cascade from it: instDecidableEqBitVec, UInt8.decEq, String.decEq, Lean.Name.hasMacroScopes, extractMacroScopes... (2) _private...isValidChar_UInt32: TooDeep at fuel 1000 (decide-style proof through decLt -> Nat.ble -> HAdd/Nat.add instance chains; Lean has no fuel): fuel () raised to 20000, then Char.ofNatAux/Char.ofNat follow. Rerun PENDING.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_export_replay_9 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY", 9u32, "2026-11-04T18:12Z", "main", "11-04 14:1x main REPLAY 3 (structure eta + fuel 20000): 1818 accepted, 19 refused. Roots: (a) isValidChar_UInt32 and two Char.utf8Size proofs TooDeep even at 20000, so something unfolds instead of computing (diagnosis added: the replay now says whether infer of the value or the final comparison ran out, with both whnf shapes); (b) UInt64.size / USize.size_eq on the 2^64 literal; (c) Quot.sound AlreadyDeclared: the kernel's quotient package declares Quot.sound itself, Lean's package is 4 primitives and Quot.sound a separate axiom. FIXES in the tree: BigNat : string term (typed Nat; decimal predecessor for unfolding, falling back to NatLit once it fits u64; Nat.beq/ble on decimals; Lean printer; export reader maps natVal > u64 to it) with 3 oracle probes (ble 1 2^64 = true, 2^64 = succ (2^64-1), beq 2^64 (2^64-1) = true refused); the replay accepts Lean's Quot.sound only when the kernel's built-in axiom has the same universe params and a syntactically equal type. Replay 4 (30 min cell budget via x's new ///- --timeout support) PENDING; box oracle with BigNat probes waits for a free Lean machine.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_export_replay_10 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY", 10u32, "2026-11-04T18:42Z", "main", "11-04 14:4x main TOODEEP ROOT (read from Lean 4.35's Init/Prelude.lean, line 2207): Decidable is now a STRUCTURE (decide := ble n m; reflects_decide), and Nat.decLt n m = Nat.decLe (n+1) m, so `decide (55296 < UInt32.size)` reaches Nat.ble (Nat.succ 55296) 4294967296. The kernel accelerated Nat.ble only when both arguments whnf to literal NODES; Nat.succ <lit> is a constructor application, so it fell back to unfolding Nat.ble's structural recursion over 4294967296 -> TooDeep (isValidChar_UInt32 via of_decide_eq_true rfl, Char.utf8Size proofs). Lean treats Nat.succ <lit> as lit+1 and Nat.zero as 0 for its GMP ops. FIX in reduce.spi: literal_arg/literal_view read an op argument through whnf as NatLit/BigNat, Nat.zero, or Nat.succ of such (u64 max + 1 becomes BigNat 2^64); oracle probe Nat.ble (Nat.succ 55296) 4294967296 = true. Lean oracle on the node (free while kit splits TRAIN22's crates) and replay 5 PENDING.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_export_replay_11 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY", 11u32, "2026-11-04T18:55Z", "main", "11-04 14:5x main NODE LEAN ORACLE 355/355 agree (cells 1/1, pins green; run on the node mirror main-kernel while kit splits TRAIN22's crates) with every kernel change the Prelude replay forced: Lean's never-zero elimination rule (families in Sort u / Sort (max ..) get recursors), structure eta in iota (struct_iota), fuel 20000, BigNat literals (3 probes around 2^64), Nat.succ <lit> read as a literal by the accelerated ops (probe Nat.ble (Nat.succ 55296) 4294967296 = true). No regression on the earlier 339 entries.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_export_replay_12 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY", 12u32, "2026-11-04T19:24Z", "main", "11-04 15:2x main EUROPA KERNEL GATE KERNEL-OK 71/71 over 13 files (incl. export.spi's 2 tests, a_family_in_a_universe_variable_still_gets_its_recursor, a_recursor_on_a_structure_variable_reduces_through_its_projections, the oracle pins) on the tree with every replay-driven fix (never-zero recursor rule, struct_iota, fuel 20000, BigNat, Nat.succ literal view). Together with the node Lean oracle 355/355 the kernel changes are proven; what remains is the Prelude replay count itself (replay 6 on the node PENDING). Slip noted: the europa gate launched although its load probe had timed out, adding to a loadavg of 6.7 there.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_export_replay_13 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY", 13u32, "2026-11-04T20:08Z", "main", "11-04 16:1x main REPLAY HARNESS NOTES: (1) three full replays (europa 19-23 min, node timed out at 30 min under TRAIN23) ended \"failed\" with no assertion line and no tally file. A new head test (first 3000 export lines -> 95 items, 0 refused, tally written, 26 s) proved the report path works, so the suspect is the TooDeep diagnostic added in replay 4 (term_text over large whnf terms, likely a Rust stack overflow the capture filters missed); it is removed now that the TooDeep root is known from Lean's source, and the full replay reruns capturing overflow/panic lines. (2) The replay writes /tmp/replay-tally.txt before asserting, and replay.spi has a ///- --timeout 1800000 header (x's directive). (3) On the node, run_notebook --gate was rejected as an unknown option at 15:0x while it worked at 14:45; passing --no-memo --no-html --output-dir directly works on both machines.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_export_replay_14 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY", 14u32, "2026-11-04T20:54Z", "main", "11-04 16:5x main INIT.PRELUDE REPLAYS WITH 0 REFUSALS: apps/kernel/replay/replay.spi (europa, 1.2 GB memory cap) -> (1837 accepted, 0 refused, 0 skipped) in 33 s, pinned as the test's expected tally. The last blocker was found by bisecting the export with a head test (33000 lines fine in 30 s, 37000 lines killed): USize.size = 2 ^ numBits with numBits = 64, so Nat.pow 2 64 overflowed u64, the accelerator returned None and the kernel unfolded Nat.pow/Nat.mul structurally over huge numbers, hence the 20 min runs, a 2.4 GB OOM on europa (which also restarted x-dumps' iggy pod via the node OOM killer) and the earlier TooDeep. FIX: decimal digit-list arithmetic in reduce.spi (big_arith: add, sub, mul, pow with exponent <= 4096; small_or_big tries u64 first), results normalised back to NatLit when they fit; oracle probes Nat.pow 2 64 = 2^64 and Nat.sub 2^64 1 = 2^64-1. CAVEATS for Done: partial defs and opaques are admitted by type only (Lean also checks the opaque value), unsafe decls are absent from the export, and Lean's recursors are not yet compared with the kernel's own. Lean oracle on the bignum probes and the kernel gate PENDING.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_export_replay_15 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY", 15u32, "2026-11-04T21:41Z", "main", "11-04 17:4x main NODE LEAN ORACLE 364/364 agree (cells 1/1, pins green; node mirror main-kernel synced 17:34, run with --no-memo --no-html --output-dir instead of --gate because of the warm-path bug x is fixing) on the tree with decimal bignum arithmetic (big_arith/small_or_big) and the 3 new probes: Builtin Nat.sub, Nat.pow 2 64 = 18446744073709551616, Nat.sub 2^64 1 = 18446744073709551615. No regression on the earlier 361 entries.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_export_replay_16 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY", 16u32, "2026-11-04T21:44Z", "main", "11-04 17:4x main DONE. Init.Prelude of Lean 4.35.0 (lean4export v4.35.0, 65406 lines, sha C0BF6167, pinned in the kit drafts store) replays through the Spiral kernel with 0 disagreements: replay/replay.spi (europa, 29 s, memory-capped) -> (1837 accepted, 0 refused, 0 skipped), and every recursor the kernel derives is definitionally equal to Lean's exported one (checked by defeq after instantiating Lean's universe parameters with the kernel's; a syntactic compare flagged 20+ multi-universe classes only because level expressions nest differently). Same tree: kernel notebooks 71/71 on europa (one by one via the warm daemon), node Lean oracle 364/364. Kernel fixes the replay forced today: Lean's never-zero elimination rule, structure eta in iota, Nat.succ <lit> read as a literal, decimal bignum arithmetic + BigNat literals, fuel 20000, Quot.sound matched to the built-in axiom. FOLLOW-UPS: CIC-REPLAY-OPAQUE-VALUES (opaque and partial values are admitted by type only), CIC-ENV-INDEX (lookups), and the next modules after Init.Prelude.")
inl note_of_cic_mega_absorb_1 () = Note ("CIC-MEGA-ABSORB", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:20Z", "regex", "regex 08:2x SOURCE: read-only research by subagent add9e665535617d64 (11-02), copy at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\cic-sps-report.md. LEGACY: main.spi 9,309 lines, 499 :=, 104 unions, 74 nominals, 133 GADT cases, 295 existential sites, 77 *_terminal claims, 0 prototypes, 0 test blocks; core corrected_cic_term ctx sort (SortZero, BoundHere/There, Constant, Definition, Lambda, Pi, DependentLambda/DependentApplication/Application/Let with an existential domain) plus strict positivity, verified eliminators and iota, contextual beta and subject reduction, renaming/lifting laws, two-cell swap, one-binder substitution, Bool-indexed dependent results, structural defeq, a conversion-constraint solver, meta assignment and WHNF; its own open list: kernel unification, general Pi in the main AST, dependent substitution, confluence and strong normalization. DOD: every row ABSORBED / PARTIAL with a landing / dropped with a reason, counts and citations. SHARED TYPEFEATURESET RULE: the runtime term is a closed `:| ^ term` with a de Bruijn depth as a runtime u32 (no growing phantom, so no wait on GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX); scope typestate is a two-value phantom (loose | closed, constant indices compile today); judgements are GADT-indexed certificates (cert has_type | cert defeq | cert whnf) with refusals as a reason union; prototypes for environment and reduction-strategy dispatch (forall prototype lists explicit, dispatch once at the boundary); existentials only for the static fixture/corpus registry; names are nominals, strings only at the Lean printer boundary. TEMPLATE: regex repo (src notebooks with `///- --package . --timeout N`, a `:# <file> static =` prelude, `///> rust`/`///> gleam`/`///> lean` pinned tests with one-line _assert_eq bodies, :~ join points for multi-use helpers, build.ps1 reading the spiral-tests total line, the Windows event-log crash reader, the 1000-line gate, cell budget 272) and kit's link: units for crate splits (not --import-types, deleted by IMPORT-TYPES-DELETE).")
inl note_of_cic_mega_absorb_2 () = Note ("CIC-MEGA-ABSORB", 2u32, "2026-11-04T11:03Z", "main", "11-04 07:1x main COVERAGE MAP of the legacy sample's negative families (mega_lean_cic_bottom_up_kernel/main.spi: 3 GADT families, 5 rejected-program builders) onto the apps/kernel tests and the Lean oracle. CicStrictPositivityRejected -> kernel 'not strictly positive' tests (single family and mutual cross-family) plus oracle Bad negative, Lean-confirmed. CicInductiveDeclarationRejected (wrapper) -> admit_inductive/admit_mutual refusals NotPositive, NotConstructorOf, NotAType. The 5 conversion-constraint rejections (pi, application, dependent application, substituted codomain) -> oracle refusals Lean confirms: Type vs (P : Prop) -> P, (fun x => x) T, @K.id.{0} T t, Eq mismatches including the lift reduction to K.t2. CicNoRecursiveOccurrenceRejected is a legacy schema artifact: Lean admits non-recursive families, so the kernel must not refuse them. Positive features: everything on the legacy list has a kernel test except meta assignment and unification, which belong to an elaborator, not a kernel. SUBJECT REDUCTION is now a law test (beta, delta and iota redexes keep their type after whnf), gating next. NEXT for parity: archive the sample under CIC-MEGA-ARCHIVE (user go).")
inl note_of_cic_mega_absorb_3 () = Note ("CIC-MEGA-ABSORB", 3u32, "2026-11-05T04:55Z", "main", "11-05 00:55 main ABSORPTION MAP, the 77 *_terminal claims of mega_lean_cic_bottom_up_kernel/main.spi vs apps/kernel (REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB format). VERDICT: a from-scratch locally-nameless kernel that absorbs the semantics, not the intrinsic encoding. ABSORBED 52: environment/nominal identity (primary_environment_nominal_identity, recursive_environment_membership_identity) -> env + typing constants/admission + replay of 25732 Lean decls; lifting/renaming/context extension (13: bound_there, two_cell/finite/composite/lambda/nested_binder lifting, context_extension composition/associativity/identity, explicit_renaming, renaming composition/identity/associativity) -> scope.spi + subst.spi de Bruijn laws (lift-lower identity, lifts compose, every shape round-trips); substitution (5: one_binder, function_binder, total_substitution_nested_lambda_let, bool_dependent_pi_substitution, parametric_substitution_sort_family) -> subst.spi substitution lemma + typing instantiation; dependent application/codomain (8: codomain, bool_dependent_application_program(+negation_involution), recursive_codomain_application, programmed/indexed_unary_constructor/indexed/scoped dependent application) -> typing + inductive indexed-family tests + Lean oracle; whnf spines (7: whnf_nested_let_beta, ordinary_identity_whnf, spine/let_spine/delta_spine_whnf, dependent_beta constant/bound bool) -> reduce.spi beta/zeta/delta/fuel; defeq/congruence (4: structural_defeq, exact_pi_defeq, application/dependent congruence) -> conversion.spi; iota/eliminators (3: iota_indexed_recursor_component, eliminator_program_direct_conclusion, recursive_sort_zero_canonical_contractum_shape) -> inductive.spi iota tests + replay recursors defeq to Lean's; subject reduction (raw_bool_contextual_chain_subject_reduction, contextual_identity_beta_direct_subject_reduction) -> inductive reduction_preserves_the_type_of_beta_delta_and_iota_redexes; contextual beta and body reduction (lambda/let/let_lambda body reduction, contextual_identity_beta(+program)) -> reduce + conversion under binders; surface (cic_active_corrected_kernel_surface) -> the apps/kernel package. FILLED TONIGHT (were MISSING, 13): local confluence (5: nested_identity/beta_let local diamonds(+programs), local_confluence_coverage_suite) -> NEW conversion test a_beta_zeta_diamond_joins_in_one_normal_form; context exchange (8: two_cell_swap and its 7 binder/program variants) -> NEW typing test swapping_independent_context_entries_keeps_the_type (both unstaged; gates PENDING on europa). DROPPED with reason, 12: metavariables/unification (7: selected_typed_meta_assignment(+program), conversion_constraint_solver, unification_solver, environment_bound_selected_meta, meta_membership_identity_spine, general_meta_environment) are elaborator-level, Lean's kernel has none either; derivation algebra of the old encoding (5: contextual_identity_beta subject_reduction_program/append, derivation_append_coherence, append_associativity, append_identity) plus intrinsic_target program/append_homomorphism are proof-object composition laws with no runtime analogue. 52 + 13 + 12 = 77. The 40 negatives are mapped on CIC-TYPING n8.")
inl note_of_cic_mega_absorb_4 () = Note ("CIC-MEGA-ABSORB", 4u32, "2026-11-05T04:55Z", "main", "11-05 00:55 main CORRECTION to the previous note's totals (the rows are right, the sums were not): ABSORBED 50 (2 env + 13 lifting/renaming + 5 substitution + 8 dependent application + 7 whnf + 4 defeq + 3 iota + 2 subject reduction + 5 contextual beta + 1 surface), FILLED 13, DROPPED 14 (7 metavariable + 5 derivation-append + 2 intrinsic_target). 50 + 13 + 14 = 77.")
inl note_of_cic_mega_absorb_5 () = Note ("CIC-MEGA-ABSORB", 5u32, "2026-11-05T04:57Z", "main", "11-05 00:57 main PROVEN on europa (run_notebook --gate, spiral head faf422c9 + the unstaged tests): conversion.spi 7/7 including a_beta_zeta_diamond_joins_in_one_normal_form (outer-beta and inner-zeta reducts of (fun x => x) (let y := a in y) both reach a and are defeq), typing.spi 10/10 including swapping_independent_context_entries_keeps_the_type (identical type under both orders of the independent entries p and q). Every row of the map is now ABSORBED, FILLED (proven) or DROPPED with a reason; the 40 negatives are on CIC-TYPING n8. DONE.")
inl note_of_bend_unsafe_minimize_1 () = Note ("BEND-UNSAFE-MINIMIZE", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:24Z", "compiler", "11-02 08:20 compiler: filed from the user's directive (relayed by resilience 11-02: \"reduce bend's unsafe and maybe leverage its proofs/laws\"). MEASURED: codegenBend emits \"@unsafe\\ndef\" unconditionally at 16 sites (spiral_compiler.fs 17318-17701: methods, closures, if/union/while helpers, array/layout helpers, main); 300 of 300 sampled main.bend files are all-unsafe (13,236 defs). STEP 1: learn exactly what @unsafe waives in bend2 (termination? totality? IO?) from the bend2 source in the cache toolchain, then classify the 16 sites (recursive, IO, partial via IO.die, or pure). STEP 2: drop @unsafe on pure non-recursive helpers and measure accepted vs rejected over the Bend matrix list. STEP 3 (laws): one generated property, e.g. a union constructor/match round-trip, stated as a Bend 2 theorem and checked. DoD: the Bend list still agrees with C, with an @unsafe count drop reported.")
inl note_of_bend_unsafe_minimize_2 () = Note ("BEND-UNSAFE-MINIMIZE", 2u32, "2026-11-02T16:10Z", "compiler", "11-02 12:30 compiler: STEP 1 DONE (read bend2 source, cache toolchains\\bend\\bend2). @unsafe waives exactly three checks. (1) THE TERMINATION WALL (bend.ts:228-235): every live self-call must descend on a strict subterm in its own case tree; an @unsafe def's self-calls skip descent. (2) FORWARD REFERENCES (bend.ts:3829-3834): a call to a def defined BELOW is a live reference to a bodiless def and errs (infer-ref) unless the caller is @unsafe, so mutual recursion cannot bypass the wall. (3) Binder domains may form + at any kind. The verdict (main.ts:900-916) is FAIL (\"N defs rely on unsafe or foreign code\") whenever a def outside Base uses @unsafe, so today every Spiral program is an unverified book. IMPLICATION FOR codegenBend: a def can drop @unsafe only if (a) it is not in a recursive SCC of the call graph (self tail loops, which Spiral emits for while/self-tail calls, can never prove descent because their recursion is not structural), AND (b) every def it calls is emitted ABOVE it. STEP 2 PLAN: emit defs in topological order of the call graph (SCCs together) and mark @unsafe only the defs in a cyclic SCC, plus main (it calls everything) unless main is non-recursive and last. Expected: pure helpers (union/array/layout getters and putters, closures without recursion, if/match helpers) become checked; loops and recursive methods stay @unsafe. MEASURE: @unsafe count over the Bend matrix list before/after, and every Bend row still agrees with C. STEP 3 (laws) stays as filed.")
inl note_of_bend_unsafe_minimize_3 () = Note ("BEND-UNSAFE-MINIMIZE", 3u32, "2026-11-03T07:31Z", "compiler", "11-03 07:3x compiler GROOM (WIP cap: Active = touched in 12 h). Parked to Planned (15 h). Next: step 2, emit @unsafe only on defs that fail the termination wall or have forward refs (the 3 waived checks of step 1).")
inl note_of_bend_unsafe_minimize_4 () = Note ("BEND-UNSAFE-MINIMIZE", 4u32, "2026-11-04T08:42Z", "compiler", "11-04 04:4x compiler: STEP 2 DRAFTED, node review running (job compiler-bendsafe; base pack34, private control copy). kit drafts BEND-UNSAFE-MINIMIZE\\1-unsafe-only-in-recursive-sccs.kitdo, 1 replacement at codegenBend's final assembly. Before emitting, the defs list is reordered callee-first by Tarjan SCCs over the call graph (edges = names of other defs found in a def's body, past its two header lines), so no def calls one defined below it, which is bend2's forward-reference wall. @unsafe stays only on defs in a recursive SCC (size > 1 or self-call) and is dropped from main. If any def lacks the expected '@unsafe\\ndef name(' header, the old order and markers are kept. Measure: @unsafe count over every main.bend after each arm, plus examples Bend -Native compared with control. Risk named in advance: bend2's third waiver (binder domains with + at any kind) may reject some newly safe defs; such rows will be named.")
inl note_of_bend_unsafe_minimize_5 () = Note ("BEND-UNSAFE-MINIMIZE", 5u32, "2026-11-04T09:08Z", "compiler", "11-04 05:0x compiler: v1 MEASURED, NOT SHIPPABLE (node job compiler-bendsafe; base pack34, private control copy). @unsafe count 15,081 -> 11,524 of 17,933 defs (-24%), but native Bend fell from 414 ran / 0 build-fail to 166 ran / 248 build-fail; 0 DISAGREE among rows that run. bend2's reason (array_bool candidate output, node): SOME PROOFS FAIL, 'expected Data, observed Type' at spiral_main '+v0 : (Chan(Array<Bool>) & U32) <- spiral_array_new_a0(...)', with 'Note: +v0 can be used many times, so its type must be Data'. That is waiver (3) from step 1: Spiral arrays are channels (Chan, a Type), and a + binder on one needs @unsafe. v2 (running, job compiler-bendsafe2) also keeps @unsafe on any def whose text mentions Chan(. Expect a smaller drop and, ideally, 0 new build-fails.")
inl note_of_bend_unsafe_minimize_6 () = Note ("BEND-UNSAFE-MINIMIZE", 6u32, "2026-11-04T09:55Z", "compiler", "11-04 05:5x compiler: v2 MEASURED (keep @unsafe on defs mentioning Chan(): @unsafe 15,081 -> 11,938 of 17,933 (-21%); native Bend 232 ran / 182 build-fail (v1 166/248); 0 DISAGREE. Next bend2 rejection, the same rule on another type: pairs are Type, not Data ('expected Data, observed Type' at spiral_main_field1 '+p: F32 & String' and spiral_main_if1 '+v8: (((U32 & String) & (U32 & String)) & U32)'). v3 (running, job compiler-bendsafe3) also keeps @unsafe on any def mentioning a pair type ' & '. The bend2 rule, as measured: a checked (non-@unsafe) def may bind with + only Data-kind types (scalars, Bool, String alone); Chan and & pairs need @unsafe.")
inl note_of_bend_unsafe_minimize_7 () = Note ("BEND-UNSAFE-MINIMIZE", 7u32, "2026-11-04T10:43Z", "compiler", "11-04 07:0x compiler: v3 NODE REVIEW RED (job compiler-bendsafe3). Candidate = SCC-ordered defs, @unsafe kept only on cyclic SCCs and on defs containing Chan( or ' & ', main not @unsafe. Examples Bend: residual identical, but native 325 ran / 89 build-fail vs control 414 ran / 0; oracle DISAGREE 0. @unsafe dropped only from 15081 to 13150 of 17933 defs (-13%). Every failure is an array of heap unions or heap closures (array_union_heap_heap, array_union_heap_pair_heaps, array_*closure_union3_*, ...), so bend2 rejects some binder kind on the non-recursive path besides Chan and pairs: heap union or closure values bound with '+'. Not landable as is; reproducing one failing sample on the box (bend2 via bun) to read the exact checker message before widening the keep rule.")
inl note_of_bend_unsafe_minimize_8 () = Note ("BEND-UNSAFE-MINIMIZE", 8u32, "2026-11-04T12:03Z", "compiler", "11-04 08:0x compiler: v4 NODE REVIEW (keep @unsafe also on defs naming a 'type X is Type'): native 376 ran / 38 build-fail (v3: 89), oracle DISAGREE 0, residual-only otherwise; @unsafe 13317 of 17933 defs (control 15081, -11.7%). Every remaining failure is a closure sample (closure_apply, closure_curry, closure_depth, closure_heap, closure_return*). Box repro of closure_apply: bend2 'expected Data, observed Type' on '+v0 : ((U32) -> IO(U32)) <- IO.pure(...)': function types are Type kind too. v5 keeps @unsafe on any def that mentions a function type outside its own return arrow (header line cut at its last ') -> '); queued on the node (compiler-bendsafe5, after compiler-gleamarr). HONEST READING: the saving is shrinking (-13% in v3, -11.7% in v4, less in v5), because most generated Bend defs bind Type-kind values with '+'. If v5 is green but saves under 10%, the item's premise (most @unsafe is unneeded) is refuted; the alternative lever is emitting fewer '+' (dup) binders for Type-kind values, which is a codegen change, not an annotation filter.")
inl note_of_bend_unsafe_minimize_9 () = Note ("BEND-UNSAFE-MINIMIZE", 9u32, "2026-11-04T12:45Z", "compiler", "11-04 08:4x compiler: v5 GREEN (node job compiler-bendsafe5; A/B on one tree, the node's 11-03 t1101 copy, so the comparison holds): examples Bend -Native, control 414 ran / 0 build-fail, candidate 414 ran / 0 build-fail; compare: 414 differing cells, ALL residual (defs reordered callee-first, @unsafe dropped), behavior cells 0, DISAGREE 0, so exit and stdout are identical on every row. Note 'oracle agree 0' on both arms: Bend rows have no C oracle in this suite, so the evidence is unchanged behavior vs control, not agreement with C. @unsafe 15081 -> 13425 of 17933 defs (-11.0%). Keep rule as landed in the draft: cyclic SCC, or the def mentions Chan(, ' & ', a 'type X is Type' name, or a function type outside its own return arrow. READING: green and landable, but the saving is modest; most Bend defs bind Type-kind values with '+', so the bigger lever is fewer '+' (dup) binders for Type-kind values (a codegen change), filed as the next step rather than more filter rules. Pack slot: pack37 with the struct-type fixes.")
inl note_of_bend_unsafe_minimize_10 () = Note ("BEND-UNSAFE-MINIMIZE", 10u32, "2026-11-04T13:05Z", "compiler", "11-04 09:1x compiler: THE BIGGER LEVER WORKS (hand test on box, bend2 via bun): in closure_apply.bend (v4 output), spiral_main bound a closure with '+v0 : ((U32) -> IO(U32)) <- IO.pure(...)' and used it once; deleting only the '+' (and leaving spiral_main without @unsafe) passes bend2's checker and runs, exit 0. So a linear (single-use) binder may have a Type-kind type; only '+' (dup) binders must be Data. Next step: codegenBend emits '+' only for binders the def body uses more than once (count uses per def, as the C refc pass counts last uses), and then the keep rule can drop the Type-kind and function-type clauses for defs whose Type-kind binders are all linear. Expected: far more than v5's -11% of @unsafe.")
inl note_of_bend_unsafe_minimize_11 () = Note ("BEND-UNSAFE-MINIMIZE", 11u32, "2026-11-04T14:32Z", "compiler", "11-04 10:3x compiler: v6 RED (node job compiler-bendsafe6): 407 ran / 7 build-fail (closure_triple, closure_u32_flag, ebpf_nest3, ...), 0 DISAGREE, @unsafe 12821 of 17933 (v5 13425; -15% vs control). All 7 are one class (box repro with the node candidate B6120DF8): a pair-typed parameter used once, only to be destructured, '(+v4, +v5, +v6) = p', loses its '+' and bend2 then cannot infer the destructure ('expected an annotated term (cannot infer), observed _ => Bool' at Pair's Sigma). Restoring '+p' by hand makes closure_triple check and run (exit 0). v7: linearize keeps '+' on any binder that is the right-hand side of a '(...) = name' destructure; queued on the node (job compiler-bendsafe7). HONEST READING: even green, linear binders only moved @unsafe from -11% to about -15%; most @unsafe defs keep it for a + binder of Type kind that is really used twice.")
inl note_of_bend_unsafe_minimize_12 () = Note ("BEND-UNSAFE-MINIMIZE", 12u32, "2026-11-04T15:30Z", "compiler", "11-04 11:3x compiler: v7 GREEN (node job compiler-bendsafe7, the git-root copy): examples Bend -Native, control and candidate both 414 ran / 0 build-fail; compare 414 differing cells, all residual, behavior cells 0, DISAGREE 0. @unsafe 15081 -> 13070 of 17933 defs (-13.3%; v5 without linear binders -11.0%). Programs 1 (SCC order, keep @unsafe only for cyclic SCCs or Type-kind dup binders) + 2 (linear binders lose '+', except destructure sources) are ready for the next pack (pack38: pack37 is already staged and in review). HONEST VERDICT on the item's premise: emitting @unsafe only where bend2 needs it removes about 2000 of 15081; the other 13000 are real: recursive SCCs or values of Type kind (pairs, closures, Type-declared unions) duplicated with '+'. Closing at 90% once installed; any further cut needs Data-kind encodings of pairs/closures, which is a Bend backend design change, not a filter.")
inl note_of_bend_unsafe_minimize_13 () = Note ("BEND-UNSAFE-MINIMIZE", 13u32, "2026-11-04T20:36Z", "compiler", "11-04 16:3x compiler: PACK38 REVIEWED and handed to main (install after pack37; one node build, job compiler-pack38rev, control = pack37 candidate bin). Source core 75AAB501 / host 5D4516B8, bin core 15FD51D7 / host 08B00F25. Delphi -Native 430 ran, residual only, 0 behavior; Bend -Native 414 ran, residual only, plus one exit cell: c_self_tail_loop_heap timing out at 120 s (slowest Bend row, control 80 s today; BOTH arms timed out on it in the v6/v7 reviews, same candidate residual 9b61078f), a timeout boundary, not behavior; C -Native 523 ran, residual 9, 0 behavior, 0 DISAGREE everywhere.")
inl note_of_bend_unsafe_minimize_14 () = Note ("BEND-UNSAFE-MINIMIZE", 14u32, "2026-11-05T00:56Z", "compiler", "11-04 20:5x compiler: PENDING INSTALL. main's pack38 install-when-clear gave up at 20:56 after 110 min: it waits for running trains as well as an idle compiler, and kit's TRAIN26 ran on the node the whole window. The box stays on pack37 (host 08B00F25 / core 5F6F6E73). pack38 (reviewed; candidate %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin-candidates\\pack38) installs first in the next run, then pack39 (reviewed; needs live = pack38). The handover commands are in main's inbox from 15:3x (pack38) and 19:2x (pack39).")
inl note_of_bend_unsafe_minimize_15 () = Note ("BEND-UNSAFE-MINIMIZE", 15u32, "2026-11-05T03:57Z", "compiler", "11-04 23:5x compiler: INSTALLED on the BOX in pack38 (23:38, compiler's install-when-clear chain with no train wait, as kit allowed for box-only installs). Dry run: the 7 pack38 programs on today's live source reproduce candidate source core 75AAB501 / host 5D4516B8. After install: SpiralCompilerCore.dll 15FD51D755DD3120 and SpiralCompiler.dll 08B00F25C65C5283, both equal=True to the reviewed candidate; system dotnet launches it. Undo: spiral-bin\\compiler-installs\\pack38-20261104-233851. Node and europa ship: main's waiter (pack-chain -SkipInstall) once pack39 lands. Done under installed-is-done.")
inl note_of_rust_dir_flatten_study_1 () = Note ("RUST-DIR-FLATTEN-STUDY", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:24Z", "compiler", "11-02 08:20 compiler: filed from the user's directive (relayed by resilience 11-02); the user is unsure and wants it studied, not rushed. CONSTRAINTS ALREADY KNOWN: the user's standing rule is lib stays FLAT (no subfolders except leptos/ui, per main 11-02), and the i574n dialect in spiral.toml will infer imports, so manual module order fades as a lib need. PROPOSED ANSWER TO VERIFY: keep lib flat; preserve the pattern (multiple openings of one folder with manual order, which upstream does not support) as a compiler regression sample under tmp/samples with Rust and Gleam rows, so the future backend rewrite keeps supporting it. STEP 1: recover the exact pre-flattening rust/ layout (git log on lib/spiral/rust and package.spiproj modules) and list what it exercised. STEP 2: reproduce it as samples/module_folder_reopen_manual_order. DoD: the user gets a one-paragraph verdict (regression or not) with the sample as evidence.")
inl note_of_rust_dir_flatten_study_2 () = Note ("RUST-DIR-FLATTEN-STUDY", 2u32, "2026-11-02T16:08Z", "compiler", "11-02 12:20 compiler: VERDICT. The flattening was a REGRESSION IN COMPILER COVERAGE, not in lib, and lib should stay flat. EVIDENCE: before commit a8dc6b62 (11-02 06:09), lib/spiral/package.spiproj opened `rust/` FOUR times, interleaved for ordering: (rust, rust_operators) early; (testing, near) after env; (near_workspaces) after routes; (clap) after stream. It was the only place in the org that exercised reopening one folder with manual order (upstream mrakgr Spiral does not support it): 0 of the compiler's samples do (scan of every tmp/samples package.spiproj). So the flattening silently removed the feature's only test, though lib itself loses nothing, since the i574n dialect in spiral.toml will infer imports and the user's rule is lib FLAT (no subfolders except leptos/ui). FIX, landed unstaged: samples/module_folder_reopen_manual_order. Modules base, tools/first, middle, tools/second, main: middle uses tools::first, tools::second uses middle, and main checks the chain sums to 15. It compiles on the installed compiler (C, 235 bytes), which shows the second `tools/` opening merges into the same tools:: namespace. NEGATIVE CONTROL (scratch copy, middle moved after the second opening) fails \"Unbound term variable: middle. In the definition: second_value\", so the sample really guards the order. Matrix: default Fsharp/C/Rust/Delphi plus the Gleam list (the future Rust/Gleam backend rewrite must keep it). Native rows run at the next node review. Close after that run is green.")
inl note_of_rust_dir_flatten_study_3 () = Note ("RUST-DIR-FLATTEN-STUDY", 3u32, "2026-11-02T18:47Z", "compiler", "11-02 15:00 compiler: CLOSED. samples/module_folder_reopen_manual_order passes on Fsharp, C, Rust, Delphi and Gleam (node, pack17 review run single-flight-20261102-140323), and the negative control (wrong order) fails as designed. Verdict stands: lib stays flat per the user's rule, and the compiler keeps the reopen-with-manual-order feature under a regression row.")
inl note_of_sps_purpose_1 () = Note ("SPS-PURPOSE", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:24Z", "regex", "regex 08:2x SOURCE: research by subagent add9e665535617d64 (11-02), copy at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\cic-sps-report.md. User 11-02 07:46: \"the only mega sample left is spiral proves spiral, which i don't know what we could do with yet, but still groom what's needed to at least migrate it to the new project style with test cells etc.\" OPTIONS: (a) keep it as an intrinsic-typing showcase (smallest migration); (b) make it the usage-graded linear/affine fragment of the apps/kernel kernel, reusing CIC-SCOPE/CIC-SUBST (one kernel, two disciplines); (c) relative consistency proper: a Spiral model of a Spiral core, checked by the apps/kernel kernel and cross-checked by Lean (largest, the name''s promise). RECOMMENDATION: (b) now, (c) once CIC-TYPING lands. DOD: the user''s choice recorded here and the destination folder fixed (apps/sps or inside apps/kernel). Ask in one line in the next decision round (memories decision-rounds-batched, subagent-relayed-user-asks).")
inl note_of_sps_purpose_2 () = Note ("SPS-PURPOSE", 2u32, "2026-11-03T07:23Z", "main", "main 11-03 03:1x DECIDED (user 11-03: 'about sps, i don't know, what's sps?' plus 'try reaching pending decisions autonomously'). SPS = the mega sample mega_spiral_proves_spiral_relative_consistency. RULE, written before choosing: pick the option that (1) reuses a kernel that exists or is in flight instead of a third one, (2) gives the 89 negatives a typed home as fails blocks, (3) keeps the larger option open without rework. By that rule: (b), the usage-graded linear/affine fragment of the apps/kernel kernel, reusing CIC-SCOPE/CIC-SUBST (one kernel, two disciplines). (a) only showcases and retires nothing. (c), relative consistency proper, needs CIC-TYPING first, and (b)'s fragment is a sub-step of it, so (c) stays the follow-up once CIC-TYPING lands. DESTINATION: inside apps/kernel (a 'linear' module family), not a new apps/sps. UNDO: none needed, since no code moves until SPS-NOTEBOOK-SPLIT starts. Done.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_absorb_map_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-ABSORB-MAP", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:25Z", "regex", "regex 08:2x SOURCE: read-only research by subagent a30fa65e0c5ec60b9 (11-02), recovered verbatim by main at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\erp-report.md. User 11-02 07:46: \"tasks to fully rewrite the erp sample in fiscal, drawing every lesson and technique to write the generic code who tries to use all generated schemas at the same time, with more countries to come\". DOD: every row classed (a) fiscal, (b) lib, (c) compiler regression sample or (d) drop with a reason; fsync/CAS durability goes to (d) pointing at WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB. NEXT STEP: grep the definition families listed in FISCAL-ERP-GENERIC n1.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_absorb_map_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-ABSORB-MAP", 2u32, "2026-11-02T16:24Z", "fiscal", "fiscal 11-02 12:24 ABSORPTION MAP of spiral/apps/compiler/tmp/samples/mega_omniledger_erp_kernel (main.spi 12,080 lines; 43 negative_* packages; all_terminals 77) into fiscal, in the REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB format. Landing: (a) fiscal, (b) lib, (c) compiler regression sample, (d) drop with a reason. Lines are main.spi.\nCONCEPTS (33):\nC1 P2P typestate: 9 unit-nominal states :3-11, GADT erp_op :117, erp_plan with existential middle :167 -> (a) FISCAL-ERP-P2P-TYPESTATE.\nC2 branded ids company/role/period/po/payment :13-30 -> (a) as RUNTIME nominals (:! company_id = string) in FISCAL-ERP-REGIME-INDEX/LEDGER. The sample's one-unit-nominal-per-instance (company_a, po_1001) is (d): static instances don't scale to runtime data (kit lesson: existentials are compile-time only).\nC3 money/quantity :35-36, ordered_partial_quantity :37 -> (b) lib decimal via FISCAL-ERP-MONEY.\nC4 tax_witness :62, erp_p2p_receipt_tax_authority :63 -> (a) the authority's proof (nProt, TFD UUID, SdI, KSeF no.) behind a private constructor, FISCAL-ERP-P2P-TYPESTATE; lifecycle.spi protocol_id is the seed.\nC5 invoice_match :65 (three-way) -> (a) FISCAL-ERP-P2P-TYPESTATE.\nC6 mirror_entry :67, opposed_mirror_pair :69 -> (a) FISCAL-ERP-LEDGER (intercompany).\nC7 settlement_fx_route :92 + ratio certificate :100 (static existential middle currency) -> (b) FISCAL-ERP-MONEY.\nC8 distinct3 :102, approval_quorum :105 -> (a) FISCAL-ERP-P2P-TYPESTATE (approvals as a prototype).\nC9 gaap_projection :113 (ifrs :32 / local_gaap :33) -> (a) FISCAL-ERP-LEDGER.\nC10 type-level naturals nat_zero/succ :228-229, nat_one..eight :231-238, nat_add :239, mul :247, lt :459, runtime_money_nat :283 -> (b) LIB-VEC-FIN (shared with regex's map).\nC11 fx_currency :307, typed_fx_rate :314, erp_rate_* :332-388, fx_rate_product :312 -> (b) FISCAL-ERP-MONEY (ISO 4217 union in lib).\nC12 rounding floor/half-up/half-even/safe-ceiling decisions :471-719 -> (b) lib decimal rounding as an evidence union; the per-regime choice (EN 16931 two decimals, NF-e TDec) is (a) FISCAL-ERP-MONEY.\nC13 existential_* + *_program pairs :830-837, :977-984, :1060-1067, :1135-1142, :1205-1212 -> (c) GADT-DOMAIN-STRESS-SAMPLES (existential program shape).\nC14 debit/credit/posting/balanced journal :938-944, signed scaled :1009-1019, minor_unit_scale :1011 -> (a) FISCAL-ERP-LEDGER (law: journal balances, totals = BT-112/BT-110).\nC15 entity-currency ledger/statement :1110-1212 -> (a) FISCAL-ERP-LEDGER.\nC16 statement commands fresh/applied :1271-1274, stream positions :1294-1389 -> (a) FISCAL-ERP-EVENT-LOG (stream-position GADT).\nC17 payload hash, identity collision, event-store decision :1401-1476 -> (a) FISCAL-ERP-EVENT-LOG (duplicate/collision evidence union).\nC18 checksummed frame/log/validation :1634-1721 -> (b) LIB-DURABLE-APPEND.\nC19 raw byte stream-position decode :2075-2277 -> (d): fiscal decodes through lib xml/json, never raw bytes.\nC20 CAS writer races two/three/recursive/stale :2410-2960 -> (d) WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB (single-writer outbox in fiscal).\nC21 durable commit phases prepared/data-synced/marker-synced :3423-3492 -> (b) LIB-DURABLE-APPEND (child of WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB).\nC22 closed history/facts/observations :3579-3860 -> (a) FISCAL-ERP-EVENT-LOG (proof an authority event is already in history).\nC23 proven retry request/result :3967-3982 -> (a) FISCAL-ERP-EVENT-LOG (idempotent resubmission with the same key: SEFAZ/SAT/SdI resend).\nC24 history enumeration/index/identity query/membership :4181-4658 -> (a) FISCAL-ERP-EVENT-LOG.\nC25 p2p unit event/store/outbox + commit tree :6008-6117 -> (a) FISCAL-ERP-EVENT-LOG (outbox).\nC26 per-step typed decode authorities :6660-8974 -> (a) XSD-DECODE-RESULT + XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES (decode returns a typed authority, never a raw payload).\nC27 payload/outbox message sequences :9145-9149 -> (a) FISCAL-ERP-EVENT-LOG.\nC28 reopened/recursive/external-crash/WAL recovery :9372-10674 -> (d) WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB (crash recovery is physical durability).\nC29 fence owner/lock/takeover/stale fence :10812-10944 -> (d) WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB (multi-writer fencing).\nC30 cross-process/multiprocess fenced commits, physical owner lineage :11020-11389 -> (d) WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB.\nC31 competing/atomic successor store+outbox, WAL recovery receipts :11666-12009 -> (d) WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB.\nC32 mega_runtime_fail :1 and 548 !!!! intrinsics, /bin/sh sync macros -> (d): lib wrappers only.\nC33 no prototypes, every authority/witness constructor forgeable -> (a) cross-cutting rule for every FISCAL-ERP-* item: prototypes per behaviour, private constructors for authorities.\nNEGATIVES (43), as `fails \"Unification failure\"` blocks beside the code, never negative_ packages:\n(a) 26: P2P-TYPESTATE 7 (erp_step_detached_result, unit_event_multistep_plan, reapply, p2p_two_event_wrong_final_stage, p2p_three_event_skipped_middle, p2p_commit_tree_skipped_middle, p2p_unit_commit_cross_stage); LEDGER 1 (net_intercompany_detached_mirrors); XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES 1 (event_payload_codec_cross_family: a codec of one family must not decode another's payload); EVENT-LOG 13 (p2p_three_event_wrong_version, p2p_three_event_wrong_version_sum, p2p_four_event_wrong_version, p2p_outbox_detached_message, p2p_unit_outbox_detached_message, equal_hash_collision, recorded_hash_changed_caller_collision, top_collision_wrong_identity, top_membership_wrong_identity, closed_fact_input_wrong_history, fact_derived_observation_cross_outcome, specialized_observation_wrong_history, unified_evidence_observation_wrong_history); plus 4 counted under (d) below.\n(c) 5 -> GADT-DOMAIN-STRESS-SAMPLES: four_owner_lineage_cannot_force_nat_two, three_owner_lineage_cannot_force_nat_four, two_owner_lineage_cannot_force_nat_three, physical_lineage_existential_wrong_fixed_depth, physical_selection_cannot_force_fixed_depth (type-level nat vs existential depth).\n(d) 16 -> WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB (durability): direct_marker_sync, external_crash_recovery_receipt_version_mismatch, recursive_payload_outbox_version_mismatch, recursive_recovery_receipt_version_mismatch, recursive_wal_recovery_receipt_version_mismatch, competing_successor_fence_wrong_after, cross_process_fence_restart_wrong_after, multiprocess_fenced_commit_wrong_endpoint, multiprocess_fenced_physical_append_wrong_endpoint, physical_owner_payload_not_fence_scalar, recoverable_fenced_lock_receipt_owner_mismatch, three_owner_fenced_lock_receipt_fence_mismatch, three_owner_fenced_lock_receipt_stale_b_source_mismatch, recursive_takeover_program_wrong_endpoint, three_owner_physical_takeover_authority_wrong_endpoint, two_takeover_program_wrong_endpoint.\nTotal 22 (a) + 5 (c) + 16 (d) = 43.\nTERMINALS (77, not 78): (a) 42 = step terminals 20 (receive 4, close 3, net 3, reserve 3, collect 2, issue 2, match 2, settle 1) + erp_p2p flow/outbox 6 -> P2P-TYPESTATE test blocks; typed_fx event-store 16 -> EVENT-LOG tests. (b) 2 = typed_fx_determined_rounding_receipt_program, typed_usd_eur_determined_tie_rounding -> FISCAL-ERP-MONEY. (d) 33 = typed_fx durability 19 + erp_p2p durability 14 -> WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB.\nCOUNTS: concepts 33 = (a) 19 rows, (b) 6, (c) 1, (d) 8 (C2's per-instance half included). About 60% of the sample (durability, C18-C21 and C28-C31) is NOT fiscal's, as the 11-02 report estimated. Every (a)/(b)/(c) row names an existing item, which is OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE's parity gate. CORRECTION (same author, same minute): the NEGATIVES (a) header should read \"(a) 22\" (P2P-TYPESTATE 7 + LEDGER 1 + XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES 1 + EVENT-LOG 13). The phrase \"26 ... plus 4 counted under (d) below\" is wrong; the total line 22 (a) + 5 (c) + 16 (d) = 43 is right.")
inl note_of_gleam_ffi_per_function_1 () = Note ("GLEAM-FFI-PER-FUNCTION", 1u32, "2026-11-02T13:15Z", "main", "main 11-02 (user: \"is this gleam array ffi necessary for all outputs? can it get super smart in only emitting when used? can all backends get that? prioritize\"). MEASURED in spiral_compiler.fs: file-level gating already exists (type GleamFfi = NoGleamFfi | GleamStorageFfi at :17801; a module that touches no array or ref gets no sidecar, :35253-35255). Not per-use: one array or ref op emits all 6 exports (array_new/get/set, ref_new/get/set) in BOTH _ffi.erl and _ffi.mjs (:17803-17807). Other backends: Wasm and the Gleam prelude already emit per use (AGENTS.md), and UnusedGlobals.prune drops unreferenced single-item globals on every backend. DoD: (1) the sidecar holds only the functions the module calls; (2) .mjs only when the project targets JavaScript (or keep both, but trimmed); (3) one census row per backend: prelude bytes emitted vs called, for Zig/Lua/C/Rust/Kotlin/Swift/Python; (4) no residual changes except dropped dead helpers. PRIORITY P2: the sidecar is ~25 lines, so this is mostly hygiene and JS-target correctness, below GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX and the linked-units work.")
inl note_of_gleam_ffi_per_function_2 () = Note ("GLEAM-FFI-PER-FUNCTION", 2u32, "2026-11-02T17:19Z", "main", "main 11-02 13:2x MEASURED in the repos: 46 Gleam outputs (x, apps/cells, tibia; build dirs excluded) carry 0 _ffi.erl / _ffi.mjs sidecars, so none of them uses arrays or refs and the existing file-level gating (NoGleamFfi) already emits nothing for all of them. The all-6-functions-in-both-targets cost only hits a future module that uses one array or ref op. Confirms P2: worth doing before array-heavy Gleam code (e.g. a DFA table on Gleam) lands, not before.")
inl note_of_gleam_ffi_per_function_3 () = Note ("GLEAM-FFI-PER-FUNCTION", 3u32, "2026-11-02T19:05Z", "compiler", "11-02 15:10 compiler: PROGRAM DRAFTED: drafts GLEAM-FFI-PER-FUNCTION\\1-ffi-per-group.kitdo (4 replacements, dry-applied on live C9CF9F36 and stacked with MODULE-TYPE-NAMESPACE\\1). GleamFfi now carries arrays/refs flags (GleamStorageFfi of arrays * refs), set separately by spiralArrays and spiralRefs; the .erl export list and bodies, and the .mjs exports, hold only the groups the program uses. Group granularity, not per function: each group's Gleam declaration references all three of its externals, so emitting fewer would break the Gleam build. With both groups in use the output is byte-identical to today's (same strings, same order and separators), so existing Gleam residuals with arrays and refs do not change. PROOF PLAN (node): the Gleam matrix list, comparing the sidecar text and native rows; expect array-only programs to lose the ref functions and nothing else to change. Wasm and the Gleam prelude already emit per use, and UnusedGlobals.prune covers globals on all backends.")
inl note_of_gleam_ffi_per_function_4 () = Note ("GLEAM-FFI-PER-FUNCTION", 4u32, "2026-11-02T21:06Z", "compiler", "11-02 16:30 compiler: PROVEN and HANDED TO MAIN in pack18 (core R2R 8960CAB701FEF46E). Node Gleam native A/B on a fixed harness: 441 rows, 0 differing cells (compile, native, exit, stdout, residual); sidecars: 12 byte-identical (both groups), 110 shrunk to their one group, 0 other. The FIRST A/B showed 39 rows exit 0 -> 1. That was a harness assumption: the native tier batches every Gleam row into one project and deduped same-named sidecars (main_ffi.*) by name, which only worked while all were identical. test.ps1:939 now keeps the largest copy per name (each group sidecar is a subset of the full one; a third, independent group would need a real union). Also: the first build failed FS3373 (a string literal inside an interpolation hole) because a dry-apply only checks anchors; fixed with a let binding.")
inl note_of_gleam_ffi_per_function_5 () = Note ("GLEAM-FFI-PER-FUNCTION", 5u32, "2026-11-02T21:19Z", "compiler", "11-02 17:20 compiler: DONE. pack18 is installed on all three machines (17:16): Gleam sidecars carry only the storage groups a program uses (110 of 122 sample sidecars shrank). The harness fix (test.ps1:939) is in main's commit guide.")
inl note_of_lib_split_review_1 () = Note ("LIB-SPLIT-REVIEW", 1u32, "2026-11-02T13:16Z", "main", "main 11-02: user directive relayed by resilience 08:11: \"the user is worried the split REGRESSED rather than improved. Reread the exported conversation on what was deliberated about lib splitting (the m-postfix renames were good; the chat suggested more abrupt changes). Compare against what actually landed.\" Landed so far: the :: respell (98 files, 11-01 14:53); R1a am'/sm'/optionm' prototypes/operators and par' renames (19:54); R1b+R2 mapm -> map and rust/ flattened into 6 flat modules (22:01); R3 dictm -> dict (11-02 00:41). Undo dirs exist for each in spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo. DoD: a table \"deliberated vs landed vs measured\" (consumer census, module count, import graph depth, lib_sweep pass counts before/after), a verdict per landed step (keep / revert / finish), and the blocked steps (am'/listm'/optionm'/resultm on MODULE-TYPE-NAMESPACE, spir merges on SINGLE-SPI-EXTENSION) re-justified or dropped. NOTE: LIB-RESHAPE itself reads 0% Planned although three rounds landed; its status was lost (agile-status-lost-updates).")
inl note_of_lib_split_review_2 () = Note ("LIB-SPLIT-REVIEW", 2u32, "2026-11-02T16:41Z", "main", "main 11-02 REVIEW DONE (user worry: \"the split REGRESSED rather than improved\"). SOURCE: the deliberation is artifact compass_artifact_wf-d05f9cdd (kit\\drafts\\regex\\BRZOZOWSKI-PRODUCT\\share-extract\\extract\\artifacts), section 4 \"Biblioteca\" (layers, the m-suffix root cause, the full module map).\nVERDICT: no regression in correctness: every land closed green, consumers unchanged in behaviour. But the reshape took the MILD path the chat warned against, so it is incomplete and adds churn.\nDELIBERATED vs LANDED (measured 11-02):\n(1) m-suffix ROOT FIX. Chat: types in UpperCamelCase (List, Option) so modules can be plain list/option, which needs type/value namespace separation in the compiler. Landed: nothing; am', listm', optionm', resultm and sm' still exist (blocked on MODULE-TYPE-NAMESPACE). This was the main point and is untouched.\n(2) MERGES. Chat: am'+am'_prototypes -> array, optionm'+operators -> option, sm'+sm'_operators+sm'_prototypes+sm'_real -> text, all as ONE module each. Landed R1a: RENAMES to interim names (array_prototypes, text_prototypes, option_operators; sm'_operators unchanged), so every consumer gets edited twice (once now, once at the merge).\n(3) dictm + mapm. Chat: merge into std/map, splitting hash_map off by semantics. Landed: two modules, map AND dict, side by side, with no semantic decision.\n(4) rust/. Chat: host/rust (a folder). Landed: flattened into 6 top-level files. That is consistent with the user's later FLAT rule, so it's correct for us.\n(5) Drawers. Chat: delete base, common, util, convert (redistribute each fn to its owner; ratchet to 0). Landed: none; base 879 lines, common 266, util 89, convert 550.\n(6) Ecosystem out of std. Chat: json, xml/xpath/xsd, iggy, routes, oauth, near, leptos as separate packages. Landed: all still in lib (13 modules). The FLAT rule rules out folders, but not separate packages.\n(7) Kept as the chat wanted: the `::` respell; dropping the m from mapm/dictm.\nDECISIONS (rule: the user's flat rule is fixed; technical sequencing is ours):\n- KEEP every landed step (no revert: reverting adds a third consumer edit).\n- NEXT, in order: (a) raise MODULE-TYPE-NAMESPACE, because it unlocks (1) and (2) in one consumer edit; do the R1a merges AT that rename, not before. (b) Decide map vs dict by semantics (one immutable map; a hash map only if dict is mutable/hashed) and merge. (c) A drawer ratchet: base/common/util/convert lines may only go down, each fn moves to its owner module. (d) Ecosystem packages: flat files stay, but a manifest tier tag (core/std/os/host/ecosystem) so dependency detectors and the user see the layers without folders. (e) physics -> samples after the literate state (PHYSICS-OUT-OF-LIB).")
inl note_of_comment_heal_1102_1 () = Note ("COMMENT-HEAL-1102", 1u32, "2026-11-02T13:16Z", "main", "main 11-02 (user: \"we still have junk comments spread out like those repeating the file name at the top, see if we find similar stuff\"). MEASURED across 13 repos: classic file-name headers (// foo.rs, # foo.ps1) 1 (i574n.github); generated outputs 0 (none of 1,012 generated .rs open with a source comment); .spi whose first content line is `/// # <own file name>`: 10, all in spiral lib (decide with Cells: if the notebook title comes from the file name, drop them). Hand comment lines (// in .spi, # in .ps1, not doc/directive): i574n.github 57/10 files (most in resilience's new scripts, e.g. claude-boost-watcher.ps1, and profile-mirror-if-due.ps1), spiral 43/9, kit 5/3, dice 5/2, tibia 2/1, x/fiscal/regex/alphabet/html 0. Also done 11-02: repo descriptions on GitHub dropped the redundant \"written in Spiral\" (fiscal, html, regex), and 3 markdown copies (x client README title, kit AGENTS.md, tibia README).")
inl note_of_comment_heal_1102_2 () = Note ("COMMENT-HEAL-1102", 2u32, "2026-11-02T16:01Z", "main", "main 11-02 SCOPE WIDENED + raised to P1 (user: \"the ps1 files are coming full of comments. don't we have a rule that code should be self explanatory somewhere? clean up all useless comments\"). Yes, the rule exists: memory no-comments-self-explanatory (no comments; names and structure explain the code). MEASURED in tracked .ps1 (# lines, not #requires/#!): i574n.github 67 lines in 12 files (worst scripts/remote.ps1 18, which is main's own; then resilience's new scripts), spiral 35 in 7 (worst apps/compiler/tmp/samples/mega_brzozowski_derivatives/bench.ps1 19), dotfiles 9 in 4, dice 5 in 2, tibia 2, polyglot 1, currency_converter 1; kit/x/fiscal/regex/html 0. The fc1943s dump and fork repos are out of scope. Plus the .spi side from n1 (10 lib files headed by their own name, hand // lines). DoD: each comment is either deleted (a better name or a split function says it) or moved to the backlog item it belongs to; then a kit standards ratchet counts comment lines per language per repo and only lets them go down. Scanner: drafts\\i574n.github\\GROOM-1102-MAIN\\repo-hygiene.ps1. Owners: each lane its repo; main does i574n.github and spiral/lib.")
inl note_of_comment_heal_1102_3 () = Note ("COMMENT-HEAL-1102", 3u32, "2026-11-02T16:03Z", "main", "main 11-02: removed the 18 comment lines from i574n.github/scripts/remote.ps1. Their facts already live in memory (kit2-lane-remote-offload: offload scope, read-only jobs, fetch not git; node-stale-compiler-dll: the L6 core guard; unlink-mirror-junctions-first: mirrors link deps/ read-only). The removed text, verbatim, for the record:\n# remote.ps1 <machine> run|job|status|sync|fetch - drive a remote kit worker node over ssh.\n# Machines: ~/.config/remote-machines.json. Transport is ssh (+ Tailscale fallback);\n# iggy is parked (unix-only fd hand-off). Internal git on the node is fine (the user\n# owns git only on this review box); the bring-back to this box is non-git (fetch).\n#\n# Offload scope (kit2): only READ-ONLY jobs - compiles, tests, reviews. Pull results\n# to scratch/job folders with `fetch`, never back into a repo tree. Jobs that write\n# into the live tree (eoie/kit regen+publish, lib land.ps1, matrix accept) stay on\n# this box: their outputs race with local edits and the sync digest cannot cover that.\n# `sync` proves the node tree matches: per-file sha256 over the changed set, verified\n# equal on both sides (Get-TreeDigest), atop `git checkout --detach HEAD` + clean.\n# L6 guard: a verify/compile offload runs only if the node's SpiralCompilerCore.dll\n# matches the expected core (the review box's for the synced HEAD). A mismatch means a\n# stale installed compiler, whose results are invalid even when the source digest matched.\n# Worktree mirrors share only tracked files; spiral's deps/ holds untracked\n# dependency clones (The-Spiral-Language, polyglot) that |core- resolution needs\n# and `git clean` strips each sync. After the clean, link deps/ read-only from the\n# node's shared source so every concurrent mirror resolves |core- (a link, no copy).")
inl note_of_comment_heal_1102_4 () = Note ("COMMENT-HEAL-1102", 4u32, "2026-11-02T16:07Z", "main", "main 11-02: removed 10 comment lines from i574n.github/scripts/node-watch.ps1 (parse ok; the two running watchers were unaffected, since they parsed the script at start). The one non-obvious fact, verbatim: \"node-jobs counts only eoie jobs; remote.ps1-run work (Cells, builds, verifies) is invisible to it, so CPU% is the real utilization signal. IDLE = cpu<IdleCpu, UNDERUTIL = cpu<UnderCpu\". Usage was \"run as a supervised job: kit job start node-watch 3600000 pwsh -NoProfile -File node-watch.ps1\". The rest of i574n.github goes to its owners: resilience (claude-boost-watcher 3, config-baseline 7, orphan-reaper 6, profile-mirror 9, profile-mirror-if-due 2, register-scheduled-tasks 1, upkeep-tick 2, wsl-policy 5, node-disk-cleanup 2) and x-dumps (linux-worker 2).")
inl note_of_comment_heal_1102_5 () = Note ("COMMENT-HEAL-1102", 5u32, "2026-11-02T16:14Z", "compiler", "11-02 12:40 compiler: apps/compiler scripts healed (unstaged; parse-checked, 0 errors each). make-corelib.ps1: help block (9 lines) and 2 notes removed. upstream.ps1: help block (21 lines) removed. env.ps1: 1. alias-count-check.ps1: 4-line header and 2 inline param notes. test-rust-exports.ps1 needs nothing: its `#[test]` is a Rust attribute inside a here-string, not a comment. test.ps1 (4 lines) follows once the running gadt5 A/B releases it; its comments may sit inside native-memo-keyed blocks, so the memo will rerun those backends once. FACTS MOVED HERE FROM THE COMMENTS: (1) make-corelib.ps1 writes runtime/corelib.cuh = upstream corelib.cuh (hcc @ 0cb0fda0) plus the CPU-host deltas; input is `git -C <fork> show \"0cb0fda0:The Spiral Language 2/corelib.cuh\"`; the delta patch goes to stdout. Upstream's dynamic_array_base::operator[] asserts `i < this->length`, a member it lacks (compile error once indexed); the fix uses max_length. Upstream's file ends without a newline; ours ends with one. (2) upstream.ps1 status|import|export <fork> refs: a `/// ## Name` section maps to `The Spiral Language 2/Name.fs` (SignalRSupervisor -> Supervisor.fs); sections without a file are i574n additions. Edits travel as normalized-line patches (blank lines, `/// ###` headings, `#!import` lines and module headers ignored), using difflib.SequenceMatcher's algorithm ported exactly; a line the target changed itself is a reported conflict. (3) env.ps1: the `lua` slot must be Scoop lua51 5.1.5 (the WoW dialect); lua54 is a side command. (4) alias-count-check.ps1 (HOPACSOTA-P2 negative gate): FFI/type-alias declarations must occur the same number of times in the parallel .fsx output as in single-flight's (multiset equal); GREEN = 0 diffs.")
inl note_of_comment_heal_1102_6 () = Note ("COMMENT-HEAL-1102", 6u32, "2026-11-02T16:14Z", "resilience", "11-02 12:1x resilience (autonomous run): started. New scripts written comment-free from the start: profile-mirror-monitor.ps1, memory-integrity-sweep.ps1. REMAINING to strip (main's list, 37 lines): profile-mirror 9, config-baseline 7, orphan-reaper 6, wsl-policy 5, claude-boost-watcher 3, profile-mirror-if-due 2, upkeep-tick 2, node-disk-cleanup 2, register-scheduled-tasks 1; also tools/claude-boost-native/Program.cs has a header+inline block. Non-obvious facts already preserved in memories node-upkeep-scripts + claude-code-git-bash-path + the item notes, so comments can be deleted outright. Will clean + parse+smoke each across the run's iterations.")
inl note_of_comment_heal_1102_7 () = Note ("COMMENT-HEAL-1102", 7u32, "2026-11-02T16:23Z", "resilience", "11-02 12:2x resilience: COMMENT-HEAL DONE for all resilience scripts. Stripped via the PSParser tokenizer (keeps #requires, write parse-gated): profile-mirror 9, config-baseline 7, orphan-reaper 5, wsl-policy 4, claude-boost-watcher 3, profile-mirror-if-due 2, register-scheduled-tasks 1, plus upkeep-tick 2 + node-disk-cleanup 2 by hand; the two new scripts (profile-mirror-monitor, memory-integrity-sweep) were written comment-free; tools/claude-boost-native/Program.cs also comment-free (source only, no rebuild - running exe unaffected). Parse-checked all; SMOKED orphan-reaper -DryRun, wsl-policy Block, config-baseline Check, + the monitor + sweep - all run clean. Non-obvious rationale preserved in memories node-upkeep-scripts/claude-code-git-bash-path + the CLAUDE-TREE-PRIORITY-BOOST/PROFILE-MIRROR-SILENT-FAIL notes. profile-mirror.ps1 was stripped atomically (read+strip+parse+write in one pass) to dodge the concurrent edit.")
inl note_of_comment_heal_1102_8 () = Note ("COMMENT-HEAL-1102", 8u32, "2026-11-02T16:48Z", "compiler", "11-02 12:55 compiler: test.ps1 done too (4 lines, parse-checked). Facts moved here: (1) Invoke-Native returns the exit code even when stdout/stderr stay open 15 s after exit, because a child (mingw gcc) can hold the redirected pipes; dropping the code turned finished compiles into build-fail. (2) cider's interpret path writes the memory dump to stdout and ignores -o. (3) The runner sets SetErrorMode(0x8003) before native children, or abort() waits on WerFault and a 30 s timeout looks like a missed exit 3. Native-memo keys of the edited blocks change, so those rows rerun once. Compiler lane total: 6 scripts, 41 comment lines removed, 0 left (mega_brzozowski bench.ps1 skipped, per main).")
inl note_of_comment_heal_1102_9 () = Note ("COMMENT-HEAL-1102", 9u32, "2026-11-02T20:24Z", "main", "main 11-02 16:3x the lib \"/// # <own name>\" headings are RESOLVED, nothing to remove. Cells takes the page <title> from the file name (apps/cells/lib/spiral/cells/html.ex:82), so the heading only adds a visible H1. But only 4 headed files remain (cli_args, json, routes, sm'; 10 this morning, so another lane cleaned the rest), and all 4 have a _real.spir pair, where headings structure the .spi/.spir interleave (document_test \"a _real.spir interleaves with its .spi by heading\"). They are structural, not junk: keep. Remaining comment work is the lanes' own .ps1 lists (resilience 37, compiler 16; x-dumps done; main's 28 done).")
inl note_of_comment_heal_1102_10 () = Note ("COMMENT-HEAL-1102", 10u32, "2026-11-03T19:43Z", "main", "main 11-03 15:4x RECOUNT i574n.github (tracked + untracked .ps1/.spi, backlog excluded; '#' lines in .ps1 except #requires/#region, '//' lines in .spi): 57 -> 1, the '<# ... #>' header of scripts/linux-worker.ps1 (x-dumps' K3S-EVERYWHERE script; it points to the backlog, so it could simply go, owner's call). main's repos are clean; the lib headings stay as structural (n1). Remaining: the lanes' own .ps1 lists (resilience 37, compiler 16 at n1). Progress 0 -> 80.")
inl note_of_comment_heal_1102_11 () = Note ("COMMENT-HEAL-1102", 11u32, "2026-11-04T05:45Z", "main", "11-04 01:4x main RECOUNT across 11 repos, comment tokens by the PowerShell parser over tracked .ps1 (#requires excluded): 29 left. 19 are spiral apps/compiler/tmp/samples/mega_brzozowski_derivatives/bench.ps1 (skipped by decision, n8); 3 are dice/contract/build.ps1, a TAGGED TODO (RUST-NIGHTLY-EVERYWHERE) that kit agile todos tracks by design, so it stays; 7 belong to owners and were notified: resilience heartbeat-staleness-guard.ps1 4 (new code), tibia tibia-mariadb-dump.ps1 2, x-dumps linux-worker.ps1 1. kit, x, fiscal, regex, html, alphabet and blog: 0.")
inl note_of_comment_heal_1102_12 () = Note ("COMMENT-HEAL-1102", 12u32, "2026-11-04T11:27Z", "main", "11-04 07:4x main RECOUNT of the 3 owner-notified scripts (PowerShell parser comment tokens, #requires excluded): heartbeat-staleness-guard.ps1 0, linux-worker.ps1 0, tibia-mariadb-dump.ps1 0. All the owners healed theirs. What remains by decision: mega_brzozowski_derivatives/bench.ps1 19 (sample, n8) and dice/contract/build.ps1 3 (tagged TODO tracked by kit agile todos). Nothing actionable is left.")
inl note_of_profile_mirror_silent_fail_1 () = Note ("PROFILE-MIRROR-SILENT-FAIL", 1u32, "2026-11-02T13:16Z", "main", "main 11-02 08:1x, found while recovering from main's 07:55 crash. The node's newest archive was profile-mirror-20261101-132405.tgz although the scheduled task ran every 15 min with result 0. CAUSE: profile-mirror.ps1:105 read `-o ServerAliveCountMax=4$route` (no space), so ssh got ServerAliveCountMax=4laptop and no host; every route failed (\"no route reached the node (laptop, laptop-ts, laptop-ip)\") from the 11-01 keepalive edit on. FIXED by main (one space, unstaged, i574n.github). It stayed invisible because profile-mirror-if-due.ps1 starts the mirror detached and exits 0, and profile-mirror.last.log is overwritten each run. DoD: (1) a manual run lands a verified archive on the node (main started one 08:1x); (2) the task or a status probe fails loudly when the newest node archive is older than 2x the interval (status-files-need-age); (3) remote.ps1 node status prints the newest archive's age; (4) the same \"no space before $var\" bug is grepped across scripts (main found 0 other `CountMax=\\d+\\$` sites). Note: resilience's 11-02 scripts (orphan-reaper.ps1, wsl-policy.ps1, claude-boost-watcher.ps1) are new .ps1 tools in a repo, against spiral-first-tooling; groom their port to kit commands.")
inl note_of_profile_mirror_silent_fail_2 () = Note ("PROFILE-MIRROR-SILENT-FAIL", 2u32, "2026-11-02T13:24Z", "main", "main 11-02 08:5x CORRECTION to n1: point (4) is wrong. main's grep DID flag a second site, profile-mirror.ps1:137 (the node-verify ssh, '=4$reached'), but main filed n1 without reading that output. resilience fixed :137 (unstaged), so all three ssh/scp lines are spaced now. main's 08:1x manual run predates that fix and fails at verify, so a re-run follows. Lesson (read-outputs-after-the-writer): never state a check's result before reading its output. resilience owns this item; its guard design is an INDEPENDENT node-side newest-archive-age monitor, never self-reported by the mirror.")
inl note_of_profile_mirror_silent_fail_3 () = Note ("PROFILE-MIRROR-SILENT-FAIL", 3u32, "2026-11-02T13:51Z", "main", "main 11-02 09:5x: the 08:40 snapshot is VERIFIED on the node by hand: profile-mirror-20261102-084014.tgz, 398307413 B / 30132 tar entries on both sides (scp landed it at 09:47; only the script's own verify step failed, because :137 was still broken during that run). So the 19 h gap is closed through 08:40. I left the schedule un-marked on purpose, so the next 15-min task runs a full mirror with all three lines fixed; that run is the end-to-end proof for DoD (1).")
inl note_of_profile_mirror_silent_fail_4 () = Note ("PROFILE-MIRROR-SILENT-FAIL", 4u32, "2026-11-02T15:07Z", "resilience", "11-02 resilience (star-exchange groom): DESIGN locked. Root cause of the 19h silent death = my 11-02 keepalive edit ServerAliveCountMax=4$route (no space) -> ssh saw '4laptop', no host; invisible because if-due launches detached + exits 0 + overwrites .last.log each run (reinforced by main #2, fiscal 'validate from outside', x 'baseline/health from outside'). FIX must NOT be self-reported: an INDEPENDENT node-side monitor reads the newest profile-mirror-*.tgz mtime ON THE NODE and FAILS LOUDLY (story note + nonzero exit) when age > 2x the 15min interval; show that age in node status. The mirror's own status.txt is insufficient - the failure happened BEFORE the status-writing step. Scheduled at Priority 5 (BelowNormal starves on the saturated box - my upkeep task crawled 130s vs 10s). DoD: alarms on a stale newest-archive regardless of the mirror's exit code; test by pointing it at a frozen dir.")
inl note_of_profile_mirror_silent_fail_5 () = Note ("PROFILE-MIRROR-SILENT-FAIL", 5u32, "2026-11-02T16:05Z", "resilience", "11-02 12:0x resilience: DELIVERED the independent monitor (scripts/profile-mirror-monitor.ps1, scheduled PT30M Priority 5). It reads the newest profile-mirror-*.tgz mtime ON THE NODE (not the self-reported status file) and fails loudly on OK->stale transition. VALIDATED: it immediately caught a REAL failure - newest node archive was 08:40, 133min stale. Root is NOT the =4$route bug (fixed) - the run stages but the 1.33GB payload (session transcripts in .claude/projects) is too slow over the saturated link to complete within the ~50min cadence, so the mirror falls behind. That slowness is MIRROR-TRANSFER-COST (incremental mirror). Detection half = DONE; the keep-up fix lives in MIRROR-TRANSFER-COST.")
inl note_of_profile_mirror_silent_fail_6 () = Note ("PROFILE-MIRROR-SILENT-FAIL", 6u32, "2026-11-02T17:17Z", "resilience", "11-02 13:1x resilience FIXED the mirror hang-forever bug (main diagnosed: the makeDir's explicit pwsh -EncodedCommand could not cold-start on the 99%-CPU node, hung 1h; ServerAlive only kills a DEAD connection, not a slow-to-START remote command). profile-mirror.ps1 fixes: (1) Invoke-Bounded = hard wall-clock timeout (Start-Process + WaitForExit(ms) + kill the ssh tree) on EVERY ssh/scp (makeDir 15s, scp 600s, verify 90s); (2) makeDir via cmd /c if not exist mkdir not remote pwsh - confirmed the node ssh shell runs cmd/c fast; (3) verify+retention now BEST-EFFORT: a tgz landed via scp is SUCCESS (still emits sha256 <hash> so if-due marks ran + the monitor sees a fresh archive) even when the saturated node cannot run the pwsh retention, instead of throwing and discarding a landed backup. Net: the mirror fail-fasts (bounded) or lands, never hangs. Parse OK; test run bqfj8m91c in flight. Deferred (main fix 3): europa fallback when the node is saturated (needs Linux-path handling).")
inl note_of_profile_mirror_silent_fail_7 () = Note ("PROFILE-MIRROR-SILENT-FAIL", 7u32, "2026-11-02T18:52Z", "resilience", "11-02 14:4x resilience: COMPLETE, all DoD proven. (1) end-to-end: full 256MB profile-mirror-20261102-142151.tgz on laptop node 14:36 + critical-20261102-144042.tar 14:40, 15min cadence (14:10/14:25/14:40); task result 0x0 only on scp success (critical-mirror.ps1:57). (2) independent node-side monitor profile-mirror-monitor.ps1 PT30M fails loudly OK->stale, validated vs real staleness. (3) remote.ps1 node status now prints archive age (verified: node mirror 2026-11-02 14:36 16min-ago 256MB). (4) =N$var bug fixed on all 3 ssh/scp lines, 0 other sites. Laptop node at 100pct CPU + free-disk 10GB (low, trending) yet mirror lands under load via Invoke-Bounded. Residual transfer-cost (incremental) tracked in MIRROR-TRANSFER-COST.")
inl note_of_profile_mirror_silent_fail_8 () = Note ("PROFILE-MIRROR-SILENT-FAIL", 8u32, "2026-11-02T19:21Z", "resilience", "11-02 15:2x resilience: hardened the mirror monitor after heartbeat-staleness-guard caught it hung. profile-mirror-monitor.ps1 rewritten: Invoke-Bounded (hard wall-clock timeout + kill ssh tree) + CMD-NATIVE newest-archive via `cmd /c dir /b /o-d`, age parsed from the filename stamp on the box (no node pwsh cold-start, no clock-skew). Ran 4s (was hanging forever), OK via laptop. Also found+fixed the SAME unbounded-remote-pwsh bug in node-utilization-monitor.ps1 (wifi CPU via node powershell -EncodedCommand) - now Invoke-Bounded, timeout->-1 (node reads unknown=not-idle, correct). profile-mirror.ps1 verify was already bounded. All node-touching watchers now hang-proof. Unstaged.")
inl note_of_profile_mirror_silent_fail_9 () = Note ("PROFILE-MIRROR-SILENT-FAIL", 9u32, "2026-11-03T04:06Z", "resilience", "monitor ALARM (OK->bad transition): profile-mirror-monitor 2026-11-03 00:06 UNREACHABLE (node down all routes)")
