inl note_of_granular_split_xsd_emit_9 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XSD-EMIT", 9u32, "2026-11-04T11:58Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 07:58 fiscal: step (6) (draft 77093E1D): the two arm walks' shared naming moved out -- group_identity owner items (group name + field) and occurs_once () (the { min = 1; max = Bounded 1 } literal) -- and each walk binds its witnessed part once. Rule-(2) bodies: repeated_group_walk 484 -> 329, choice_content_walk 366 -> 312 (content_walk 469, element_content_walk 204). europa pack27: --check exit 0, format clean. The remaining overage is the constructor of the witnessed part (two prototype calls with five arguments each); identity proof for (5)+(6) queued.")
inl note_of_granular_split_xsd_emit_10 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XSD-EMIT", 10u32, "2026-11-04T12:18Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 08:18 fiscal: steps (7)-(8) in the draft (2CB1BEAB, base refreshed to the decode draft 5B274B48 after its dead staged_of removal): (7) builtin classification -- one builtin_kind_of replaces every builtin local-name string compare (builtin_example, is_calendar_builtin, prefers_builtin_example, positive_example, builtin_white_space, the attribute ID example; recorded on XSD-FACET-TYPES as its first step); (8) staging_prelude split into staging_types_text / staged_read_text / staged_access_text, concatenated in the original order. europa pack27: --check exit 0, format clean. Identity: (1)-(5) proven 0 differing; (6) running; FINAL run queued (fresh decode 5B274B48 reference vs the full draft, all families).")
inl note_of_granular_split_xsd_emit_11 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XSD-EMIT", 11u32, "2026-11-04T12:32Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 08:32 fiscal: FULL SPLIT PROVEN OUTPUT-IDENTICAL (europa pack27, one script, both sides): fresh decode reference (draft 5B274B48) vs the whole split draft (2CB1BEAB, steps 1-8): both compile + rustc exit 0, both generate exit 36 (same as every prior run), units 69 vs 69, differing files 0. Step (6) separately 0 differing. So every split step changes no generated byte in any family. Lands right after the XSD-DECODE-RESULT joint land (its base is that draft); the land is a straight swap of xsd_emit.spi with -BaseHash = the decode draft's hash.")
inl note_of_granular_split_xsd_emit_12 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XSD-EMIT", 12u32, "2026-11-04T13:15Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 09:15 fiscal: proven draft confirmed = 2CB1BEAB (europa split8 bytes identical). Next steps in separate files: (9) pattern_checks (body 1408) -> pattern_check picking coded_pattern / table_pattern (dfa_table_function_text) / regex_pattern via uncoded_pattern; plain_item builder replaces 5 literal PlainItem records (2 in pattern_checks + named-type, emit_choice, shared union); (10) collect_content (1298) -> one-line dispatch to collect_repeated_group / collect_choice / collect_element / collect_inline_element (+ plain referenced_field). Both --check exit 0, format 0; identity runs (regen all 69 units, diff vs the decode reference) queued on europa.")
inl note_of_granular_split_xsd_emit_13 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XSD-EMIT", 13u32, "2026-11-04T13:31Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 09:31 fiscal: steps (11)-(14) drafted, each --check exit 0 + formatter fixed point: (11) dereferenced_in -> collapsed_sequence / collapsed_choice (plain) + referenced_root (group member; fallback passed as the rebuilt 'Element e', so no GADT-refined item crosses a call); (12) choice_cases -> element_case / group_case reusing collected_with (x :: l = append [x] l; append [] l = l); (13) coded_text -> coded_table/parse/print/example_text sections, union_text -> union_parse_text / union_print_text (++# is associative: identical bytes); (14) emit_simple_text -> inherits_base + simple_type_text + plain_item (the 5th PlainItem site), recursive_text -> builds_record / record_constructors. PROOF PLAN CHANGED to save europa (load avg 7.7 on 2 vCPU, shared): each split file contains every earlier step, so one 0-diff identity run of a later file proves all steps below it; the per-step runs (9/10/11) were stopped while still waiting (no heavy step started). Running: split12 (9-12) in rustc now, then split13 (9-13), then split14 (9-14); a diff would be bisected with the earlier files.")
inl note_of_granular_split_xsd_emit_14 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XSD-EMIT", 14u32, "2026-11-04T13:45Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 09:45 fiscal: identity PROVEN (europa pack27, regen of all 69 units vs the decode reference, 0 differing files): split12 (steps 9-12), split13 (9-13), split16 (9-16). Steps (15) module_parts_by -> shared_items / aliased_kinds_items / module_parts_of, witness_children -> witness_walk_lines; (16) split_family -> core_functions_of / family_core_text, versioned_type_text lambdas -> versioned_case_line / versioned_read_line; (17) simple_example -> patterned/unpatterned/searched_example, occurs_part binding -> is_coded_kind guard, emit_enumeration -> coded_enumeration / union_enumeration, units_of_parts -> module_body. split17 (9-17) identity running. Left as-is pending a ruling: constant-text templates (codec_prelude, staged_read_text) and the walk functions with the long trait-constraint header.")
inl note_of_granular_split_xsd_emit_15 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XSD-EMIT", 15u32, "2026-11-04T13:52Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 09:52 fiscal: METRIC CHECK against DONE WHEN (overflow counter <= 10% of top-level defs over 280, tests excluded; my trimmed-char approximation of the counter): decode base 5B274B48 = 431 defs, 85 over (19.7%), largest 1561 -> split18 = 498 defs, 95 over (19.1%), largest 781. The steps so far halved the outliers but barely moved the RATIO: many new helpers landed at 300-400 (coded_pattern 322, table_pattern 349, collect_repeated_group 358, group_case 321). Correction from here: each split must leave EVERY piece under 280, and the next batches target the 280-400 band (about 45 defs must drop below 280 to reach 10%). Identity proven so far: steps 9-17 (split17, 0 differing of 69 units); split18 (attribute_binding / group_members / generate_complements) running. Also: kit's rule (1) text says 'ONE match', so xpath_eval greedy_step was rewritten as a greedy_token classifier + flat ?= dispatch (L13 proving) rather than waiting on the chain ruling.")
inl note_of_granular_split_xsd_emit_16 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XSD-EMIT", 16u32, "2026-11-04T14:17Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 10:17 fiscal: RATIO UNDER 10% in the draft (7FDA3007, split23): 542 top-level non-test defs, 97 flat dispatches, 53 over 280 = 9.8% (decode base was 431 / 81 = 18.8%; largest body 1561 -> 781). Measured with my scratch approximation of the counter: trimmed body chars, kit rule (1) flat dispatch = longest arm + match header, rule (2) headers excluded; NOT kit's exact weight script (no dot defusing), so kit's number may differ by a few defs -- please run the real counter on the draft before closing. Batches (19)-(23) each kept every new piece under 280 (with_pattern, collected_with reuse, choice_case dispatch, dereferenced_parts shared by staged_type_names + module_parts_by, written_and_exampled shared by function_texts + walk_texts_with, own_namespace-style dedups). Identity PROVEN on europa (all 69 units, 0 differing vs the decode reference): split19 (steps 9-19), split20 (9-20), split21 (9-21); split22 + split23 queued. One slip caught by --check on a work copy: definition_name is 'definition_name form' (phantom-typed), fixed before any proof.")
inl note_of_granular_split_xsd_emit_17 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XSD-EMIT", 17u32, "2026-11-04T15:02Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 11:02 fiscal: CORRECTION of note 16 (9.8%): that figure was my scratch approximation. kit's ACTUAL counter (Spiral.Cells.CellBudget.over_budget, default profile, top_level_blocks for the denominator; run on europa's synced Cells, private MIX_BUILD_PATH), test blocks excluded: xsd_emit decode base 145/329 = 44.1%, split draft 7FDA3007 177/432 = 41.0%; live xpath_eval 63/235 = 26.8%; fiscal src: families 56.5, generator 60.0 (granular draft 56.3), canon 28.0, corpus_checks 27.7, generated_runtime 25.0, sunat 22.4, document 17.4, posting 16.7, lifecycle 15.4, p2p 14.3, profiles 11.8, reports 10.9, fiscal_paths 0. Main gap vs my scratch counter: the real weight counts EVERY character incl. leading indentation (mine trimmed it), and the counter does not apply the 11-04 rules (1)/(2). So the split moved the real measure only 44.1 -> 41.0. The draft stays proven output-identical and worth landing (outliers halved, duplication removed), but the ratio target is NOT met.")
inl note_of_granular_split_xsd_emit_18 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XSD-EMIT", 18u32, "2026-11-04T15:07Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 11:07 fiscal: kit RULED (b) at ~11:0x by message: the DoD is the counter WITH rules (1)/(2); signature-only and flat-dispatch overages count as compliant until kit's CellBudget change lands in apps/cells, then re-measure. Ruled measure meanwhile via my draft Spiral.Cells.CellBudgetRuled (kit drafts cells\\CELLBUDGET-RULES, real weights incl. indentation, tests excluded, run on europa): split draft 84/432 = 19.4% (decode base 93/329 = 28.3%). Next: split the 84 that are over on their BODIES, each piece under the limit, targeting ~41 more to reach 10%.")
inl note_of_granular_split_xsd_emit_19 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XSD-EMIT", 19u32, "2026-11-04T15:47Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 11:47 fiscal: UNDER 10% ON THE RULED MEASURE (kit ruling (b)): split draft 502A863C = 47 of 490 non-test blocks over budget = 9.59% (unrounded), measured with Spiral.Cells.CellBudgetRuled (the version kit adopted into apps/cells; real weights incl. indentation, rule (1) flat dispatch, rule (2) header excluded) on europa. Path: decode base 28.3% -> split23 19.4% -> 24: 17.0 -> 25: 15.7 -> 26: 13.9 -> 27: 12.8 -> 28: 11.5 (+ one cell per ':&' member) -> 29: 10.7 -> 30: 10.3 -> 31: 9.59. Every step splits a body that was over (signature-only overages left alone, per kit); notable dedups: sequence_of (shared by group_case + collapsed_sequence), with_codec_instance, mapped_value_text, family_third, root_own. Also fixed a merged block (codec_instances + module_body had no blank line between). Identity PROVEN (all 69 units, 0 differing vs the decode reference): splits 24, 25, 26, 27, 28; split29 and split31 (all steps) queued on europa. The remaining 47 are mostly emitted-text templates and the long trait-constrained walk functions (template ruling still open, GRANULAR-STATS 32). Re-measure with kit's landed 'mix spiral.cell_budget --granular' before closing.")
