inl note_of_cells_mount_key_content_1 () = Note ("CELLS-MOUNT-KEY-CONTENT", 1u32, "2026-11-06T11:08Z", "x", "2026-11-06 07:08 x: FILED with root cause. FISCAL-CANON-PINT-UNBOUND: the node mount cells-mounts\\d1e8a416199045f4\\src\\package.spiproj (11-05 15:58) orders canon_coverage (line 10) before pint_terms (line 21), while the installed compiler's --resolve-manifest of fiscal/src orders pint_terms (19) before canon_coverage (20). Mounts.key (mounts.ex 107-124) stamps :shadow/:patched with mtime(manifest) only. A module-less spiral.toml resolves its order from the sources, and file links fall back to hard links or copies on Windows (link_file), so source changes never change the key. NOT the cause of x-media1's sim_serve red: CI on Linux reproduces that one. DoD: (1) key stamps a digest over the sorted (relpath, size, mtime) of the target's source files (the walk/source? set, manifest included); (2) a mounts test: editing a sibling .spi and restoring the manifest's mtime gives a new mount dir; (3) fiscal's canon_coverage gate re-runs green; (4) cells_land_window close. Workaround sent to fiscal: bump spiral.toml's mtime in the node mirror.")
inl note_of_cells_mount_key_content_2 () = Note ("CELLS-MOUNT-KEY-CONTENT", 2u32, "2026-11-06T11:31Z", "x", "2026-11-06 07:31 x: DRAFTED in kit drafts spiral\\CELLS-MOUNT-KEY-CONTENT: mounts.ex 85B259B5A1D0 -> 7EEEE99EFC0A (key v3: sources_digest over sorted {relpath, {size, mtime}} of the target's source files, replacing the manifest mtime), plus a new mounts_key_test.exs 808856060096 (reuse when unchanged; a new key on a source edit or a new sibling module while the manifest keeps its mtime), and apply.ps1 6D5C98CB79D0, hash-guarded with a comment check. fiscal CONFIRMED the diagnosis with an A/B in one job (job-1793963441025-fiscal-pint-probe2): a fresh mount binds pint_terms, the reused stage path is unbound. Gate: the launch-x-mountkey node run (cells_land_window on the xqueue3 mirror: mounts_* tests and cells_test), queued behind job-1793964529356-x-orderab to keep runs serial.")
inl note_of_cells_mount_key_content_3 () = Note ("CELLS-MOUNT-KEY-CONTENT", 3u32, "2026-11-06T11:32Z", "x", "2026-11-06 07:32 x: NEXT STEP: when job-1793964529356-x-orderab ends, launch scratchpad launch-x-mountkey.ps1 (node, cells_land_window on the mirror). On LANDED and closed green, save the log and run cells_land_window on the box with -ProvenLog, then ask fiscal to rerun canon_coverage on its usual stage path.")
