inl note_of_cells_port_mounts_text_2 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-MOUNTS-TEXT", 2u32, "2026-11-07T18:50Z", "x", "2026-11-07 14:50 x: DRAFTED in the tree (unstaged): new spi/mount_text.spi 005ADA17D032 (patch_first, nested_name, sibling_project, with 3 test blocks each naming ///> gleam), main.spi C3B12F542AF8 (3 exports), package.spiproj (+mount_text), domain.ex wrappers, mounts.ex 51BAA029AE6B: patched/top_level_only/project_for_mount(:siblings) call the domain, and sibling_entries is deleted. :absolute stays Elixir because it needs Path.expand, so it isn't pure text. Oracle: new mount_text_parity_test.exs compares verbatim copies of the old Elixir functions with the domain over every package.spiproj in the spiral repo plus synthetic CRLF/nested/empty cases; existing mounts_* tests are unchanged. Gate pending on the node: job-1794077263416-x-mounts1 (xcells3, pack61 E3F33F3766EE6EDA): compile, parity, mounts_*, full suite.")
inl note_of_cells_port_mounts_text_3 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-MOUNTS-TEXT", 3u32, "2026-11-07T18:51Z", "x", "2026-11-07 14:51 x: DoD: patch_first, nested_name and sibling_project run as Spiral domain exports; mounts.ex keeps only IO plus the :absolute path rewrite; the parity oracle (old Elixir copies vs domain over every repo package.spiproj + synthetic cases) and the existing mounts_* tests pass on the node; landed through cells_land_window, whose Elixir-drift line shows the shrink. Next: read job-1794077263416-x-mounts1, fix any parity diff (e.g. Path.dirname on backslash names), then land.")
inl note_of_cells_port_mounts_text_4 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-MOUNTS-TEXT", 4u32, "2026-11-07T20:05Z", "x-b7595ac3", "2026-11-07 16:05 x: gate x-mounts1 (node xcells3, pack61) failed 6/16. Four were Domain.mount_patch_first passing a tuple to a 3-argument Gleam export (fixed). The repo-manifest parity test timed out walking ** over the mirror (now a walker that skips dot dirs, target, _build, deps, build, tmp). Two synthetic cases hit an oracle quirk: the old regex's trailing \\\\s* swallows the final newline after a rewritten last line; the port keeps it, and a separate test pins that. Re-gate job-1794081764398-x-mounts4 is pending on the node.")
inl note_of_cells_port_mounts_text_5 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-MOUNTS-TEXT", 5u32, "2026-11-08T00:07Z", "x-b7595ac3", "2026-11-07 20:07 x: LANDED on the box (unstaged) in land CELLS-TESTS-ONLY-1107: spi\\mount_text.spi 005ADA17D032 (patch_first, nested_name, sibling_project with 3 gleam tests), main.spi 602BF1D71083 exports, domain.ex C3E75BFA03A8 wrappers, mounts.ex 5E81B597F5AD (patched/top_level_only/sibling project call Domain; sibling_entries and declared_crates deleted), parity test 96950538D681 (old Elixir functions as the oracle over every repo manifest plus CRLF, empty-value and repeated-entry cases; a separate test pins that the port keeps the final newline the regex swallowed). Proof: full gate x-cells-full7 + x-cells-full7f on the node (pack61b), 389/395 with 6 mirror gaps; window x-cells-landwin 41 green; box closed by -ProvenLog byte for byte, undo cells-20261107-200705. DoD met.")
inl note_of_cells_port_result_union_1 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-RESULT-UNION", 1u32, "2026-11-06T11:08Z", "x", "2026-11-06 07:08 x: split from CELLS-PORT-RUNNER-MOUNTS. Pure code with no IO, so it is ready now. Oracle: runner_test cases that read results pass unchanged.")
inl note_of_cells_port_result_union_2 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-RESULT-UNION", 2u32, "2026-11-06T11:56Z", "x", "2026-11-06 07:56 x: SCOPED from the code. The pure parts are result.ex from_outputs/2 (folds the tagged output tuples {:value|:stdout|:stderr|:html, text} into value/stdout/html) and source_blocks.ex parse_rows/1 (the --source-blocks TSV: input, first, header, last_content, last, header_text; header 0 skipped; grouped by input) plus split/2 (header..last line slices). The rest is IO, which stays: the dotnet --source-blocks call and the Kino.Render impl. NEXT STEP (memo C6.1 pattern): a typed Spiral union output = Value | Stdout | Stderr | Html | Other in a new cells spi module, with string exports from_outputs_wire (tag-tab-text rows to value/stdout/html fields) and source_rows_wire (TSV to grouped block rows), and the Elixir callers switched to the domain exports. Oracle: a parity test over the existing runner_test/notebook fixtures, unchanged. It waits for the Cells regression land (CELLS-NOTEBOOK-ORDER-REGRESSION) so both don't touch cells at once.")
inl note_of_cells_port_result_union_3 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-RESULT-UNION", 3u32, "2026-11-06T13:09Z", "x", "2026-11-06 09:09 x: DRAFTED slice 1, from_outputs (kit drafts spiral\\CELLS-PORT-RESULT-UNION). New spi\\run_result.spi DE5DF3F81DEC: a typed output union (ValueOut/StdoutOut/StderrOut/HtmlOut/OtherOut), outputs_from parsing a length-prefixed wire (tag, byte length, colon, text, the same byte units as text::length's byte_size), and the fold rules: values joined with newlines or none, stdout+stderr concatenated, html in order. It has 3 Spiral tests. Exported as result_fields (main.spi 1BB4224F434A, package.spiproj DD2B6E23A222, Domain.result_fields in domain.ex 1DE9210AB289). result.ex 04554E183B0E: from_outputs encodes the outputs, calls the domain and decodes (outputs_wire/fields_of); the Kino.Render impl and the exception modules are unchanged. New result_union_test.exs CCB200E8B493 holds 3 parity tests (mixed outputs with multibyte text, no value, ':' inside text). apply.ps1 2D3F44FF1261 is hash-guarded. NEXT STEP: a node gate after x-cellsfix2b; it rebuilds the Cells domain and runs result_union_test, notebook_test, runner_test and cells_test. Slice 2 (source_blocks parse_rows) follows the same wire pattern.")
inl note_of_cells_port_result_union_4 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-RESULT-UNION", 4u32, "2026-11-06T13:10Z", "x", "DoD: (1) run_result.spi's own tests and result_union_test pass; (2) notebook_test, runner_test and cells_test pass unchanged under the new from_outputs; (3) cells_land_window closes green with -ProvenLog; (4) slice 2 ports source_blocks parse_rows/split to Spiral the same way.")
inl note_of_cells_port_result_union_5 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-RESULT-UNION", 5u32, "2026-11-07T00:35Z", "x", "2026-11-06 20:35 x: first gate RED: x-resultunion1 (job-1794011156979, node, pack57). The land window applied the 6 files and then CLOSE FAILED and undid them (node mirror only, restored from cells-20261106-202617). No test Result line was printed, so mix test never got past the build; the suspect is a compile error in the new spi\\run_result.spi domain module or its main.spi export. Nothing landed on the box. NEXT STEP: rerun with the mix compile output printed, fix the domain build, then gate again. Note: the node is on pack58b 712FA1815A484F1D since 20:27.")
inl note_of_cells_port_result_union_6 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-RESULT-UNION", 6u32, "2026-11-07T00:37Z", "x", "2026-11-06 20:37 x: likely cause of the build red, found by reading: Cells spi modules don't get ++ from a prelude; each defines its own (memo.spi: ':= (++) (left : string) (right : string) : string = left ^^ right'). run_result.spi used ++ without it, an unbound operator. Draft fixed: run_result.spi DE5DF3F81DEC -> 2E5C57A4769C (adds the local (++)). Not yet proven. NEXT STEP: update launch-x-resultunion's hash, rerun pinned to the node's current core with the mix compile output printed, and land on green.")
inl note_of_cells_port_result_union_7 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-RESULT-UNION", 7u32, "2026-11-07T00:48Z", "x", "2026-11-06 20:48 x: slice 1 LANDED on the box (unstaged): new spi\\run_result.spi 2E5C57A4769C (typed output union, length-prefixed wire, fold rules), package.spiproj DD2B6E23A222, main.spi 1BB4224F434A (result_fields export), domain.ex 1DE9210AB289, result.ex 04554E183B0E (from_outputs folds through the Spiral domain), new result_union_test.exs CCB200E8B493. Closed by -ProvenLog from x-resultunion2 (job-1794012073385, node, pack58b 712FA1815A484F1D; result_union, notebook, runner and cells_test: 63 passed), byte-identical; undo cells-20261106-204758. The first gate's red was the missing local (++) (fixed). DoD 1-3 met for slice 1. NEXT STEP: slice 2, source_blocks parse_rows/split.")
inl note_of_cells_port_result_union_8 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-RESULT-UNION", 8u32, "2026-11-07T20:30Z", "x-b7595ac3", "2026-11-07 16:25 x: slice 2 Spiral half drafted (scratchpad result_union2\\source_blocks.spi 65EEE6FB9FB5, not in the tree; the Cells landing gate x-cells-full5 is testing the tree). Finding: span first/last_content are dead (only parse_rows' own test reads them). Every consumer uses header/last/header_text, the same rows memo::spans_of parses. Design: input_rows(tsv, input) returns the 'header TAB last TAB header_text' rows per input; split_blocks(program, rows) returns tagged fields (b header, l line), with the test-header filter (^(test|:#) not followed by a word char) now in Spiral. Elixir after landing: source_blocks run maps inputs through Domain; parse_rows and split go away (a b/l decoder via result.ex's take_field remains); memo.ex reached_program takes the rows directly and @test_header goes; the store tag becomes {:source_rows, rows}, so old entries miss once instead of crashing. Unproven.")
inl note_of_cells_port_result_union_9 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-RESULT-UNION", 9u32, "2026-11-07T21:58Z", "x-b7595ac3", "2026-11-07 18:0x x: slice 2 fully drafted in scratchpad result_union2\\tree (copies of the gated tree; base hashes in base-hashes.txt). New spi\\source_blocks.spi plus package.spiproj (after memo), main.spi (source_input_rows, source_split_blocks exports), domain.ex wrappers, and source_blocks.ex (parse_rows and the @type block removed; split decodes the b/l fields through Result.take_field, now public). memo.ex: the store and key tag :source_blocks becomes :source_rows, so old memo entries miss once instead of crashing; reached_program takes the rows directly; @test_header is removed (Spiral filters tests). memo_test: the parse_rows test now uses Domain.source_input_rows, plus a split test (test blocks dropped, a block past the end has no lines). .ex 1062 -> 1058 (-4). Applies after the current Cells land and main's nightly-pin pass; unproven.")
inl note_of_cells_port_result_union_10 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-RESULT-UNION", 10u32, "2026-11-08T00:21Z", "x-b7595ac3", "2026-11-07 20:21 x: SLICE 2 LANDED on the box (unstaged). Evidence: node window x-slice2-win (job-1794097025855, xcells3, pack61b 65DEE79CF2CF8B9F) applied the draft from a real applier (apply_slice2.ps1, which refuses unless each tree file is at its base hash or already the draft) and closed green, 41 passed (memo_test, result_union_test, memo_deps_test, builders_test, run with --timeout 900000); box closed by -ProvenLog, 8 files byte for byte, undo cells-20261107-202108. Hashes: spi\\source_blocks.spi 65EEE6FB9FB5 (new), source_blocks.ex A21911D5FE43, memo.ex 2A380248EB22, domain.ex 6B774EAAB5AF, result.ex 6F8F887DB86E, main.spi 24C88ED02E16, package.spiproj 9E18ADE4CCA4, memo_test.exs DB4C68A3FBFF. Elixir drift .ex 1062 -> 1058 (-4); this is the first land whose drift line measures a real delta. What stays Elixir by design: SourceBlocks.host/run (dotnet System.cmd and temp files), since IO has no Spiral home until CELLS-TYPED-UNITS. DoD met for both slices.")
inl note_of_giant_state_1_trace_1 () = Note ("GIANT-STATE-1-TRACE", 1u32, "2026-11-06T11:14Z", "compiler", "11-06 07:2x compiler: split from COMPILER-GIANT-STATE-PROFILE (360 min; main 07:0x: steps of 120 min or less). DoD: per slice (full ~15 MB, 1/2, 1/4, cut at top-level binding boundaries), the wall ms of --check and the inclusive ms of the top 10 frames grouped by phase (lex/parse/infer/peval), from scripts/profile-speedscope.ps1, on the node, with the core hash. The compiler has no built-in phase timer, so the trace frames are the phase split.")
inl note_of_giant_state_1_trace_2 () = Note ("GIANT-STATE-1-TRACE", 2u32, "2026-11-06T11:20Z", "compiler", "11-06 07:2x compiler: QUEUED on the node: job-1793964004208-compiler-giant-trace (--after the P6 promotion job, so timings are not disturbed; 2 h cap; script C:\\home\\remote\\compiler-giant\\giant-run.ps1). Slices of agile.spi at 15,196,498 B: header (44 lines of unions) plus the first 1/4 (4,410 inl, 3.80 MB), 1/2 (8,820, 7.52 MB) and all 17,639 bindings (15.20 MB). Each binding is one independent line, so every slice checks standalone (package.spiproj modules: agile). Per slice: 3 timed --check rounds with peak working set and load-before, then dotnet-trace --format Speedscope and profile-speedscope.ps1. Compiler: the installed pack52 on the node, core A688EE5AD426A5A0 (same as the box). Box baseline: a 200-binding 204 KB slice checks in 4.0 s wall, including about 1 s of startup.")
inl note_of_giant_state_1_trace_3 () = Note ("GIANT-STATE-1-TRACE", 3u32, "2026-11-06T11:20Z", "compiler", "11-06 07:2x compiler: NEXT STEP: when job-1793964004208-compiler-giant-trace ends, read its stdout on the node, record per-slice wall/peak/top frames here at 100%, then pull GIANT-STATE-2-EXPONENT. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: no Spiral code in this step (measurement only). Step 3 fix code follows typefeatureset: phases as a union, timings with phantom ms units.")
inl note_of_giant_state_1_trace_4 () = Note ("GIANT-STATE-1-TRACE", 4u32, "2026-11-06T12:34Z", "compiler", "11-06 08:4x compiler: STEP 1 DONE, node (job-1793964004208-compiler-giant-trace, 08:22-08:28, installed pack52 core A688EE5AD426A5A0). CAVEAT: load-before was 91-100% on every round (other lanes' builds), so wall times are noisy; the sampled CPU time from the trace (busy over 17 threads) is the robust measure. WALL (3 rounds, --check, default 30 s timeout): 1/4 = 3.80 MB: 31.8 s (exit 3 = timeout), 13.3 s, 9.9 s, peak 207 MB. 1/2 = 7.52 MB: 13.7, 22.5, 16.0 s, peak 337 MB. full = 15.20 MB: 30.8 s (exit 3), 31.4 s (exit 3), 25.7 s, peak 562 MB. Under load, --check of the full state file hits its own 30 s default timeout in 2 of 3 runs, the starvation step 4 targets. TRACE busy ms: 1/4 6,819; 1/2 12,333; full 26,433. Inclusive phase share at full: parser.Invoke 56.4% (top_inl_or_let 27%, parse_block 14.7%), tokenize_line 22.0%, infer 12.7% (typecheck 11.2%), the rest scheduling/GC. Parsing plus tokenizing, not inference, is about 3/4 of the check.")
inl note_of_giant_state_1_trace_5 () = Note ("GIANT-STATE-1-TRACE", 5u32, "2026-11-06T12:35Z", "compiler", "proof: the trace step exited 0 for all three slices (q, h, full), and profile-speedscope printed the phase frames above; job-1793964004208-compiler-giant-trace finished exit 0.")
inl note_of_giant_state_2_exponent_1 () = Note ("GIANT-STATE-2-EXPONENT", 1u32, "2026-11-06T11:14Z", "compiler", "11-06 compiler: split from COMPILER-GIANT-STATE-PROFILE. DoD: exponent = log2(t(full)/t(half)) per phase, printed; for each phase above 1.2, the spiral_compiler.fs function and line that dominates it, quoted at the core hash.")
inl note_of_giant_state_2_exponent_2 () = Note ("GIANT-STATE-2-EXPONENT", 2u32, "2026-11-06T12:34Z", "compiler", "11-06 08:4x compiler: FIRST EXPONENTS from step 1's single trace per slice (busy ms times inclusive share; load 91-100%, so LOW confidence): total q->h 0.85, h->full 1.10 (near linear). parser q->h 0.85, h->full 1.34. tokenize 0.62, 1.21. infer 1.46, 0.82. Only parser h->full is above 1.2, and the infer swing (1.46 then 0.82) shows how noisy one loaded trace per slice is. NEXT STEP: a quiet-gated rerun on the node (skip a round unless LoadPercentage <= 40%, 3 traces per slice, timeout = rounds x (run + max wait), per tibia's rule), then name the parser function behind the full-size tail with profile-speedscope -View Thread on the full trace (C:\\home\\remote\\compiler-giant\\full*.speedscope.json). DoD: exponent per phase from medians of 3 quiet traces; any phase above 1.2 gets function + line. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: none (measurement).")
inl note_of_giant_state_2_exponent_3 () = Note ("GIANT-STATE-2-EXPONENT", 3u32, "2026-11-06T13:02Z", "compiler", "11-06 09:0x compiler: the quiet-gated rerun (job-1793968595884-compiler-giant-trace2) skipped its first round: the node stayed at 100% for 15 min with 4 other lanes' jobs running (x-cellsfix2, kit-probe1106b, fiscal-fieldmeta-gate, tibia-cifix-build), so the gate would have skipped nearly every round. Stopped it. Requeued UNGATED as job-1793970142961-compiler-giant-trace3 (--after the P6 Rust arms): 3 traces per slice, load-before recorded per round, exponents taken from the MEDIAN sampled busy time (CPU time, much less load-sensitive than wall), with the caveat stated. NEXT STEP: read trace3; per-phase exponent from medians; name the parser function behind any exponent above 1.2 with -View Thread.")
inl note_of_giant_state_2_exponent_4 () = Note ("GIANT-STATE-2-EXPONENT", 4u32, "2026-11-06T14:31Z", "compiler", "11-06 10:4x compiler: STEP 2 VERDICT. Data: trace3 (job-1793970142961-compiler-giant-trace3, ungated, 3 rounds per slice, node at 100% load in every round) plus the step-1 trace. Sampled busy time, ms, rounds 1/2/3 -> median: q (3.80 MB) 12287 / 9080 / 9018 -> 9080; h (7.52 MB) 16804 / 16855 / 10224 -> 16804; full (15.20 MB) 29429 / 19048 / 19767 -> 19767. Total exponent from the medians: q->h 0.89, h->full 0.23. From step 1: 0.85, 1.10. NO estimate of the total exceeds 1.10. The single parser-phase reading above 1.2 (step 1, h->full 1.34) came from one trace per slice and did not reproduce; under 100% load the sampled time is starvation-distorted, so the per-phase shares from trace3 are unusable (their frame shares swing from 0 to 5% between rounds). CONCLUSION: --check on the state file scales about linearly in size. There is NO superlinear phase to fix; the cost is a constant: parse plus tokenize about 3/4 of the check (step-1 inclusive shares 56% + 22% at full size), inference about 13%. Peak working set 562 MB at 15 MB. Consequence for step 3: its premise (\"fix the top superlinear phase\") does not hold. Re-scoped to the constant: the per-binding parse work and the 30 s default --check timeout, which the full file hits under load (2 of 3 step-1 rounds exited 3). proof: both trace jobs exited 0 and the numbers are quoted from their logs.")
inl note_of_xsd_field_descriptors_1_design_1 () = Note ("XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS-1-DESIGN", 1u32, "2026-11-06T11:25Z", "fiscal", "DoD: a note on this item naming the xsd_emit definitions to change (with line refs), the GADT/field_meta/fields-prototype spellings, the per-step gate list, and the edition-3 traps that apply (tuple-lambda open records, GADT existential export erasure). NEXT: read xsd_emit record_walk/record_texts. TYPEFEATURES: GADT indexed by owner x value, existential field list, fields prototype.")
inl note_of_xsd_field_descriptors_1_design_2 () = Note ("XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS-1-DESIGN", 2u32, "2026-11-06T11:28Z", "fiscal", "DESIGN (step 1, 11-06 07:3x, against live lib xsd_emit D00BE390; text reading only, no compile). FOUND: the field GADT the 11-01 spec asks for ALREADY EXISTS, but only in the Writing pass. witness = {case; t; field; fragment} (xsd_emit:1957); part = {text; witness : option witness} (1959). witness_union (1983) emits \"union <ty>_field r = | <Case> :: <ty>_field (<t>)\"; witness_get (1987) emits \"<ty>_get forall r. (f : <ty>_field r) (x : <ty>) : r\"; witness_walk_lines (1992) walks \"list (exists r. <ty>_field r)\"; witness_children (2005) builds <ty>_children over it. Prototypes witness_items / element_witness / choice_witness / any_witness (2069-2072); only Writing fills them (2304-2319); Reading (2187-2190) and Exampling (2425-2428) return []/None; staged_writing returns None for staged owners (2371-2379). WRONG IN THE 11-01 PLAN: codec instances are not emitted from a record walk; codec_shape_of (3126) text-scans emitted function keys for <ty>_of_xml/_to_xml. Descriptors come from the parts walk (walked 2013, push_part 2039), not from codec emission. BASELINE (fiscal/generated, 83 .spi): 8745 record writers (<ty>_children), 4969 with a field GADT = 56.8%. The rest fall back because all_witnessed (1975) is all-or-nothing: one part without a witness (attribute_step 2064 makes none; derived_prefix base parts are plain at 2249; staged owners) drops the whole record. REVISED STEPS (same IDs, now measurable): 2-GADT = hoist witness emission out of Writing, so union <ty>_field r + <ty>_get + \"<ty>_fields : list (exists r. <ty>_field r)\" emit once per record for every pass, plus <ty>_field_meta forall r. (f : <ty>_field r) : xml_codec.field_meta with {name; occurs; namespace}; the lib test a_record_field_list_is_typed_by_its_owner. 3-READ = attribute_step and derived_prefix base parts produce witnesses (coverage metric up from 56.8%; target >= 95%), the reading instance reads through <ty>_fields. 4-WRITE = staged owners get witnesses (the staged_writing None arms go), writer unchanged in output. 5/6 unchanged. TRAPS (edition 3): name pair projections as annotated functions (tuple lambdas infer open records); a GADT whose implicit existential leaks into an export erases it (gadt-implicit-existential-erases-exports): keep <ty>_fields an inl, not an export; prove in a fresh Cells stage (stale-mount lesson, x CELLS-MOUNT-KEY-CONTENT). GATES per step: lib draft round trip via lib_land_window (no -Apply), then the xsd_emit node Cells gate on a fresh stage path, then regen of the named families with the coverage count printed by the same Select-String census used here. DoD of step 1 met: definitions named with line refs, spellings fixed, per-step gates and traps listed. NEXT: step 2 draft.")
inl note_of_linked_union_emitted_local_1 () = Note ("LINKED-UNION-EMITTED-LOCAL", 1u32, "2026-11-06T11:37Z", "compiler", "11-06 07:4x compiler, from main 07:3x: html HEAD f600c82, unchanged cli/html.spi, built with installed pack52 (host A1BF06EB, core A688EE5AD426): the output declares a local enum US<n>, and let mut v2: US<n> = html_pages::html_pages_viewer(&v1), where the committed html.rs (an older compiler) types it as html_model viewer (exported via viewer_same). cargo: E0308 expected viewer, found US<n>, at the html_pages_file and html_pages_viewer call sites. Reproduced on the box on main's working tree (US6 at line 368). DoD: bisect the pack that changed it (box before-copies pack44..pack52, cores quoted), fix with a kitdo, add a regression sample (a linked union crossing two units into a consumer), and prove with html regen plus cargo build on the fixed compiler. NEXT STEP: the bisect is running on a clean git-archive copy of html HEAD in the compiler scratchpad (units rebuilt per compiler, then cli). TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: the fix stays in codegenRust linked-shape passes; no new stringly state.")
inl note_of_linked_union_emitted_local_2 () = Note ("LINKED-UNION-EMITTED-LOCAL", 2u32, "2026-11-06T11:47Z", "compiler", "11-06 08:0x compiler: ROOT CAUSE, not a pack regression. Box evidence (%LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin\\units, keyed by package path): the real tree's html_model graph (e6b0c227fc6a0d01, written 11-03 13:15) and html_pages graph (1102afdf9fcec606, 11-03 13:18) record viewer = {Direct | Source | Delimited | Prose}, but html HEAD f600c82 declares 6 cases (+ Picture, Diagram). main rebuilt only cli/html.spi, so the consumer's 6-case viewer matched no (source, shape) key, and linkedUnionName (spiral_compiler.fs 12804) returned None, so codegen emitted a local US<n>. Bisect on a clean git-archive copy of HEAD (units rebuilt per compiler, then cli): pack52 core A688EE5AD426 and pack44 core 657DA4B173F9 both emit \"let mut v2: viewer = html_pages::html_pages_viewer(&v1)\" (pack48/50/51 arms still running). Unblock for main: rebuild the units before cli (html build.ps1 does this in order). FIX (scope narrowed to the silent fallback): kitdo 1-stale-graph-error.kitdo in kit drafts LINKED-UNION-EMITTED-LOCAL. When the owner unit's graph records the same union source name with a DIFFERENT SET OF CASE NAMES, it raises a named codegen error (\"the graph is stale: rebuild <unit> ...\"). Case names never vary across instantiations, so a generic union instantiated differently (same case names, other payload types) still stays local as today. All 3 linkedUnionName callers (Rust 15133, 16610, 19492) get it. NEXT STEP: candidate pack53 (building on the box); proof = the stale-graph repro gives the named error on pack53 and a local enum on pack52; parity of linked rows and all-backend rows vs pack52 is byte-identical. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: no new state; one pure helper over the recorded shape text.")
inl note_of_linked_union_emitted_local_3 () = Note ("LINKED-UNION-EMITTED-LOCAL", 3u32, "2026-11-06T12:00Z", "compiler", "11-06 08:1x compiler: PROOF of the fix, box. (1) The bisect finished: on fresh units every arm emits \"let mut v2: viewer = html_pages::html_pages_viewer(&v1)\": pack44 657DA4B173F9, pack48 0BA4A6087F0F, pack50 D3FD5378A74E, pack51 E190545B5F30, pack52 A688EE5AD426. No pack regressed. (2) Candidate pack53 = pack52 source + 1-stale-graph-error.kitdo: SpiralCompiler.dll A1BF06EB9AD87F00 (host unchanged), SpiralCompilerCore.dll 1D53F0E39CC4F505. (3) Stale repro on the scratch copy: units built by pack52, then the viewer shape in html_model's and html_pages' graphs replaced by the 4-case one, i.e. main's real-tree state. pack52 exit 0 with \"let mut v2: US8 = ...\" (main's symptom exactly). pack53 exit 5: \"FatalError: The link: unit html_model's unit graph records union viewer as {Direct : () | Source : () | Delimited : () | Prose : ()}, but this build declares it as {... | Picture : () | Diagram : ()}. The graph is stale: rebuild html_model, and every unit between it and this one, before this unit.\" NEXT STEP: linked+smoke parity pack53 vs pack52 (running on the box), then add a regression sample if the linked matrix can express a stale graph (otherwise the repro above is the record), then install.")
inl note_of_linked_union_emitted_local_4 () = Note ("LINKED-UNION-EMITTED-LOCAL", 4u32, "2026-11-06T12:09Z", "compiler", "DoD: the stale-graph repro raises the named error on the candidate (proven 08:1x on pack53); linked and smoke parity vs pack52 byte-identical; installed node first, then box; main regenerates html after rebuilding units.")
inl note_of_linked_union_emitted_local_5 () = Note ("LINKED-UNION-EMITTED-LOCAL", 5u32, "2026-11-06T12:30Z", "compiler", "11-06 08:3x compiler: PARITY on the box, pack53 vs pack52 (review-candidate): linked 14 rows, 14 pass on both, compare-runs differing cells 0, behavior 0, DISAGREE 0; smoke 159 rows (158 ok, 1 error on both), differing cells 0, DISAGREE 0. The install candidate is pack53c = this program + COMPILER-MISSING-ARM-REAL-SITE 1 + COMPILER-CHECK-TYPES-TEST-BODIES 1 (core 24D3967377735A37, host 734CEF2EBF4E7DD4); its own linked/smoke/error-row review is running, then install.")
inl note_of_linked_union_emitted_local_6 () = Note ("LINKED-UNION-EMITTED-LOCAL", 6u32, "2026-11-06T12:54Z", "compiler", "11-06 08:5x compiler: pack53c REVIEW GREEN on the box (core 24D3967377735A37, host 734CEF2EBF4E7DD4 = pack52 source + LINKED-UNION-EMITTED-LOCAL 1 + COMPILER-MISSING-ARM-REAL-SITE 1 + COMPILER-CHECK-TYPES-TEST-BODIES 1). Results: linked 14/14 pass, 0 differing cells vs pack52. smoke 159 rows, residuals identical; 2 TypeScript native timeouts (function_call, managed_string_concat) under 100% box load reran exit 0 and agree with C (DISAGREE 0). Error rows (examples, filter backend_switch_missing_arm): the negative is at parity on Fsharp/C/Rust/Pascal, and the new backend_switch_missing_arm_site carries \"Reached from: main.spi:21 <\" on all 4 backends. INSTALLING on the box now (install-when-clear, %TEMP%\\compiler-pack53c-chain.log). It waits for the record-update census, which is holding the installed compiler. Node and europa ship: main.")
inl note_of_linked_union_emitted_local_7 () = Note ("LINKED-UNION-EMITTED-LOCAL", 7u32, "2026-11-06T13:08Z", "compiler", "11-06 09:1x compiler: INSTALLED pack53c on the BOX (install-pack exit 0; installed SpiralCompilerCore.dll 24D3967377735A37 = reviewed candidate, equal=True; host 734CEF2EBF4E7DD4; the system dotnet launches it; undo dir spiral-bin\\compiler-installs\\pack53c-20261106-090108). The programs are now in the tree core and host (unstaged). PENDING: node and europa, asked of main (ship). Done when main confirms the node runs core 24D39673.")
inl note_of_linked_union_emitted_local_8 () = Note ("LINKED-UNION-EMITTED-LOCAL", 8u32, "2026-11-06T13:15Z", "compiler", "11-06 09:2x compiler: DONE. pack53c is installed on the box (09:1x, core 24D3967377735A37) and shipped to the node by main (09:12, live host 734CEF2EBF4E7DD4, a fresh-process launch exits 0). Proof: the review is green (linked 14/14, smoke 159 identical residuals, error rows on 4 backends), all noted above. europa is DEFERRED by main (MemAvailable 2065-2089 MB < 2100 needed for its 1500M build cap) and stays on pack52 until there is headroom; the change touches only error paths, so pack52 there builds the same outputs.")
inl note_of_tibia_nugget_lsh_table_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUGGET-LSH-TABLE", 1u32, "2026-11-06T12:17Z", "tibia", "11-06 08:17 tibia: split from TIBIA-LEARNING-NUGGETS (main: steps of 120 min or less). Source: ML-library inventory 1.2 (local_binarize :817-821). DoD: a hashed_tactic in src with test blocks (same view -> same bucket on c and rust; k=0 degenerates to one bucket), and one node lanes run at robust_plan with held-out next to train against the network's -68,350 median. NEXT: write the hyperplane and bucket functions with golden tests. TypeFeatures: modes and decisions are unions, not int ids or bool flags (the nugget inventory's remodel rule).")
inl note_of_tibia_nugget_lsh_table_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUGGET-LSH-TABLE", 2u32, "2026-11-06T12:29Z", "tibia", "11-06 08:29 tibia: CODE IN PLACE (tibia, unstaged; the formatter is clean on all three files). (1) network.spi: dot_with (coef : i32 -> i32) over the 8 sensed features (sensed_dot + flag_dot), so a plane needs no weights array. (2) NEW src/hashed.spi (module registered after typed_network): 4 planes whose 32 coefficients in [-256,255] come from a murmur-style u32 mix of the slot index (golden: plane_value 0 = 19, 3 = 228), bucket = the sign bits of the plane dots (16 buckets), decide = the bucket's 3 table cells through network::decision_of. The table is a plain network::weights (48 of its 66 cells are used), so the existing climb and evolve_by train it unchanged. Tests on c and rust: golden buckets 13/7/11/5 for 4 input states (computed by hand from the same mix), and table cells decide heal/retreat. (3) hunting_pack: brain gains Hashed : network::weights with hashed_heals and hashed_plan beside the Network arms, plus hashed_tactic. NOTE: the 8-input sensed view, not the 25-input typed view (that one is typed_network's). PENDING: the node rerun of build.ps1 after the CI-fix build. NEXT: a lanes variant (hashed_tactic in lane_fitness) at robust_plan, held-out against the network's -68,350.")
inl note_of_tibia_nugget_lsh_table_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUGGET-LSH-TABLE", 3u32, "2026-11-06T12:31Z", "tibia", "11-06 08:31 tibia: MEASUREMENT QUEUED on the node: job-1793968277925-tibia-hashed-lanes (timeout 6 h), last in the node chain, so it doesn't load the timing jobs. Program hashed_lanes.spi (scratchpad hashed): lanes 0-3, evolve_by with judge pf2 = worth on hashed_tactic at robust_plan (8 gen x 64 offspring x 4x training seeds), with rows of train (seeds 1-100) and held-out (held_out_first, 100 seeds), matching the network rows of TIBIA-BATCHED-EVOLUTION (x4 held-out median -68,350). Built from the local src (network, hashed, hunting_pack, spiral.toml) and lanes.spi overlaid on the mirror's src, OMP 8, gcc -O2. Pending.")
inl note_of_tibia_nugget_lsh_table_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUGGET-LSH-TABLE", 4u32, "2026-11-06T12:44Z", "tibia", "11-06 08:44 tibia: tibia build.ps1 -ChecksOnly is GREEN on the box over the whole tree: formatter check clean, cell budget 0 over_budget (26 findings, all pre-existing autolink/mention). Getting there split 8 over-budget definitions of mine: hashed's golden test into two plus a heal_and_retreat_in helper; hunting_pack's Network/Hashed arms behind learned_heals/learned_plan (a catch-all arm in wants_heal/after_heal_plan); regret's share, learn, round_of, play_round, seeded, rock_heavy and near_third. The queued hashed-lanes node job runs the pre-split copies, which compute the same thing. Tests still PENDING: the node build.ps1 rerun.")
inl note_of_tibia_nugget_lsh_table_5 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUGGET-LSH-TABLE", 5u32, "2026-11-06T12:58Z", "tibia", "11-06 08:58 tibia: PROOF green. Node job-1793969567058-tibia-newmods-cells ran Cells run_notebook on a scratch copy of the local tibia src (outside the mirror, mirror lib), exit 0: hashed: discovered 3, executed 3, passed 3 (c+rust each): golden buckets 13/7/11 and 5, plane values 19/228, and table cells decide. The offline golden values held on both backends on the first run.")
inl note_of_tibia_nugget_lsh_table_6 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUGGET-LSH-TABLE", 6u32, "2026-11-07T01:55Z", "tibia", "11-06 21:5x tibia: PR-29 VOID, no verdict. node job-1793968277925-tibia-hashed-lanes hit its wall-clock timeout (exit 124 after ~13.4 h incl. queue) with no lane row printed: compiled hashed_lanes.c (5.6 MB), omp 0, then nothing; the node ran at 100 percent all day with kit/compiler/fiscal jobs. robust_plan (8 generations x 64 offspring x 4 x training seeds) x 4 lanes is too long for a shared node. Next: rerun on a quiet host, or a smaller pre-registered plan (tiny_plan smoke first to time one lane), before writing PR-29's RESULT row.")
inl note_of_tibia_nugget_lsh_table_7 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUGGET-LSH-TABLE", 7u32, "2026-11-07T15:53Z", "tibia", "11-07 11:5x tibia groom round 2 (stale Active, no note in 12 h): Planned. PR-29's run was VOID (job timed out with no lane row on a node at 100 percent). Next step: a tiny_plan smoke of hashed_lanes on the node to time one lane, then pick a plan that fits and pre-register it.")
inl note_of_tibia_nugget_lsh_table_8 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUGGET-LSH-TABLE", 8u32, "2026-11-07T21:43Z", "tibia", "11-07 17:4x tibia: SMOKE STARTED. The measurement program now lives in the repo: tibia apps/predict/hashed_lanes.spi 1A5C9FDB8FAF (unstaged), registered AFTER lanes in apps/predict/spiral.toml. Two faults found on the way, both mine. (1) predict.ps1 registers a new module right after predict, i.e. before lanes, so `:< lanes` gave ETY-UnboundModule and every later definition cascaded into unbound or unification errors; I chased the cascade before reading the first error. (2) It now uses network::evolve (plain fitness function) instead of a judge instance, with no `:< network` open. It prints a hunts row so predict.ps1 reports hunts/s. Box --check is green. Node job-1794087750728-tibia-hsmoke runs it at tiny_plan (4 lanes x (1 gen x 2 offspring x 2 seeds + 200 report hunts)), single-threaded C, with a waiter. NEXT STEP: from its hunts/s, size a plan that fits about 1 h on the node, pre-register PR-29b against the network's held-out -68,350, and run it.")
inl note_of_tibia_nugget_lsh_table_9 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUGGET-LSH-TABLE", 9u32, "2026-11-07T22:42Z", "tibia", "11-07 18:5x tibia: SMOKE READ (job-1794087750728-tibia-hsmoke, exit 0): 816 hunts in 105.7 s, 7 hunts/s single-threaded on the loaded node; every tiny-plan lane at the no-clear floor (about -1,000,600,000), as expected from 2 offspring. That sizes PR-29's VOID: robust_plan is 204,800 hunts per lane, about 32 h for 4 lanes. PR-29 got its VOID RESULT row. PR-29b was pre-registered in BENCHMARK.md before running: both arms (hashed_tactic and network_tactic) trained by network::evolve at the SAME small_plan (4 generations x 16 offspring x 100 seeds), lanes 0-3, held-out seeds 1001-1100. Prediction: the table is weaker in at least 3 of 4 paired lanes. Program apps/predict/hashed_lanes.spi 13ECD31AEC00 (box --check green, formatter-clean). RUNNING: job-1794091321041-tibia-pr29b-run (52,800 hunts, about 2 h at the smoke's rate, 5 h cap), with a waiter. BLOCKER: that job. NEXT STEP: read it in full and write the PR-29b RESULT row by its rule.")
inl note_of_tibia_nugget_lsh_table_10 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUGGET-LSH-TABLE", 10u32, "2026-11-07T23:56Z", "tibia", "11-07 20:0x tibia: DONE, PR-29b HOLDS (node job-1794091321041-tibia-pr29b-run read in full; 52,800 hunts in 4,208 s; RESULT row in tibia docs/BENCHMARK.md, unstaged). At an equal small budget (4 generations x 16 offspring x 100 seeds) the hashed table is weaker in 4 of 4 paired lanes, held-out: -286,450 vs -78,700; -1,000,097,788 vs -98,400; -399,750 vs -247,200; -1,000,096,435 vs -68,600. Two table lanes never clear; the network median is -88,550. The table stays a non-NN baseline only, as the rule says. Descriptive: the network's best small-budget lane (-68,600) already matches the 11-05 robust-plan median (-68,350), at 1/32 of the search. Code kept: src/hashed.spi (tests green 11-06) and apps/predict/hashed_lanes.spi 13ECD31AEC00 with both arms, plus the predict.ps1 fix that registers a new module AFTER its siblings.")
inl note_of_tibia_nugget_lsh_table_11 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUGGET-LSH-TABLE", 11u32, "2026-11-08T00:03Z", "tibia", "11-07 20:1x tibia: housekeeping after closing. tibia build.ps1 -ChecksOnly (the whole-tree layout + cell-budget gate) flagged apps/predict/hashed_lanes.spi twice: a missing final newline, and arm_row over the cell budget (weight 400). Fixed by adding the newline and splitting the score columns into arm_scores, so the file is now 82D6BE0ABB39 (a refactor with the same output; PR-29b ran 13ECD31AEC00). The gate is now green on the box: formatter clean, 0 over_budget (26 pre-existing autolink/mention findings). Lesson: the box gate passes --path (repo .editorconfig) and checks the cell budget of every file, so run it after editing tibia, not only per-file checks.")
inl note_of_tibia_nugget_tabular_cfr_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUGGET-TABULAR-CFR", 1u32, "2026-11-06T12:17Z", "tibia", "11-06 08:17 tibia: split from TIBIA-LEARNING-NUGGETS (main: steps of 120 min or less). Source: inventory 1.4 cfr.spi:144-253, 3 (train_cfr.spi single call site, hd enumerative CFR+). DoD: regret-matching+ with a golden exploitability that falls monotonically on a 2-action toy, then the arena abstraction's average strategy compared live-sim against retreat-at-2 on held-out seeds. NEXT: the toy game plus the golden test. TypeFeatures: modes and decisions are unions, not int ids or bool flags (the nugget inventory's remodel rule).")
inl note_of_tibia_nugget_tabular_cfr_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUGGET-TABULAR-CFR", 2u32, "2026-11-06T12:33Z", "tibia", "11-06 08:33 tibia: TOY plus GOLDEN TESTS in place (tibia, unstaged; formatter clean; module registered after hashed). NEW src/regret.spi: regret-matching+ in integer per-mille (strategy from positive regrets; CFR+ clamps regrets at 0; linear averaging weights iteration t). Toy union = Dominated | RockPaperScissors, with payoff in thousandths. Self-play of two learners. Tests on c and rust: (1) a dominant action takes >= 990 of the average within 200 rounds; (2) RPS from a biased start (rock regret 3000) averages each action into [280, 390] after 500 rounds; (3) a uniform start stays exactly 333/333/333 (worked by hand: sums 424575 of total 1273725 over 50 rounds). Overflow bounds checked by hand: payoff products <= 3e6, linear sums <= 1.3e8. PENDING: the node build.ps1 rerun after the CI-fix build. NEXT: the arena abstraction (heal/attack/retreat over bucketed hp and adjacency) as a toy case, and its average strategy against retreat-at-2 on held-out seeds.")
inl note_of_tibia_nugget_tabular_cfr_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUGGET-TABULAR-CFR", 3u32, "2026-11-06T12:44Z", "tibia", "11-06 08:44 tibia: tibia build.ps1 -ChecksOnly is GREEN on the box over the whole tree: formatter check clean, cell budget 0 over_budget (26 findings, all pre-existing autolink/mention). Getting there split 8 over-budget definitions of mine: hashed's golden test into two plus a heal_and_retreat_in helper; hunting_pack's Network/Hashed arms behind learned_heals/learned_plan (a catch-all arm in wants_heal/after_heal_plan); regret's share, learn, round_of, play_round, seeded, rock_heavy and near_third. The queued hashed-lanes node job runs the pre-split copies, which compute the same thing. Tests still PENDING: the node build.ps1 rerun.")
inl note_of_tibia_nugget_tabular_cfr_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUGGET-TABULAR-CFR", 4u32, "2026-11-06T12:58Z", "tibia", "11-06 08:58 tibia: PROOF green. Node job-1793969567058-tibia-newmods-cells ran Cells run_notebook on a scratch copy of the local tibia src (outside the mirror, mirror lib), exit 0: regret: discovered 3, executed 3, passed 3 (c+rust each): a_dominant_action_takes_the_average, rock_paper_scissors_averages_to_a_third_from_a_biased_start, a_uniform_start_stays_uniform. The offline golden values held on both backends on the first run.")
inl note_of_tibia_nugget_tabular_cfr_5 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUGGET-TABULAR-CFR", 5u32, "2026-11-06T14:39Z", "tibia", "11-06 10:39 tibia: DESIGN NOTE for the arena abstraction (TIBIA-CFR-ARENA-DESIGN; sized from policy.spi's thresholds: heal_below 124-160 on max 515, retreat_at 2, strike_above 10-23). INFORMATION STATE (knight): hp bucket over 0-515 at the decision-relevant cuts {<100, 100-159, 160-259, >=260} (4), adjacent attackers {0, 1, 2, 3+} (4), potion ready {yes, no} (2) = 32 states. The opponent sees its own crowd size only, so this is imperfect information on purpose. ACTIONS (knight): Heal, Strike, StepAway (3, the stance union policy::engagement already names). OPPONENT: the camp, abstracted to an adversary that picks Press (all adjacent hit) or Spread (one hits, others reposition) per state, i.e. a zero-sum 2-player game in which CFR is the right tool. PAYOFF: the simulator's expected values per (state, knight action, camp action), from hunting_pack's damage (cyclops melee 0-105 per 2 s, block charges) and the potion (125-175 heal, 1 s cooldown), as the potion cost plus the expected damage taken, in thousandths. A death bucket (hp < 0 after the step) costs 14000 gp, the README's profit rule. Terminal after 30 steps or when the camp is clear. SOLVER: regret.spi's regret-matching+ per information state with linear averaging (already tested on the toys); exploitability = best-response value minus the game value, computed by enumeration over 32 x 3 x 2 (well under 1 s). TESTS: (1) exploitability falls monotonically over 50, 100 and 200 iterations on this game; (2) the average strategy at hp < 100 with a ready potion puts >= 900 on Heal; (3) against the camp's Press, StepAway's share rises with 2+ attackers (the retreat-at-2 rule emerging). DoD of the parent then: the average strategy as a hunting_pack brain, held-out against retreat-at-2 in the simulator, pre-registered first.")
inl note_of_tibia_nugget_tabular_cfr_6 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUGGET-TABULAR-CFR", 6u32, "2026-11-06T21:29Z", "tibia", "11-06 17:2x tibia: VERDICT (PR-30): cfr worth -1,000,600,000, 126 deaths, 0 clears of 100; cfr_argmax -1,000,600,000, 127 deaths, 0 clears; retreat2 -150,600, 38 deaths, 100 clears. Prediction HOLDS (A far below B): the CFR brain never clears, consistent with the abstraction paying Melee nothing. Decision as pre-registered: the CFR table stays a non-NN baseline; TIBIA-NUGGET-TABULAR-CFR closes on this verdict; the next game version is TIBIA-CFR-KILL-VALUE-CODE (now unblocked by this run). DONE for this nugget: regret-matching+ toys, the arena game with exact hp, the depth-3 tree, the strategy table and the brain are in src with tests, and the measured comparison its DoD names is PR-30. Follow-up game work is TIBIA-CFR-KILL-VALUE-CODE. Proof: PR-30 RESULT row; unit tests job-1793991326784-tibia-cfrbrain-cells.")
inl note_of_tibia_nugget_tabular_cfr_7 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUGGET-TABULAR-CFR", 7u32, "2026-11-06T23:48Z", "tibia", "11-06 19:5x tibia: REOPEN NOTE: PR-32 reproduced PR-30's numbers to the digit with a different game and table, so PR-30's verdict (the abstraction pays Melee nothing) is not established; the identity suggests the brain does not reach play. Diagnosis in TIBIA-CFR-BRAIN-TRACE. The nugget's code and unit tests stand; its measured comparison is reopened.")
inl note_of_tibia_nugget_tabular_cfr_8 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUGGET-TABULAR-CFR", 8u32, "2026-11-07T15:53Z", "tibia", "11-07 11:5x tibia groom round 2 (stale Active, no note in 12 h): Blocked on: TIBIA-CFR-RETREAT-MODEL (the trace showed the abstract game makes Retreat dominant, so the measured comparison is reopened). Resume when: that item is Done and PR-35 (CFR vs retreat2 on the fixed game) is pre-registered.")
inl note_of_tibia_nugget_tabular_cfr_9 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUGGET-TABULAR-CFR", 9u32, "2026-11-07T20:16Z", "tibia", "11-07 16:1x tibia: CLOSES by PR-35's pre-registered rule (\"clears at least 50: the retreat model was the blocker, and TIBIA-NUGGET-TABULAR-CFR closes with the CFR brain as a measured baseline\"). The measured baseline, held-out seeds 1001-1100, lanes.spi's spot: the sampled CFR brain clears 63 with 64 deaths, worth -1,000,378,953; argmax clears 53 with 175 deaths; retreat-at-2 clears 100 with 38 deaths, worth -150,600. Its arc: PR-30 (0 clears; Melee had no value), then the kill value (PR-32, identical to the digit), then TIBIA-CFR-BRAIN-TRACE (Retreat dominant), then TIBIA-CFR-RETREAT-MODEL, validated by an exact oracle, then PR-35. Still open, and out of the nugget's scope: the abstraction's flat 52 damage, one bucket per step, and the press/spread camp. A follow-up would refine those, not the solver.")
inl note_of_tibia_nugget_importance_sampling_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUGGET-IMPORTANCE-SAMPLING", 1u32, "2026-11-06T12:17Z", "tibia", "11-06 08:17 tibia: split from TIBIA-LEARNING-NUGGETS (main: steps of 120 min or less). Source: inventory 1.4 (models.spi:37-76, path_probs.spi). DoD: a log-space path probability per hunt (sum of log action probs, integer fixed-point for bit-exactness across backends) with tests, and an IS estimate whose error against fresh sims of the same tactic is quoted on 100 seeds. NEXT: the fixed-point log-prob type and its tests. TypeFeatures: modes and decisions are unions, not int ids or bool flags (the nugget inventory's remodel rule).")
inl note_of_tibia_nugget_importance_sampling_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUGGET-IMPORTANCE-SAMPLING", 2u32, "2026-11-06T12:47Z", "tibia", "11-06 08:47 tibia: STEP 1 in place (tibia, unstaged; -ChecksOnly green: formatter clean, cell budget 0 over). NEW src/logprob.spi, registered after regret: log2_q16 (x : u32) is an exact fixed-point log2 in Q16 by integer squaring (bit length for the integer part, 16 squarings of the mantissa normalized to [1,2) in u64), the same bits on every backend; per_mille_log2 p = log2(p/1000) in Q16; path_log2 sums a hunt's per-mille action probabilities. Golden tests on c and rust, computed by the same integer algorithm offline: log2 1/2/3/1000/1024 = 0/65536/103872/653117/655360; a half is exactly -65536; path [500;500;1000] = -131072. PENDING: the node build.ps1 rerun. NEXT: exp2_q16 for the IS weight (the inverse) with golden round-trip tests, then the IS estimate against fresh sims.")
inl note_of_tibia_nugget_importance_sampling_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUGGET-IMPORTANCE-SAMPLING", 3u32, "2026-11-06T12:49Z", "tibia", "11-06 08:49 tibia: STEP 2 in place (-ChecksOnly green). exp2_q16 (x : i64) : i64 inverts log2: floor-split x into integer k and Q16 fraction (explicit floor for negatives, no reliance on signed shifts), multiply 1.0 in Q30 by 2^(2^-i) for each set fraction bit, using a 16-entry constant table (root_high/root_low, Q30, rounded offline), then shift by k-14. Golden test on c and rust: exp2 0 / 1 / -1 / 0.5 = 65536 / 131072 / 32768 / 92681, and exp2 (log2 3) = 196607 (3.0 = 196608, one unit off). NEXT: is_weight = exp2 (path_log2 target - path_log2 behavior) and the IS estimate against fresh sims on 100 seeds, which needs a logged-hunt format, i.e. the next node slice.")
inl note_of_tibia_nugget_importance_sampling_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUGGET-IMPORTANCE-SAMPLING", 4u32, "2026-11-06T12:51Z", "tibia", "11-06 08:51 tibia: STEP 3 in place (-ChecksOnly green): is_weight_q16 target behavior = exp2_q16 (path_log2 target - path_log2 behavior), the per-hunt importance weight in Q16. Test on c and rust: a target twice as likely per step over 2 steps weighs 4.0 (262144), and equal paths weigh 1.0 (65536). DESIGN NOTE for the estimate: a deterministic tactic has per-step probability 0 or 1, so IS needs a STOCHASTIC behavior policy (ensemble sampling with a temperature, the nugget's other half, or RandomControl). NEXT: an ensemble behavior policy that logs per-decision per-mille probabilities in the hunt trace.")
inl note_of_tibia_nugget_importance_sampling_5 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUGGET-IMPORTANCE-SAMPLING", 5u32, "2026-11-06T12:58Z", "tibia", "11-06 08:58 tibia: PROOF green. Node job-1793969567058-tibia-newmods-cells ran Cells run_notebook on a scratch copy of the local tibia src (outside the mirror, mirror lib), exit 0: logprob: discovered 4, executed 4, passed 4 (c+rust each): the golden log2 values, half = -1 and paths add, exp2 inverts log2 within one unit, and the IS weight (4.0 and 1.0). The offline golden values held on both backends on the first run.")
inl note_of_tibia_nugget_importance_sampling_6 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUGGET-IMPORTANCE-SAMPLING", 6u32, "2026-11-06T14:41Z", "tibia", "11-06 10:41 tibia: DESIGN (TIBIA-SOFT-WIRE-DESIGN, from reading hunting_pack/pack_sim). (1) BRAIN: brain gains `Softened : soft_brain` with soft_brain = { inner : brain_core; epsilon : i32 }, where brain_core is Network or Hashed weights (not Rules, whose thresholds have no per-bit decision). wants_heal and after_heal_plan route Softened through learned_heals/learned_plan: take the inner network::decision, then soft_policy::sampled with three rolls. (2) ROLLS: pack_roll gains `PackSoftDecision` (purpose code 21, next to target_code's 17-20 and 40/41). The test every_pack_roll_has_its_own_purpose_code moves from 12 to 13 rolls, with codes still distinct. The three bits use entity offsets 0/1/2 on key seed tick (call-sign slot) PackSoftDecision, so the draws are independent and replayable. (3) LOG: hunter_tally gains `log_path : i32` (Q16 sum of logprob::per_mille_log2 over every sampled bit, starting at 0 in the fresh tally at hunting_pack.spi:715), added where the decision is taken. A deterministic brain adds 0 (per_mille 1000 means log 0), so existing tallies keep their values. (4) REPORT: pack_sim's tally5 becomes tally6 with log_path, and clear_tallied sums it; the IS estimate then reweights each logged hunt by logprob::exp2_q16 (target_log_path - behavior_log_path). Sites to touch: hunting_pack 172 (tally), 715 (fresh), the 2 dispatch arms, the roll union plus its test, and pack_sim 195-200. Rules arms stay untouched.")
inl note_of_tibia_nugget_importance_sampling_7 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUGGET-IMPORTANCE-SAMPLING", 7u32, "2026-11-06T15:06Z", "tibia", "11-06 11:04 tibia: soft_policy PROOF green (same node job): discovered 4, passed 4 on c and rust: a low roll keeps the greedy act (950), a high roll flips it (50), epsilon 0 always keeps the greedy act (1000), a sampled decision logs 950/50/950, and those probabilities feed logprob::path_log2. Next slice: TIBIA-SOFT-WIRE-CODE.")
inl note_of_tibia_nugget_importance_sampling_8 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUGGET-IMPORTANCE-SAMPLING", 8u32, "2026-11-06T21:33Z", "tibia", "11-06 17:3x tibia: VERDICT (PR-31): target 90 clear ms IS 54,635 vs fresh 57,999 (-5.8 pct), potions 16.935 vs 17.760 (-4.6 pct), ess 53.6, 0 off path; target 50 clear ms 76,428 vs 51,850 (+47 pct), potions 26.170 vs 9.860 (+165 pct), ess 1.0; target 0 no estimate, 100 of 100 off path. Prediction HOLDS on every point. Decision as pre-registered: path IS only scores small policy steps; per-decision weighting is next (TIBIA-IS-PER-DECISION-CODE, now unblocked by this run). The DoD's \"IS estimate whose error against fresh sims is quoted on 100 seeds\" is met: -5.8 pct (clear ms) and -4.6 pct (potions) at epsilon 90, with the collapse at 50 and 0 quoted too. Pieces in src: logprob (log2/exp2, path weights, is_estimate with ess and target paths), soft_policy (sampling and target probabilities), hunting_pack (Softened brain, scored_by, logged_hunts). Closes when ci-final proves the final tree. Proof: PR-31 RESULT row.")
inl note_of_tibia_nugget_importance_sampling_9 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUGGET-IMPORTANCE-SAMPLING", 9u32, "2026-11-06T22:45Z", "tibia", "11-06 18:3x tibia: PROOF OF RECORD green for this code: node job-1793996115107-tibia-ci-final (build.ps1 -Files on a scratch tree outside the mirror, tree EF7486F7554A, log read in full): layout clean, cell budget 0 over; arena_cfr 13/13 (77FB224B574E, table + game node), hunting_pack 13/13 (7406AE9BAF88, Cfr brain + scored_by + logged_hunts), logprob 10/10 (A01AA2C151BA, estimator + target paths), pack_sim 41/41 (14AD5EE944CC), soft_policy 6/6 (the earlier lock_timeout rows pass here), sweep 1/1. Proof: job-1793996115107-tibia-ci-final. With PR-31's RESULT this closes the nugget (per-decision IS continues as TIBIA-IS-PER-DECISION-CODE / PR-33).")
inl note_of_record_update_type_change_1 () = Note ("RECORD-UPDATE-TYPE-CHANGE", 1u32, "2026-11-06T12:19Z", "compiler", "11-06 08:2x compiler, from main (SPIRAL-UNFORGEABLE-WITNESSES depends on this). Probes on the installed host A1BF06EB: (1) a nominal record update keeps the nominal: `:! point = { x : i32; y : i32 }` with `:= moved (p : point) : point = { p ?| x = 5i32 }` compiles. (2) GAP: `:= changed (r : { x : i32; y : i32 }) = { r ?| x = \"text\" }` compiles with no diagnostic. DESIGN QUESTION FIRST: on a STRUCTURAL record, a type-changing update is a coherent operation (the result is a new structural type {x : string; y : i32}), and lib or corpus code may use it on purpose. On a NOMINAL record it would forge a value of a type its constructor never built, which is the unforgeability hole. DoD: (a) a census of type-changing record updates over lib, apps, samples and kit (the parser forms: RawRecordWithSymbol / RawRecordWithInjectVar under `with` / `?|`), counted by structural vs nominal base; (b) a typed error for any update whose base is a nominal record and whose new field type differs (\"updating x would change it from i32 to string; a nominal record keeps its field types, build a new value instead\"), plus the structural case per the census (error if the census finds 0 intended uses, else a stated rule); (c) samples: main's two probes as a positive and a negative (Contains on the error text). NEXT STEP: run the census (read-only grep plus a typed probe on the hits). TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: the error carries the field name and both types as Ty, printed by show_ty, not strings built ad hoc.")
inl note_of_record_update_type_change_2 () = Note ("RECORD-UPDATE-TYPE-CHANGE", 2u32, "2026-11-06T12:30Z", "compiler", "11-06 08:3x compiler: CENSUS PLAN, using the instrument already installed (RecordWithRetypeCensus, SPIRAL_RECORD_WITH_CENSUS_OUT; SPIRAL-UNFORGEABLE-WITNESSES n9/n10, decision rule fixed there, main 11-06: nominal retype = error regardless; structural: 0 intended uses -> error, else legal but named in the error text and docs). Text census first: 523 record-update sites across spiral 55, kit 50, fiscal 3, x 240, tibia 165, regex 9, blog 1. Typed census running on the box (BelowNormal; the node runs the timing-sensitive giant-state trace): --check, inference only, on each of the 126 outermost package roots of spiral/kit/fiscal/x/tibia/regex/blog, rows same/retyped per update. NEXT STEP: read census/summary.tsv. DoD: retyped count recorded with sites; nominal-retype typed error + samples (main's 2 probes); structural rule applied per the count.")
inl note_of_record_update_type_change_3 () = Note ("RECORD-UPDATE-TYPE-CHANGE", 3u32, "2026-11-06T12:32Z", "compiler", "11-06 08:3x compiler: PROBED on installed pack52 (core A688EE5AD426, --check with SPIRAL_COMPILER_PACKAGE_DIR set). NOMINAL retype is ALREADY a typed error: `:! point = { x : i32; y : i32 }` with `:= moved (p : point) : point = { p ?| x = \"text\" }` -> \"main.spi:3:43: ETY-TermError: Unification failure. Got: i32 Expected: string In the definition: moved.\" The nominal path (spiral_compiler.fs 5998-6008, nominal_record_fields) unifies the new value with the declared field type. So the forging hole is closed today; only the message is generic (and states the two types swapped from the reader's view). STRUCTURAL retype is silent: `:= changed (r : { x : i32; y : i32 }) = { r ?| x = \"text\" }` -> \"checked package\", exit 0 (the eval path, 5900-5915, Map.add with the new var and no check). Remaining: (1) a clearer nominal message naming the field (\"updating x of point would change it from i32 to string\"); (2) the structural rule from the census (running).")
inl note_of_record_update_type_change_4 () = Note ("RECORD-UPDATE-TYPE-CHANGE", 4u32, "2026-11-06T12:57Z", "compiler", "11-06 09:0x compiler: CENSUS RESULT (installed pack52, --check with SPIRAL_RECORD_WITH_CENSUS_OUT; stopped after 4 of 126 package roots: blog, fiscal generated_cfdi_pagos_2_0 (+certificates), generated_cfdi_tfd_1_1, because each check took 100-174 s at BelowNormal on a 100% box, and all four infer the same shared lib). 147 distinct update rows: same 107, retyped 40. ALL 40 retypes keep the type constructor and change only a type argument: phantom/state indexes in lib's xsd model, e.g. name: definition_name 'ta -> definition_name b, content: xsd particle 'tb -> xsd particle b, attributes: list (xsd attribute_decl 'tb) -> list (xsd attribute_decl b), inline: option (xsd type_def 'td) -> option (xsd type_def form). These are intended typed-state transitions. PROPOSED RULE (sharper than \"legal or error\"): a record update may change a field's type ARGUMENTS but not its type CONSTRUCTOR. i32 -> string (main's probe 2) becomes a typed error naming the field and both types; all 40 lib uses stay legal; nominal records keep their exact field types as today. NEXT STEP: kitdo = new TypeError RecordUpdateRetypesField (field, old, new) raised in Infer's structural eval when both heads are known and differ, then --check over all 126 roots on the candidate (node, after its queue) to prove no other corpus update changes a head. DoD: candidate passes the 126 roots, main's probe 2 errors with the named message, probe 1 still compiles, and the lib xsd updates still compile.")
inl note_of_record_update_type_change_5 () = Note ("RECORD-UPDATE-TYPE-CHANGE", 5u32, "2026-11-06T13:18Z", "compiler", "11-06 09:2x compiler: CANDIDATE pack54 = pack53c + 1-retype-keeps-constructor.kitdo (kit drafts RECORD-UPDATE-TYPE-CHANGE; core 9FB7E911100489BC, host 734CEF2EBF4E7DD4). Probes, --check: structural i32 -> string: \"main.spi:1:48: ETY-RecordUpdateRetypesField: This record update changes the field x from i32 to string. An update may change a field's type arguments (a phantom or state index) but not its type constructor; build a new record instead. In the definition: changed.\", exit 5. Nominal retype: unchanged unification failure. Nominal same type: checked, exit 0. Regression sample (unstaged): samples/record_update_retype_negative + its ExpectedErrors row. RUNNING: --check of all 126 package roots on pack54 (box, 3 at a time, BelowNormal). Rule: no package may fail with ETY-RecordUpdateRetypesField (any such site is an unintended constructor change and gets fixed or the rule revisited).")
inl note_of_record_update_type_change_6 () = Note ("RECORD-UPDATE-TYPE-CHANGE", 6u32, "2026-11-06T15:13Z", "compiler", "11-06 11:1x compiler: pack55d REVIEW GREEN on the box (core 257DB91886B97811, host 734CEF2EBF4E7DD4 = pack53c tree + RECORD-UPDATE-TYPE-CHANGE 1 + FORMATTER-JOIN-LONE-THEN 1 + LINKED-UNITS-GLEAM-RECORDS 1 + LINKED-EXPORT-LAMBDA-WARN 1). Linked 15/15 pass vs installed 14/15 (the only differing cells are the new linked_rust_lambda_export_warn row, which runs exit 35 with the warning). Smoke 159 rows, 0 differing cells. Gleam examples 446 rows: the 3 differing rows (portable_console_lines, portable_convert_parse, portable_math_rounding) were compile TIMEOUTS on installed under load; compiled directly, both compilers give byte-identical Gleam (6394E1EE27AF, 5E0C9760F020, B875341559F0). Error rows: backend_switch_missing_arm_negative at parity, backend_switch_missing_arm_site and record_update_retype_negative error with their named text on Fsharp/C/Rust/Pascal. Formatter gates green (see FORMATTER-JOIN-LONE-THEN). INSTALLING on the box now (install-when-clear, %TEMP%\\compiler-pack55d-chain.log); node and europa ship via main.")
inl note_of_record_update_type_change_7 () = Note ("RECORD-UPDATE-TYPE-CHANGE", 7u32, "2026-11-06T15:20Z", "compiler", "11-06 11:2x compiler: CORPUS CHECK of the retype rule on pack54 (--check per package root, census rows on), PARTIAL. Checked: 38 roots of the first pass (blog + 37 fiscal generated families) plus 7 of the 42 remaining = 45 roots, with 0 ETY-RecordUpdateRetypesField and 1520 retyped-argument rows still accepted (the phantom-index updates). Non-zero exits, none from the rule: (1) generated_cr_factura_exportacion_4_4 failed once on a mid-edit read of lib physics.spi (rewritten 10:09 by another lane), and passed on rerun on both pack53c and pack54; (2) kit compiler-contracts typed-predicate wrong-input / wrong-carrier are intentional negative contracts; (3) kit src / kit state: \"Package C:/home/git/kit/src/spiral is not loaded\", because kit resolves spiral- through its own package dir, which a plain --check does not set up (it fails the same on pack53c), so kit is NOT covered by this method; (4) fiscal src: the 900 s attestation timeout on a 100% box. PAUSED at 7/42 to free memory for the pack55d install window (it was blocked at 957 MB free). REMAINING: x, tibia, regex and spiral apps roots after the install; kit via its own gate (kit's regen train) once pack55d ships.")
inl note_of_record_update_type_change_8 () = Note ("RECORD-UPDATE-TYPE-CHANGE", 8u32, "2026-11-06T15:21Z", "compiler", "11-06 11:2x compiler: INSTALLED pack55d on the BOX (installed SpiralCompilerCore.dll 257DB91886B97811 = reviewed candidate, equal=True; host 734CEF2EBF4E7DD4; the system dotnet launches it; undo compiler-installs\\pack55d-20261106-111308). The programs are now in the tree core (unstaged). PENDING: node ship (asked of main), then each item's remaining DoD.")
inl note_of_record_update_type_change_9 () = Note ("RECORD-UPDATE-TYPE-CHANGE", 9u32, "2026-11-06T16:14Z", "compiler", "11-06 12:1x compiler: pack55d is on ALL THREE hosts (main 12:1x): box 11:2x (core 257DB91886B97811), node 11:33 (live host 734CEF2EBF4E7DD4, fresh launch exit 0), europa 11:35 (Linux build from the box's live sources: core 9464633ADF9FB8CC, host 9452B1A2EBD761EB, launch exit 0). main's own probe confirms the message (\"changes the field x from i32 to string ... build a new record instead\"). Corpus check on the installed core: 24 of the last 35 roots done, 0 ETY-RecordUpdateRetypesField; the only failures are intentional negatives (apps/zed/fixtures/bad) and the Cells new_project template, whose manifest holds placeholders (parse error, not inference). Remaining: tibia's 9 roots and x's 2; Done when they report 0 retype errors.")
inl note_of_record_update_type_change_10 () = Note ("RECORD-UPDATE-TYPE-CHANGE", 10u32, "2026-11-06T16:34Z", "compiler", "11-06 12:4x compiler: DONE. Corpus check on the installed core 257DB91886B97811 (pack55d) finished all 35 remaining roots (census-pack55d, box): 33 exit 0, including all 9 tibia roots (arena, canary, host, map, offscreen, predict, suite, results, src) and both x roots (apps/client, apps/sim/spi); 0 ETY-RecordUpdateRetypesField anywhere. The 2 non-zero roots are the intentional negative apps/zed/fixtures/bad (Unification failure) and the Cells new_project template (placeholder manifest, parse error), both unrelated to the rule. The rule is installed on box, node and europa (n above).")
inl note_of_fiscal_regen_incremental_1_changed_gates_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGEN-INCREMENTAL-1-CHANGED-GATES", 1u32, "2026-11-06T12:44Z", "fiscal", "DoD: build.ps1 hashes every generated unit before and after the regen step, writes target/ci-metrics/regen-units.tsv (unit, before, after), and the unit-gate step runs only changed rows (an -AllUnits switch restores the full run); a run with an unchanged lib gates 0 units, a one-family XSD change gates that family. The pattern already works in scratch job scripts (node-es-object.ps1, 11-04). NEXT: read build.ps1 regen + gate steps.")
inl note_of_fiscal_regen_incremental_1_changed_gates_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGEN-INCREMENTAL-1-CHANGED-GATES", 2u32, "2026-11-06T12:46Z", "fiscal", "08:5x DoD CORRECTED before any code (read build.ps1): a full build (no -Files) deletes generated/, samples/, notebooks/ and target/ci-metrics/, regenerates, and checks drift against git; each unit's Cells result depends on its bytes AND on the lib packages, the compiler and generated_fiscal_runtime. So 'unit bytes unchanged' alone is NOT a safe skip: a lib or compiler change can change behaviour with identical unit text. NEW DoD: build.ps1 skips a generated unit's gate only when the key (unit sha256, lib digest = sha256 over lib/spiral/*.spi sorted, SpiralCompilerCore.dll sha256, runtime unit sha256) equals a row recorded green in target/unit-gate-cache/green.tsv (outside ci-metrics, which a full build wipes); every other unit is gated and green ones are recorded. CI runners start empty, so CI still gates everything (safe by construction). A -NoGateCache switch disables it. Proof: two consecutive local builds on the box with no change gate 0 units the second time; touching one family's XSD gates exactly that family; changing one lib file gates all. NEXT: implement in build.ps1 (in place, backup first).")
inl note_of_fiscal_regen_incremental_1_changed_gates_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGEN-INCREMENTAL-1-CHANGED-GATES", 3u32, "2026-11-06T12:48Z", "fiscal", "09:0x IMPLEMENTED in place, unstaged: fiscal/scripts/build.ps1 7FE74D33 -> 4D70767E (backup build.before-gate-cache-7FE74D33.ps1 in the session scratchpad; +34 -1). New -NoGateCache switch; Set-GateContext (after formatting) = lib digest (sha256 over lib/spiral/*.spi name:hash rows) + SpiralCompilerCore.dll sha256 + generated_fiscal_runtime unit sha256, loads target/unit-gate-cache/green.tsv; Invoke-TestFile skips a generated_* unit whose key (name, unit sha256, context) is recorded green and records green ones; src modules and generator are never keyed. Parse 0. LOGIC PROOF (box, functions extracted from the edited script, real tree, lib D6094C881D2B, core A688EE5AD426): key deterministic (5 parts), hit after record, MISS when the lib digest differs, disabled by -NoGateCache, src module never keyed. PENDING (heavy, host not chosen): the build-level proof (two consecutive builds, the second gates 0 generated units; one XSD change gates that family only), since every build also runs the 1,523 s format pass. Skipped units add no fileRows/testRows, so local reports omit them; CI runners start with an empty cache, so CI is unchanged.")
inl note_of_fiscal_regen_incremental_1_changed_gates_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGEN-INCREMENTAL-1-CHANGED-GATES", 4u32, "2026-11-06T13:43Z", "fiscal", "09:5x build-level proof PREPARED, not run: scratchpad buildproof\\run.ps1 builds a scratch fiscal (copies of scripts + src, generated_cfdi_tfd_1_1_certificates + the runtime unit, read-only junctions to deps/spiral and deps/corpus, so the live tree's samples/notebooks are untouched) and runs build.ps1 -Files <unit> twice; pass 2 must print 'gate cache: ... skipped' and green.tsv must hold 1 row. NOT RUN: the box reads 100% CPU with 2.3 GB free (other lanes), the node queue holds 6 fiscal proofs behind tibia/compiler jobs, and europa has no fiscal build setup. Pending, host: box when its load drops (one small Cells gate), else the node after job-1793971916580.")
inl note_of_fiscal_regen_incremental_1_changed_gates_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGEN-INCREMENTAL-1-CHANGED-GATES", 5u32, "2026-11-06T13:47Z", "fiscal", "09:4x build-level proof QUEUED on the node: job-1793972780376-fiscal-buildproof (after the docgate job): a scratch fiscal (build.ps1 4D70767E, src, generated_cfdi_tfd_1_1_certificates + runtime unit; read-only junctions to the t1101 mirror's spiral and corpus, scratch under remote-stage, not in the mirror) runs build.ps1 -Files <unit> twice; pass 2 must log the gate-cache skip and green.tsv must hold 1 row. Pending, host node.")
inl note_of_fiscal_regen_incremental_1_changed_gates_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGEN-INCREMENTAL-1-CHANGED-GATES", 6u32, "2026-11-06T15:56Z", "fiscal", "DONE 11:5x. PROOF (node job-1793972780376-fiscal-buildproof, scratch fiscal with build.ps1 4D70767E, lib digest 6B27C74FDBF9, core 257DB91886B9): pass 1 (436 s) formatted 2 units, gated generated_cfdi_tfd_1_1_certificates (discovered 1 executed 1 passed 1) and recorded 1 green row; pass 2 (87 s) formatted 0 (2 from cache, FISCAL-REGEN-INCREMENTAL-2 behaviour) and logged 'gate cache: same unit, lib, compiler and runtime as a green run; skipped'; green.tsv = 1 row. With the 09:0x logic proof (a changed lib digest misses), the DoD holds; CI runners start empty, so CI still gates everything.")
inl note_of_fiscal_regen_incremental_2_format_cache_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGEN-INCREMENTAL-2-FORMAT-CACHE", 1u32, "2026-11-06T12:44Z", "fiscal", "DoD: after a regen, format-generated.ps1 formats only units listed as changed in regen-units.tsv and reports the skipped count; a no-op regen formats 0 units (today a fixed 1,523 s for 83). NEXT: after step 1.")
inl note_of_fiscal_regen_incremental_2_format_cache_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGEN-INCREMENTAL-2-FORMAT-CACHE", 2u32, "2026-11-06T12:50Z", "fiscal", "Closed 11-06 09:0x: ALREADY MET by the existing scripts/format-generated.ps1 (0C8D80B8): its cache key is (formatter identity = sha256 of SpiralCompiler + SpiralCompilerCore, raw unit sha256) and it stores the formatted text, so a unit whose raw bytes did not change is restored from cache without formatting. PROOF (box, scratch root with 2 units generated_cfdi_pagos_2_0_certificates + generated_cfdi_tfd_1_1_certificates, pinned compiler a688): pass 1 '2 formatted, 0 from cache, 26 s'; pass 2 '0 formatted, 2 from cache, 0 s'. The 11-04 '0 from cache every time' was correct cache behaviour: the node's compiler core changed 7+ times that day (a new formatter each time) and lib changes rewrote every unit; target/format-cache is not cleared by build.ps1. No code change.")
inl note_of_fiscal_generic_nfe_checks_data_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-GENERIC-NFE-CHECKS-DATA", 1u32, "2026-11-06T13:35Z", "fiscal", "From the GENERIC-PROVABLE counter (1) re-run 11-06 09:3x: the generator's only per-country code left is nfe_model_checks + the NfeModelChecks branch of unit_checks_of (~36 lines, down from 489 on 11-01; the 20 family literals are data in families.spi since 11-03). DoD: family_extra NfeModelChecks carries its check text (or a list of typed checks) from families.spi, and the generator emits it generically; counter (1) on generator.spi = 0 outside tests; regen byte-identical (166 files, 0 differing). NEXT: after the GRANULAR v3 families land (same file).")
inl note_of_fiscal_generic_nfe_checks_data_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-GENERIC-NFE-CHECKS-DATA", 2u32, "2026-11-06T16:05Z", "fiscal", "12:0x DRAFT (kit drafts fiscal FISCAL-GENERIC-NFE-CHECKS-DATA\\src: families 4F24439F over live 6FEB454F, generator 482D799B over live 3B3D0A0E): family_extra NfeModelChecks -> ModelChecks : string; nfe_model_checks moved verbatim (33 lines) into families.spi; nfe_v4_00 = { (nfe_v4_base ()) with extras = [ Signed; ModelChecks (nfe_model_checks ()) ] }; generator unit_checks_of = model_check_texts family::extras (generic). Counter (1) on the draft generator: 0 per-country lines before its tests. format --check 0 both; GRANULAR 0 code overages both; box --check families 0 + generator 0. PROOF QUEUED: node job-1793981107602-fiscal-identity3, arm 'nfe' vs live must be byte-identical (166 files).")
inl note_of_fiscal_generic_nfe_checks_data_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-GENERIC-NFE-CHECKS-DATA", 3u32, "2026-11-06T20:29Z", "fiscal", "16:3x PROOF + LANDED. Identity (node laptop, core 257DB91886B97811, job-1793981107602-fiscal-identity3 arm 'nfe'): the full generator over the draft families 4F24439F + generator 482D799B compiles (103 s), rustc 1103 s, writes 166 files: 'nfe vs live / files 166, differing 0' (byte-identical regen, the DoD). Landed in place in fiscal/src (unstaged; backups families.before-nfe-checks-6FEB454F.spi and generator.before-nfe-checks-3B3D0A0E.spi in the session scratchpad): families 6FEB454F -> 4F24439F, generator 3B3D0A0E -> 482D799B. The generator's per-country code is now 0 before its tests (counter 1). DONE. Next on top: FISCAL-FAMILY-MANIFEST S3 (draft stacked on these exact bytes).")
inl note_of_fiscal_generic_nfe_checks_data_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-GENERIC-NFE-CHECKS-DATA", 4u32, "2026-11-06T20:30Z", "fiscal", "DoD: met (generator per-country lines 0 before tests; regen byte-identical).\nPROOF: green, node laptop job-1793981107602-fiscal-identity3 'nfe vs live / files 166, differing 0', core 257DB91886B97811; landed families 4F24439F + generator 482D799B in fiscal/src.")
inl note_of_fiscal_generic_laws_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-GENERIC-LAWS", 1u32, "2026-11-06T13:35Z", "fiscal", "DESIGN step (60 min, text only). Today every unit already gets generator-emitted law tests (writes_its_example: example round trip + real documents read back + twin), written once in generator.spi and instantiated per unit, which may already meet target (C)'s 'laws checked for every family by one generic test'. DoD: a note that lists each law, where it is stated once (generator function) and its per-unit instance name, plus the laws still missing (e.g. a generic example-validates-against-its-XSD law, today done outside Spiral by family-gates.ps1), each filed as its own item or marked met. NEXT: read generator family_checks / family_document_cells.")
inl note_of_fiscal_generic_laws_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-GENERIC-LAWS", 2u32, "2026-11-06T13:37Z", "fiscal", "DESIGN DONE 09:4x (generator.spi 3B3D0A0E, text only). Laws stated ONCE in the generator and emitted into every unit: L1 example round trip (xsd_example_check / json_example_check -> <unit>_writes_its_example); L2 real documents read back unchanged + recorded defects pinned (document_checks / read_back_list / defect_lines, same test); L3 JSON twin equality (twin generator draft CD099775, unlanded; FISCAL-MYINVOIS-SIGNATURE-TWIN); L4 validated types keep raw strings out, a type-level negative (family_nominal_check -> <unit>_keeps_raw_strings_out fails 'Unification failure'); L5 certificates hold (certificate_check -> <unit>_certificates_hold). Bench (family_bench) is a measurement, not a law. So target (C) is met in form: one statement per law, one instance per unit. MISSING: L6 'a missing required element is reported with its path, not raised' exists only for NF-e inside nfe_model_checks -> filed FISCAL-LAW-MISSING-REPORTED. NAMED GAP (kept outside Spiral on purpose): example-validates-against-its-official-XSD / JSON Schema runs in scripts/family-gates.ps1 (.NET XmlSchemaSet, Test-Json); a Spiral XSD validator is out of scope, and S3 of FISCAL-FAMILY-MANIFEST derives its rows from the manifest. DoD met.")
inl note_of_fiscal_generic_laws_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-GENERIC-LAWS", 3u32, "2026-11-06T13:38Z", "fiscal", "PROOF: a design step, so its evidence is the census itself, read from live generator.spi 3B3D0A0E by definition and line (family_example_check :412, family_nominal_check :509, certificate_check :519, document_checks :393, nfe_model_checks :544); no run was needed or claimed. The missing law is filed as FISCAL-LAW-MISSING-REPORTED.")
inl note_of_disk_alarm_rearm_1 () = Note ("DISK-ALARM-REARM", 1u32, "2026-11-06T13:47Z", "resilience-614162e5", "main+resilience 11-06: node-utilization-monitor DISK-LOW/WASTE/UNKNOWN dedupe on alarm TYPE (prior log line matches the keyword via $priorReal), so a WORSENING condition (node disk 14->10GB over 2h) fires ONCE at threshold and never re-alarms as it approaches 0 - owners get no update. FIX: store the last-alarmed level in the dedup marker (e.g. the stored line gets [ALARMED@10GB]) and re-alarm when the metric drops a further N GB (e.g. 3) below it, not just on keyword match. Keep the fail-open UNKNOWN logic + the call-operator delivery. Risky to edit the live alarm path mid-run; do carefully with a known-good test. Found during the 11-06 node-disk-exhaustion watch.")
inl note_of_disk_alarm_rearm_2 () = Note ("DISK-ALARM-REARM", 2u32, "2026-11-06T13:50Z", "resilience-614162e5", "IMPLEMENTED + TESTED 11-06: node-utilization-monitor dedup now stores the last-alarmed node-disk GB and re-alarms DISK-LOW only when the disk drops >=3GB below it (diskWorsened check on $priorReal). TESTED both ways: (1) baseline 14GB + current 10GB (4GB drop) -> RE-ARMED (new note, count 3->4); (2) stable 10GB -> DEDUPED (no spam, stayed 4). Delivery path (call-operator) untouched. Covers the worsening-condition gap found on the 11-06 node-disk watch. Remaining (optional): extend the same last-level dedup to WASTE/UNKNOWN; DISK-LOW (the one that bit us) is done.")
inl note_of_disk_alarm_rearm_3 () = Note ("DISK-ALARM-REARM", 3u32, "2026-11-06T13:52Z", "resilience-614162e5", "CLOSING Done: the meaningful DoD (DISK-LOW re-alarms on each further >=3GB drop, not deduping a worsening disk) is implemented + tested both ways (re-arm on a 4GB drop PASS; stable disk dedup PASS; delivery path untouched). The \"extend to WASTE/UNKNOWN\" idea is N/A - those are binary conditions (box-saturated-while-idle / probe-failed), not numeric-worsening metrics, so there is no level to re-arm on. Shipped in node-utilization-monitor.ps1 (unstaged). Closes the gap found on the 11-06 node-disk watch.")
inl note_of_fiscal_lib_granular_1_small_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-LIB-GRANULAR-1-SMALL", 1u32, "2026-11-06T13:56Z", "fiscal", "DoD: europa counter 0 code overages in the three modules; lib_land_window round trip; their :# blocks pass in the europa lib-body harness (eff-lib-run.sh) and a node Cells gate before landing. NEXT: read the 7 bodies.")
inl note_of_fiscal_lib_granular_1_small_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-LIB-GRANULAR-1-SMALL", 2u32, "2026-11-06T13:58Z", "fiscal", "TYPEFEATURES: none new; splits move existing match arms and string builders into named helpers with the same types. NEXT: read the 7 bodies.")
inl note_of_fiscal_lib_granular_1_small_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-LIB-GRANULAR-1-SMALL", 3u32, "2026-11-06T14:13Z", "fiscal", "10:1x DRAFTS (kit drafts spiral FISCAL-LIB-GRANULAR-1-SMALL\\v1): schematron_run F4C999DF (base 01691C2B6B7C: assertion_fires, fired_failure, assertion_failure, context_failure, rule_failures, nodes_step, rule_step, pattern_namespaces, start_scope), xsd_census A1D0EED7 (base 17B2E8ECEB0C: inline_census + typed_census in construct_walk's mutual group), xsd_constraints 2B606C8C (base 0E68DB26CFCD: constraint_of, is_constraint_tag, inner_owner, element_constraints in the group, missing_key, duplicate_of, seen_step, item_step, unselected). Europa GRANULAR counter: 0 CODE OVERAGES in all three (remaining findings are test blocks). Round trip PASSED for the three together (lib_land_window dry run, label fiscal-libgran1-1106). PROOF RUNNING on europa (load 0.65, 2.1 GB free; harness copy capped at MemoryMax 1500M per the MemAvailable - 600 rule): each module's :# bodies via eff-lib-run (check, compile, rustc, run), log ~/remote-stage/fiscal-check/libgran-1106.log.")
inl note_of_fiscal_lib_granular_1_small_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-LIB-GRANULAR-1-SMALL", 4u32, "2026-11-06T14:23Z", "fiscal", "10:2x EUROPA BODY PROOF GREEN (~/remote-stage/fiscal-check/libgran-1106b.log; europa compiler core dd18614c6b1e38cf, rustc capped MemoryMax 1500M, avail ~2070 MB, load <= 1.5): schematron_run F4C999DF check 0 / 5 bodies compile 0 / rustc 0 / run 0; xsd_census A1D0EED7 check 0 / 1 body / 0 / 0 / 0; xsd_constraints 2B606C8C check 0 / 1 body / 0 / 0 / 0. (First attempt VOID: stage had only lib's top-level .spi, so state_core's open leptos was unbound; rebuilt with the full lib tree, 150 files.) Cells confirmation QUEUED on the node: job-1793974969967-fiscal-libgran1-gate (draft-only, pinned compiler, fresh stage, after the buildproof job). Land after it is green.")
inl note_of_fiscal_lib_granular_1_small_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-LIB-GRANULAR-1-SMALL", 5u32, "2026-11-06T16:22Z", "fiscal", "DONE 12:2x. PROOF: node job-1793974969967-fiscal-libgran1-gate (core 257DB918, fresh stage, drafts over the box lib): schematron_run 5/5, xsd_census 1/1, xsd_constraints 1/1 green; plus the europa body run (all exit 0) and europa GRANULAR 0 code overages. LANDED via lib_land_window -Apply, label fiscal-libgran1-1106: type-probe 3/3 PASS, 0 respell drift, schematron_run 01691C2B -> F4C999DF, xsd_census 17B2E8EC -> A1D0EED7, xsd_constraints 0E68DB26 -> 2B606C8C; lib digest 802255DD84EF3FDF; undo %USERPROFILE%\\AppData\\Local\\spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261106-121457. In place, unstaged.")
inl note_of_fiscal_lib_granular_2_xpath_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-LIB-GRANULAR-2-XPATH", 1u32, "2026-11-06T13:56Z", "fiscal", "DoD: as step 1 for xpath and xpath_eval; the Peppol/ZATCA/RO corpus_checks rule tests stay green (they run xpath_eval). NEXT: after step 1.")
inl note_of_fiscal_lib_granular_2_xpath_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-LIB-GRANULAR-2-XPATH", 2u32, "2026-11-06T14:15Z", "fiscal", "10:1x PLAN from x's rows: 32 code overages, led by xpath parse_expr 7005, xpath_eval domain_items 4312, xpath function_of 2929, xpath_text 1996, lift_code_lists 1491, tokens_from 1426, node_count 1253; then step_axis_of 722, operator_of 646, comparison_of 607 and ~20 bodies of 274-505. The four *_of functions are string -> constructor dispatch: rewrite each as a literal (name, constructor) table (pure literals weigh 0 under GRANULAR) + one shared lookup, which turns code into data. parse_expr / domain_items / xpath_text / node_count / lift_code_lists are one-arm-per-constructor walks: split by constructor family into named helpers. Estimate raised: two 120-min windows (2a tables + small bodies, 2b the walks). TYPEFEATURES: none new. NEXT: after step 1 lands.")
inl note_of_fiscal_lib_granular_2_xpath_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-LIB-GRANULAR-2-XPATH", 3u32, "2026-11-06T14:30Z", "fiscal", "10:3x STEP 2a DRAFT xpath.spi 1322B960 (base 913055B1E126; kit drafts spiral FISCAL-LIB-GRANULAR-2-XPATH\\v1): table_lookup + literal tables axis_names / comparison_names / operator_names / bool_function_names (20) / value_function_names (34; 54 distinct keys) replace the string dispatch in step_axis_of, comparison_of, operator_of, function_of; comparison_text split by flavor; name_end via colon_then + is_star. Europa counter: xpath code overages 11 -> 5 (left: tokens_from 1426, parse_expr 7005, xpath_text 1996, node_count 1253, lift_code_lists 1491 = step 2b walks). Round trip PASSED. Europa bodies: xpath 4/4 green (check/compile/rustc/run 0); xpath_eval VOID (rustc killed 137 at the 1500M cap; europa's MemAvailable - 600 cannot fit its 26 bodies). Node Cells gate QUEUED: job-1793975408096-fiscal-libgran2-gate (xpath + xpath_eval over the draft, after libgran1). xpath_eval's ~20 near-budget bodies (274-505): weights do not track body text as expected (third_text stays 495 when reshaped onto 4 lines; budget prints 272 or 271 within one file), so asked kit for the rule before splitting them.")
inl note_of_fiscal_lib_granular_2_xpath_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-LIB-GRANULAR-2-XPATH", 4u32, "2026-11-06T14:39Z", "fiscal", "10:4x kit's counter rule (cell_budget.ex, 10:3x): a CELL is a blank-line block (a run of definitions with no blank line between them is ONE cell); weight = code points (2 for chars above U+10FF; autolink tokens 23); a ?= match weighs its header line + longest arm; header excluded when it splits off; limit = 280 - cell header (272 for cells 1-9, 271 for 10-99). Applied: xpath_text's multi-line arms moved to xpath_step_text / xpath_binary_text / xpath_quantified_text / xpath_if_text / xpath_castable_text in its :& group, and the group's members separated by blank lines (memory: a blank line before :& keeps the group); xpath code overages 5 -> 4 (left: tokens_from, parse_expr, node_count, lift_code_lists). xpath_eval: blank-line pass over the code region (19 blank lines, non-blank text identical to live) 21 -> 18 code overages (domain_items 4312 was mostly its shared block); the 18 left are real small bodies at 274-318. Drafts: xpath 71C7C7C1, xpath_eval AF12C4E2; round trip of both PASSED (70 s). The queued node gate job-1793975408096 now reads both (inputs replaced and hash-verified before start).")
inl note_of_fiscal_lib_granular_2_xpath_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-LIB-GRANULAR-2-XPATH", 5u32, "2026-11-06T15:19Z", "fiscal", "11:2x xpath_eval CODE OVERAGES 21 -> 0 (draft 0FA9326A): 18 helper splits (mod11_holds, abn_sum, namespaced_name_matches, bool_value_text, within_slack, clamped_bounds, anchor_skip, flagged_match, token_value, last_token, has_group_reference, pattern_replace, cents_digits, designator_step, date_parts_valid, time_parts_valid, undigited_value, first_argument, second_text, mapped_one in the mapped_each group) + castable_checks table over xpath's table_lookup (so xpath_eval and xpath land together) + the blank-line pass. Names checked for collisions across lib. Box --check (pin a688): xpath_eval 0, schematron_run 0, xsd_constraints 0. Round trip of xpath 71C7C7C1 + xpath_eval 0FA9326A PASSED (97 s). The queued node gate job-1793975408096 now reads 0FA9326A (hash-verified on the node before start). Left in step 2: xpath's 4 walks (tokens_from, parse_expr, node_count, lift_code_lists) = step 2b.")
inl note_of_fiscal_lib_granular_2_xpath_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-LIB-GRANULAR-2-XPATH", 6u32, "2026-11-06T16:05Z", "fiscal", "12:0x step 2b DONE in draft (by a fiscal subagent, VERIFIED by fiscal): xpath C9624585 = 0 code overages (parser group split into 17 xpath_parse_* helpers; parse_expr's quantifier/for heads now share xpath_parse_binding with the same order and fallback; parse_axis_step splits on the first token, preserving the old precedence); tests identical to live; LF; round trip of xpath C9624585 + xpath_eval 0FA9326A PASSED; agent --check xpath/xpath_eval/schematron_run 0 and format --check 0. The queued node gate job-1793975408096 now reads xpath C9624585 (swapped and hash-verified before start). Whole step 2: xpath 11 -> 0, xpath_eval 21 -> 0.")
inl note_of_fiscal_lib_granular_2_xpath_7 () = Note ("FISCAL-LIB-GRANULAR-2-XPATH", 7u32, "2026-11-06T17:29Z", "fiscal", "13:1x PROOF green (node laptop, core 257DB91886B97811): job-1793975408096-fiscal-libgran2-gate exit 0 over xpath C9624585 + xpath_eval 0FA9326A: xpath 4/4 and xpath_eval 26/26 passed in 2110 s. Correction to the 12:0x note: xpath_eval 0FA9326A FAILED format --check on the box pin (first_argument's one-line ?= match); the formatted copy 049AED14 differs only in that layout, 0 GRANULAR code overages (europa counter), tests identical, LF (draft v2). LANDED via lib_land_window (label fiscal-libgran2-1106): xpath C9624585A404, xpath_eval 049AED14CC23, lib digest 0674A5613059E8E9, undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261106-131555; consumers compile, document_test 26/26, type_probe PASS 2/2 (4 + 26 tests typed), 0 respell-drift. The first -Apply (12:59) was refused by an unrelated red: the user's dice push 3c50872 (12:46) replaced the contract's lib.dice.rotate_numbers call with roll_within_bounds, so document_test.exs:553 asserted a string that no longer exists; updated that assertion to 'lib.dice.roll_within_bounds max' (spiral apps/cells/test/spiral/document_test.exs, unstaged). Step 2 DONE.")
