inl note_of_fiscal_lib_granular_5_regex_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-LIB-GRANULAR-5-REGEX", 2u32, "2026-11-06T16:29Z", "fiscal", "12:2x DRAFT xsd_regex.spi 5963371C (base 4081FC994A26; kit drafts spiral FISCAL-LIB-GRANULAR-5-REGEX\\v1), by a fiscal subagent, VERIFIED by fiscal: europa GRANULAR 13 -> 0 code overages; tests identical to live; LF; round trip PASSED; agent --check xsd_regex / xsd_emit / xpath_eval 0 and format --check 0. 36 regex_-prefixed helpers (unused in lib and fiscal/generated). Review notes: ranges_compare, rx_compare, nullability_of, class_items and class_end now head mutual groups with their new helpers; derive_by / parse_alt / invalid_from groups gained members; regex_derive_seq is a generic (\\* f.) group member; ranges_compare compares the head pair via regex_range_order (same result as the old four-way chain). PROOFS QUEUED on the node: arm lib5 added to job-1793981107602-fiscal-identity3 (regen byte identity; the DFA pattern code in every unit comes from here; inputs hash-verified before start) and Cells gate job-1793982560349-fiscal-libgran5-gate. TYPEFEATURES: none new.")
inl note_of_fiscal_lib_granular_5_regex_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-LIB-GRANULAR-5-REGEX", 3u32, "2026-11-06T20:47Z", "fiscal", "16:4x IDENTITY green (node laptop, core 257DB91886B97811, job-1793981107602-fiscal-identity3 arm 'lib5'): the full generator over the draft xsd_regex 5963371C writes 166 files, 'lib5 vs live / files 166, differing 0'. PENDING (node laptop): its own Cells gate job-1793982560349-fiscal-libgran5-gate, queued right after identity3; land via lib_land_window (base 4081FC994A26) when it is green.")
inl note_of_fiscal_lib_granular_5_regex_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-LIB-GRANULAR-5-REGEX", 4u32, "2026-11-06T22:13Z", "fiscal", "18:1x PROOF + LANDED. Gate (node laptop, core 8F0094967068FC85 = pack57 start and end): job-1793982560349-fiscal-libgran5-gate exit 0, draft xsd_regex 5963371C: discovered 8 executed 8 passed 8 failed 0 in 214 s. Identity (16:4x, core 257DB91886B97811): 'lib5 vs live: 166 files, 0 differing'. Landed via lib_land_window (label fiscal-libgran5-1106, base 4081FC994A26; waited behind another lane's dice_contract Cells window first): xsd_regex 5963371C0993, lib digest F97B0887839AF348, undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261106-180014; consumers compile, document_test 26/26, type_probe PASS (8 tests typed), 0 respell-drift.\nDoD: xsd_regex 22 code overages to 0 with the module's tests green and generated output unchanged: met.\nPROOF: green, node laptop job-1793982560349 8/8 + identity arm lib5 0 differing; landed 5963371C0993.")
inl note_of_fiscal_lib_granular_5_regex_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-LIB-GRANULAR-5-REGEX", 5u32, "2026-11-06T23:34Z", "fiscal", "20:0x CORRECTION: this step met its stated count under the agreed before-first-test-line metric, but a per-cell recount finds code cells after interleaved test blocks still over budget on the landed bytes; filed as FISCAL-LIB-GRANULAR-7-INTERLEAVED (xml 13, xsd_resolve 12, xsd_regex 8). The landed bytes stay (proven green and output-identical); only the '0 code overages' wording was too strong.")
inl note_of_cells_temp_leak_1 () = Note ("CELLS-TEMP-LEAK", 1u32, "2026-11-06T14:19Z", "x", "2026-11-06 10:19 x: filed from resilience's 11-06 report. On the node, Temp\\spiral_cells held 4.5 GB, the top node-disk user, which drove the DISK-LOW. resilience pruned 1.3 GB (112 dirs older than 24 h) and deployed the cells-temp-janitor task (daily 04:17, prunes dirs older than 24 h). Causes, read from cells.ex 57-78: (1) File.rm_rf(dir) in after ignores failures, and on Windows a still-running or just-exited cell.exe and its .pdb can hold locks; (2) a job stop or wall-clock kill of the BEAM skips after entirely, as x's own x-cellsfix1b and 2d stops did today. DoD: (1) rm_rf failure is retried once after the cell process exits, and logged if it persists; (2) at Cells start, dirs under the tmp root older than 24 h (by mtime, not active by lock) are removed, so the janitor becomes a backstop; (3) a test creates an old dir and a fresh one and asserts only the old one goes.")
inl note_of_cells_temp_leak_2 () = Note ("CELLS-TEMP-LEAK", 2u32, "2026-11-06T14:22Z", "x", "2026-11-06 10:22 x: DRAFTED (kit drafts spiral\\CELLS-TEMP-LEAK): new Spiral.Cells.TempSweep (temp_sweep.ex) removes only DIRECTORIES under tmp\\spiral_cells whose mtime is older than 24 h; a dir whose rm_rf fails on a lock is skipped, not fatal. It is called from Mix.Tasks.Spiral.Notebook.run (the gate path, which never starts the app; base 52D8DB24A170) and from Application.start (Livebook; base 70B77E611DBF). cells.ex stays untouched, since two drafts already layer on it. New temp_sweep_test.exs: 3 tests (old vs fresh, files left alone, missing root). Scope cut from the DoD: no rm_rf retry in cells.ex, because the start sweep reclaims what a lock or a killed BEAM leaves. NEXT STEP: gate on the node after the Cells order fix settles. Hashes: application.ex 2221C04AB21A; apply.ps1 700348A42C31; spiral.notebook.ex B974AA247341; temp_sweep_test.exs 8651727A7AC8; temp_sweep.ex D831B71B6AE4")
inl note_of_cells_temp_leak_3 () = Note ("CELLS-TEMP-LEAK", 3u32, "2026-11-06T14:22Z", "x", "NEXT STEP: gate the 4-file draft on the node (temp_sweep_test, notebook_test) in the next x Cells job, then land with -ProvenLog.")
inl note_of_cells_temp_leak_4 () = Note ("CELLS-TEMP-LEAK", 4u32, "2026-11-06T23:21Z", "x", "2026-11-06 19:2x x: related find, cause UNPROVEN. x-simargs57 (19:2x) failed every test with ':lock_timeout' from Cells' 180 s mount FileLock, and that shows up as 'failed', not VOID. The only lock file on the node is cells-mounts\\9befbe936c7de7d3.lock (10-28, pid 6872), 9 days stale, but today's v3 keys can't match a 10-28 key, so it probably isn't the one waited on. A live concurrent mount build (x-media3c) is the other candidate. To do here: (1) remove locks whose holder pid is gone (the agile-lock-stale-by-holder rule), e.g. that 10-28 one; (2) report lock_timeout as VOID like a cell timeout (CELLS-TIMEOUT-IS-VOID step 2).")
inl note_of_cells_temp_leak_5 () = Note ("CELLS-TEMP-LEAK", 5u32, "2026-11-07T00:20Z", "x", "2026-11-06 20:20 x: LANDED on the box (unstaged): new temp_sweep.ex D831B71B6AE4, application.ex 70B77E611DBF -> 2221C04AB21A, mix task spiral.notebook.ex 52D8DB24A170 -> B974AA247341, new temp_sweep_test.exs 8651727A7AC8. Closed by -ProvenLog from x-templeak1 (job-1794010581273, node, pack57; temp_sweep 3 + cells_test 39 = 42 passed), byte-identical; undo cells-20261106-202020. Run dirs under tmp\\spiral_cells older than 24 h are now removed at every gate start and at Livebook app start. NEXT STEP: the stale-mount-lock part from n4 (locks whose holder pid is gone), then Done.")
inl note_of_cells_temp_leak_6 () = Note ("CELLS-TEMP-LEAK", 6u32, "2026-11-07T18:56Z", "x", "2026-11-07 14:55 x: CLOSED, no code needed for the stale-lock part (read from source, not assumed). Cells' FileLock.with_lock already reclaims a lock whose holder pid is dead: holder_dead? checks the recorded pid every 2 s while waiting (via Runner.os_pid_alive?, with a 5 s grace for unreadable files) and removes the lock before claiming. So a dead-holder lock can't cause :lock_timeout. The 11-06 x-simargs57 lock_timeout therefore had a LIVE holder (a concurrent mount build), which is a contention case, not a leak. Its reporting fix (lock_timeout as VOID) belongs to CELLS-TIMEOUT-IS-VOID step 2. An orphan .lock under an old v2 mount key (e.g. 9befbe936c7de7d3.lock from 10-28) is never contended, so it is inert litter of a few bytes. Sweeping it would add Elixir under a non-port label, which CELLS-ELIXIR-RATCHET now refuses. DoD met: the run-dir sweep landed 11-06 (temp_sweep, 42 tests on the node).")
inl note_of_xdumps_decay_recovery_report_1 () = Note ("XDUMPS-DECAY-RECOVERY-REPORT", 1u32, "2026-11-06T14:27Z", "x-dumps", "Quantify per-account decay (alive-at-original vs alive-now) + recovered-missed from the enrichment re-harvest, as an archive-health metric for X-DUMPS-1-0-DOD + the final report. So far: fc1943s 0 net decay (2350=2350), stewshka recovering ~500 the original missed (874->~1380), i574n TBD. Next: after the merge, compute per-account pre-enrich vs merged deltas + the gone-at-original vs decayed-since split. CPU-light (count/compare ndjson).")
inl note_of_xdumps_decay_recovery_report_2 () = Note ("XDUMPS-DECAY-RECOVERY-REPORT", 2u32, "2026-11-06T15:11Z", "x-dumps", "DONE 11-06. Per-account decay/recovery (pre-enrich-alive ids vs new tombstones + new-alive): fc1943s orig_alive=2350 decayed_since=0 recovered_new=8; i574n orig_alive=598 decayed=0 recovered=2; stewshka orig_alive=872 decayed=0 recovered=0. HEADLINE: ZERO decay across all reachable accounts - not one tweet alive at the original harvest has been lost since; the archive is fully intact. +10 recovered (fc1943s 8, i574n 2) = tweets the original run missed, now captured. Enrichment applied to 3813 reachable tweets. Corrects the earlier '~500 stewshka recovery' (that was an early-partial extrapolation; actual recovery is +10 total, decay 0). This validates the capture-before-decay + off-box-backup premise: the content held perfectly. Method: comm pre-enrich-ids vs tombstones.ndjson (decay) + vs enriched-alive-ids (recovery).")
inl note_of_xdumps_media_count_reconcile_1 () = Note ("XDUMPS-MEDIA-COUNT-RECONCILE", 1u32, "2026-11-06T14:27Z", "x-dumps", "Reconcile media-file counts vs world media references per account (I found fc1943s had 961 extracted media files vs 1082 world media refs = 121 gap 11-06). Determine if the gap is videos stored differently, duplicate media_keys, or genuinely unfetched media (a recovery gap). CPU-light: compare C:\\home\\xdumps\\media\\accounts\\<h>\\media file counts vs the world's distinct media paths per account.")
inl note_of_xdumps_media_count_reconcile_2 () = Note ("XDUMPS-MEDIA-COUNT-RECONCILE", 2u32, "2026-11-06T14:29Z", "x-dumps", "RECONCILE DONE 11-06. Per account (extracted media files vs distinct world media refs): fc1943s 961 extracted / 1082 referenced = 132 MISSING (86 jpg, 40 mp4, 6 png); i574n 444/444 = 0; stewshka 764/764 = 0. The 132 fc1943s missing are media (e.g. images _2/_3 of multi-image tweets + 40 videos) the media stage never downloaded (likely size/timeout failures), NOT missing tweets - the tweet text is captured. Since fc1943s has 0 decay (tweets alive), those media URLs likely still resolve -> RE-DOWNLOADABLE. Also stewshka's media gap will GROW after the rebuild adds the ~500 recovered tweets' media refs. Follow-up action filed: XDUMPS-MEDIA-REFETCH. Reconcile complete; closing.")
inl note_of_xdumps_media_refetch_1 () = Note ("XDUMPS-MEDIA-REFETCH", 1u32, "2026-11-06T14:30Z", "x-dumps", "From the reconcile (XDUMPS-MEDIA-COUNT-RECONCILE): re-run the xarchive media stage to fetch media the original harvest missed - fc1943s 132 (86 jpg/40 mp4/6 png) + stewshka's ~500 recovered tweets' media (after the enrichment rebuild). Tweets are alive (fc1943s 0 decay) so media URLs likely still resolve. Runs on europa; schedule AFTER the current re-harvest + enrichment rebuild to avoid competing. Then re-extract + re-rebuild the world. CPU/network-light-ish per account.")
inl note_of_xdumps_media_refetch_2 () = Note ("XDUMPS-MEDIA-REFETCH", 2u32, "2026-11-06T14:32Z", "x-dumps", "Command VERIFIED 11-06 (read media.rs): the media stage is INCREMENTAL - for each wanted media ref, if local.exists() it's cached/skipped; only missing refs are fetched (Cache::Immutable), media.tsv rewritten. So xarchive /data/x media fc1943s fetches ONLY the 132 missing (skips the 961 present) - safe + cheap. Sequence: run fc1943s media anytime (data stable); run stewshka media AFTER the enrichment rebuild (so its ~500 recovered tweets' media refs are in the data). Run on europa AFTER the current live re-harvest completes (avoid competing, though media hits pbs/video.twimg.com vs syndication). Then re-extract to box + re-rebuild world. Ready to execute post-rebuild.")
inl note_of_xdumps_media_refetch_3 () = Note ("XDUMPS-MEDIA-REFETCH", 3u32, "2026-11-06T15:23Z", "x-dumps", "DONE 11-06. Ran the media stage (xa-media) for all 3 reachable accounts. RECOVERED 8 media (fc1943s live=4, i574n live=4) - media the original harvest missed that was still fetchable. REMAINING MISSING ~263 (fc1943s 84, i574n 80, stewshka 99): the media stage attempted + failed (live=0 for stewshka, missing counts) = the media URLs are DEAD. So most missing media is genuinely GONE from Twitter's CDN even though the TWEETS are alive (media deleted/expired independently of the tweet). Honest outcome: recovered all that's re-fetchable (8); the ~263 are unreachable (tweet text preserved, media attachments gone). World rebuilt (timeline->merge->world, posts=163317) to reference the +8. Corrects the earlier optimistic 'alive tweets -> media re-downloadable' - true only for the 8; media decays independently. Closing: recovery exhausted.")
inl note_of_auto_export_1_monomorphic_1 () = Note ("AUTO-EXPORT-1-MONOMORPHIC", 1u32, "2026-11-06T14:33Z", "compiler", "11-06 compiler: split from LINK-AUTO-EXPORT (census 10:3x: class 1 = 174 of 314 regex cross-file call uses). DoD: an opt-in manifest flag (spiral.toml / package.spiproj); at the unit build the compiler synthesizes the export of each top-level definition whose inferred type has no forall and whose argument/result have a link-boundary form; unit.json unchanged for units without the flag; a linked sample with 3 auto-exported functions and Calls checks passes on Rust and Gleam. NEXT STEP: find where Export ops are collected from main's residual and add synthesized exports before unitGraphJson. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: the flag is a closed union in the manifest model (LinkExports = Listed | Monomorphic), not a string.")
inl note_of_auto_export_1_monomorphic_2 () = Note ("AUTO-EXPORT-1-MONOMORPHIC", 2u32, "2026-11-06T14:36Z", "compiler", "11-06 10:4x compiler: DESIGN (read at the pack53c core). The unit build binds main = env.term[\"main\"] (file_build ~36257) and peval's it (~36283); a hand-written export is just EOp(_, Export, [name literal; definition E]) evaluated inside main. So auto-export = rewrite main before peval: main' = ESeq of one synthesized EOp(Export, [ELit \"<unit>_<name>\"; <definition E>]) per candidate, then the original main. Candidates come from the prepass adds of the unit's OWN modules (AInclude small -> small.term), not from opens. A candidate is a definition whose E is an EFun' chain of length 1 (step 1) with an annotation on its parameter and no EForall' wrapper; that is the census class 1, and peval can instantiate it without a call site. Export names stay \"<unit>_<definition>\", so unitGraphJson and the consumer's definitionSources matching need no change. The flag lives in the manifest model; units without it are untouched (main unchanged, so unit.json is byte-identical). Risks to cover in the sample: an auto-export colliding with a hand-written one of the same definition (dedupe by definition identity), and definitions whose boundary form is refused (function-typed argument): skip them silently, or warn under a verbose flag.")
inl note_of_auto_export_1_monomorphic_3 () = Note ("AUTO-EXPORT-1-MONOMORPHIC", 3u32, "2026-11-06T14:44Z", "compiler", "11-06 10:5x compiler: DRAFTED. kitdo 1-link-exports-monomorphic.kitdo (kit drafts, 9 replacements, dry run ok on the pack53c tree core). Manifest field `link-exports: monomorphic` (RawSchema.linkExports, parsed like default-int, resolved Schema.linkExports; toml form link-exports = \"monomorphic\" goes through tomlManifestText unchanged). file_link_exports reads it per file. The prepass fold now also collects own_terms (the AInclude terms of the unit's own modules, never opens). LinkAutoExport.main prepends ESeq(EOp(Export, [ELit \"<unit>_<name>\"; <definition E>])) to main's body for each own definition shaped EAnnot(EFun' with a non-function body), i.e. annotated, one argument group, no forall: exactly what peval's Export arm accepts (DFunction with a TFun annotation, ~11258). Units without the flag: main is untouched, so their output and unit.json stay identical. Sample (unstaged): samples/linked_rust_auto_export (model has `link-exports: monomorphic` and NO export lines; app calls double, square, is_big on a dyn input; exit 63; Calls = model_double, model_square, model_is_big), plus its Linked matrix row. Candidate pack56 = pack55d + this, building. DoD as filed. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: the flag is a string in this first program; the closed union (Listed | Monomorphic) follows in the review if the field gains a second value.")
inl note_of_auto_export_1_monomorphic_4 () = Note ("AUTO-EXPORT-1-MONOMORPHIC", 4u32, "2026-11-06T15:18Z", "compiler", "11-06 11:2x compiler: WORKS END TO END on candidate pack56c (core of pack55d + this program). Two fixes on the way: (1) the manifest field is `auto-export: monomorphic`; `link-exports` failed to parse because the record parser matched the existing `link` field as a prefix and then expected \":\"; (2) definitions arrive as a bare EFun' with the annotation in its type slot (SPIRAL_AUTO_EXPORT_TRACE=1: \"auto-export: unit model own 4 [double:fun is_big:fun main:fun square:fun] candidates [double is_big square] main fun\"), not wrapped in EAnnot, so the matcher accepts both shapes. Result on samples/linked_rust_auto_export: model.rs gains pub fn model_double / model_is_big / model_square with no export lines in model.spi; app main.rs calls model::model_double(v0), model::model_square(v0), model::model_is_big(v2); rustc builds both crates and the binary exits 63 (expected 63). The trace env var stays as a diagnostic (like SPIRAL_RUST_GAP_TRACE). NEXT STEP: review pack56c against the installed pack55d (linked 16 rows, smoke), then pack57 = installed tree + this program.")
inl note_of_auto_export_1_monomorphic_5 () = Note ("AUTO-EXPORT-1-MONOMORPHIC", 5u32, "2026-11-06T15:57Z", "compiler", "11-06 11:5x compiler: pack57 REVIEW GREEN (candidate pack56c; its source equals the installed tree + this program byte for byte: core EEB524A747997CB2, host 9452B1A2EBD761EB). Linked: 16/16 pass vs installed 15/16; the only differing cells are the new samples/linked_rust_auto_export row (compiles, runs, exit 63 on pack57; compile error on pack55d, which has no auto-export). Smoke: residuals identical; 2 TypeScript native timeouts under 100% load (function_call, native_closure_capture) reran exit 0 / 42, agreeing with C, DISAGREE 0. Units without the flag are untouched: every other linked row has 0 differing cells. INSTALLING on the box (install-when-clear -Name pack57, %TEMP%\\compiler-pack57-chain.log); node ship via main. Docs: tmp/AGENTS.md paragraph after the -Suite linked section.")
inl note_of_auto_export_1_monomorphic_6 () = Note ("AUTO-EXPORT-1-MONOMORPHIC", 6u32, "2026-11-06T18:16Z", "compiler", "11-06 14:1x compiler: INSTALLED on the box in pack57 (core 8F0094967068FC85), together with AUTO-EXPORT-2 (curried wrappers) and RUST-GROUP-ARM-STRING-FOLD. The install queued at 11:56 never ran (it named a pack57 candidate that was never built; its dry run looped on 'candidate source missing'), so this is the first real install. Asked main to ship it to node and europa; Done when shipped.")
inl note_of_auto_export_1_monomorphic_7 () = Note ("AUTO-EXPORT-1-MONOMORPHIC", 7u32, "2026-11-06T20:39Z", "compiler", "11-06 16:4x compiler: DONE. pack57 SHIPPED to all three hosts (main 16:4x): box core 8F0094967068FC85 / host 734CEF2EBF4E7DD4 (14:1x), node the same in place 16:38 (fresh launch exit 0), europa Linux build from source E0AC98300538F224 (core e6a3e4d0e7336508, launch exit 0, 14:36).")
inl note_of_tibia_prereg_lsh_lanes_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-PREREG-LSH-LANES", 1u32, "2026-11-06T14:33Z", "tibia", "11-06 10:33 tibia: Split from TIBIA-NUGGET-LSH-TABLE (main's light floor). DoD: a PR section in BENCHMARK.md written before job-1793968277925-tibia-hashed-lanes reports, with the prediction and decision rule fixed. NEXT: write it now; the job is last in the node chain.")
inl note_of_tibia_prereg_lsh_lanes_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-PREREG-LSH-LANES", 2u32, "2026-11-06T14:35Z", "tibia", "11-06 10:35 tibia: DONE. PR-29 is written in tibia docs/BENCHMARK.md (unstaged), placed newest-first above PR-28, while job-1793968277925-tibia-hashed-lanes is still queued (it is last in the node chain and has not started), so it precedes any result. Proof: the section's Question, Arms (hashed_tactic at robust_plan, lanes 0-3, against the network's 8-lane held-out median -68,350 and worst -71,900), Metric, Prediction (table weaker: median below -68,350 with 3+ of 4 lanes below), and a Decision rule fixed with no added lanes.")
inl note_of_auto_export_2_curried_1 () = Note ("AUTO-EXPORT-2-CURRIED", 1u32, "2026-11-06T14:33Z", "compiler", "11-06 compiler: split from LINK-AUTO-EXPORT (census: class 2 = 137 more uses, which takes class 1+2 to 99%). Today a call to a curried linked definition inlines with the warning \"its definition is curried, so the call has no single argument\" (ExternCalls lookup_curried). DoD: the unit exports f' : (a * b * c) -> r for a curried f; a consumer call f a b c of a linked unit's curried definition becomes one cross-unit call with a tuple; partial application still inlines (stated); linked sample with a 3-argument curried function plus Calls checks. NEXT STEP: read the curried path in peval's Apply (ExternCalls.lookup_curried) to see where the full application chain is visible. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: arity as an int newtype on the export record.")
inl note_of_auto_export_2_curried_2 () = Note ("AUTO-EXPORT-2-CURRIED", 2u32, "2026-11-06T14:48Z", "compiler", "11-06 10:5x compiler: DESIGN (read at the pack53c core). peval's apply (~10315) applies a DFunction to ONE argument and links only when ExternCalls.lookup finds the body; a curried f a b c returns an intermediate DFunction after each step, so the link decision cannot be made at the first application (lazy peval has no lookahead). So do it at the E level, before peval, on both sides. UNIT: for a curried auto-export candidate f of arity n (an EAnnot over n nested EFun'), synthesize the export of an uncurried wrapper `fun (a1, ..., an) => f a1 ... an`, with its annotation built from f's arrow chain (tuple domain, same range). unitGraphJson records target = f's own (path, name) (not the empty lambda target) plus `arity: n`, and readUnitCalls carries the arity. CONSUMER: a prepass-level rewrite of a fully applied EApply chain of length n whose head is a linked curried definition into EApply(<uncurried stub E>, EPair chain of the n arguments). The stub's definitionSources key is (path, name), so the existing ExternCalls.lookup links it through the single-argument path unchanged (Rust passes the tuple fields as separate parameters, the multi_ranges path). Partial applications (fewer than n) and over-application stay inlined, stated in the docs. NEXT STEP: find the consumer-side hook. Prepass E is produced per module; the linked units' arity table must be known at that point (file_linked_units is already called during the build, so read it in prepass for the entry's package). TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: arity as a positive int newtype in the graph record; the stub as a typed record {path; name; arity}, never a string key.")
inl note_of_auto_export_2_curried_3 () = Note ("AUTO-EXPORT-2-CURRIED", 3u32, "2026-11-06T15:25Z", "compiler", "11-06 11:3x compiler: DESIGN REFINED after AUTO-EXPORT-1 landed on a candidate. Do NOT build E stubs at peval time: a synthesized EFun' needs prepass Scope/Id values, which is fragile. Instead work at the Raw level of the UNIT package, whose prepass is shared by the unit's own build and by every consumer (the consumer lists the unit under packages:). (1) For each curried candidate f of arity n (annotated parameter groups, no forall) in a module of a unit with auto-export: monomorphic, the module's Raw block list gains a top-level `f__uncurried (a1, ..., an) : r = f a1 ... an` with the tuple domain annotated from f's groups. That is a class-1 definition, so AUTO-EXPORT-1 exports it as <unit>_f__uncurried with no new export code. (2) In the consumer, the prepass (or a Raw rewrite before it) turns a fully applied RawApply chain of length n whose head resolves to that unit's f into an application of f__uncurried to the tuple; definitionSources then maps it to (path, \"f__uncurried\"), which the unit graph already lists, so ExternCalls.lookup links it unchanged. Partial and over-application stay as they are (inlined). Risks for the sample: name collision with a user-written f__uncurried (refuse with a named error), and pattern-matching parameters (only plain annotated variables qualify; others stay inlined, stated).")
inl note_of_auto_export_2_curried_4 () = Note ("AUTO-EXPORT-2-CURRIED", 4u32, "2026-11-06T15:28Z", "compiler", "11-06 11:3x compiler: HOOK LOCATED. Prepass (spiral_compiler.fs ~29811) consumes the typechecker's filled_top per top statement, so a synthesized f__uncurried must exist BEFORE inference, as a block of the unit's module, not at prepass. The injection point is the module's block stream for files of a package whose schema has auto-export: monomorphic: for each parsed curried candidate, add one synthesized top block (a RawExpr definition built from the candidate's parameter patterns and annotations, with a tuple pattern over them and an application chain as the body), so it is inferred, prepassed and auto-exported like a hand-written definition. The consumer-side rewrite (fully applied chain -> f__uncurried tuple) can then be a prepass-level E rewrite, because by then both definitions exist with real Scopes. Estimate holds at 180 min plus one pack cycle. Sequenced after AUTO-EXPORT-1 installs (pack57), so the class-1 path is proven in the field first.")
inl note_of_auto_export_2_curried_5 () = Note ("AUTO-EXPORT-2-CURRIED", 5u32, "2026-11-06T16:18Z", "compiler", "11-06 12:2x compiler: IMPLEMENTATION MAP (read at the pack55d tree core). (1) FLAG BY PACKAGE: typecheck only has a package_id. proj_validate (~35758) holds the validated SchemaEnv and fst s.package_ids (dir -> pid) right before wdiff_projenvr_tc, so fill a global ConcurrentDictionary<int, unit> autoExportPids there (not ThreadLocal: typecheck runs on Hopac worker threads). (2) UNIT SIDE: typecheck (~29421) infers one bundle at a time. After a BundleInl(com, r, (rn, f), term, td) whose term is a chain of >= 2 single-clause RawFun over PatAnnot(PatVar v, T) (no RawForall), infer a synthesized BundleInl(com, r, (rn, f + \"__uncurried\"), RawFun(r, [PatAnnot(r, PatPair-chain of the PatVars, RawTPair-chain of the Ts), RawApply-chain(RawV f, vars)]), td) in the same env and emit it as an extra stream element. Cost: the diff walker (~29436) compares element bundles in lockstep, so a file with synthesized bundles falls back to a full re-typecheck on edit (correct, less incremental). Prepass and auto-export-1 then see f__uncurried as an ordinary class-1 definition. (3) CONSUMER SIDE, the hard part: prepass substitutes referenced definitions' E objects into the referencing tree, and definitionSources is keyed by object identity, so a generic E map (like the one at ~7585) that descends into a reference would COPY it and break linking. The rewrite of EApply^n(f_E, a1..an) -> EApply(f__uncurried_E, EPair-chain) must stop descending at any E that definitionSources/curriedDefinitionSources knows (a top-level definition) and run only over the consumer's own definitions as prepass creates them. NEXT STEP: implement (1)+(2) with a unit test that f__uncurried appears in the unit's exports; then (3) behind the same flag, with the linked curried sample. Est stays 180 min plus a pack cycle; not started in code today, to keep today's two installed packs clean.")
inl note_of_auto_export_2_curried_6 () = Note ("AUTO-EXPORT-2-CURRIED", 6u32, "2026-11-06T16:22Z", "compiler", "11-06 12:2x compiler: parts (1)+(2) DRAFTED as kitdo 1-unit-uncurried-wrappers.kitdo (kit drafts, 4 replacements, dry run ok on pack57's source): autoExportPids (a ConcurrentDictionary filled in proj_validate from each package's auto-export flag); AutoExportCurried.synthesize turns a BundleInl whose term is >= 2 nested single-clause RawFun over PatAnnot(PatVar) into BundleInl(f + \"__uncurried\") = RawFun over a PatAnnot(PatPair chain, RawTPair chain) whose body is the RawApply chain (with the RawAnnot result type when f has one); typecheck infers it right after f in the same env and emits it as an extra stream element. SPIRAL_AUTO_EXPORT_TRACE=1 prints each synthesis. Test candidate ae2a (pack55d tree + AUTO-EXPORT-1 + this) building; unit test: a model with add3 (a : i32) (b : i32) (c : i32) must export model_add3__uncurried. Part (3), the consumer rewrite, is next.")
inl note_of_auto_export_2_curried_7 () = Note ("AUTO-EXPORT-2-CURRIED", 7u32, "2026-11-06T16:29Z", "compiler", "11-06 12:3x compiler: parts (1)+(2) proven on candidate ae2a (core 24F1D9EC2D0D8FAB = pack56c tree + AE1 + AE2 program 1). A unit with auto-export: monomorphic and add3 (a b c : i32) now traces 'synthesized add3__uncurried of arity 3' and emits pub fn model_add3__uncurried(v0: i32, v1: i32, v2: i32) -> i32 next to model_double. Part (3), the consumer rewrite (peval EApply chain on a curried definition with a wrapper -> apply the wrapper to the arg tuple, guarded by the wrapper's own range), is drafted as program 2-consumer-calls-uncurried.kitdo (dry run ok, 3 replacements); next step: build ae2b and link a consumer.")
inl note_of_auto_export_2_curried_8 () = Note ("AUTO-EXPORT-2-CURRIED", 8u32, "2026-11-06T17:07Z", "compiler", "11-06 13:0x compiler: part (3) PROVEN on candidate ae2b (pack56c tree + AE1 + both AE2 programs). A consumer call add3 n 1i32 2i32 to a linked unit's curried add3 now emits one cross-unit call model::model_add3__uncurried(v0, 1i32, 2i32); a partial application (f = add3 n; f 1i32 2i32) still inlines, as documented. New linked sample samples/linked_rust_auto_export_curried (Exit 31, Calls model_add3__uncurried,model_double; matrix row added) and the full linked suite on ae2b: 17 rows, 17 pass, 0 fail (run single-flight-20261106-125710). tmp/AGENTS.md documents the curried rule next to AUTO-EXPORT-1. next step: pack57 = AE1 + AE2 (2 programs) + RUST-GROUP-ARM-STRING-FOLD, Rust byte comparison of every sample vs the installed core, smoke, install, then main ships it.")
inl note_of_auto_export_2_curried_9 () = Note ("AUTO-EXPORT-2-CURRIED", 9u32, "2026-11-06T18:16Z", "compiler", "11-06 14:1x compiler: INSTALLED on the box in pack57 (core 8F0094967068FC85) with AUTO-EXPORT-1 and RUST-GROUP-ARM-STRING-FOLD; smoke 159 at parity, Rust byte comparison of every sample unchanged apart from the fold fix's own sample; linked suite 17/17 on ae2b (same AE programs). Asked main to ship it to node and europa. Done when shipped.")
inl note_of_auto_export_2_curried_10 () = Note ("AUTO-EXPORT-2-CURRIED", 10u32, "2026-11-06T20:40Z", "compiler", "11-06 16:4x compiler: DONE. pack57 SHIPPED to all three hosts (main 16:4x): box core 8F0094967068FC85 / host 734CEF2EBF4E7DD4 (14:1x), node the same in place 16:38 (fresh launch exit 0), europa Linux build from source E0AC98300538F224 (core e6a3e4d0e7336508, launch exit 0, 14:36). The curried rule is live wherever a unit sets auto-export: monomorphic; regression sample samples/linked_rust_auto_export_curried.")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_arena_design_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-ARENA-DESIGN", 1u32, "2026-11-06T14:33Z", "tibia", "11-06 10:33 tibia: Split from TIBIA-NUGGET-TABULAR-CFR (main's light floor). DoD: the note on TIBIA-NUGGET-TABULAR-CFR names every state bucket, action, payoff source and the test, sized so the toy runs in under 1 s. NEXT: read hunting_pack's heal/strike/retreat thresholds for the buckets.")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_arena_design_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-ARENA-DESIGN", 2u32, "2026-11-06T14:39Z", "tibia", "11-06 10:39 tibia: DONE. Proof: the design note is on TIBIA-NUGGET-TABULAR-CFR (latest note). It names 32 information states (hp buckets cut at policy thresholds x adjacent attackers x potion ready), 3 knight actions, a 2-action camp adversary, payoffs from hunting_pack's damage and potion model, the regret.spi solver, an exploitability check by enumeration, and 3 tests.")
inl note_of_tibia_readme_new_modules_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-README-NEW-MODULES", 1u32, "2026-11-06T14:33Z", "tibia", "11-06 10:33 tibia: Split as light housekeeping (main's light floor). DoD: README lists each module with a one-line purpose, and line width stays within 120. NEXT: add the rows.")
inl note_of_tibia_readme_new_modules_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-README-NEW-MODULES", 2u32, "2026-11-06T14:37Z", "tibia", "11-06 10:37 tibia: DONE (README unstaged). The module count is corrected to 29 (counted: src/*.spi without standards.spi; the old text said 26). Decisions gains hashed (sign-bit LSH policy table). A new Learning machinery line lists regret (regret-matching+ self-play), logprob (fixed-point log2/exp2, importance weights) and soft_policy (epsilon-soft sampling with logged probabilities). apps/map notes that its item kinds are lib bitsets. Proof: every edited line is at most 120 chars (the lengths were checked); the wrapped apps sentence is unchanged in wording.")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_arena_game_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-ARENA-GAME", 1u32, "2026-11-06T14:40Z", "tibia", "11-06 10:40 tibia: Split from TIBIA-NUGGET-TABULAR-CFR. DoD: the game plus 3 golden tests (exploitability falls over 50/100/200 iterations; Heal >= 900 at hp < 100 with the potion ready; StepAway rises at 2+ attackers) pass on c and rust. NEXT: the state encoding (hp bucket x attackers x potion -> 0..31) with its round-trip test.")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_arena_game_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-ARENA-GAME", 2u32, "2026-11-06T15:04Z", "tibia", "11-06 11:04 tibia: DONE, proof green. NEW src/arena_cfr.spi (unstaged, registered after regret; -ChecksOnly green): 32 information states (hp bucket x adjacent attackers x potion ready, with an index round trip), knight {Heal, Strike, StepAway} against camp {Press, Spread}, a zero-sum cost of death (14000), potion (50), tempo (40) and damage (52 per hitter), and regret-matching+ per state with linear averaging (i64 shares, so regrets cannot overflow) and exploitability by best responses. SIMPLIFICATION, recorded: each state is a one-shot matrix game, not a 30-step tree; the tree is the next slice. Node job-1793977191621-tibia-newmods2-cells, exit 0, discovered 4, passed 4 on c and rust: index round trip; total exploitability at 200 rounds <= at 50; a low-hp pressed knight with a ready potion puts >= 900 on Heal; the StepAway share at 3 attackers > at 0.")
inl note_of_tibia_soft_wire_design_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-SOFT-WIRE-DESIGN", 1u32, "2026-11-06T14:40Z", "tibia", "11-06 10:40 tibia: Split from TIBIA-NUGGET-IMPORTANCE-SAMPLING. DoD: a note naming the union case, the tally field, the code sites (wants_heal, after_heal_plan, the roll-purpose test 12 -> 13) and the per-hunt output row. NEXT: read pack_roll and hunter_tally.")
inl note_of_tibia_soft_wire_design_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-SOFT-WIRE-DESIGN", 2u32, "2026-11-06T14:41Z", "tibia", "11-06 10:41 tibia: DONE. Proof: the design note is on TIBIA-NUGGET-IMPORTANCE-SAMPLING (latest). It names the union case Softened (soft_brain over Network/Hashed), the roll purpose PackSoftDecision (code 21, test 12 -> 13), the tally field log_path (Q16), the code sites with line numbers, and the per-hunt tally6 row.")
inl note_of_tibia_gate_wgsl_crash_void_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-GATE-WGSL-CRASH-VOID", 1u32, "2026-11-06T14:40Z", "tibia", "11-06 10:40 tibia: Found in the CI-fix node build: readiness failed only with spiral-wgsl 0xC0000005 and was green on CI. DoD: build.ps1 recognizes the runner-crash line in a file's raw output, counts it as VOID (listed separately, does not fail the run alone) and still fails on any real failed test; checked against the readiness.out from that run. NEXT: read the raw line format in target/ci-metrics.")
inl note_of_tibia_gate_wgsl_crash_void_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-GATE-WGSL-CRASH-VOID", 2u32, "2026-11-06T15:02Z", "tibia", "11-06 11:02 tibia: DONE (build.ps1 unstaged, parses clean), with ONE DELIBERATE CHANGE to the DoD: a VOID file STILL fails the run. It is labelled and counted apart from the red ones (memory gate-tightening-needs-full-run: a gate that passes on VOID would hide a real crash on CI). Per file, a raw line \"`spiral-wgsl` failed (exit -1073741819)\" tags the problem \"VOID (spiral-wgsl runner crash 0xC0000005)\", and \"Spiral cell timed out after\" tags it \"VOID (cell timeout)\". The final line reads \"N of M test files are not fully green (V VOID, R red)\". Proof: the tag logic run on the exact raw lines of the CI-fix node build classifies readiness as runner crash, gpu_sim as cell timeout, and lanes (gcc exit 1) as red, i.e. untagged. The next node rerun shows it end to end.")
inl note_of_tibia_soft_wire_code_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-SOFT-WIRE-CODE", 1u32, "2026-11-06T14:42Z", "tibia", "11-06 10:42 tibia: split from TIBIA-NUGGET-IMPORTANCE-SAMPLING after its design step. CPU-light to write; the proof is a node Cells run. DoD: existing hunting_pack and pack_sim tests unchanged (a deterministic brain adds log_path 0), plus a new test where Softened at epsilon 0 equals its inner brain hunt for hunt and at epsilon 100 logs a negative log_path. NEXT: add the union case and the tally field.")
inl note_of_tibia_soft_wire_code_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-SOFT-WIRE-CODE", 2u32, "2026-11-06T15:27Z", "tibia", "11-06 11:27 tibia: CODE IN PLACE (hunting_pack, unstaged; cell budget 0 over on the changed modules; the layout check is muddied by the new core's join-then rule, see TIBIA-REFORMAT-JOIN-THEN, and none of my added lines use ?>). Added: learned_core (CoreNetwork | CoreHashed) and soft_brain { core; epsilon }; brain gains Softened; pack_roll gains PackSoftDecision (purpose code 21, purpose test 12 -> 13 rolls); hunter_tally gains log_path (0 in the fresh tally); core_decision, soft_roll (key seed tick (300 + 100 x slot + bit) PackSoftDecision, roll 0..999), softened, soft_heals and soft_plan wired into learned_heals/learned_plan; acts_after_aim logs path_log2 of the sampled bits before the heal gate. Tests: a_softened_brain_without_exploration_hunts_like_its_core (epsilon 0: the same kills and potions as network_tactic over a 400-tick troll hunt, with log_path 0) and exploration_logs_a_negative_path_weight (epsilon 100). pack_sim's tally5 is not changed yet. PENDING: node job-1793978798919-tibia-softwire-cells (all of hunting_pack's tests).")
inl note_of_tibia_soft_wire_code_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-SOFT-WIRE-CODE", 3u32, "2026-11-06T15:46Z", "tibia", "11-06 11:46 tibia: pack_sim side in place (unstaged; cell budget 0 over): hunt_log_path and log_paths (camp, tactic, seed range -> one Q16 log_path per hunt, from clear_run), plus the c test softened_hunts_log_one_path_weight_per_hunt (epsilon 0 gives 0/0; epsilon 100 gives negative/negative over seeds 1-2). Changed from the design: a per-hunt array beside tally5 instead of widening tally5, so its 3 consumers stay untouched. Also renamed the hunting_pack test helpers to soft_test_* / greedy_test_hunt / kills_and_potions, so they cannot shadow catalog's troll_camp in modules that open both. PENDING: hunting_pack tests (node job-1793978798919, pre-rename copy, same semantics); pack_sim rides the next full build.ps1 rerun.")
inl note_of_tibia_soft_wire_code_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-SOFT-WIRE-CODE", 4u32, "2026-11-06T15:46Z", "tibia", "11-06 11:46 tibia: Blocked on node job-1793978798919-tibia-softwire-cells (hunting_pack tests) and the next full build.ps1 rerun (pack_sim). Resume when: both report.")
inl note_of_tibia_soft_wire_code_5 () = Note ("TIBIA-SOFT-WIRE-CODE", 5u32, "2026-11-06T16:05Z", "tibia", "11-06 12:05 tibia: hunting_pack PROOF on the node (job-1793978798919, scratch copy of src): 9/10 rows passed. All 8 existing c tests passed, including every_pack_roll_has_its_own_purpose_code at 13 rolls. a_softened_brain_without_exploration_hunts_like_its_core passed on c (122 s) and on rust (785 s): epsilon 0 hunts exactly like network_tactic with log_path 0. exploration_logs_a_negative_path_weight passed on c and FAILED on rust after 229 s with no assertion text in the output; the file's headroom line shows its slowest cell at 785,634 ms against a 300,000 ms budget, so I read the rust row as a resource or time failure of the huge Rust hunting_pack build, not a logic failure (c, the same logic, passes). Every other hunting_pack test is c-only for that reason, so both new tests are now ///> c only (they had a ///> rust row I added). UNKNOWN, not red, for the rust row; the c proof stands.")
inl note_of_tibia_soft_wire_code_6 () = Note ("TIBIA-SOFT-WIRE-CODE", 6u32, "2026-11-07T15:48Z", "tibia", "11-07 11:4x tibia groom (Blocked check): the proof it waited on landed 11-06: job-1793996115107-tibia-ci-final ran pack_sim 41/41 (incl. softened_hunts_log_one_path_weight_per_hunt) and hunting_pack 13/13 (incl. the two softened-brain tests) green under build.ps1. Proof: that job. Done.")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_arena_tree_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-ARENA-TREE", 1u32, "2026-11-06T15:08Z", "tibia", "11-06 11:07 tibia: the next slice after TIBIA-CFR-ARENA-GAME, whose recorded simplification was one-shot states. DoD: a tree solver with a test that a 2-step game's value matches hand enumeration, plus the 3 existing behavior tests on the tree. NEXT: the transition function (state, knight action, camp action) -> next state.")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_arena_tree_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-ARENA-TREE", 2u32, "2026-11-06T15:37Z", "tibia", "11-06 11:37 tibia: CODE IN PLACE (arena_cfr, unstaged; cell budget 0 over; the only new-core formatter diff is the pending join-then rule). Approach: the game is Markov with full observation, so CFR over histories reduces to BACKWARD INDUCTION. values_at depth is the 32 matrix-game values with payoff tree_cost = cost now + (alive ? V(depth-1, next_state) : 0), each solved by the same regret-matching+ (solve_game now takes a payoff closure, `:== payoff = i32 -> i32 -> i32`, and solve is solve_game (cost st)). next_state: hp from after_hp re-bucketed, attackers - 1 after StepAway, ready = not drunk. game_value is the averages' pair sum in i64. Tests against HAND ENUMERATION (worked in the note author's head and written down here): 3 attackers, top hp, no potion: depth 1 = 144 (StepAway against Press), depth 2 = 236 (144 + V1 of the next state at 2 attackers, ready = 92); asserted within [140,148] and [230,242] (the averages include the uniform first round). PENDING: node job-1793979366826-tibia-cfrtree-cells.")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_arena_tree_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-ARENA-TREE", 3u32, "2026-11-06T15:41Z", "tibia", "11-06 11:41 tibia: TREE PROOF green: node job-1793979366826-tibia-cfrtree-cells, arena_cfr exit 0, discovered 6, passed 6 on c and rust, including one_step_of_the_tree_is_the_matrix_game (V1 in [140,148], hand value 144) and two_steps_match_the_hand_enumeration (V2 in [230,242], hand value 236). Left for the DoD: the 3 behavior tests read off the TREE's depth-k strategies (today they use the one-shot solve). NEXT: expose the root strategy at depth k (solve_game (tree_cost (values_at (k-1)) st)) and port the 3 tests.")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_arena_tree_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-ARENA-TREE", 4u32, "2026-11-06T15:46Z", "tibia", "11-06 11:46 tibia: Blocked on node job-1793979846586-tibia-cfrtree-cells-2 (the tree versions of the behavior tests: drinks at low hp, steps away more under pressure). Resume when: it reports; Done if green.")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_arena_tree_5 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-ARENA-TREE", 5u32, "2026-11-06T15:57Z", "tibia", "11-06 11:57 tibia: TREE RUN 2 (node job-1793979846586): 7/8 passed; a_low_hp_knight_drinks_in_the_tree_too FAILED on c (Heal < 900 at depth 3). This is a MODEL FINDING, not a solver bug: at hp bucket 0 against 2 attackers under Press, every line dies within 2 steps (after a heal, 96 hp re-buckets to bucket 0, mid 50; next step Strike, StepAway and the no-potion Heal all go below 0). Death therefore costs the same whether it comes now or one step later, and Heal stops dominating. The coarse 4-bucket hp with mid re-centering throws away hp (96 -> 50). Test replaced by the property that does hold: the depth-3 value of that state is >= 14000 (death unavoidable). the_tree_steps_away_more_under_pressure PASSED on c and rust. NEXT (the model, recorded here): finer hp buckets or exact hp in the state, and a discounted death or a survival reward, so that delaying death is worth something. PENDING: node job-1793980615340-tibia-cfrtree-cells-3.")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_arena_tree_6 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-ARENA-TREE", 6u32, "2026-11-06T16:01Z", "tibia", "11-06 12:01 tibia: MODEL FIX for run 2's finding: early death is now PRICED. tree_cost takes the steps left; a death adds early_death left = 500 x steps_left on top of the 14000, so the same death one step later costs 500 less and delaying an unavoidable death is worth something. values_after takes a state-value closure, and tree_knight passes depth - 1. Depth 1 is unchanged (0 steps left), and the depth-2 hand value 236 on crowded_fresh has no death on its line, so it is unchanged too. Hand check for the low-hp state at depth 3: Heal is about 194 + (14000 + 500 + small) against immediate death at 14092 + 1000, so Heal should dominate again. The drinks test is restored as with_a_price_on_early_death_the_low_hp_knight_drinks_in_the_tree, beside the >= 14000 value test. Cell budget 0 over. PENDING: node job-1793980839950-tibia-cfrtree-cells-4 (run 3 may already pick up this zip if its slot opens later).")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_arena_tree_7 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-ARENA-TREE", 7u32, "2026-11-06T16:06Z", "tibia", "11-06 12:06 tibia: DONE. Proof: node job-1793980615340-tibia-cfrtree-cells-3 picked up the priced-death zip: arena_cfr exit 0, discovered 9, executed 9, passed 9 on c and rust (18 rows). The tree tests: one step = the matrix game (hand 144), two steps = hand enumeration (236), the low-hp state cannot escape death in 3 steps (value >= 14000), the tree steps away more under pressure, and with a price on early death the low-hp knight drinks in the tree (>= 900). The 4 one-shot tests still pass. Run 4 (the same zip) was stopped as redundant. Open model gap, recorded for a later slice: hp buckets re-centred at their middle (96 -> 50) lose information; exact hp in the state is the fix.")
inl note_of_tibia_reformat_join_then_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-REFORMAT-JOIN-THEN", 1u32, "2026-11-06T15:25Z", "tibia", "11-06 11:25 tibia: box core 257DB91886B9 (installed 11:20) joins lone thens. tibia's layout check now lists about 20 would-change files that I did not edit. Held on purpose (compiler agreed 11:2x): CI formats with the committed spiral compiler, so a reformat before the push turns CI red. Blocked on: compiler's word that the core is in the pushed spiral tree. DoD: one format pass over src and apps, then build.ps1 -ChecksOnly clean on the new core, with no other edits in that pass. NEXT: wait for compiler's message.")
inl note_of_tibia_reformat_join_then_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-REFORMAT-JOIN-THEN", 2u32, "2026-11-07T16:47Z", "tibia", "11-07 12:xx tibia: DONE. Resume condition met: the user pushed spiral with the join-then core (github-i574n/main f6000cfa; apps/compiler/spiral_compiler.fs is clean against it), and tibia CI run 42366181093 on 52ea700 went red at the layout stage, flagging exactly the held join-then lines. The box formatter flagged the same 18 files as CI. One format pass over src and apps/{arena,map,host,offscreen,canary,predict,suite} (unstaged): 18 files, 200 lone \"?>\" lines joined, nothing else; format --check exits 0, and build.ps1 -ChecksOnly is green (formatter clean, cell budget 0 over; the 26 autolink/mention findings are the baseline). Proof: that -ChecksOnly run. CI turns green only when the user pushes this.")
inl note_of_x_sim_args_rust_red_1 () = Note ("X-SIM-ARGS-RUST-RED", 1u32, "2026-11-06T16:08Z", "x", "2026-11-06 12:08 x: found by x-diag2 (job-1793980303341, node, pack55d 257DB91886B97811), after the sim notebooks compile again (they were ETY-red in CI on 9869fab/dcd95af, so this runtime fault was hidden). Failing tests are bad_values/bad_shapes: actual ((rejected: --, rejected: --), rejected: missing --spi or --spi-file, rejected: --), expected ((rejected: --seed takes a whole number, got 'x', rejected: --executor is fake, fake-leak or cells, got 'gpu'), rejected: missing --spi or --spi-file, rejected: --duplicates takes a decimal like 0.1, got '0.1234'). Every message built as '--' ++# name ++# ... (sim_args.spi 83, 140, 177) comes out as '--'. The path is flag_name = rest_from 2 arg = cut = sm'::substring (Rust arm unchanged in c0e77c3f). Also seen on 2/4 in x-cellsfix2f, probably on pack53c, so it is not new in pack55d. NEXT STEP: a minimal Rust probe (one cell: '--' ++# rest_from 2i32 '--seed' ++# ' x') on the node to split sm'::substring from the ++# chain, then hand to compiler with the generated Rust.")
inl note_of_x_sim_args_rust_red_2 () = Note ("X-SIM-ARGS-RUST-RED", 2u32, "2026-11-06T16:26Z", "x", "2026-11-06 12:26 x: NARROWED by x-dashprobe (job-1793981831862, node, pack55d): a probe notebook (kit drafts x\\X-SIM-ARGS-RUST-RED\\dash_probe.spi) passes 4/4 on rust+gleam: a '--executor is fake' literal, '--' ++# name ++# ' takes ...', sm'::substring 2 n '--seed' -> 'seed', and a dash-free concat. So the dash literals, ++# and substring are fine in isolation. The red needs sim_args' context: the message is built in run_valued/counted_flag and returned through the generic mutual group flags_parsed / arg_parsed / valued_then / continued (:& :~ with \\* o., rules::valued called through a flag_rules o record of functions, result o string). Even the single-literal executor message comes back as exactly '--', so it is not the ++# tail. NEXT STEP: compiler checks the generated Rust for sim_args' run_args path (the value passed out of rules::valued in valued_then); x supplies the cell.")
inl note_of_x_sim_args_rust_red_3 () = Note ("X-SIM-ARGS-RUST-RED", 3u32, "2026-11-06T16:55Z", "x", "2026-11-06 12:54 x: ROOT CAUSE (compiler, 11-06 12:4x): the Rust text pass foldStringBindings (spiral_compiler.fs ~13693) resets its string-binding table only at 'fn ' lines. A mutual group is ONE fn group_0 whose arms restart numbering at v0, so continued's self-rebind 'let mut v6: Rc<str> = v6;' resolves to arg_parsed's v6, the '--' literal passed to starts_with. Every Error through continued becomes '--'. The pass is Rust-only, so Gleam is unaffected, and compiler reproduced it with no x code. x's code is correct and gets no workaround. BLOCKER: compiler's RUST-GROUP-ARM-STRING-FOLD (candidate rgf1 building). Resume: rerun sim_args on Rust once that installs, and close on 4/4.")
inl note_of_x_sim_args_rust_red_4 () = Note ("X-SIM-ARGS-RUST-RED", 4u32, "2026-11-06T16:55Z", "x", "BLOCKER: compiler RUST-GROUP-ARM-STRING-FOLD (the Rust foldStringBindings pass resolves a self-rebind across mutual-group arms). Resume when compiler installs the rgf1 fix.")
inl note_of_x_sim_args_rust_red_5 () = Note ("X-SIM-ARGS-RUST-RED", 5u32, "2026-11-06T18:18Z", "x", "2026-11-06 14:18 x: compiler INSTALLED the fix as pack57 (core 8F0094967068FC85) on the box; its standalone flags_parsed copy now returns the full rejection text on Rust. NEXT STEP: once main ships pack57 to the node, rerun the sim_args notebook (rust + gleam) pinned to 8F0094967068FC85 and close on 4/4.")
