inl note_of_x_sim_args_rust_red_7 () = Note ("X-SIM-ARGS-RUST-RED", 7u32, "2026-11-07T00:10Z", "x", "2026-11-06 20:09 x: CLOSED Done. sim_args notebook 4/4 (rust + gleam, failed_tests []) on pack57 8F0094967068FC85: x-simargs57b, job-1794009801506, node, mirror xqueue3. compiler's RUST-GROUP-ARM-STRING-FOLD fix (the Rust foldStringBindings self-rebind across mutual-group arms) is proven on x's real group; no x code changed.")
inl note_of_node_proof_start_error_visible_1 () = Note ("NODE-PROOF-START-ERROR-VISIBLE", 1u32, "2026-11-06T16:38Z", "x", "2026-11-06 12:38 x: filed from a real miss. On 11-06 09:4x, x-cellsfix2c's start was refused by -RequireCore (the node had gone pack52 -> pack53c), and node-proof showed only '     | verifying)', the tail of remote.ps1's multi-line throw ('node single-flight core 24D39673... does not match required A688EE5A...'). It cost x a relaunch plus a manual reproduction. DoD: on a non-'job start ok' result, node-proof prints every line of the start output (or the first error line plus the last), and exits non-zero with 'node-proof / job start failed'.")
inl note_of_node_proof_start_error_visible_2 () = Note ("NODE-PROOF-START-ERROR-VISIBLE", 2u32, "2026-11-06T18:02Z", "main", "main 11-06 14:0x DONE. proof: i574n.github/scripts/node-proof.ps1 (unstaged) collects the whole remote.ps1 job start output. On a 'kit job start ok ' line it prints just that line, which is unchanged for callers. Otherwise it prints EVERY line, then throws 'node-proof / job start failed for <label> (the job may still run: check remote.ps1 <machine> job list before any relaunch)', so pwsh exits non-zero. Parse 0 errors. A simulation of both outcomes (an ok line; the 2-line RequireCore mismatch) printed the ok line in one case, and both error lines plus the throw in the other. Consumer: x/scripts/node-run.ps1:59-63 matches 'job start ok' and prints the last 8 lines on failure, so it now sees the full error. Its 4-try relaunch loop can duplicate a job whose start errored but which runs anyway (memory node-job-start-error-still-runs); flagged to x.")
inl note_of_rust_group_arm_string_fold_1 () = Note ("RUST-GROUP-ARM-STRING-FOLD", 1u32, "2026-11-06T16:52Z", "compiler", "11-06 12:5x compiler: ROOT CAUSE of X-SIM-ARGS-RUST-RED. The Rust text pass foldStringBindings (spiral_compiler.fs ~13693) keeps a known table of string values for 'let mut vN: Rc<str> = ...' lines and clears it only at 'fn ' lines. A mutual group compiles to ONE fn group_N whose arms 'GroupN::Mk(...) => {' each restart variable numbering at v0, so a later arm's rebind of a pattern binder ('Error(v6) => { let mut v6: Rc<str> = v6;') reads an EARLIER arm's v6 (there the '--' literal of starts_with) and is rewritten to that literal. x's sim_args returned 'rejected: --' for every Error that went through continued. Reproduced on the installed core 257DB91886B97811 standalone (scratchpad simargs-probe: a=rejected: --, while the direct call is right) and with a core-only sample (scratchpad group-fold-sample: Rust exit 1, correct 0). FIX drafted as kitdo RUST-GROUP-ARM-STRING-FOLD\\1-clear-known-per-arm.kitdo (3 replacements, dry run ok): clear known at each group arm header, and never resolve a self-rebind 'vN = vN' from the table (its rhs is always a fresh binder). DoD: candidate rgf1 makes both repros right; regression sample samples/rust_group_arm_string_rebind passes on every backend in the matrix; Rust examples parity; install; x reruns sim_args 4/4 on Rust. next step: rgf1 build + both repros.")
inl note_of_rust_group_arm_string_fold_2 () = Note ("RUST-GROUP-ARM-STRING-FOLD", 2u32, "2026-11-06T16:53Z", "compiler", "11-06 12:5x compiler: typefeatureset plan: none applies; the fix is a two-line scoping change inside an existing text pass (a regex for the arm header and a self-rebind guard), with no new data shapes. The regression sample is a plain core-only program whose exit code is the check.")
inl note_of_rust_group_arm_string_fold_3 () = Note ("RUST-GROUP-ARM-STRING-FOLD", 3u32, "2026-11-06T17:04Z", "compiler", "11-06 13:0x compiler: candidate rgf1 (live tree + the fix; core DDCF55A8FA702277) makes both repros right on Rust (rustc 1.99.0, box): simargs-probe now prints a=rejected: --executor is fake, fake-leak or cells, got 'gpu' (was a=rejected: --), and the new regression sample samples/rust_group_arm_string_rebind exits 0 (installed core: exit 1). The sample is in the tree (unstaged, core-only, positive, so every backend runs it against the C oracle). next step: Rust byte comparison of every sample, installed core vs rgf1 (only group fns that read a stale value may change), then the pack.")
inl note_of_rust_group_arm_string_fold_4 () = Note ("RUST-GROUP-ARM-STRING-FOLD", 4u32, "2026-11-06T17:10Z", "compiler", "11-06 13:1x compiler: AUDIT of the other Rust text passes for the same per-fn-table assumption (read at the pack56c source). immutableRustLets and rustMoveOnLastUse scan a whole fn text, so reused arm numbers only make them more conservative (more mut kept, more clones kept): safe. cacheRustStringLiterals keeps no variable table. inlineRustEmits (~13914) keeps a snippets table that is NEVER cleared (not even at fn lines): the emit's code variable is normally a literal bound on the line just before, so the latest entry is right, but an emit whose code arrives through a parameter or pattern binder would inline a stale snippet from an earlier fn and drop that fn's binding line. No repro exists (emit code is static in every known caller), so it is not changed in this pack; resume when: an emit with a non-literal code variable appears.")
inl note_of_rust_group_arm_string_fold_5 () = Note ("RUST-GROUP-ARM-STRING-FOLD", 5u32, "2026-11-06T17:52Z", "compiler", "11-06 13:5x compiler: BYTE COMPARISON on candidate pack57 (core 8F0094967068FC85 = live tree + AUTO-EXPORT-1 + AUTO-EXPORT-2 x2 + this fix) vs the installed core 257DB91886B97811, every samples main.spi (1204 inputs, linked_ excluded) through --batch to Rust on the box: 550 Rust outputs on each side, 549 byte-identical, 1 differs, and the ok/error status of all 1204 inputs is unchanged. The one diff is the regression sample itself, exactly the intended line (group_0 arm US1_Bad(v6): let v6 = the '--' literal -> let v6: Rc<str> = v6;). Coverage note: only 8 of the 550 outputs contain a group fn, so a large real program (apps/spiral to Rust) gets the same comparison on the node when the split oracle frees it. next step: the sample on every backend vs the C oracle (running, box), then install pack57.")
inl note_of_rust_group_arm_string_fold_6 () = Note ("RUST-GROUP-ARM-STRING-FOLD", 6u32, "2026-11-06T17:55Z", "compiler", "11-06 14:0x compiler: the regression sample on every backend the matrix gives it (examples suite, candidate pack57, box): Fsharp, Pascal, C and Rust all ran exit 0, oracle agree 3 / DISAGREE 0, baseline 4 new (run single-flight-20261106-135146). Its generated outputs sit next to the source like every sample's. next step: pack57 smoke review (running), then install and ask main to ship it.")
inl note_of_rust_group_arm_string_fold_7 () = Note ("RUST-GROUP-ARM-STRING-FOLD", 7u32, "2026-11-06T18:15Z", "compiler", "11-06 14:1x compiler: INSTALLED on the box as pack57 (core 8F0094967068FC85, host 734CEF2EBF4E7DD4, equal to the reviewed candidate; smoke 159 at parity, DISAGREE 0; Rust byte comparison of all 1204 sample inputs: the only diff is this item's regression sample). Field check with the installed compiler: the standalone sim_args group now prints a=rejected: --executor is fake, fake-leak or cells, got 'gpu'. Asked main (i574n) to ship pack57 to node and europa, and told x. Done when x reruns sim_args 4/4 on Rust on a pack57 host.")
inl note_of_rust_group_arm_string_fold_8 () = Note ("RUST-GROUP-ARM-STRING-FOLD", 8u32, "2026-11-06T20:41Z", "compiler", "11-06 16:4x compiler: pack57 SHIPPED to all three hosts (main 16:4x): box core 8F0094967068FC85 / host 734CEF2EBF4E7DD4 (14:1x), node the same in place 16:38 (fresh launch exit 0), europa Linux build from source E0AC98300538F224 (core e6a3e4d0e7336508, launch exit 0, 14:36). Only x's rerun of sim_args 4/4 on Rust remains (asked).")
inl note_of_rust_group_arm_string_fold_9 () = Note ("RUST-GROUP-ARM-STRING-FOLD", 9u32, "2026-11-06T23:21Z", "compiler", "11-06 19:2x compiler: x's first rerun on pack57 (x-simargs57, job-1794004764065, node core 8F0094967068FC85) is VOID, not a verdict: Cells failed to mount packages (':lock_timeout', a stale mount lock from x's killed runs, filed under CELLS-TEMP-LEAK), so its 1/4 says nothing about this fix. Stays open; x reruns cleanly after its x-media3c gate frees the node. The fix's own evidence is unchanged (standalone repro right on the installed pack57, byte comparison clean).")
inl note_of_rust_group_arm_string_fold_10 () = Note ("RUST-GROUP-ARM-STRING-FOLD", 10u32, "2026-11-06T23:23Z", "compiler", "11-06 19:2x compiler: CORRECTION to n9 (per x): the cause of x-simargs57's ':lock_timeout' is UNPROVEN. The only lock file on the node dates from 10-28 and can't match today's mount keys, so 'a stale lock from killed runs' was a guess. What stands: that run is VOID, not a verdict, and x reruns cleanly.")
inl note_of_rust_group_arm_string_fold_11 () = Note ("RUST-GROUP-ARM-STRING-FOLD", 11u32, "2026-11-07T00:11Z", "compiler", "11-06 20:1x compiler: DONE. x's clean rerun (x-simargs57b, job-1794009801506, node, core 8F0094967068FC85 = pack57): the sim_args notebook is 4/4 on Rust and Gleam, failed_tests [], and the bad_values/bad_shapes rejection messages come back whole; x closed X-SIM-ARGS-RUST-RED. Every DoD point is met: root cause (foldStringBindings' per-fn table vs per-arm numbering), fix shipped to box/node/europa in pack57, regression sample rust_group_arm_string_rebind on its 4 matrix backends, Rust byte comparison of all 1204 sample inputs clean except that sample, field proof by x.")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_exact_hp_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-EXACT-HP", 1u32, "2026-11-06T17:01Z", "tibia", "11-06 13:01 tibia: implemented (unstaged; cell budget 0 over). state_count = 516 x 8 = 4128; hp_middle and bucket_of are gone; next_state clamps after_hp to 0..515. Hand values re-derived for the exact model: crowded (390 hp, 3 attackers, no potion) is still 144 at depth 1 and 236 at depth 2 (next 286 hp, then StepAway against Press 92). The bucket artifact test is replaced by with_exact_hp_a_low_hp_knight_who_drinks_survives_two_steps: V2 of (50 hp, 2 attackers, ready) = Heal 194 + V1(96, 2, not ready) StepAway 92 = 286, asserted within [280,292]; the old \"cannot escape death\" value only existed because of the 96 -> 50 re-centring. DoD: all 9 arena_cfr tests green on c and rust. PENDING: node job-1793984475334-tibia-cfr-exact-cells.")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_exact_hp_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-EXACT-HP", 2u32, "2026-11-06T17:02Z", "tibia", "11-06 13:01 tibia: Blocked on node job-1793984475334-tibia-cfr-exact-cells. Resume when: it reports.")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_exact_hp_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-EXACT-HP", 3u32, "2026-11-06T17:14Z", "tibia", "11-06 13:14 tibia: DONE. Proof: node job-1793984475334-tibia-cfr-exact-cells, arena_cfr exit 0, discovered 9, passed 9 on c and rust (18 rows) with 4128 exact-hp states. The hand values held: crowded 144 at depth 1 and 236 at depth 2, and with_exact_hp_a_low_hp_knight_who_drinks_survives_two_steps sits in [280,292] (hand value 286, which the bucket model could not express). The drinks, step-away and exploitability tests stay green.")
inl note_of_tibia_is_estimator_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-IS-ESTIMATOR", 1u32, "2026-11-06T17:33Z", "tibia", "11-06 13:31 tibia: split from TIBIA-NUGGET-IMPORTANCE-SAMPLING (light floor). DoD: src/logprob.spi (or a sibling module) gains is_estimate over an array of (target log_path, behavior log_path, reward) giving the self-normalized mean and ess = (sum w)^2 / sum w^2 in Q16, with golden tests on c: equal paths reduce to the plain mean, a target that only follows one logged hunt returns that hunt's reward with ess 1.0, and two hunts weighted 3:1 give the 3:1 mix; build.ps1 -ChecksOnly green. NEXT: write the record type for one logged hunt. TypeFeatures: the logged hunt is a record, not a tuple of ints; no bool flags.")
inl note_of_tibia_is_estimator_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-IS-ESTIMATOR", 2u32, "2026-11-06T18:09Z", "tibia", "11-06 14:0x tibia: CODE in place (tibia src/logprob.spi, unstaged): records logged_hunt { target_log; behavior_log; reward }, estimate { mean; ess_q16 }, weight_sums { w; w2; wr }; is_estimate : array logged_hunt -> option estimate (None on an empty log). Weights are taken RELATIVE to the largest log ratio before exp2_q16 (a self-normalized mean is scale-free), so each weight is in (0, 1.0] Q16 and w2 cannot overflow i64; ess_q16 = (sum w)^2 / sum w^2 as quotient * 65536 + remainder * 65536 / w2. Golden tests on c and rust, hand-computed with whole-bit ratios so exp2 is exact: equal paths -> plain mean 30 with ess 3.0 (196608); a target that follows one hunt -> its reward 70 with ess 1.0 (65536; the other weight is 2^-41 -> 0); 1.0 vs 0.25 weights -> the 4:1 mix 200 with ess 1.4706 (96376). The DoD's 3:1 became 4:1 so the golden is exact. Box checks: formatter no change, cell budget 0 (is_estimate split into estimate_of). PENDING: node job-1793988374943-tibia-ci-rest (logprob is in its file list).")
inl note_of_tibia_is_estimator_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-IS-ESTIMATOR", 3u32, "2026-11-06T19:14Z", "tibia", "11-06 15:3x tibia: logged_hunt reshaped by TIBIA-IS-TARGET-LOG-CODE (target : target_path instead of target_log : i32; hunt still builds OnPath, so the 3 golden tests are unchanged). job-1793988374943-tibia-ci-rest tests the OLD shape (340DF00B1B5C); the proof of record becomes job-1793991326784-tibia-cfrbrain-cells (logprob A01AA2C151BA).")
inl note_of_tibia_is_estimator_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-IS-ESTIMATOR", 4u32, "2026-11-06T20:42Z", "tibia", "11-06 16:4x tibia: code done and checked on the box (format, cell budget, --check); only the node proof is left. Blocked on: node job-1793996115107-tibia-ci-final (logprob in its file list), queued on tree EF7486F7554A behind job-1793991326784-tibia-cfrbrain-cells, with a background waiter. Resume when: that job finishes; read its log in full, then close or fix.")
inl note_of_tibia_is_estimator_5 () = Note ("TIBIA-IS-ESTIMATOR", 5u32, "2026-11-06T21:18Z", "tibia", "11-06 17:1x tibia: job-1793991326784-tibia-cfrbrain-cells FINISHED (log read in full; Cells run_notebook per module on a scratch src snapshot from before the logged_hunts move): arena_cfr 13/13 (c+rust: table rows, state_for, low-hp drinks, calm rarely retreats, and the 9 earlier tests), hunting_pack 13/13 (c), pack_sim 41/41 (c, incl. a_target_equal_to_the_behavior_reweights_nothing), soft_policy 4/6 and logprob 6/10, where EVERY failure is VOID: \"could not start the compiler on port 13953: :lock_timeout\" (the Cells compiler daemon lock under node load), mismatches {} (no assertion failed), and the failing rows include unchanged tests that passed at 08:58 and 11:04. Proof of record stays job-1793996115107-tibia-ci-final (now starting, tree EF7486F7554A).")
inl note_of_tibia_is_estimator_6 () = Note ("TIBIA-IS-ESTIMATOR", 6u32, "2026-11-06T22:38Z", "tibia", "11-06 18:3x tibia: PROOF OF RECORD green for this code: node job-1793996115107-tibia-ci-final (build.ps1 -Files on a scratch tree outside the mirror, tree EF7486F7554A, log read in full): layout clean, cell budget 0 over; arena_cfr 13/13 (77FB224B574E, table + game node), hunting_pack 13/13 (7406AE9BAF88, Cfr brain + scored_by + logged_hunts), logprob 10/10 (A01AA2C151BA, estimator + target paths), pack_sim 41/41 (14AD5EE944CC), soft_policy 6/6 (the earlier lock_timeout rows pass here), sweep 1/1. Proof: job-1793996115107-tibia-ci-final.")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_prereg_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-PREREG", 1u32, "2026-11-06T17:33Z", "tibia", "11-06 13:31 tibia: split from TIBIA-NUGGET-TABULAR-CFR (its DoD: the average strategy as a hunting_pack brain, held out against retreat-at-2, pre-registered first). DoD: a PR-30 section in tibia/docs/BENCHMARK.md written before TIBIA-CFR-POLICY-TABLE's brain exists: arms (CFR table brain vs the shipped Rules brain with retreat_at 2), lanes and seeds (the held-out 8 lanes x 4 seeds PR-29 uses), the metric (median profit and worst lane), and the decision rule (adopt only if median AND worst lane do not get worse). NEXT: read PR-29's wording and copy its lane list.")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_prereg_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-PREREG", 2u32, "2026-11-06T17:36Z", "tibia", "11-06 13:36 tibia: DONE. PR-30 written in tibia/docs/BENCHMARK.md above PR-29 (unstaged) at 13:35, before strategy_table or any CFR brain exists. Arms: A the CFR brain drawing from strategy_table 3 shares per think, B live_retreat_tactic 160 2; A reuses B's ReachFirst order, StepAwayLikeTheLiveProbe footing and patrol so only the brain differs. Camp lanes.spi spot (), held-out seeds 1001-1100, worth CheapClearWithin 94934 plus deaths and clears. Prediction: A below B (Strike has no kill value in the abstraction, flat 52 damage per hitter). Decision: holds = CFR stays a baseline and TABULAR-CFR closes on it; fails = candidate, second pre-registered 8-block run. Proof: the section text (docs only, no build).")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_policy_table_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-POLICY-TABLE", 1u32, "2026-11-06T17:33Z", "tibia", "11-06 13:31 tibia: split from TIBIA-NUGGET-TABULAR-CFR. DoD: src/arena_cfr.spi gains strategy_table depth : array i32 (3 shares per state) and state_for (hp, attackers, ready), clamping hp to 0-515 and attackers to 3; tests on c and rust: the low_hp_pressed row puts >= 900 on Heal, a calm full-hp row puts < 100 on StepAway, and state_for round-trips through index_of; build.ps1 -ChecksOnly green. NEXT: the table builder reusing tree_knight's values_at once per table, not once per state. TypeFeatures: the action is the policy::engagement union at the boundary, shares stay an array only inside the table.")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_policy_table_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-POLICY-TABLE", 2u32, "2026-11-06T18:21Z", "tibia", "11-06 14:2x tibia: CODE in place (tibia src/arena_cfr.spi 50A2558EE358, unstaged). New union arena_action = Potion | Melee | Retreat (NOT policy::engagement: that union is Strike | Approach | Hold, so the 10:39 design note's claim was wrong; names checked free of other union cases, since Strike and StepAway already exist in policy and hunting_pack) with action_index. strategy_table depth computes values_at (depth - 1) ONCE and fills 3 shares per state for all 4128 states (fill_table, top-level so the cell budget holds); share_of table st action; state_for hp attackers ready clamps hp to 0-515 and attackers to 0-3. Tests on c and rust: state_for clamps (4127, 0, 405); a table row equals tree_knight's strategy for its state (exact, same computation); the low-hp knight drinks (>= 900 on Potion); a calm knight rarely retreats (< 100). Box checks: cell budget 0, formatter only the held join-then line 110, max line 120. PENDING: node job-1793989280250-tibia-cfrtable-cells (queued after tibia-ci-rest).")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_policy_table_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-POLICY-TABLE", 3u32, "2026-11-06T18:56Z", "tibia", "11-06 14:5x tibia: proof job replaced: job-1793989280250-tibia-cfrtable-cells was stopped while still queued; its arena_cfr run is now part of job-1793991326784-tibia-cfrbrain-cells (same arena_cfr 50A2558EE358, plus hunting_pack and pack_sim).")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_policy_table_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-POLICY-TABLE", 4u32, "2026-11-06T20:42Z", "tibia", "11-06 16:4x tibia: code done and checked on the box (format, cell budget, --check); only the node proof is left. Blocked on: node job-1793996115107-tibia-ci-final (arena_cfr in its file list), queued on tree EF7486F7554A behind job-1793991326784-tibia-cfrbrain-cells, with a background waiter. Resume when: that job finishes; read its log in full, then close or fix.")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_policy_table_5 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-POLICY-TABLE", 5u32, "2026-11-06T21:18Z", "tibia", "11-06 17:1x tibia: job-1793991326784-tibia-cfrbrain-cells FINISHED (log read in full; Cells run_notebook per module on a scratch src snapshot from before the logged_hunts move): arena_cfr 13/13 (c+rust: table rows, state_for, low-hp drinks, calm rarely retreats, and the 9 earlier tests), hunting_pack 13/13 (c), pack_sim 41/41 (c, incl. a_target_equal_to_the_behavior_reweights_nothing), soft_policy 4/6 and logprob 6/10, where EVERY failure is VOID: \"could not start the compiler on port 13953: :lock_timeout\" (the Cells compiler daemon lock under node load), mismatches {} (no assertion failed), and the failing rows include unchanged tests that passed at 08:58 and 11:04. Proof of record stays job-1793996115107-tibia-ci-final (now starting, tree EF7486F7554A).")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_policy_table_6 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-POLICY-TABLE", 6u32, "2026-11-06T22:40Z", "tibia", "11-06 18:3x tibia: PROOF OF RECORD green for this code: node job-1793996115107-tibia-ci-final (build.ps1 -Files on a scratch tree outside the mirror, tree EF7486F7554A, log read in full): layout clean, cell budget 0 over; arena_cfr 13/13 (77FB224B574E, table + game node), hunting_pack 13/13 (7406AE9BAF88, Cfr brain + scored_by + logged_hunts), logprob 10/10 (A01AA2C151BA, estimator + target paths), pack_sim 41/41 (14AD5EE944CC), soft_policy 6/6 (the earlier lock_timeout rows pass here), sweep 1/1. Proof: job-1793996115107-tibia-ci-final.")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_brain_design_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-BRAIN-DESIGN", 1u32, "2026-11-06T18:23Z", "tibia", "11-06 14:22 tibia: split from TIBIA-NUGGET-TABULAR-CFR for PR-30 (light floor). DoD: a design note on this item naming the brain union case and its payload (the strategy table, built once per run, not per think), the observable-to-state mapping (sources for hp, adjacent attackers and potion cooldown in hunting_pack), the roll purpose (a new pack_roll code next to PackSoftDecision 21, with the purpose-code test count), how Potion, Melee and Retreat become the brain's heal and plan answers, and every site to touch with line numbers. NEXT: read wants_heal, after_heal_plan and the Softened arms. TypeFeatures: the brain case carries a record, not a bare array plus ints.")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_brain_design_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-BRAIN-DESIGN", 2u32, "2026-11-06T18:26Z", "tibia", "11-06 14:3x tibia: DESIGN (read from src/hunting_pack.spi at the 14:2x tree). (1) BRAIN: `:== cfr_brain = { table : array i32; depth : i32 }` next to soft_brain (line 229), and brain (231-237) gains `| Cfr : cfr_brain`. The table is arena_cfr::strategy_table depth, built ONCE by the constructor `cfr_tactic depth` (bound in the tactic record, so every seed of a worth block reuses it), never per think. (2) STATE: arena_state_of b attackers p = arena_cfr::state_for (o::health * 515 / units::value_of (player_max_health b::camp)) attackers o::heal_ready, with o = observe b::now p (1360: health is absolute, heal_ready is the potion cooldown). The hp is SCALED to the abstraction's 515, not only clamped, because knight_max_health depends on level (16: 185 + 15 x (level - 8)); attackers is the attackers_of count (1887) every brain already gets. (3) ROLL: pack_roll (44-57) gains `PackArenaDecision`, target_code (59-67) maps it to 22u32 (free; 17-21 and 40/41 taken), and every_pack_roll_has_its_own_purpose_code (94-95) moves from 13 to 14 rolls. One roll per think: conv (keyed_rng::roll_between 0 999 (key b::seed b::tick (slot_number p::hunter::call_sign) PackArenaDecision)). (4) ACTION: arena_act draws by cumulative shares: Potion if roll < s0, Melee if roll < s0 + s1, else Retreat. cfr_heals = o::heal_ready && action = Potion. cfr_plan = (action = Retreat), network_engagement o (action = Melee), so Potion holds (the abstraction prices Potion with tempo 40 and no swing). The plan re-reads the state after the heal gate like every other brain, so a heal in the same tick can move the knight to another row; the roll key is the same, so the draw is the same number. (5) LOG: logged (1937-1940) gains `| Cfr c => with_log_path (logprob::per_mille_log2 (share of the drawn action)) p`, so the CFR brain is IS-ready like Softened. (6) SITES: types 229-237, pack_roll 44-67 + test 95, new functions next to soft_roll (1663-1672: arena_state_of, arena_roll, arena_act, cfr_heals), cfr_plan next to soft_plan (1724), learned_heals 1674-1679 and learned_plan 1728-1733 (one arm each; wants_heal and after_heal_plan already route other brains there), logged 1937-1940, and cfr_tactic next to softened_tactic (2264) with PR-30's shape: order ReachFirst, footing StepAwayLikeTheLiveProbe, patrol Stays (live_retreat_tactic 2283-2286). Every other brain match (player_acts 1950, hunt_sim 240) has a wildcard, so no exhaustive match breaks. Module order already has arena_cfr before hunting_pack (spiral.toml). (7) TEST (c, pack_sim): the CFR brain heals a knight at hp 50 with 2 attackers and a ready potion within its first think (low_hp_pressed's row puts >= 900 on Potion, so a single seed may draw Melee or Retreat: use 5 seeds and assert at least 4 heal). DONE: this note is the DoD.")
inl note_of_tibia_is_target_log_design_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-IS-TARGET-LOG-DESIGN", 1u32, "2026-11-06T18:23Z", "tibia", "11-06 14:22 tibia: split from TIBIA-NUGGET-IMPORTANCE-SAMPLING (its DoD: an IS estimate whose error against fresh sims of the same tactic is quoted on 100 seeds; light floor). DoD: a design note naming where the target's per-mille probability of each sampled bit is computed (same greedy decision, the target's epsilon), the tally field (target_log next to log_path), how pack_sim turns a block of hunts into an array of logprob::logged_hunt (reward = the hunt's profit or the objective's worth), and the measurement: behavior epsilon 100, target epsilon 50 and 0, 100 seeds each, IS estimate vs the fresh-sim mean, pre-registered as PR-31. NEXT: read soft_heals/soft_plan and hunt_log_path. TypeFeatures: the target is a soft_brain record, not a bare epsilon int.")
inl note_of_tibia_is_target_log_design_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-IS-TARGET-LOG-DESIGN", 2u32, "2026-11-06T18:31Z", "tibia", "11-06 14:3x tibia: DESIGN (read from src/soft_policy.spi, hunting_pack.spi 225-235 and 1658-1672 and 1933-1944, pack_sim.spi 196-224). (0) BUG FOUND first: logprob::per_mille_log2 0 is NOT minus infinity: log2_q16 0 returns 0 (bit_length 0 is 0), so a zero-probability step scores as log2(1/1000). A greedy target (epsilon 0) would give every hunt that deviated a weight of about 1/1000 per deviation instead of 0. Fix in the code step: a typed path, `:| target_path = | OnPath : i32 | OffPath`, where any per-mille 0 makes the path OffPath for good, and is_estimate never sees OffPath hunts (dropping a zero-weight hunt is exact for a self-normalized mean; all dropped = the existing None). (1) TARGET: `:== soft_target = { core : learned_core; epsilon : i32 }` and soft_brain (229) gains `scored_as : option soft_target` (None in softened_tactic, so existing tallies are unchanged). Per sampled bit the target's probability of the TAKEN act is (act = target greedy) ? 1000 - eps/2 : eps/2, with the target greedy from core_decision target::core on the same features (a target with another core needs its own decision, so the core is part of the record, not assumed equal). New in soft_policy: per_mille_under (greedy : bool) (epsilon : i32) (act : bool) : i32 and target_probs (greedy : network::decision) (epsilon : i32) (taken : network::decision) : array i32. (2) TALLY: hunter_tally gains `target_log : target_path` (OnPath 0 in the fresh tally next to log_path); logged (1937-1940) adds to it in the Softened arm when scored_as is Some. (3) REWARD: per hunt, additive: the hunt's clear ms and its potions, each scored with its own is_estimate over the same weights. CheapClearWithin is a block statistic (clear_ledger_of over the count), not additive per hunt, so it is not the IS reward. (4) PACK_SIM: logged_hunts camp t r : array logprob::logged_hunt from clear_run per seed (target_log, behavior_log = log_path, reward), OffPath hunts dropped, plus a count of the dropped ones for the report. (5) PR-31 (to pre-register in BENCHMARK.md before the run): behavior soft_troll 100 (CoreNetwork cavebot_network, troll camp), 100 seeds; targets epsilon 90, 50 and 0 on the same core; each IS estimate of mean clear ms and potions against fresh sims of that target on the same 100 seeds. PREDICTION written now: path-level weights over a whole hunt (3 bits per think) are very skewed, so ess falls fast with distance from the behavior: target 90 keeps an ess of at least 10 of 100 and lands within 10 percent of the fresh mean; target 50 has ess under 10; target 0 is OffPath on nearly every hunt (0.95 to the power 3 x thinks), so None or ess 1. If that holds, the nugget's verdict is that path IS only scores small policy steps here, and per-decision weighting needs per-step rewards the sim does not log yet. DONE: this note is the DoD; code goes to a new item.")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_brain_code_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-BRAIN-CODE", 1u32, "2026-11-06T18:23Z", "tibia", "11-06 14:22 tibia: split from TIBIA-NUGGET-TABULAR-CFR. DoD: the brain case and dispatch arms from the design note in src/hunting_pack.spi, the pack roll purpose added with its test updated, a c test in pack_sim that the CFR brain heals a low-hp knight under two attackers, build.ps1 -ChecksOnly clean apart from the held join-then lines, node Cells green. NEXT: wait for the design note. TypeFeatures: as the design note says.")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_brain_code_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-BRAIN-CODE", 2u32, "2026-11-06T18:29Z", "tibia", "11-06 14:3x tibia: design landed on TIBIA-CFR-BRAIN-DESIGN (sites with line numbers, roll code 22, roll count 13 -> 14, test with 5 seeds and >= 4 heals). Still waits on TIBIA-CFR-POLICY-TABLE's node proof (job-1793989280250-tibia-cfrtable-cells).")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_brain_code_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-BRAIN-CODE", 3u32, "2026-11-06T18:56Z", "tibia", "11-06 14:5x tibia: CODE in place ahead of the table's node proof (deps are code-ready locally; tibia src/hunting_pack.spi 3D6C7026DB9D, unstaged). cfr_brain { table; depth }, brain case Cfr, arena_state_of (hp scaled to 515 by player_max_health), arena_roll, row_total, cuts, drawn_action, arena_act, arena_share, cfr_heals, cfr_plan, cfr_logged, cfr_tactic (live_retreat_tactic 160 2 with the brain swapped, so PR-30's arms differ only in the brain). DEVIATIONS from the design, both forced by the cell budget: (a) no new pack_roll case: pack_roll was already at the cell limit, so PackSoftDecision is RENAMED PackPolicyDraw (code 21 unchanged, roll count stays 13) and the arena draw keys entity 900 + slot (soft keys 300-302 and 400-402), so the streams stay disjoint; (b) learned_heals/learned_plan split into weights_heals/weights_plan for Network and Hashed, and logged into soft_logged/cfr_logged. ADDED: the draw scales the roll by the row total (roll x total / 1000), because per-mille averages can sum to 999, and a raw roll of 999 would then draw a zero-share action (whose per_mille_log2 0 is the log2(0) bug found in TIBIA-IS-TARGET-LOG-DESIGN). Test (c): cfr_draws_follow_cumulative_shares on a hand row (600, 300, 100): rolls 599/600/899/900 -> Potion/Melee/Melee/Retreat, and a (999, 0, 0) row at roll 999 -> Potion. The design's 5-seed heal test is replaced by this deterministic one (a hunt-level check is PR-30's job). Box checks: cell budget 0, max line 120, formatter diffs only join-then. PENDING: node job-1793991326784-tibia-cfrbrain-cells (arena_cfr + hunting_pack + pack_sim, after tibia-ci-rest; it replaces the stopped job-1793989280250-tibia-cfrtable-cells).")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_brain_code_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-BRAIN-CODE", 4u32, "2026-11-06T19:14Z", "tibia", "11-06 15:3x tibia: proof job widened while queued: job-1793991326784-tibia-cfrbrain-cells now runs the current src (hunting_pack 82B8DEB5C308, which adds the IS target fields on top of the CFR brain) over arena_cfr, logprob, soft_policy, hunting_pack, pack_sim.")
