inl note_of_tibia_is_target_log_code_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-IS-TARGET-LOG-CODE", 1u32, "2026-11-06T18:32Z", "tibia", "11-06 14:3x tibia: from TIBIA-IS-TARGET-LOG-DESIGN. DoD: the design's (0)-(4) in src (soft_policy, hunting_pack, pack_sim), golden tests on c: per_mille_under both ways, a target equal to the behavior gives target_log = log_path on a softened hunt, a greedy target turns a deviating hunt OffPath, logged_hunts drops OffPath hunts; build.ps1 -ChecksOnly clean apart from the held join-then lines; node Cells green. NEXT: target_path in logprob with its test. TypeFeatures: OnPath | OffPath union, soft_target record, no sentinel log values.")
inl note_of_tibia_is_target_log_code_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-IS-TARGET-LOG-CODE", 2u32, "2026-11-06T19:14Z", "tibia", "11-06 15:3x tibia: CODE in place ahead of IS-ESTIMATOR's node proof (tibia src unstaged: logprob A01AA2C151BA, soft_policy D9528C7FE895, hunting_pack 82B8DEB5C308, pack_sim EF262AEBADBE). One change from the design: logged_hunt now CARRIES the target_path (target : OnPath i32 | OffPath) instead of pack_sim dropping OffPath hunts (arrays are fixed-size, so dropping meant two passes or a copy). is_estimate gives an OffPath hunt weight 0 (exactly the self-normalized meaning) and returns None when no hunt is on the path; the top log ratio is an option folded over the hunts. logprob: target_path, step_target (per-mille <= 0 -> OffPath for good), along, off_path_hunt, has_estimate, path_pair. soft_policy: decision alias, per_mille_under, target_probs. hunting_pack: soft_target, soft_brain.scored_as (None in softened_tactic), hunter_tally.target_log (OnPath 0 fresh), target_probs_of, with_target_path, scored_step, with_target_log (in soft_logged), scored_by. pack_sim: troll_core, scored_troll, reward_of, logged_hunt_of, fill_hunts over hunting_pack::seed_run, logged_hunts, clear_ms. Tests: logprob (c, rust) a zero step leaves the path for good, off-path hunts weigh nothing (mean 20, ess 2.0), no hunt on path = no estimate; soft_policy (c, rust) the behavior epsilon scores the same path, a greedy target gives a flipped act 0; hunting_pack (c) a target equal to the behavior logs its path, a greedy target leaves an exploring hunt's path; pack_sim (c) a target equal to the behavior reweights nothing (IS mean = plain mean of 2 clear times, ess 2.0). Box checks on the 4 files: cell budget 0, max line 120, formatter only join-then. PENDING: node job-1793991326784-tibia-cfrbrain-cells (widened while queued to arena_cfr, logprob, soft_policy, hunting_pack, pack_sim at these hashes).")
inl note_of_tibia_is_target_log_code_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-IS-TARGET-LOG-CODE", 3u32, "2026-11-06T20:38Z", "tibia", "11-06 16:5x tibia: LOCAL TYPE CHECK caught a compile error before any node time (SpiralCompiler --check on a scratch copy with the predict manifest extended, the way predict.ps1 extends it): apps/predict could not use pack_sim::, because src/pack_sim.spi is a test NOTEBOOK, not a module of the src package (src/spiral.toml lists no pack_sim), so the IS design's 'pack_sim logged_hunts' was in the wrong place. FIX: reward_of, logged_hunt_of, fill_hunts and logged_hunts moved into hunting_pack (after seed_run_of; logged_hunts takes a seed_run); pack_sim keeps only test helpers (scored_run, self_scored); is_softened builds its own troll_spot, troll_core, behavior, scored (logged renamed logged_for, since hunting_pack already has logged); cfr_arena reads deaths from ledger_on ... (held_out_block ()) instead of pack_sim::sums_over. --check now passes for the src package and for apps/predict (both programs). The queued jobs were refreshed while still queued: job-1793993684886-tibia-pr30-run, job-1793994599738-tibia-pr31-run and job-1793996115107-tibia-ci-final all unpack tree EF7486F7554A, and ci-final now runs build.ps1 -Files sweep,arena_cfr,logprob,soft_policy,hunting_pack,pack_sim, so it is the proof of record for the final tree (job-1793991326784-tibia-cfrbrain-cells is running an earlier snapshot).")
inl note_of_tibia_is_target_log_code_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-IS-TARGET-LOG-CODE", 4u32, "2026-11-06T21:06Z", "tibia", "11-06 17:1x tibia: job-1793991326784-tibia-cfrbrain-cells, partial read (still running pack_sim): hunting_pack 13/13 green on c (cfr_draws_follow_cumulative_shares, a_target_equal_to_the_behavior_logs_its_path, a_greedy_target_leaves_the_path_of_an_exploring_hunt, the purpose-code count 13). soft_policy 4/6: both failures are VOID, not red: no_exploration_always_keeps_the_greedy_act (rust) and the_logged_probabilities_feed_the_path_weight (c, its rust row not run) died with \"could not start the compiler on port 13953: :lock_timeout\" (the Cells compiler daemon lock under node load); both tests are unchanged and passed at 11:04, and the two new target tests passed on c and rust. soft_policy reruns in job-1793996115107-tibia-ci-final.")
inl note_of_tibia_is_target_log_code_5 () = Note ("TIBIA-IS-TARGET-LOG-CODE", 5u32, "2026-11-06T21:18Z", "tibia", "11-06 17:1x tibia: job-1793991326784-tibia-cfrbrain-cells FINISHED (log read in full; Cells run_notebook per module on a scratch src snapshot from before the logged_hunts move): arena_cfr 13/13 (c+rust: table rows, state_for, low-hp drinks, calm rarely retreats, and the 9 earlier tests), hunting_pack 13/13 (c), pack_sim 41/41 (c, incl. a_target_equal_to_the_behavior_reweights_nothing), soft_policy 4/6 and logprob 6/10, where EVERY failure is VOID: \"could not start the compiler on port 13953: :lock_timeout\" (the Cells compiler daemon lock under node load), mismatches {} (no assertion failed), and the failing rows include unchanged tests that passed at 08:58 and 11:04. Proof of record stays job-1793996115107-tibia-ci-final (now starting, tree EF7486F7554A).")
inl note_of_tibia_is_target_log_code_6 () = Note ("TIBIA-IS-TARGET-LOG-CODE", 6u32, "2026-11-06T22:44Z", "tibia", "11-06 18:3x tibia: PROOF OF RECORD green for this code: node job-1793996115107-tibia-ci-final (build.ps1 -Files on a scratch tree outside the mirror, tree EF7486F7554A, log read in full): layout clean, cell budget 0 over; arena_cfr 13/13 (77FB224B574E, table + game node), hunting_pack 13/13 (7406AE9BAF88, Cfr brain + scored_by + logged_hunts), logprob 10/10 (A01AA2C151BA, estimator + target paths), pack_sim 41/41 (14AD5EE944CC), soft_policy 6/6 (the earlier lock_timeout rows pass here), sweep 1/1. Proof: job-1793996115107-tibia-ci-final.")
inl note_of_tibia_is_prereg_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-IS-PREREG", 1u32, "2026-11-06T18:32Z", "tibia", "11-06 14:3x tibia: from TIBIA-IS-TARGET-LOG-DESIGN. DoD: a PR-31 section above PR-30 in tibia/docs/BENCHMARK.md written before TIBIA-IS-TARGET-LOG-CODE runs any hunt: arms, camp (pack_sim troll_camp), seeds, metric (IS estimate vs fresh mean, relative error, ess, dropped count), prediction (target 90 ess >= 10 and within 10 percent; 50 ess < 10; 0 None or ess 1) and decision. NEXT: copy PR-30's table shape.")
inl note_of_tibia_is_prereg_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-IS-PREREG", 2u32, "2026-11-06T18:33Z", "tibia", "11-06 14:3x tibia: DONE. PR-31 written in tibia/docs/BENCHMARK.md above PR-30 (unstaged) at 14:35, before any target is logged (TIBIA-IS-TARGET-LOG-CODE has no code yet). Arms: behavior soft_troll 100, targets epsilon 90/50/0 on the same core, fresh control on the same held-out seeds 1001-1100. Metric: IS estimate of mean clear ms and potions vs the fresh mean, relative error, ess of 100, dropped off-path hunts. Prediction: target 90 ess >= 10 and both within 10 percent; target 50 ess < 10; target 0 no estimate or ess 1. Decision: holds = path IS only scores small policy steps (the nugget verdict); fails with target 50 within 10 percent at ess >= 10 = IS becomes the cheap candidate screen and a second pre-registered run tries another core. Proof: the section text (docs only).")
inl note_of_lib_layers_1_census_1 () = Note ("LIB-LAYERS-1-CENSUS", 1u32, "2026-11-06T19:04Z", "main", "Split from LIB-LAYERS (2400 min > the 240 cap). DoD: a table in a note covering every lib/spiral module, with its own host macros (\\$' and !!!! count), direct lib imports (:< plus qualified refs), and pure = no own macros and every import pure; plus the count of core candidates and the top blocking edges. Next step: scan lib/spiral with a scratchpad probe and post the table. TypeFeatures: none; this is a measurement, not code.")
inl note_of_lib_layers_1_census_2 () = Note ("LIB-LAYERS-1-CENSUS", 2u32, "2026-11-06T19:12Z", "main", "main 11-06 15:3x CENSUS DONE. proof: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\LIB-LAYERS-1-CENSUS\\lib-layers.ps1 (-Lib <dir>; git ls-files based, fails closed on 0 files; :# test blocks and // lines excluded) and its full output lib-layers-20261106.out. RESULT over lib/spiral (155 modules): 65 have no host macro of their own ($' / $\" / !!!!), but only 22 are TRANSITIVELY pure: array_prototypes bitset conversation f32_kernels file_system_operators fin_vector fixed_views iter_prototypes keyed_rng markup option_operators pickler rust_operators sized_array sm'_operators text_prototypes tuple_list units unsupported util wire xsd_certificate. TOP BLOCKERS (an impure module: the macro-free modules it taints directly): sm' 22 (351 own macros), xml 9 (8), convert 7 (111), am' 6 (124), erlang_term 6 (12), listm' 5 (95), decimal 4 (0, impure only via sm'), resultm 4 (97), leptos 3, reflection 3, xpath 3 (3), xsd 3 (0). FINDINGS: (1) xml is the cheapest lever, 8 macros tainting 9 modules (the xsd/schematron family). Two of the 8 are OS calls inside a parser module: read_text_replacing_invalid_utf8 (std::fs::read) and is_file (Path::is_file / FileExists). They belong in file_system (the os layer), and their callers are lib xsd_resolve plus fiscal corpus, corpus_checks, families, generator, sunat and reports, so the move is fiscal's call. The other 6 are char decoding and find, which belong behind sm'/unicode. (2) sm' is the structural blocker: a pure text core can't exist while string primitives are per-backend host macros, so a 'core' layer that covers WGSL/eBPF must exclude text, and std is where sm' lives. That makes the layer rule 'core imports no sm''; it is not a goal of purifying sm'. Next step: LIB-LAYERS assigns each module its layer from this table and adds the ratchet (core-candidate count may only grow). The xml os-split goes to fiscal.")
inl note_of_xdumps_bin_media_type_1 () = Note ("XDUMPS-BIN-MEDIA-TYPE", 1u32, "2026-11-06T19:09Z", "x-dumps", "The 392 geygey_hadid bin media are progressive JPEGs (magic ffd8ffe0) the harvester could not classify (ambiguous CDN content-type). They serve as octet-stream so the UI img src=...bin shows broken. FIX: (1) serve-side timeline_serve content_type sniff magic bytes -> image/jpeg|png|gif|webp (img renders by content-type, no data change); (2) harvest-side xarchive media stage sniff magic bytes to assign real ext+type so future harvests never emit .bin. ~2% of media; 98% photo+video already render. See XDUMPS-TIMELINE-MEDIA notes 11-06.")
inl note_of_xdumps_bin_media_type_2 () = Note ("XDUMPS-BIN-MEDIA-TYPE", 2u32, "2026-11-06T19:24Z", "x-dumps", "Harvest-side fix IMPLEMENTED + verified 11-06 (unstaged, xarchive/src/media.rs). Root: extension(url) returned 'bin' for extension-less media URLs (Wayback im_, bare CDN paths) though the bytes were JPEG. Added sniff_ext(body) magic-byte sniff (ffd8=jpg, 8950..=png, GIF8=gif, RIFF..WEBP=webp, ..ftyp=mp4, else bin), used at SAVE time when the URL ext is 'bin', so the file is written with its real extension and the UI <img> renders it. Unit test media::tests::sniff_ext_reads_magic_bytes PASSES; crate compiles (cargo test exit 0). So FUTURE harvests won't emit .bin. REMAINING for full item: (a) reprocess the existing 392 geygey .bin -> re-run the media stage (reclassifies .bin->.jpg on disk + media.tsv via the new sniff; HTTP cache Immutable so no re-download), then timeline->merge->world + re-transfer world to the box serve, to make the CURRENT 392 render -- DELIBERATE (world rebuild + live-serve re-transfer), deferred, not rushed as wait-filler while the serve is freshly live; (b) optional: serve-side content-type sniff in x's gated timeline_serve for zero-reprocess rendering. Progress ~45%.")
inl note_of_xdumps_bin_media_type_3 () = Note ("XDUMPS-BIN-MEDIA-TYPE", 3u32, "2026-11-06T19:35Z", "x-dumps", "CORRECTION to the reprocess plan (verified the media flow). The world's media path = media.tsv col4 (local path from the media stage); world.rs media_type() derives the type from the EXTENSION (.jpg/.png/.webp->photo, .mp4->video, .gif->animated_gif, else the raw ext e.g. 'bin'). So re-running the media stage does NOT fix existing .bin: the stage's existence check (dir.join({id}_{n}.{url_ext}) with url_ext='bin') finds the .bin and keeps it. CORRECT SAFE existing-.bin fix (non-destructive, no refetch, no data-loss risk since geygey .bin may be the only copy): (1) on europa cp each geygey_hadid/media/*.bin -> same-stem .jpg (the .bin ARE progressive JPEGs; keep .bin as backup); (2) sed -i 's/\\\\.bin\\\\t/.jpg\\\\t/' geygey media.tsv (col4 only; url col has no .bin); (3) timeline (5) -> merge -> world => world media becomes .jpg/photo; (4) scp world->box + restart serve => the 392 render as <img>. LIMITATION: the sniff_ext code fix (media.rs) only affects FUTURE downloads (new .bin get a sniffed ext); a future media RE-run would re-emit .bin for these existing ones (existence check keeps .bin) and revert media.tsv, until the code fix is improved to prefer an existing sibling .jpg or to re-sniff an existing .bin. Sequenced into the combined media-quote rebuild (heartbeat) to avoid a double serve restart.")
inl note_of_xdumps_bin_media_type_4 () = Note ("XDUMPS-BIN-MEDIA-TYPE", 4u32, "2026-11-06T20:16Z", "x-dumps", "DONE + LIVE 11-06. Existing-.bin fix complete and verified on :8787: all 392 geygey + 1 i574n .bin were progressive JPEGs (388) / PNGs (4) misclassified by extensionless URLs. Reclassified (non-destructive cp .bin->.jpg/.png, keeping .bin backups) on BOTH europa and box (C:\\home\\xdumps\\media\\accounts\\<h>\\media), sed media.tsv col4, rebuilt timeline->merge->world (bin-type now 0, posts 163,348), swapped the world into the serve file + restarted the serve. VERIFIED live: former-.bin now serve with correct content-type (geygey 1283961648244563968_0.jpg -> 200 image/jpeg; 1542667749125750785_0.png -> 200 image/png) so the UI <img> renders them; /timeline 200, media renders, dark mode on. Side benefit: rebuilding geygey's timeline with the enriched binary gave its 125,528 posts the full enriched schema (uniform with other accounts; world 120->146MB). FORWARD-FIX: xarchive/src/media.rs sniff_ext (unstaged) stops future harvests emitting .bin -- but it only affects NEW downloads on europa, so it must be deployed to europa (scp media.rs + rebuild) to take effect for future harvests; LIMITATION: a future media re-run with the current code keeps existing .bin (existence check) so re-apply the cp+sed if re-harvesting geygey. Marking Done (render goal met).")
inl note_of_tibia_pr30_program_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-PR30-PROGRAM", 1u32, "2026-11-06T19:26Z", "tibia", "11-06 15:3x tibia: split from TIBIA-NUGGET-TABULAR-CFR (light floor). DoD: the program in apps/predict with a ///> _ main printing one tab-separated row per arm (arm, worth, deaths, clears), runnable as scripts/predict.ps1 -Module cfr_arena -SkipChecks; cell budget 0, lines <= 120; no run (that is TIBIA-PR30-RUN). NEXT: copy lanes.spi's spot and clear limit. TypeFeatures: the arm is a record { name; tactic }, not parallel strings.")
inl note_of_tibia_pr30_program_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-PR30-PROGRAM", 2u32, "2026-11-06T19:35Z", "tibia", "11-06 15:4x tibia: PROGRAM in place (tibia apps/predict/cfr_arena.spi 4E759BBF9823, unstaged; not in the predict spiral.toml: predict.ps1 -Module adds it to its scratch copy). Arms as records { name; tactic }: cfr (cfr_tactic 3), cfr_argmax (each row hardened to its largest share = 1000, PR-30's descriptive variant), retreat2 (live_retreat_tactic 160 2). Per arm: held-out worth (CheapClearWithin 94934 over held_out_first/held_out_count = 1001-1100), deaths (pack_sim::sums_over), clears (all_killed per seed). Box checks: formatter no change, cell budget 0, max line 116. Compile is unproven until the run: queued as node job-1793993684886-tibia-pr30-run (tree E6F7C8609C7F) after job-1793991326784-tibia-cfrbrain-cells; if the brain's tests fail there, this run's numbers are void.")
inl note_of_tibia_pr30_program_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-PR30-PROGRAM", 3u32, "2026-11-06T20:38Z", "tibia", "11-06 16:5x tibia: LOCAL TYPE CHECK caught a compile error before any node time (SpiralCompiler --check on a scratch copy with the predict manifest extended, the way predict.ps1 extends it): apps/predict could not use pack_sim::, because src/pack_sim.spi is a test NOTEBOOK, not a module of the src package (src/spiral.toml lists no pack_sim), so the IS design's 'pack_sim logged_hunts' was in the wrong place. FIX: reward_of, logged_hunt_of, fill_hunts and logged_hunts moved into hunting_pack (after seed_run_of; logged_hunts takes a seed_run); pack_sim keeps only test helpers (scored_run, self_scored); is_softened builds its own troll_spot, troll_core, behavior, scored (logged renamed logged_for, since hunting_pack already has logged); cfr_arena reads deaths from ledger_on ... (held_out_block ()) instead of pack_sim::sums_over. --check now passes for the src package and for apps/predict (both programs). The queued jobs were refreshed while still queued: job-1793993684886-tibia-pr30-run, job-1793994599738-tibia-pr31-run and job-1793996115107-tibia-ci-final all unpack tree EF7486F7554A, and ci-final now runs build.ps1 -Files sweep,arena_cfr,logprob,soft_policy,hunting_pack,pack_sim, so it is the proof of record for the final tree (job-1793991326784-tibia-cfrbrain-cells is running an earlier snapshot).")
