inl note_of_tibia_cfr_game_node_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-GAME-NODE", 1u32, "2026-11-06T19:56Z", "tibia", "11-06 16:1x tibia: found while re-reading TIBIA-LEARNING-NUGGETS' 08:17 split: it says the game-node state machine rides along inside TABULAR-CFR's abstraction, but tree_cost branches on a bool (alive = death_cost st k c = 0). DoD: `:| arena_node = | Alive : arena_state | Fallen`, next_node st k c : arena_node as the single step site, tree_cost matches on it (Fallen pays early_death left), the 12 arena_cfr tests unchanged and green on c and rust, cell budget 0. NEXT: write the union and next_node. TypeFeatures: union, no bool flag.")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_game_node_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-GAME-NODE", 2u32, "2026-11-06T20:17Z", "tibia", "11-06 16:2x tibia: CODE in place (tibia src/arena_cfr.spi 77FB224B574E, unstaged): `:| arena_node = | Survives : arena_state | Dies` (Fallen is taken by vitality's GADT), next_node st k c is the single step site, and tree_cost matches on it (Dies pays early_death left). Same semantics by construction (Dies exactly where the old alive bool was false), so the existing 12 arena_cfr tests are the proof. Box checks: cell budget 0, max line 113, formatter only the held join-then line. PENDING: node job-1793996115107-tibia-ci-final (arena_cfr in its file list).")
