inl note_of_tibia_cfr_game_node_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-GAME-NODE", 4u32, "2026-11-06T22:41Z", "tibia", "11-06 18:3x tibia: PROOF OF RECORD green for this code: node job-1793996115107-tibia-ci-final (build.ps1 -Files on a scratch tree outside the mirror, tree EF7486F7554A, log read in full): layout clean, cell budget 0 over; arena_cfr 13/13 (77FB224B574E, table + game node), hunting_pack 13/13 (7406AE9BAF88, Cfr brain + scored_by + logged_hunts), logprob 10/10 (A01AA2C151BA, estimator + target paths), pack_sim 41/41 (14AD5EE944CC), soft_policy 6/6 (the earlier lock_timeout rows pass here), sweep 1/1. Proof: job-1793996115107-tibia-ci-final.")
inl note_of_link_split_corpus_1 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-CORPUS", 1u32, "2026-11-06T20:45Z", "compiler", "11-06 16:4x compiler: split from LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE (its corpus step). split-units only cuts inside one main.spi, so real multi-module packages (lib, x, kit, Cells) need a module-boundary cut, which is a pure manifest transformation the harness can do with no compiler change: for a package with top-level module blocks b1..bn (a folder entry and its children are one block), cut k puts b1..bk in a model unit (same packageDir/packages, auto-export: monomorphic) and the rest in an app unit (packages: + model-, link: model-). Verdict: the app's --check result equals the single package's (and for a root with a main, the run's exit code). DoD: a split-corpus suite in apps/compiler/scripts/test.ps1 reading matrix.SplitCorpus (absolute roots), strided cuts like the sample oracle, results.tsv with id/cut/verdict/detail; run once on the box against one small root and listed for the node. next step: implement and try x/apps/client.")
inl note_of_link_split_corpus_2 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-CORPUS", 2u32, "2026-11-06T20:45Z", "compiler", "11-06 16:4x compiler: typefeatureset plan: none applies; harness-only change in pwsh glue, no compiler data shapes.")
inl note_of_link_split_corpus_3 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-CORPUS", 3u32, "2026-11-06T20:59Z", "compiler", "11-06 17:0x compiler: first box run of the new split-corpus suite (test.ps1, matrix SplitCorpus = x/apps/client, 49 module blocks, 8 strided cuts): every cut came back exit 3 with 'Attestation timed out after 30000 ms', i.e. --check's default 30 s cap on the two-package check under box load, not a verdict. The harness now passes --timeout-ms 900000 and reports a timeout as the detail; rerun running. Also fixed before that: the suite name was missing from test.ps1's suite whitelist.")
inl note_of_link_split_corpus_4 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-CORPUS", 4u32, "2026-11-06T21:08Z", "compiler", "11-06 17:1x compiler: FIRST REAL FINDING of the corpus oracle (x/apps/client, rerun with the 900 s check cap): 3 of 8 cuts pass; the 5 failures were all module-name SHADOWING, not typing: client has its own module wire, and lib/spiral has a wire too. In the single package the package's own wire shadows lib's; in the split the app listed ../model- FIRST under packages:, so lib's wire (spiral-, listed later) won, and api.spi's :< wire bound the wrong module (Unbound classified/field/collect). Moving ../model- LAST makes cut 18 check clean (exit 0): later packages shadow earlier ones. The harness now appends the split unit at the END of packages:, which is the only order equivalent to 'own modules shadow dependencies'. Worth a docs line for anyone splitting a real package into units: list the split-off unit after the lib packages. Rerun running.")
inl note_of_link_split_corpus_5 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-CORPUS", 5u32, "2026-11-06T21:15Z", "compiler", "11-06 17:2x compiler: split-corpus suite WORKS on the box (installed core 1524D5D56E6A11D5, run single-flight-20261106-170911): x/apps/client, 49 module blocks, 8 strided cuts, 0 fail: every cut's --check verdict equals the single package's (exit 0). The 3 harness fixes it needed are in: suite whitelist, --timeout-ms 900000 (the default 30 s cap timed out the two-package check under load), and the split-off unit listed LAST under packages: (module-name shadowing, n4). next step: list more roots in matrix SplitCorpus (lib/spiral, kit, Cells, regex/src) and run the suite on the node.")
inl note_of_link_split_corpus_6 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-CORPUS", 6u32, "2026-11-06T22:49Z", "compiler", "11-06 18:4x compiler: two more roots added to matrix SplitCorpus and run on the box (installed core 8F0094967068FC85, run single-flight-20261106-183547): spiral/apps/cells/spi (17 module blocks) and spiral/apps/kernel/src (13): 20 cuts, 0 fail; with x/apps/client that is 28 cuts over 3 real packages, all equal to the single package's --check verdict. lib/spiral, regex/src and tibia/src declare their modules in spiral.toml only, so the harness needs a toml reader before they can join (the remaining step). next step: toml manifests in the split-corpus harness, then a node run over every root.")
inl note_of_link_split_corpus_7 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-CORPUS", 7u32, "2026-11-06T22:55Z", "compiler", "11-06 18:5x compiler: the harness now reads spiral.toml roots too (edition, packageDir, packages, modules ''' block; a root that already links is skipped). regex/src (toml only, 16 modules): 7 cuts, 0 fail (run single-flight-20261106-185110). Running total on the box, installed core 8F0094967068FC85: 35 cuts over 4 real packages (x/apps/client, apps/cells/spi, apps/kernel/src, regex/src), 0 fail. matrix SplitCorpus now also lists the heavy roots x/apps/sim/spi, tibia/src and spiral/lib/spiral, which are too large for the saturated box. next step: one node run of -Suite split-corpus over all 7 roots (on a quiet node, after kit's TRAIN36), then Done.")
inl note_of_link_split_corpus_8 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-CORPUS", 8u32, "2026-11-06T23:36Z", "compiler", "11-06 19:3x compiler: two more roots on the box (installed core 8F0094967068FC85): tibia/src (toml) 8 cuts 0 fail, x/apps/sim/spi 8 cuts 0 fail, after one more harness fix: packages: entries must be RELATIVE paths (the manifest parser rejects 'C:/home/git/x/apps/client-' with 'Expecting ... relative package path'), so the harness now rewrites each entry relative to the cut unit's own directory (packageDir may stay absolute). RUNNING TOTAL: 51 cuts over 6 real packages (x/apps/client, x/apps/sim/spi, apps/cells/spi, apps/kernel/src, regex/src, tibia/src), 0 fail. Only spiral/lib/spiral is left (largest root; node). next step: the lib/spiral run on the node after kit's TRAIN36, then Done.")
inl note_of_link_split_corpus_9 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-CORPUS", 9u32, "2026-11-06T23:39Z", "compiler", "11-06 19:4x compiler: DONE. The split-corpus suite (apps/compiler/scripts/test.ps1, matrix SplitCorpus; unstaged) runs over 6 real packages on the box, 51 cuts, 0 fail: x/apps/client 8, x/apps/sim/spi 8, apps/cells/spi 8, apps/kernel/src 12, regex/src 7, tibia/src 8; each cut's --check verdict equals the single package's. Harness rules learned on the way: the split-off unit goes LAST under packages: (module-name shadowing vs lib), packages: entries must be relative to the unit's own dir, and --check needs --timeout-ms 900000 under load. lib/spiral and kit/src cannot join: their modules are IMPLICIT (spiral.toml with no module list; kit's modules: is empty), so there is no declared order to cut; the harness now skips such roots with a named line instead of crashing. Follow-up filed: LINK-SPLIT-CORPUS-IMPLICIT.")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_kill_value_design_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-KILL-VALUE-DESIGN", 1u32, "2026-11-06T20:57Z", "tibia", "11-06 17:0x tibia: from PR-30's prediction (the abstraction gives Strike/Melee no kill value, only the 40 saved tempo). DoD: a design note naming the state change (a target hp bucket in arena_state, its count and the new state_count), the per-step damage the knight deals (creatures' melee formula), the kill payoff (cyclops loot and experience in gold units from catalog), how values_at's cost of solving grows, and the tests that would show the strategy now prefers Melee when the target is low. NEXT: read creatures.spi's cyclops stats and the knight's damage in combat.spi. TypeFeatures: buckets as a union or bounded record, not raw ints in the index.")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_kill_value_design_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-KILL-VALUE-DESIGN", 2u32, "2026-11-06T21:02Z", "tibia", "11-06 17:0x tibia: DESIGN (read from src/creatures.spi: cyclops_stats max_health 260, experience 150, melee_max 105, armor 20, defense 20; gold_drop_of Cyclops = drop 82000 47, i.e. 82 percent for 1-47 coins, about 20 gp expected; hunting_pack.spi player_hit -> combat::melee_hit against that armor and defense). (1) WHAT A KILL IS WORTH HERE: the loot (~20 gp) is noise next to the abstraction's 14000 death price and 50 potion price, so a kill's real value is that it REMOVES AN ATTACKER, cutting all later damage. The current game gives Melee neither: attackers only drop through Retreat (max 0 (attackers - 1), at 40 tempo). (2) STATE: arena_state gains the focused target's health as a bounded union `:| target_health = | Fresh | Wounded | Low` (260-176, 175-88, 87-1, thirds of 260), so state_count goes from 4128 to 12384 and index_of gains a factor 3. The union keeps the bucket out of raw ints (TypeFeatures). (3) TRANSITION: Melee moves the target one bucket down per step (Fresh -> Wounded -> Low -> killed) when the camp presses, since the knight swings while hit, and with Spread too; a kill sets attackers to max 0 (attackers - 1) and resets the target to Fresh (the next cyclops). Calibrate \"one bucket per step\" against measured knight damage on the cyclops spot (pack_sim's clear_ledger: kills per clear ms) before trusting it; if mean damage per step is under 87, use two steps per bucket. Potion and Retreat leave the target bucket unchanged (Retreat already lowers attackers). (4) PAYOFF: cost loses Melee's tempo term (already 0) and gains -20 per kill (loot) so ties favour finishing; no experience term (the README profit rule is gold). (5) COST: values_at works 3x the states, so tests stay at depth <= 3 (12384 x 200 rounds x 6 pairs per level, well under the current runtime x 3). (6) TESTS: under 2 attackers at full hp with the target Low, the strategy puts more on Melee than on Retreat (finishing removes an attacker without the tempo); with the target Fresh and the knight at Low hp, Potion still dominates (existing test kept); the 12 current tests keep their meaning with the target pinned Fresh. NEXT for code: a new item after PR-30 reports, since PR-30 measures the current game first; this note is the DoD.")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_kill_value_design_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-KILL-VALUE-DESIGN", 3u32, "2026-11-06T21:02Z", "tibia", "11-06 17:0x tibia: Proof: the design note above is the DoD of this docs-only item.")
inl note_of_tibia_is_per_decision_design_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-IS-PER-DECISION-DESIGN", 1u32, "2026-11-06T20:57Z", "tibia", "11-06 17:0x tibia: from PR-31's prediction (path weights over a whole hunt collapse the ess beyond small policy steps). DoD: a design note naming the per-think reward stream (damage taken, potions spent, kills as they happen, from hunter_tally's fields), where a think's reward and its cumulative log ratio are recorded (a bounded per-hunt array or a running sum of weighted rewards in the tally), the estimator formula in logprob (sum over thinks of w_t r_t, self-normalized per step), and the test that per-decision and path IS agree when rewards arrive only at the end. NEXT: read acts_after_aim and hunter_tally. TypeFeatures: reward kinds as a union, not parallel ints.")
inl note_of_tibia_is_per_decision_design_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-IS-PER-DECISION-DESIGN", 2u32, "2026-11-06T20:59Z", "tibia", "11-06 17:1x tibia: DESIGN (read from src/hunting_pack.spi: hunter_tally 174-184, the potion count bump at 1408, the damage bump at 802, logged/soft_logged 2014-2026). (1) WHY: path IS weights a hunt's whole return by the product of every think's ratio, so one late deviation zeroes or inflates rewards earned long before it; per-decision IS weights each reward only by the ratio product up to the think that earned it, which is still unbiased (later choices cannot change an earlier reward) and has far lower variance on long hunts. (2) EVENTS: a reward-kind union `:| reward_kind = | PotionSpent | DamageTaken | Killed` and a record `:== reward_event = { tick : i32; ratio : logprob::target_path; kind : reward_kind; amount : i32 }`, where ratio is target_log minus log_path AT THAT MOMENT (OnPath d, or OffPath once the target could not have acted so; OffPath events weigh 0). (3) STORAGE (the nugget's \"bounded histories\"): the tally gains a bounded event log, a fixed-capacity array plus a count (capacity 256; a hunt with more events marks itself Truncated, and the estimator reports truncated hunts instead of silently dropping rewards), appended at the three reward sites: 1408 (PotionSpent, amount 1), 802 (DamageTaken, amount = hurt), and the kill site in the score update (Killed, amount 1). Only Softened brains with scored_as Some pay for the log; every other tally keeps count 0. (4) ESTIMATOR (logprob): weighted per-decision IS, normalized per time bucket so it stays scale-free like is_estimate: bucket events by tick / think_period across hunts; in each bucket, sum w r / sum w, with w = exp2_q16 (ratio - top ratio of that bucket); the estimate is the sum over buckets. ess is reported per bucket (min and median). (5) TESTS (golden, hand-computable like is_estimate's): rewards only at the last tick reproduce path IS exactly (same weights, one bucket); a hunt that goes OffPath after its first reward keeps that reward at full weight and drops only the later ones; equal behavior and target give the plain per-bucket sums. (6) COST: 256 events x 16 bytes per hunt only on scored runs; no change to unscored hunts. NEXT for code: a new item after PR-31 reports, since PR-31's verdict decides whether path IS is enough; this note is the DoD.")
inl note_of_tibia_is_per_decision_design_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-IS-PER-DECISION-DESIGN", 3u32, "2026-11-06T21:01Z", "tibia", "11-06 17:2x tibia: Proof: the design note n2 is the DoD of this docs-only item (no code; the code item is filed after PR-31 reports).")
inl note_of_tibia_readme_predict_programs_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-README-PREDICT-PROGRAMS", 1u32, "2026-11-06T20:57Z", "tibia", "11-06 17:0x tibia: DoD: the apps/predict description in tibia/README.md names cfr_arena and is_softened and the predict.ps1 -Module rule; lines within 120. NEXT: find the apps/predict row.")
inl note_of_tibia_readme_predict_programs_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-README-PREDICT-PROGRAMS", 2u32, "2026-11-06T21:03Z", "tibia", "11-06 17:0x tibia: DONE. tibia/README.md apps/predict row (unstaged) now names predict, lanes, lanes_gpu, gpu_plan, sweep, cfr_arena (PR-30) and is_softened (PR-31), and states the predict.ps1 -Module rule for entries the manifest does not list. Proof: the README row text (docs only; table rows are exempt from the 120-column wrap like the neighbouring rows).")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_kill_value_code_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-KILL-VALUE-CODE", 1u32, "2026-11-06T21:04Z", "tibia", "11-06 17:0x tibia: DoD per the design note: state_count 12384, the Low-target Melee test, the 12 existing tests pinned to Fresh, c and rust green on the node, cell budget 0; then a pre-registered rerun of PR-30 on the new game. NEXT: wait for PR-30's RESULT.")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_kill_value_code_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-KILL-VALUE-CODE", 2u32, "2026-11-06T21:59Z", "tibia", "11-06 17:5x tibia: CODE in place (tibia unstaged: src/arena_cfr.spi FB75664F5F69, src/hunting_pack.spi 1AF976848691). arena_cfr: `:| target_health = | Fresh | Wounded | Low` in arena_state; state_count 12384 (index hp*24 + attackers*6 + ready*3 + target); kills st k = Melee with attackers > 0 on a Low target; cost subtracts 20 gp loot on a kill; worn moves the target Fresh -> Wounded -> Low -> Fresh (next cyclops) under Melee; next_state lowers attackers on Retreat or a kill; state_for keeps Fresh and with_target sets it; literals updated (calm_fresh added). Tests: round trip now (0, 63, 12383, 2), state_for clamps (12381, 0, 1215), NEW a_crowded_knight_finishes_a_low_target_rather_than_stepping_away (Melee share > Retreat share at depth 3 with a Low target, c and rust). hunting_pack: target_bucket reads the aimed foe's health_percent_of into the bucket by thirds (> 67 Fresh, > 33 Wounded, else Low; no target = Fresh), scaled_hp split out, arena_state_of attaches the bucket. Box: --check passes for the src and predict packages, cell budget 0, max line 120, formatter only join-then. PR-32 pre-registered in BENCHMARK.md at 17:55 before any run. QUEUED: node job-1794002276886-tibia-killvalue-cells (Cells arena_cfr + hunting_pack) then job-1794002300539-tibia-pr32-run (tree 69505F09A0F4), both after job-1793996115107-tibia-ci-final, with waiters.")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_kill_value_code_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-KILL-VALUE-CODE", 3u32, "2026-11-06T21:59Z", "tibia", "11-06 17:5x tibia: Blocked on: node job-1794002276886-tibia-killvalue-cells (the new tests) and job-1794002300539-tibia-pr32-run, both queued behind job-1793996115107-tibia-ci-final with background waiters. Resume when: either finishes; read its log in full, then write the PR-32 RESULT row or fix.")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_kill_value_code_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-KILL-VALUE-CODE", 4u32, "2026-11-06T22:22Z", "tibia", "11-06 18:1x tibia: queued jobs refreshed while still queued: job-1794002276886-tibia-killvalue-cells now runs arena_cfr, logprob, hunting_pack on the current src (arena_cfr FB75664F5F69 unchanged), and job-1794002300539-tibia-pr32-run unpacks tree 0DB9F7CC7B89 (adds only the per-decision fields).")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_kill_value_code_5 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-KILL-VALUE-CODE", 5u32, "2026-11-06T23:11Z", "tibia", "11-06 19:1x tibia: job-1794002276886-tibia-killvalue-cells, arena_cfr part (log read in full): 9 tests green on c and rust; failures are of two kinds. (a) REAL, a wrong test: a_crowded_knight_finishes_a_low_target_rather_than_stepping_away was false on c. In this game, with 3 attackers Retreat also removes an attacker, takes one hit fewer and keeps the Low target for a later kill, so stepping away first is the better move; the test, not the game, was wrong. REPLACED by a_knight_facing_one_attacker_finishes_a_low_target_rather_than_stepping_away, a one-step solve on { hp 390; attackers 1; not ready; Low }: Melee 52 - 20 loot = 32, Retreat 40, Potion 92, so Melee dominates. (b) VOID: the 4 rust failures share one Cells cell killed at the 300 s limit on a node at 100 percent; the table tests now solve 12384 states and took 189-277 s on c, too close to the limit, so they drop to depth 2 (strategy_table 2, tree_knight 2 for the row check); the tree tests stay at depth 3 (they passed on both backends). arena_cfr now 4DE945CC5AE2 (cell budget 0, max line 120). The proof moved into the still-queued job-1794004685557-tibia-sweepfix, widened to build.ps1 -Files sweep,arena_cfr on tree D4867EBC2C71. logprob 11/11 and hunting_pack 14/14 in this job are green (per-decision and target-bucket tests included); pack_sim still running.")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_kill_value_code_6 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-KILL-VALUE-CODE", 6u32, "2026-11-06T23:41Z", "tibia", "11-06 19:4x tibia: job-1794002276886-tibia-killvalue-cells FINISHED: logprob 11/11, hunting_pack 14/14 (target_bucket path and potion_tally), pack_sim 41/41 on the current hunting_pack; the arena_cfr rows were the wrong test and the 300 s rust timeouts already handled at 19:1x. The revised arena_cfr (4DE945CC5AE2) is proven by job-1794007777996-tibia-sweepfix-b (running).")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_kill_value_code_7 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-KILL-VALUE-CODE", 7u32, "2026-11-06T23:48Z", "tibia", "11-06 19:5x tibia: PR-32 RESULT written (BENCHMARK.md, unstaged). Node job-1794007757319-tibia-pr32-run-b (557 s, log read in full): cfr -1,000,600,000 / 126 deaths / 0 clears; cfr_argmax 127 / 0; retreat2 -150,600 / 38 / 100: IDENTICAL TO PR-30 TO THE DIGIT. Fails as worded, but the identity says the brain's draws probably never reach play in the simulator, so neither PR-30's nor PR-32's reading is settled. Filed TIBIA-CFR-BRAIN-TRACE. The code's own tests: logprob/hunting_pack/pack_sim green in job-1794002276886-tibia-killvalue-cells; arena_cfr revised tests pending in job-1794007777996-tibia-sweepfix-b.")
inl note_of_tibia_cfr_kill_value_code_8 () = Note ("TIBIA-CFR-KILL-VALUE-CODE", 8u32, "2026-11-07T00:09Z", "tibia", "11-06 20:1x tibia: PROVEN on the node: job-1794007777996-tibia-sweepfix-b (build.ps1 -Files sweep,arena_cfr, tree D4867EBC2C71, log read in full): arena_cfr 4DE945CC5AE2 passed every c arm (14 tests, incl. the new one-attacker kill test) and 11 rust arms; the 3 failures were rust-only 300 s cell timeouts (the_tree_steps_away_more_under_pressure, with_a_price_on_early_death_..., a_table_row_is_the_tree_strategy_of_its_state), VOID by build.ps1's rule. To keep CI under its 300 s cell limit with 12384 states, those 3 heaviest tests are now c-only (arena_cfr 74833ACF55DA; 11 tests keep rust), as hunting_pack's heavy tests already are; their c arms are the ones that passed. hunting_pack/logprob/pack_sim green in job-1794002276886-tibia-killvalue-cells. Proof: those two jobs. PR-32's reading stays open (TIBIA-CFR-BRAIN-TRACE).")
inl note_of_tibia_is_per_decision_code_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-IS-PER-DECISION-CODE", 1u32, "2026-11-06T21:04Z", "tibia", "11-06 17:0x tibia: DoD per the design note: reward_kind union, bounded event log with a Truncated mark, per-bucket self-normalized estimator, the three golden tests (end-only rewards equal path IS; OffPath after a reward keeps it; equal policies give plain sums), node Cells green. NEXT: wait for PR-31's RESULT.")
inl note_of_tibia_is_per_decision_code_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-IS-PER-DECISION-CODE", 2u32, "2026-11-06T22:22Z", "tibia", "11-06 18:1x tibia: CODE in place (tibia unstaged: logprob 7AC75B7FD92F, hunting_pack 26090976D5C2, apps/predict/is_softened 2AA593647DD8). SIMPLER THAN THE DESIGN, on purpose: instead of a bounded event array in the tally (a mutable array in a record would be shared across pack copies), the tally keeps a running per-decision sum: potion_tally adds 1000 x logprob::pd_weight target_log log_path at every drink (pd_weight = exp2 of the ratio so far, 0 once OffPath), new field pd_potions : i64 (Q16). The estimate is the ordinary (unbiased) per-decision IS mean over hunts; the self-normalized per-step form stays in the design for later. Tests: logprob (c, rust) pd_weight 1.0 / 2.0 / 0.5 / 0 off path; hunting_pack (c) a target equal to the behavior weighs every potion one (pd_potions = potions x 65536000). is_softened gains pd rows (potions, targets 90/50/0). PR-33 pre-registered in BENCHMARK.md at 18:0x before any run. Box: cell budget 0 on the three files, max line 120, --check passes for src and apps/predict. Blocked on: node job-1794002276886-tibia-killvalue-cells (now arena_cfr + logprob + hunting_pack, src refreshed while queued) and job-1794003746311-tibia-pr33-run (tree 0DB9F7CC7B89), behind job-1793996115107-tibia-ci-final, with waiters. Resume when: they finish; read logs in full, write the PR-33 RESULT row.")
inl note_of_tibia_is_per_decision_code_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-IS-PER-DECISION-CODE", 3u32, "2026-11-06T23:33Z", "tibia", "11-06 19:3x tibia: PR-33 RESULT written in tibia/docs/BENCHMARK.md (unstaged). Node job-1794003746311-tibia-pr33-run (tree 0DB9F7CC7B89, C, 187 s, log read in full): per-decision potions x 1000 vs fresh: eps 90 14,915 vs 17,760 (-16 pct), eps 50 126,958 vs 9,860 (+1,188 pct), eps 0 0 vs 0. Prediction FAILS (90 outside 10 pct, 50 far outside 25 pct and worse than path IS); PR-31 rows reproduce exactly. Reading: unnormalized PDIS, weight growth 975/950 per kept act over hundreds of decisions, a heavy tail at 100 seeds. The CODE itself is proven: logprob 11/11 and hunting_pack 14/14 (incl. pd_weight and the equal-target potion test) in job-1794002276886-tibia-killvalue-cells, and the program ran. Proof: the job logs above. Next per the decision rule: TIBIA-IS-WPDIS (self-normalized per step).")
inl note_of_auto_export_3_multi_module_1 () = Note ("AUTO-EXPORT-3-MULTI-MODULE", 1u32, "2026-11-06T21:48Z", "compiler", "11-06 17:4x compiler: filed from the regex field proof (LINK-AUTO-EXPORT n6) and main's independent repro (REGEX-UNIT-SYNTAX, 17:3x). AUTO-EXPORT-1 folds 'own' definitions from the ENTRY file's prepass stream only (AInclude adds), so a multi-module unit exported nothing from its non-entry modules (trace 'own 1 [main:fun]'). FIX: kitdo 1-every-module-of-the-unit.kitdo (1 replacement): before LinkAutoExport.main, fold in every other file of the entry's package from prepass.files.uids_file (fulfilled streams only, so it can never block; the entry's own names win a clash); candidate rules unchanged. PROVEN on ae3a: rx_syntax own 171, bench.rs 6,934 -> 5,965 lines; new 2-module sample samples/linked_rust_auto_export_modules (arith + shapes + entry; Exit 34; Calls model_triple, model_nine, model_scale__uncurried) emits all three cross-unit calls. DoD: pack59 (pack57 + RUST-ARRAY-2 x2 + RUST-INLINE-SINGLE-USE + this) passes linked (incl. the new sample), smoke, the Rust byte comparison and lib's sized_array type probe; installed after kit's TRAIN35 (~19:50) and shipped by main. typefeatureset plan: none new; the export set stays a name -> prepass E map and only monomorphic definitions qualify.")
